window.GRV_DATA = {"passages": {"v205_p1": {"text": "Animals live longer when their calorie intake is restricted to two-thirds of what is considered normal for their species. Animals so restricted are also generally healthier: most diseases, including cancer, diabetes, and neurodegenerative illness, are forestalled. This phenomenon was long attributed to a simple slowing of metabolism (cells’ production of energy from fuel molecules) and consequent reproduction of its toxic by-products in response to less food. In fact, however, calorie restriction does not slow mammalian metabolism and in yeast and worms, metabolism is both sped up and altered. Some scientists now theorize that calorie restriction is a biological stressor that, like natural food scarcity, induces a more complex defensive response, which in mammals includes changes in cellular defenses and repair.", "highlight": "in yeast and worms, metabolism is both sped up and altered"}, "v201_p1": {"text": "Benjamin Franklin is portrayed in American history as the quintessential self-made man. In “Self-reliance”, Emerson asks, “Where is the master who could have instructed Franklin?” In fact, Franklin took instruction widely, and his scientific work was highly collaborative. Friends in England sent equipment needed for his electrical experiments, others, in Philadelphia, helped him set up his workshop there. Philip Syng constructed a device for generating electrical charges, while Tomas Hopkinson demonstrated the potential of pointed conductors. Franklin, in addition to being the group’s theoretician, wrote and published its results. His fame as an individual researcher is partly a consequence of the shorthand by which when one person writes about a group’s discoveries, history sometimes grants singular credit for collective effort.", "highlight": "His fame as an individual researcher is partly a consequence of the shorthand by which when one person writes about a group’s discoveries, history sometimes grants singular credit for collective effort."}, "v234_p2": {"text": "The manuscripts of the eight extant Latin tragedies identify the plays as the Marci Lucii Annei Senecae Tradoediae. Since nobody of that name is known, modern scholars believe the dramas to be the work of Lucius Annaeus Seneca the Younger, the well-known philosopher, orator, and politician. Clearly, the tragedies were written during Seneca’s lifetime: internal refrences to earlier poets, most notably Ovid, indicate that the dramas cannot have been composed prior to the second decade C.E., and the plays must have been written by 96 C.E., when Quintilian quotes Medea, one of the tragedies.\n\nIt is remarkable, however, that Seneca himself never mentions the plays, since there are certainly passages in them that could be used to illustrate points of his philosophy. There are at least two possible explanations. In the early Roman Empire, playwrights were sometimes exiled or executed for lines construed as directed against the emperor; thus, Seneca’s silence may be simple prudence. But if anyone could safely attach his name to dramas, surely it would be Seneca, the emperor’s tutor. And although Herrmann offers Seneca’s modesty as an explanation, Seneca is not averse to referring to his other writings. The evidence for equating Seneca with the author of the tragedies seems circumstantial.", "highlight": null}, "v11_p1": {"text": "The novel 《Georges》, published under Alexander Dumas' name, may actually have been written by Felicien Mallefille. A comparison of 《Georges》 with well-known Dumas' novels such as 《The Count of Monte Cristo》 suggests that Dumas had little to do with 《Georges》. For example, the characters of 《Georges》 are tiresomely earnest, while those from Dumas' well-known novels crack jokes and utter colorful oaths. Meanwhile, in a technical sense, 《Georges》 is well-written, while 《The Count of Monte Cristo》, with all its verve and sparkle, is full of redundancies, repetitions, and non sequiturs. As Umberto Eco discovered while attempting to translate 《The Count of Monte Cristo》, the charm of Dumas' novel and its \"narrative wisdom\" are inseparable from its \"linguistically sludgy and gasping\" prose.", "highlight": null}, "v226_p4": {"text": "The phonograph never merely recorded music: it changed both how people listened and how they played. Early recordings of violinists suggest that vibrato─the trembling action of hand or fingerboard that gives notes a warbling sweetness─was once used more sparingly than it is today. By the 1930s, many leading violinists had adopted continuous vibrato, which became the approved style taught in conservatories. Musicologist Mark Katz proposes that technology prompted the change. When vibrato’s wobble was added to violin tone, the phonograph could pick it up more easily; acoustically, it's a \"wider\" sound. Also, vibrato's fuzzier focus enabled players to cover up inaccuracies of intonation, and phonographs made players self-conscious about intonation. What worked in recording studios spread to concert stages.", "highlight": null}, "v222_p7": {"text": "This passage is excerpted from an article discussing archaeologists' recovery of wooden combs from an ancient Roman fortress.\n\nWhen writing about combs, Roman archaeologists and ancient historians have nearly invariably associated these 'toilet articles' with female beauty and the mundus muliebris, the world of women. Such an interpretation is in striking contrast with many other periods of the European past, when combs appear to have been either ungendered or tokens of an exclusive male identity. From the Middle Bronze Age through to the Iron Age as well as in the Middle Ages, combs and other grooming tools often served as references to masculine beauty and as such became part of the grave furnishings arranged around the dead bodies of warriors. The question then comes to mind: why there would have been nothing of an equivalent in the Roman interlude? Moreover, the numerous finds that have recently been reported from various Roman army camps make one feel uneasy about the strengths of the traditional interpretation. Admittedly, the presence of women in and around Roman army camps is no longer a point of discussion, and some of the combs from such military contexts may indeed have been in use by the wives of officers or the concubines of ordinary soldiers, but can they account for the numbers that have been found? In view of these thoughts, one is tempted to consider whether the combs were perhaps rather used by the soldiers themselves.", "highlight": null}, "v224_p5": {"text": "Wildcats are improbable candidates for domestication. Like all felids (cats), wildcats are obligate carnivores, meaning they have a limited metabolic ability to digest anything except proteins. Wildcats live a solitary existence and defend exclusive territories, making them more attached to places than to people. Furthermore, cats do not perform directed tasks and their actual utility is debatable; even as mousers, in this latter role, terrier dogs and ferrets are preferable. Accordingly, there is little reason to believe an early agricultural community would have sought out and selected the wildcat as a house pet. Rather, the best inference is that wildcats exploiting human environments were simply tolerated by people and, over time and space, they gradually diverged from their \"wild\" relatives.", "highlight": "Rather, the best inference is that wildcats exploiting human environments were simply tolerated by people and, over time and space, they gradually diverged from their \"wild\" relatives."}, "v230_p3": {"text": "Most of the studies of the effect of aging on short-term memory have led researchers to conclude that younger adults perform short-term-memory tasks better than people over the age of 65. But these studies were all conducted in afternoon sessions. In a recent study conducted both in morning and in afternoon sessions, the older participants performed much better in morning sessions than in afternoon sessions. The younger participants did not, however, perform any better in the morning", "highlight": null}, "v224_p7": {"text": "In her study of New Haven, Connecticut, covering the period 1639-1789, Cornelia Dayton argues that during the seventeenth century, colonial women had easy access to New Haven's courts, where their concerns and complaints were taken seriously by Puritan magistrates. These magistrates deviated from English legal practice by eschewing lawyers and simplifying procedures, thereby allowing, even encouraging, women's participation in litigation.\n\nBut by the early eighteenth century, Dayton contends New Haven's courts, like those of other British colonial areas, were reverting to English legal procedures, engaging lawyers to argue cases, and focusing more on property issues. These changes resulted primarily from an expanding economy that brought about new forms of credit, vastly augmented indebtedness, contact with nonlocal markets, and sharper class and racial distinctions. These factors worked to marginalize colonia women's economic contributions to their families and to diminish their influence in their communities and their usefulness to judges and juries in what Dayton calls the \"litigated economy.\" In this \"anglicized legal environment,\" patriarchal authority became more deeply entrenched, the spheres of public and private activity were restructured, and colonial women became less visible participants in a legal arena that now catered primarily to colonial men's interests.", "highlight": null}, "v199_p2": {"text": "Early in the twentieth century, San Francisco was the main venue for African American jazz musicians on the West Coast of the United States. Musical activity was centered in a district known as the Barbary Coast, where an abundance of nightclubs provided ample work opportunities for local players and drew musicians and other entertainers, many of them African American, from throughout the country. In 1921, as part of its Prohibition-era efforts, the government closed the Barbary Coast. This closure was the decisive event that established Los Angeles as the premier center for jazz on the West Coast. Once the Barbary Coast was shut down, it became far harder for jazz musicians to make a living in San Francisco; thus, many headed south to Los Angeles.\n\nYet even before that closing, the center of jazz activity had begun to swing southward. With the largest and fastest growing African American urban community in the West, as well as the growing movie industry and an emerging recording industry, Los Angeles was already a magnet for jazz musicians from other parts of the country, especially New Orleans, where jazz players suffered a devastating blow with closing of the Storyville district in 1917.", "highlight": null}, "v23_p1": {"text": "Isobel Grundy rightly argues that in researching pre-nineteenth-century women's historical writing, scholars must define history broadly and include historical fiction, biography, court memoirs, and family history. Grundy also believes that these writings provide \"a history of a whole female culture, while embodying a pre-nineteenth-century feminine\" relationship to history. On this point, I am skeptical, as I do not believe there was a characteristic women's relationship to history. Instead, my research suggests that pre-nineteenth-century British women writers' engagement with historical discourse depended on such things as their political commitments and class affiliations and their perceptions of developing historical genres and markets. We must give sufficient attention to the myriad individual authors and texts before generalizing widely about women writers' engagements with history.", "highlight": null}, "v230_p2": {"text": "In the absence of reliable data concerning the relationship between the material quality (i.e., physical condition) and the price of used books, it is impossible to offer statistically exact information for the impact of the used-book market on the cost of reading in eighteenth-century England. Yet, it can hardly be doubted that such an impact occurred, not only through the standard behavior of markets but inferentially through the innovative design and packaging strategies that London booksellers increasingly resorted to from 1760 in order to identify (and no doubt also create) more finely differentiated classes of readers. Fortunately, we can also call on extensive, independent price lists for eighteenth-century books published in Britain to track differences in the cost of new and used volumes of the same title, edition, and format. To the extent that new list prices for successive editions of the same work in a uniform format remain constant or increase at a lesser rate than consumer prices generally, the hypothesis that the secondary book market exercised a drag on book prices would gain fresh support. At the same time, variance in price among new and used copies of any given title and edition can be used as a proxy for material quality determinations in the two markets.", "highlight": null}, "v208_p2": {"text": "The hypothesis that paranormal phenomena are real but lie outside the limits of science is supported by considerable evidence. The society of Psychical Research has collected stories of ordinary people apparently demonstrating paranormal abilities. Entirely anecdotal, this evidence has nothing to do with science, since it cannot be reproduced under controlled conditions. But the society took great trouble to interview first-hand witnesses and to document the stories carefully. One fact that emerges clearly from the stories is that paranormal events occur, if they occur at all, only when people are experiencing strong emotion. This would immediately explain why paranormal phenomena are not observable under the conditions of a well-controlled scientific experiment. Strong emotion is inherently incompatible with controlled scientific procedures.", "highlight": "Strong emotion is inherently incompatible with controlled scientific procedures."}, "v231_p1": {"text": "New underwater tunnel projects increasingly rely upon immersed tube technology, which involves digging a channel in the seabed and then sinking prefabricated tunnel sections into it. As well as being more resilient in earthquakes, immersed tubes are generally faster and less expensive to build than traditional bored tunnels. To begin with, problems with one section of tunnel won’t necessarily delay the entire project, and because immersed tubes can have a rectangular cross-section, they are a more efficient shape than circular tunnels for side-by-side railway lines. And while bored tunnels are usually considered stable only if their depth under the seabed at least equals their diameter, immersed tubes can sit immediately under the seafloor, allowing shallower approach gradients.", "highlight": "To begin with, problems with one section of tunnel won’t necessarily delay the entire project, and because immersed tubes can have a rectangular cross-section, they are a more efficient shape than circular tunnels for side-by-side railway lines."}, "v10_p3": {"text": "Between 2500 and 2000 B.C., numerous statues representing real, historical people were produced in southern Mesopotamia. In the standard Western division of genres, mimetic resemblance is the first criterion of portraiture. However, the Mesopotamian images are portraits in that they represent individuals, even though they do not mimetically imitate the individual's features. These statues were to be placed in temples where they stood in for the individual as a worshipper and could function as a form of presence of that individual. They were therefore linked to the person in ways even closer than the modern notion of portrait, since the person's essence continued to exist in the image: numerous ancient texts demonstrate that images, for the Mesopotamians, had agency and were therefore powerful objects.", "highlight": null}, "v208_p1": {"text": "Having a larger assortment to choose from increases consumers’ expectations about matching their preferences. The heightened expectations seem logical, since assortments containing more or more varied items should increase the degree to which preferences can be matched. In practice, however, as assortment size increases, the degree to which consumers realize better preference matches often rises relatively little. Larger assortments may not actually offer more variety, the market may simply not supply an envisioned offering, or in the absence of sophisticated search tools, consumers may miss a better preference match even if it is available. Therefore, larger assortments can increase the likelihood that expectations will not be met, leaving consumers less satisfied with options chosen from larger rather than smaller assortments.", "highlight": "leaving consumers less satisfied with options chosen from larger rather than smaller assortments"}, "v224_p14": {"text": "For good reasons, economists prefer to study people’s revealed preferences; that is, to look at individuals’ actual choices and decisions rather than their (sometimes deceptive) stated intentions or their subjective reports of likes and dislikes. Yet people’s choices often bear a mixed relationship to their own happiness. Studies from behavioral economics and psychology find that people depart from the standard model of the rational economic agent in various ways; they make inconsistent choices, fail to learn from experiences, and base their own satisfaction on how their situation compares with that of others. If people display bounded rationality when it comes to maximizing utility, then their choices do not necessarily reflect their \"true\" preferences, and an exclusive reliance on choices to infer what people desire loses some appeal.", "highlight": null}, "v236_p1": {"text": "After Henry IV usurped the English throne from Richard II in 1399, evidence suggests the new king censored records that portrayed the new regime unfavorably. While no censorship orders are preserved, one chronicler mentions that Henry ordered all chronicles inspected. That not a single English chronicle is critical of the coup is a pretty good indication that Henry suppressed any hostile material. Moreover, the single voice with which the English chronicles praise Henry and defame Richard after 1399 is challenged by the contrary version of events recorded in the French chronicles. For most of the nineteenth and twentieth centuries, this discrepancy was attributed to French Anglophobia, but the accuracy and value of the French chronicles has now been reappraised.", "highlight": null}, "v201_p2": {"text": "As of the late 1980’s, neither theorists nor large-scale computer climate models could accurately predict whether cloud systems would help or hurt a warming globe. Some studies suggested that a four percent increase in stratocumulus clouds over the ocean could compensate for a doubling in atmospheric carbon dioxide, preventing a potentially disastrous planetwide temperature increase. On the other hand, an increase in cirrus clouds could increase global warming.\n\nThat clouds represented the weakest element in climate models was illustrated by a study of fourteen such models. Comparing climate forecasts for a world with double the current amount of carbon dioxide, researchers found that the models agreed quite well if clouds were not included. But when clouds were incorporated, a wide range of forecasts was produced. With such discrepancies plaguing the models, scientists could not easily predict how quickly the world's climate would change, nor could they tell which regions would face dustier droughts or deadlier monsoons.", "highlight": null}, "v30_p3": {"text": "Carla L. Peterson’s 《Doers of the Word》 (1997), a study of African American women speakers and writers from 1830-1880, is an important addition to scholarship on nineteenth-century African American women. Its scope resembles that of Frances Smith Foster’s 1993 study, but its approach is quite different. For Foster, the Black women who came to literary voice in nineteenth-century America were claiming their rights as United States citizens, denying that anything should disqualify them from full membership in an enlightened national polity. Peterson sees these same women as having been fundamentally estranged from the nation by a dominant culture unsympathetic to Black women, and by a Black intelligentsia whose male view of race concerns left little room for Black female intellect.", "highlight": null}, "v32_p2": {"text": "The pepper Capsicum chinense grows as a native wild plant only in South America. Birds swallow the pepper’s fruit whole, thereby providing the plant with its means of distributing seeds. Domesticated varieties of C.chinense grow in the Caribbean islands as well as in South America. Although it is unknown just when C.chinense was introduced into the islands, the introduction of the species was probably the result of human activity, because _____.", "highlight": null}, "v236_p4": {"text": "Whereas Carlos Bulosan aimed through fiction and personal testimony to advance both Filipino civil rights in the United States and the social transformation of the Philippines, Yen Le Espiritu has set herself the task of recovering life histories of Filipino Americans. Her work brings Filipino Americans of the generation following the 1934-1965 immigration hiatus graphically to life. A special strength is the representation of Filipino American women, who were scarce among immigrants before the 1934 American curb on Filipino immigration but composed more than half of the immigrants to America since liberalization in 1965. Espiritu’s subjects document their changing sense of Filipino identity in the United States, much as Bulosan did as a member of the first substantial wave of immigrants.", "highlight": null}, "v202_p4": {"text": "Though respectful of the groundbreaking work in translating Native American oral narratives done by Dell Hymes and Dennis Tedlock in the 1970s, Robert Parker notes that their work emerged when \"Romanticized ideas of 'the Indian' ... and of poetry” converged to create a surprisingly uncritical reception of their claim that Native American stories are in fact poetry. Parker objects that by claiming to discover poetry as the true nature of Native American narrative and asserting the value of such narrative on that ground, Hymes and Tedlock \"misconstrue the social relation between power, genre, and value.\" Parker's own position is that Native American literature, on its own terms, matches the best canonical literature in the European tradition and need not be validated by that tradition's notions of value.", "highlight": null}, "v30_p4": {"text": "The distinction between the nutritional quality and quantity of prey is one component of the hypotheses that attempt to explain the declining populations of Steller sea lions in the Gulf of Alaska beginning in the 1970s. One view holds that the quantity of prey available was high overall, but because of the species composition of available prey (primarily non-fatty fish of the gadid family), the diet was nutritionally inferior—the junk food hypothesis. An alternative view is that gadids are nutritionally adequate but were not available in sufficient numbers because of fishing or some other factor. In either case, juvenile sea lions would be affected more than mature individuals because of the younger animals’ higher energy requirements and relative inexperience at foraging.", "highlight": "An alternative view is that gadids are nutritionally adequate but were not available in sufficient numbers because of fishing or some other factor."}, "v214_p2": {"text": "In 1776, the state of New Jersey adopted a constitution that ignored gender in its suffrage clause, defining voters simply as adult residents worth at least fifty pounds. After 1776, women routinely participated in the state's electoral process, until, in 1801, the state legislature passed a law redefining voters solely as adult White male taxpaying citizens. Political historians have been perplexed by New Jersey's deviation from the established norm of exclusive male suffrage, finding no sign of public agitation either for or against the voting rights of women prior to their enfranchisement in 1776 or disenfranchisement in 1801. Consequently, historians have downplayed the extent to which suffrage resulted from careless constitutional construction and have viewed the 1801 disenfranchisement as a legislative effort to remedy this carelessness. Yet examination of revolutionary-era manuscripts indicates that the 1776 suffrage clause underwent close legislative scrutiny that led to several significant changes; thus, the absence of gender references in the final version was probably not accidental. Indeed, the evidence suggests that New Jersey's legislators believed that all who possessed sufficient net worth were entitled to vote. However, they also saw the net worth qualification as serving to prevent an overdemocratization of the voting process.", "highlight": null}, "v8_p3": {"text": "The hypothesis that paranormal phenomena are real but lie outside the limits of science is supported by considerable evidence. The Society for Psychical Research has collected stories of ordinary people apparently demonstrating paranormal abilities. Entirely anecdotal, this evidence has nothing to do with science, since it cannot be reproduced under controlled conditions. But the society took great trouble to interview first-hand witnesses and to document the stories carefully. One fact that emerges clearly from the stories is that paranormal events occur, if they occur at all, only when people are experiencing strong emotion. This would immediately explain why paranormal phenomena are not observable under the conditions of a well-controlled scientific experiment. Strong emotion is inherently incompatible with controlled scientific procedures.", "highlight": "Strong emotion is inherently incompatible with controlled scientific procedures."}, "v18_p3": {"text": "Because densely populated urban centers concentrate human activity, we think of them as pollution crisis zones. Ecology-minded discussions often focus on ways to make cities seem somewhat less oppressively man-made, such as increasing the area devoted to parks or easing the intensity of development. But most such changes would actually undermine cities' extraordinary energy efficiency. Per unit of area, cities in the United States generate more greenhouse gases, use more energy, and produce more solid waste than most other American regions of comparable size. On a map depicting negative environmental impacts in relation to surface area, therefore, cities would look like intense hot spots. If you plotted the same negative impacts by resident or household, however, the reverse would hold.", "highlight": null}, "v197_p2": {"text": "This passage is adapted from material published in 2019.\n\nIn 2018, the U.S. Congress passed the \"45Q legislation,\" which significantly increases corporate tax credits for various uses of CO2 (carbon dioxide). The most controversial use is \"enhanced oil recovery.\" An oil company purchases CO2, transports it by pipeline and injects it into depleted oil wells, pushing out extra oil it could not extract by conventional means. A climate change solution that entails producing more fossil fuels may sound Orwellian, and some environmental critics have attacked 45Q as just another fossil-fuel subsidy program in disguise. But enhanced oil recovery appears to reduce current emissions because the CO2 typically captured from natural gas or ethanol refineries gets sequestered underground. Some environmentalists, such as Kurt Waltzer of the Clean Air Task Force, argue that turning carbon capture into an energy technology rather than an emission technology is the first step toward broad commercial adoption of CO2 removal. It turns recaptured CO2 into a product to be bought or sold rather than simply a cost to be endured.", "highlight": null}, "v198_p3": {"text": "Amatrox is a highly infectious disease common in the tropics. When people suffering from amatrox are given the drug vericol, their symptoms cease and the amatrox virus can no longer be detected. When treatment with vericol is discontinued, however, amatrox symptoms sometimes return within a few months and the virus is again detectable. Therefore, although treatment with vericol suppresses the amatrox virus below detectable levels, it does not always eliminate the virus entirely from the body.", "highlight": null}, "v13_p2": {"text": "Biologists know that some marine algae can create clouds by producing the gas dimethylsulphide (DMS), which reacts with oxygen in air above the sea to form solid particles. These particles provide a surface on which water vapor can condense to form clouds. Lovelock contends that this process is part of global climatic-control system. According to Lovelock, Earth acts like a super organism, with all its biological and physical systems cooperating to keep it healthy. He hypothesized that warmer conditions increase algal activity and DMS output, seeding more clouds, which cool the planet by blocking out the Sun. Then, as the climate cools, algal activity and DMS level decrease and the cycle continues. In response to biologists who question how organisms presumably working for their own selfish ends could have evolved to behave in a way that benefits not only the planet but the organisms as well, Lovelock points out that cooling benefits the algae, which remain at the ocean surface, because it allows the cooled upper layers of the ocean to sink, and then the circulating water carries nutrients upward from the depths below. Algae may also benefit from nitrogen raining down from clouds they have helped to form.", "highlight": null}, "v233_p1": {"text": "Recent studies of ancient Maya water management have found that the urban architecture of some cities was used to divert rainfall runoff into gravity-fed systems of interconnected reservoirs. In the central and southern Maya Lowlands, this kind of water control was necessary to support large populations throughout the year due to the scarcity of perennial surface water and the seasonal availability of rainfall. Some scholars argue that the concentration of water within the urban core of these sites provided a centralized source of political authority for Maya elites based largely on controlled water access. Such an argument is plausible; however, it is less useful for understanding the sociopolitical implications of water use and control in other, water-rich parts of the Maya region.", "highlight": null}, "v200_p2": {"text": "Astronomers who study planet formation once believed that comets—because they remain mostly in the distant Oort cloud, where temperatures are close to absolute zero—must be pristine relics of the material that formed the outer planets. The conceptual shift away from seeing comets as pristine relics began in the 1970s, when laboratory simulations revealed there was sufficient ultraviolet radiation reaching comets to darken their surfaces and there were sufficient cosmic rays to alter chemical bonds or even molecular structure near the surface. Nevertheless, astronomers still believed that when a comet approached the Sun—where they could study it—the Sun’s intense heat would remove the corrupted surface layer, exposing the interior. About the same time, though, scientists realized comets might contain decaying radioactive isotopes that could have warmed cometary interiors to temperatures that caused the interiors to evolve.", "highlight": null}, "v30_p1": {"text": "During the 1920s, most advocates of scientific management, Frederick Taylor`s method for maximizing workers’ productivity by rigorously routinizing their jobs, opposed the five-day workweek. Although scientific managers conceded that reducing hours might provide an incentive to workers, in practice they more often used pay differentials to encourage higher productivity. Those reformers who wished to embrace both scientific management and reduced hours had to make a largely negative case, portraying the latter as an antidote to the rigors of the former.\n\nIn contrast to the scientific managers, Henry Ford claimed that shorter hours led to greater productivity and profits. However, few employers matched either Ford’s vision or his specific interest in mass marketing a product—automobiles—that required leisure for its use, and few unions succeeded in securing shorter hours through bargaining. At its 1928 convention, the American Federation of Labor (AFL) boasted of approximately 165,000 members working five-day, 40-hour weeks. But although this represented an increase of about 75,000 since 1926, about 70 percent of the total came from five extremely well-organized building trades’ unions.", "highlight": "At its 1928 convention, the American Federation of Labor (AFL) boasted of approximately 165,000 members working five-day, 40-hour weeks."}, "v234_p1": {"text": "Experiments and field observations show that in a Mediterranean plant community, drought has a counterintuitively positive effect on shrub seedling establishment. Due to decreased competition by annuals, droughts increase opportunities for shrub seedlings. Under nondrought conditions, annuals competed with shrub seedlings more effectively, confirming the experimenters' assumption that annuals benefit more than shrub seedlings from an increase in water availability. This may be attributed to their faster or more efficient uptake of soil resources. Similar patterns can be observed in other semi-arid communities. Jurena and Archer showed for a savanna community that root biomass of grasses increased in wetter conditions, decreasing grassland susceptibility to encroachment by shrub seedlings.", "highlight": null}, "v10_p1": {"text": "Astronomers have had difficulty accounting for certain planets discovered outside our solar system. They are called hot Jupiters because each is similar in mass to Jupiter, the largest solar-system planet, but orbits its parent star at a fraction of the distance at which Earth, let alone Jupiter, orbits the Sun. In the standard, solar-system-based theory of planetary formation, such a massive planet could not form so close to a star. So most attempts to explain a hot Jupiter's existence envision it forming farther away, then migrating inward. According to one hypothesis, the planet's gravitational field tugs on the proto-planetary disk of dust and gas from which it formed. The disk exerts its own gravitational tug, and this interplay of forces robs the planet of momentum in its orbital path, forcing it to spiral in toward the star. According to another hypothesis, the planet's gravitational field is so strong that it creates a groove in the disk, partitioning it into inner and outer regions; the resulting gravitational interactions between the planet and these regions cause the planet to lose orbital momentum and spiral inward. Another question remains: what prevents the planet from continuing its spiral until it collides with the star?", "highlight": null}, "v33_p2": {"text": "Zora Neale Hurston’s 1942 autobiography, 《Dust Tracks on a Road》, has received some of the most negative criticism of any of Hurston’s books. Among critics’ complaints—some from Hurston's warmest admirers—is the work’s fragmentary nature, a nature which, while presented in other Hurston texts, including the universally acclaimed novel 《Their Eyes Were Watching God》, is particularly conspicuous in 《Dust Tracks》. The complaints about 《Dust Tracks》 are valid if one insists on the cardinal conventions of autobiography: traditional autobiographical structure and formal organization, and a focused projection of the autobiographical persona. But 《Dust Tracks》 portrays a persona that resists reduction to a coherent unity—a person of many moods who is in tension with the world in which she moves. In order to correspond better to this persona, 《Dust Tracks》 focuses on the fragmented life of Hurston’s imagination: the psychological dynamics of her family, community stories, and characters of friends.", "highlight": null}, "v6_p1": {"text": "Unlike the static, classically composed portraits produced by her mentor Walker Evans, twentieth-century New York photographer Helen Levitt's photographs seem candid and spontaneous. Whereas Evans' subjects look directly into the camera, so that photographer and subject conspire in the making of a portrait, Levitt's subjects seem caught unawares. As a \"street\" photographer, before the term's invention, Levitt has claimed to have attempted to capture life as she found it. But there is a paradox to her technique. Her off-the-cuff aesthetic seemingly guarantees objectivity, since she was recording street scenes she happened upon, yet her photographs could be said to be highly subjective, to be reflections of Levitt's own distinctive preoccupations and ways of seeing. Unlike Evans' images, Levitt's are solely the products of the photographer without the conscious participation of their subjects. The repetitions evident in Levitt's choices of subjects, for example, her many photographs of children in masks and disguises, reveal more about Levitt herself than about those subjects.", "highlight": null}, "v234_p4": {"text": "Recent scholarship has explored collaborative authorship in the English Renaissance. Critics have studied well-known collaborative teams, such as that of Beaumont and Fletcher, and have now increasingly acknowledged that even some of Shakespeare's plays were likely written with collaborators. Indeed, every major English Renaissance playwright probably worked collaboratively at times. Some critics, such as Jeffrey Masten, hoped that this realization might dislodge traditional notions of authorship as a solitary activity. However, scholars analyzing plays written collaboratively often attempt to attribute acts, scenes, or speeches to individual authors who are thought to have worked separately before joining their work together. Thus, scholars' acceptance of the fact of collaborative writing has done little to change the model of the author; it simply multiplies the number of authors.", "highlight": null}, "v209_p1": {"text": "As the United States shifted from an agricultural, production-oriented economy to an urban, bureaucratized, consumer-oriented economy, children were removed from the labor force and valued for sentimental rather than instrumental reasons. Children were increasingly studied, regulated, and protected through the rise of pediatrics, child psychology, child-welfare agencies, compulsory schooling, child-study programs, and so-called scientific parenting regimes. These changes shifted public attention away from the child considered to be in need of saving and toward the kind of child whose development would preoccupy parents, and whom advertisers would showcase—and eventually appeal to directly—in their promotion of goods. The redefinition of childhood served not to separate children from the commercial realm, but, rather, to advance the commoditization of childhood and the broader transformation to a consumer economy.", "highlight": null}, "v203_p2": {"text": "French painter Édouard Manet's 1863 painting 《Le Bain》 sparked controversy in part for its depiction of figures in contemporary dress. Though as long ago as 1824 the novelist Stendhal had urged artists to depict \"the men of today and not those who probably never existed,\" serious paintings of modern-day Parisians were still relatively rare; the foremost painter of Manet's era, Ernest Meissonier, was celebrated for his idyllic scenes of the past. Manet's teacher Thomas Couture had achieved renown for his historical tableau of Roman times, 《The Romans of the Decadence》, and he required his students to copy the works of old masters. However, he also urged his students to take as the subjects of their own paintings contemporary sights such as workmen, public holidays, and examples of modern technology. Manet may have seemed an unlikely convert to the cause, with the inspiration for his early paintings coming mostly from old masters he had sketched in the Louvre and the Uffizi. Still, Manet had begun paying heed to the advice of his teacher with canvases such as 《The Absinthe Drinker》 (1858) and 《The Old Musician》 (1862). He continued this trend in 《Le Bain》, even if he appropriated his figures' poses directly from a 1518 Raphael drawing.", "highlight": null}, "v34_p4": {"text": "Recent studies of the gender gap in the history of United States policies tend to focus on candidate choice rather than on registration and turnout. This shift in focus from gender inequality in political participation may be due to the finding in several studies of voting behavior in the United States that since 1980, differences in rates of registration and voting between men and women are not statistically significant after controlling for traditional predictors of participation. However, Fullerton and Stern argue that researchers have overlooked the substantial gender gap in registration and voting in the South. While the gender gap in participation virtually disappeared outside the South by the 1950s, substantial gender differences persisted in the South throughout the 1950s and 1960s, only beginning to decline in 1970s.", "highlight": null}, "v225_p4": {"text": "A recent study shows that southern fulmars bring 40 percent more food to their chicks than do the closely related Antarctic petrels. Yet, fulmar chicks are only 10-20 percent heavier than petrel chicks. Hence, petrel chicks appear to be more efficient at converting their food into body mass. How can this be explained? First, while both species feed their chicks via regurgitation, petrels go on longer foraging trips. These trips may allow petrels to extract more water from the food or to partially digest their stomach contents, thereby creating more energy-rich meals. Thus, petrel chicks may receive more nutritious meals than fulmar chicks. Second, fulmar chicks are less well-insulated than are petrel chicks and may need to allocate a higher proportion of food energy to thermoregulation rather than growth.", "highlight": "Thus, petrel chicks may receive more nutritious meals than fulmar chicks."}, "v27_p2": {"text": "The theory of motivated reasoning suggests that, in legal decisions, different judges will assess the same information differently, depending on their backgrounds and fundamental values. Attitudinalists (theorists who contend that judges' decisions are driven by their own policy preferences) have concurred that their findings on ideological decision-making could be explained by the \"human reflex\" to \"convince oneself of the propriety of what one prefers to believe—motivated reasoning.\"\n\nMotivated reasoning, however, is subject to \"reasonableness constraints.\" For example, the accuracy of decision-making is enhanced when the stakes for the decision are higher, when the decision must be justified, and when the decision will be made public. Such circumstances often apply to judicial decisions. The presence of stronger arguments contrary to preferences reduces the influence of motivations. The limitations of the power of motivated reasoning are apparent from the numerous unanimous opinions of the United States Supreme Court (whose members generally represent a range of ideological predispositions) and other cases in which justices appear to vote contrary to their ideological preferences. One would anticipate that the influence of such motivated reasoning is at its apex when the law is relatively less determinate, which is consistent with the findings of empirical research.", "highlight": "the United States Supreme Court"}, "v239_p1": {"text": "Livestock-grazing programs in arid zones that are based on the equilibrium view of rangelands—that grazing-induced land degradation will occur if livestock numbers exceed the availability of food—have failed. Contrary to the equilibrium view, traditional pastoral systems of land use are more appropriate. Such systems involve a high degree of opportunism to cope with unpredictable rainfall and fluctuating food distribution. Livestock mobility relieves areas of concentration and allows herds to exploit unevenly distributed resources. A strategy of managing multiple livestock species allows optimal use of these variable grazing resources. These approaches to land use are similar to those recommended by nonequilibrium models, which assume that plant dynamics in arid zones are influenced more by rainfall than by grazing.", "highlight": null}, "v33_p1": {"text": "Scientific consensus is that humans first began to have a warming effect on Earth’s climate within the past century, after coal-burning factories, power plants, and motor vehicles began releasing carbon dioxide (CO2) and other greenhouse gases in significant quantities into the air. However, evidence suggests that human agricultural activities may have had such an effect much earlier: concentrations of CO2 started rising about 8000 years ago, even though natural trends indicate they should have been dropping; methane levels rose similarly about 3,000 years later. Without these rises, however, current temperatures in northern parts of North America and Europe would be cooler by three to four degrees Celsius—enough to inhibit agriculture—and an ice age would probably have begun several thousand years ago in northeastern Canada.", "highlight": "However, evidence suggests that human agricultural activities may have had such an effect much earlier: concentrations of CO2 started rising about 8000 years ago, even though natural trends indicate they should have been dropping; methane levels rose similarly about 3,000 years later."}, "v214_p1": {"text": "One difficulty in convincing early scientists that craters formed as a result of impacts from space is that most craters are circular. Impacts could come in at any angle, and experiments firing projectiles in the laboratory show that low-angle impacts lead to elliptical craters, not circular ones. Furthermore, while there was rarely evidence of any impacting object, there was often silicate melt around, suggesting that craters were caused by volcanic processes. The breakthrough in understanding crater origin was the recognition that the shock caused by the impacting object—not the object itself—creates a circular crater some twenty times larger than the diameter of the impactor. The impact also generates enough heat to largely vaporize the impactor and melt the native rock.", "highlight": null}, "v233_p2": {"text": "Scholars have advanced various reasons for the small number of biographies that have been written about African American subjects. Some have observed that biographical studies are not considered ambitious projects by academic institutions and thus are avoided by scholars who are seeking tenure and promotion. A more important reason, however, may be that autobiography has been the favored medium of expression in African American culture from its inception, while biography has been accorded lower status. The \"I\" of autobiography receives considerably more cultural respect than the \"she\" or \"he\" of biography. This preference can best be understood in light of the project of reclaiming personal identity. For example, autobiographical slave narratives were works through which African Americans articulated their individual identities in the face of oppression. Another reason for the paucity of biographies is that the existence of autobiographical narratives by African Americans can deter biographical writing about them.", "highlight": null}, "v28_p1": {"text": "Ecologists had assumed that trees in the consistently warm tropics grew at a slow but steady rate, unvarying from year to year. However, a study at La Selva, Costa Rica, showed that trees grew less in hotter years and more in cooler ones: between 1984 and 2000, dramatic differences occurred in the six species of trees studies, with trees adding twice as much wood in some cooler years as they did in the scorching El Nino year of 1997-1998. Because tree growth is an index of the balance between photosynthesis, in which trees absorb carbon dioxide (CO2) from the atmosphere and release oxygen, and respiration, in which the opposite occurs, the La Selva data were the first hint that rapidly rising global temperatures, driven by human-generated emissions of CO2, may be pushing tropical forests to release more CO2, thereby intensifying global warming. This raised serious questions about a popular theory that tropical forests act as a sponge, soaking up much of the excess CO2 that humans pump into the atmosphere. The La Selva data are consistent with a model of global CO2 flux developed by Keeling, who concluded that the amount of CO2 taken up in tropical landmasses rose in cooler years and fell in hotter ones, accounting for year-to-year changes in the amount of CO2 that stays in the atmosphere.", "highlight": null}, "v23_p2": {"text": "Many theorists now doubt that heat loss from Earth's core and radioactive decay are sufficient by themselves to produce all the energy driving the tectonic plates whose movements have helped shape Earth's surface. This leaves a loose end in current geological theory. Herbert Shaw argues that because scientists have underestimated the input of substantial amounts of energy from extraterrestrial impactors (asteroids and comets striking Earth), they have difficulty accounting for the difference between the quantity of energy produced from sources intrinsic to Earth and that involved in plate tectonics. Whereas most geologists have treated the addition of energy through the bombardment of Earth's surface by such impactors as a process separate and independent from the movement of Earth's tectonic plates, Shaw asserts that these processes are indivisible. Shaw's revolutionary \"open-system\" view recognizes a continuum between terrestrial and extraterrestrial dynamics, whereas modern plate tectonic theory, like the classical geology developed during the nineteenth century, is founded on the view that Earth's geological features have changed through gradual, regular processes intrinsic to Earth, without reference to unique catastrophic events. Classical geology borrowed a decisive, if unspoken, premise from Newton—the independence of Earth's processes from any astronomical context.", "highlight": null}, "v1_p2": {"text": "Given that ants and aphids are both abundant insect groups that often share the same habitats, that aphids excrete energy-rich honeydew, and that ants aggressively defend resources, it is difficult to understand why so few species of aphid have evolved a close relationship with ants. For example, only a quarter of the aphid species in the Rocky Mountain region are attended by ants, and in Central Europe, about one third are obligate myrmecophiles (animals that closely associate with ants). More than a dozen hypotheses have been proposed to account for the variability in aphid-ant relationships and the low proportion of attended species. First among them is the plant permissive hypothesis, which suggests that host-plant quality plays a critical role in determining the attractiveness of aphids for ants. Both variation in the quality of different hosts or different parts of the same host plant may affect the quality of honeydew, which is either more or less attractive to ants. However, this hypothesis ignores the fact that several species of aphids may feed on the same host plant or even plant organ but have very different degrees of associations with ants and assumes that the quality of phloem sap determines that of the honeydew. Recent studies have found that feeding on woody plant parts is positively associated with ant attendance, whereas mobility, feeding in isolation, and having winged adults are negatively associated with ant attendance.", "highlight": "Both variation in the quality of different hosts or different parts of the same host plant may affect the quality of honeydew, which is either more or less attractive to ants."}, "v198_p2": {"text": "A significant proportion of meteorites contain chondrules, small, glassy silicate spheres. The importance of chondrules is that they show that at some time the temperature was so high that the chondrule material was vaporized. The vapor then cooled quickly and the liquid silicates, condensing out of the vapor, formed small silicate spheres under the influence of surface tension. When these spheres solidified, they were incorporated into silicate fragments, and the material was eventually compressed into rock by gravitational forces.\n\nThe fact that the chondrules cooled very quickly is revealed by the composition of the minerals within them. In the vapor phase, whole minerals would not have existed, but there would have been components that, combined in various ways, can form different minerals. Combinations of these components produced an initial collection of minerals within chondrules when they formed. While the silicate was hot, the components changed partners to form more stable minerals─meaning ones of lower energy. Given enough time, the minerals in chondrules would have reached the lowest possible energy while using all available components. The mixture of minerals would then have been equilibrated. However, the mixtures of minerals in chondrules are nonequilibrated─corresponding to a total energy far greater than the minimum possible. This shows that the chondrules became solid and cooled so quickly that the nonequilibrate state became frozen in, since individual components did not have enough energy to jostle their way through the material to form more stable minerals.", "highlight": "In the vapor phase, whole minerals would not have existed, but there would have been components that, combined in various ways, can form different minerals."}, "v215_p1": {"text": "The participation of women in the economy of Britain’s North American colonies in the eighteenth century has been underrated because of the assumption that household production could not become commercial. Such an assumption ignores the reality that women produced goods at home for exchange and sale. Barter among neighbors knitted the women of a community into vital trade networks that constituted the underground economy of eighteenth-century colonial North America. Unlike other informal local trade networks in early America, the economy of women never totally ceased to exist. The informal nature of these transactions did not provide the women who engaged in them with much economic power, but it did allow them a small measure of control over how they spent their time.", "highlight": null}, "v4_p4": {"text": "Since the 1970s, there has been a movement in African literary studies toward the recognition of national literatures in newly independent African states, such as Cameroon, Senegal, and Benin. But while in some of these national literatures there has undoubtedly emerged a sense of corporate identity, often marked by clear thematic and formal progressions, it remains an incontrovertible fact that the European languages in which these literatures are expressed have only an official acceptance: they are neither indigenous to the cultures on which they have been imposed, nor are they national in any real sense of the word. This must limit the claims of any of these literatures to national significance, however abundant the corpus or coherent the internal configurations.", "highlight": "they are neither indigenous to the cultures on which they have been imposed, nor are they national in any real sense of the word."}, "v216_p4": {"text": "Conspicuous structural inconsistencies distinguish Xenophon’s 《Ephesiaka》 from other ancient Greek novels. Its narrative texture is uneven, the story's pace varies erratically, and, compared with other novels, it is inferior in composition. The quality of the 《Ephesiaka》 was first questioned by Burger, who maintained that much of the work is an epitome (i.e., a summary). This idea was used to account for the work's narrative shortcomings: the choppy pace, the lack of motivation for certain events, the abrupt introduction of characters. However, it is doubtful that 《Ephesiaka》 is an epitome because, as an epitome, it is a worse job than it is as a novel. Even in passages Burger thinks to be epitomized, inconsequential details such as Anthia feeding her dogs are retained, but potentially significant actions of gods are excised.", "highlight": null}, "v228_p2": {"text": "Despite the magnitude of his accomplishments and praise from certain later philosophers, philosopher and scientist Charles Peirce (1839-1914) remains largely ignored in modern philosophy. This neglect stems from the inherent difficulty of his theories, the chaotic state of his voluminous writings, and the dissonance of his doctrines, which range from an insistence on rigorous scientific methodology to a cosmological metaphysics of \"evolutionary love.”\n\nCertainly, much of Peirce's work is of mere historical interest, and many of his discoveries are partial anticipations of work done better by others. Still, he had a wider range of interests, a deeper knowledge of the history of philosophy, and a greater command of scientific culture than any philosopher of his day. Although Peirce never welded his views into a system and his writing is often slapdash, its tangled quality results directly from his immense erudition and his refusal to oversimplify. What he offers the patient reader is great breadth and complexity.", "highlight": null}, "v224_p13": {"text": "When rats are placed under conditions of stress, their adrenal glands immediately increase production of the hormone corticosterone, and soon thereafter the rats’ white blood cell count drops substantially. Yet rats without functioning adrenal glands experience little decrease in white blood cell count when placed under conditions of stress. It is likely, therefore, that an increase in corticosterone produced by a rat’s adrenal glands causes the rat’s white blood cell count to decrease.", "highlight": null}, "v217_p2": {"text": "Eighteenth-century women played a significant part in British political life. Up and down the social scale, they performed a variety of political acts, everything from purchasing political artifacts such as plates, handkerchiefs, and fans to penning political pamphlets, starving themselve in civic processions, sponsoring boycotts, arguing over public issues in their own debating societies, rioting, and uttering seditious words. Whereas historians used to see female political involvement in this century as isolated or aberrant, they now stress the continuity and normalcy of such activity, especially for aristocratic women. Given the familial nature of aristocratic politics, noble women were actually expected to act as political advisors and agents for their husbands, to canvass in elections, to serve as political hostesses, to seek and dispense political patronage. They did so routinely long before the eighteenth and deep into the nineteenth century. Patrician women had so much far-reaching political influence, it has been argued recently, that they actually stood to lose by expansion of the electorate to include women. Fruitful as this new historiography has been, however, it has also been criticized for its focus on the machinations of high politics and its inattention to ideology. Given the widespread hostility to “public” women in the eighteenth century, was female political activity quite so unproblematic as these new studies tend to assume? Anna Clark has pointed out that celebration of elite politicizing neglects both the condition of ordinary women and the nitpicking contemporary attacks on just this sort of upper-class influence peddling.", "highlight": "Anna Clark has pointed out that celebration of elite politicizing neglects both the condition of ordinary women and the nitpicking contemporary attacks on just this sort of upper-class influence peddling."}, "v35_p2": {"text": "Some archaeologists speculate that the Americas might have been initially colonized between 40,000 and 25,000 years ago. However, to support this theory it is necessary to explain the absence of generally accepted habitation sites for that time interval in what is now the United States. Australia, which has a smaller land area than the United States, has many such sites, supporting the generally accepted claim that the continent was colonized by humans at least 40,000 years ago. Australia is less densely populated (resulting in lower chances of discovering sites) and with its overall greater aridity would have presented conditions less favorable for hunter-gatherer occupation. Proportionally, at least as much land area has been lost from the coastal regions of Australia because of postglacial sea-level rise as in the United States, so any coastal archaeological record in Australia should have been depleted about as much as a coastal record in the United States. Since there are so many resource-rich rivers leading inland from the United States coastlines, it seems implausible that a growing population of humans would have confined itself to coasts for thousands of years. If inhabitants were present 25,000 years ago, the chances of their appearing in the archaeological record would seem to be greater than for Australia.", "highlight": null}, "v8_p2": {"text": "Manatees are large marine mammals that inhabit the coastal waters of southern Florida and feed on the vegetation that grows in shallow waters. They frequently gather in the vicinity of power stations that release heated water into the sea. Since the warmer water supports abundant vegetation, some biologists have hypothesized that manatees gather in these areas because they are attracted to this convenient source of food.", "highlight": null}, "v226_p1": {"text": "Findings in biological anthropology suggest that Native Americans' ancestors probably came to the Americas from northeastern Asia. Turner, for example, has studied the dentition of prehistoric and living Native Americans and northeastern Asians. Based on approximately twenty dental traits, including tooth-crown shape and number of roots, he has defined an overall dental pattern called Sinodonty, which includes three-rooted lower first molars and shovel-shaped incisors. This distinctive pattern is shared among most Native Americans and people from northeastern Asia, but is not found in people who originated in southern Asia, Africa, or Europe. Another less complex pattern—Sundadonty—is shared among the people of southeastern Asia and is also found in prehistoric American populations, but Turner believes that widespread Sinodonty demonstrates most Native Americans' northeastern Asian origins.", "highlight": null}, "v30_p2": {"text": "In the 1950’s sixty percent of treated cancer patients lived at least five years after detection of the disease. Now, sixty percent live at least seven years after detection. This fact demonstrates that, because of improved methods of treatment, cancer patients now live longer after they contract the disease than cancer patients did in the 1950’s.", "highlight": null}, "v24_p1": {"text": "Paintings of property—anything that was possessed—such as those created by eighteenth-century British painter George Stubbs were condemned by several of Stubbs's contemporaries: objects thus \"individualized\" would appeal to our appetite to own and enjoy them, whereas \"generalized\" objects in other paintings were no longer merely things but abstract ideas. To collect or commission paintings displaying lofty unconcern with materiality was considered by these commentators a mark of taste and civic virtue, the ability to subordinate private material interests to the abstract, public interest. Yet this notion of disinterested taste and virtue was founded on private interest: it was because the \"public\" man or woman already owned enough that he or she was presumed to be free from the urge to own more. Political power and status were thus based on the ownership of property, while at the same time they were legitimated by the claim that the avaricious behavior associated with the acquisition of property was somehow transcended by those who had already acquired it.", "highlight": "paintings displaying lofty unconcern with materiality"}, "v31_p2": {"text": "In the shallow end of Lake Tomwa, there are remains of numerous Jeffery pine trees that grew there during a lengthy drought. Researchers had believed that this drought lasted at least 150 years, but carbon dating reveals that pines were growing in the lake bed for only 120 years, from 1200 until 1320. Since the Jeffrey pines, which cannot survive in water, must have died at the end of the drought, the dating shows that the drought lasted less than 150 years.", "highlight": null}, "v18_p1": {"text": "Buell's study of village sketches (a type of fiction popular in the United States in the 1830s and 1840s) provides a valuable summary of sketches that portray the community as homogeneous and fixed, but it ignores those by women writers, which typically depicted the diversity that increasingly characterized actual village communities at that time. These women's geographical mobility was restricted (although women writers of the time were not uniformly circumscribed in this way), and their subject matter reflected this fact. Yet their texts were enriched by what Gilligan, writing in a different context, has called the ability to attend to voices other than one's own. To varying degrees, the women's sketches portray differences among community members: all stress differences among men and among women (particularly the latter) as well as differences between the sexes, and some also depict cultural diversity. These writers represent community as dynamic, as something that must be negotiated and renegotiated because of its members' divergent histories, positions, expectations, and beliefs.", "highlight": null}, "v19_p2": {"text": "Much recent work has examined the claim that women encounter increasing obstacles relative to men as they move up the organizational ladder in business. This proposition, which we term the increasing-disadvantage model, is a core element of the popular glass ceiling metaphor. Despite continued widespread public acceptance of the glass ceiling idea and some consistent findings, most research to date has failed to support the increasing disadvantage model. Indeed, several studies based on private-sector firms find that women's mobility prospects improve, rather than decline, as they climb upward in corporate hierarchies. In the public sector, researchers have found either no sex differences in mobility or a larger female disadvantage in lower grades.\n\nComparing cross-sectional national samples of workers, Baxter and Wright found no evidence in the United States, and only limited evidence in Sweden and Australia, that women's probability of being located in a higher versus a lower hierarchical level declined relative to men's at higher levels. Taken together, these findings suggest that the glass ceiling may be a myth. Women's scarcity in top organizational ranks may simply represent the cumulative effect of a constant—or even decreasing-disadvantage at successive hierarchical levels.", "highlight": null}, "v199_p1": {"text": "The finding that there were rock-melting temperatures on asteroids for sustained periods is puzzling: asteroids’ heat source is unknown, and unlike planet-sized bodies, such small bodies quickly dissipate heat. Rubin suggests that asteroids’ heat could have derived from collisions between asteroids. Skeptics have argued that a single impact would raise an asteroid’s overall temperature very little and that asteroids would cool too quickly between impacts to accumulate much heat. However, these objections assumed that asteroids are dense, solid bodies. A recent discovery that asteroids are highly porous makes Rubin’s hypothesis more plausible. When solid bodies collide, much debris is ejected, dissipating energy. Impacts on porous bodies generate less debris, so more energy goes into producing heat. Heat could be retained as debris fall back into impact craters, creating an insulating blanket.", "highlight": null}, "v26_p4": {"text": "Simulations indicate, and observations confirm, that the particles constituting Saturn's rings are giving up angular momentum to moons of the planet. The simulations predict that over just a few hundred million years, the related energy transfer will cause the rings' collapse. An analogous process occurs around young stars in the disks of matter from which planets emerge, and these protoplanetary disks do vanish that quickly, computer models show. Yet if Saturn's rings are so short-lived, a large comet or moon—the rings' presumed source—must have broken apart in Saturn's vicinity within the past several hundred million years. That is quite unlikely. It would have been much more probable in the young solar system—4 billion years ago or more.", "highlight": "protoplanetary disks"}, "v15_p2": {"text": "In \"The Franklin's Tale,\" from Chaucer's fourteenth-century 《The Canterbury Tales》, a clerk uses medieval astronomical tables, calculating lunar and solar positions, to predict an extraordinarily high flood tide. Literary scholar Phyllis Hodgson has concluded that Chaucer's purpose here is artistic, not scientific, and that even though Chaucer was a master of astronomy and author of an astrolabe treatise, this \"highly technical account of the clerk's astrological calculations need not be taken too seriously.\" Recently, however, astronomer Don Olson concluded that Chaucer's account actually describes a very rare astronomical configuration of the Sun, Moon, and Earth that produced an exceptionally high tide in December 1340. But why would Chaucer be aware of a high tide that occurred in 1340, some five decades before \"The Franklin's Tale\" was written. Some scholars place Chaucer's birth in late 1340 or early 1341. When Chaucer was studying astronomy during the 1380s and 1390s, it is plausible that he investigated his own horoscope. Chaucer may have discovered the remarkable tide-raising configuration in 1340 while calculating celestial positions at the time of his own birth and then used this knowledge as inspiration for the plot device in \"The Franklin's Tale.\"", "highlight": null}, "v223_p10": {"text": "Mercury, the planet closest to the Sun, is not much bigger than Earth's moon, yet its density is typical of that of a far larger planet. Since the density of terrestrial (nongaseous) planets increases with depth, they have high-density cores, probably composed largely of iron. Mercury's high density suggests that it may have the largest metallic core relative to its size of all the terrestrial planets. Astronomers believe that all the planets condensed from the solar nebula at about the same time, so why would Mercury have such an anomalous density? The composition of the solar nebula might have been dramatically different in the vicinity of Mercury's orbit─much more so than theoretical models would predict. Or the Sun may have been so energetic early in the life of the solar system that the more volatile, low-density elements on Mercury were vaporized and driven off by the Sun's heat. It is also possible that a massive object collided with Mercury soon after its formation, vaporizing the less dense material.", "highlight": "Astronomers believe that all the planets condensed from the solar nebula at about the same time, so why would Mercury have such an anomalous density?"}, "v220_p7": {"text": "Researchers suspect that meteorites (particles of matter that fall to Earth's surface from space) are pieces of asteroids, the many minor planets primarily inhabiting the region between Mars and Jupiter called the asteroid belt. The most common meteorites are ordinary chondrites-rocks containing tiny flecks of metal. By analyzing the spectrums of sunlight reflected by asteroids to determine the asteroids' chemical composition, researchers have found that most of the brighter asteroids contain the same silicates and other compounds that dominate chondrites. These silicaceous, or S-type, asteroids are the most abundant type in the inner asteroid belt, the part of the asteroid belt from which objects are most likely to escape and travel to Earth. However, S-type asteroids reflect red and infrared light much better than they reflect green, blue, and violet light, suggesting that they have a higher metal content than do ordinary chondrites. This has led at least one researcher to posit that meteorites come from other types of asteroids that are too small and too dim to be detected. However, S-type asteroids could be ordinary chondrites that have been weathered by the effects of the space environment, making them seem redder and more metallic than they really are.", "highlight": null}, "v220_p14": {"text": "American and British critics who wrote enthusiastic reviews of west African writer Amos Tutuola's 1952 book 《The Palm-Wine Drinkard》 typically dwelt less on his rhetorical skills and more on the text as an exemplar of naïve art. While these metropolitan critics were enchanted by the book, the initial literary reception in west Africa was by contrast highly critical. Concerned to avoid stereotyping, critics there objected to what they saw as very poor writing and expressed dismay at the uncritical promotion of the book. Many protested against what they saw as a metropolitan celebration of exoticism. For example, Adeagbo Akinjogbin attributed the novel's success in the West to ignorance and a desire to believe \"all sorts of fantastic tales about Africa.\"", "highlight": null}, "v227_p1": {"text": "Invasions of nonnative species are clearly reducing species diversity on a global scale. On the regional scale, these invasions cause a change in species composition, but the impact of these invasions on diversity is less certain. Changes in diversity within a region depend on the number of extinctions of native species. In some cases, broad losses of native diversity have followed the establishment of nonnative species; for example, the introduction of the brown tree snake led to the extinction of several bird species on Guam. In other cases, many nonnative species have had no detectable effects on native flora and fauna. Consequently, in regions where many nonnative species have become established without coincident extinctions, diversity has increased.", "highlight": "Changes in diversity within a region depend on the number of extinctions of native species."}, "v228_p1": {"text": "Among the scientific anachronisms in the United States Endangered Species Act is the absence of specific reference to interactions among species, which can greatly affect ecological and species diversity. It is now understood that the disappearance of a strongly interactive species can cause profound changes in ecosystem composition and structure. For instance, decimation of great whales by industrial whaling affected other species that, like the whales, consume krill (small, shrimplike crustaceans), and the dynamics of coastal marine ecosystems worldwide have been greatly altered by overfishing of certain species. Decreased numbers and reduced geographic range may render a species functionally extinct in terms of its interactions well before the species itself has completely disappeared. Nevertheless, most conservation laws emphasize short-term, single-species demographic viability in only a few circumscribed areas.", "highlight": null}, "v14_p3": {"text": "Astronomers can measure any given star's radial velocity by examining its spectrum—light spread out into its constituent wavelengths. If an object is moving toward us, its spectral lines shift to shorter wavelengths; if it's moving away, the lines swing to longer wavelengths. The higher the velocity, the greater the shift. Although this sort of spectral analysis is straightforward for nearby stars, it becomes far more difficult for distant stars in the Milky Way's outer halo. Even large telescopes can't gather enough of their light. For this reason, astronomer Ulrich Heber conjectures that there are probably several low-mass hypervelocity stars yet to be discovered. Although these diminutive objects live longer than B-type stars, which are extremely luminous and blue, they radiate much less light.", "highlight": "Even large telescopes can't gather enough of their light."}, "v202_p1": {"text": "One reason researchers have long believed that Mars never enjoyed an extensive period of warm and wet climate is that much of the surface not covered by wind-borne dust appears to be composed of unweathered material. If water flowed for an extended period, researchers reasoned, it should have altered and weathered the volcanic minerals, creating clays or other oxidized, hydrated phases (minerals that incorporate water molecules in their crystal structure).\n\nIt turns out, though, that the scientists were not looking closely enough. New high resolution mapping data and close-up surface studies have revealed clays and other hydrated minerals in many regions. The clay deposits are scattered all over, in ancient volcanic surfaces and heavily cratered highland regions, some of which have apparently been exposed by erosion only recently.", "highlight": "If water flowed for an extended period, researchers reasoned, it should have altered and weathered the volcanic minerals, creating clays or other oxidized, hydrated phases (minerals that incorporate water molecules in their crystal structure)."}, "v236_p2": {"text": "Where grazing reduces species diversity, a rangeland can be considered overgrazed. Conversely, where species diversity is increased by grazing, that grazing can be considered well managed. Although popular consensus characterizes the intensive grazing of rangelands surrounding the Mediterranean Basin as overgrazing, such intensive grazing is not necessarily destructive.\n\nCrawley argues that the primary way in which herbivores affect plant species diversity is not by eating plants to extinction but by selective feeding, which modifies competition among plant species. For example, some species can survive because competition from more aggressive species that have been grazed is reduced. This mechanism is one of several that underlie the intermediate-disturbance hypothesis, which holds that biodiversity is higher with moderate disturbance of the ecosystem than with low or heavy disturbance. The impact of grazing in Mediterranean ecosystems can be considered in terms of this hypothesis. However, the grazing intensity that is necessary to cause intermediate disturbance in the grazing-resistant Mediterranean shrublands is generally quite high, and low-intensity to moderate-intensity grazing is often ineffective in preventing the encroachment and dominance of woody vegetation. In a study comparing two Greek islands, one \"heavily overgrazed\" by the Cretan wild goat and the other undergrazed, Papageorgiou found that there were many more species on the \"overgrazed\" island.", "highlight": null}, "v2_p3": {"text": "New Zealand's lesser short-tailed bat, Mystacina tuberculata, is one of only two bat species to use a true walking gait when maneuvering on the ground. It has been assumed that the specialized terrestrial habits of mystacinids evolved in New Zealand following their isolation there. Absence of native terrestrial mammalian predators in New Zealand has been hypothesized to have facilitated evolution of terrestriality. However, although it is likely that terrestrial foraging by extant Mystacina tuberculata makes it vulnerable to introduced mammalian predators, there is as yet limited available data on the actual risk of terrestriality. Indeed, Lloyd argues that although some individuals may be caught on the ground, generally they would not be easy prey: they are cryptic, fast-moving, with acute hearing and olfaction, and can quickly take flight.", "highlight": null}, "v2_p4": {"text": "More appropriate water pricing would promote the treatment and reuse of urban wastewater for agricultural irrigation and also encourage improvements in irrigation efficiency. Treatment and reuse is more expensive than most irrigation-related conservation and efficiency measures but often less expensive than developing new water sources. Wastewater contains nitrogen and phosphorus, which can be pollutants when released to lakes and rivers but are nutrients when applied to farmland. Moreover, unlike many other water sources, treated wastewater will be both an expanding and fairly reliable supply, since urban water use will likely double by 2025. Many large cities located along coastlines currently dump their wastewater, treated or untreated, into the ocean, rendering it unavailable for any other purpose and harming coastal marine life.", "highlight": null}, "v225_p10": {"text": "In 《The Life of Charlotte Bronte》 (1857), the first and the most celebrated biography of novelist Charlotte Bronte, Elizabeth Gaskell promoted the long-persisting romantic view of Bronte as having no connection with the rest of English society at a time when industrialization was causing much turbulence, but as having sprung naturally, like so much purple heather, out of the English countryside. Gaskell also portrayed Bronte as irreproachably proper, incapable of \"unladylike\" feelings or dangerous views; this was at variance with the subversive spirit Matthew Arnold accurately discerned, albeit with distance, deep within Bronte’s fiction. While correcting many of Gaskell’s errors and omissions at last, even Winifred Gerin’s 《Charlotte Bronte: The Evolution of Genius》 (1967) failed to discard Gaskell’s viewpoint. Feminists have introduced new interpretations of Bronte’s life, but it is primarily Juliet Barker who takes into account the larger world that impinged on that life─the changing England in which old divisions of class and gender were under pressure.", "highlight": null}, "v5_p1": {"text": "Historical demographers have generally agreed on two interrelated features of the urban populations in early-modern Germany. First in accordance with the law of natural decrease, extremely high mortality rates in cities (urban areas with more than 10,000 inhabitants) meant that their populations could not be sustained by reproduction alone. Population density, inadequate sanitary conditions, and poor housing made cities too vulnerable to disease and death. Second, when city populations did increase, it was as a result of in-migration sufficient to overcome the population losses caused by the high mortality. But because the parish registers of urban communities with fewer than 10,000 inhabitants show that the annual number of births usually equaled or exceeded that of deaths, historical demographers assume that the law of natural decrease did not apply to small towns.", "highlight": null}, "v231_p2": {"text": "In the book《China Men》 (1980), Maxine Hong Kingston tells of Chinese Americans establishing identities in the United States. She acknowledges the importance of ethnicity (the national origins of one's ancestors or one's self), yet also the importance of geographical location aside from one's \"homeland\" and interactions with other cultures in identity formation. These latter ideas suggest similarity between Kingston and \"border identity\" theorists. These theorists challenge the arbitrariness of ethnic identities based on national boundaries, claiming that individual identity is influenced by the various cultures with which one interacts, especially in a mobile global society. Moreover, such theorists argue that identity requires redefinition either in terms of multiple nationalities or in terms of geographic units different from nations, such as cities.\n\nYet, redefining what it means to be an \"American\" without abandoning the term itself, Kingston distances herself from some border theorists. While recognizing multiple identities, she also counters border theorists' emphasis on mobility and disconnection from specific countries by emphasizing the importance of a sense of belonging for people occupying a land with others. Even so, to belong to America in Kingston's world is not to have a set identity, but rather to have the opportunity to reconstruct identity through group interactions.", "highlight": null}, "v20_p3": {"text": "Edith Wharton's reputation may be secure, but it is the wrong kind of reputation: she is celebrated as a novelist concerned with elegant surfaces and manners. Critics have misunderstood the nature of her contribution to modern fiction largely because they misperceive her subject matter as genteel and effete. Even sympathetic critics fail to acknowledge the extent to which Wharton challenged contemporary mores. Between her early novel, 《The House of Mirth》 (1905) and her last, 《The Buccaneers》 (1938), Wharton addressed subjects that many might think of as decidedly un-Whartonesque, including marital strife and rural and urban poverty. Yet she remains firmly enshrined as a scion of rarefied, upper-class America, an image reinforced by Martin Scorsese's sumptuous 1993 film adaptation of 《The Age of Innocence》.", "highlight": "Even sympathetic critics fail to acknowledge the extent to which Wharton challenged contemporary mores."}, "v31_p1": {"text": "Setting conservation objectives often mixes scientific knowledge with political feasibility in such a way that one cannot tell where the science stops and the political pragmatism takes over. For example, Tear found that for endangered species with recovery plans, over a quarter of the plans set quantitative recovery objectives at or below the species’ existing population size or number of populations. Most likely these objectives were so low because they were politically palatable. Another possible explanation for such modest recovery objectives is what is known as the shifting-baseline syndrome. In this scenario, successive generations of wildlife managers use as their baseline the conditions they experienced at the start of their careers, resulting in lower expectations with each new generation.", "highlight": "shifting-baseline syndrome"}, "v34_p2": {"text": "Because of strong overall stylistic similarities, prehistoric cave paintings in El Castillo, Spain and others in Altamira, Spain, were thought to date from the same period. Recent pigment analyses, however, established the Altamira paintings as by far the older and as about the same age as a third group of paintings done in a different overall style. Nevertheless, this case does not prove that stylistic similarities cannot be a reliable indicator of closeness in age, since _____.", "highlight": null}, "v24_p3": {"text": "Saturn's E ring consists of particles so small that they would be dispersed by solar radiation pressure in a few tens of thousands of years. That the ring exists today suggests, therefore, that it originated in the relatively recent past—but how? Researchers suggest that Enceladus, one of Saturn's moons, may be responsible. This icy moon has no craters, possibly because liquid water from its interior flowed across the surface in the relatively recent past, erasing all preexisting impact features. An impact into Enceladus within the past thousand years or so may have blasted liquid water into space. Water droplets would have frozen quickly into ice crystals, which may then have drifted through the Saturnian system and formed into the E ring.", "highlight": null}, "v19_p1": {"text": "When studying shrimp feeding from hydrothermal vents at the bottom of the ocean, biologists were surprised that the shrimps' reproductive cycles followed seasonal patterns. Far beyond the reach of sunlight, and with food abundant around the vents all year round, why should such animals reproduce seasonally? The answer might involve their offspring, which in their larval form drift in the currents to colonize new vents. The larvae must feed during their trip, and their springtime release coincides with a peak in algae raining down from surface waters. So far, researchers have found no evidence of seasonal breeding among vent-dwelling species that provide their offspring with yolk to sustain them or among vent-dwelling species found in areas of the ocean with no seasonal algae blooms.", "highlight": "So far, researchers have found no evidence of seasonal breeding among vent-dwelling species that provide their offspring with yolk to sustain them or among vent-dwelling species found in areas of the ocean with no seasonal algae blooms."}, "v212_p4": {"text": "Harrison has argued that nineteenth-century French government administrators generally ignored the activities of women's associations, and most historians agree that female groups appear to have garnered little notice from authorities. While Grange suggests that this may be because so few female associations existed throughout much of the nineteenth century, Duprat has uncovered numerous female societies, especially sociétés de bienfaisance (charitable societies), many of which received more generous treatment from municipal and national officials than their male counterparts. However, she suggests that their official “silence”—the absence of general assemblies and of frequent publications, as well as their careful cultivation of the traditional, nonthreatening image of dames de charité (charitable women)—kept these associations largely out of public view.", "highlight": null}, "v27_p1": {"text": "Biologists have long debated about whether egg production in birds is biologically highly costly, some theorizing that egg production is energetically or nutritionally demanding. Lack, however, suggested that clutch size—the number of eggs a bird lays per breeding cycle—is far below the potential limit of egg production. He suggested that clutch size had instead evolved in relation to the number of young that the parents could successfully rear. Subsequently, most studies focused on limitations operating during chick rearing, particularly among altricial species (species in which the parents feed their young in the nest). Lack later recognized that in precocial species (species in which young feed themselves), clutch size might be explained by different factors—the availability of food for egg-laying females, for example.", "highlight": null}, "v221_p4": {"text": "Most seismologists assume that following a major earthquake and its aftershocks, the fault (a break in Earth’s crust where pressure can trigger an earthquake) will remain quiet until stresses have time to rebuild, typically over hundreds or thousands of years. Recent evidence of subtle interactions between earthquakes may overturn this assumption, however. According to the stress-triggering hypothesis, faults are unexpectedly responsive to subtle stresses they acquire as neighboring faults shift. Rather than simply dissipating, stress relieved during an earthquake travels along the fault, concentrating in sites nearby; even the smallest additional stresses may then trigger another quake along the fault or on a nearby fault. Although scientists have long viewed such subtle interactions as nonexistent, the hypothesis has explained the location and frequency of earthquakes following several destructive quakes in California, Japan, and Turkey.", "highlight": null}, "v215_p2": {"text": "In the early twentieth century, Clements proposed an ecological theory that, while challenged by scientists from its inception, has continued to influence popular conceptions of nature. Clements argued that plants form communities of interdependent species and that these communities function as \"superorganisms\" that develop over time in a predictable succession of stages to a ”climax\" formation. Thus, forests, for example, if undisturbed by humans, will evolve toward a stable community of old-growth trees. However, many botanists immediately pointed out that these supposed superorganisms have no clear edges: while pine forests and hardwood forests might appear to constitute two distinct superorganisms, one of them can blend imperceptibly into the other. Gleason pointed out in 1927 that what Clements called succession often proceeds in both directions simultaneously: prairie gives way to pine woods in one spot while pines give way to prairie in another. Gleason also emphasized the role that chance disturbance, such as fire or variations in rainfall, plays in determining the shape of the landscape.", "highlight": null}, "v20_p4": {"text": "The discovery of subsurface life on Earth, surviving independently from surface life, refuted the belief that biological processes require not only liquid water but sunlight as well, thus greatly enhancing the possibility of life beyond Earth. Take Jupiter's moon Europa. Space probes show a body covered with a thick layer of ice. As Europa orbits its planet, however, it flexes due to the gravitational tug-of-war between it, its sister moons, and Jupiter. Through friction, this flexing produces heat in the moon's interior capable of melting ice. Indeed, observations suggest liquid water exists beneath Europa's icy crust. Photosynthetic life is impossible there because sunlight is completely absent, but life such as the microbes that flourish deep within earth may still be possible.", "highlight": "Take Jupiter's moon Europa."}, "v16_p4": {"text": "Some economists suggest that all firms would be expected to pay workers doing identical jobs the same wage. However, studies show that high-profit industries tend to pay more. While some of this observed wage gap could be due to difficulties in measuring workers' talent, it is unlikely that such measurement problems can explain everything. Although talent is hard to measure, factors with which it is presumably correlated, such as education and tenure, are not. Yet studies that control for those factors still find big wage disparities. Moreover, although receptionists, for example, do not become less talented when they leave a high-profit industry to work in an industry with lower profits, their pay tends to drop in line with the wage gap between the two.", "highlight": "Moreover, although receptionists, for example, do not become less talented when they leave a high-profit industry to work in an industry with lower profits, their pay tends to drop in line with the wage gap between the two."}, "v214_p4": {"text": "It is often said that art forgery has existed as long as has the demand for artwork, but this is not strictly true. There is no clear evidence that art forgeries as such existed in antiquity. There were many collectors, but they seem to have found copies as desirable as originals. Even the presence of a signature was not necessarily taken as an indication that the object in question was made by that artist. The notion of art forgery, as we understand it today, seems to require the idea that originals possess certain qualities not found even in the best copies. It also requires the presence of an expert who can distinguish between the two; but such expertise seems not to have existed in antiquity.", "highlight": null}, "v12_p2": {"text": "The ship Mary Rose, first launched in 1511, underwent extensive repairs in 1528 and 1536 and sank in 1543. Researchers raised the ship in 1982 and analyzed the wreck's preserved timbers; some timbers came from trees felled after 1511, so they must have been added during repair. There were some beams, however, that came from trees felled before 1511. It is likely, therefore, that these beams were part of the original ship.", "highlight": null}, "v239_p2": {"text": "Nineteenth-century historian Jacob Burckhardt's remarkable assertion that \"women stood on a footing of perfect equality with men\" in sixteenth-century Italy resulted from his close identification with the early humanists, a small, elite group in Renaissance Italy. Ironically, as Margaret King has shown, humanist texts actually reflect inequalities between men and women. One example is the programs of study recommended for girls. A pedagogic imperative like Leonardo Bruni's—that women should study the liberal arts as men did, with the exception of rhetoric, which \"lies wholly outside the province of women\"—went unnoticed by Burckhardt because he shared the humanist assumption that women's province was the private sphere rather than the public sphere. The relegation of women to a \"private\" sphere was a complex historical phenomenon that should be analyzed in light of other social and economic changes occurring during the Renaissance. Historians desirous of understanding women's experience cannot view the period, as Burckhardt did, through the lens provided by the humanists.", "highlight": null}, "v12_p4": {"text": "While captive orangutans learn to use tools, wild orangutans have not been observed doing so until recently when researchers witnessed orangutans near Suaq Balimbing in Sumatra using tools to extract insects from tree holes and seeds from the Neesia fruit. What explains this population's tool use? It is doubtful that the Suaq orangutans are intrinsically smarter: captive orangutans have demonstrated that the species has the brain capacity to use tools. Another explanation is environmental. While previously studied orangutans mostly inhabited dry forests, the Suaq orangutans inhabit a lush swamp where insects flourish in tree holes and Neesia fruit is abundant. However, orangutans in other habitats where Neesia grows do harvest the seeds, but without tools they obtain fewer than do the Suaq orangutans.", "highlight": null}, "v200_p4": {"text": "In the United States, studying the territoriality of nonnative ants such as the red fire ant, a species native to South America, may seemingly unlikely to yield generalizable results─but it does have distinct advantages. Most importantly, whereas the fire ant shares habitat with many ant competitors in South America, its communities in the United States are much simpler. Colonizable landscape is blanketed almost continuously with fire ant territories, so all territorial boundaries are with other fire ant colonies. We can study the complexities of territoriality in almost pure, continuous populations of a single species, without the complicating influences of other competitors. Furthermore, the high densities of many fire ant populations ensure that interactions among competing colonies will be intense and obvious.", "highlight": "Colonizable landscape is blanketed almost continuously with fire ant territories, so all territorial boundaries are with other fire ant colonies."}, "v210_p2": {"text": "As they unearth long-ignored women's writings, some feminist literary scholars have a tendency to evaluate those writings according to current ideological standards. This tendency, however understandable, has certain pitfalls, as feminist response to three late-seventeenth- and early-eighteenth-century English female playwrights demonstrates. Mary Pix, Catharine Trotter, and Delarivier Manley each wrote at least four plays and were known collectively as the “Female Wits.” These women saw themselves as participating in a common endeavor, but feminist scholars have evaluated their works in very different terms. Trotter and Manley have been praised for their depiction of “feminist” themes─Trotter because of her insistence on feminine virtue, and Manley because of her depiction of strong, if sometimes villainous, heroines─while Pix's works, because they depict women in ways now considered stereotypically “feminine,” are often dismissed.\n\nYet Pix is conservative only within a present-day context: within the context of late-seventeenth- and early-eighteenth-century English drama, Pix's plays were more formally innovative than Manley's and more successful than either Manley's or Trotter's. She also broke new ground regarding subject matter, addressing contemporary social issues such as class upheaval. However, these acts are rarely acknowledged by scholars of the Female Wits.", "highlight": null}, "v202_p2": {"text": "Stylistic analysis of ancient works of visual art can help in determining their time and place of origin. It is therefore important to identify the elements that constitute style and their relative value for establishing relationships among artworks. Most helpful in this regard is Schapiro’s breakdown of style into the three properties of art: form elements, form relationships, and qualities (including overall expression). Particularly helpful is his distinction between the first two categories. Citing the wide distribution over time of pointed and rounded arches in architecture, for example, Schapiro points out that form elements alone are insufficient for characterizing a style: one must also look at the different ways that the elements are combined─the compositional pattern or syntax. He compares style directly to language as having a similar internal order and expressiveness; this order (or grammar) can distinguish one stylistic group from another. The way visual motifs are articulated and combined is crucial when dealing with themes that are shared by a number of different cultures contemporary with one another. As Winter has noted, subject matter or iconography then becomes much less important than style in determining the place of origin of a particular artwork.", "highlight": null}, "v16_p1": {"text": "The seemingly unrelated aims of functional strength and aesthetic appeal had been not only successfully integrated in many of the classic suspension bridges of the past two centuries but also commonly achieved by engineers alone or leading teams. Thomas Telford was in fact both engineer and architect of his Menai Suspension Bridge, and John Roebling was both engineer and architect of his Brooklyn Bridge. That these engineering structures especially have come to be regarded as architectural icons demonstrates the aesthetic heights that an engineer can achieve.\n\nEngineers less artistically confident than Telford and Roebling have engaged consulting architects to advise them on the design of everything from the facades placed on massive anchorages and skyscraper-high towers to the finishing details like deck railings and lampposts. Othmar Ammann, the chief engineer of the George Washington and many other New York City bridges, often sought the help of famous architects. When the George Washington was but an idea on paper, Ammann engaged Cass Gilbert, the architect of the Woolworth Building and other landmarks, to depict how the towers might be finished in stone. Since money was tight when the bridge was being completed, however, the steel-framed towers were left bare—a look that the Swiss architect Le Corbusier found extremely appealing—and bare steel became the new aesthetic standard for monumental bridge towers.", "highlight": null}, "v221_p10": {"text": "Some historians have recently challenged the “party period paradigm,” the view, advanced by McCormick and others, that political parties—especially the two major parties—in the United States between the years 1835 and 1900 evoked extraordinary loyalty from voters and dominated political life. Voss-Hubbard cites the frequency of third-party eruptions during the period as evidence of popular antipathy to the two-party regime. He correctly credits third parties with helping generate the nineteenth-century’s historically high rates of voter turnout by forcing major parties to bolster supporters’ allegiance, lest minor parties siphon off their votes, and with pushing policy demands that the major parties ignored. Formisano stresses the pervasive record of nonpartisan and antiparty governance at the local level, and women’s frequent participation in nineteenth-century public life, prior to their enfranchisement, in nonpartisan and antiparty ways as evidence of the limitations of the party period paradigm. Yet McCormick would deny that the existence of antiparty sentiment during the period undermines the paradigm, since he has always acknowledged the residual strength of such sentiment during the nineteenth century. In any case, the strength of the paradigm is its comparative thrust: the contrast it draws between the period in question and later political eras.", "highlight": null}, "v238_p2": {"text": "What accounts for the low-lying, flat surface of Mars's north? On Earth's surface, higher- and lower-lying areas have different types of crust: one, thin and dense, is pulled toward Earth's center more strongly by gravity, and the planet's water naturally comes to sit over it, creating oceans. The processes that generate this oceanic crust drive plate tectonics. Is Mars's north similarly characterized by a sort of crust different from other areas of the planet? Some researchers do see signs of tectonic activity surrounding the northern basin that suggest that it was created through the formation of new crust, like ocean basins on Earth.\n\nHowever, McGill points to northern bedrock structures that predate the features said to mark the start of the tectonic process. McGill instead believes that through some novel mechanism the ancient surface sank to its current depth as a single unit. This would explain why features around the basin's edge, which would have formed as the surface dropped, seem to be younger than structures at its floor.\n\nThe third possibility is that the northern lowlands result from impacts. Some researchers suggest they formed as a series of big overlapping impact craters. Others, arguing that the odds against such a pattern of impacts are large, postulate a single event─the impact of an object bigger than any asteroid the solar system now contains.", "highlight": null}, "v216_p2": {"text": "Huron Indian culture in the seventeenth century valued conformity and strongly discouraged idiosyncratic behavior. Since few wished to endure dishonor or reproach, public criticism was often used effectively as a strong pressure for conformity. However, it is a fallacy to equate intolerance of idiosyncratic behavior with lack of respect for individual dignity. While most individuals attempted to live up to society's ideals, they remained highly sensitive to the preservation of individual honor, and personal independence remained highly important. Overt attempts to coerce anyone were strongly opposed. And if such coercion came from outside a person's clan, it was considered an affront to the clan, as well as to the individual. The individual's right to be free from overt constraint was also reinforced by Huron custom and by the vigor with which each clan guarded its independence and privileges. Custom did not permit society as a whole to punish offenders. Responsibility for an individual's actions was assumed by the individual's own clan.", "highlight": null}, "v217_p1": {"text": "Ecologists tend to focus on pristine environments and ignore urban areas. Human beings, and especially their cities, fail to fit neatly into ecological theory—they are seen as an exogenous, perturbing force in nature. Yet people are a global force capable of affecting every ecosystem on the planet. In cities, people mobilize some nutrients and deplete others, create habitats that never before existed, increase temperatures, and, by intent or by accident, manipulate the communities of other species found within city boundaries and beyond. If there is a laboratory where ecological change can be viewed at close hand, it is the city. The processes and dynamics within cities, however, largely elude understanding based on traditional ecological theories.", "highlight": null}, "v240_p4": {"text": "Much of ecological theory consists of models that are so highly idealized that they are of little real-world predictive value. In addition, many of the parameters used in models such as birth and death rates are exceedingly difficult to estimate accurately in the field. Consequently, ecological theory is rarely directly relevant to the practice of conservation biology. One notable exception is MacArthur's theory of island biogeography, which predicts the species richness of an island on the basis of its size and degree of isolation. This theory could provide important insights into nature preserves, which can be analogous to islands, often consisting of relatively undisturbed ecosystems surrounded by biologically distinct areas.", "highlight": "Consequently, ecological theory is rarely directly relevant to the practice of conservation biology."}, "v14_p4": {"text": "Typical of Argentine melodrama of the 1930s were the films starring Libertad Lamarque, the genre's biggest box-office attraction. Her most frequent role was that of the tango singer whose romance with a wealthy suitor is blocked by his elitist family. Despite its widespread social acceptance by the 1930s, tango continued to be associated in film melodramas with criminality and vice. As Diana Paladino remarks, in these films, \"the tango songstress was doomed from the start.\" Nevertheless, if melodramatic logic dictated that Lamarque be punished for the transgressive act of singing tango, surely that judgment was not shared by the members of the audience, many of whom were drawn to her early movies precisely because of her fame as a tango singer.", "highlight": null}, "v16_p2": {"text": "The infectious disease known as whooping cough is commonly thought to be a childhood illness, but a recent study suggests that more adults contract this illness than was previously suspected. Although the disease is life-threatening in children, in adults it typically causes only a persistent cough which, though annoying, is rarely serious. Therefore, the incidence of whooping cough in adults poses no significant public health threat.", "highlight": null}, "v25_p3": {"text": "Historically, more cold-adapted antelope species originating in Eurasia have migrated into Africa, where the climate is generally warmer, than have warm-adapted African species into Eurasia. A likely explanation for this involves the fact that intercontinental migrations require both a land bridge connecting the two continents and the suitable habitat both on and across that land bridge. During periods of climatic cooling, such as the various ice ages, the land bridge is open for a long time (because sea level remains low) and is usable by cold-adapted species because cool habitats then extend across it. Thus, during cooling most migrants would be expected to travel toward Africa, which is near the equator, since this is the direction dictated by habitat changes on a cooling Earth. In contrast, when the Earth is warm, the land bridge is reduced or gone because sea level is relatively high then. Only during the short lag between onset of global temperature change and sea level response can warm-adapted species migrate from the equator toward higher latitudes.", "highlight": "short lag"}, "v200_p1": {"text": "In late imperial China (circa 1650-1850), excessive exploitation came not from the sovereign but from his agents, who had shorter-term goals and narrower interests than their ruler did. While the emperor’s interest in preempting rebellion militated against overtaxation, his agents had incentives to exploit the taxpayers for their own benefit. Due to weak oversight, the emperor had to keep the taxes low and his bureaucracy small to mitigate this “tyranny at the bottom” effect. This fiscal weakness of the Chinese state had long been masked by its huge tax base; however, the economic expansion of the eighteenth century exacerbated the problems of administrative control, further squeezing the nation’s finances and leaving China ill prepared for the challenges of the nineteenth century.", "highlight": null}, "v6_p4": {"text": "Despite today's more efficient electrical generators, modern electric-only power plants waste more of their fuel sources' potential energy than did Thomas Edison's power plants of the late 1800s. Edison used cast-off steam from his generators to warm nearby homes and factories. But few modern power plants use this residual heat, instead venting it into the air. When newer, larger plants required more real estate, they were built farther from customers. Moreover, because electricity travels easily, plants were located wherever they could tap the energy of a river or where local coal was especially cheap. The heat generated during the production of electricity does not travel far, however, so when power plants moved out to the horizon, the steam went to waste.", "highlight": null}, "v32_p1": {"text": "Except in special situations, human beings' battle with mosquitoes will not be won by a simple campaign to eliminate the insects. Social tradition and habits, it seems, do much to ensure continual contact between mosquitoes and people. On the slopes of Mount Kilimanjaro, for example, mosquitoes breed in the leaf axils of a plant called dracaena. Although dracaena is not a food plant for humans, its use as a hedge or boundary marker is deeply rooted in tradition. Here, as in other parts of the world, human behavior ensures contact and conflict between people and mosquitoes.\n\nI am not advocating a policy of living with mosquitoes; we already know that living with them is very unpleasant. But until we accomplish the difficult task of understanding how our habits often perpetuate─even create─our problems, efforts to resolve our battle with mosquitoes will probably fail.", "highlight": null}, "v228_p3": {"text": "Prehistoric humans domesticated wolves, which eventually developed into dogs. Based on all available archaeological evidence, archaeologists are certain that there were no dogs in Europe much earlier than 14,000 years ago. According to current genetic divergence theory, however, dogs must have started becoming a distinct species from wolves as early as 135,000 years ago, and it is extremely unlikely that dogs would have started becoming a distinct species unless they had been domesticated.", "highlight": null}, "v207_p2": {"text": "In his essay \"Classical Jazz and the Black Arts Movement,\" Lorenzo Thomas argues that the Black Arts movement of the 1960s grew out of the Harlem Renaissance of the 1920s, during which African American artists produced work consciously grounded in their cultural heritage. Both movements hoped to advance African Americans' social position through cultural expression. Yet Black Arts movement scholar Larry Neal pronounced the Harlem Renaissance, which produced enduring works in many genres, \"essentially a failure.\" According to Thomas, Neal's statement reflects a difference in the two movements' political and aesthetic philosophies. Whereas leaders of the Harlem Renaissance championed the cause of African Americans by demonstrating their achievements in \"high art\" as defined by European tradition, the Black Arts movement's leaders celebrated an African American aesthetic conceived as openly oppositional to that tradition. This is evident in the status held by jazz within the two movements. Commentators of the Harlem Renaissance cited, as evidence of the sophistication of jazz, the adaptation of jazz elements by European classical composers such as Antonin Dvorák. Some hoped that jazz musicians themselves would develop jazz into forms resembling European orchestral music. By contrast, asserts Thomas, Black Arts movement participants celebrated jazz as a musical form grounded in African Americans' historical experience that could not be evaluated using European aesthetic values.", "highlight": null}, "v240_p2": {"text": "Lichens consist of a fungus and an alga living in symbiotic union. Testing the widely held hypothesis that lichen-forming fungi are a closely knit, peripheral group of fungi, a team of scientists compared DNA sequences from 10 lichen-forming and 65 non-lichen-forming fungus species. These scientists classified the lichen-forming fungi into five kinds that were more closely related to kinds of non-lichen-forming fungi than to one another. The closest relatives of the lichen-forming kinds included some fungi that benefit, and others that cause disease to, associated organisms. Therefore, lichen-forming fungi probably evolved from various species whose effects on associated organisms ranged from benign to malignant. Furthermore, lichen-forming fungi seem to have given rise to other fungi that act as harmful parasites on lichens themselves. These considerations undermine the long-standing hypothesis that symbiotic relationships normally evolve in an orderly progression from those that are harmful to one partner to those that are mutually beneficial.", "highlight": null}, "v232_p1": {"text": "In 1961, Julia Child published 《Mastering the Art of French Cooking》, frequently described as revolutionary. According to legend, Child inspired Americans to exchange their bland cooking for French cuisine's rich flavors. Yet, Child's book was hardly singular among cookbooks. One publishing catalog lists almost as many books about French cooking in the decade before Child's book as in the decade after. While Child's book influenced a particular American cohort, its effect on the American publishing industry was minimal, a fact at odds with popular assumptions both about publishers and about Child's importance. We might expect Child's success to foster many imitations. Instead, American cookbooks pursued themes popular before Child's book was published, including a growing interest in the American cooking styles allegedly vanquished by Child.", "highlight": null}, "v35_p1": {"text": "Unlike herbivores and omnivores, predators have traditionally been thought not to balance nutrient intake because of the assumption that animal tissue as a food source varies little and is nutritionally balanced. But chemical analysis of invertebrate prey reveals remarkable variation in nutrient composition among species; even within species, nutrient composition may vary considerably. Greenstone suggested that predators may select food items according to their nutrient contents. Jensen et al (2011) have shown experimentally that even sit-and-wait invertebrate predators with limited mobility can work to address nutrient deficiencies. The wolf spider, for instance, has been shown to regulate nutrient intake by extracting more dry mass from a prey item if it contains a higher proportion of a nutrient that was deficient in the previous prey.", "highlight": null}, "v12_p1": {"text": "Progressivism, the wave of reform movements in the early twentieth century whose stated intention was to make United States society more democratic, has undergone significant scholarly reevaluation by historians over the years. In the 1960s, leftist scholars dismissed progressive reform as a mask for the empowerment of individuals forming a corporate, capitalist elite. In the two subsequent decades, many scholars began to question whether there was any such thing as progressivism; the phenomenon seemed so diverse and amorphous that the word itself, some claimed, had no meaning. In the early 1990s, however, the tone, if not always the substance, of historical accounts of progressivism changed again. Although some scholars admitted that progressivism was diverse, they insisted that there is an identifiable \"progressive minimum\", a core of belief and action that lends coherence to the concept. Further, some scholars, while acknowledging that progressivism had some conservative and even reactionary results, argue that the motives behind many of the reform movements of the era were genuinely democratic.", "highlight": null}, "v232_p2": {"text": "Domesticated crops have long been observed to differ strongly from their wild progenitors in morphological traits (form and structure). The enlargement of specific plant structures is the most widely emphasized of all of the changes that arise from domestication. Striking examples of gigantism can be found by comparing crops such as tomato (Lycopersicon esculentum), maize (Zea mays), beans (Phaseolus vulgaris), artichokes (Cynara cardunculus var. scolymus), sunflower (Helianthus annuus), and squash (Cucurbita pepo) with their wild ancestors.\n\nThe plant vigor hypothesis proposed by Price predicts that insect herbivores will tend to oviposit (lay eggs) on plant organs that grow faster and larger. Researchers found some support for this idea. For instance, in domesticated sunflowers, increased flower size from domestication is positively correlated with landing and egg-laying effort of female sunflower moths, Homoeosoma electellum, but increased seed size is negatively associated with parasitoid accessibility to H. electellum larvae. As a result, selection for gigantism may interfere with natural control and explain the observation that H. electellum is parasitized less frequently in sunflower agroecosystems than in natural sunflower ecosystems. However, parasitoids have a slightly greater effect on the banded sunflower moth, Cochylis hospes, which has a life history similar to that of H. electellum. Therefore, the life history of natural enemies and herbivores may influence whether selection for gigantism could result in enemy-free space for herbivores.", "highlight": null}, "v206_p1": {"text": "The dramatic growth of sugar production after the mid-seventeenth century enabled the articulation of a relatively new distinction within the European understanding of food taste, namely, the difference between savory and sweet. Earlier, salty and sweet tastes had been intermingled in medieval and Renaissance cooking, but with ever-increasing quantities of sugar available on the market, it became possible and desirable to distinguish between the two. Sweetness became relegated to fewer dishes, but much greater amounts of sugar were used in those dishes. The distinction between sweet and savory ended the older tradition of strongly flavored, deeply spiced sauces and condiments that marked European elite cuisine for centuries, heralding a new cuisine which claimed to pay more respect to its ingredients' intrinsic flavors.", "highlight": null}, "v226_p3": {"text": "Most Oakville residents want a community swimming pool to be built but do not want to finance it with local tax revenues. Oakville's mayor argues that although the town has no financial reserves, building a pool will not lead to higher taxes, since an unused town-owned land parcel is available and admission fees will cover the entire cost of operating the pool as well as repayment of the $3 million debt for construction.", "highlight": null}, "v210_p1": {"text": "The border decoration in medieval manuscripts referred to as pen flourishing reached great artistic heights in the northern Netherlands in the 1400s. The regional variants in form that evolved make flourishing a useful tool for localizing and roughly dating manuscripts. When the first printed books appeared in that region, many copies were still traditionally decorated by hand with such flourishing. Since books’ publication can usually be dated with far more accuracy than manuscripts, studying these decorations in early printed books might lead to a more precise dating of the penwork in manuscripts. It is of less help in localizing the flourishing. Upon completion, copies of printed books were often sold unadorned, to be decorated elsewhere as commissioned by their buyers.", "highlight": "Upon completion, copies of printed books were often sold unadorned, to be decorated elsewhere as commissioned by their buyers."}, "v235_p2": {"text": "Projecting the idea of a distinctive female demand in seventeenth and eighteenth-century England was a groundbreaking departure in the history of marketing. The pioneers were the booksellers and printers who addressed specialist titles to the ladies in the 1600s, while the post-1688 print boom saw the publication of custom-designed ladies’ pocket diaries, a proliferation of female manuals of all kinds, 《The Female Spectator》 in the 1740s and the long-running 《The Lady’s Magazine》 from 1770. The leap to objects was made when leading furniture makers started classifying furniture by the sex, age, and specialist needs of the implied user in the new illustrated catalogs of the 1760s. Of course, sex distinctions in clothes are as old as civilization, while the idea of furniture suited to female needs is not unprecedented (think of birthing stools), but making difference systematic and concrete by means of word, image, and object was a decisive innovation. The rapid diffusion of ladies’ and gentlemen’s furniture suggests that gender distinctions already resonated powerfully with male and female consumers, but in the extension of the range of differentiated furniture, the projection of the trope by manufacturers thereafter, and its acceptance by consumers, conventional ideas of masculine importance and femininity delicacy were amplified and fixed. In the process, femininity was expressed in a specific and narrowly defined aesthetic register.", "highlight": "The pioneers were the booksellers and printers who addressed specialist titles to the ladies in the 1600s, while the post-1688 print boom saw the publication of custom-designed ladies’ pocket diaries, a proliferation of female manuals of all kinds, 《The Female Spectator》 in the 1740s and the long-running 《The Lady’s Magazine》 from 1770."}, "v213_p2": {"text": "Julie Roy Jeffrey’s recent book 《The Great Silent Army of Abolitionism》 shows how women participated in all aspects of the antislavery movement in the United States, from its inception in the early 1830s through the end of the Civil War (1861–1865). While scholars have already pointed out the importance of women’s work in early abolitionist circles, especially in spreading a grassroots antislavery message through the constant and tireless circulation of petitions, Jeffery disputes certain aspects of the traditional account of their participation. For example, even though the abolitionist movement split into political and nonpolitical wings at the end of the 1830s and women were largely relegated to the less politicized faction, Jeffrey does not accept the view that women’s participation became marginalized as a result. She demonstrates that women found numerous ways to persist effectively in the cause, such as by organizing the antislavery fund-raising fairs of the 1840s. She also disputes the notion that African American women were relegated to secondary positions in the largely White movement. Their own abolitionist societies, she argues, often responded to the crises of the pre-Civil War decades, such as the Fugitive Slave Law, more directly than did integrated abolitionist groups.", "highlight": null}, "v5_p2": {"text": "In 1886 approximately 20 percent of United States workers belonged to the Knights of Labor, a labor-activist fraternal order. Nonetheless, soon after reaching this peak, the Knights membership began a rapid decline, and the organization never regained its national prominence. This collapse had wide-ranging repercussions: subsequent worker organizations took a less active and less broad-based organizational approach. The Knights' defeat demoralized those who championed radical reform and the organization of workers as a class, while empowering those who promoted a less inclusive strategy.\n\nCurrent scholarship has tended to attribute the Knights calamitous decline to two factors: persistent tension between skilled and unskilled workers, and fierce opposition from employer associations, which used extralegal means to undermine unions. Voss examined both factors and found that employer associations' opposition, not conflict among the Knights, led to the Knights' rapid decline. But Voss's account fails to explain why the Knights succumbed so easily when other union movements thrived. It seems that the Knights' particular organizational structure prompted factional disputes among members and, more important, that competition from rival trade and fraternal organizations lured members away. While dissension within the order might not itself have sufficed to cause its demise, the profusion of organizational alternatives during this period induced mass defection, and, subsequently, the transformation of the American labor movement.", "highlight": "organizations"}, "v13_p1": {"text": "Modern scholarship's view of women's labor in Han dynasty China (B.C. 206 – A.D. 220) shows women performing a wide variety of work roles. According to most modern scholars, for a household (the main economic organization in early Chinese society) to succeed economically, a man and a woman each had to work at many different kinds of gendered tasks. In contrast, writers during the Han dynasty, rather than emphasizing the multitude of daily tasks women performed, constructed an idealized representation of female labor, singling out cloth production as the most important job and linking it to the concept of successful womanhood. In reality, however, a woman who devoted herself to making cloth, ignoring other work, would have been considered irresponsible.", "highlight": null}, "v230_p1": {"text": "Using radar instruments to analyze the exact nature of geological features on Saturn's moon Titan is challenging, because radar images are unlike ordinary photographs. With radar, the brightness of the reflected signal correlates with the roughness of the surface. Thus, the smooth surfaces of Titan's methane-filled lakes look dark in radar images, while bright areas usually suggest rough hilly terrain. However, the data don't always follow this pattern. Many detected river valleys and lakes appear bright compared to the surrounding terrain, suggesting a generally dry riverbed or lake bed filled with gravel or cobble. As for the dark, meandering river valleys, one theory proposes that they are deeply incised bedrock channels whose steep walls shadow the signal, making the radar images appear dark.", "highlight": "Thus, the smooth surfaces of Titan's methane-filled lakes look dark in radar images, while bright areas usually suggest rough hilly terrain."}, "v216_p1": {"text": "Predators of herbivores can influence the structure and dynamics of plant communities in two ways: by reducing herbivore density or by modifying herbivore behavior. Whereas density-mediated effects generally affect all plants, behavioral effects often cause herbivores to change their relative use of different parts of their habitat. This can lead to a redistribution of herbivore damage on different plant species, for example, when plant-eating insects shift from preferred but risky plant species to less nutritious plants that offer refuge. A well-documented example involves predatory nursery-web spiders—a species that typically inhabits only the upper canopy of grasses. In systems where the spiders are present, grasshoppers shift their feeding activity toward ground level, thereby increasing the relative consumption of goldenrod over Kentucky bluegrass.", "highlight": null}, "v212_p2": {"text": "Only in the collecting sciences are raw data—specimens, fossils, artifacts—regarded as communal property, to which legitimate practitioners have rights of access. Collections are an intellectual commons on which all producers depend, and the owners or keepers of collections are understood to be responsible for keeping them in good order and accessible to users. These moral precepts doubtless reflect the fact that important collections tend to end up in public museums. But I think they also derive from the reality that found objects, unlike manufactured data, are a unique and irreplaceable resource, the loss of which deprives all practitioners of the means of best practice.\n\nThe moral economy of facts is quite different in sciences that generate facts artificially through measurement or experimentation. In these sciences, raw data are regarded as private: because, I think, they are in principle unlimited and if lost, can be produced again. Manufactured data become public only when published, and though publishing is expected, it is also understood to be selective and a personal matter, impelled more by ambition and career imperatives than by moral obligation. Individuals may perish professionally if they neglect to publish, but if they do perish, someone else can always produce equivalent data, so there is no loss to the common good. Raw data are not an intellectual commons, as are collections. The experimental sciences operate more in a market economy than a moral one.", "highlight": "Individuals may perish professionally if they neglect to publish, but if they do perish, someone else can always produce equivalent data, so there is no loss to the common good."}, "v236_p3": {"text": "A cave in Central America was occupied by humans for much of the period from 9,000 to 500 years ago. Archaeological excavations in the cave have discovered remains of food plants at every level of habitation, increasing from fewer than ten food plant species in the earliest (lowest) levels to over 30 species in the latest levels. Clearly, later inhabitants of the cave used a greater variety of plants as food than earlier inhabitants did.", "highlight": null}, "v22_p1": {"text": "While direct bite-inflicted injury is the most commonly observed mechanism for Komodo dragons to dispatch prey, the role of bacteria in aiding prey death is poorly known. One study identified in the lizards' saliva and oral cavities 58 species of bacteria 93 percent of which are classified as potentially pathogenic. Auffenberg proposed that the bacteria are beneficial to the lizards; in essence a slow-acting venom facilitates prey capture by attacking lizards. He offered no mechanism by which the bacteria are acquired by lizards, however. Fry et al. questioned this interpretation, and proposed that sepsis-inducing bacteria are more plausibly acquired passively from prey and other environmental sources, with no role in prey acquisition. That model fits the observation that captive lizards (and presumably newborns) lack sepsis-inducing bacteria.", "highlight": null}, "v237_p1": {"text": "One of the reasons why many early British colonies in North America failed amid the New World's abundance was that the settlers' mindset prevented them from living like the native inhabitants. From Native Americans, the settlers learned such skills as building brushwood weirs to trap fish, but they did not adopt the real key to success: mobility. The whole intellectual foundation of European civilization was fixity─a worldview profoundly different from that of Native Americans, who moved in response to changing food resources. Settlers were drawn to North America by tales of its extraordinary abundance, not realizing that abundance is seasonal. Culture and ecological knowledge allowed Native Americans to exploit different food sources at different time of year.", "highlight": null}, "v204_p2": {"text": "Studies comparing children's memory for television news stories with their recall of print versions containing exactly the same verbal information generally show that television news is remembered best. Paivio's dual-coding hypothesis, a frequent explanation, suggests that audiovisual information is stored in memory as two separate but associated codes—one verbal and one visual—whereas text-only information is stored as a verbal code only. During recall, the visual-memory code serves as an extra retrieval cue, which could account for the superior recall of television stories.\n\nHowever, experiments show that learning is enhanced only by the addition of \"redundant\" pictures, which convey the same basic meaning as the words. When pictures and words do not coincide, children do not remember more and sometimes remember less from television presentations than from purely verbal presentations. Theories based on the concept of \"limited attentional capacity\" posit that when verbal and visual information do not correspond, viewers' attentional capacity is exceeded and part of the information is lost. In the case of nonredundant audiovisual information, viewers tend to direct their attention to the visual images because meaning is conveyed more readily through pictures; this preference may hinder learning because the main message in television news is usually provided in the spoken commentary.", "highlight": null}, "v218_p14": {"text": "Washburn’s examination of textile designs from the precolonial Kuba Kingdom in Africa reveals that, despite a theoretical embrace of infinite formal variation, there exists in practice a limited number of pattern structures with creativity channeled into developing nuanced variations on those designs. A parallel sensibility informs the Kuba approach to the ndop fiqurative sculptures depicting paramount leaders. While one might assume royal portraits capture the unique image of each leader, in practice Kuba sculptors adapted a preferred figurative convention. Although the ndop figures themselves are so homogeneous that they are essentially expunged of any idiosyncratic physiognomic features, the embedded ibol signifier (a symbolic emblem incorporated into the base of each sculpture) and an accompanying explanatory proverb invest each image with a particular identity.", "highlight": null}, "v230_p4": {"text": "The concept of \"soul food,\" popularized in northern and western American cities in the 1960s, presented a simplified narrative of African American cooking to unify diverse communities and instill cultural pride. Traditionally explained by reciting its constituent recipes and ingredients, the cuisine became synonymous with foods such as catfish and black-eyed peas. But renowned African American chef and cookbook author Edna Lewis rebelled against the strictures of this invented tradition. Lewis was a proponent of the living custom of southern food, which emphasized the diversity of the cuisine of her southern childhood. For Lewis, soul food constituted a limited and static rendition of southern food; however, Americans who first encountered the cuisine in the North or the West lacked the same regional frame of reference.", "highlight": null}, "v240_p1": {"text": "During the early nineteenth century, the demand for ever-louder sound led to ever-increasing tension on piano strings, making evident the need for stronger framing. Even long after factories had taken over the manufacture of other commodities, the Industrial Revolution nevertheless shaped the attitudes of those who decided whether to accept this innovation. To build pianos with steam-powered tools was one thing, and to put a cast-iron frame at the center of the instrument, making the product itself a modern factory of sound rather than a fully handcrafted artwork in wood, was quite another. The resulting debate was vigorous, with many feeling certain that iron in the piano would ruin the tone.", "highlight": null}, "v210_p3": {"text": "Centuries ago, the Maya of Central America produced elaborate, deeply cut carvings in stone. Given the technology available to the Maya, the carvings could only have been made with tools of stone or iron. Mayan stone tools have been found, but experiments reveal that these tools are not hard enough to make anything but very small markings in the stone used for the carvings. Therefore, the Maya must have used iron tools for the carvings.", "highlight": null}, "v205_p2": {"text": "The area of literary rights is confusing for scholars whose work focuses on collaborative materials, particularly materials of earlier Native American writers. Questions arise over authorship and the determination of literary heirs. For example, recognition of heirs turns on the European-based assumption of the private ownership of a written statement. The first person to write down an oral tale can become legally recognized as the owner of that version of the story, just as the first chemist to patent a tribal healing practice becomes the owner of the resulting chemical formula. This insistance on private rather than collective ownership, derived from the nineteenth-century notion of the autonomous, creative, authorial voice, flies in the face of those who come from an oral tradition. Thus, a scholar concerned with finding literary heirs in order to afford them the benefits of copyright laws must in so doing accede to legal concept of ownership that has been used to appropriate knowledge from community-based cultures.", "highlight": null}, "v238_p3": {"text": "Many Namibian farmers raise cattle on farmland that is part of a cheetah’s territory. Cheetahs are solitary hunters that hunt in and defend exclusive territories. For decades the farmers have been trapping and killing cheetahs on their land but have found that the frequency with which cheetahs are trapped has not decreased during this period. The Namibian cheetah population, therefore, must not have suffered any significant reduction as a result of the farmers' practice.", "highlight": null}, "v226_p2": {"text": "To evaluate any given intellectual property policy, we must weigh the costs and benefits of awarding copyright protection. If an innovation and the benefits of the protection are nonexistent, then, by the cost-benefit criterion, it is unwarranted. Such a situation arose in 1998, when the United States Congress extended the term of copyright from 50 years after an author's death to 70. Book buyers are harmed by this. A book's price is higher under copyright because the publisher continues to owe royalties to the author's heirs and does not compete with others printing the same book. Against that drawback, there is no countervailing benefit. Authors are hardly likely to find motivation in the prospect of earnings that will arrive more than 50 years after their death. Moreover, the extension was applied retroactively to existing copyrights─but authors do not need incentives to write books they have already written.", "highlight": "Authors are hardly likely to find motivation in the prospect of earnings that will arrive more than 50 years after their death."}, "v212_p3": {"text": "Sunlight is composed of different colors of light, which differ in how far they penetrate a given medium. Seawater is most deeply penetrated by blue light, and at depths near 1,000 meters the sunlight is almost entirely blue. However, a few fish species living at such depths have eyes with lenses tinted so that they filter out blue light but not light of any other color.", "highlight": null}, "v28_p3": {"text": "Feminist scholars have tended to regard women in the nineteenth-century United States who elected to remain single as champions of women’s autonomy and as critics of marriage as an oppressive institution. Indeed, many nineteenth-century American women who participated in reform movements or who distinguished themselves as writers and professionals were single. Yet this view of single women tends to distort the meaning of their choices. The nineteenth century saw the elevation of marriage for love as a spiritual ideal. Consequently, it became socially acceptable for women not to marry if such an ideal marriage could not be realized with an available suitor. Thus, many women’s choice to remain single reflected not a negative view of marriage but a highly idealistic one.", "highlight": null}, "v218_p7": {"text": "The trader's dilemma, which typically occurs in peasant villages, arises in two contexts. First, the trader buys agricultural products in his or her village; although these products are often resold outside the village at a market, where laws of supply and demand exist and profit margins are rather limited, the trader nevertheless feels morally obliged to pay fellow villagers a good price for their products or even eventually to share profits with those villagers. Second, in his or her village shop, the trader sells imported products, but because of villagers' constrained finances must do so at reduced price, or even on credit. In both cases, the trader confronts the risk of either losing working capital or losing the respect and moral support of neighbors and kinfolk.\n\nA classical way out of the dilemma, according to Evers, is sociocultural differentiation of peasants and traders into two separate, locally coexisting moral communities. Evers' point is theoretically significant because it implies that such differentiation may be economically rather than politically motivated. Thus, while in many societies traders are strangers, a migrant minority, it may also happen that a resident trading minority itself creates cultural distance in order to find a solution for the trader's dilemma, which thus may drive sociocultural change.", "highlight": null}, "v228_p4": {"text": "Because Chopin concentrated on musical genres considered trivial─nocturnes, mazurkas, waltzes─critics labeled him a miniaturist. This view of Chopin, which remained orthodox into the later twentieth century, is now largely discredited. Many of Chopin's large works─such as scherzos and sonatas─are longer than an average movement of Beethoven. Chopin was, in fact, the only composer of his generation who never, after the age of twenty-one, wrote a long piece that was ineffective. There are deserts with few oases in a number of works of Berlioz; and not many works of Liszt are completely exempt from some facile pages. But the elegance, distinction, and efficacy of Chopin's large forms are almost unique for the time in their success.", "highlight": null}, "v232_p4": {"text": "Few central Asian textiles from the Timurid period(1370~1526 C.E.) have survived to be dated. Scholars have long assumed that Timurid rugs with geometric patterns were replaced in royal courts by floral-patterned rugs only at the end of the 1400s, under the influence of the painter Behzad(circa 1455~circa 1536). Nevertheless, the presence of floral-patterned rugs in court scenes from two paintings in a 1440s Timurid manuscript suggests that floral-patterned rugs were already being used at that time. Whether the occasional presence of geometric rugs in similar paintings after the 1440s means that the tradition of weaving rugs with geometric patterns also continued, or whether here the painters simply followed a well-established formula, is still an open question.", "highlight": null}, "v238_p4": {"text": "A review of the chemical composition of Sierra Nevada mountain spring waters in 1964 revealed surprising differences in concentrations of total dissolved solids (TDS) among springs. Given the relatively uniform composition of the granite through which all the water flowed, review authors had expected more uniformity in the mineral content. They noted, however, that some of the springs were ephemeral, flowing only in springtime, while others were perennial. Though the two kinds of springs contained similar proportions of dissolved calcium, magnesium, sodium, bicarbonate, sulfate, and chloride, TDS levels in perennial springs were about twice those in ephemeral springs. Perennial springs' waters circulate more deeply into the earth and have a longer residence time than those of ephemeral springs, reacting more completely with granitic rocks.", "highlight": "Perennial springs' waters circulate more deeply into the earth and have a longer residence time than those of ephemeral springs, reacting more completely with granitic rocks."}, "v16_p3": {"text": "We take it for granted that island populations must have a continental origin, and not the other way around. The number of islands that acquire their biota [i.e., plant and animal life] from a larger source supports this notion. There is, however, no fundamental mechanism in the equilibrium theory of island biogeography to preclude island species from colonizing the mainland. The belief in one-way biogeographic traffic has only begun to erode as phylogenetic analyses have revealed island origins for continental rodents and lizards. Among plants, the genus Exostema has successfully diversified in the continental Neotropics, while two populations in the angiosperm genus Erithalis have colonized Florida. At least two Neotropical bat lineages can be added to the growing list of island-to-continent colonizers.", "highlight": null}, "v211_p1": {"text": "This passage is adapted from material published in 2009.\n\nOnce “talkies” replaced silent movies that had live musical accompaniment, over 3,200 New York City pit musicians were suddenly jobless. The musicians union waged a campaign, culminating in a strike, to return live music to movie theaters, but it ended in utter disaster in 1937, when it became clear that the rest of the working class would not support them. The union was struggling against an inevitable tide. Working-class people not only preferred sound films but appreciated the ticket price, which was lower without the live talent. Freed from paying wages and from union regulations governing musicians' hours, theater owners could show films all day, and the Depression-era jobless could escape the weather or their troubles by spending afternoons at the movies for a few cents.", "highlight": null}, "v235_p1": {"text": "Exotic insect pests can produce both short- and long-term effects of forest ecosystems. Short-term effects include the disturbances directly associated with the action of the pest, which may cause the defoliation, loss of vigor, or death of trees. Long-term effects are primarily mediated by changes in tree species composition and the consequent alternations of forest structure, productivity, and nutrient uptake. Exotic pests are more efficient than most abiotic disturbances (e.g., fire or wind) at producing long-term changes in species composition. Pests often target specific tree species and, if they become established, they usually remain as permanent components of the ecosystem. Shifts in forest species composition ramify through the ecosystem in many ways because tree species have different, often unique properties.", "highlight": null}, "v1_p1": {"text": "Early scholars described square dances as a type of ancient English country dance carried to the southern Appalachian Mountains and preserved unchanged for generations. However, while the Appalachian fiddle repertoire does include traditional reels that can be traced back to the British Isles, it also includes breakdowns, rags, and other musical features native to America. Appalachian songs similarly range from British ballads to African American blues. Given this musical diversity—not to mention the iconic presence of the banjo, an instrument with African roots—it would be naive to think the accompanying dances are purely English forms. While sections of Appalachia are relatively isolated, trade, travel, and immigration have continually introduced new cultural elements, including innovations in social dances, into the region's rural traditions.", "highlight": null}, "v197_p1": {"text": "Critical neglect of Emily Bronte’s poetry is long-standing and once resulted from an idea of Victorian poetry as essentially a male preserve. Feminist critics have challenged this understanding of Victorian poetry largely by displacing critical approaches that required a particular subject matter or point of view and therefore undervalued women poets whose work did not conform. But feminist critics’ own assumptions about Victorian women’s poetry have also threatened to exclude Emily Bronte. Virginia Blain’s anthology of Victorian women’s poetry is representative, not eccentric, in omitting Bronte. Blain aimed to provide wide-ranging coverage of “the kinds of subjects and poetic treatments most often employed by Victorian women poets.” Yet, as Emily’s sister Charlotte said, Emily’s poetry is not “at all like the poetry women generally write.”", "highlight": null}, "v2_p2": {"text": "All the music from fourteenth-century Europe for which written scores survive is so complex and is written in such difficult notation that it could have been played only by musicians whose lives were dedicated solely to such performance. Yet fourteenth-century European accounts, which in this respect probably give accurate portrayals of their times, describe many members of the nobility who excelled not only in musical performance, but also in dancing, poetry, and painting.", "highlight": null}, "v202_p3": {"text": "A year ago, the government of Portran predicted that Torre City would experience strong net job growth for the following year but that Glanville, Portran’s other major city, would not. Events have clearly proved otherwise, however; in Torre City, but not in Glanville, the number of people who are unemployed is greater now than it was a year ago.", "highlight": null}, "v238_p1": {"text": "For American artist Lucy Lippard, politically engaged art necessarily existed primarily outside of traditional art venues, in public spaces and in direct confrontation with political power. But for some other 1970s New York artists, it was inside the art world—and especially within museums—that the machinations of power could best be exposed and examined. Artists such as Adrian Piper worked within the genre known as \"institutional critique\" that explored and confronted the political and economic entanglements of museum patronage. Artists engaged in such work were often criticized for participating in the very art world system they purported to challenge. Yet their rigorous methodologies for researching and dramatically staging interventions in museum spaces yielded some of the era's most politically astute and influential artworks.", "highlight": null}, "v6_p3": {"text": "More than two decades after the death of George Balanchine, the choreographer's legacy is strangely unclear. In part this is because ballet has shallow roots in American culture. When Balanchine arrived in the United States in 1933, American ballet was little more than a vaudeville act. During the next 50 years, he raised American ballet to an internationally recognized art, producing an impressive body of great ballets and laying a foundation for generations to come—or so it was thought at the time of his death. But dance has no written tradition and disappears easily from collective memory: unless Balanchine's dances are alive and interesting now, we are likely to forget why they ever seemed so important.", "highlight": null}, "v211_p2": {"text": "Aristotle (384–322 BC) was admired in the ancient world for the clarity of his style. Unfortunately, the writings that earned him this esteem have not survived. What we read today are not the books Aristotle prepared for publication, but lecture notes compiled for his own use. These have one great advantage: making no concessions to a lay readership, the Aristotelian works available to us are the ones that intellectually sophisticated commentators in late antiquity (AD 300–600) found philosophically most rewarding. But they also have disadvantages. These texts were not designed for public consumption and are consequently often difficult to understand. The process by which they took their present form is unclear: in some cases, there are signs of editorial activity either by Aristotle or by a later hand, so different versions of the same text may have been spliced together. In general, their style is cryptic, condensed, and allusive; the 《Poetics》, in particular, is frequently very obscure. This obscurity has created difficulties for later readers of Aristotle. The 《Poetics》, though not widely known in antiquity, became extraordinarily influential beginning around 1500 in the Renaissance, especially among literary critics. Yet the text’s obscurities have left it open to conflicting interpretations. There are still fundamental disagreements about the meaning even of key concepts, such as katharsis.", "highlight": "writings"}, "v4_p2": {"text": "Opponents of a proposal to extend the city's subway line to two new stations claim that the project will benefit only a small portion of the city's population. These opponents are misguided. After all, the last time the line was extended, the greater availability of quick transport to the city reduced the number of private cars on city streets, thus benefiting everyone by easing rush-hour traffic.", "highlight": "the project will benefit only a small portion of the city's population."}, "v234_p3": {"text": "A hoard of coins recently unearthed at an ancient Carthagian site bear an image of a face in profile with what appears to be a large mole on the cheek. Pointing out that an artist would be unlikely to include such a specific detail in a generalized portrayal of a face, some archaeologists have concluded that these coins portray an actual individual rather than an idealized type. However, this conclusion is unwarranted, since _____.", "highlight": null}, "v213_p1": {"text": "In the late 1970s, bird populations were found to be declining in India’s Bharatpur Bird Sanctuary in Rajasthan. Grazing cattle and buffalo were the suspected culprits: they were entering the preserve in sufficient numbers to disrupt what was believed to be an otherwise balanced ecosystem. Accordingly, grazing was banned in Bharatpur. Yet by the mid-1980s, studies found that bird diversity within the preserve had declined further since the ban, and it continued to plummet. The absence of grazing animals, it turns out, had disturbed the park’s ecology. Weed species were taking over wetlands and choking canals, thereby reducing the fish populations that had once attracted so many birds, and avian species then went elsewhere in search of more suitable nesting places.", "highlight": null}, "v7_p1": {"text": "Some studies have shown that red-backed salamanders (RBS) are scarce in areas with acidic soils and that those present in such conditions have smaller-than-average bodies. Explanations have included the possibility that young RBS are adversely affected by acidic soil, that adult RBS can sense and may avoid acidic soil conditions, or that loss of RBS prey populations due to acidic soil could result in reduced RBS populations. Yet researchers found fairly high densities of large-bodied RBS at Lake Claire Watershed, where soil conditions are acidic. One hypothesis is that intraspecific geographical variation in acidity tolerance (i.e., local adaptation to an acidic environment) could exist for RBS. Previous studies showed potential local adaptation of some salamander species to acidity.", "highlight": "Some studies have shown that red-backed salamanders (RBS) are scarce in areas with acidic soils and that those present in such conditions have smaller-than-average bodies."}, "v220_p5": {"text": "This passage is adapted from material published in 2007.\n\nWilson has suggested that the methodological orientations of the political science discipline might account for political science's lagging behind history and sociology in the publication of mainstream journal articles on African American topics. He explained these relative disciplinary differences regarding publication as partially resulting from pressure to do large-scale voter studies; this pressure placed those interested in African American politics at a disadvantage, because the relevant empirical data on the Black population were insufficient to render findings that were externally valid and generalizable. Wilson's second explanation pointed to the discipline's traditional focus on politics and decision-making processes at levels to which African Americans have historically had limited access—a narrow focus reflected in the types of research articles favored in mainstream political science journals.", "highlight": null}, "v240_p3": {"text": "In an attempt to reduce the number of violent crimes committed by juveniles, the city of Fiera imposed a curfew requiring juveniles─everyone younger than eighteen─to be indoors between the hours of 11 P.M. and 6 A.M. In the two years since the curfew was imposed, the number of violent crimes committed by juveniles in Fiera has fallen by almost ten percent. Clearly, therefore, the curfew has proven effective at reducing violent juvenile crime.", "highlight": null}, "v25_p2": {"text": "When on an airplane, Consuelo never enjoys movies that have been widely recommended because the poor quality of the picture spoils her enjoyment. Since in no circumstances does she ever enjoy movies that have been widely derided, it follows that she never enjoys movies on airplanes.", "highlight": null}, "v21_p3": {"text": "The recently announced discovery of the first known planet orbiting a pulsar (the ultradense, pulsating remnant off the supernova explosion of a star) turned out to be based on faulty data. Had this discovery been confirmed, theorists would have had difficulty accounting for the existence of such a planet. The supernova would certainly have destroyed any preexisting planets. This particular pulsar is relatively young, allowing little time for a new planet to have coalesced, and it rotates relatively slowly, implying that it has not interacted with any nearby star since the supernova.\n\nBut newer evidence of a different pulsar with planets is more promising. This is a rapidly spurring \"millisecond pulsar\" thought to be a much older object that has pulled gaseous material from a stellar neighbor, causing its rotational speed to increase. Leftover, unconsumed gas around such a pulsar could, in theory, coalesce into planets. Or the pulsar's radiation might have vaporized a companion star, providing new material for planetary formation.", "highlight": null}, "v26_p1": {"text": "Late-eighteenth-century English cultural authorities seemingly concurred that women readers should favor history, seen as edifying, over fiction, which was regarded as frivolous and reductive. Readers of Mary Ann Hanway's novel Andrew Stewart, or the Northern Wanderer, learning that its heroine delights in David Hume's and Edward Gibbon's histories, could conclude that she was more virtuous and intelligent than her sister, who disdains such reading. Likewise, while the naïve, novel-addicted protagonist of Jane Austen's Northanger Abbey, Catherine Morland, finds history a chore, the sophisticated, sensible character Eleanor Tilney enjoys it more than she does the Gothic fiction Catherine prefers.\n\nYet in both cases, the praise of history is more double-edged than it might actually appear. Many readers have detected a protofeminist critique of history in Catherine's protest that she dislikes reading books filled with men \"and hardly any women at all.\" Hanway, meanwhile, brings a controversial political edge to her heroine's reading, listing the era's two most famous religious skeptics among her preferred authors. While Hume's history was generally seen as being less objectionable than his philosophy, there were widespread doubts about his moral soundness even as a historian by the time that Hanway was writing, and Gibbon's perceived tendency to celebrate classical paganism sparked controversy from the first appearance of his history of Rome.", "highlight": "Readers of Mary Ann Hanway's novel Andrew Stewart, or the Northern Wanderer, learning that its heroine delights in David Hume's and Edward Gibbon's histories, could conclude that she was more virtuous and intelligent than her sister, who disdains such reading."}, "v206_p2": {"text": "Archaeologists in Australia have never found sites where large extinct animals were killed, and it seems likely that many species of megafauna had become extinct prior to the arrival of humans. This might mean that there was minimal coexistence between humans and megafauna; yet there are sites that may well display temporal overlap, such as Cuddie Springs. If humans exploited megafauna, then why are there no kill sites? While Flannery (1990) argued that the rapid speed of the extermination may be responsible, it is more likely that lack of preservation of material dating to more than 40,000 years ago is responsible. Nevertheless, environmental signatures consistently point to the reduction in range and density of large animals, if not their final extinction, between 40,000 and 50,000 years ago, coincident with the arrival of people, and so the appearance of human hunters in the landscape is implicated in the extinction process. The timing of extinction trends in these mega-animals coincides with intensification of long-term continental drying, reductions in resource levels, and restructuring of the environment, and so even low levels of predation by the new human hunters may have tipped some species into terminal declines or accelerated declines already underway. Most likely, it was not intensive or exclusive hunting of these large animals that reduced their populations perilously, but merely the addition of a new social carnivore to stressful ecological circumstances.", "highlight": "While Flannery (1990) argued that the rapid speed of the extermination may be responsible, it is more likely that lack of preservation of material dating to more than 40,000 years ago is responsible."}, "v220_p13": {"text": "The crustaceans known as harpacticoids are very widespread in marine sediments, where they feed on microorganisms by ingesting the sediment particles to which the microorganisms adhere. Heavy metals, such as those found in industrial pollution, readily adhere to sediment particles. Harpacticoids are poisoned by heavy metals but are unaffected by most other pollutants. Therefore, the concentration of harpacticoids in an area is a good indication of whether that marine environment contains heavy metals.", "highlight": null}, "v223_p4": {"text": "At roughly four thousand lines, the second quarto version of Hamlet—the closest surviving version to what Shakespeare first wrote in late 1599—could not have been performed uncut. Though the Elizabethan stage dispensed with time-consuming intermissions and scenery changes, this version would still have taken four hours to perform; even at top speed, actors couldn't rattle off much more than a thousand lines of verse an hour. With outdoor performances beginning at two in the afternoon and the sun setting at around five o'clock, an uncut Hamlet staged in late fall or winter would have left actors stumbling about on a dark stage. Contemporary references to other plays mention their running time as being closer to two hours.", "highlight": "Contemporary references to other plays mention their running time as being closer to two hours."}, "v9_p2": {"text": "Pueblo Bonito, the most impressive of the \"great houses\" at the prehistoric Chaco Canyon site in New Mexico, comprised over 600 rooms and 4 to 5 stories. Traditional interpretations have viewed the great houses as almost entirely residential, with some archaeologists estimating the population of Pueblo Bonito at 1,200. But Windes recently challenged this view by pointing out the paucity of hearths recorded during the excavation of Pueblo Bonito, which revealed only 3 upper-story hearths, in contrast to 59 ground-floor hearths: habituation rooms would have required hearths for cooking and heat. It is possible, however, that the collapse of upper-story floors disturbed evidence of upper-story hearths to such an extent that they were not revealed by early excavations such as those conducted by Pepper's field crews in the 1890s and Judd's in the 1920s. Additionally, reliance on room features for early population estimates is complicated by the Chacoan's later remodeling, especially given Judd's disinclination to destroy later structures and features to expose earlier ones. The failure of early excavations to strip off intact floors may have concealed evidence of hearths in upper-story rooms.", "highlight": null}, "v219_p10": {"text": "Though long acknowledged internationally as one of India's major nonfiction writers, Nirad Chaudhuri (1897-1999), largely because of controversial political opinions, has been shunned by much of the Indian intelligentsia and his work had been unavailable to Indian readers until 1997. In fact, only since then has his 1951 《Autobiography》, the book that made his international reputation, been brought back into print in India after an absence of many years. Though he has enjoyed support among novelists—VS. Naipaul has called the 《Autobiography》 a great book about the English colonization of India, and Doris Lessing has called it “one of the great books of the twentieth century”—Chaudhuri's work has been more discussed than read. For example, until recently none of his books were available in the United States, but a critical work about him is a standard university text. At his best, says William Dalrymple, Chaudhuri is a superb writer of descriptive prose; but in his sometimes indulgent meandering and excessive allusion, Chaudhuri's work resembles that of a later Indian writer of genius, Salman Rushdie.", "highlight": null}, "v222_p5": {"text": "The period between the two world wars (1918-1939) was characterized by a broadening of the definition of women's roles in the United States. In 1920, American women won the right to vote; building on this right, some now participated actively in politics. Increasing numbers of middle-class women joined their working-class contemporaries in the workplace, and a small but growing minority of them continued working after marriage. Divorce rates increased as work patterns and women's expectations of marriage changed. While these trends continued throughout the interwar period, their momentum was slowed in its later years, as the prosperity of the 1920s abruptly ended. Many Americans responded to the economic crisis of the 1930s by reasserting traditional value that discouraged women from entering traditionally male occupations.", "highlight": null}, "v218_p5": {"text": "Scholars hotly debate the date of the first decorative use of copper in the manufacture of Korean celadon ceramics. Some authorities argue that because one of the earliest examples featuring such decoration, a lotus-shaped ewer, was excavated from a tomb dated to 1257, the use of the technique in Korea probably dates from the 1200s. Other authorities contend this ewer instead dates to the previous century, citing the similarity of its incised lotus-petals to other surviving pieces of that era. They maintain that the ewer must have been old─perhaps a treasured antique─when it was buried. Either dating of the method's introduction would support scholars' claims that copper was used in decorating ceramics in Korea before it was used in China.", "highlight": "They maintain that the ewer must have been old─perhaps a treasured antique─when it was buried."}, "v28_p4": {"text": "In European lowland heathlands, heather bushes, grasses, and bracken compete with one another for the sandy soil's scarce nutrients, with none acquiring permanent dominance. In Dutch heathlands, however, atmospheric nitrogen pollution produced by intensive animal farming has turned heathlands into grassland, the result of an interaction between nitrogen pollution and heather-eating beetles. Additional nitrogen usually increases growth of both grass and heather, and at first heather usually thrives because the grasses cannot penetrate the canopy of its bushes. Heather beetle population size, like that of many herbivorous insects, varies from year to year. When heather beetles are abundant, their larvae grow particularly well on the nitrogen-enriched heather shoots. Voraciously feeding larvae and adults then defoliate the bushes, tipping the competitive balance between heather and grasses irrevocably.", "highlight": "Heather beetle population size, like that of many herbivorous insects, varies from year to year."}, "v206_p4": {"text": "W.E.B. Du Bois’ exhibit of African American history and culture at the 1900 Paris Exposition Universelle attracted the attention of a world of sociological scholarship whose value his work challenged. Du Bois believed that Spencerian sociologists failed in their attempts to gain greater understanding of human deeds because their work examined not deeds but theories and because they gathered data not to affect social progress but merely to theorize. In his exhibit, Du Bois sought to present cultural artifacts that would shift the focus of sociology from the construction of vast generalizations to the observation of particular, living individual elements of society and the working contributions of individual people to a vast functioning social structure.", "highlight": null}, "v10_p4": {"text": "Bat studies in Indiana between 1961 and 1993 recorded bat roost locations. All of the roosts of evening bats were in buildings. Consequently, the fact that all evening bats radio-tracked since 1993 have roosted in trees was notable. The building roosts may have been the result of spillover from large populations of evening bats in the woods along rivers, where, prior to 1993, scientific data were not collected. The building roosts may also indicate that this species had adapted well to human structures. However, the disappearance after 1993 of previously known roosts in buildings suggests that this adaptation became less successful. Big brown bat populations have been increasing in Indiana, and perhaps evening bats do not compete successfully with them for roosts in buildings.", "highlight": null}, "v198_p1": {"text": "Before feminist literary criticism emerged in the 1970s, the nineteenth-century United States writer Fanny Fern was regarded by most critics (when considered at all) as a prototype of weepy sentimentalism─a pious, insipid icon of conventional American culture. Feminist reclamations of Fern, by contrast, emphasize her non-sentimental qualities, particularly her sharply humorous social criticism. Most feminist scholars find it difficult to reconcile Fern’s sardonic social critiques with her effusive celebrations of many conventional values. Attempting to resolve this contradiction, Harris concludes that Fern employed flowery rhetoric strategically to disguise her subversive goals beneath apparent conventionality. However, Tompkins proposes an alternative view of sentimentality itself, suggesting that sentimental writing could serve radical, rather than only conservative, ends by swaying readers emotionally, moving them to embrace social change.", "highlight": "Attempting to resolve this contradiction, Harris concludes that Fern employed flowery rhetoric strategically to disguise her subversive goals beneath apparent conventionality."}, "v222_p13": {"text": "Virtually everyone who speaks Torvic lives in Torvia, a small country that takes pride in its unique culture. Since Torvia trades with many other countries, however, most people who live in Torvia speak several languages, and many languages are taught in Torvia's public schools. Nevertheless, from these facts it should not be inferred that most speakers of Torvic speak several languages, because _____.", "highlight": null}, "v20_p2": {"text": "Iridium, a hard, whitish metal similar to platinum, is extremely rare on Earth. Extremely high concentrations of iridium on Earth result from only two scenarios: massive volcanic eruptions that release iridium from deep within the Earth and meteorites that shower down on Earth from space. When scientists found concentrations of iridium 30 times higher than normal in rock stratum from 65 million years ago, they concluded that a massive meteor or comet hit the Earth and caused the massive extinction of the dinosaurs.", "highlight": null}, "v11_p2": {"text": "Availability and management of water greatly influenced human settlement in the Maya Lowlands, and much of Mayan social innovation was centered on storing excess water for times of need. In northern Yucatan, the permanent water table is sufficiently shallow that it can be accessed by natural wells known as cenotes. However, over much of the Maya Lowlands, the water table is too deep to have been available to the Maya. In response, they constructed artificial reservoirs to trap runoff. For example, Gallopin estimates that the reservoirs at Tikal (an ancient Mayan city) could have provided for the domestic needs of about 9,600 people for a period of 6 to 18 months. Even with elaborate water capture and management systems, the Maya were greatly dependent upon adequate rainfall over much of their empire and were thus susceptible to frequent or prolonged droughts that approached or exceeded the capacity of their reservoirs. In fact, evidence of droughts in the region based on studies of lake and shallow ocean sediments has led many researchers to suspect that climate was responsible for the Classic Maya collapse.", "highlight": null}, "v4_p1": {"text": "In 2018, the U.S. Congress passed the \"45Q legislation,\" which significantly increases corporate tax credits for various uses of CO₂ (carbon dioxide). The most controversial use is \"enhanced oil recovery.\" An oil company purchases CO₂, transports it by pipeline and injects it into depleted oil wells, pushing out extra oil it could not extract by conventional means. A climate change solution that entails producing more fossil fuels may sound Orwellian, and some environmental critics have attacked 45Q as just another fossil-fuel subsidy program in disguise. But enhanced oil recovery appears to reduce current emissions because the CO₂ typically captured from natural gas or ethanol refineries gets sequestered underground. Some environmentalists, such as Kurt Waltzer of the Clean Air Task Force, argue that turning carbon capture into an energy technology rather than an emission technology is the first step toward broad commercial adoption of CO₂ removal. It turns recaptured CO₂ into a product to be bought or sold rather than simply a cost to be endured.", "highlight": null}, "v204_p1": {"text": "What makes alien species so successful in their new habitats? They all share certain basic biological characteristics—opportunism, explosive population growth, mobility, and voraciousness—but these merely describe, rather than explain, their power. Classically, biologists have ascribed to invaders a robustness tempered by long stretches of competition with enemies. They are not necessarily dominant in their original habitats. When they find new territory, they escape competitors and predators and exploit their full evolutionary potential. Biologists have used similar arguments to explain the dramatic invasions of whole faunas and floras over the past million years. For example, marauding mammals from North America tempered by competition from other migrating mammals were suddenly unleashed on the south after the rise of the Isthmus of Panama.", "highlight": null}, "v198_p4": {"text": "The label “memoir” has been attached by authors and publishers to quite different kinds of writing over the past two centuries. Julie Rak’s genealogy of the term in her article \"Are Memoirs Autobiography?' highlights the term’s radical instability, pointing out that \"memoir\" has been used to refer both to first- and to third-person narrative; to private and public, unofficial and official, life writing. Notably, literary critics have often conceived “memoir” as a subgenre of “autobiography” and while the basis for this distinction has been somewhat inconstant, the distinction itself has not: “memoir” has been devalued as a minor and subliterary form while \"autobiography” has literary status. Recently, however, as interest in memoirs has grown, writers and publishers have outflanked critics: “memoir” is now the prestige term.", "highlight": null}, "v216_p3": {"text": "Demographic data for Ollene Province indicate that over the next ten years the number of teenagers will decline and the number of children under the age of ten will rise. Most parents whose children are under ten and who want childcare during evening hours hire a babysitter who comes to their home, and virtually all babysitters are teenagers. Therefore, parents who want childcare during evening hours will have an increasingly hard time finding an available babysitter.", "highlight": null}, "v12_p3": {"text": "After the identification of three of the main macronutrients that plants need to grow—nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium (N-P-K)—and the development of manufactured nitrogen fertilizer in the 1910s, agricultural soils began receiving large doses of N-P-K but little else. Early agronomists overlooked the importance of biological activity provided by the underground ecosystem of soil microbes, earthworms, and Mycorrhizal fungi. Chemical fertilizers such as N-P-K depress this activity, increasing plants' vulnerability to pests and diseases. They might also diminish crops' nutritional quality, which has declined substantially since the widespread adoption of chemical fertilizers. Some researchers attribute this decline to the condition of the soil; others cite the tendency of modern plant breeding to select for characteristics such as yield rather than nutritional quality.", "highlight": null}, "v6_p2": {"text": "In 431 B.C., several hundred cavalry soldiers received a state burial outside the gates of Athens. Archaeologists excavating at the location of these gates found the bones of hundreds of men that dated to the period of the funeral. There are other gravesites in the area; however, examination of the bones in question indicates that the men frequently rode horses, as would be true of cavalry soldiers. Therefore, the bones are probably those of the soldiers, since _____.", "highlight": null}, "v229_p1": {"text": "For many Irish American women in the nineteenth century, domesticity, in the sense of exclusive devotion to the home, was an unrealistic and unwelcome ideal. After 1850, many Irish immigrant women settled in New England's textile towns and constituted a large percentage of the workforce. They participated in boycotts, strikes, and other forms of economic protest. American-born Irish women embraced occupations like teaching as careers, and these women generally experienced significantly higher occupational mobility than Irish males in the United States. Women's wages were crucial to the economic health of Irish American households and helped support Irish families in the United States and Ireland. For such women, a life removed from the public world of wage labor and capitalist production was hardly a reality.", "highlight": null}, "v9_p1": {"text": "Calculating hydroelectric plants' environmental impact is not simple. Dam building requires steel and cement, the manufacture of which entails greenhouse gas emissions. Estimates for these emissions are relatively straightforward to make and show that the consequences are small compared to the benefits of generating greenhouse gas-free hydroelectric power. But more difficult-to-estimate greenhouse gas contributions occur during the plants' operation. The submerging of large areas behind dams results in the microbial decomposition of vegetation, which produces substantial quantities of methane—a potent greenhouse gas. Furthermore, eradicating vegetation eliminates the consumption of the greenhouse gas CO₂ by that vegetation. Estimating amounts of these gases is difficult, and amounts vary depending upon the specific location, terrain, and power intensity of the dam with its associated lake.", "highlight": "Estimates for these emissions are relatively straightforward to make and show that the consequences are small compared to the benefits of generating greenhouse gas-free hydroelectric power."}, "v18_p2": {"text": "Normally, seeds of Emmenanthe penduliflora stay dormant for years and germinate only when a fire burns through their habitat. Nitrogen dioxide in the smoke induces the seeds to germinate. Fires clear the brush, allowing germinating seeds to receive the sunlight they need to grow. The plants mature quickly, produce seeds, and then die. In areas with heavy automobile traffic, however, the seed germinates in the absence of fire, with automobile exhaust supplying the required nitrogen dioxide.", "highlight": null}, "v4_p3": {"text": "While export prices remained robust, British India's Tea Cess Committee (TCC) made only sporadic, small-scale attempts to create demand for tea in India by giving away pre-brewed cups in selected locations and selling small packets of leaf fragments. Still, by 1930 only a fraction of the Indian population had tasted tea, and more than 90 percent of the crop was exported. The Great Depression decisively changed the picture, however. International tea prices plunged, and by 1935 growers faced an unsold surplus of more than a hundred million pounds. The prospect of a huge \"uninitiated\" market suddenly seemed appealing, and the TCC, reorganized as the Indian Tea Market Expansion Board (ITMEB) and provided with an expanded budget, began the largest marketing campaign in Indian history.", "highlight": null}, "v24_p2": {"text": "In Stanton the average number of people injured per automobile accident is consistently higher for accidents involving a taxicab than for those not involving a taxicab. Although all Stanton taxicabs are equipped with passenger seat belts, taxicab drivers report that passengers tend not to use them. It is likely, therefore, that if taxicab passengers were required to use seat belts, the number of people injured per accident would soon be no higher for taxicabs than for other automobiles.", "highlight": null}, "v212_p1": {"text": "African American soul music's commercial influence gradually declined during the early 1970s as newer styles such as funk and disco began to dominate the airwaves and as other, larger changes occurred within the American music industry. After the Second World War, African American popular music had largely been the province of independent record labels. By the 1970s, though, these labels were either going out of business or, to an increasing degree, coming under the control of major corporations. This shift had dire consequences for the production of soul music. Whereas independent labels had achieved success through a skillful balance of commercial and artistic considerations, the emphasis now became fixed upon marketing a product, resulting in the more individualized voices in African American popular music being quelled.", "highlight": null}, "v210_p4": {"text": "The traditional picture of planet formation starts with small grains that collide and build into boulders, then larger and larger objects. If this is correct, the Kuiper Belt, an outer region of the solar system that exists beyond the planets, should hold leftover planetary building blocks. But that idea is undermined by Jupiter’s moon Europa. One would expect that over millions of years Europa could have been repeatedly impacted by small comets formed from leftover planetary material in the Kuiper Belt. In fact, Europa’s surface reveals very few small comet impact craters. Perhaps the comets disappear when they enter the inner solar system and are heated by the Sun. Or perhaps the Kuiper Belt contains no leftover planetary material from which comets could have formed.", "highlight": "One would expect that over millions of years Europa could have been repeatedly impacted by small comets formed from leftover planetary material in the Kuiper Belt."}, "v14_p2": {"text": "Mayor: Vehicle exhaust produces dangerously high ozone levels in our city in hot, humid weather. As an incentive for people to commute by bus rather than by car, special free commuter buses will be scheduled on hot, humid days. Since a bus can carry about 40 people but produces only about 20 times as much exhaust as a car, ozone levels will be lower as long as the buses are more than half full.", "highlight": null}, "v219_p4": {"text": "Because coal contains toxic materials such as arsenic and lead, and its use contributes to air pollution and acid rain, one might therefore conclude that no good case could be made for burning it for fuel. But that depends on where one is starting from. Switching to coal from firewood is beneficial for both the environment and the health of the individual. Firewood use results in deforestation, loss of ecosystems, and degradation of soil quality. Wood fires are also sooty, and their particulates contribute to global warming by decreasing the reflectivity of snowfields. Finally, firewood is generally burned in homes with poor ventilation and poses a greater health risk to the individuals than they would experience from a coal-fired utility that provides electricity to their homes.", "highlight": null}, "v22_p3": {"text": "Sport fishers introduced the zander, a type of perch, to Britain's rivers and canals in the 1970s. Because zander eat large numbers of smaller fish, they have had a devastating effect on native fish populations. To protect the native fish, a government program removed a significant proportion of the zander from Britain's waterways last year. Surprisingly, this year the loss of native fish to zander has been greater than before.", "highlight": null}, "v10_p2": {"text": "Belnovia's government provides health care to all its citizens. Five years ago, with costs incurred from smoking-related health problems accounting for 5 percent of annual government expenditures, Belnovia's health agency initiated a nationwide antismoking campaign. Although the campaign succeeded in reducing the number of smokers in Belnovia substantially, it clearly failed to reduce the annual costs incurred from smoking-related health problems, since these costs currently account for 6 percent of annual government expenditures.", "highlight": null}, "v22_p4": {"text": "Meltzoff and Moore reported experiments showing that human newborns possess the ability to imitate certain facial expressions, such as a protruding tongue or an open mouth. Yet numerous researchers challenge Meltzoff's interpretation that such neonatal imitation is the origin of later imitation, which appears at approximately eight to twelve months of age. These researchers point out that the neonatal imitative response disappears or is lessened at approximately two months. Moreover, since in follow-up studies only one type of imitative response toward a facial expression (that is, tongue protrusion) was observed, some researchers assert that neonatal imitation is not imitation at all but may simply be a form of exploratory behavior in response to interesting stimuli.", "highlight": null}, "v17_p1": {"text": "Biologists generally agree that birds and dinosaurs are somehow related to one another. The agreement ends there. Hypotheses regarding dinosaurian and avian evolution are unusually diverse—and often at odds with one another. Confusion consequently reigns over a broad spectrum of unanswered questions dealing with avian origins and the biology of dinosaurs and early birds. This confusion has been exacerbated by a paucity of serious attempts to synthesize and evaluate available data on the details of avian and dinosaurian evolution. Too often, the job of summarizing current knowledge of these subjects has fallen to well-meaning but naïve lay authors or reporters. Consequently, both the public and the scientific community have often been misled by widespread dissemination of sensational but weakly founded hypotheses.", "highlight": "Consequently, both the public and the scientific community have often been misled by widespread dissemination of sensational but weakly founded hypotheses."}, "v209_p2": {"text": "\"Flight-Initiation Distance\" (FID) is the distance at which birds flee from an approaching human. Birds adjust their FIDs in relation to a range of factors, including body mass, encounter rates with stimuli, and aspects of the stimulus such as starting distance (the distance at which a human approach begins), stimulus type (e.g., vehicle or walker), proximity to refuge, directness and speed of approach. The ability to discriminate between stimuli within species demonstrates that cognition is involved in the specifics of bird escape, and the substantial cognitive ability of at least some birds has recently been highlighted. Accurate judgment of risk, and appropriate mediation of response, is likely to be critical for the survival of many birds that encounter potentially threatening stimuli such as humans in increasing numbers and places. The \"cognitive buffer\" hypothesis suggests larger-brained birds will be better able to adapt to novel environmental conditions, such as those created by anthropogenic landscape change. In theory, these birds may be able to more accurately judge risk when presented with a stimulus, or be able to learn (habituate or sensitize) to adjust responses appropriately based on their previous experience. If so, one would predict that there would be a negative association between FID and brain size within and across species.", "highlight": null}, "v200_p3": {"text": "The damage that trucks do to highways escalates dramatically with the weight borne per axle. New regulations increase the maximum permitted vehicle weight; these regulations will therefore allow onto the highway trucks capable of doing even more damage than those currently permitted.", "highlight": null}, "v20_p1": {"text": "There is mounting evidence that the frequency and magnitude of landsliding is changing in many parts of the world in response to climate change. This is not surprising, given that precipitation is one of the two external triggering mechanisms—the other being seismic activity—involved in the formation of landslides. Evidence from the past clearly indicates that cycles of elevated landslide activity have been followed by cycles of low activity, and that these are correlated with climate fluctuations over a variety of timescales.\n\nWhat sets current changes in landslide activity apart is the likely influence of anthropogenic (i.e., human-caused) factors, either acting alone or in concert with climate, which can further modify the process of landsliding and the nature of ecosystem responses. Among these factors, deforestation and land-use change have the potential to influence the frequency and magnitude of landsliding because of their direct effects on vegetation attributes that influence slope stability. The extent and conditions under which mountain ecosystems are resilient to these changes—that is, the amount of disturbance they can absorb before changing into states with different structure and function—are not known. Addressing this issue is crucial for the long-term conservation of mountainscapes.", "highlight": null}, "v227_p2": {"text": "In the late 1920s, the noted writer Lu Xun, who was also the primary figure behind the modern Chinese woodcut movement, began to introduce modern Western woodcuts into China. Lu Xun believed that Western artists' emphasis on linearity and sharp black-and-white contrasts gave their art a distinctly serious quality, very different from the largely decorative nature of the traditional, richly colored Chinese woodcut. But he also believed that the most important ingredient in the Western woodcut was its close link to the broader society, an element missing in the Chinese woodcut tradition. It is true that Lu Xun was deeply impressed by the Western artists’ techniques, which enabled them to evoke human emotions through gestures and facial expressions, but his decision to introduce their works was prompted more by his admiration of the works' role in the struggle for social and political justice than by his interest in technique and craftsmanship. Lu Xun realized that woodcuts could do more than evoke emotions; they could be used as an educational tool to reshape public consciousness.", "highlight": "It is true that Lu Xun was deeply impressed by the Western artists’ techniques, which enabled them to evoke human emotions through gestures and facial expressions, but his decision to introduce their works was prompted more by his admiration of the works' role in the struggle for social and political justice than by his interest in technique and craftsmanship."}, "v28_p2": {"text": "A law has been proposed requiring the cargo boxes of trucks carrying gravel to be covered by a tarpaulin, because vehicles driving close behind open-topped gravel trucks can be damaged by gravel flying off these trucks. The law is unlikely to substantially reduce such damage, however: flying gravel is much less likely to come from the cargo box itself than from the grooves of the tires, in which gravel can become wedged during loading.", "highlight": null}, "v206_p3": {"text": "Tropical forests typically have many more species of plants and animals than do temperate forests of comparable size. During the Ice Age, forests in temperate regions were destroyed, while those in the tropics were not. Accordingly, one proposed explanation of this difference in the number of species is that tropical forests typically had a much longer period than temperate forests in which different species could take hold.", "highlight": null}, "v207_p1": {"text": "Female Australian Dunatothrips (small, sap-sucking insects) create tent-like structures on the surface of leaves to protect themselves and their eggs and larvae from desiccation in the arid Australian climate. Bono and Crespi compared survival and reproduction of thrips that founded structures alone with those in groups of two or more individuals. They found that although per capita egg production fell with increasing group size, foundresses were more likely to survive and lay eggs in groups than when alone. Several studies of other species of nest-building insects have concluded that foundress associations are beneficial to all parties. It is likely that the relative success of groups is at least in part accounted for by a reduction of energy use in the modification of a shared nest.", "highlight": null}, "v232_p3": {"text": "Some people deplore the fact that many of the world's major rivers, such as the Yellow River, the Colorado, and the Nile, now run dry before reaching the sea. The primary reason these rivers run dry is that their water is diverted for irrigation of food crops. The world's increasing population requires an increasing food supply. Thus, as a response to this need, at least, the draining of the major rivers is beneficial.", "highlight": null}, "v3_p2": {"text": "One characteristic of terrestrial cratering is the presence of doublet craters: 3 of the 28 large impact craters on Earth (greater than 20 kilometers diameter) have partner craters. For example, the Kamensk crater in Russia, 25 kilometers in diameter, is partnered by the Gusev crater, 3 kilometers wide and of identical age. Since such doublets form when two well-separated asteroids impact Earth nearly simultaneously, their relatively frequent occurrence serves as evidence for the existence of a substantial population of co-orbiting asteroids.\n\nAre other rocky planets subject to impacts from co-orbiting asteroids? Venus is a promising planet to search for doublets because its surface is young, erosion is nearly nonexistent, and its crater population is significantly larger than Earth's, but not so large that there is a high probability of chance associations. Researchers found that the proportion of doublet craters on Venus is significantly smaller than on Earth. However, Venus' denser atmosphere may screen out the smaller member of some asteroid pairs. If Earth had a similar screening effect, only one of its three known doublets would have formed, making the proportion of doublet craters on Earth (3.6%) identical to Venus' (2.2%) within uncertainties. The researchers concluded that co-orbiting asteroids must be common among both the near-Earth and near-Venus asteroid populations.", "highlight": null}}, "tests": [{"set": 1, "sections": [[{"id": "v11_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "As companies dealing in satellite imagery begin to _____ their data products diurnally, people will soon be able to see huge swaths of the planet change daily.", "choices": ["encrypt", "refine", "update", "repurpose", "discount"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: diurnally(매일) → 결과절 'see huge swaths of the planet change daily'.\n매일 변화를 볼 수 있으려면 회사가 데이터를 매일 '새로 고쳐야' 한다.\n빈칸 = 데이터를 최신 상태로 바꾸다.\nupdate(갱신하다)가 정확히 맞는다.\n정답: C (update)", "trap": "refine(정제하다)도 그럴듯하지만, 다듬는다고 해서 '매일 변화'를 보게 되는 것은 아니다. 핵심은 새 데이터로 바꾸는 것.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"diurnally": "매일", "encrypt": "암호화하다", "refine": "정제하다, 다듬다", "update": "갱신하다, 최신화하다", "repurpose": "다른 용도로 바꾸다", "discount": "할인하다; 무시하다"}, "src": "verbal11 Q1"}, {"id": "v199_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The psychologist's new findings present the discipline with a (i) _____: her results pose a problem for the standard theory, although the alternative theories she proposes are (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["predicament", "paradigm", "prototype"], ["unconvincing", "persuasive", "versatile"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 (i)을 설명한다: 기존 이론에 문제를 제기하는데, although 뒤 대안 이론은 (ii).\n(i) 기존 이론도 흔들리고 대안도 시원찮은 '곤란한 상황' → predicament(곤경).\n(ii) although가 '문제 제기'와 대조 → 대안 이론도 해결책이 못 된다 = 부정 → unconvincing.\n정답: A (predicament), D (unconvincing)", "trap": "paradigm은 '이론 틀'이라 psychology 문맥에 어울려 보이지만, 콜론 뒤의 '딜레마' 구조를 설명하지 못한다. persuasive를 고르면 곤경이 사라진다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"predicament": "곤경, 궁지", "paradigm": "패러다임, 이론적 틀", "prototype": "원형, 시제품", "unconvincing": "설득력 없는", "persuasive": "설득력 있는", "versatile": "다재다능한, 다용도의"}, "src": "verbal199 Q2 · 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v213_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Give a computer (i) _____ task, winning at chess, say, or predicting the weather, and the machine beats humans nearly every time. Yet when problems are (ii) _____, or require combining varied sources of information, computers are (iii) _____ human intelligence.", "choices": null, "columns": [["a well-defined", "a random", "an open-ended"], ["nuanced", "inconsequential", "solvable"], ["not matching", "unyielding", "able to dwarf"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 예시 'winning at chess, predicting the weather' = 규칙·목표가 명확한 과제 → a well-defined.\n(ii) Yet으로 대조 + 'or require combining varied sources' 와 병렬 → 명확하지 않고 미묘한 문제 → nuanced.\n(iii) 앞 문장은 컴퓨터가 이김 → Yet 뒤에선 인간에 못 미친다 → not matching.\n정답: A (a well-defined), D (nuanced), G (not matching)", "trap": "(i)에서 an open-ended를 고르면 (ii)와의 대조가 무너진다. (iii)의 able to dwarf는 Yet 대조를 무시한 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"a well-defined": "명확히 정의된", "a random": "무작위의", "an open-ended": "열린, 정해진 답이 없는", "nuanced": "미묘한 차이가 있는", "inconsequential": "사소한, 중요하지 않은", "solvable": "풀 수 있는", "not matching": "~에 못 미치는", "unyielding": "굴하지 않는, 단호한", "able to dwarf": "~를 왜소하게 만들 수 있는(압도하는)"}, "src": "verbal213 Q3 · 25/4, 22/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v35_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage supplies information for answering which of the following questions?", "choices": ["Do invertebrate predators with full mobility address nutrient needs in the same fashion as sit-and-wait invertebrate predators with limited mobility?", "Why would there be a considerable variation in nutrient composition within prey of a given species?", "Is all of the nutrient content of invertebrate prey contained in the dry mass?", "What would a wolf spider do if a fly it was eating contained a higher proportion of a certain nutrient than was present in the spider’s recent prey?", "How is a wolf spider able to determine that some prey it is eating contains a higher proportion of a nutrient that was deficient in the previous prey?"], "columns": null, "pid": "v35_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 마지막 문장 'The wolf spider ... regulate nutrient intake by extracting more dry mass from a prey item if it contains a higher proportion of a nutrient that was deficient in the previous prey.'\nD는 '이전 먹이보다 특정 영양소 비율이 높은 먹이를 먹으면 늑대거미는 어떻게 하나?'를 묻고, 지문은 '더 많은 dry mass를 추출한다'로 답해 준다.\nA(이동성 높은 포식자 비교), B(종 내 변이의 이유), C(영양소가 모두 dry mass에 있는지), E(어떻게 감지하는지)는 지문에 정보 없음.\n정답: D", "trap": "E가 가장 헷갈린다. 지문은 거미가 '무엇을 하는지'만 말하고 '어떻게 알아내는지(메커니즘)'는 말하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sit-and-wait predator": "매복형 포식자", "invertebrate": "무척추동물", "dry mass": "건조 질량", "deficient": "부족한, 결핍된"}, "src": "verbal35 Q4"}, {"id": "v35_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the organization of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["A phenomenon is described, and an interpretation is offered.", "A claim is made, and the corroborating evidence is evaluated.", "A hypothesis is presented and undermined by recent findings.", "A contrast is noted and shown to be specious based on recent findings.", "A series of assumptions is presented and shown to be based on sound reasoning."], "columns": null, "pid": "v35_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문장: 포식자는 영양 균형을 맞추지 않는다고 '전통적으로 여겨져 왔다' → 가설(hypothesis) 제시.\nBut 이후: 먹이의 영양 구성 변이가 크다, Greenstone 제안, Jensen 등 실험, 늑대거미 사례 → 최근 연구가 그 가설을 무너뜨림.\n→ '가설 제시 + 최근 발견으로 약화' = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "D가 함정. 'Unlike herbivores and omnivores'라는 대조가 나오긴 하지만 그 대조는 주변적인 배경일 뿐, 지문의 축은 '전통적 가정'과 그 반박이다. B는 증거를 '평가'하지 않고, E는 방향이 반대.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"specious": "그럴듯하지만 틀린", "corroborating": "확증하는, 뒷받침하는", "undermine": "약화시키다", "nutrient composition": "영양 구성"}, "src": "verbal35 Q5"}, {"id": "v239_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "It is troubling that blogs, which may be among the least reliable sources of information in human history, occupy such _____ positions in Internet search engine results.", "choices": ["enviable", "conspicuous", "suspect", "dubious", "controversial", "prominent"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: It is troubling that 신뢰도가 가장 낮은 블로그가 검색 결과에서 'such ___ positions'를 차지한다.\n문제가 되는 이유 = 눈에 잘 띄는, 상위의 위치에 있기 때문.\n빈칸 = '두드러진, 눈에 띄는'.\nconspicuous와 prominent가 같은 뜻의 짝.\n정답: B (conspicuous), F (prominent)", "trap": "suspect/dubious는 '수상한'으로 짝을 이루지만, 의심스러운 것은 블로그(정보)이지 '위치'가 아니다. enviable도 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"enviable": "부러운, 탐나는", "conspicuous": "눈에 잘 띄는", "suspect": "의심스러운", "dubious": "의심스러운, 미심쩍은", "controversial": "논란이 많은", "prominent": "두드러진, 눈에 띄는"}, "src": "verbal239 Q7 · 25/7, 25/6, 22/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v201_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Human hearing is remarkably _____: an attentive listener knows if a band's drummer is as little as one thousandths of a second late on the beat.", "choices": ["sophisticated", "adaptable", "independent", "sensitive", "versatile", "discerning"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 빈칸의 예시: 드러머가 1/1000초만 늦어도 알아챈다.\n아주 작은 차이를 감지 = '예민한, 식별력이 뛰어난'.\nsensitive와 discerning이 짝.\n정답: D (sensitive), F (discerning)", "trap": "sophisticated(정교한)도 그럴듯하지만 '미세한 차이를 감지한다'는 핵심을 직접 표현하지 못하고 짝도 없다. adaptable/versatile은 '적응력'으로 다른 짝이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sophisticated": "정교한, 세련된", "adaptable": "적응력 있는", "independent": "독립적인", "sensitive": "민감한, 예민한", "versatile": "다재다능한, 다용도의", "discerning": "식별력 있는, 안목 있는"}, "src": "verbal201 Q8 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v27_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Three of the nation's largest airlines could be operating under bankruptcy protection in coming weeks, analysts say, the latest sign of the industry's _____ as it lurches through a historic transformation.", "choices": ["upheaval", "exorbitance", "affluence", "peril", "convulsion", "opulence"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 대형 항공사 3곳이 파산 보호 신청 가능 + 'lurches through a historic transformation'(역사적 변혁 속에서 휘청거림).\n빈칸 = 업계의 '격변, 대혼란'.\nupheaval과 convulsion이 짝.\n정답: A (upheaval), E (convulsion)", "trap": "peril(위험)도 파산과 어울리지만 'transformation'(변화)과의 연결이 약하고 짝이 없다. affluence/opulence는 '부유함'으로 짝은 있으나 문맥과 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"upheaval": "격변, 대변동", "convulsion": "격동, 경련", "exorbitance": "터무니없음, 과도함", "affluence": "부유함", "peril": "위험", "opulence": "호화로움, 풍요"}, "src": "verbal27 Q9"}, {"id": "v35_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although in his new book he tends to repeat himself like a _____ uncle, McHughen makes a persuasive case for the safety of thinking with genes to create new foods.", "choices": ["taciturn", "reserved", "prototypical", "cantankerous", "loquacious", "garrulous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "EF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'tends to repeat himself like a ___ uncle'.\n같은 말을 반복하는 삼촌 = 말이 많은 삼촌.\nAlthough 뒤에 '그래도 설득력 있는 주장을 한다'가 대조로 나온다.\nloquacious와 garrulous가 '수다스러운' 짝.\n정답: E (loquacious), F (garrulous)", "trap": "taciturn/reserved는 '과묵한'으로 짝은 맞지만 반복해서 말하는 것과 정반대. cantankerous(심술궂은)는 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"taciturn": "말수가 적은", "reserved": "내성적인, 말을 아끼는", "prototypical": "전형적인", "cantankerous": "심술궂은, 툭하면 시비거는", "loquacious": "말이 많은", "garrulous": "수다스러운"}, "src": "verbal35 Q6"}, {"id": "v213_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with", "choices": ["using specific examples to illustrate certain shortcomings in historians' traditional approach to a particular historical period", "outlining the issues underlying a debate among scholars about a particular historical period", "considering the work of a particular scholar on a certain subject in contrast to other work on the same subject", "identifying some of the most important influences on a particular historian's recent work", "pointing out certain inconsistencies in a recent work about a particular historical period"], "columns": null, "pid": "v213_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문 흐름: Jeffrey의 신간 소개 → 'While scholars have already pointed out...' 기존 학자들의 설명 → 'Jeffrey disputes certain aspects of the traditional account' → 구체적 반박 2가지.\n즉 한 학자(Jeffrey)의 연구를 같은 주제에 대한 다른(전통적) 연구와 대비해서 다룬다.\n정답: C", "trap": "A가 함정. 전통적 설명의 '단점'을 지적하는 주체는 저자가 아니라 Jeffrey이고, 지문의 중심은 Jeffrey의 책이다. B는 학자 간 '논쟁의 쟁점'을 개괄하는 글이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inception": "시작, 개시", "relegate": "(낮은 지위로) 밀어내다", "marginalize": "주변화하다, 소외시키다", "grassroots": "풀뿌리의, 일반 대중의"}, "src": "verbal213 Q10 · 25/4, 25/1, 24/12, 24/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v213_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is cited by the \"scholars\" as an example of the important work done by early abolitionist women?", "choices": ["The organization of fund-raising fairs", "The campaign against the Fugitive Slave Law", "The integration of the abolitionist movement", "The circulation of antislavery petitions", "The formation of African American abolitionist societies"], "columns": null, "pid": "v213_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'While scholars have already pointed out the importance of women's work in early abolitionist circles, especially in spreading a grassroots antislavery message through the constant and tireless circulation of petitions'.\n학자들이 예로 든 것 = 청원서 회람.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(모금 박람회)는 Jeffrey가 '여성의 참여가 주변화되지 않았다'는 근거로 든 것이지 기존 scholars의 예가 아니다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": "scholars", "glosses": {"abolitionist": "노예제 폐지론자", "petition": "청원서", "circulation": "회람, 유통"}, "src": "verbal213 Q11 · 25/4, 25/1, 24/12, 24/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v213_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions the \"fund-raising fairs of the 1840s\" primarily in order to", "choices": ["provide an example of the kind of grassroots work cited by scholars in support of their claim that women played an important role in early abolitionist circles", "give an example of evidence used by Jeffrey to support her challenge to the claim that women's participation in the abolitionist movement became marginalized at the end of the 1830s", "support Jeffrey's claim that in the decades preceding the Civil War, African American women's abolitionist groups were often more effective than were integrated abolitionist groups", "show how a split in the abolitionist movement into political and nonpolitical factions resulted in the marginalization of women's participation", "make a comparison between the kinds of abolitionist activities favored by integrated abolitionist groups and those favored by African American women's abolitionist groups"], "columns": null, "pid": "v213_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거 문맥: 'Jeffrey does not accept the view that women's participation became marginalized as a result. She demonstrates that women found numerous ways to persist effectively in the cause, such as by organizing the antislavery fund-raising fairs of the 1840s.'\n1830년대 말 분열 후 여성 참여가 주변화되었다는 주장에 Jeffrey가 반박하며 든 증거 예시.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 '기존 학자들'의 근거로 착각하게 만든다. 모금 박람회는 Jeffrey의 반박 근거다. C는 다음 문장(흑인 여성 단체) 내용과 섞은 오답.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "fund-raising fairs of the 1840s", "glosses": {"faction": "분파, 파벌", "marginalized": "주변화된", "persist": "끈질기게 지속하다"}, "src": "verbal213 Q12 · 25/4, 25/1, 24/12, 24/4 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v224_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Those who had once been his _____ within the bureaucracy, responsive to his every string-pulling maneuver, were now distressingly prone to independent judgment, and amicable enough but with an infuriating, vaguely superior manner.", "choices": ["colleagues", "friends", "mentors", "marionettes", "proteges"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'responsive to his every string-pulling maneuver'(그가 줄을 당기는 대로 반응하던).\n줄 조종(string-pulling)에 반응하는 존재 = 꼭두각시.\n'were now ... prone to independent judgment'와 대조 → 예전엔 독립성 없던 사람들.\n정답: D (marionettes)", "trap": "proteges(제자, 피후견인)도 그럴듯하지만 '줄을 당기면 움직인다'는 비유와 '독립적 판단'과의 대조를 정확히 살리는 것은 marionettes.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"colleagues": "동료", "friends": "친구", "mentors": "멘토, 조언자", "marionettes": "꼭두각시 인형(조종당하는 사람)", "proteges": "피후견인, 제자"}, "src": "verbal224 Q1 · 25년 7월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v218_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Though acknowledging the unstated assumptions that commentators on her paper had identified, the geologist pointed out that such assumptions were (i) _____ the context of her research, and therefore their existence did not (ii) _____ her conclusions.", "choices": null, "columns": [["antithetical to", "legitimate within", "implausible in"], ["prefigure", "validate", "impede"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: Though 가정이 있음을 인정하면서도 → 그 가정들은 (i)했고, therefore 그 존재가 결론을 (ii)하지 않는다.\n(i) 지질학자가 자기 연구를 방어하는 문맥 → 가정이 연구 맥락에서 '정당하다' → legitimate within.\n(ii) 정당한 가정이므로 결론을 '방해/훼손하지' 않는다 → impede.\n정답: B (legitimate within), F (impede)", "trap": "(ii)의 validate는 'did not validate'가 되어 자기 결론을 깎아내리는 말이 된다. 방어하는 흐름과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"antithetical to": "~와 정반대인", "legitimate within": "~안에서 정당한", "implausible in": "~에서 믿기 어려운", "prefigure": "예시하다, 미리 보여주다", "validate": "입증하다, 타당성을 확인하다", "impede": "방해하다, 저해하다"}, "src": "verbal218 Q3 · 25/5, 25/4, 23/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v2_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Defying expectation, the electorate seems poised to (i) _____ a number of political tenets so (ii) _____ that they are often paraded as fact.", "choices": null, "columns": [["propound", "reject", "uphold"], ["entrenched", "intricate", "tenuous"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Defying expectation(예상을 깨고) + 'so ___ that they are often paraded as fact'.\n(ii) 사실처럼 내세워질 정도로 = 깊이 뿌리박힌 → entrenched.\n(i) 그렇게 확고한 신조를 예상을 깨고 → 거부하다 → reject.\n정답: B (reject), D (entrenched)", "trap": "uphold(지지하다)를 고르면 'Defying expectation'과 맞지 않는다. 확고한 신조를 지지하는 것은 예상대로다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"electorate": "유권자", "propound": "제기하다, 제안하다", "reject": "거부하다", "uphold": "지지하다, 유지하다", "entrenched": "확고히 자리 잡은", "intricate": "복잡한", "tenuous": "빈약한, 미약한"}, "src": "verbal2 Q3"}, {"id": "v236_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "A (i) _____ assumption of the model is that (ii) _____ the living standards of people living adjacent to a protected area will necessarily enhance conservation within the protected area. Studies of conservation attitudes of people in South Africa and Tanzania have found a positive correlation between affluence and conservation attitudes, but it is unlikely that an improvement in the living standards of communities near protected areas will inevitably (iii) _____ the long-term viability of many species within the protected areas.", "choices": null, "columns": [["misguided", "conservative", "compelling"], ["raising", "discounting", "assessing"], ["increase", "inhibit", "prevent"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(iii) 먼저: 'it is unlikely that an improvement in living standards will inevitably ___ the long-term viability' → 생활 수준 향상이 보존을 반드시 '높이는' 것은 아니다 → increase.\n(ii) 모델의 가정 = 인근 주민의 생활 수준을 '높이면' 보존이 강화된다 → raising.\n(i) 저자는 그 가정이 성립하지 않는다고 봄 → misguided(잘못된).\n정답: A (misguided), D (raising), G (increase)", "trap": "(i) compelling은 'positive correlation' 연구에 끌려 고르기 쉽지만, but 이후 저자는 그 가정을 부정한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"misguided": "잘못 판단된", "conservative": "보수적인", "compelling": "설득력 있는", "raising": "높이는", "discounting": "무시하는, 할인하는", "assessing": "평가하는", "increase": "증가시키다", "inhibit": "억제하다", "prevent": "막다"}, "src": "verbal236 Q3 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that the metropolitan critics who praised Tutuola's book would most likely agree with which of the following claims about literature?", "choices": ["Works that lack apparent sophistication might nevertheless have artistic value.", "Poor writing is never acceptable in a literary work, even one presented as naïve art.", "One can only fully appreciate a work of literature that is produced within a culture that one understands thoroughly.", "Nonliterary agendas often hamper the production of great literature.", "The value of a given literary work is mostly determined by the rhetorical skills of the author."], "columns": null, "pid": "v220_p14", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 서구 비평가들은 'dwelt less on his rhetorical skills and more on the text as an exemplar of naïve art' 하면서도 'enchanted by the book'.\n즉 문장력(세련됨)이 부족해 보여도 '소박한 예술'로서 가치가 있다고 봄.\n→ A 'Works that lack apparent sophistication might nevertheless have artistic value.'\n정답: A", "trap": "E는 반대: 그들은 수사적 기술(rhetorical skills)에 덜 주목했다. B는 서아프리카 비평가의 입장에 가깝다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exemplar": "본보기, 전형", "naïve art": "소박파 예술", "metropolitan": "(식민) 본국의, 대도시의", "exoticism": "이국 취향"}, "src": "verbal220 Q14 · 25/11, 25/8, 24/9, 24/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author cites “Akinjogbin” in order to", "choices": ["challenge a claim made by some west African literary critics", "illustrate some critics' opinions about the rhetorical style of Tutuola's book", "introduce an alternative explanation for the response to Tutuola's book", "articulate an objection to the positive critical response to Tutuola's book", "defend the promotion of Tutuola's book as an example of naive art"], "columns": null, "pid": "v220_p14", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Many protested against what they saw as a metropolitan celebration of exoticism. For example, Adeagbo Akinjogbin attributed the novel's success in the West to ignorance...'\nFor example → 서아프리카 비평가들이 서구의 호평에 반대했다는 앞 문장의 예시.\n→ 긍정적 비평 반응에 대한 반대를 표현.\n정답: D", "trap": "C가 함정. Akinjogbin은 서구 성공의 원인(무지)을 제시하지만, 이는 '대안적 설명'을 새로 소개하는 것이 아니라 반대 입장의 예시다. B는 문체에 대한 의견이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Adeagbo Akinjogbin", "glosses": {"attribute A to B": "A를 B 탓으로 돌리다", "articulate": "명확히 표현하다", "stereotyping": "고정관념화"}, "src": "verbal220 Q15 · 25/11, 25/8, 24/9, 24/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v6_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following appears to ensure the objectivity of Levitt's photographs?", "choices": ["She took photographs in public places rather than in a studio.", "She was not personally acquainted with the subjects of her photographs.", "She did not arrange the scenes or pose the subjects she photographed.", "She avoided using classical principles of composition.", "She was guided by her subjects' preoccupations rather than by her own."], "columns": null, "pid": "v6_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Her off-the-cuff aesthetic seemingly guarantees objectivity, since she was recording street scenes she happened upon'.\n우연히 마주친 장면을 기록 = 장면을 연출하거나 포즈를 취하게 하지 않음.\n또 'Levitt's subjects seem caught unawares'도 뒷받침.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(스튜디오가 아닌 공공장소)는 거리 사진의 특징이지만, 객관성을 보장하는 이유는 '장소'가 아니라 '연출하지 않음'이다. B(개인적 친분)는 언급 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"off-the-cuff": "즉흥적인", "candid": "꾸밈없는, 자연스러운", "caught unawares": "무방비 상태로 포착된", "objectivity": "객관성"}, "src": "verbal6 Q5"}, {"id": "v6_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage asserts which of the following about Evans' portrait photographs?", "choices": ["Evans' photographs indicate a conscious rejection of the approaches associated with street photography.", "The subjects in an Evans' photograph become collaborators in the portrait's creation.", "Evans' photographic portraits usually reveal more about Evans than they do about his subjects.", "Evans' static, classically composed portraits reveal Evans' preoccupation with maintaining an appearance of objectivity.", "Evans' static, classically composed portraits reveal little about his distinctive way of seeing."], "columns": null, "pid": "v6_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Whereas Evans' subjects look directly into the camera, so that photographer and subject conspire in the making of a portrait'.\n또 'Unlike Evans' images, Levitt's are ... without the conscious participation of their subjects' → Evans는 피사체의 의식적 참여가 있다.\nconspire(공모하다) = collaborators(협력자).\n정답: B", "trap": "C는 Levitt에 대한 설명(작가 자신을 더 드러냄)을 Evans에게 뒤바꾼 오답. D/E는 지문에 없는 추론.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"conspire": "공모하다, 함께 작용하다", "static": "정적인", "classically composed": "고전적으로 구성된"}, "src": "verbal6 Q6"}, {"id": "v6_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about street photography?", "choices": ["It characteristically depicts groups of people rather than individual subjects.", "It tends to depict a narrow and repetitious range of subject matter.", "It creates the impression of spontaneity but often actually involves scenes contrived by the photographer.", "Its early practitioners were not accorded much recognition for their aesthetic achievements.", "It had not been named as such when Levitt began practicing this kind of photography."], "columns": null, "pid": "v6_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'As a \"street\" photographer, before the term's invention, Levitt...'\nLevitt이 활동할 때는 'street photography'라는 용어가 아직 만들어지지 않았다.\n정답: E", "trap": "C는 지문의 '역설'을 오해한 오답. 주관적이라는 것은 작가의 관심사가 반영된다는 뜻이지 장면을 연출(contrived)했다는 뜻이 아니다. B는 Levitt 개인의 반복을 거리 사진 전체로 일반화.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"contrived": "인위적으로 꾸민", "practitioner": "실천가, 종사자", "accord": "부여하다"}, "src": "verbal6 Q7"}, {"id": "v14_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "By eating tiny organisms and incorporating their prey's nutrients into their own bodies, large insects become \"nutrient packages\" for larger insectivores for whom the pursuit of tiny organisms would be _____.", "choices": ["unwieldy", "insalubrious", "unremunerative", "unnecessary", "inopportune", "unprofitable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 큰 곤충이 작은 생물을 먹고 '영양 꾸러미'가 됨 → 더 큰 식충동물에게는 작은 생물을 직접 쫓는 것이 ___.\n작은 먹이를 쫓는 데 드는 노력에 비해 얻는 영양이 적다 = '수지가 안 맞는'.\nunremunerative와 unprofitable이 짝.\n정답: C (unremunerative), F (unprofitable)", "trap": "unwieldy(다루기 힘든)나 unnecessary(불필요한)도 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없다. 핵심은 '노력 대비 이득이 없다'는 경제적 의미.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"insalubrious": "건강에 해로운", "unwieldy": "다루기 힘든, 거추장스러운", "unremunerative": "보수가 없는, 수지가 안 맞는", "unnecessary": "불필요한", "inopportune": "때가 안 좋은", "unprofitable": "이익이 없는"}, "src": "verbal14 Q10"}, {"id": "v216_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Despite the general _____ of Roman archaeological studies toward the major cities and their monuments, archaeology has contributed much to a better understanding of rural developments in Roman territory.", "choices": ["openness", "indifference", "hostility", "animus", "bias", "orientation"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "EF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Despite → 대조. '___ toward the major cities' 에도 불구하고 고고학이 농촌 이해에 기여했다.\n빈칸 = 대도시 쪽으로 '치우침, 쏠림'.\nbias와 orientation이 'toward'와 결합해 '~ 쪽으로의 경향/치우침'.\n정답: E (bias), F (orientation)", "trap": "hostility/animus는 '적대감'으로 짝이지만 'toward the major cities'와 함께 쓰면 도시를 적대한다는 뜻이 되어 Despite 대조가 무너진다. indifference는 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"openness": "개방성", "indifference": "무관심", "hostility": "적대감", "animus": "적의, 반감", "bias": "편향, 치우침", "orientation": "지향, 방향성"}, "src": "verbal216 Q11 · 25/6, 25/2, 25/1, 23/4, 22/10, 22/9, 22/7, 22/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v32_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Consuming 25 to 35 percent of their body weight each day, sea otters are not only _____ but highly specialized eaters, organizing themselves into groups that zero in on specific kinds of prey.", "choices": ["prodigious", "undiscriminating", "fastidious", "picky", "voracious", "omnivorous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 매일 체중의 25~35%를 먹는다 → 엄청난 대식가.\n'not only ___ but highly specialized eaters' → not only A but B는 대조가 아니라 추가(A이면서 B).\n빈칸 = '먹는 양이 엄청난'.\nprodigious(엄청난)와 voracious(게걸스러운)가 짝.\n정답: A (prodigious), E (voracious)", "trap": "fastidious/picky(까다로운)는 'specialized'와 겹쳐 그럴듯하지만, 빈칸은 앞의 '체중의 25~35%' 정보를 받는 자리다. undiscriminating/omnivorous는 'specialized'와 모순.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"prodigious": "엄청난, 거대한", "undiscriminating": "가리지 않는", "fastidious": "까다로운", "picky": "까다로운", "voracious": "게걸스러운, 식욕이 왕성한", "omnivorous": "잡식성의"}, "src": "verbal32 Q10"}, {"id": "v216_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "The reasoning in the passage is most strongly supported if the demographic data also indicate that", "choices": ["parents who have children under ten will spend an increasing number of evenings at home", "the average age of babysitters will increase slightly", "the number of children in daytime childcare will increase", "the proportion of teenagers who babysit regularly will increase", "there will be a decrease in the average number of children per household who are under ten"], "columns": null, "pid": "v216_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 저녁 돌봄을 원하는 부모가 베이비시터를 구하기 점점 어려워진다.\n근거: 십대(공급) 감소 + 10세 미만 아이 수 증가. 하지만 '아이 수' 증가가 곧 '베이비시터를 원하는 가정' 증가는 아니다(한 집에 아이가 더 많아질 수도 있음).\nE: 가구당 10세 미만 아이 수가 감소 → 아이 수는 늘고 가구당 수는 줄어드니 어린아이가 있는 가구 수가 확실히 증가 → 수요 증가 → 결론 강화.\n정답: E", "trap": "D는 오히려 약화(베이비시터를 하는 십대 비율 증가 → 공급 보완). A도 저녁에 집에 있는 부모가 늘면 수요 감소로 약화.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"demographic": "인구통계의", "decline": "감소하다", "virtually": "사실상"}, "src": "verbal216 Q13 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v238_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage ascribes some of the impact of \"institutional critique\" to which of the following attributes of the artists engaged in it?", "choices": ["Their refusal to directly confront powerful institutions", "The economic entanglements between them and established art institutions", "The meticulousness with which they approached their subject", "The diversity of media in which they worked", "The thorough knowledge of art history they typically possessed"], "columns": null, "pid": "v238_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Yet their rigorous methodologies for researching and dramatically staging interventions in museum spaces yielded some of the era's most politically astute and influential artworks.'\n영향력의 원인 = rigorous methodologies(엄밀한 방법론) → meticulousness(꼼꼼함).\n정답: C", "trap": "B(경제적 얽힘)는 그들이 비판한 대상(museum patronage)이지 영향력의 원인이 아니다. A는 그들이 미술관 '안에서' 맞섰다는 내용과 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "institutional critique", "glosses": {"rigorous": "엄밀한", "meticulousness": "꼼꼼함", "entanglement": "얽힘, 연루", "patronage": "후원"}, "src": "verbal238 Q5 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v238_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author's characterization of certain artwork as \"politically astute\" serves to", "choices": ["elucidate the goals of an artistic practice mentioned earlier in the passage", "respond to a rebuke of certain artists that is mentioned earlier in the passage", "support a claim made in the preceding sentence", "provide an example of the criticism leveled at certain artists", "characterize some types of art as superior to others"], "columns": null, "pid": "v238_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "직전 문장: 'Artists engaged in such work were often criticized for participating in the very art world system they purported to challenge.'(비판)\n다음 문장 'Yet ... yielded some of the era's most politically astute and influential artworks' → Yet으로 그 비판에 맞서 반박.\n→ 앞서 언급된 질책(rebuke)에 대응.\n정답: B", "trap": "C가 함정. 앞 문장의 '주장'을 뒷받침하는 것이 아니라, Yet으로 앞 문장의 비판을 반박한다. D는 비판의 예가 아니라 칭찬.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "politically astute", "glosses": {"astute": "통찰력 있는, 기민한", "rebuke": "질책", "purport": "~라고 주장하다(표방하다)", "elucidate": "명료하게 설명하다"}, "src": "verbal238 Q6 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.1 / S2 2.7"}, {"set": 2, "sections": [[{"id": "v221_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "His _____ speaking style notwithstanding, William Perkins has long been seen as the moderate face of his political party.", "choices": ["genteel", "mundane", "affable", "captivating", "vehement"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: notwithstanding(~에도 불구하고) → 대조.\n그는 당의 '온건한(moderate)' 얼굴로 여겨졌다 → 빈칸은 온건함과 반대되는 말투.\n빈칸 = 격렬한, 과격한.\n정답: E (vehement)", "trap": "genteel/affable은 온건함과 같은 방향이라 notwithstanding 대조가 성립하지 않는다. captivating은 온건함과 대립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"genteel": "품위 있는, 점잖은", "affable": "상냥한, 붙임성 있는", "vehement": "격렬한, 열정적인", "mundane": "평범한, 재미없는", "captivating": "매혹적인"}, "src": "verbal221 Q1 · 25년 6월, 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v25_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The prime minister's spokesman faces a difficult task in defending his boss from what he sees as the (i) _____ of a decidedly prejudiced press. To make his defense effectively, he will certainly have to give specific examples of the media coverage he finds so (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["overwrought panegyrics", "lowly calumnies", "justified fulminations"], ["objectionable", "confusing", "unexciting"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'decidedly prejudiced press'(명백히 편향된 언론)로부터 상관을 방어 → 언론이 하는 것은 부당한 비방 → lowly calumnies.\n(ii) 방어하려면 자신이 그렇게 '불쾌하다/부당하다'고 여기는 보도 사례를 제시해야 → objectionable.\n정답: B (lowly calumnies), D (objectionable)", "trap": "justified fulminations는 '비난'이라는 의미는 맞지만 justified(정당한)가 대변인의 관점(prejudiced press)과 모순. overwrought panegyrics는 찬사라서 방어할 필요가 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"panegyrics": "찬사", "overwrought panegyrics": "과도한 찬사", "lowly calumnies": "저열한 비방", "justified fulminations": "정당한 맹비난", "objectionable": "불쾌한, 못마땅한", "confusing": "혼란스러운", "unexciting": "흥미 없는"}, "src": "verbal25 Q2"}, {"id": "v227_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The power of laughter to affect the perceived funniness of television programming is (i) _____: most researchers have found that the inclusion of laughter on a program's soundtrack (ii) _____ the overall perception of humor, although it appears that it can (iii) _____ humor at specific points and thus boost the total comic appeal of the program.", "choices": null, "columns": [["cumulative", "measurable", "unclear"], ["allows variations in", "tends to accentuate", "has little effect on"], ["dampen", "enhance", "mask"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 (i)을 설명: 대부분 연구는 (ii), although (iii) → 서로 엇갈리는 결과.\n(ii) although 대조 + (iii) 뒤 'thus boost the total comic appeal' → (ii)는 전체 유머 인식에 효과 없다 → has little effect on.\n(iii) 특정 지점에서 유머를 높여 전체 매력을 boost → enhance.\n(i) 효과 없다는 연구와 높인다는 결과가 공존 → 웃음의 힘은 불분명하다 → unclear.\n정답: C (unclear), F (has little effect on), H (enhance)", "trap": "(ii) tends to accentuate를 고르면 although 뒤와 대조가 사라진다. (i) measurable은 '측정 가능'이라 그럴듯하지만 결과가 엇갈린다는 콜론 뒤 내용과 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cumulative": "누적되는", "measurable": "측정 가능한", "unclear": "불분명한", "allows variations in": "~에 변동을 허용하다", "tends to accentuate": "강조하는 경향이 있다", "has little effect on": "~에 거의 영향이 없다", "dampen": "약화시키다", "enhance": "높이다, 강화하다", "mask": "가리다"}, "src": "verbal227 Q3 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v9_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author would most likely agree with which of the following assertions about the environmental impact of hydroelectric power plants?", "choices": ["It cannot be inferred from calculations of the environmental impact of a few hydroelectric plants.", "It is not primarily determined by the effects of dam building on vegetation.", "It cannot be calculated with sufficient accuracy to justify the requirement of environmental impact studies prior to plant construction.", "It could be significantly improved if the amounts of steel and cement used for dam building could be decreased.", "It is too substantial, when all factors are considered, to justify the building of new dams."], "columns": null, "pid": "v9_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 마지막 문장 'amounts vary depending upon the specific location, terrain, and power intensity of the dam with its associated lake.'\n배출량이 댐마다 다르다 → 몇몇 발전소의 계산으로 전체를 추론할 수 없다.\n정답: A", "trap": "B가 함정. 저자는 식생 효과(메탄, CO2 흡수 상실)가 '추정하기 어렵다'고 할 뿐, 주된 요인이 아니라고 말하지 않는다(오히려 substantial하다고 함). C/E는 지문에 없는 극단적 결론.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"submerge": "물에 잠기게 하다", "microbial decomposition": "미생물 분해", "eradicate": "근절하다", "potent": "강력한"}, "src": "verbal9 Q4"}, {"id": "v9_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The highlighted sentence (\"Estimates for these emissions ~ hydroelectric power\") serves primarily to", "choices": ["support a claim made at the beginning of the passage", "acknowledge a problem inherent in a particular kind of calculation", "anticipate and respond to a possible criticism of the author's overall argument", "introduce a problem that will be explored later in the passage", "point out an exception to a general claim"], "columns": null, "pid": "v9_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문장(일반 주장): 'Calculating hydroelectric plants' environmental impact is not simple.'\n하이라이트 문장: 철강·시멘트 제조 배출량 추정은 'relatively straightforward' → 계산이 간단한 예외적인 부분.\n이어서 'But more difficult-to-estimate ... during the plants' operation' → 다시 일반 주장으로 복귀.\n→ 일반 주장(계산은 간단치 않다)에 대한 예외를 지적.\n정답: E (출처 키는 C, note 참조)", "trap": "C는 '반론 예상 후 대응'이지만, 이 문장은 저자 주장에 대한 비판에 답하는 것이 아니라 양보(쉬운 부분도 있다)에 해당한다. A는 오히려 첫 문장과 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"straightforward": "간단한, 명확한", "entail": "수반하다", "anticipate": "예상하다", "exception": "예외"}, "src": "verbal9 Q5", "note": "⚠ 원본 답안표 정답은 C이지만, 검토 풀이로는 E이(가) 더 타당해 보입니다. 채점은 원본 기준이며 아래 해설은 검토 풀이 기준입니다. 근거: 출처 키는 C. 하이라이트 문장은 '계산이 간단치 않다'는 첫 문장(일반 주장)에 대해 '건설 단계 배출 추정은 비교적 간단하다'고 인정하는 양보/예외이며, 바로 뒤 But으로 어려운 부분을 제시한다. 저자 주장에 대한 '비판'에 응답하는 문장으로 보기 어려워 E(일반 주장에 대한 예외)가 더 타당하다고 판단. 확신도는 높지만 원 출처 확인 권장."}, {"id": "v209_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "While the _____ of reliable sources in later narratives make many details of the early history of China's Zhou dynasty unverifiable, the Zhou rulers' successful rise to power is certain.", "choices": ["dearth", "ambiguity", "paucity", "opacity", "authenticity", "credibility"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 신뢰할 만한 자료의 ___ 때문에 많은 세부 사항을 '검증할 수 없다(unverifiable)'.\n검증 불가의 원인 = 자료가 '부족'함.\ndearth와 paucity가 '부족, 결핍' 짝.\n정답: A (dearth), C (paucity)", "trap": "ambiguity/opacity(모호함, 불투명)도 검증을 어렵게 하지만 'of reliable sources'와 결합하면 어색하고, 서로 정확한 동의어 짝도 아니다. authenticity/credibility는 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dearth": "부족, 결핍", "ambiguity": "모호함", "paucity": "부족, 소량", "opacity": "불투명함, 난해함", "authenticity": "진짜임, 진정성", "credibility": "신뢰성"}, "src": "verbal209 Q6 · 25년 1월, 23년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v25_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Asteroids of diameter less than 100 km never melted but asteroids with larger diameters did so and became _____ with the heavier Fe-Ni material forming the core and the silicates forming the crust.", "choices": ["stratified", "destabilized", "weakened", "liquefied", "differentiated", "distinguished"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 녹은 뒤 'with the heavier Fe-Ni material forming the core and the silicates forming the crust' → 무거운 것은 핵, 가벼운 것은 지각으로 '층이 나뉨'.\n빈칸 = 층상으로 분리된.\nstratified(층을 이룬)와 differentiated(분화된, 지질학에서 층으로 분리된)가 짝.\n정답: A (stratified), E (differentiated)", "trap": "liquefied는 'melted'에 끌린 오답. 빈칸은 녹은 '결과'로 핵-지각 구조가 생긴 상태다. distinguished는 '구별된/저명한'으로 differentiated와 비슷해 보이지만 층 분리 의미가 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"differentiated": "분화된(층으로 분리된)", "stratified": "층을 이룬, 계층화된", "destabilized": "불안정해진", "weakened": "약해진", "liquefied": "액화된", "distinguished": "구별된, 저명한"}, "src": "verbal25 Q9"}, {"id": "v213_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Despite the _____ of medical information available through e-mail, the Internet, and mobile devices, not many patients are taking advantage of the potential of electronic communications for health-related needs.", "choices": ["wealth", "complexity", "intricacy", "profusion", "resurgence", "overload"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Despite → 대조. 의료 정보가 ___ 함에도 불구하고 많은 환자가 활용하지 않는다.\n빈칸 = 정보가 '풍부함'.\nwealth와 profusion이 짝.\n정답: A (wealth), D (profusion)", "trap": "overload(과부하)도 양이 많다는 뜻이지만 부정적 의미라 '활용하지 않는다'와 대조가 안 되고 짝이 없다. complexity/intricacy는 짝이지만 Despite 대조가 성립하지 않는다(복잡하면 안 쓰는 게 당연).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"wealth": "풍부함, 다량", "complexity": "복잡성", "intricacy": "복잡함", "profusion": "풍부, 다량", "resurgence": "부활, 재기", "overload": "과부하"}, "src": "verbal213 Q6 · 25/1, 24/9, 23/10, 23/7, 22/10 중국후기"}, {"id": "v237_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Scrupulous accounting by businesses tends to be swept aside during periods when frenzied investing and speculation seem to promise huge profits, demonstrating once again that _____, in the presence of lucre, may erode honesty.", "choices": ["enthusiasm", "insight", "eagerness", "acumen", "optimism", "persistence"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'frenzied investing and speculation'(광적인 투자·투기) 시기에 꼼꼼한 회계가 무시된다.\n→ 돈(lucre) 앞에서 ___이 정직함을 잠식한다 = 열광, 열의.\nenthusiasm과 eagerness가 짝.\n정답: A (enthusiasm), C (eagerness)", "trap": "optimism(낙관)도 '큰 이익을 약속하는 듯' 부분과 어울리지만 짝이 없다. insight/acumen(통찰, 예리함)은 짝이지만 정직을 훼손하는 원인이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"enthusiasm": "열광, 열의", "insight": "통찰", "eagerness": "열망, 열의", "acumen": "예리함, 통찰력", "optimism": "낙관", "persistence": "끈기"}, "src": "verbal237 Q9 · 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v25_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true of a Eurasia-Africa land bridge during ice ages?", "choices": ["It offers suitable habitats for cold-adapted species of antelope.", "It encourages migration from Africa to Eurasia of cold-adapted species of antelope.", "It allows the survival of warm-adapted species of antelope that might otherwise become extinct.", "It is more likely to exist early in an ice age than later in an ice age.", "The habitats it offers change more quickly than do those offered by land bridges during other periods."], "columns": null, "pid": "v25_p3", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'During periods of climatic cooling, such as the various ice ages, the land bridge is open for a long time ... and is usable by cold-adapted species because cool habitats then extend across it.'\n빙하기 육교 = 한랭 적응 종에게 적합한 서식지 제공.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 방향이 반대: 빙하기 이동은 Africa 쪽(toward Africa)이다. D는 지문에 없는 내용.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"land bridge": "육교(대륙을 잇는 땅)", "migrate": "이주하다", "habitat": "서식지"}, "src": "verbal25 Q10"}, {"id": "v25_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage implies that during the \"short lag,\" a land bridge between Africa and Eurasia would", "choices": ["be inhabited primarily by species of antelope originating in Eurasia", "be characterized by areas of widely varying elevation above sea level", "be inhabited by a wide diversity of antelope species", "contain habitats that could sustain warm-adapted antelope species", "contain habitats similar to habitats at much higher latitudes in Eurasia"], "columns": null, "pid": "v25_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Only during the short lag between onset of global temperature change and sea level response can warm-adapted species migrate from the equator toward higher latitudes.'\n이동하려면 육교와 '그 위의 적합한 서식지'가 모두 필요하다(2문장).\n→ 짧은 지연 기간에는 육교가 아직 있고 따뜻한 서식지가 있어야 온난 적응 종이 이동 가능.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 반대: 이 기간에 이동하는 것은 아프리카 출신 온난 적응 종이다. E는 '높은 위도와 비슷한 서식지'로 한랭 서식지를 암시해 틀림.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lag": "지연, 시간 차", "latitude": "위도", "onset": "시작, 개시"}, "src": "verbal25 Q11"}, {"id": "v25_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following best accounts for the apparent bias in antelope-migration direction?", "choices": ["Warm-adapted antelope species are rarely able to tolerate cool habitats, whereas cold-adapted antelope species usually can tolerate warm habitats.", "During global warming periods, land bridges, when present, lack habitats suitable for sustaining warm-adapted antelope species.", "Under most climatic conditions, Africa offers a larger number of suitable antelope habitats than does Eurasia.", "Many more species of antelope have originated in Eurasia than have originated in Africa.", "Land bridges are more likely to exist when climate change favors migration to warmer climates than when climate change favors migration to cooler climates."], "columns": null, "pid": "v25_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 냉각기에는 해수면이 낮아 육교가 오래 열리고, 이 방향(아프리카로)이 서식지 변화가 가리키는 방향. 온난기에는 해수면이 높아 육교가 줄거나 사라진다.\n→ 따뜻한 쪽(아프리카)으로의 이동이 유리할 때 육교가 존재할 가능성이 높다.\n정답: E", "trap": "B가 함정. 지문은 온난기에 육교가 '줄거나 없어진다'고 했지 '있지만 서식지가 부적합하다'고 하지 않았다. A는 내성(tolerance) 차이라는 지문에 없는 설명.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"bias": "치우침, 편향", "sea level": "해수면", "dictate": "좌우하다, 지시하다"}, "src": "verbal25 Q12"}], [{"id": "v12_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Some film historians argue that film narrative was inspired in large part by stage plays, whereas others argue that the theater, far from being a _____, obstructed the development of film narrative.", "choices": ["hindrance", "by-product", "successor", "catalyst", "rival"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: whereas로 두 견해 대조. 한쪽은 연극이 영화 서사에 '영감을 주었다', 다른 쪽은 연극이 'far from being a ___' 오히려 방해했다.\nfar from being X, obstructed → X는 'obstructed'의 반대 = 촉진제.\n정답: D (catalyst)", "trap": "hindrance(방해물)는 obstructed와 같은 뜻이라 'far from being'과 모순. by-product/successor는 대조의 축(도움 vs 방해)과 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hindrance": "방해물", "by-product": "부산물", "successor": "후계자, 후속물", "catalyst": "촉매, 촉진제", "rival": "경쟁자"}, "src": "verbal12 Q1"}, {"id": "v238_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "He was never (i) _____: he was nothing if not (ii) _____, so he forbore for the present to declare his passion.", "choices": null, "columns": [["chivalrous", "impetuous", "thoughtful"], ["boorish", "circumspect", "spontaneous"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 마지막 'so he forbore for the present to declare his passion'(당장은 고백을 삼갔다) → 신중함.\n(ii) nothing if not ___ = 무엇보다도 ~했다 → circumspect(신중한).\n(i) 'never ___' + 콜론으로 (ii)와 같은 의미 → 결코 충동적이지 않았다 → impetuous.\n정답: B (impetuous), E (circumspect)", "trap": "(i) chivalrous(기사도적인)는 사랑 고백 문맥 때문에 끌리지만 'never'와 결합하면 의미가 맞지 않는다. (ii) spontaneous는 고백을 삼간 것과 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"forbore for the present": "당장은 삼갔다", "chivalrous": "기사도적인, 정중한", "impetuous": "충동적인, 성급한", "thoughtful": "사려 깊은", "boorish": "무례한, 촌스러운", "circumspect": "신중한, 조심성 있는", "spontaneous": "즉흥적인"}, "src": "verbal238 Q2 · 24/2, 23/11, 23/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v226_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Animals whose behavioral traits are (i) _____ thereby have a level of (ii) _____ when environmental conditions vary. However, studies of animal personality also suggest that the behavior of individual animals can be constrained to certain behavioral types, leading to consistent differences between individuals.", "choices": null, "columns": [["plastic", "habitual", "understood"], ["camouflage", "constancy", "flexibility"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: However 뒤 '행동이 특정 유형에 제약되어(constrained) 개체 간 일관된 차이' → 앞 문장은 그 반대 = 행동이 변할 수 있다.\n(i) 행동 특성이 '유연하게 변하는' → plastic(가소성 있는).\n(ii) 환경이 변할 때 그런 동물은 '유연성'을 가진다 → flexibility.\n정답: A (plastic), F (flexibility)", "trap": "habitual/constancy는 However 뒤의 '제약된 행동'과 같은 방향이라 대조가 무너진다. plastic을 '플라스틱'으로만 알면 놓치기 쉽다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"plastic": "가소성 있는, 변형 가능한", "habitual": "습관적인", "understood": "이해된", "camouflage": "위장", "constancy": "불변성", "flexibility": "유연성"}, "src": "verbal226 Q3 · 24년 6월, 22년 10월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The guarantee of academic freedom to professors is intended to encourage intellectual independence. But so long as faculty members receive training in a specific academic discipline and are appointed to positions defined by discipline, and so long as colleges and universities are organized by departments that (i) _____ long-standing disciplinary traditions, academic freedom will also (ii) _____ unique discipline-specific expectations. Yet the right to (iii) _____ disciplinary paradigms is also fundamental to academic freedom.", "choices": null, "columns": [["flout", "inherit", "reinvent"], ["tend to embody", "fail to communicate", "begin to transcend"], ["resist", "delineate", "perpetuate"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 학과 중심 조직이 '오래된 학문 전통'을 어떻게? so long as 조건은 학과에 묶인 상황 → 물려받다 → inherit.\n(ii) 그 결과 학문의 자유도 학과별 고유한 기대를 '구현하는 경향' → tend to embody.\n(iii) Yet → 대조. 학과 패러다임에 '저항할' 권리도 학문의 자유의 핵심 → resist.\n정답: B (inherit), D (tend to embody), G (resist)", "trap": "(iii) perpetuate(영속시키다)는 Yet의 대조를 무시한 오답. (i) flout(무시하다)는 '학과 중심 조직'이 전통을 이어간다는 흐름과 반대.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"flout": "(규칙을) 무시하다", "inherit": "물려받다", "reinvent": "재창조하다", "tend to embody": "구현하는 경향이 있다", "fail to communicate": "전달하지 못하다", "begin to transcend": "넘어서기 시작하다", "resist": "저항하다", "delineate": "묘사하다, 윤곽을 그리다", "perpetuate": "영속시키다"}, "src": "verbal224 Q4 · 25/12, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v216_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions \"Anthia feeding her dogs\" primarily in order to support", "choices": ["a comparison between the 《Ephesiaka》 and other ancient Greek novels", "a criticism of Burger's view about what the 《Ephesiaka》 is", "an explanation of the 《Ephesiaka》's narrative shortcomings", "a reassessment of the 《Ephesiaka》's quality as a work of literature", "a claim about the effect of inconsequential details on the overall quality of 《Ephesiaka》"], "columns": null, "pid": "v216_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'However, it is doubtful that Ephesiaka is an epitome because, as an epitome, it is a worse job than it is as a novel. Even in passages Burger thinks to be epitomized, inconsequential details such as Anthia feeding her dogs are retained...'\n요약본이라면 사소한 세부는 빠져야 하는데 남아 있다 → Burger의 '요약본' 견해를 반박하는 근거.\n정답: B", "trap": "E가 함정. 사소한 세부가 작품 '전체 품질'에 미치는 영향을 말하려는 것이 아니라, '요약본이 아니다'라는 주장을 위한 증거다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Anthia feeding her dogs", "glosses": {"epitome": "요약본, 발췌", "inconsequential": "사소한", "excise": "삭제하다", "erratically": "불규칙하게"}, "src": "verbal216 Q14 · 25/11, 25/7, 25/4, 25/3, 23/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v216_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage disagrees with Burger about which of the following?", "choices": ["Whether it can be determined which ancient Greek texts are epitomes", "The explanation for some apparent deficiencies in the 《Ephesiaka》", "The overall literary quality of the 《Ephesiaka》"], "columns": null, "pid": "v216_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Burger: 작품이 요약본(epitome)이라서 서사적 결함(choppy pace 등)이 생겼다고 설명.\n저자: 'it is doubtful that Ephesiaka is an epitome' → 결함의 원인 설명에 동의하지 않음 → B 맞음.\nC: 저자도 'inferior in composition', 'Conspicuous structural inconsistencies'라고 해 품질이 낮다는 점은 Burger와 같다 → 불일치 아님.\nA: 어떤 텍스트가 요약본인지 판별 가능한가는 논의되지 않음.\n정답: B", "trap": "C가 함정. 'The quality ... was first questioned by Burger'를 보고 저자가 반대한다고 착각하기 쉽지만, 저자 자신도 작품의 질이 낮다고 첫 문단에서 단언한다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"epitome": "요약본", "deficiency": "결함", "conspicuous": "눈에 띄는", "composition": "구성, 작문"}, "src": "verbal216 Q15 · 25/11, 25/7, 25/4, 25/3, 23/5 중국후기", "note": "원본 답안표가 회차마다 달랐던 문항입니다(B / BC). 지문 근거로 B를 정답으로 확정했습니다. 복수 사본 키 충돌(B vs BC): 저자는 첫 두 문장에서 작품이 'inferior in composition'이라고 해 품질 평가는 Burger와 일치하므로 C는 불일치 항목이 아님. 따라서 B로 확정."}, {"id": "v206_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The highlighted sentence serves to", "choices": ["offer a possible explanation for why archaeologists have never found evidence of megafaunal killings in Australia", "substantiate the belief that the demise of Australian megafauna was inevitable with the arrival of humans", "provide evidence of how human hunters expedited the rate of the extinction of Australian megafauna", "document that archaeologists had drastically overestimated the assumed ranges of Australian megafauna", "suggest that the megafaunal extinction in Australia coincided with megafaunal extinctions in other locations"], "columns": null, "pid": "v206_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "직전 질문: 'If humans exploited megafauna, then why are there no kill sites?'\n하이라이트 문장: Flannery는 빠른 멸종 속도 때문이라 했지만, 저자는 4만 년 이상 된 물질이 보존되지 않았기 때문일 가능성이 더 높다고 함.\n→ 사냥 유적(kill sites)이 발견되지 않는 이유에 대한 가능한 설명.\n정답: A", "trap": "C가 함정. 인간 사냥이 멸종을 가속했다는 '증거'가 아니라, 증거가 '없는' 이유를 설명하는 문장이다. B는 inevitable로 너무 극단적.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"megafauna": "거대 동물상", "preservation": "보존", "extermination": "몰살, 근절"}, "src": "verbal206 Q7 · 24년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author discusses the possible impact of \"low levels of predation by the new human hunters\" primarily to", "choices": ["explain why humans probably had a negligible impact on megafauna in Australia", "suggest why the megafauna in Australia lasted as long as they did", "establish the primary cause of the megafauna extinction in Australia", "point to an important consequence of continental drying for megafauna in Australia", "suggest the precarious state of megafauna when humans arrived in Australia"], "columns": null, "pid": "v206_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'coincides with intensification of long-term continental drying, reductions in resource levels... and so even low levels of predation ... may have tipped some species into terminal declines or accelerated declines already underway.'\n낮은 수준의 사냥만으로도 멸종에 이를 수 있었다 = 이미 거대동물이 위태로운 상태였다는 뜻.\n정답: E", "trap": "C가 함정. 저자는 사냥을 '주된 원인'으로 보지 않는다(마지막 문장: 집중적 사냥이 아니라 스트레스 환경에 새 포식자가 '추가'된 것). A는 영향이 없었다고 해 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "low levels of predation by the new human hunters", "glosses": {"precarious": "위태로운", "terminal decline": "회복 불가능한 쇠퇴", "predation": "포식", "tip into": "~로 기울게 하다"}, "src": "verbal206 Q8 · 24년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q9", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following can be verified about Australian megafauna?", "choices": ["The majority of them went extinct approximately 50,000 years ago.", "Between 40,000 and 50,000 years ago, their population was drastically affected.", "A reduction in their food supply was the primary culprit leading to their extinction."], "columns": null, "pid": "v206_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "B 근거: 'environmental signatures consistently point to the reduction in range and density of large animals ... between 40,000 and 50,000 years ago' → 이 시기 개체군이 크게 영향받음 → 확인 가능.\nA: 'many species ... had become extinct prior to the arrival of humans'라고만 하며 '대다수가 약 5만 년 전 멸종'은 확인 불가.\nC: 자원 감소는 여러 요인 중 하나일 뿐, '주된 원인'이라는 말은 없음.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 숫자(50,000)를 재활용한 함정. 지문은 '분포·밀도 감소'를 말했지 '대다수 멸종'을 말하지 않았고 'if not their final extinction'으로 멸종 시점은 유보했다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"range": "서식 범위", "density": "밀도", "coincident with": "~와 동시에 일어나는", "culprit": "주범"}, "src": "verbal206 Q9 · 24년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v24_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Sokari Douglas Camp was __________ in the early 1990s by many of London's commercially driven art dealers and galleries, some of whom apparently found her themes difficult to market.", "choices": ["criticized", "lionized", "misrepresented", "neglected", "forsaken", "eulogized"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'commercially driven' 화랑들이 그녀의 주제를 '팔기 어렵다(difficult to market)'고 여겼다.\n→ 상업적 화랑이 그녀를 '외면했다'.\nneglected와 forsaken이 짝.\n정답: D (neglected), E (forsaken)", "trap": "criticized는 부정적이라 끌리지만, 팔기 어려워서 하는 행동은 비판이 아니라 외면이며 짝도 없다. lionized/eulogized(찬양)는 짝이지만 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"criticized": "비판받은", "lionized": "치켜세워진, 명사 대접받은", "misrepresented": "잘못 전달된, 왜곡된", "neglected": "방치된, 외면당한", "forsaken": "버림받은", "eulogized": "찬사를 받은"}, "src": "verbal24 Q10"}, {"id": "v224_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Millville has its share of suburban eyesores─cement-block strip malls, rows of fast-food restaurants, and _____ split-level homes marching up hillsides denuded of trees.", "choices": ["magnificent", "superlative", "abysmal", "banal", "lackluster", "diminutive"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'suburban eyesores'(교외의 흉물) 목록 – 시멘트 블록 상가, 패스트푸드점 줄, ___ 주택.\n빈칸 = 부정적이되 '흉물' 목록에 어울리는 '평범하고 개성 없는'.\nbanal과 lackluster가 짝.\n정답: D (banal), E (lackluster)", "trap": "abysmal(최악의)은 부정적이지만 너무 강하고 짝이 없다. diminutive(작은)는 크기 정보일 뿐 흉물과 연결되지 않는다. magnificent/superlative는 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"eyesores": "눈에 거슬리는 것들", "superlative": "최상급의, 최고의", "lackluster": "생기 없는, 밋밋한", "magnificent": "웅장한", "abysmal": "최악의, 끔찍한", "banal": "진부한, 평범한", "diminutive": "아주 작은"}, "src": "verbal224 Q10 · 25년 5월, 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v2_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The tools of science are so specialized that we accept them as a kind of _____ machinery for producing knowledge: we know that they work, but cannot explain why.", "choices": ["occult", "efficacious", "potent", "arcane", "impersonal", "reliable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 빈칸 설명: 작동한다는 건 알지만 '왜 작동하는지 설명할 수 없다'.\n앞부분 'so specialized'(너무 전문화되어)도 같은 방향.\n빈칸 = 이해하기 어려운, 신비한.\noccult와 arcane이 짝.\n정답: A (occult), D (arcane)", "trap": "efficacious/reliable(효과적인/믿을 만한)은 'we know that they work'에 끌린 오답. 빈칸의 핵심은 'cannot explain why', 즉 불가해함이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"occult": "신비한, 불가사의한", "efficacious": "효과적인", "potent": "강력한", "arcane": "난해한, 비밀스러운", "impersonal": "비인격적인", "reliable": "믿을 만한"}, "src": "verbal2 Q8"}, {"id": "v238_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is an assumption on which the argument depends?", "choices": ["The average size of a Namibian cattle herd has not significantly increased in the past several decades.", "The killing of adult cheetahs by farmers does not often result in the death of cheetah cubs from starvation or predators.", "Cheetahs do not hunt healthy adult cattle.", "Cheetahs are seldom killed except on farmland.", "Namibian cheetah territories located away from farmland have not been increasingly likely to be abandoned in favor of territories that include at least some farmland."], "columns": null, "pid": "v238_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 덫에 걸리는 빈도가 줄지 않았으므로 치타 개체수는 크게 줄지 않았다.\n빈틈: 개체수가 줄어도 농지 밖 치타들이 비어 있는 농지 영역으로 계속 옮겨 온다면 덫 빈도는 유지될 수 있다(치타는 배타적 영역을 지킴 → 빈 영역이 생기면 다른 치타가 차지).\nE는 이 대안을 차단: 농지 밖 영역을 버리고 농지 포함 영역으로 옮기는 일이 늘지 않았다.\n부정 테스트: 그런 이동이 늘었다면 → 덫 빈도 유지가 개체수 유지의 증거가 못 됨 → 논증 붕괴.\n정답: E", "trap": "B(새끼의 죽음)는 개체수 감소를 시사해 그럴듯하지만, 논증의 연결고리(덫 빈도 ↔ 개체수)와 무관하다. D도 농지 밖 사망은 논증의 범위 밖.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exclusive territory": "배타적 영역", "abandon": "버리다", "in favor of": "~을 택하여", "solitary": "단독 생활하는"}, "src": "verbal238 Q13 · 26/1, 25/7, 25/4, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that the \"positive effect\" occurs because", "choices": ["water ceases to be a limiting factor", "seedlings require less water than mature plants do", "the growth of certain other plants is inhibited", "drier conditions favor diverse species of annuals", "shrub seedlings use soil resources more efficiently than other seedlings"], "columns": null, "pid": "v234_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Due to decreased competition by annuals, droughts increase opportunities for shrub seedlings.'\n가뭄이 경쟁자(일년생 식물)의 성장을 억제 → 관목 묘목에 유리.\nC '다른 특정 식물의 성장이 억제된다'가 정확한 paraphrase.\n정답: C", "trap": "E는 반대: 자원 흡수가 더 빠르고 효율적인 것은 일년생 식물(annuals)이다. A는 가뭄인데 물이 제한 요인이 아니라는 것은 모순.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "positive effect", "glosses": {"counterintuitively": "직관에 반하여", "annuals": "일년생 식물", "seedling establishment": "묘목 정착", "encroachment": "침범, 잠식"}, "src": "verbal234 Q5 · 25/11, 25/5, 24/8, 24/6, 24/5, 23/2, 22/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage would most likely agree with which of the following statements about the growth of shrub seedlings?", "choices": ["In naturally occurring conditions, water availability is positively correlated with seedling growth.", "In semi-arid climates, wetter than normal conditions have no appreciable effect on seedling growth.", "When seedlings are grown in isolation, water restriction will not positively affect their growth.", "Where there is competition among annual plants, shrub seedling growth will benefit from increased rainfall.", "Where annual plants are well established, drought will have a negative elect on shrub seedling growth."], "columns": null, "pid": "v234_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심: 가뭄의 긍정적 효과는 오직 '일년생 식물과의 경쟁 감소' 때문이다('Due to decreased competition by annuals').\n묘목을 단독으로(in isolation) 키우면 경쟁이 없으므로, 물 제한이 성장에 긍정적 효과를 줄 이유가 없다.\n→ C에 저자가 동의할 것.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 자연 조건에서는 경쟁 때문에 물이 많을수록 오히려 묘목에 불리할 수 있어 틀림. E는 반대(일년생이 있는 곳에서 가뭄은 묘목에 긍정적). D도 반대.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"semi-arid": "반건조의", "biomass": "생물량", "susceptibility": "취약성", "appreciable": "상당한, 눈에 띄는"}, "src": "verbal234 Q6 · 25/11, 25/5, 24/8, 24/6, 24/5, 23/2, 22/12 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.8 / S2 2.9"}, {"set": 3, "sections": [[{"id": "v9_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "To some extent, the relationship between nitrous oxide and methane in Earth's atmosphere could be described as _____: nitrous oxide releases oxygen when destroyed by ultraviolet radiation, while methane is an oxygen consumer.", "choices": ["necessary", "ephemeral", "inverse", "anomalous", "ubiquitous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 빈칸의 내용을 설명한다.\n아산화질소는 파괴될 때 산소를 '방출'하고, 메탄은 산소를 '소비'한다.\n즉 산소에 대해 서로 반대 방향으로 작용 → 빈칸 = '반대의, 역의' 관계.\ninverse(역의, 반대의)가 정확히 이 대조를 담는다.\n정답: C (inverse)", "trap": "necessary는 두 기체가 서로 필요하다는 뜻인데, 문장은 상호 의존이 아니라 정반대 작용만 말하므로 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"necessary": "필수적인", "ephemeral": "덧없는, 순간적인", "inverse": "역의, 정반대의", "anomalous": "비정상적인, 변칙적인", "ubiquitous": "어디에나 있는"}, "src": "verbal9 Q1"}, {"id": "v7_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Rocks of the Morrison Formation in the western United States yield many dinosaur fossils but few plant fossils. This apparent (i) _____ of plants leads some scientists to speculate that the region was once mostly barren. But others have (ii) _____, noting that the herbivorous dinosaurs there would have needed an abundant food supply.", "choices": null, "columns": [["attrition", "dearth", "attenuation"], ["abdicated", "acceded", "demurred"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 앞 문장: 공룡 화석은 많지만 식물 화석은 'few' → 식물의 '부족, 결핍'. dearth(부족)가 정답.\n'leads some scientists to speculate ... barren(불모의)'도 식물이 적다는 뜻과 연결된다.\n(ii) But others ... noting that 초식공룡에게는 풍부한 먹이가 필요했을 것 → 앞의 '불모지' 추측에 반대 의견을 낸 것.\n빈칸 = '이의를 제기하다' → demurred.\n정답: B (dearth), F (demurred)", "trap": "attrition은 '점진적 감소/마모'라 식물이 '줄어든 과정'을 뜻하고, 단순히 '적다'는 상태와 다르다. acceded(동의하다)는 But 뒤 반론과 정반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"attrition": "마모, 점진적 감소", "abdicated": "(권리·책임을) 포기했다", "acceded": "동의했다, 응했다", "dearth": "부족, 결핍", "attenuation": "약화, 희석", "demurred": "이의를 제기했다"}, "src": "verbal7 Q2"}, {"id": "v25_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The general statement that all objects are (i) _____ by gravity (ii) _____ is not (iii) _____. In reality, if a feather and a lump of iron were dropped at the same time from the same place, we should not expect them to hit the floor at the same time. In order to reconcile the general statement with real-world phenomena, we must take into consideration all of the forces that act upon objects.", "choices": null, "columns": [["molded", "accelerated", "constrained"], ["in proportion to their mass", "at the same rate", "under special circumstances"], ["self-contradictory", "novel", "self-evident"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BEI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i)(ii) 일반 진술: '모든 물체는 중력에 의해 같은 비율로 가속된다' → accelerated + at the same rate.\n다음 문장(깃털과 쇳덩이가 동시에 떨어지지 않는다)은 바로 이 '같은 비율' 진술을 반박하는 현실 사례다.\n(iii) In reality로 시작하는 반례 → 그 진술은 현실에서 '자명하지' 않다. 즉 not self-evident.\n마지막 문장 '조화시키려면 다른 힘들을 고려해야 한다'도 진술이 직관적으로 명백하지 않음을 뒷받침.\n정답: B (accelerated), E (at the same rate), I (self-evident)", "trap": "self-contradictory를 고르면 '자기모순이 아니다'가 되어 반례 문맥과 무관하다. in proportion to their mass는 깃털/쇠 예시와 맞는 듯하지만, 그러면 반례가 진술을 반박하지 못한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"molded": "형성된, 빚어진", "accelerated": "가속된", "constrained": "제약된", "in proportion to their mass": "질량에 비례하여", "at the same rate": "같은 비율로", "under special circumstances": "특수한 상황에서", "self-contradictory": "자기모순적인", "novel": "새로운", "self-evident": "자명한"}, "src": "verbal25 Q3"}, {"id": "v225_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following statements about southern fulmars is true?", "choices": ["Adult fulmars regurgitate less food to their chicks than adult petrels do.", "Adult fulmars are less well-insulated than adult petrels.", "Adult fulmars spend more time foraging than adult petrels.", "Fulmar chicks grow more slowly than petrel chicks.", "Fulmar chicks tend to weigh relatively more than petrel chicks."], "columns": null, "pid": "v225_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'fulmar chicks are only 10-20 percent heavier than petrel chicks.'\n풀머 새끼가 페트렐 새끼보다 10~20% 더 무겁다 → E 'Fulmar chicks tend to weigh relatively more' 그대로 재진술.\nA는 반대(풀머가 40% 더 많이 가져다줌), C도 반대(페트렐이 더 긴 먹이 여행).\nB는 단열이 덜 된 것은 '새끼'이지 성체가 아님.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(더 느리게 자란다)는 '페트렐 새끼가 먹이를 체중으로 더 효율적으로 바꾼다'는 말에서 끌리지만, 성장 속도는 언급되지 않았고 실제로 풀머 새끼가 더 무겁다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"regurgitation": "(먹이를) 게워 냄", "thermoregulation": "체온 조절", "foraging": "먹이 찾기"}, "src": "verbal225 Q4 · 25/11, 25/3, 23/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v225_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence in the context of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["It evaluates a claim.", "It identifies an implication of a conjecture.", "It reinterprets experimental results.", "It undermines a hypothesis.", "It qualifies a theory."], "columns": null, "pid": "v225_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: 페트렐의 긴 먹이 여행이 물을 빼거나 부분 소화하여 에너지가 많은 먹이를 만들 '수도 있다(may)' → 추측(conjecture).\n강조 문장 'Thus, petrel chicks may receive more nutritious meals' → Thus로 그 추측에서 도출되는 결과(함의)를 말한다.\n= B 'identifies an implication of a conjecture'.\n정답: B", "trap": "A(주장을 평가)나 E(이론을 한정)는 강조 문장이 앞 추측에 대해 판단하거나 제한한다고 보는 것인데, 실제로는 그 추측을 받아 결론을 이어갈 뿐이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"conjecture": "추측", "implication": "함의, 귀결", "qualify": "(주장을) 한정·수정하다"}, "src": "verbal225 Q5 · 25/11, 25/3, 23/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v199_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Some historians claim that geography and climate shaped the course of history, an assertion that implies a fairly _____ role for individuals as agents of historical change.", "choices": ["erratic", "circumscribed", "limited", "ephemeral", "inconsistent", "counterintuitive"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지리와 기후가 역사의 흐름을 형성했다는 주장 → 개인의 역할은 상대적으로 작아진다.\n빈칸 = 개인의 역할이 '제한된, 작은'.\ncircumscribed(제한된)와 limited(한정된)가 같은 뜻의 짝.\n정답: B (circumscribed), C (limited)", "trap": "erratic/inconsistent도 '일관성 없는'이라는 짝을 이루지만, 지리·기후 결정론이 함의하는 것은 역할의 '크기 축소'이지 불규칙성이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"erratic": "불규칙한, 변덕스러운", "circumscribed": "제한된, 한정된", "limited": "제한된", "ephemeral": "덧없는, 일시적인", "inconsistent": "일관성 없는", "counterintuitive": "직관에 반하는"}, "src": "verbal199 Q8 · 24년 7월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v197_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although initially it may be difficult to discern the essay's message of peace and conciliation, a close reading reveals its essentially _____ nature.", "choices": ["pacific", "indolent", "banal", "lethargic", "austere", "dovish"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although: 처음에는 '평화와 화해'의 메시지를 알아보기 어렵지만, 자세히 읽으면 그 본질이 드러난다.\n빈칸 = 평화와 화해를 추구하는 본질 → '평화적인'.\npacific(평화로운, 화해적인)과 dovish(비둘기파의, 평화 지향의)가 짝.\n정답: A (pacific), F (dovish)", "trap": "indolent/lethargic은 '게으른, 무기력한'으로 짝을 이루지만 '평화'와는 다른 의미다. pacific을 '태평양'으로만 알면 놓치기 쉽다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pacific": "평화로운, 유화적인", "indolent": "게으른, 나태한", "banal": "진부한", "lethargic": "무기력한", "austere": "엄격한, 소박한", "dovish": "비둘기파의, 평화 지향적인"}, "src": "verbal197 Q6 · 25/7, 25/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v237_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "With its many islands, the Pacific Ocean had from early times been the habitat of _____ civilizations─ones that had mastered the skills of sea travel.", "choices": ["expansionist", "nautical", "cloistered", "migratory", "isolated", "maritime"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "대시(─) 뒤가 빈칸을 정의: '바다 여행 기술을 터득한' 문명.\n빈칸 = 바다·항해와 관련된.\nnautical(항해의)와 maritime(해양의)가 짝.\n정답: B (nautical), F (maritime)", "trap": "islands에서 cloistered/isolated(고립된)가 짝처럼 끌리지만, 대시 뒤 정의(항해 기술 숙달)와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"nautical": "항해의, 선박의", "cloistered": "세상과 격리된", "expansionist": "팽창주의의", "migratory": "이주하는", "isolated": "고립된", "maritime": "바다의, 해양의"}, "src": "verbal237 Q7 · 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v23_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "It is a sign of John Dramani Mahama's maturity as a writer that he is willing to consider his country's future so __________: his memoir is appealingly honest, given to clear-eyed assessments rather than exaggerated accounts of achievements.", "choices": ["cheerfully", "dispassionately", "insightfully", "evocatively", "analytically", "blithely"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤가 빈칸을 설명: 회고록이 정직하고 'clear-eyed assessments rather than exaggerated accounts'.\n빈칸 = 감정·과장 없이 냉철하게 → dispassionately(감정에 치우치지 않고), analytically(분석적으로).\n'성숙함의 표시'라는 말과도 맞는다.\n정답: B (dispassionately), E (analytically)", "trap": "insightfully는 긍정적이라 끌리지만 '과장 대신 냉철한 평가'라는 핵심 대조를 담지 못하고 짝도 없다. cheerfully/blithely는 짝이지만 '태평하게'라 문맥과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cheerfully": "쾌활하게", "dispassionately": "냉정하게, 감정 없이", "insightfully": "통찰력 있게", "evocatively": "환기시키듯, 생생하게", "analytically": "분석적으로", "blithely": "태평하게, 무심하게"}, "src": "verbal23 Q9"}, {"id": "v207_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage introduces the subject of jazz primarily in order to", "choices": ["identify an exception to a generalization about the goals and values of the Black Arts movement", "contrast the formal qualities distinctive of jazz with those distinctive of European orchestral music", "suggest that, despite their differences, participants in the Harlem Renaissance and the Black Arts movement held many views in common", "illustrate an essential difference between the political and aesthetic philosophies of participants in the Harlem Renaissance and the Black Arts movement", "demonstrate that jazz held a special place among the art forms produced by African Americans during both the Harlem Renaissance and the Black Arts movement"], "columns": null, "pid": "v207_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "jazz는 'This is evident in the status held by jazz within the two movements.' 직후에 나온다.\n'This'는 바로 앞의 두 운동의 정치·미학 철학 차이(유럽 고급예술 기준 vs 그에 대립하는 아프리카계 미국인 미학).\n즉 재즈는 그 차이를 보여주는 예시 → D.\n정답: D", "trap": "C(공통점 강조)는 첫머리 '두 운동 모두 사회적 지위 향상을 원했다'에서 끌리지만, 재즈 부분은 차이를 보여준다. E는 재즈의 '특별한 지위'를 말하지만 저자의 목적은 차이를 드러내는 것.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"oppositional": "대립하는", "aesthetic": "미학, 미적 기준", "championed": "옹호했다"}, "src": "verbal207 Q10 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v207_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that, according to Thomas, the leaders of the Harlem Renaissance would probably agree with which of the following statements about the European artistic tradition?", "choices": ["Its greatest achievements have been in the area of music rather than in the other arts.", "Its possibilities have been more thoroughly explored by African American artists than by European artists.", "It has been unable to absorb or respond to artistic achievements in the traditions of other cultures.", "It has been a vehicle for a political philosophy that does not support the interests of African Americans.", "It sets a standard by which the accomplishments of non-European artists may be measured."], "columns": null, "pid": "v207_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 할렘 르네상스 지도자들은 'demonstrating their achievements in \"high art\" as defined by European tradition'.\n또 유럽 작곡가의 재즈 차용을 재즈의 세련됨의 증거로 들었다.\n즉 유럽 전통을 비유럽 예술 성취를 재는 기준으로 삼은 것 → E.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(유럽 전통이 흑인 이익에 반하는 정치철학의 수단)는 오히려 Black Arts 운동 쪽 관점에 가깝다. 할렘 르네상스 지도자의 입장과 정반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"high art": "고급 예술", "sophistication": "세련됨, 정교함", "adaptation": "각색, 차용"}, "src": "verbal207 Q11 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v207_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that proponents of the Black Arts movement did not view jazz in the same way as the commentators of the Harlem Renaissance primarily because proponents of the Black Arts movement", "choices": ["favored work that was consciously grounded in their cultural heritage", "did not feel that music necessarily needs to express a people's historical experience", "regarded European aesthetic norms as an inappropriate standard for critiquing the jazz tradition", "considered European orchestral music less sophisticated than jazz", "felt that European composers should not borrow elements from an African American musical form"], "columns": null, "pid": "v207_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Black Arts 참가자들은 재즈를 'could not be evaluated using European aesthetic values'라고 보았다.\n할렘 르네상스 논평가들은 유럽 작곡가의 차용과 유럽 관현악 형식을 기준으로 재즈를 평가.\n차이의 핵심 = 유럽 미적 기준이 재즈 평가에 부적절하다는 시각 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(문화유산에 의식적으로 기반한 작품 선호)는 할렘 르네상스에도 해당하는 공통점(첫 문장)이라 차이의 이유가 될 수 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"proponents": "지지자", "norms": "규범, 기준", "aesthetic values": "미적 가치"}, "src": "verbal207 Q12 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v236_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The best argument in favor of one space after a period over two is _____ one: one space is simpler, cleaner, and more visually pleasing.", "choices": ["an aesthetic", "a pragmatic", "a technological", "a historical", "a philosophical"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 'simpler, cleaner, and more visually pleasing'.\n특히 visually pleasing(보기 좋다)은 미적 판단.\n빈칸 = 미적인 논거 → an aesthetic.\n정답: A (an aesthetic)", "trap": "pragmatic은 'simpler'에서 끌리지만 cleaner, visually pleasing은 실용성이 아닌 미적 기준이다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"period": "마침표", "an aesthetic": "미적인", "a pragmatic": "실용적인", "a technological": "기술적인", "a historical": "역사적인", "a philosophical": "철학적인"}, "src": "verbal236 Q1 · 25/7, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v16_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "It is (i) _____ that the toucan's bill is (ii) _____; in fact it isn't particularly heavy and seems not to unbalance the bird especially.", "choices": null, "columns": [["an advantage", "a misconception", "a surprise"], ["occasionally hazardous", "unusually strong", "uncomfortably bulky"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론 + in fact: 뒤에서 '실제로는 별로 무겁지 않고 균형을 깨지도 않는다'.\n→ (ii) 부리가 '거추장스럽게 크다'는 통념을 반박 → uncomfortably bulky.\n(i) 그 통념은 사실이 아니므로 '오해'다 → a misconception.\n정답: B (a misconception), F (uncomfortably bulky)", "trap": "unusually strong은 부리에 대한 그럴듯한 말이지만 뒤의 반박 근거(무겁지 않다, 균형)와 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"bill": "부리", "an advantage": "이점", "a misconception": "오해, 잘못된 통념", "a surprise": "놀라운 일", "occasionally hazardous": "가끔 위험한", "unusually strong": "유난히 강한", "uncomfortably bulky": "거추장스럽게 큰"}, "src": "verbal16 Q2"}, {"id": "v222_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Thomsen may have tried to explain his recent egregious actions as those of an obedient civil servant, but to his fellow citizens the former security chief (i) _____ the threatening tactics employed by the security forces that have maintained authoritarian rule in the country for 300 years and have (ii) _____ everything from elections to eligibility for free medical prescriptions.", "choices": null, "columns": [["anticipated", "embodied", "recoiled from"], ["insisted on", "interfered with", "contributed to"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "may have tried ... but: 본인은 '순종적 공무원'이라 했지만 시민들에게는 다르게 보였다.\n(i) 그는 보안군의 위협 전술 자체를 '구현한' 사람 → embodied.\n(ii) 300년 권위주의 통치를 유지한 보안군이 선거부터 무료 처방까지 모든 것에 '간섭했다' → interfered with.\n정답: B (embodied), E (interfered with)", "trap": "(ii) insisted on은 대상이 선거·처방 자격처럼 다양한 영역이라 어색하고, contributed to는 긍정적 뉘앙스라 위협적 권위주의 문맥과 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"egregious": "악명높은", "anticipated": "예상했다, 앞서 했다", "embodied": "구현했다, 상징했다", "recoiled from": "~에 움찔 물러섰다", "insisted on": "고집했다", "interfered with": "간섭했다, 방해했다", "contributed to": "기여했다"}, "src": "verbal222 Q3 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v202_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Preservation of historically significant architecture once (i) _____. But as preservation’s scope has widened from individual buildings to entire urban districts, it has become a cultural (ii) _____. Much of the debate involves modernist architecture’s role in areas preserved as historic districts. Although preservation professionals often (iii) _____ modernist additions to these settings, there is strong public support for keeping new buildings traditional.", "choices": null, "columns": [["faced much opposition", "was widely misunderstood", "provoked little controversy"], ["panacea", "catastrophe", "battleground"], ["loathe", "misconstrue", "advocate"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) once ... But ~ has become: 과거와 현재 대조. 현재는 '문화적 ( )'이고 그 뒤 '논쟁(debate)'이 이어지므로 과거에는 논란이 적었다 → provoked little controversy.\n(ii) 범위가 넓어지며 논쟁의 장이 됨 → battleground.\n(iii) Although: 대중은 새 건물을 전통적으로 두길 강하게 지지 ↔ 전문가는 모더니즘 추가물을 '옹호' → advocate.\n정답: C, F (battleground), I (advocate)", "trap": "(iii) loathe는 대중 입장과 같은 방향이라 Although의 대조가 사라진다. (i) faced much opposition은 But 뒤의 '논쟁화'와 대조가 성립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"faced much opposition": "많은 반대에 부딪혔다", "was widely misunderstood": "널리 오해받았다", "provoked little controversy": "논란을 거의 일으키지 않았다", "panacea": "만병통치약", "catastrophe": "재앙", "battleground": "격전지, 논쟁의 장", "loathe": "몹시 싫어하다", "misconstrue": "오해하다", "advocate": "옹호하다"}, "src": "verbal202 Q4 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, could be most plausibly cited as evidence in support of the \"legend\"?", "choices": ["The segment of the American public that purchased cookbooks grew significantly after 1961.", "Child's 《Mastering the Art of French Cooking》 outsold all other books on French cooking in 1961.", "American cooking became less marked by regional differences than it had been prior to 1961.", "Many American dishes typically prepared by home cooks prior to 1961 declined in popularity.", "Culinary experts in France came to regard American cooking differently than they had prior to 1961."], "columns": null, "pid": "v232_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'legend' = 'Child inspired Americans to exchange their bland cooking for French cuisine's rich flavors.'\n이 전설을 지지하려면 미국인이 기존(밋밋한) 미국 요리를 버렸다는 증거가 필요.\nD: 1961년 이전 가정에서 만들던 미국 요리들의 인기가 떨어졌다 → '기존 요리를 바꿨다'를 직접 뒷받침.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(차일드 책이 1961년 프랑스 요리책 중 최다 판매)는 책의 인기일 뿐 미국인의 요리 습관 변화를 보여주지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "According to legend, Child inspired Americans to exchange their bland cooking for French cuisine's rich flavors.", "glosses": {"at odds with": "~와 상충하는", "vanquished": "정복된, 패배한", "bland": "밋밋한, 싱거운", "cohort": "집단, 세대"}, "src": "verbal232 Q5 · 24년 8월, 23년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that the “growing interest\"", "choices": ["has been mischaracterized by some observers of American culinary trends of the 1960s", "would not have occurred if Child's book had been the watershed some believed it was", "reflected Americans' aspirations to be perceived as sophisticated about food and cooking", "bolstered certain trends in the publishing industry that accelerated the release of new cookbooks", "confirms Child's influence on at least one segment of the American public"], "columns": null, "pid": "v232_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'a growing interest in the American cooking styles allegedly vanquished by Child'.\n'allegedly vanquished(정복되었다고 주장되는)' → 실제로는 미국 요리가 패배하지 않았다는 뜻.\n차일드 책이 일부 사람들의 믿음처럼 결정적 전환점(watershed)이었다면 미국 요리에 대한 관심이 커지지 않았을 것 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "E(차일드의 영향력 확인)는 반대 방향이다. A(관찰자들이 잘못 규정)는 '오해된 것'은 차일드의 영향이지 '관심 증가' 자체가 아니므로 대상이 어긋난다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "a growing interest in the American cooking styles allegedly vanquished by Child", "glosses": {"watershed": "분수령, 결정적 전환점", "allegedly": "주장되는 바로는", "bolstered": "강화했다"}, "src": "verbal232 Q6 · 24년 8월, 23년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v202_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with doing which of the following?", "choices": ["Comparing two writers’ definitions of style", "Refining a classification of stylistic elements", "Describing a tool for the study of ancient works of art", "Drawing a comparison between visual and verbal arts", "Discussing formal characteristics of ancient works of"], "columns": null, "pid": "v202_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 양식(스타일) 분석은 고대 미술품의 시기와 출처를 결정하는 데 도움이 된다.\n이후 Schapiro의 양식 분류(특히 형식 요소 vs 형식 관계)와 Winter의 견해로 그 분석이 어떻게 쓰이는지 설명.\n→ 고대 미술 연구 도구(양식 분석)를 설명 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "B(분류 체계를 다듬는다)는 Schapiro의 분류가 나와 끌리지만, 저자는 분류를 수정·정교화하지 않고 소개·활용할 뿐이다. A도 두 저자의 '정의 비교'가 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"stylistic": "양식의", "syntax": "구문, 결합 방식", "iconography": "도상(학), 주제·소재"}, "src": "verbal202 Q7 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v202_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the passage, the point of comparing visual style to language is to emphasize that", "choices": ["similar cultures often share similar form elements in their visual art", "subject matter is relatively unimportant in determining the place of origin of a work of visual art", "the elements that constitute visual style differ in their value for establishing relationships between artworks", "the arrangement of form elements in works of visual art observes certain conventions", "the distinguishing features of a particular visual style are likely to have analogs in the literary style that prevails in the same time and place"], "columns": null, "pid": "v202_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'He compares style directly to language as having a similar internal order ... this order (or grammar)'.\n언어에 문법이 있듯 시각 양식도 요소를 결합하는 일정한 질서(규칙)가 있다는 점을 강조.\n= D '형식 요소의 배열이 특정 관례를 따른다'.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(소재는 출처 판단에 덜 중요)는 지문 마지막에 있는 내용이지만 Winter의 언급이고, 언어 비교의 요점은 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "He compares style directly to language as having a similar internal order and expressiveness", "glosses": {"analog": "유사물, 대응물", "convention": "관례, 규칙", "articulated": "표현된, 구성된"}, "src": "verbal202 Q8 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v202_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Pointed arches are mentioned in the passage in order to do which of the following?", "choices": ["underscore the importance of compositional pattern for the stylistic analysis of works of visual art", "highlight a connection between form elements and visual motifs in works of visual art", "illustrate a means of dating ancient architectural works through form elements", "cite a means of identifying ancient architectural works that may lead to errors in dating", "provide an example of a visual motif used by Schapiro in the iconographical analysis of ancient architectural works"], "columns": null, "pid": "v202_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 아치의 넓은 분포를 들어 'form elements alone are insufficient ... one must also look at ... the compositional pattern or syntax.'\n뾰족·둥근 아치는 여러 시대에 퍼져 있어서 요소만으로는 양식을 특정 못함 → 구성 패턴이 중요함을 강조.\n= A.\n정답: A", "trap": "C(형식 요소로 연대를 측정하는 방법)는 정반대다. 아치 예시는 형식 요소만으로는 부족하다는 것을 보여준다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Citing the wide distribution over time of pointed and rounded arches in architecture", "glosses": {"underscore": "강조하다", "compositional": "구성의", "motif": "모티프, 반복 요소"}, "src": "verbal202 Q9 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v28_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Our mass media are much more fascinated by bad ideas or the failure of good ones than by successes: we drown in bad news—tales of how things went wrong—but we have only the most _____ discussion on how they might go right.", "choices": ["incisive", "tantalizing", "trenchant", "cursory", "illusory", "perfunctory"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 앞: 대중매체는 실패에 훨씬 더 매료된다. but: 나쁜 소식에는 빠져 있지만, 잘되는 방법에 대한 논의는 '가장 ( )한' 것뿐.\n빈칸 = 부정, '피상적인, 대충 하는'.\ncursory(피상적인)와 perfunctory(형식적인)가 짝.\n정답: D (cursory), F (perfunctory)", "trap": "incisive/trenchant도 '날카로운'으로 짝을 이루지만 긍정어라 but 뒤의 부족함 대조와 반대다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incisive": "날카로운, 예리한", "trenchant": "신랄한, 예리한", "cursory": "피상적인, 대충의", "perfunctory": "형식적인, 마지못해 하는", "tantalizing": "감질나게 하는", "illusory": "착각의, 환상의"}, "src": "verbal28 Q10"}, {"id": "v218_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In his article, Bazerman highlights Edison's _____ manipulation of the press, including gifts of stock to friendly reporters.", "choices": ["modest", "decorous", "bashful", "brazen", "criminal", "barefaced"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'including gifts of stock to friendly reporters' → 우호적 기자에게 주식을 줌, 노골적인 언론 조작.\n빈칸 = '뻔뻔한, 노골적인'.\nbrazen과 barefaced가 짝.\n정답: D (brazen), F (barefaced)", "trap": "criminal은 뜻이 통할 듯하지만 짝이 없고, 주식 선물이 반드시 범죄라는 근거도 없다. modest/bashful은 반대 의미.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"brazen": "뻔뻔한, 노골적인", "bashful": "수줍은", "barefaced": "뻔뻔한, 노골적인", "modest": "겸손한, 적당한", "decorous": "예의 바른, 점잖은", "criminal": "범죄의"}, "src": "verbal218 Q10 · 25/8, 25/7, 25/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v20_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Well organized and researched and including all significant discoveries of medical scientists, The History of Western Medicines has been justly called __________.", "choices": ["encyclopedic", "long-winded", "exhaustive", "rambling", "overbearing", "undiscriminating"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Well organized and researched and including all significant discoveries' + 'justly(정당하게)'.\n빈칸 = 긍정, '모든 것을 망라한'.\nencyclopedic(백과사전적인)과 exhaustive(철저한, 망라한)가 짝.\n정답: A (encyclopedic), C (exhaustive)", "trap": "long-winded/rambling은 '길다'는 점에서 짝이지만 부정어라 'well organized', 'justly'와 모순된다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"long-winded": "장황한", "rambling": "두서없는", "overbearing": "고압적인, 위압적인", "encyclopedic": "백과사전적인, 망라한", "exhaustive": "철저한, 빠짐없는", "undiscriminating": "무분별한, 안목 없는"}, "src": "verbal20 Q10"}, {"id": "v206_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, most strongly supports the proposed explanation?", "choices": ["The greater warmth of tropical forests enables them to sustain a greater density of plants and animals than temperate forests can.", "There is virtually no overlap between the species that are found in tropical forests and those found in temperate forests.", "Some areas that were temperate forests before the Ice Age are no longer forested.", "The number of plants and animal species is no greater in tropical forests that have arisen since the Ice Age than in temperate forests of comparable size.", "A change in climate tends to increase the rate at which new species become established in a region."], "columns": null, "pid": "v206_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론(설명): 열대림에 종이 더 많은 이유는 빙하기 때 파괴되지 않아 종이 정착할 시간이 더 길었기 때문.\n가정: 차이의 원인은 '열대'라는 환경이 아니라 '시간'이다.\nD: 빙하기 이후 생긴 열대림은 같은 크기의 온대림보다 종이 많지 않다 → 시간이 같으면 차이가 사라짐, 열대 자체는 원인이 아님 → 설명 강화.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(열대의 따뜻함이 더 많은 동식물을 지탱)는 다른 원인을 제시하므로 오히려 설명을 약화시킨다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"temperate": "온대의", "take hold": "자리 잡다, 정착하다", "comparable": "비슷한, 비교할 만한"}, "src": "verbal206 Q13 · 25/8, 25/7, 24/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v30_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage indicates that proponents of the junk food hypothesis assert which of the following about non-fatty fish of the gadid family?", "choices": ["They provide adequate nourishment for sea lions when supplemented with a small number of other species.", "They provide adequate nutrition for adult sea lions but not for juveniles.", "They have been steadily declining in quantity in the Gulf of Alaska since the 1970s.", "They are inadequate to satisfy sea lions’ nutrition requirements even when available in abundance.", "They are too challenging for juvenile sea lions to catch in significant numbers."], "columns": null, "pid": "v30_p4", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the quantity of prey available was high overall, but ... the diet was nutritionally inferior—the junk food hypothesis.'\n먹이 양은 많았지만 비지방성 대구과 어류라 영양적으로 열등 → 풍부해도 영양 필요를 채우지 못함 = D.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(성체에는 충분, 새끼에는 부족)는 마지막 문장의 '새끼가 더 영향받는다'에서 끌리지만, 지문은 성체에게 충분하다고 말하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"gadid": "대구과 어류", "nutritionally inferior": "영양적으로 열등한", "foraging": "먹이 찾기"}, "src": "verbal30 Q14"}, {"id": "v30_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The highlighted sentence (“An alternative … factor.”) performs which of the following functions in the passage?", "choices": ["It demonstrates that over-fishing in the Gulf of Alaska is the likely cause of Steller sea lion decline.", "It supports an argument that the reason for the Steller sea lion decline in the Gulf of Alaska is unlikely to be determined.", "It gives an explanation for the decline in Steller sea lions in the Gulf of Alaska that is at odds with the junk food hypothesis."], "columns": null, "pid": "v30_p4", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "강조 문장 'An alternative view ...': 대구과 어류는 영양적으로 충분하지만 '수량'이 부족했다는 견해.\n이는 '양은 많았지만 질이 낮았다'는 junk food 가설과 상충 → C 맞음.\nA: 'fishing or some other factor'라고 했으므로 남획이 원인이라고 '증명'하지 않음.\nB: 원인을 밝힐 수 없다는 주장은 지문에 없음.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 fishing이 언급돼 끌리지만 'demonstrates ... likely cause'는 지나치게 강하다. 문장은 가능성 있는 견해 하나를 소개할 뿐이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"at odds with": "~와 상충하는", "alternative": "대안적인", "decline": "감소"}, "src": "verbal30 Q15"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.2 / S2 2.5"}, {"set": 4, "sections": [[{"id": "v1_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "While Zora Neale Hurston never avowed an affiliation with surrealism, an artistic movement celebrating the unconscious mind's creative power, French surrealist Guy Ducornet's citing her as an inspiration seems quite _____ given Hurston's intensely imaginative work.", "choices": ["tenable", "arcane", "audacious", "prescient", "eccentric"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "While: 허스턴은 초현실주의와의 관계를 공언한 적이 없지만 → 그래도 뒤 내용은 긍정.\ngiven 'Hurston's intensely imaginative work' → 무의식의 창조력을 찬양하는 초현실주의자가 그녀를 영감의 원천으로 든 것은 '타당하다'.\n빈칸 = 긍정, '납득할 만한' → tenable.\n정답: A (tenable)", "trap": "audacious(대담한)는 While 절(관계 공언 없음)에서 '무리한 주장'처럼 보여 끌리지만, given 이하의 근거는 그 인용이 합당하다는 쪽을 가리킨다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tenable": "타당한, 옹호할 수 있는", "prescient": "선견지명이 있는", "arcane": "난해한, 불가사의한", "audacious": "대담한, 무모한", "eccentric": "별난, 기이한"}, "src": "verbal1 Q1"}, {"id": "v205_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Shark teeth are among the most (i) _____ of all vertebrate fossils. While such (ii) _____ may befit creatures renowned for their appetites, it contrasts with the rarity of shark skeletons.", "choices": null, "columns": [["durable", "useful", "common"], ["utility", "abundance", "stability"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 문장: 그런 ( )은 식욕으로 유명한 생물(이빨이 많이 필요/많이 빠짐)에 어울리지만, 상어 골격의 '희귀함'과 대조된다.\nrarity의 반대 → 풍부함 = abundance.\n(i) 그렇다면 상어 이빨은 가장 '흔한' 화석 중 하나 → common.\n정답: C (common), E (abundance)", "trap": "durable/stability 조합도 '이빨은 단단하다'는 상식으로 끌리지만, 대조 대상이 rarity(희귀성)이므로 양을 나타내는 말이 필요하다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"durable": "내구성 있는", "useful": "유용한", "common": "흔한", "utility": "유용성", "abundance": "풍부함", "stability": "안정성"}, "src": "verbal205 Q2 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v199_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Some critics claim that because medical journals receive (i) _____ selection of findings from clinical trials─mainly those trials that show (ii) _____ results for the drugs being tested─readers of those journals believe that some medications are more (iii) _____ than they really are, even when those medications are little more than placebos.", "choices": null, "columns": [["a heterogeneous", "an predictable", "a winnowed"], ["controversial", "inconclusive", "positive"], ["expensive", "prevalent", "effective"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 대시 안: 'mainly those trials that show ( ) results' → 결과가 독자를 오도하는 방향이므로 positive.\n(i) 그런 시험만 실린다 → 선별된, 걸러낸 표본 → a winnowed.\n(iii) 위약과 다름없는 약도 실제보다 더 '효과적'이라고 믿게 됨 → effective.\n정답: C (a winnowed), F (positive), I (effective)", "trap": "(iii) prevalent는 '흔한'이라 placebo(효과 없음)와의 대조가 성립하지 않는다. (i) a heterogeneous(다양한)는 선별(bias) 논리와 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"winnowed": "골라낸, 추려낸", "a heterogeneous": "이질적인, 다양한", "an predictable": "예측 가능한", "a winnowed": "선별된, 걸러낸", "controversial": "논란이 많은", "inconclusive": "결론이 나지 않는", "positive": "긍정적인", "expensive": "비싼", "prevalent": "널리 퍼진", "effective": "효과적인"}, "src": "verbal199 Q3 · 24년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v7_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["cite evidence that appears to contradict a widely held assumption", "present contrasting interpretations of a particular research finding", "explain how a particular environmental change can produce diverse outcomes", "note an unexpected finding and summarize new possible explanation for it", "identify a correlation and explain why one hypothesis about it is more persuasive than others"], "columns": null, "pid": "v7_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 기존 연구(산성 토양에서 RBS 적고 작다) + 가능한 설명들 → Yet 레이크 클레어에서 산성인데도 크고 많은 RBS 발견(예상 밖 결과) → 'One hypothesis' 지역 적응이라는 새 설명 제시.\n= D '예상 밖의 발견을 언급하고 그에 대한 새 가능한 설명을 요약'.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(널리 받아들여진 가정을 반박하는 증거 제시)는 Yet 문장에서 끌리지만, 지문의 중심은 새 가설 제시이고 '널리 퍼진 가정'이라는 말도 과하다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"intraspecific": "종 내의", "local adaptation": "지역 적응", "watershed": "유역"}, "src": "verbal7 Q4"}, {"id": "v7_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred about the studies mentioned in the highlighted portion of the passage?", "choices": ["They may have undercounted RBS in their study areas due to faulty methodology.", "They focused less on adult RBS than on RBS in the early stages of their development.", "They found evidence that acidic conditions adversely affect the prey on which RBS depend.", "They drew unsubstantiated conclusions about the possible adverse effects of acidic conditions on RBS.", "They were conducted in areas where the soil conditions were similar to those at Lake Claire Watershed."], "columns": null, "pid": "v7_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "강조 부분: 연구들이 'areas with acidic soils'에서 RBS가 적고 작다는 것을 보였다.\nYet 레이크 클레어도 'soil conditions are acidic' → 두 곳 모두 산성 토양이라 비교가 성립.\n= E '레이크 클레어와 비슷한 토양 조건에서 수행되었다'.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(근거 없는 결론)는 레이크 클레어 결과가 반례처럼 보여 끌리지만, 지문은 기존 연구를 비판하지 않고 지역 적응 가능성만 제시한다. C는 먹이 감소를 '가능성'으로만 언급했다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"scarce": "드문, 부족한", "acidity tolerance": "산성 내성", "unsubstantiated": "입증되지 않은"}, "src": "verbal7 Q5"}, {"id": "v233_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "By and large, the writing of professional philosophers over the last century gets high marks for lucidity, though one can certainly point to a few whose prose is notably _____.", "choices": ["slipshod", "muddled", "pretentious", "turbid", "methodical", "systematic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "though: 대체로 철학자들의 글은 lucidity(명료함)로 높은 점수 ↔ 몇몇은 눈에 띄게 ( )하다.\n빈칸 = lucidity의 반대 '불명료한, 흐릿한'.\nmuddled(혼란스러운)와 turbid(탁한, 불분명한)가 짝.\n정답: B (muddled), D (turbid)", "trap": "slipshod(엉성한)와 pretentious(허세 부리는)도 부정적이라 끌리지만, 명료함의 반대를 정확히 담지 못하고 짝이 없다. methodical/systematic은 짝이지만 긍정어.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lucidity": "명료험", "muddled": "혼란스러운, 뒤죽박죽인", "turbid": "탁한, 불분명한", "slipshod": "엉성한, 대충의", "pretentious": "허세 부리는", "methodical": "체계적인, 꼼꼼한", "systematic": "체계적인"}, "src": "verbal233 Q9 · 25/11, 25/4, 25/1 중국후기"}, {"id": "v31_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Miller reminded his clients that labor relationships are inherently _____; the interests of business owners are diametrically opposed to those of employees.", "choices": ["adversarial", "exploitative", "mercenary", "antagonistic", "variable", "changeable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론 뒤가 빈칸을 설명: 사업주의 이익은 직원의 이익과 'diametrically opposed(정반대)'.\n빈칸 = '대립적인'.\nadversarial과 antagonistic이 짝.\n정답: A (adversarial), D (antagonistic)", "trap": "exploitative(착취적인)는 노사관계에 대해 그럴듯하지만, 문장은 이익이 '대립한다'고만 말하지 한쪽이 착취한다고 말하지 않는다. variable/changeable은 짝이지만 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"adversarial": "적대적인, 대립하는", "exploitative": "착취적인", "mercenary": "돈만 밝히는", "antagonistic": "적대적인, 대립하는", "variable": "변동하는", "changeable": "변하기 쉬운"}, "src": "verbal31 Q6"}, {"id": "v33_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "His own writing style was _____: colorful and tart in its choice of language, willing to run risks in its allusions, metaphors, and verbal juxtapositions, prone to irreverent conclusions designed to surprise or startle.", "choices": ["effusive", "audacious", "lyrical", "striking", "ornate", "emotional"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤가 빈칸을 설명: 'willing to run risks' + 'designed to surprise or startle'.\n위험을 감수 → audacious(대담한), 놀라게 하는 → striking(인상적인, 눈에 띄는).\n두 단어 모두 '대담하고 눈길을 끄는' 문체를 나타내는 짝.\n정답: B (audacious), D (striking)", "trap": "ornate/lyrical/effusive는 'colorful'에서 끌리지만, 화려함·감정 분출이지 위험 감수·놀라게 함의 의미가 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"effusive": "감정이 넘치는", "audacious": "대담한", "lyrical": "서정적인", "striking": "눈에 띄는, 인상적인", "ornate": "화려하게 장식된", "emotional": "감정적인"}, "src": "verbal33 Q9"}, {"id": "v215_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Even the cleverest use of time management techniques is powerless to _____ sum of minutes in a person’s life, so people squeeze as much as they could into each one of them.", "choices": ["justify", "quantify", "augment", "enrich", "measure", "extend"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "so: 시간 관리 기술도 인생의 총 분(minutes)의 합을 ( )하지 못한다 → 그래서 한 분 한 분에 최대한 많이 밀어 넣는다.\n총량을 '늘리지' 못하니 밀도를 높인다는 인과 → 빈칸 = '늘리다'.\naugment와 extend가 짝.\n정답: C (augment), F (extend)", "trap": "quantify/measure는 서로 짝을 이뤄 가장 위험한 함정이다. 하지만 '측정할 수 없어서 더 채워 넣는다'는 인과가 성립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"justify": "정당화하다", "quantify": "수량화하다", "augment": "늘리다, 증대하다", "enrich": "풍부하게 하다", "measure": "측정하다", "extend": "늘리다, 연장하다"}, "src": "verbal215 Q8 · 25년 3월, 24년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v23_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author's primary purpose is to", "choices": ["identify the influences informing a particular geological theory about the processes that have shaped Earth's surface", "identify differences between two views of the extraterrestrial impactors and argue that the phenomenon has influenced the development of plate tectonic theory", "argue that an explanation is based on dubious evidence and propose an alternative explanation", "discuss an explanation and place that explanation under theoretical context", "suggest that an apparent discrepancy poses a serious problem for a particular theory that many have believed"], "columns": null, "pid": "v23_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: 판 운동 에너지 설명의 '빈틈(loose end)' → Shaw의 외계 충돌체 설명 소개 → 이를 기존 판구조론·고전 지질학(뉴턴의 전제)과 대비하며 이론적 맥락 안에 위치시킴.\n= D '한 설명을 논의하고 그것을 이론적 맥락 속에 놓는다'.\n정답: D", "trap": "E(겉보기 불일치가 기존 이론에 심각한 문제)는 'loose end'에서 끌리지만 도입부일 뿐, 지문의 중심은 Shaw의 설명이다. C는 저자가 기존 설명을 반박하거나 새 설명을 '제안'하지 않으므로 틀림.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"impactor": "충돌체", "intrinsic": "본질적인, 내재하는", "continuum": "연속체", "catastrophic": "격변의, 재앙적인"}, "src": "verbal23 Q10"}, {"id": "v23_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage mentions the \"continuum\" in order to", "choices": ["point out a relationship between plate tectonics and the nineteenth-century geology", "explain how a theory of Newton's could influence geology and plate tectonic theory", "distinguish between two sources of energy that contributed to the development of Earth's surface", "point out a similarity between the surface of impactors and the surface of Earth", "identify a feature of Shaw's view that deviates from current scientific theories"], "columns": null, "pid": "v23_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Shaw's revolutionary \"open-system\" view recognizes a continuum ..., whereas modern plate tectonic theory ...'\ncontinuum(지구·외계 역학의 연속성)은 Shaw 견해의 특징이며, whereas로 현재 판구조론과 대비된다.\n= E '현재 과학 이론과 어긋나는 Shaw 견해의 특징을 밝힌다'.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(두 에너지원을 구분)는 오히려 반대다. continuum은 둘을 '분리할 수 없다(indivisible)'는 생각을 나타낸다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Shaw's revolutionary \"open-system\" view recognizes a continuum between terrestrial and extraterrestrial dynamics", "glosses": {"continuum": "연속체", "deviate": "벗어나다", "indivisible": "분리할 수 없는"}, "src": "verbal23 Q11"}, {"id": "v23_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about tectonic theory?", "choices": ["It has led scientists to overlook an important contribution to classical geologists from Newton.", "It has been more successful than was classical geology in accounting for heat loss from Earth's core.", "It is based on a premise about Earth's processes discerned in Newton's thought.", "It has correctly explained the effects of extraterrestrial impactors on Earth's surface.", "It corrects a fundamental flaw in classical geology."], "columns": null, "pid": "v23_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 판구조론은 '고전 지질학처럼(like classical geology)' 지구 내재적·점진적 과정에 기반.\n그리고 'Classical geology borrowed a decisive ... premise from Newton—the independence of Earth's processes from any astronomical context.'\n→ 판구조론도 뉴턴에게서 나온 그 전제(지구 과정의 독립성)에 기반 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "E(고전 지질학의 근본 결함을 수정)는 반대다. 지문은 두 이론이 같은 전제를 공유한다고 말한다. D는 판구조론이 충돌체를 '과소평가'했다는 Shaw 주장과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"premise": "전제", "discerned": "식별된, 간파된", "astronomical": "천문학의"}, "src": "verbal23 Q12"}], [{"id": "v30_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Many creative photographers were delighted to find in instant photography a mode that encouraged them to stop viewing photography as _____ and start viewing it as something they could handle with spontaneity, even derision.", "choices": ["sacrosanct", "ephemeral", "malleable", "egalitarian", "autonomous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "stop viewing photography as ( ) and start viewing it as ... spontaneity, even derision(조롱).\n빈칸은 '즉흥적으로, 심지어 조롱하듯 다룰 수 있는 것'의 반대 → '신성불가침의, 함부로 못 하는'.\nsacrosanct가 정답.\n정답: A (sacrosanct)", "trap": "ephemeral은 '인스턴트' 사진에서 연상되지만 즉흥성·조롱과 대조되는 개념이 아니다. malleable(유연한)은 오히려 뒤쪽 의미와 같은 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sacrosanct": "신성불가침의", "ephemeral": "덧없는, 일시적인", "malleable": "유연한, 다루기 쉬운", "egalitarian": "평등주의적인", "autonomous": "자율적인"}, "src": "verbal30 Q1"}, {"id": "v4_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "During the decade 2000–2010 in the United States, the increase in self-employed Hispanic entrepreneurs (i) _____ the increase in Hispanic workers overall. Historically, Hispanics have been (ii) _____ in the self-employment sector, so this change reduced the amount by which the Hispanic self-employment rate trailed the overall self-employment rate.", "choices": null, "columns": [["catalyzed", "tracked", "exceeded"], ["underrepresented", "undercompensated", "underappreciated"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "마지막 결과: 히스패닉 자영업 비율이 전체 자영업 비율에 뒤처진 정도가 '줄었다'.\n(ii) 원래 뒤처져 있었다 = 자영업 부문에서 과소 대표됨 → underrepresented.\n(i) 격차가 줄었으려면 자영업자 증가가 히스패닉 노동자 전체 증가를 '넘어섰다' → exceeded.\n정답: C (exceeded), D (underrepresented)", "trap": "(i) tracked(따라갔다)는 같은 속도라 비율 격차가 줄지 않는다. catalyzed는 인과관계라 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"trailed": "뒤쳐져서 따라가다", "catalyzed": "촉진했다", "tracked": "따라갔다, 비슷하게 움직였다", "exceeded": "넘어섰다", "underrepresented": "과소 대표된", "undercompensated": "보수를 적게 받는", "underappreciated": "과소평가된"}, "src": "verbal4 Q2"}, {"id": "v10_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The origin tales of the Native American Koasati people, which offer explanations of how the universe came into being, use two different strategies: some are direct, presenting an explanation that is central to the tale, while others are (i) _____ in that the explanation is (ii) _____ the tale.", "choices": null, "columns": [["oblique", "episodic", "veracious"], ["incidental to", "explicit in", "dependent on"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "some are direct ... while others are (i): direct와 대조 → 간접적인 = oblique.\n'presenting an explanation that is central to the tale'과 대조 → (ii) 설명이 이야기의 '부수적인' 요소 = incidental to.\n정답: A (oblique), D (incidental to)", "trap": "(i) episodic(삽화식의)은 이야기 구조를 말하는 것 같아 끌리지만 direct의 반대가 아니다. (ii) explicit in은 direct 쪽 특징이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"veracious": "진실한", "oblique": "간접적인, 우회적인", "episodic": "삽화식의, 에피소드 형식의", "incidental to": "~에 부수적인", "explicit in": "~에 명시된", "dependent on": "~에 의존하는"}, "src": "verbal10 Q3"}, {"id": "v18_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "For whom is Shipton's 《A New History of Jazz》 intended? It is written in (i)__________ language and contains no extended musical analysis, suggesting that it is meant for amateurs. But as it is twice as long as the next-longest history of the subject, my guess is that general readers will be put off by its (ii)__________. On the other hand, its great length is precisely what enables Shipton to avoid (iii)__________ the story of jazz's development.", "choices": null, "columns": [["accessible", "ornate", "graphic"], ["paucity of exposition", "proliferation of detail", "preponderance of jargon"], ["belaboring", "oversimplifying", "extolling"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AEH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 음악 분석이 없어 아마추어용으로 보인다 → '쉬운, 이해하기 쉬운' 언어 = accessible.\n(ii) 다음 가장 긴 역사책의 두 배 → 일반 독자는 그 '세부 사항의 과다'에 질릴 것 = proliferation of detail.\n(iii) On the other hand: 그 길이 덕분에 이야기를 '지나치게 단순화'하지 않을 수 있다 = oversimplifying.\n정답: A (accessible), E (proliferation of detail), H (oversimplifying)", "trap": "(iii) belaboring(장황하게 늘어놓기)은 '길이'와 연관돼 끌리지만, 긴 길이가 '피하게 해주는' 것은 단순화이지 장황함이 아니다. (ii) preponderance of jargon은 (i)의 쉬운 언어와 모순.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"belaboring": "장황하게 늘어놓기", "accessible": "이해하기 쉬운", "ornate": "화려한, 수식이 많은", "graphic": "생생한", "paucity of exposition": "설명의 부족", "proliferation of detail": "세부 사항의 과다", "preponderance of jargon": "전문용어의 과다", "oversimplifying": "지나치게 단순화하기", "extolling": "극찬하기"}, "src": "verbal18 Q4"}, {"id": "v16_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true of the \"equilibrium theory\"?", "choices": ["It implies that very few island populations are able to colonize continental areas.", "It can accommodate two-way biogeographic traffic between islands and the mainland.", "It necessarily assumes that island species originate on continents.", "It has been undermined recently by phylogenetic analyses.", "It questions the distinction between island and continental populations."], "columns": null, "pid": "v16_p3", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'There is, however, no fundamental mechanism in the equilibrium theory ... to preclude island species from colonizing the mainland.'\n섬 종이 대륙으로 가는 것을 막는 메커니즘이 없다 → 양방향 이동을 수용할 수 있다 = B.\n정답: B", "trap": "D(계통 분석으로 약화됨)는 함정이다. 약화된 것은 '일방통행이라는 믿음(belief)'이지 평형 이론이 아니다. C는 정반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "There is, however, no fundamental mechanism in the equilibrium theory of island biogeography to preclude island species from colonizing the mainland.", "glosses": {"biota": "생물상", "preclude": "막다, 배제하다", "phylogenetic": "계통 발생의", "colonize": "군집을 형성하다, 정착하다"}, "src": "verbal16 Q12"}, {"id": "v16_q13", "type": "RC_select", "blanks": null, "stem": "Select the sentence that presents a presupposition.", "choices": null, "columns": null, "pid": "v16_p3", "answer": "SENTENCE", "answer_sentence": "We take it for granted that island populations must have a continental origin, and not the other way around.", "explanation": "presupposition(전제, 당연시되는 가정)을 찾는 문제.\n첫 문장 'We take it for granted that ...'은 '당연하게 여긴다'는 표현 그대로 섬 개체군이 대륙에서 기원했다는 전제를 제시.\n이후 문장들은 이 전제가 흔들리고 있음을 보여준다.\n정답: 'We take it for granted that island populations must have a continental origin, and not the other way around.'", "trap": "'The belief in one-way biogeographic traffic ...' 문장도 같은 믿음을 언급하지만, 이는 전제가 '무너지고 있다'는 내용이지 전제를 제시하는 문장이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"presupposition": "전제", "take it for granted": "당연하게 여기다", "biogeographic": "생물지리학적인"}, "src": "verbal16 Q13"}, {"id": "v4_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with", "choices": ["discussing a controversial aspect of specific legislation relating to CO₂", "explaining the science of a new process for capturing CO₂", "highlighting the shortcomings of a specific method of combating climate change", "arguing that emission technologies are the most effective method of combating climate change", "summarizing the advantages of relying on legislation to combat climate change"], "columns": null, "pid": "v4_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문: 45Q 법안 소개 → 가장 논란이 되는 용도(enhanced oil recovery) 설명 → 비판자 입장 → 옹호 논리(배출 감소, Waltzer).\n= A '특정 CO₂ 관련 법안의 논란이 되는 측면을 논의한다'.\n정답: A", "trap": "C(특정 방법의 단점 부각)는 비판 부분만 본 것이다. 지문은 단점과 장점을 모두 다루고 오히려 옹호 쪽으로 마무리된다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sequestered": "격리된, 저장된", "Orwellian": "(전체주의적) 기만적인", "subsidy": "보조금"}, "src": "verbal4 Q5"}, {"id": "v4_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, \"some environmental critics\" object to the 45Q legislation on which of the following grounds?", "choices": ["It will drive up the price of captured CO₂.", "The process of extracting extra oil could have unforeseen environmental consequences.", "Fossil fuels extracted via enhanced oil recovery typically produce more carbon emissions than ethanol or natural gas.", "It will replace current subsidy programs that have been proven effective.", "Its proponents' claims that it is part of a climate change solution are misleading."], "columns": null, "pid": "v4_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'may sound Orwellian, and some environmental critics have attacked 45Q as just another fossil-fuel subsidy program in disguise.'\n'기후 해법'이라 하면서 실은 화석연료 보조금의 위장 → 기후 해법이라는 주장이 기만적이다 = E.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(그렇게 얻은 화석연료가 더 많은 배출)는 그럴듯한 환경 논리지만 지문에 언급되지 않았다. B도 예측 못 한 결과 언급 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "some environmental critics have attacked 45Q as just another fossil-fuel subsidy program in disguise", "glosses": {"in disguise": "위장한", "Orwellian": "기만적인, 전체주의적인", "misleading": "오해를 부르는"}, "src": "verbal4 Q6"}, {"id": "v4_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that Kurt Waltzer would likely agree with which of the following statements about the 45Q legislation?", "choices": ["It will likely replace some of the fossil-fuel subsidy programs that are currently in effect.", "It is likely to impede the development of economically efficient ways of recapturing CO₂ for sequestration.", "The positive effects of other portions of the legislation will likely outweigh the environmental harm caused by its controversial aspects.", "The incentives it provides for the production of more fossil fuel are an ineffective means of reducing the production of CO₂ byproducts.", "Its provision of corporate tax credits for using CO₂ for enhanced oil recovery may offer a net gain in environmental terms."], "columns": null, "pid": "v4_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Waltzer는 탄소 포집을 '에너지 기술'로 만드는 것이 CO₂ 제거의 광범위한 상업적 채택을 향한 'first step'이라고 본다.\n또 바로 앞 문장: enhanced oil recovery가 CO₂를 지하에 격리해 현재 배출을 줄이는 듯하다.\n→ 석유 생산이 늘어나도 환경적으로 순이익이 있을 수 있다는 E에 동의할 것.\n정답: E", "trap": "C('법안의 다른 부분'의 긍정 효과)는 범위 밖이다. 지문은 법안의 다른 부분을 다루지 않는다. D는 Waltzer 입장과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"net gain": "순이익", "impede": "방해하다", "incentive": "유인, 장려책"}, "src": "verbal4 Q7"}, {"id": "v12_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Restoring the old practice of producing fish in rice fields does not just make environmental and economic sense; it has the added advantage that it _____ benefits the very poor.", "choices": ["abnormally", "predominantly", "eminently", "moderately", "particularly", "unnaturally"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "does not just ... ; it has the added advantage: 환경·경제적 이점에 더해 '특히' 극빈층에게 이익이 된다.\n빈칸 = 강조 부사 '특히, 두드러지게'.\neminently(두드러지게, 매우)와 particularly(특히)가 짝.\n정답: C (eminently), E (particularly)", "trap": "predominantly(주로)는 단독으로 자연스럽지만 짝이 없다(이익이 '주로' 빈곤층에만 간다는 뜻이 됨). abnormally/unnaturally는 짝이지만 부정적이라 'advantage'와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rice fields": "논", "eminently": "두드러지게, 매우", "abnormally": "비정상적으로", "predominantly": "주로, 대부분", "moderately": "적당히", "particularly": "특히", "unnaturally": "부자연스럽게"}, "src": "verbal12 Q8"}, {"id": "v6_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The early stages of being trained to ride a motorcycle are all about developing muscle memory, repeating combinations of hand-foot movements until they are _____ and precise.", "choices": ["aberrant", "innate", "reflexive", "inborn", "automatic", "calculated"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근육 기억 = 반복 연습으로 동작이 생각 없이 나오게 하는 것.\n빈칸 = '저절로 나오는' + and precise.\nreflexive(반사적인)와 automatic(자동적인)이 짝.\n정답: C (reflexive), E (automatic)", "trap": "innate/inborn(타고난)은 서로 짝이라 위험하지만, 훈련과 반복으로 '만들어지는' 것은 타고난 것이 될 수 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"aberrant": "일탈적인, 비정상적인", "innate": "타고난", "reflexive": "반사적인", "inborn": "타고난", "automatic": "자동적인", "calculated": "계산된, 의도적인"}, "src": "verbal6 Q9"}, {"id": "v16_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The auditors are relying on the failing bank to make changes that it has steadfastly resisted for years and even now does not seem _____ to carry out.", "choices": ["able", "impatient", "destined", "disinclined", "loath", "keen"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "은행은 그 변화를 수년간 '완강히 저항(steadfastly resisted)'했고, 지금도 그것을 실행하려고 ( )해 보이지 않는다.\n저항의 연장선 → 'does not seem eager' 즉 빈칸 = '열망하는'.\nimpatient(~하고 싶어 안달하는)와 keen(열망하는)이 짝.\n정답: B (impatient), F (keen)", "trap": "disinclined/loath는 서로 짝이고 '저항'과 비슷해 보이지만, 앞의 not과 결합하면 '꺼리지 않는다'가 되어 의미가 뒤집힌다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"impatient": "~하고 싶어 안달하는", "able": "할 수 있는", "destined": "운명 지어진", "disinclined": "내키지 않는", "loath": "꺼리는", "keen": "열망하는"}, "src": "verbal16 Q8"}, {"id": "v28_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, provides the strongest support for the argument given?", "choices": ["The drivers of vehicles behind a gravel truck are more likely to remain close behind the truck if the trucks cargo box is covered than if it is uncovered.", "Most trucks that carry gravel already carry tarpaulins that their drivers use to cover the cargo box when they are carrying sand, which can blow out of the cargo box in significant quantities.", "Of all the damage that occurs to vehicles on the highway, debris that flies off trucks is the cause of only a very small fraction.", "The proposed law allows open-topped trucks on the highway to have uncovered cargo boxes whenever their cargo boxes are empty.", "Because of the great weight of a load of gravel, the driver of a gravel truck is often driving much more slowly than most of the other vehicles on the road."], "columns": null, "pid": "v28_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 덮개 법안은 피해를 크게 줄이지 못할 것이다. 근거: 날아오는 자갈은 적재함보다 타이어 홈에서 나온다.\nA: 적재함이 덮여 있으면 뒤차가 트럭 바로 뒤에 붙어 있을 가능성이 더 크다 → 타이어 자갈에 더 노출 → 피해가 줄지 않거나 오히려 늘 수 있음 → 결론 강화.\n정답: A", "trap": "C(트럭 파편은 전체 차량 피해의 작은 부분)는 '자갈 트럭으로 인한 피해'라는 논의 범위와 무관하다. D(빈 적재함은 덮지 않아도 됨)도 빈 트럭에는 적재함에서 날아올 자갈이 없으므로 결론에 영향 없음.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tarpaulin": "방수포", "cargo box": "적재함", "wedged": "끼인"}, "src": "verbal28 Q11"}, {"id": "v202_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, scientists are able to discover weathered material on the Martian surface because they have benefited from which of the following?", "choices": ["A new method to analyze volcanic craters created on the Martian surface", "An improved ability to detect hydrated materials on the Martian surface", "A more sophisticated understanding of the effect of wind-borne dust on the Martian surface", "A decision to look for water primarily in heavily cratered highland regions", "A better understanding of how erosion might affect clay deposits"], "columns": null, "pid": "v202_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'New high resolution mapping data and close-up surface studies have revealed clays and other hydrated minerals.'\n고해상도 지도·근접 조사 = 수화 광물을 탐지하는 능력 향상 → B.\n'the scientists were not looking closely enough'도 같은 맥락.\n정답: B", "trap": "D(크레이터 고지대에서 찾기로 결정)는 'heavily cratered highland regions'가 나와 끌리지만, 그곳은 점토가 발견된 장소일 뿐 새 탐색 전략이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hydrated": "수화된(물 분자를 포함한)", "unweathered": "풍화되지 않은", "oxidized": "산화된"}, "src": "verbal202 Q5 · 24년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v202_q6", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that the author would agree with which of the following statements regarding the reasoning discussed in the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["It provides the basis for an explanation of why water on Mars has been difficult to find until recently.", "It correctly identifies a consequence of water flowing on the Martian surface.", "It depends on a false assumption about how water and volcanic materials interact on Mars."], "columns": null, "pid": "v202_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "강조 문장: 물이 오래 흘렀다면 화산 광물을 풍화시켜 점토 등 수화 광물을 만들었을 것이다.\n저자: 'the scientists were not looking closely enough' → 이후 실제로 점토·수화 광물이 발견됨.\n→ 추론 자체(물 흐름 → 수화 광물)는 옳았고, 관찰이 부족했을 뿐 → B만 맞음.\nC는 반대(가정이 틀린 것이 아님). A: 그 추론은 물을 찾기 어려웠던 이유를 설명하지 않는다.\n정답: B", "trap": "C(잘못된 가정에 의존)는 '과학자들이 틀렸다'는 흐름 때문에 끌리지만, 틀린 것은 관찰의 정밀도이지 추론 속 가정이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"weathered": "풍화된", "hydrated phases": "수화된 상(광물)", "extended period": "오랜 기간"}, "src": "verbal202 Q6 · 24년 6월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.7 / S2 2.7"}, {"set": 5, "sections": [[{"id": "v35_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The prime minister's reputation for _____ was sullied when it was revealed that he had known of fraudulent activities taking place in the country's banking system but failed to report them.", "choices": ["solicitude", "impassivity", "probity", "diplomacy", "forbearance"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: reputation for ___ was sullied(평판이 더럽혀졌다) + 은행 사기를 알고도 보고하지 않음.\n사기를 묵인한 행위로 '손상된' 평판이므로, 원래 평판은 정직·청렴이었어야 한다.\n빈칸 = 긍정, '정직함/청렴'이라는 뜻.\nprobity(청렴, 정직)가 정확히 맞는다.\n정답: C (probity)", "trap": "diplomacy(외교술)나 forbearance(인내)도 긍정적 평판이지만, 사기를 '보고하지 않은 것'으로 훼손되는 덕목은 정직/청렴이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"solicitude": "배려, 염려", "impassivity": "무감각, 냉담", "probity": "청렴, 정직", "diplomacy": "외교(술), 수완", "forbearance": "인내, 관용"}, "src": "verbal35 Q1"}, {"id": "v225_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Although trains may use energy more (i) _____ than do automobiles, the latter move only when they contain at least one occupant, whereas railway carriages spend a considerable amount of time running up and down tracks (ii) _____, or nearly so.", "choices": null, "columns": [["lavishly", "efficiently", "routinely"], ["vacant", "unimpeded", "overloaded"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although(양보) 구조: 기차가 에너지를 더 ___하게 쓸지 몰라도, (그러나) 자동차는 사람이 탈 때만 움직이는 반면 기차는 ___ 상태로 오간다.\n(i) 양보절이므로 기차에 유리한 내용 → efficiently(효율적으로).\n(ii) 'at least one occupant'와 대조 + 'or nearly so(거의 그런 상태)' → 승객이 없는 상태, vacant(텅 빈).\n즉 효율은 좋아도 빈 차로 다니는 시간이 많다는 반전 논리.\n정답: B (efficiently), D (vacant)", "trap": "(ii) overloaded(과적된)는 occupant 대비와 정반대이고, unimpeded(방해받지 않는)는 'or nearly so'와 승객 대비 논리에 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lavishly": "아낌없이, 낭비적으로", "efficiently": "효율적으로", "routinely": "일상적으로, 판에 박힌 듯", "vacant": "비어 있는", "unimpeded": "방해받지 않는", "overloaded": "과적된, 너무 많이 실은"}, "src": "verbal225 Q2 · 24년 2월, 23년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v235_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Whatever the level of the museum's past (i) _____ American art, it pales beside its current (ii) _____. Since opening its renovated and expanded building, the museum has relegated American paintings to hard-to-find corners of the museum. It is as if American art is (iii) _____ the overwhelmingly European narrative that dominates the permanent collection galleries.", "choices": null, "columns": [["advocacy of", "enthusiasm for", "neglect of"], ["craze", "disdain", "support"], ["fundamental to", "excluded from", "privileged over"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CEH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심 단서: 미국 회화를 'hard-to-find corners'로 밀어냈다(relegated) → 현재 태도는 부정적.\n(ii) 현재 태도 = 부정 → disdain(경멸).\n(i) 'Whatever the level of past ___, it pales beside its current ___' = 과거의 ___도 지금에 비하면 아무것도 아니다 → 같은 방향(부정)이어야 비교가 성립 → neglect of(무시).\n(iii) 미국 미술이 유럽 중심 서사에서 '배제된' 것 같다 → excluded from.\n정답: C (neglect of), E (disdain), H (excluded from)", "trap": "(i)에 advocacy/enthusiasm(긍정)을 넣으면 'pales beside(~앞에서 무색하다)'의 비교 방향이 깨진다. 같은 성질의 정도 비교임에 주의.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pales beside": "A가 B 앞에서 무색해지다", "advocacy of": "~에 대한 옹호", "enthusiasm for": "~에 대한 열광", "neglect of": "~에 대한 무시, 방치", "craze": "열풍, 대유행", "disdain": "경멸, 무시", "support": "지지", "fundamental to": "~에 근본적인", "excluded from": "~에서 배제된", "privileged over": "~보다 우대받는"}, "src": "verbal235 Q3 · 25/4, 25/3, 25/1 중국후기"}, {"id": "v237_q4", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author suggests which of the following about the early British colonies in North America that failed?", "choices": ["Their inhabitants’ worldview was deeply affected with native people and practices.", "Their inhabitants experienced critical food shortages in part because their culture hindered their ability to exploit seasonally available resources.", "Their longevity would have been greater had the inhabitants adopted more of the fishing technologies used by Native Americans."], "columns": null, "pid": "v237_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the settlers' mindset prevented them from living like the native inhabitants', 'abundance is seasonal', 원주민은 계절마다 다른 식량원을 이용.\nB: 실패한 식민지 주민들은 문화(고정성, fixity) 때문에 계절별 자원을 이용하지 못해 식량 부족을 겪었다 → 'failed amid abundance' + mindset + seasonal의 결합으로 지지됨.\nA: 정착민의 세계관은 원주민과 '근본적으로 달랐다(profoundly different)' → 반대.\nC: 어업 기술(weirs)은 이미 배웠고, 핵심은 기술이 아니라 mobility였다 → 지지 안 됨.\n정답: B", "trap": "C는 지문에 나온 weirs를 이용한 함정. 저자는 기술 부족이 아니라 '이동성(mobility)'을 받아들이지 못한 것을 핵심으로 본다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"weir": "어살(물고기 잡는 울타리)", "fixity": "고정성, 정착성", "mindset": "사고방식", "longevity": "존속 기간, 수명"}, "src": "verbal237 Q4 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v237_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions \"brushwood weirs” primarily in order to", "choices": ["demonstrate that Native Americans provided certain forms of assistance to colonial settlers", "identify a skill that allowed Native Americans to thrive in regions where colonies failed to", "distinguish the kinds of technologies used by Native Americans from those used by colonial settlers", "acknowledge that colonial settlers adopted certain American ways, even though they failed in the New World", "contrast the assumptions of British colonial settlers and Native Americans in the New World"], "columns": null, "pid": "v237_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'From Native Americans, the settlers learned such skills as building brushwood weirs..., but they did not adopt the real key to success: mobility.'\nweirs는 정착민이 원주민에게서 '배운(받아들인)' 기술의 예이고, but 이후 '그래도 핵심(이동성)은 못 받아들여 실패했다'로 이어진다.\nD: 정착민이 일부 원주민 방식을 받아들였음을 인정(acknowledge)하면서도 실패했다 → 정확한 기능.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 '원주민이 도움을 줬다'는 데 초점이 있어 기능이 빗나간다. B는 weirs가 원주민 번성의 원인이라 하지만 지문은 mobility가 핵심이라 한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "brushwood weirs", "glosses": {"brushwood": "잡목, 덤불 가지", "weir": "어살, 둑", "acknowledge": "인정하다", "thrive": "번성하다"}, "src": "verbal237 Q5 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v9_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The reliable production of usable energy through the controlled fusion of hydrogen atoms into helium remains an elusive dream: even the most ardent efforts to achieve it have thus far been _____.", "choices": ["concealed", "debated", "thwarted", "maligned", "veiled", "frustrated"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: remains an elusive dream(여전히 잡히지 않는 꿈) + 콜론(:) → 뒤는 앞의 부연 설명.\n아무리 열렬한 노력도 지금까지 '좌절되었다'는 뜻이 필요.\n빈칸 = 부정, '실패하다/좌절되다'.\nthwarted와 frustrated가 같은 의미로 짝을 이룬다.\n정답: C (thwarted), F (frustrated)", "trap": "concealed/veiled(숨겨진)는 짝은 맞지만 '꿈이 잡히지 않는다'는 의미와 무관하다. debated, maligned도 실패의 의미가 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"maligned": "비방을 받은", "concealed": "숨겨진", "debated": "논쟁된", "thwarted": "좌절된, 방해받은", "veiled": "베일에 싸인, 숨겨진", "frustrated": "좌절된, 실패한"}, "src": "verbal9 Q9"}, {"id": "v1_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Nicolaus Copernicus was much less _____ than commonly thought: he wanted to improve the cosmological theory of his day by introducing one important change while preserving as many of its conceptual foundations as possible.", "choices": ["visionary", "philosophical", "revolutionary", "iconoclastic", "diplomatic", "circumspect"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: much less ___ than commonly thought + 콜론 뒤 설명: 변화는 하나만, 기존 개념적 토대는 최대한 보존하려 했다.\n즉 생각보다 덜 '급진적/기존 질서 파괴적'이었다.\n빈칸 = 기존 체계를 뒤엎는 성향.\nrevolutionary와 iconoclastic(우상파괴적, 인습타파적)이 짝.\n정답: C (revolutionary), D (iconoclastic)", "trap": "visionary(선견지명 있는)는 그럴듯하지만 '기존 토대 보존'과 정확히 대비되지 않고 짝도 없다. circumspect(신중한)는 오히려 설명과 일치해서 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"visionary": "선견지명이 있는, 몽상적인", "iconoclastic": "우상파괴적인, 인습타파의", "philosophical": "철학적인", "revolutionary": "혁명적인", "diplomatic": "외교적인, 수완 있는", "circumspect": "신중한"}, "src": "verbal1 Q9"}, {"id": "v223_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Flawed as it may be for it is constructed by subjective scientists, science itself has methods that help us _____ our bias and talk about objective reality with some validity.", "choices": ["bypass", "reduce", "exacerbate", "magnify", "acknowledge", "circumvent"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Flawed as it may be(결함이 있긴 하지만, 양보) → 그래도 과학은 편향을 ___하고 객관적 실재를 말하게 해 주는 방법이 있다.\n빈칸 = 편향의 영향을 피하다/넘어서다(긍정적 방향).\nbypass와 circumvent(우회하다, 피해 가다)가 짝.\n정답: A (bypass), F (circumvent)", "trap": "reduce(줄이다)는 단독으로 잘 맞지만 짝이 되는 동의어가 없다. exacerbate/magnify(악화·확대)는 반대 방향의 짝.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"Flawed as it may be": "~이긴 하지만", "bypass": "우회하다, 피해 가다", "reduce": "줄이다", "exacerbate": "악화시키다", "magnify": "확대하다, 과장하다", "acknowledge": "인정하다", "circumvent": "우회하다, 회피하다"}, "src": "verbal223 Q7 · 24년 1월, 23년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v5_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The _____ of Craig's government had left the nation almost totally unprepared for war when it came.", "choices": ["somnolence", "inexperience", "lethargy", "obstinacy", "perspicacity", "acuity"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 정부의 ___ 때문에 전쟁이 왔을 때 나라가 거의 완전히 무방비 상태였다(결과).\n빈칸 = 부정, '무기력/무활동, 준비를 안 함'.\nsomnolence(졸림, 무활동)와 lethargy(무기력)가 짝.\n정답: A (somnolence), C (lethargy)", "trap": "inexperience(경험 부족)는 단독으로 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없다. perspicacity/acuity(명민함)는 짝이지만 긍정이라 결과와 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"somnolence": "졸림, 무활동", "lethargy": "무기력, 무감각", "obstinacy": "고집", "perspicacity": "통찰력, 명민함", "acuity": "예리함, 명민함", "inexperience": "경험 부족"}, "src": "verbal5 Q6"}, {"id": "v205_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The example of a chemical patent is used to illustrate a", "choices": ["legal mechanism by which community knowledge can be turned into private property", "technological development that goes beyond the scope of nineteenth-century science", "government action that creates a temporary form of intellectual property", "kind of expression that exists only in written, rather than oral, form", "way in which medical innovation can be rewarded"], "columns": null, "pid": "v205_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 구전 이야기를 처음 글로 쓴 사람이 소유자가 되는 것 'just as the first chemist to patent a tribal healing practice becomes the owner'.\n마지막 문장: 이 소유 개념은 'used to appropriate knowledge from community-based cultures'.\n즉 화학 특허 예시는 공동체의 지식(부족의 치료법)이 법적 장치(특허)를 통해 개인 재산이 되는 방식을 보여 준다.\nA가 그대로 paraphrase.\n정답: A", "trap": "E(의학 혁신이 보상받는 방식)는 특허의 일반적 기능이지만 저자는 이를 공동체 지식의 '전유(appropriation)' 사례로 비판적으로 든다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "just as the first chemist to patent a tribal healing practice becomes the owner of the resulting chemical formula", "glosses": {"appropriate": "(무단으로) 전유하다", "accede to": "~에 동의하다, 따르다", "collaborative": "공동의, 협업의", "fly in the face of": "~에 정면으로 반하다"}, "src": "verbal205 Q10 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v205_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage focuses on a contrast between", "choices": ["patents and copyrights as ways of protecting ownership", "oral and written as means of artistic expression", "literary heirs and authors of literary works as creative thinkers", "individual and collective ownership of cultural products", "contemporary and nineteenth-century views of authorship"], "columns": null, "pid": "v205_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'This insistence on private rather than collective ownership... flies in the face of those who come from an oral tradition.'\n지문 전체가 유럽식 개인 소유 vs 구전 공동체의 집단 소유의 충돌을 다룬다.\nD: 문화적 산물의 개인 소유 vs 집단 소유 → 정확.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(구전 vs 문자)는 소재로 등장하지만 '예술적 표현 수단'으로서의 대조가 아니라 '소유 개념'의 대조가 핵심이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"literary heir": "저작권 상속자", "copyright": "저작권", "autonomous": "자율적인, 독립된", "community-based": "공동체 기반의"}, "src": "verbal205 Q11 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v205_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, the notion of a literary heir depends on a presupposition that can be traced to", "choices": ["a confusion over the purposes of collaboration", "a misunderstanding between people from different cultures", "a nineteenth-century view of authors as creative individuals", "oral traditions that hand down knowledge through generations", "scholars who first recorded oral tales in written form"], "columns": null, "pid": "v205_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 상속자 인정은 'European-based assumption of the private ownership'에 달려 있고, 이 개인 소유 고집은 'derived from the nineteenth-century notion of the autonomous, creative, authorial voice'.\n즉 전제(presupposition)의 기원 = 19세기의 자율적·창조적 저자 관념.\nC가 그대로 paraphrase.\n정답: C", "trap": "E(구전 이야기를 처음 기록한 학자들)는 지문의 예시를 이용한 함정. 그들은 전제의 '기원'이 아니라 그 전제로 인해 소유자가 되는 사례일 뿐이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"presupposition": "전제", "derive from": "~에서 유래하다", "autonomous": "자율적인", "heir": "상속인"}, "src": "verbal205 Q12 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v230_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "An earlier generation of writers of historical novels, less _____ than today's writers about the need to distinguish fact from fiction, were accordingly careful to point out exactly what was invented in their works.", "choices": ["worried", "punctilious", "informed", "forthright", "jaded"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: less ___ than today's writers about the need to distinguish fact from fiction, were accordingly careful(그래서 신중했다).\n'accordingly'는 인과: 빈칸 성질이 '덜' 했기 때문에 사실/허구 구분에 신중했다.\n따라서 빈칸 = 그 필요성에 대해 '무감각하고 시큰둥한' 태도(부정).\njaded(싫증 난, 무감각해진)가 '덜 시큰둥 → 더 신경 씀 → 신중'으로 논리가 맞는다.\n정답: E (jaded)", "trap": "worried, punctilious(꼼꼼한)를 넣으면 '덜 걱정/덜 꼼꼼 → 그래서 신중했다'가 되어 accordingly와 모순된다. less + 빈칸의 이중 부정 구조에 주의.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"punctilious": "꼼꼼한, 격식을 따지는", "jaded": "싫증 난, 무감각해진", "worried": "걱정하는", "informed": "잘 아는, 정통한", "forthright": "솔직한"}, "src": "verbal230 Q1 · 25년 6월, 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v214_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Lorena de la Paz Carrete Lucero and her colleagues found (i) _____ brand loyalty among Mexican car purchasers, which suggests that regardless of customers' current brand preferences, customers may be (ii) _____ competitors' marketing strategies.", "choices": null, "columns": [["rising", "uniform", "little"], ["ignorant of", "confused by", "responsive to"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'regardless of customers' current brand preferences' → 현재 선호 브랜드가 있어도 상관없다 = 충성도가 약하다.\n(i) brand loyalty가 낮아야 이 결론이 나온다 → little.\n(ii) 충성도가 낮으면 경쟁사 마케팅에 '반응할' 수 있다 → responsive to.\n정답: C (little), F (responsive to)", "trap": "(i) rising/uniform은 충성도가 높거나 일정함을 암시해 'regardless of current preferences'와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rising": "증가하는", "uniform": "균일한", "little": "거의 없는", "ignorant of": "~을 모르는", "confused by": "~에 혼란스러워하는", "responsive to": "~에 반응하는"}, "src": "verbal214 Q2 · 25년 6월, 23년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "That there were a dozen complex debates on the lawyer's mind at any given moment did not (i) _____ his ability to perform physical work; on the contrary, he labored more vigorously when simultaneously engaged in such (ii) _____ forensic exercises.", "choices": null, "columns": [["enhance", "restore", "impede"], ["elementary", "cerebral", "tangential"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: on the contrary(오히려) → 앞은 부정된 내용, 뒤는 그 반대.\n(i) 뒤에서 '더 힘차게 일했다'고 하므로 앞은 '방해하지 않았다' → did not impede.\n(ii) 'a dozen complex debates on the lawyer's mind'를 받는 표현 → 머리를 쓰는, cerebral(지적인).\n정답: C (impede), E (cerebral)", "trap": "(i) enhance를 넣으면 'did not enhance; on the contrary, labored more vigorously'가 되어 on the contrary 논리가 깨진다. (ii) elementary는 complex와 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tangential": "주변적인, 관계없는", "enhance": "향상시키다", "restore": "회복시키다", "impede": "방해하다", "elementary": "기초적인", "cerebral": "지적인, 머리를 쓰는"}, "src": "verbal230 Q3 · 25/7, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v22_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Belief in the harmful effects of the drug has all the hallmarks of a viewpoint that is not (i)__________ even though the notion that the drug has negative consequences has been (ii)__________ multiple epidemiological studies over the past decade. Yet the true believers have (iii)__________, critiquing each new study that challenges their views and continuing to lean on supporting research that was retracted long ago.", "choices": null, "columns": [["amenable to refutation", "driven by self-interest", "capable of propagation"], ["refined by", "cited by", "upended by"], ["persisted", "splintered", "capitulated"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심: 'true believers'가 새 연구를 비판하고 철회된 연구에 계속 기댄다 → 반증을 받아들이지 않는 신념.\n(i) 반박 불가능한 관점 = not amenable to refutation(반박을 받아들이지 않는).\n(ii) even though → 여러 역학 연구가 그 생각을 '뒤집었음에도' → upended by.\n(iii) Yet + 계속 비판하고 의존 → persisted(고집했다).\n정답: A (amenable to refutation), F (upended by), G (persisted)", "trap": "(ii) cited by(인용된)는 even though 양보 관계를 만들지 못한다. (iii) capitulated(항복했다)는 뒤의 '계속 기댄다'와 정반대.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"amenable to refutation": "반박을 받아들일 수 있는", "driven by self-interest": "사리사욕에 따른", "capable of propagation": "전파될 수 있는", "refined by": "~에 의해 정교해진", "cited by": "~에 인용된", "upended by": "~에 의해 뒤집힌", "persisted": "고집했다, 지속했다", "splintered": "분열했다", "capitulated": "항복했다, 굴복했다"}, "src": "verbal22 Q4"}, {"id": "v238_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about the waters from different Sierra Nevada springs?", "choices": ["Those that had the highest concentrations of TDS came from springs that had more abundant water flow than those with the lowest concentrations.", "Those from springs that flowed primarily in the springtime were less uniform in their mineral content than those from perennial springs.", "Their chemical composition varied largely as a result of the types of granite through which the waters flowed.", "They varied more in their overall TDS level than in their relative proportions of specific minerals.", "They were not identifiable as having come from perennial or ephemeral springs on the basis of their TDS."], "columns": null, "pid": "v238_p4", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the two kinds of springs contained similar proportions of dissolved calcium, magnesium...', 그러나 'TDS levels in perennial springs were about twice those in ephemeral springs'.\n즉 개별 광물의 상대 비율은 비슷하고, 전체 TDS 수준은 크게 달랐다.\nD가 그대로 paraphrase.\n정답: D", "trap": "E는 반대: TDS가 약 2배 차이 나므로 오히려 TDS로 영구천/일시천을 구별할 수 있다. C는 화강암 조성이 'relatively uniform'이라는 내용과 모순.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ephemeral": "일시적인, 덧없는", "perennial": "연중 계속되는, 영구적인", "residence time": "체류 시간", "dissolved": "용해된"}, "src": "verbal238 Q14 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v238_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The highlighted sentence serves primarily to", "choices": ["emphasize the importance of a particular distinction", "establish a framework within which to evaluate an established opinion", "present evidence to qualify an assertion made at the beginning of the passage", "anticipate and correct a possible misconception about the author's central claim", "claim provide context for a point made in the preceding sentence"], "columns": null, "pid": "v238_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: 영구천의 TDS가 일시천의 약 2배였다(현상).\n밑줄 문장: 영구천의 물은 더 깊이 순환하고 체류 시간이 길어 화강암과 더 완전히 반응한다(이유).\n즉 앞 문장의 사실을 설명해 주는 배경/맥락을 제공한다.\nE(앞 문장의 요점에 대한 맥락 제공)가 정확. (선택지의 'claim'은 원문 오타)\n정답: E", "trap": "C(처음 주장을 한정하는 증거)는 그럴듯하지만, 이 문장은 첫 문장을 수정·한정하지 않고 바로 앞 문장의 차이를 설명한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"qualify": "(주장을) 한정하다, 제한하다", "residence time": "체류 시간", "circulate": "순환하다", "anticipate": "예상하다, 미리 대비하다"}, "src": "verbal238 Q15 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to present one scholar's", "choices": ["revision of the standard view of a particular historical period", "evaluation of a theory concerning a particular historical development", "description of economic change at a particular time and place in history", "account of a change in women's attitude toward the legal system at a particular point in history", "analysis of a particular development in the evolution of a colonial legal system"], "columns": null, "pid": "v224_p7", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문 전체: Dayton이 17세기 뉴헤이븐 법원(여성 접근 용이) → 18세기 초 영국식 법 절차로 회귀(여성 주변화)한 변화를 분석하고, 원인(확장되는 경제)까지 설명.\n즉 한 학자의 '식민지 법체계 진화의 특정 전개'에 대한 분석.\nE가 정확.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(경제 변화의 묘사)는 경제가 원인으로 나오긴 하지만 초점은 법원·법체계의 변화다. A는 '기존 표준 견해'가 지문에 언급되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"eschew": "피하다, 삼가다", "litigation": "소송", "anglicized": "영국화된", "entrenched": "확고히 자리 잡은", "marginalize": "주변화하다"}, "src": "verbal224 Q7 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that colonial men's interests differed from colonial women's interests in which of the following ways?", "choices": ["Men's interests pertained primarily to the public sphere, whereas women's interests pertained primarily to the private sphere.", "Men's interests were more concerned with property issues than were women's interests.", "Men's interests coincided with those of the Puritan magistrates less often than did women's interests.", "Men's interests were more directly affected by sharper class and racial distinctions than were women's interests.", "Men's interests were more dependent on easy access to the courts than were women's interests."], "columns": null, "pid": "v224_p7", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 18세기 법원은 'focusing more on property issues'로 바뀌었고, 결국 'a legal arena that now catered primarily to colonial men's interests'가 되었다.\n재산 문제 중심의 법원이 남성의 이익에 봉사했다 → 남성의 이익이 여성보다 재산 문제와 더 관련이 깊었다고 추론.\nB가 정답.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 지문의 'spheres of public and private activity were restructured'를 이용한 함정. 공/사 영역 재편은 언급되지만 남녀 이익이 각각 공/사에 속한다고는 말하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cater to": "~의 요구에 부응하다", "patriarchal": "가부장적인", "indebtedness": "부채", "litigated economy": "소송 경제"}, "src": "verbal224 Q8 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that New Haven's courts in the seventeenth century differed from New Haven's courts in the eighteenth century in which of the following ways?", "choices": ["In the seventeenth century, the procedures and practices of New Haven's courts were sharply divergent from those of other British colonial areas.", "In the seventeenth century, a woman was as likely to win a suit against a man as she was to win a suit against another woman.", "In the seventeenth century, a lower proportion of court cases was concerned with property issues.", "In the eighteenth century, the authority of Puritan magistrates was curtailed.", "In the eighteenth century, the courts did not recognize a woman's right to own property independently."], "columns": null, "pid": "v224_p7", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 18세기 초 법원은 'focusing more on property issues'로 변화.\n'more'는 17세기보다 재산 문제 비중이 커졌다는 뜻 → 17세기에는 재산 관련 사건 비율이 더 낮았다.\nC가 이 비교를 그대로 추론.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 17세기 법원은 '영국' 법 관행과 달랐다고 했지, 다른 영국 식민지들과 크게 달랐다고는 하지 않았다('like those of other British colonial areas'는 18세기 회귀에 대한 말). D, E는 언급 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"divergent": "다른, 갈라지는", "curtail": "줄이다, 제한하다", "revert": "되돌아가다", "magistrate": "치안판사"}, "src": "verbal224 Q9 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v226_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In our solar system, Earth is the most _____ of the rocky, or terrestrial, planets, so when first searching beyond the solar system, scientists were not accustomed to planets of similar composition but many times the mass.", "choices": ["complex", "temperate", "clement", "sizable", "intricate", "substantial"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: so(결과) → 과학자들은 비슷한 조성이지만 질량이 몇 배인 행성에 익숙하지 않았다.\n즉 지구가 암석형 행성 중 가장 '큰' 것이었기 때문에 그보다 훨씬 큰 암석 행성은 낯설었다.\n빈칸 = 크기/질량이 큼.\nsizable과 substantial(상당히 큰)이 짝.\n정답: D (sizable), F (substantial)", "trap": "complex/intricate(복잡한)는 짝이지만 '질량이 몇 배'라는 결과와 연결되지 않는다. temperate/clement(온화한)도 짝이지만 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"complex": "복잡한", "temperate": "온화한", "clement": "(기후가) 온화한", "sizable": "상당히 큰", "intricate": "복잡한, 정교한", "substantial": "상당한, 큰"}, "src": "verbal226 Q12 · 25/11, 25/9, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v236_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The writer assumes that most people feel some version of vexed ambivalence toward large corporations: _____ the convenience they deliver, yet resentful of the trade-offs that they continually demand.", "choices": ["wary of", "enthralled by", "appreciative of", "encouraged by", "suspicious of", "dazzled by"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: vexed ambivalence(복잡한 양가감정) + 'yet resentful of the trade-offs' → 빈칸은 resentful과 대비되는 강한 긍정.\n편리함에 '매혹된/현혹된' 상태.\nenthralled by와 dazzled by(~에 매료된, 눈이 멀 만큼 반한)가 짝.\n정답: B (enthralled by), F (dazzled by)", "trap": "appreciative of(고마워하는)는 단독으로 자연스럽지만 짝이 없다(encouraged by와 의미가 다름). wary of/suspicious of는 짝이지만 yet 대비가 깨진다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"vexed": "성가신", "appreciative of": "~를 고마워하는", "wary of": "~을 경계하는", "enthralled by": "~에 매료된", "encouraged by": "~에 고무된", "suspicious of": "~을 의심하는", "dazzled by": "~에 현혹된, 매료된"}, "src": "verbal236 Q11 · 26/1, 25/9, 25/8, 25/7, 25/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v238_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be _____ to see well-known historical figures played in films by actors who have become firmly associated in our minds with contemporary celebrity culture.", "choices": ["enlightening", "unsettling", "offensive", "illuminating", "gratifying", "disconcerting"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 역사적 인물을 '현대 셀럽 문화와 강하게 연결된' 배우가 연기할 때의 느낌.\n두 이미지가 충돌하므로 어색하고 불편한 느낌 → 빈칸 = 부정, '불편하게 만드는'.\nunsettling과 disconcerting(당혹스럽게 하는)이 짝.\n정답: B (unsettling), F (disconcerting)", "trap": "enlightening/illuminating(깨달음을 주는)도 짝이지만, 셀럽 이미지와 역사 인물의 충돌이 깨달음을 준다는 근거가 문장에 없다. offensive는 너무 강하고 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"enlightening": "깨우침을 주는", "unsettling": "불안하게 하는", "offensive": "불쾌한, 모욕적인", "illuminating": "이해를 돕는, 계몽적인", "gratifying": "만족스러운", "disconcerting": "당혹스럽게 하는"}, "src": "verbal238 Q12 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "The statements given are structured to lead to which of the following conclusions?", "choices": ["Most previous studies led researchers to underestimate the ability of older adults to perform short-term-memory tasks.", "In the morning, people over 65 perform short-term-memory tasks better than younger adults do.", "There is no significant overall difference in long-term memory between older adults and younger adults.", "The results of most previous studies of the effect of aging on short-term memory are best interpreted as showing that age has no effect on the ability to perform short-term-memory tasks.", "Younger adults are able to perform short-term-memory tasks better if they perform them in the afternoon than if they perform them in the morning."], "columns": null, "pid": "v230_p3", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 기존 연구들은 모두 오후에 실시 → 노인이 젊은이보다 단기기억이 나쁘다는 결론.\n새 연구: 노인은 오전에 훨씬 더 잘했고, 젊은이는 오전에 더 낫지 않았다.\n→ 기존 연구는 노인에게 불리한 시간대(오후)만 측정했으므로 노인의 능력을 과소평가했다.\nA가 이 결론.\n정답: A", "trap": "B(오전엔 노인이 젊은이보다 낫다)는 과도한 비교. 노인이 오전에 '자기 오후 성적보다' 나았다는 것만 알 뿐, 젊은이를 앞섰는지는 알 수 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"short-term memory": "단기 기억", "underestimate": "과소평가하다", "session": "(실험) 회기"}, "src": "verbal230 Q13 · 24년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v6_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that, in general, locating modern power plants closer to population centers would have?", "choices": ["compromised efforts to conserve energy in populated areas", "decreased the demand for heating within those population centers", "resulted in higher costs for the fuel used by those plants", "required much larger plants than those currently operating", "obliged power companies to find an alternative to coal as a fuel source"], "columns": null, "pid": "v6_p4", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'plants were located wherever they could tap the energy of a river or where local coal was especially cheap.'\n즉 발전소 위치는 연료가 싼(또는 강 에너지를 쓸 수 있는) 곳을 따라 정해졌다.\n그러므로 인구 밀집지 가까이에 두었다면 그런 저렴한 연료 이점을 잃어 연료비가 올랐을 것.\nC가 정답.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(에너지 절약 노력 저해)는 반대: 가까우면 폐열을 난방에 쓸 수 있어 오히려 절약에 도움이 된다. E는 석탄 대신 다른 연료를 써야 한다는 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"residual heat": "잔열, 폐열", "vent": "배출하다", "tap": "(자원을) 이용하다", "cast-off": "버려진, 폐기된"}, "src": "verbal6 Q14"}, {"id": "v6_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author suggests that steam generated by modern power plants is not used for heating because", "choices": ["steam generally proves incompatible with most modern industrial needs", "other means of heating have become more cost-effective", "steam is no longer produced in sufficient quantities to be useful", "insufficient demand for heating exists nearby", "transporting steam long distances would prove to be prohibitively expensive"], "columns": null, "pid": "v6_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'The heat generated during the production of electricity does not travel far, however, so when power plants moved out to the horizon, the steam went to waste.'\n발전소가 소비자에게서 멀어졌고, 열(증기)은 멀리 보낼 수 없으므로 버려진다.\nE: 증기를 먼 거리로 운반하는 것은 감당 못 할 만큼 비용이 크다(비현실적이다) → 'does not travel far'의 paraphrase로 본 것이 정답 키.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(근처에 난방 수요가 부족)도 '소비자에게서 멀리 지어졌다'는 내용으로 상당히 지지되어 가장 헷갈리는 선택지다. 키는 열이 멀리 이동하지 못한다는 마지막 문장의 직접 원인을 E로 본다. B(다른 난방이 더 경제적)는 언급 없음.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"prohibitively": "엄두를 못 낼 만큼", "residual": "남은, 잔여의", "real estate": "부지, 부동산", "horizon": "지평선(먼 곳)"}, "src": "verbal6 Q15"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.3 / S2 3.0"}, {"set": 6, "sections": [[{"id": "v213_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Age data from meteorites suggests that, in contrast to the relatively _____ pace of planetary evolution we are witnessing today, the first ten million years or so of our solar system history were extremely eventful.", "choices": ["structured", "uncertain", "pedestrian", "productive", "menacing"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: in contrast to(대조) the relatively ___ pace we are witnessing today ↔ 초기 1천만 년은 extremely eventful(사건이 아주 많은).\n빈칸 = eventful의 반대, '단조롭고 평범한, 느린'.\npedestrian(평범한, 단조로운)이 맞는다.\n정답: C", "trap": "structured(체계적인)나 uncertain은 eventful과 대조를 이루지 않는다. pedestrian을 '보행자'로만 알면 놓치기 쉽다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pedestrian": "평범한, 단조로운", "structured": "체계적인, 구조화된", "uncertain": "불확실한", "productive": "생산적인", "menacing": "위협적인"}, "src": "verbal213 Q1 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v33_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The guilty-pleasure of the play lies in its invitation for us to identify with its characters attractive, articulate young women and young men, and to (i) _____ their behavior that, from the outside, may look more than a little (ii) _____: though these actions are initially repugnant, we cannot help but share the point of the view of the characters committing them.", "choices": null, "columns": [["lament", "execrate", "rationalize"], ["trivial", "turbulent", "monstrous"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: guilty pleasure(죄책감 드는 즐거움), 콜론 뒤: 'though these actions are initially repugnant, we cannot help but share the point of view of the characters'.\n(ii) 밖에서 보면 '혐오스러운' 행동 → repugnant와 호응하는 monstrous(끔찍한).\n(i) 그런 행동을 인물의 관점에서 공감하며 '정당화'하게 된다 → rationalize.\n정답: C (rationalize), F (monstrous)", "trap": "(i) lament/execrate(한탄/혐오하다)는 '인물의 관점을 공유하게 된다'는 공감 논리와 반대. (ii) trivial은 repugnant와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lament": "한탄하다", "execrate": "혐오하다, 저주하다", "rationalize": "합리화하다, 정당화하다", "trivial": "사소한", "turbulent": "격동의, 소란스러운", "monstrous": "끔찍한, 괴물 같은"}, "src": "verbal33 Q2"}, {"id": "v231_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The general claim that artists are the preeminent specialists in (i) _____ is refuted by the obvious fact that the great mathematical and scientific discoveries of the past and present have been as much the result of (ii) _____ thinking as have great (iii) _____ discoveries.", "choices": null, "columns": [["revelation", "creativity", "symbolization"], ["original", "anachronistic", "systematic"], ["historical", "empirical", "artistic"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: '예술가가 ___의 탁월한 전문가'라는 주장이 반박된다 → 과학·수학 발견도 위대한 예술적 발견만큼 ___한 사고의 결과이기 때문.\n(iii) 과학·수학과 대비되는 것은 artists의 영역 → artistic.\n(ii) 예술과 과학 모두에 공통된 사고 = original(독창적인).\n(i) 예술가가 독점한다고 여겨지는 영역 = creativity(창의성).\n정답: B (creativity), D (original), I (artistic)", "trap": "(ii) systematic(체계적인)은 과학에는 맞지만 예술과 공통되는 '창의성' 주장을 반박하는 데 쓰이지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"revelation": "계시, 폭로", "creativity": "창의성", "symbolization": "상징화", "original": "독창적인", "anachronistic": "시대착오적인", "systematic": "체계적인", "historical": "역사적인", "empirical": "경험적인, 실증적인", "artistic": "예술적인"}, "src": "verbal231 Q3 · 24년 10월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v197_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The reference to what “Emily’s sister Charlotte said” serves primarily to", "choices": ["illustrate an attitude toward Victorian poetry that has been common among feminist critics", "provide a vindication for those scholars who have given critical attention to Emily Bronte’s poetry", "suggest that Emily Bront’s poetry would not be well served by being included in an anthology of poetry by women", "identify an aspect of Emily Bronte’s poetry that is increasingly of interest to literary critics", "shed light on a particular oversight common among feminist critics studying Victorian poetry"], "columns": null, "pid": "v197_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: 페미니스트 비평가들의 가정도 Emily를 배제할 위험 → Blain은 '여성 시인들이 가장 흔히 쓴 주제와 방식'을 포괄하려 함 → Yet, Charlotte 말대로 Emily의 시는 '여성들이 대개 쓰는 시와 전혀 다르다'.\n즉 '전형적 여성 시' 기준을 쓰는 페미니스트 비평이 Emily를 놓치는 맹점을 드러낸다.\nE(페미니스트 비평가들에게 흔한 간과를 조명)가 정답.\n정답: E", "trap": "A는 Charlotte의 말이 페미니스트 비평가들의 태도를 '예시'한다고 하지만, 실제로는 그 태도의 한계를 드러내는 반례다. C는 지문이 주장하지 않는 처방.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "Emily’s sister Charlotte said", "glosses": {"preserve": "(특정 집단의) 전유물, 영역", "eccentric": "별난, 예외적인", "vindication": "정당성 입증", "oversight": "간과, 실수"}, "src": "verbal197 Q4 · 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v197_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions “Virginia Blain’s anthology” primarily in order to", "choices": ["represent a voice opposing the feminist critics mentioned in the second sentence", "elaborate on a claim made in the third sentence", "provide an example of an omission decried by feminist critics", "cite a tendency that preceded the advent of feminist criticism", "note an exception to a tendency described earlier in the passage"], "columns": null, "pid": "v197_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세 번째 문장: 'feminist critics' own assumptions... have also threatened to exclude Emily Bronte.'\n바로 다음: Blain의 선집은 'representative, not eccentric'하게 Bronte를 빠뜨렸다.\n즉 Blain은 세 번째 문장 주장의 대표적 사례로서 그 주장을 구체화(elaborate)한다.\n정답: B", "trap": "E(경향의 예외)는 정반대: 지문은 Blain이 'not eccentric(예외가 아닌)' 대표 사례라고 명시한다. C는 페미니스트들이 비판한 누락이 아니라 그들 자신의 누락이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Virginia Blain’s anthology", "glosses": {"anthology": "선집", "representative": "대표적인", "omit": "빠뜨리다, 생략하다", "decry": "공공연히 비난하다"}, "src": "verbal197 Q5 · 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v17_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "To say that John Adams was forthright was to be ___________; friends as well as enemies were more likely to characterize his stark honesty and direct manner as blunt and awkward.", "choices": ["fickle", "charitable", "facetious", "unreasonable", "forbearing", "capricious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 세미콜론 뒤 설명: 친구든 적이든 그의 솔직함을 오히려 'blunt and awkward(무뚝뚝하고 서투른)'라고 부르기 쉬웠다.\n즉 'forthright(솔직한)'라고 부르는 것은 실제보다 좋게 봐주는, 너그러운 표현이다.\n빈칸 = 관대하게 평가하는.\ncharitable과 forbearing(관대한, 너그러운)이 짝.\n정답: B (charitable), E (forbearing)", "trap": "fickle/capricious(변덕스러운)는 짝이 있어 끌리지만 문맥과 무관하다. unreasonable은 '사실과 다르다'는 느낌만 주고 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"facetious": "경솔한, 농담조의", "fickle": "변덕스러운", "charitable": "너그러운, 관대한", "unreasonable": "불합리한", "forbearing": "참을성 있는, 관대한", "capricious": "변덕스러운"}, "src": "verbal17 Q6"}, {"id": "v231_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "We might be much closer to building the next generation of observatories if competing groups of astronomers had not _____ repeated chances to collaborate; instead, three separate projects with common goals are fighting one another for funding.", "choices": ["spurned", "avoided", "sabotaged", "rebuffed", "initiated", "commenced"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 반사실 조건(if ... had not ___) + instead: 세 프로젝트가 서로 자금을 두고 싸우고 있다.\n즉 협력할 기회를 '거절했다'.\n빈칸 = 협력 기회를 거부하다.\nspurned와 rebuffed(퇴짜 놓다)가 짝.\n정답: A (spurned), D (rebuffed)", "trap": "avoided(피했다)는 단독으로 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없다. initiated/commenced(시작했다)는 짝이지만 논리가 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"spurned": "퇴짜 놓았다, 거절했다", "avoided": "피했다", "sabotaged": "방해했다, 파괴했다", "rebuffed": "거절했다, 퇴짜 놓았다", "initiated": "시작했다", "commenced": "시작했다"}, "src": "verbal231 Q7 · 25년 1월, 23년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v215_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The manufacturing company's swift maneuver enabled it to evade the full impact of the increasing cost of raw materials, which brought the downfall of firms that responded less _____.", "choices": ["ruthlessly", "deftly", "adroitly", "carefully", "extravagantly", "cautiously"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 이 회사의 swift maneuver(재빠른 대응)가 충격을 피하게 했다 ↔ 덜 ___하게 대응한 회사들은 몰락.\n빈칸 = swift maneuver의 성질, '능숙하게, 재빠르게'.\ndeftly와 adroitly(능숙하게)가 짝.\n정답: B (deftly), C (adroitly)", "trap": "carefully/cautiously(신중하게)는 짝이지만 swift maneuver(재빠름)와 성질이 다르다. 신중함이 아니라 능숙한 대처가 핵심.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"adroitly": "능숙하게", "ruthlessly": "무자비하게", "deftly": "능숙하게, 솜씨 좋게", "carefully": "주의 깊게", "extravagantly": "사치스럽게, 과도하게", "cautiously": "조심스럽게"}, "src": "verbal215 Q6 · 25/10, 25/7, 25/6, 25/4, 23/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v29_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Caricature can be revealing as well as amusing, and Ager’s novel is both: Ager’s delineation of class, ethnic, and generational struggle is exaggerated for comical effect, but it _____ nonetheless.", "choices": ["resonates", "entertains", "diverts", "confuses", "rings true", "falls short"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Caricature can be revealing as well as amusing, and Ager's novel is both.\nbut ... nonetheless: 웃기려고 과장했지만(amusing) 그럼에도 ___ → revealing(진실을 드러냄)에 해당.\n빈칸 = 진실하게 와닿다.\nresonates(공감을 불러일으키다)와 rings true(진실하게 들리다)가 짝.\n정답: A (resonates), E (rings true)", "trap": "entertains/diverts(즐겁게 하다)는 짝이지만 이미 'comical effect'에 해당하는 amusing 쪽이라 but nonetheless 대조가 성립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"resonates": "공감을 불러일으키다, 울림이 있다", "entertains": "즐겁게 하다", "diverts": "즐겁게 하다, 기분을 전환시키다", "confuses": "혼란스럽게 하다", "rings true": "진실처럼 들리다", "falls short": "기대에 못 미치다"}, "src": "verbal29 Q7"}, {"id": "v223_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["speculate on the composition of Mercury's core", "point out a difference between Mercury and gaseous planets", "present possible explanations for Mercury's unusual density", "critique an argument concerning Mercury's formation", "answer a question about Mercury's history"], "columns": null, "pid": "v223_p10", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 수성의 밀도가 크기에 비해 이례적임 → 'so why would Mercury have such an anomalous density?' 질문 → 세 가지 가능한 설명(성운 조성 차이, 태양열에 의한 휘발, 거대 충돌).\n즉 이례적 밀도에 대한 가능한 설명들을 제시.\n정답: C", "trap": "E(질문에 답한다)는 너무 단정적이다. 지문은 하나의 답을 내리지 않고 might/may/possible로 여러 가설만 나열한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"anomalous": "이례적인", "condense": "응축하다", "volatile": "휘발성의", "nebula": "성운"}, "src": "verbal223 Q10 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v223_q11", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage supports which of the following statements about Mercury?", "choices": ["Its density is atypical for a terrestrial planet of its size.", "Its core is probably composed mainly of iron.", "Its composition includes a high percentage of volatile, low-density elements."], "columns": null, "pid": "v223_p10", "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'not much bigger than Earth's moon, yet its density is typical of that of a far larger planet' → 그 크기의 지구형 행성으로는 이례적 → 지지.\nB: 지구형 행성은 'high-density cores, probably composed largely of iron'이고 수성은 지구형 행성이며 큰 금속 핵을 가졌을 수 있음 → 지지.\nC: 오히려 휘발성·저밀도 원소가 날아갔을 가능성을 제시 → 반대.\n정답: A, B", "trap": "B는 지문이 '수성'이 아니라 '지구형 행성 일반'에 대해 말해서 빼기 쉽지만, 수성도 지구형 행성이므로 적용된다. C는 지문의 설명과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"terrestrial": "지구형의(암석형)", "metallic core": "금속 핵", "volatile": "휘발성의", "vaporize": "증발시키다"}, "src": "verbal223 Q11 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v223_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence in the context of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["It offers a possible explanation for a puzzling fact about the planet Mercury.", "It presents evidence that counters a claim made in the previous sentence.", "It describes an outmoded idea about the nature of the solar nebula.", "It articulates the central scientific issue that is under discussion in the passage.", "It suggests that astronomers are in disagreement about certain crucial facts concerning planet formation."], "columns": null, "pid": "v223_p10", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "밑줄 문장: 모든 행성이 같은 시기에 성운에서 응축했다면 '왜 수성은 이렇게 이례적인 밀도를 갖는가?'\n이 질문이 지문의 핵심 문제이고, 이후 문장들이 모두 이에 대한 가설이다.\nD(지문에서 논의되는 핵심 과학적 문제를 제시)가 정확.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 밑줄 문장이 '설명'을 제시한다고 하지만, 이 문장은 질문을 던질 뿐이고 설명은 그 뒤 문장들이 한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"articulate": "명확히 표현하다", "outmoded": "구식의", "solar nebula": "태양 성운", "anomalous": "이례적인"}, "src": "verbal223 Q12 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v216_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "A core assumption of evolutionary biology is that adaptation is always _____: organisms adapt to their environment, never vice versa.", "choices": ["beneficial", "gradual", "reversible", "contingent", "asymmetrical"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 콜론(:) 뒤 부연: 생물이 환경에 적응하지, 그 반대(환경이 생물에 적응)는 결코 아니다.\n한쪽 방향으로만 작용한다는 뜻 → 빈칸 = '비대칭적, 일방향의'.\nasymmetrical이 정확.\n정답: E", "trap": "beneficial(이로운)이나 gradual(점진적)은 진화 관련 흔한 개념이라 끌리지만 'never vice versa(결코 반대 방향 아님)'를 설명하지 못한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"beneficial": "이로운", "gradual": "점진적인", "reversible": "되돌릴 수 있는", "contingent": "우연적인, ~에 달린", "asymmetrical": "비대칭적인"}, "src": "verbal216 Q1 · 25/11, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Svitlana Mayboroda's recent work, though (i) _____ pure mathematics, is already being (ii) _____ by physicists, distinguishing it from most mathematical advances, for which the development of any practical use is long delayed.", "choices": null, "columns": [["largely irrelevant to", "familiar to scholars of", "in the realm of"], ["applied", "overlooked", "questioned"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: though(양보) + 'distinguishing it from most mathematical advances, for which the development of any practical use is long delayed'.\n대부분의 수학 성과와 달리 이 연구는 이미 실용적으로 쓰이고 있다 → (ii) applied(응용되고 있다).\n(i) 양보절: '순수 수학의 영역에 속하지만' → in the realm of.\n정답: C (in the realm of), D (applied)", "trap": "(i) largely irrelevant to(순수 수학과 무관)는 though 양보 관계를 만들지 못한다. (ii) overlooked/questioned는 '실용성이 빨리 생겼다'는 대조와 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"largely irrelevant to": "~와 대체로 무관한", "familiar to scholars of": "~ 학자들에게 친숙한", "in the realm of": "~의 영역에 속하는", "applied": "응용된", "overlooked": "간과된", "questioned": "의문시된"}, "src": "verbal240 Q3 · 26년 2월, 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Whereas in earlier kinds of writing about manners, such as conduct books, advice about behavior was (i) _____ an eternal and autonomous ethical ideal, the early-nineteenth-century etiquette book based its precepts on more (ii) _____ norms: as do ever-shifting fashion trends, etiquette's imperatives rose and fell routinely.", "choices": null, "columns": [["substituted for", "subordinated to", "distinguished from"], ["clearly defensible", "broadly acceptable", "socially contingent"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Whereas(대조): 예전 예절서는 영원하고 자율적인 윤리 이상에 ___ ↔ 19세기 초 에티켓 책은 더 ___한 규범에 근거, 콜론 뒤: 유행처럼 수시로 오르내렸다.\n(ii) 유행처럼 변하는 규범 = socially contingent(사회적 상황에 따라 달라지는).\n(i) 예전 조언은 영원한 윤리 이상에 '종속되었다(따랐다)' → subordinated to.\n정답: B (subordinated to), F (socially contingent)", "trap": "(i) distinguished from(구별된)은 Whereas 대조를 거꾸로 만든다. (ii) broadly acceptable은 'ever-shifting'의 변화성을 담지 못한다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"substituted for": "~을 대신한", "subordinated to": "~에 종속된", "distinguished from": "~와 구별된", "clearly defensible": "명백히 옹호 가능한", "broadly acceptable": "널리 받아들여지는", "socially contingent": "사회적 상황에 좌우되는"}, "src": "verbal206 Q3 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The theater presented directors and designers with a remarkably (i) _____ space, since the placement of the stage and of the audience could be (ii) _____ the needs of the production. And though audiences were sometimes unsettled when they found themselves thrust into the midst of the action, on balance they saw this as adding to the (iii) _____ of the performance.", "choices": null, "columns": [["plastic", "compact", "recalcitrant"], ["irrelevant to", "preferred over", "dictated by"], ["deficiencies", "remoteness", "excitement"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) since(이유): 무대와 관객 배치가 공연의 필요에 의해 '결정될' 수 있었다 → dictated by.\n(i) 그래서 연출가에게 매우 '유연한(형태를 바꿀 수 있는)' 공간 → plastic.\n(iii) though 관객이 때로 불안했지만, on balance 이를 공연의 '흥미/생동감'을 더하는 것으로 봤다 → excitement.\n정답: A (plastic), F (dictated by), I (excitement)", "trap": "(i) plastic을 '플라스틱'으로만 알면 놓친다(= 유연한, 가변적인). compact는 배치를 바꿀 수 있다는 이유와 무관하고 recalcitrant(다루기 힘든)는 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"plastic": "유연한, 형태를 바꿀 수 있는", "compact": "아담한, 조밀한", "recalcitrant": "다루기 힘든, 고집 센", "irrelevant to": "~와 무관한", "preferred over": "~보다 선호되는", "dictated by": "~에 의해 결정되는", "deficiencies": "결함", "remoteness": "거리감, 멀리 떨어짐", "excitement": "흥분, 흥미"}, "src": "verbal198 Q4 · 25/1, 24/9, 23/10, 23/5, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["identify the origins of a particular distinction", "describe how the definition of a literary term has changed", "correct a misunderstanding about a literary genre", "evaluate competing definitions of a particular kind of writing", "account for a recent change in literary preferences"], "columns": null, "pid": "v198_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: 'memoir'라는 용어가 지난 두 세기 동안 매우 다른 글에 붙여져 왔다(불안정성) → 비평가들은 autobiography의 하위 장르로 낮게 봄 → 최근엔 오히려 'memoir is now the prestige term'.\n즉 한 문학 용어의 정의·지위가 어떻게 변해 왔는지 서술.\nB가 정답.\n정답: B", "trap": "E(최근 문학 선호 변화 설명)는 마지막 문장만 반영하는 부분적 답. A는 memoir/autobiography 구분의 '기원'을 밝히지 않는다(기준이 inconstant하다고만 함).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"genealogy": "계보", "instability": "불안정성", "subliterary": "문학 수준에 못 미치는", "outflank": "허를 찌르다, 앞지르다", "prestige": "위신, 명성"}, "src": "verbal198 Q14 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions the “article” primarily to", "choices": ["show how a particular distinction has become blurred", "cite an argument that challenges a widespread view", "demonstrate that a change has occurred over time", "note an example of a scholarly controversy", "illustrate a claim about a particular term"], "columns": null, "pid": "v198_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장 주장: 'memoir'라는 용어는 매우 다른 종류의 글에 붙여져 왔다.\nRak의 글은 'highlights the term's radical instability' — 1인칭/3인칭, 사적/공적 등 모두에 쓰였다는 예를 제시.\n즉 특정 용어에 대한 주장을 구체적으로 보여 준다.\n정답: E", "trap": "B(널리 퍼진 견해에 도전하는 주장 인용)는 그럴듯하지만, Rak의 글은 저자의 주장을 뒷받침하는 예시이지 통념에 대한 반박으로 소개되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Julie Rak’s genealogy of the term in her article", "glosses": {"genealogy": "계보, 유래 추적", "radical": "근본적인, 극심한", "instability": "불안정성", "illustrate": "예증하다"}, "src": "verbal198 Q15 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v28_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["present additional evidence to support a popular theory", "show the underlying similarities of two seemingly contradictory theories", "point out the implications of a particular study for two related theories", "provide an alternative explanation for a well-documented phenomenon", "reconcile two competing theories that explain a phenomenon"], "columns": null, "pid": "v28_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: La Selva 연구 소개 → (1) 열대림이 CO2를 흡수하는 스펀지라는 대중적 이론에 의문을 제기('raised serious questions') → (2) Keeling의 CO2 흐름 모델과는 일치('consistent with').\n즉 한 연구가 두 관련 이론에 갖는 함의를 제시.\nC가 정확.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 반대: 연구는 대중적 이론(스펀지)을 지지하지 않고 오히려 의문을 제기한다. E는 두 이론을 '화해'시키지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"respiration": "호흡", "photosynthesis": "광합성", "flux": "흐름, 유동", "intensify": "강화하다"}, "src": "verbal28 Q5"}, {"id": "v28_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage supports which of the following statements about the trees in the La Selva study?", "choices": ["During the El Nino year, they added considerably less wood than they did in cooler years during the period of 1984-2000.", "During the El Nino year, they typically had higher rates of photosynthesis than they did in other years during the period of 1984-2000.", "During the El Nino year, they released considerably more oxygen than they did in cooler years during the period of 1984-2000.", "During the El Nino year, they took up considerably more CO2 than they did in cooler years during the period of 1984-2000.", "The amount of CO2 that they absorbed remained constant throughout the entire period of 1984- 2000."], "columns": null, "pid": "v28_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'trees adding twice as much wood in some cooler years as they did in the scorching El Nino year of 1997-1998.'\n즉 엘니뇨 해에는 서늘한 해보다 나무가 훨씬 적게 자랐다.\nA가 그대로 paraphrase.\n정답: A", "trap": "B, C, D는 더운 해에 광합성(산소 방출, CO2 흡수)이 늘었다고 하여 지문과 반대. 더운 해에는 성장이 줄고 CO2 방출이 늘 수 있다는 것이 요지.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"scorching": "타는 듯이 더운", "El Nino": "엘니뇨(해수 온난화 현상)", "index": "지표"}, "src": "verbal28 Q6"}, {"id": "v28_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that as temperatures rise, trees in the tropical regions", "choices": ["continue to grow at a slow but steady rate", "grow less and intensify photosynthesis", "emit more CO2 and oxygen", "increase overall respiration and decrease overall photosynthesis", "grow more and absorb more CO2"], "columns": null, "pid": "v28_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 성장은 광합성(CO2 흡수)과 호흡(CO2 방출) 사이의 균형 지표. 더운 해에는 덜 자랐고, 기온 상승이 'pushing tropical forests to release more CO2'.\n덜 자라고 CO2를 더 방출 → 호흡이 광합성보다 상대적으로 커졌다.\nD(전체 호흡 증가, 전체 광합성 감소)가 정확.\n정답: D", "trap": "C(CO2와 산소를 더 방출)는 그럴듯하지만, 산소 방출은 광합성의 결과이므로 광합성 감소와 모순된다. B는 '덜 자람'과 '광합성 강화'가 충돌.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"respiration": "호흡", "photosynthesis": "광합성", "steady": "꾸준한", "emit": "방출하다"}, "src": "verbal28 Q7"}, {"id": "v34_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "As a way of _____ the negative impacts of overdependence on a single export product─crude oil─the Nigerian government passed legislation in 1999 intended to revitalize the moribund solid minerals’ sector.", "choices": ["assuming", "checking", "disguising", "stemming", "downplaying", "shouldering"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 단일 수출품(원유) 과의존의 부정적 영향을 ___하는 방법으로, 침체한 고체 광물 부문을 살리려는 법을 통과.\n다각화로 부정적 영향을 '억제/막다'라는 뜻이 필요.\nchecking(억제하다)과 stemming(막다, 저지하다)이 짝.\n정답: B (checking), D (stemming)", "trap": "disguising/downplaying(감추다/축소해 말하다)은 짝처럼 보이지만 법으로 산업을 살리는 실제 조치와 맞지 않는다. assuming/shouldering(떠맡다)도 짝이지만 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"assuming": "떠맡다, 가정하다", "checking": "억제하다, 저지하다", "disguising": "위장하다, 감추다", "stemming": "막다, 저지하다", "downplaying": "축소하다, 경시하다", "shouldering": "떠맡다, 짊어지다"}, "src": "verbal34 Q10"}, {"id": "v228_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "When first introduced, cubicle workspaces were seen as having _____ effect on office workers, but as cubicle sizes steadily shrank, the aspirations of the people working in them became increasingly constrained.", "choices": ["a revitalizing", "a soothing", "a liberating", "a protecting", "an emancipatory", "a calming"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: but(대조) → 칸막이가 줄어들면서 직원들의 포부가 점점 'constrained(제약된)'되었다.\n처음에는 그 반대, 즉 '자유롭게 해 주는' 효과로 여겨졌다.\n빈칸 = constrained의 반대.\na liberating과 an emancipatory(해방적인)가 짝.\n정답: C (a liberating), E (an emancipatory)", "trap": "a soothing/a calming(진정시키는)은 짝이지만 'constrained'와 직접 대조되지 않는다. 대조 대상은 '제약 ↔ 해방'.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"a revitalizing": "활력을 주는", "a soothing": "진정시키는", "a liberating": "해방감을 주는", "a protecting": "보호하는", "an emancipatory": "해방적인", "a calming": "진정시키는"}, "src": "verbal228 Q10 · 24년 9월, 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v14_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In literature, thrillers thrive on heroes and villains, and usually the characterization is not very _____; writers don't want to confuse or slow the plot.", "choices": ["nuanced", "trite", "realistic", "monotonous", "banal", "subtle"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 스릴러는 영웅과 악당(선명한 대립)으로 굴러가고, 세미콜론 뒤 이유: 작가들은 플롯을 혼란스럽게 하거나 늦추고 싶어 하지 않는다.\n그래서 인물 묘사가 그다지 '미묘하지/섬세하지' 않다.\nnuanced와 subtle이 짝.\n정답: A (nuanced), F (subtle)", "trap": "trite/banal(진부한)은 짝이지만 'not very ___'와 결합하면 '진부하지 않다'가 되어 의미가 반대. realistic은 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"nuanced": "미묘한 차이가 있는, 섬세한", "trite": "진부한", "realistic": "현실적인", "monotonous": "단조로운", "banal": "평범한, 진부한", "subtle": "미묘한, 섬세한"}, "src": "verbal14 Q8"}, {"id": "v236_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true of the cave, most weakens the argument?", "choices": ["Some of the plant species found in the earlier (lower) levels of habitation are not found at all in the later (upper) levels of habitation.", "The remains of some plant species, such as squash and chili peppers, show changes from the middle to the later (upper) levels that indicate domestication.", "At certain points during the period from 9,000 to 500 years ago, the cave was abandoned for a time and later reoccupied by people who were probably of a different culture than the earlier inhabitants.", "Virtually all the plant remains found at the earliest (lowest) levels of habitation are tough fibers that are relatively resistant to decomposition.", "The total volume of food plant remains found in the earlier (lower) layers was greater than that found in the later (upper) layers."], "columns": null, "pid": "v236_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 후기 거주자가 초기 거주자보다 더 다양한 식물을 먹었다.\n근거: 아래(초기) 층은 식물 종 10개 미만, 위(후기) 층은 30종 이상 발견.\n가정: 발견된 잔해가 실제 먹은 식물을 비슷하게 반영한다(보존 정도가 같다).\nD: 초기 층의 잔해는 거의 다 분해에 강한 질긴 섬유 → 연한 식물은 썩어 없어졌을 수 있음 → 발견 종 수 차이는 보존 편향일 수 있다 → 약화.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(초기 종 일부가 후기엔 없음)는 종의 '교체'일 뿐 다양성 비교를 약화시키지 못한다. E(총량은 초기가 더 많음)는 양이지 종의 다양성이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"habitation": "거주", "domestication": "작물화, 가축화", "decomposition": "분해, 부패", "reoccupy": "다시 점유하다"}, "src": "verbal236 Q13 · 24년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions \"Jeffrey Masten\" primarily to", "choices": ["note a significant influence on scholars' views about authorial collaboration", "explain how scholars concluded that certain authors worked collaboratively", "challenge a particular argument about the significance of authorial collaboration", "exemplify a particular scholarly point of view regarding authorship", "counter a claim about the ways in which scholars have understood authorial collaboration"], "columns": null, "pid": "v234_p4", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Some critics, such as Jeffrey Masten, hoped that this realization might dislodge traditional notions of authorship as a solitary activity.'\n'such as'로 소개 → 협업 인식이 단독 저자 개념을 바꾸리라 기대한 학자들의 관점을 예시.\nD(저자성에 관한 특정 학자적 관점을 예시)가 정확.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(학자들 견해에 큰 영향을 미침)는 반대에 가깝다. 이어지는 However에서 그 기대가 실현되지 않았다(done little to change)고 한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Jeffrey Masten", "glosses": {"dislodge": "몰아내다, 제거하다", "solitary": "혼자의, 단독의", "attribute A to B": "A를 B의 것으로 보다", "collaborative": "공동의"}, "src": "verbal234 Q14 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, the \"model of the author\"", "choices": ["is compatible with some scholars' views on authorial collaboration by English Renaissance playwrights", "is not easy to reconcile with what scholars now understand about the working methods used by playwrights like Beaumont and Fletcher", "has been primarily useful for scholars attempting to understand authorship during the English Renaissance rather than for those thinking about authorship in other eras", "reflects an assumption that most authors during the English Renaissance collaborated with others at least some of the time", "was intended to help distinguish the working methods of playwrights like Beaumont and Fletcher from those of playwrights like Shakespeare"], "columns": null, "pid": "v234_p4", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 학자들은 협업 희곡에서도 장면·대사를 '따로 작업한' 개별 작가에게 귀속시키려 한다 → 'acceptance of the fact of collaborative writing has done little to change the model of the author; it simply multiplies the number of authors.'\n즉 전통적 저자 모델(단독 저자)이 협업을 인정하는 학자들의 견해와 공존한다 = 양립 가능하다.\n정답: A", "trap": "B(Beaumont와 Fletcher의 작업 방식과 조화시키기 어렵다)는 Masten식 기대에 맞는 직관적 답이지만, 지문은 오히려 학자들이 모델을 바꾸지 않고 협업을 설명해 냈다고 말한다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "the model of the author", "glosses": {"compatible with": "~와 양립 가능한", "reconcile": "조화시키다", "attribute": "~의 것으로 보다", "multiply": "늘리다, 배가하다"}, "src": "verbal234 Q15 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.8 / S2 2.9"}, {"set": 7, "sections": [[{"id": "v19_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "For Confucius, names had __________ contents; no matter how time marched on and the affairs of the world changed, the proper names of things absolutely could not vary.", "choices": ["largely transparent", "uniquely adaptive", "eternally stable", "dangerously slippery", "increasingly conventional"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론(;) 뒤가 앞 내용을 풀어 설명하는 구조.\n단서: no matter how time marched on ... the proper names of things absolutely could not vary (시간이 흘러도 이름은 절대 변할 수 없다).\n빈칸 = '변하지 않는, 영원히 고정된'이라는 뜻.\neternally stable(영원히 안정된)이 정확히 일치.\n정답: C", "trap": "uniquely adaptive / increasingly conventional은 '변화'를 암시하므로 정반대. largely transparent는 변화 여부와 무관.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"largely transparent": "대체로 명료한", "uniquely adaptive": "독특하게 적응력 있는", "eternally stable": "영원히 안정된", "dangerously slippery": "위험할 정도로 모호한", "increasingly conventional": "점점 관습적인"}, "src": "verbal19 Q1"}, {"id": "v13_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Though nations no longer (i) _____ nuclear physicists—the men and women who once delivered the destructive power of the atom bomb—physics still has the same power to (ii) _____, but in another way, by revealing the basic truths that underpin reality.", "choices": null, "columns": [["compete for", "worry about", "cower before"], ["produce awe", "incite debates", "challenge orthodoxy"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Though(양보) 구조: 국가들이 더 이상 물리학자를 (i)하지 않지만, 물리학은 여전히 '같은 힘'을 갖는다.\n(i) 단서: 원자폭탄의 파괴력을 전달한 사람들 → 예전엔 두려워했다 → cower before(앞에서 움츠러들다).\n(ii) 'the same power ... but in another way': 두려움과 같은 계열의 힘이되 다른 방식 → 경외감을 일으키다(produce awe). 진리를 드러내 경외심을 준다.\n정답: C, D", "trap": "(i) compete for는 그럴듯하지만 '같은 힘(파괴력에 대한 두려움)'과 이어지지 않음. (ii) challenge orthodoxy는 진리를 드러내는 것과 비슷해 보이나 '같은 힘'과 연결되지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cower before": "~앞에서 움츠러들다", "compete for": "~을 두고 경쟁하다", "worry about": "~을 걱정하다", "produce awe": "경외감을 불러일으키다", "incite debates": "논쟁을 촉발하다", "challenge orthodoxy": "정설에 도전하다"}, "src": "verbal13 Q2"}, {"id": "v211_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Parker’s model of human affairs reflects (i) _____ outlook, in stark contrast to the generally (ii) _____ premises that her colleagues in the economics department adopt in their work. Accordingly, her conclusions (iii) _____ theirs.", "choices": null, "columns": [["a sanguine", "an introspective", "a technical"], ["pessimistic", "theoretical", "distinctive"], ["are somewhat more accessible than", "are not so sunny as", "diverge markedly from"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i)(ii): 'in stark contrast to'로 Parker의 관점과 동료들의 전제가 정반대여야 함.\n선택지 중 반의어 쌍은 sanguine(낙관적) ↔ pessimistic(비관적)뿐.\n(iii) Accordingly(따라서): 출발점이 정반대이므로 결론도 크게 다르다 → diverge markedly from.\nare not so sunny as는 Parker가 낙관적이므로 방향이 반대.\n정답: A, D, I", "trap": "(iii) are not so sunny as: '밝음'이라는 소재에 끌리지만 낙관적인 Parker의 결론이 덜 밝다는 것은 모순.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sanguine": "낙관적인", "a sanguine": "낙관적인", "an introspective": "내성적인, 자기성찰적인", "a technical": "기술적인", "pessimistic": "비관적인", "theoretical": "이론적인", "distinctive": "독특한", "are somewhat more accessible than": "~보다 다소 이해하기 쉽다", "are not so sunny as": "~만큼 밝지(낙관적이지) 않다", "diverge markedly from": "~와 현저히 다르다"}, "src": "verbal211 Q3 · 25년 3월, 24년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v33_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence (“However, evidence ~ years later.”)?", "choices": ["It undermines the assumption that human activity has had a significant impact on Earth’s climate.", "It supports the assumption that Earth’s temperatures have risen appreciably over the past 100 years.", "It questions the assumption that greenhouse gases have had a warming effect on Earth’s climate.", "It challenges the assumption that human activity began to affect Earth’s climate after the advent of industrialization.", "It supports the assumption that greenhouse gases are a direct by-product of industrial activities."], "columns": null, "pid": "v33_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 과학적 합의 = 인간은 지난 100년 내(공장, 자동차 등 산업화 이후)부터 기후를 데웠다.\n강조 문장: However, ... agricultural activities may have had such an effect much earlier (8000년 전부터).\n즉 '산업화 이후에 인간이 기후에 영향을 주기 시작했다'는 가정에 이의를 제기.\n정답: D", "trap": "A: 인간 활동이 기후에 큰 영향을 미쳤다는 것을 약화시키는 게 아니라 오히려 더 일찍부터 영향을 줬다고 주장하므로 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"advent": "출현, 도래", "industrialization": "산업화", "undermine": "약화시키다"}, "src": "verbal33 Q4"}, {"id": "v33_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions “natural trends” most likely in order to", "choices": ["propose a possible explanation for why current temperatures in North America and Europe are not as low as they might otherwise be", "explain why levels of methane in Earth’s atmosphere began to rise approximately 5,000 years ago", "suggest that Earth’s climate would have become even warmer without the advent of human agricultural activities", "identify factors that may have contributed to the rise of greenhouse gases in Earth’s atmosphere approximately 8,000 years ago and again some 3,000 years later", "support the claim that human activity may have played a role in the rise in CO2 and methane levels in the atmosphere thousands of years ago"], "columns": null, "pid": "v33_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: concentrations of CO2 started rising about 8000 years ago, even though natural trends indicate they should have been dropping.\n자연적 추세로는 줄었어야 했는데 늘었다 → 자연이 아닌 다른 원인(인간 농업)이 있었음을 뒷받침.\n즉 'natural trends'는 인간 활동이 수천 년 전 CO2·메탄 증가에 역할을 했다는 주장을 지지하기 위해 언급됨.\n정답: E", "trap": "D: natural trends가 온실가스 증가에 기여한 요인이라고 하지만, 지문에서는 오히려 감소를 가리켰으므로 관계를 뒤집음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "natural trends", "glosses": {"natural trends": "자연적 추세", "concentration": "농도", "methane": "메탄"}, "src": "verbal33 Q5"}, {"id": "v203_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "While the band's music is loud and aggressive, it is never _____.", "choices": ["simpleminded", "unsophisticated", "subdued", "restrained", "melodious", "disingenuous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "While(양보): 음악이 시끄럽고 공격적이지만, 결코 ___하지 않다.\n시끄럽고 공격적이면 '단순·저급하다'고 오해받기 쉬움 → 그 예상을 부정.\n빈칸 = 부정적, '단순한/세련되지 못한'이라는 뜻.\nsimpleminded(단순한)와 unsophisticated(세련되지 못한)가 같은 의미 쌍.\n정답: A, B", "trap": "subdued / restrained도 쌍이지만 '시끄럽지만 결코 절제되지 않았다'는 양보가 아닌 동어반복이 되어 While 구조와 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"simpleminded": "단순한, 우둔한", "subdued": "억눌린, 차분한", "disingenuous": "솔직하지 못한, 위선적인", "unsophisticated": "세련되지 못한, 단순한", "restrained": "절제된", "melodious": "선율이 아름다운"}, "src": "verbal203 Q6 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v235_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Though she said nothing at all, Jane thoroughly understood her mother; she was not the _____ child that everyone thought her to be.", "choices": ["laconic", "obtuse", "underhanded", "taciturn", "dull", "enigmatic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Though she said nothing, Jane thoroughly understood: 말은 안 했지만 완전히 이해했다.\n'she was not the ___ child that everyone thought' → 사람들이 생각한 것과 달리 이해력이 있었다.\n빈칸 = '이해력이 둔한'이라는 뜻.\nobtuse(둔한)와 dull(아둔한)이 쌍.\n정답: B, E", "trap": "laconic / taciturn(과묵한)도 쌍이지만, 실제로 아무 말도 안 했으므로 '과묵한 아이가 아니었다'는 모순.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"laconic": "말수가 적은, 간결한", "obtuse": "둔한, 이해가 느린", "underhanded": "음흉한, 부정직한", "taciturn": "과묵한", "dull": "둔한, 아둔한", "enigmatic": "수수께끼 같은"}, "src": "verbal235 Q7 · 25년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v35_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "To call Kermode the finest English critic of his generation would be a _____ compliment, since not many of its population are professionally engaged in literary criticism.", "choices": ["sincere", "backhanded", "paltry", "heartfelt", "meager", "plausible"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "since(이유): 그 세대 사람들 중 직업적으로 문학비평을 하는 사람이 많지 않다.\n→ 경쟁자가 적으니 '최고의 비평가'라는 칭찬은 별 가치가 없다.\n빈칸 = 부정적, '보잘것없는, 빈약한'이라는 뜻.\npaltry(하찮은)와 meager(빈약한)가 쌍.\n정답: C, E", "trap": "backhanded(비꼬는 듯한) compliment는 숙어로 단독으로는 아주 그럴듯하지만 짝이 되는 동의어가 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sincere": "진심 어린", "backhanded": "빈정대는 듯한, 간접적인", "paltry": "하찮은, 보잘것없는", "heartfelt": "진심에서 우러난", "meager": "빈약한, 적은", "plausible": "그럴듯한"}, "src": "verbal35 Q9"}, {"id": "v27_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The baseball player's performance during last night's game was impressive, although not _____; others have performed similar feats.", "choices": ["decisive", "unexampled", "significant", "novel", "outstanding", "spectacular"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "although not ___; 세미콜론 뒤 단서: others have performed similar feats(다른 선수들도 비슷한 업적을 냈다).\n빈칸 = '전례 없는, 새로운'이라는 뜻.\nunexampled(전례 없는)와 novel(새로운)이 쌍.\n정답: B, D", "trap": "outstanding / spectacular는 '인상적'과 비슷해 끌리지만, 남들도 해냈다는 단서와 연결되지 않음(그리고 impressive와 거의 같은 말이라 although 대조가 약함).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"decisive": "결정적인", "unexampled": "전례 없는", "significant": "중요한", "novel": "새로운, 참신한", "outstanding": "뛰어난", "spectacular": "장관인, 화려한"}, "src": "verbal27 Q8"}, {"id": "v233_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["examine a questionable notion", "analyze a historical process", "question the soundness of a method", "propose explanations for a situation", "discuss two rival theories"], "columns": null, "pid": "v233_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: Scholars have advanced various reasons for the small number of biographies.\n이후 Some have observed... / A more important reason... / Another reason... 로 이유를 여러 개 제시.\n상황(전기 수가 적음)에 대한 설명들을 제안하는 글.\n정답: D", "trap": "E: 두 개의 '경쟁 이론'을 논하는 게 아니라 여러 이유를 나열·보완하는 것. A: 의심스러운 개념을 검토하는 글이 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"paucity": "부족, 결핍", "tenure": "종신 재직권", "inception": "시작, 개시"}, "src": "verbal233 Q10 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v233_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage suggests which of the following as a reason for the difference in status between autobiography and biography in African American culture?", "choices": ["Autobiography has been more closely studied in academic institutions than has biography.", "Autobiography has been regarded as more objective than biography.", "Autobiography has been more important in reclaiming personal identity than has biography.", "Autobiography conventionally has been written in a more formal style than has biography.", "Autobiography has been regarded as an older and thus more respectable genre of writing than has biography."], "columns": null, "pid": "v233_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: This preference can best be understood in light of the project of reclaiming personal identity.\n자서전이 노예 서사처럼 억압 속에서 개인 정체성을 표현하는 수단이었기 때문에 더 높은 지위를 가짐.\nC가 이를 그대로 paraphrase.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 학계에서 더 많이 연구됐다는 말은 없음(학계 언급은 전기를 피하는 이유로만 나옴).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"reclaim": "되찾다", "articulate": "명확히 표현하다", "oppression": "억압"}, "src": "verbal233 Q11 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v233_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true of autobiographical works?", "choices": ["They have occupied an important place in African American literature from its beginnings.", "Their study has been systematically neglected in academic institutions.", "They are the main vehicle that African Americans have used to reclaim personal identity.", "They are more likely to be written by oppressed individuals than by those who have not experienced oppression.", "They enjoy higher status among nonacademics than among academics."], "columns": null, "pid": "v233_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: autobiography has been the favored medium of expression in African American culture from its inception.\nfrom its inception = from its beginnings, favored medium = important place.\n정답: A", "trap": "C: 'the main vehicle'은 지문보다 과도한 주장. 자서전이 정체성 회복과 관련된다고만 했지 주된 수단이라고 단정하지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"reclaim": "되찾다", "inception": "시작, 개시", "favored medium": "선호되는 표현 수단", "deter": "단념시키다, 막다"}, "src": "verbal233 Q12 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v198_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The results of the latest survey being _____, earlier results gave researchers little relevant experience for the new data’s interpretation.", "choices": ["superfluous", "inconsequential", "tedious", "unexampled", "familiar"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "분사구문(being ~)이 이유를 나타냄: 최신 결과가 ___했기 때문에, 이전 결과들은 새 데이터 해석에 별 도움이 되는 경험을 주지 못했다.\n빈칸 = '전례 없는, 처음 보는'이라는 뜻.\nunexampled(전례 없는)가 정확.\n정답: D", "trap": "familiar는 정반대(익숙하면 이전 경험이 도움이 됨). inconsequential은 해석 경험 부족과 인과관계가 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"superfluous": "불필요한, 과잉의", "inconsequential": "중요하지 않은", "tedious": "지루한", "unexampled": "전례 없는", "familiar": "익숙한"}, "src": "verbal198 Q1 · 25/7, 24/8, 24/6, 22/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Seemingly (i) _____ her reputation for tediousness, the university president (ii) _____ a casual, chatty style in the speech she delivered.", "choices": null, "columns": [["intrigued by", "embarrassed by", "resigned to"], ["provoked", "affected", "expected"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "총장이 지루하다는 평판을 '의식해서' 일부러 가볍고 수다스러운 스타일을 썼다는 흐름.\n(i) 평판 때문에 스타일을 바꿨다 → embarrassed by(부끄러워하는).\n(ii) 원래 스타일이 아닌 것을 꾸며서 사용 → affected(가장하다, 일부러 꾸미다).\n정답: B, E", "trap": "(i) resigned to(체념한)는 체념했다면 스타일을 바꿀 이유가 없음. (ii) affected를 '영향을 주다'로만 알면 놓치기 쉬움.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"intrigued by": "~에 흥미를 느낀", "embarrassed by": "~을 부끄러워하는", "resigned to": "~을 체념한", "provoked": "유발했다, 자극했다", "affected": "가장했다, 일부러 꾸며 썼다", "expected": "기대했다"}, "src": "verbal234 Q3 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v20_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "In China, beginning in the 1920s, the field of geography was (i)__________ discourse, alive to indigenous Chinese traditions even as it (ii)__________ key elements of Western scientific geography.", "choices": null, "columns": [["an arcane", "a hybrid", "a subjective"], ["ignored", "questioned", "absorbed"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: alive to indigenous Chinese traditions even as it ___ key elements of Western scientific geography.\neven as(~하면서도 동시에): 중국 전통에 민감하면서 서양 요소도 받아들였다.\n(ii) absorbed(흡수했다).\n(i) 두 전통이 섞였으므로 a hybrid(혼합된) 담론.\n정답: B, F", "trap": "(ii) ignored/questioned는 전통 중시와 서양 거부로 단순하게 읽을 때 끌리지만 even as는 공존을 나타내므로 hybrid와 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"even as": "~하면서도 동시에", "an arcane": "난해한", "a hybrid": "혼합된, 잡종의", "a subjective": "주관적인", "ignored": "무시했다", "questioned": "의문을 제기했다", "absorbed": "흡수했다"}, "src": "verbal20 Q2"}, {"id": "v236_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Biographies tumble off the presses in profusion these days, a (i) _____ linked, for better or worse, to the current obsession with celebrity. Some critics complain that biographers too often (ii) _____ the messy reality of a life, and it's true that lesser authors simply glorify or, more often, vilify their subjects. But good biographers are far more respectful of (iii) _____: the best see not one monolithic truth about a person but many overlapping truths.", "choices": null, "columns": [["boom", "paucity", "felicity"], ["impose a specious coherence on", "provide excessive detail about", "are completely overwhelmed by"], ["privacy", "complexity", "partiality"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 전기들이 쏟아져 나온다(tumble off the presses in profusion) → boom(호황).\n(ii) 비평가들의 불만 + messy reality: 어수선한 삶에 '그럴듯한 가짜 일관성을 부여한다' → impose a specious coherence on. 뒤의 '단순히 미화하거나 비방한다'와도 일치.\n(iii) But 좋은 전기 작가는 하나의 진실이 아닌 여러 겹친 진실을 본다 → complexity.\n정답: A, D, H", "trap": "(ii) provide excessive detail about은 '어수선함'과 연결돼 보이지만 단순 미화/비방(단순화)과 반대. (iii) partiality는 편파성이라 맥락과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tumble off the presses": "쏟아져 나오다", "lesser authors": "수준 낮은 작가들", "boom": "호황, 급증", "paucity": "부족", "felicity": "큰 행복, 적절함", "impose a specious coherence on": "~에 그럴듯한(허울뿐인) 일관성을 강요하다", "provide excessive detail about": "~에 대해 지나치게 상세히 서술하다", "are completely overwhelmed by": "~에 완전히 압도되다", "privacy": "사생활", "complexity": "복잡성", "partiality": "편파성, 편애"}, "src": "verbal236 Q4 · 25년 5월, 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage suggests that the increase in sugar production during the seventeenth century", "choices": ["changed the types of flavors highlighted in elite European cuisine", "had detrimental effects on the health of Europeans", "lowered the price of sugar to levels affordable by the masses", "was accompanied by the popularization of strongly flavored condiments", "encouraged the intermingling of salty and sweet tastes"], "columns": null, "pid": "v206_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: sugar 증가 → 짭짤한(savory)과 단(sweet) 맛의 구분이 생김, 강한 향신 소스 전통이 끝나고 재료 본연의 맛을 존중하는 새 요리가 등장.\n'elite cuisine'의 강조되는 맛의 종류가 바뀐 것 → A.\n정답: A", "trap": "E: 짠맛과 단맛의 혼합은 설탕 증가 '이전'의 특징으로, 이후엔 구분됨 → 관계를 뒤집음. D도 강한 양념 전통이 끝났으므로 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"savory": "짭짤한, 감칠맛 나는", "relegate": "격하시키다, 밀어내다", "condiment": "양념, 조미료", "herald": "예고하다"}, "src": "verbal206 Q5 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that proponents of the \"new cuisine\" would be most likely to agree with which of the following statements about sugar?", "choices": ["It should be used primarily in dishes that are served with deeply spiced sauces.", "It can obscure the distinctive flavors of certain ingredients used in many dishes.", "Its more extensive availability had a regrettable effect on the preparation of many dishes.", "Its frequent appearance in savory dishes contrasted sharply with earlier traditions of cooking.", "It should be used sparingly even in dishes intended to be sweet."], "columns": null, "pid": "v206_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: a new cuisine which claimed to pay more respect to its ingredients' intrinsic flavors.\n새 요리는 재료 고유의 맛을 존중 → 단맛을 몇몇 요리로 제한(sweet와 savory 구분).\n따라서 설탕은 여러 재료의 고유한 맛을 가릴 수 있다고 볼 것 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "E: 단 요리에도 설탕을 아껴 써야 한다는 것은 지문과 반대(그런 요리에는 훨씬 더 많은 설탕을 사용). C: 설탕 확산 자체를 유감스럽게 여긴다는 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "new cuisine", "glosses": {"intrinsic": "본질적인, 고유한", "proponent": "지지자", "obscure": "가리다, 흐리게 하다"}, "src": "verbal206 Q6 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v26_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author's primary purpose is to suggest that", "choices": ["the evidence used in support of a particular argument is questionable", "a distinction between two genres of writing has been overlooked", "a particular issue is more complex than it might appear", "two apparently different works share common features", "two eighteenth-century authors held significantly different attitudes toward a particular issue"], "columns": null, "pid": "v26_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문단: 당시 권위자들은 역사(교훈적) > 소설(경박함)이라고 여겼고, 두 소설에서도 역사를 찬양하는 듯 보임.\n2문단 핵심: Yet in both cases, the praise of history is more double-edged than it might actually appear.\n즉 겉보기보다 문제가 더 복잡하다는 것이 주제 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "D: 두 작품의 공통점(둘 다 역사 찬양이 이중적)이 나오긴 하지만 주목적은 '보이는 것보다 복잡하다'는 점. E는 두 작가의 태도 차이를 말하지 않으므로 오답.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"edifying": "교훈적인", "double-edged": "양날의, 이중적인", "protofeminist": "초기 페미니즘적인", "skeptic": "회의론자"}, "src": "verbal26 Q5"}, {"id": "v26_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true of Hume's reputation in the late eighteenth century?", "choices": ["He was more highly regarded as a historian than Gibbon.", "His historical writing, like his philosophical writing, came to be regarded as problematic.", "He was more well-known for his historical writing than for his philosophical writing.", "His historical writing came to be regarded as morally questionable because of his association with Gibbon.", "His views about classical paganism brought him disapproval among the general reading public."], "columns": null, "pid": "v26_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: While Hume's history was generally seen as being less objectionable than his philosophy, there were widespread doubts about his moral soundness even as a historian.\n철학뿐 아니라 역사 저술도 결국 문제시됨(even as a historian) → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "C: 역사가 '덜 문제시'됐다는 말을 '더 유명했다'로 바꿔 읽는 함정. E: 고대 이교 찬양은 Gibbon에 관한 내용.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"objectionable": "불쾌한, 이의가 있는", "soundness": "건전성", "paganism": "이교, 다신교"}, "src": "verbal26 Q6"}, {"id": "v26_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The highlighted sentence exemplifies which of the following?", "choices": ["Cultural authorities' attempt to use novels to support their view about the value of reading fiction", "Eighteenth-century women authors' attempts to embody in their work certain cultural authorities' views about reading", "A point about the educational value of reading books about history", "An instance in which a particular judgment about the value of reading history is apparently presupposed", "A challenge to an assumption about eighteenth-century women's reading habits"], "columns": null, "pid": "v26_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "강조 문장: 독자들은 역사를 좋아하는 여주인공이 그렇지 않은 자매보다 더 덕망 있고 지적이라고 결론 내릴 수 있다.\n이 결론은 '역사 독서가 가치 있다'는 판단을 전제로 함 → 해당 판단이 겉으로 전제된 사례.\napparently presupposed: 2문단에서 실제로는 이중적이라고 하므로 'apparently'가 정확.\n정답: D", "trap": "C: 역사 독서의 교육적 가치에 대한 '주장'을 펴는 문장이 아니라, 그 가치가 전제된 사례일 뿐. A: 권위자들이 소설을 이용한 것이 아님.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"presuppose": "전제하다", "exemplify": "예시하다", "disdain": "경멸하다"}, "src": "verbal26 Q7"}, {"id": "v6_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The problem a generation ago was not the new art itself but the heightened intensity of conviction surrounding it, which is thankfully absent in our wonderfully _____ times.", "choices": ["fervid", "impassioned", "undogmatic", "receptive", "nostalgic", "optimistic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: the heightened intensity of conviction ... which is thankfully absent in our times.\n지금 시대에는 '강한 신념의 열기'가 다행히 없음 → 빈칸 = 긍정적, '독단적이지 않고 열린'이라는 뜻.\nundogmatic(독단적이지 않은)과 receptive(수용적인)가 쌍.\n정답: C, D", "trap": "fervid / impassioned(열렬한)는 서로 동의어 쌍이라 끌리지만 '신념의 열기가 없다'는 단서와 정반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"conviction": "신념", "impassioned": "열정적인", "undogmatic": "독단적이지 않은", "receptive": "수용적인", "fervid": "열렬한", "nostalgic": "향수에 젖은", "optimistic": "낙관적인"}, "src": "verbal6 Q8"}, {"id": "v204_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "It is Alice Hoffman' s achievement as a novelist that we do not wonder at the fabulous in her work but accept what seems _____ as an idiom of the affective extremes and nuances that are simply facts of life.", "choices": ["grandiose", "unseemly", "incredible", "inappropriate", "unexceptional", "improbable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: we do not wonder at the fabulous in her work but accept what seems ___ as ... facts of life.\n'the fabulous(믿기 어려운 환상적인 것)'을 재진술하는 빈칸.\n빈칸 = '믿기 어려운, 있을 법하지 않은'이라는 뜻.\nincredible과 improbable이 쌍.\n정답: C, F", "trap": "grandiose(거창한)는 fabulous의 '과장된' 느낌과 비슷해 보이지만 '믿기 어려운'의 의미가 아니고 짝도 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unseemly": "보기 흉한, 부적절한", "inappropriate": "부적절한", "grandiose": "거창한, 과장된", "incredible": "믿기 어려운", "unexceptional": "평범한", "improbable": "있을 법하지 않은"}, "src": "verbal204 Q12 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v10_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Carbon fiber, though more resistant to pressure than steel, is less _____ microscopic fractures.", "choices": ["beset with", "responsible for", "troubled by", "proof against", "dependent upon", "forgiving of"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "though(양보): 탄소섬유는 강철보다 압력에 강하지만, 미세 균열에 대해서는 덜 ___하다.\n대조 구조이므로 '균열에는 약하다' = 균열에 덜 견딘다.\n빈칸 = '~에 잘 견디는'이라는 뜻.\nproof against(~에 견디는)과 forgiving of(~을 잘 허용하는/견디는)가 쌍.\n정답: D, F", "trap": "beset with / troubled by(~에 시달리는)는 쌍이지만 '균열에 덜 시달린다' = 장점이 되어 though 대조가 깨짐.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"proof against": "~에 견디는, 끄떡없는", "forgiving of": "~을 잘 견디는, 너그러운", "beset with": "~에 시달리는", "troubled by": "~으로 곤란을 겪는", "responsible for": "~의 원인이 되는", "dependent upon": "~에 의존하는"}, "src": "verbal10 Q8"}, {"id": "v200_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "The argument is open to criticism on the grounds that it", "choices": ["fails to establish that the level of damage done by trucks is a serious problem", "omits evidence about one of the two relevant factors", "ignores the possibility that careful driving can lessen damage to highways", "presumes that trucks are the only vehicles capable of causing substantial damage to highways", "presumes that something is bound to happen just because it is allowed to happen"], "columns": null, "pid": "v200_p3", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "전제: 도로 손상은 '차축당 무게(weight per axle)'에 따라 급격히 증가.\n근거: 새 규정은 '차량 최대 총중량'을 늘림.\n결론: 더 큰 손상을 줄 수 있는 트럭이 허용될 것.\n허점: 차축당 무게 = 총중량 ÷ 차축 수. 차축 수가 함께 늘면 차축당 무게는 늘지 않을 수 있는데 이 요소를 빼먹음 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "E: 결론이 '허용할 것(allow)'이고 실제로 손상이 일어난다고 주장하지 않으므로 이 비판은 해당하지 않음.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"escalate": "급격히 증가하다", "axle": "차축", "presume": "가정하다"}, "src": "verbal200 Q13 · 25년 4월, 22년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v218_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is an accurate statement about Kuba ndop sculptures as they are described in the passage?", "choices": ["The ibol signifiers they contain show insignificant formal variation.", "There are minimal differences in their facial features.", "The identification of each with a historical person is a modern-day assumption.", "Individual sculptures have historically been associated with specific textile patterns.", "The proverbs that accompany them were chosen by the leaders they portray."], "columns": null, "pid": "v218_p14", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: the ndop figures themselves are so homogeneous that they are essentially expunged of any idiosyncratic physiognomic features.\n얼굴(관상)의 개성적 특징이 거의 없음 = 얼굴 생김새 차이가 미미함 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "A: ibol 상징은 오히려 각 조각에 개별 정체성을 부여하는 요소이므로 변형이 미미하다는 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"homogeneous": "균질한, 동질의", "expunge": "지우다, 삭제하다", "idiosyncratic": "특유의, 개인 특유의", "physiognomic": "관상의, 얼굴 생김새의"}, "src": "verbal218 Q14 · 24/2, 23/7, 22/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v218_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage mentions “Washburn’s examination” in order to", "choices": ["correct a misconception regarding the role of creativity in Kuba art", "reassert a widely accepted theory regarding the pattern structures found in Kuba textiles", "compare the ways in which two types of Kuba art developed historically", "draw attention to a similarity between two genres of Kuba art", "provide an example of a genre for which Kuba artists are renowned"], "columns": null, "pid": "v218_p14", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Washburn의 직물 연구: 무한한 변형을 표방하지만 실제로는 제한된 패턴 구조 안에서 미세한 변형.\n다음 문장: A parallel sensibility informs the Kuba approach to the ndop ... sculptures.\n즉 직물과 조각이라는 두 장르의 유사성을 보여주기 위해 언급 → D.\n정답: D", "trap": "A: 창의성에 대한 오해를 '바로잡는' 글이 아님. C: 두 예술의 역사적 발전 과정을 비교하지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Washburn’s examination", "glosses": {"parallel": "유사한, 평행한", "nuanced": "미묘한 차이가 있는", "figurative convention": "형상 표현의 관례"}, "src": "verbal218 Q15 · 24/2, 23/7, 22/9 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.2 / S2 2.9"}, {"set": 8, "sections": [[{"id": "v229_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Although the nonscientist is amazed by the orderliness of elements in the periodic table, chemists consider this orderliness _____ because of the common origin and similarity of the units of matter that compose the elements.", "choices": ["inexplicable", "inappropriate", "unnatural", "unsurprising", "unexpected"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although(대조): 비과학자는 주기율표의 질서에 놀라지만, 화학자들은 그 질서를 ___라고 여긴다.\nbecause 단서: 원소를 이루는 물질 단위가 같은 기원과 유사성을 가지므로 → 당연하다.\n빈칸 = '놀랍지 않은'이라는 뜻.\n정답: D", "trap": "inexplicable / unexpected는 비과학자의 반응(놀람)에 가까워 Although 대조와 반대.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inexplicable": "설명할 수 없는", "inappropriate": "부적절한", "unnatural": "부자연스러운", "unsurprising": "놀랍지 않은", "unexpected": "예상치 못한"}, "src": "verbal229 Q1 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v15_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The idea that arguments based on probability are deployed only by (i) _____ persons is (ii) _____ even among scientists. Perhaps such an evaluation has partly to do with the origins of the subject in the mathematics of gambling games, not generally regarded as pastimes for people of good character.", "choices": null, "columns": [["exacting", "disreputable", "prominent"], ["widespread", "controversial", "deplored"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "뒤 문장 단서: 확률은 도박 게임에서 기원했고, 도박은 'people of good character'의 취미로 여겨지지 않음.\n(i) 확률 논증은 평판 나쁜 사람들만 쓴다 → disreputable.\n(ii) 'such an evaluation has partly to do with...': 이런 평가가 존재하는 이유를 설명 → 과학자들 사이에서도 널리 퍼져 있다 → widespread.\n정답: B, D", "trap": "(ii) deplored/controversial은 '그 생각이 비판받는다'는 뜻이 되어, 다음 문장이 왜 그런 평가가 있는지 설명하는 흐름과 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"disreputable": "평판이 나쁜", "exacting": "엄격한, 까다로운", "prominent": "저명한", "widespread": "널리 퍼진", "controversial": "논란이 많은", "deplored": "개탄되는"}, "src": "verbal15 Q2"}, {"id": "v21_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The notion of \"island-centered\" history, which mirrored the trend that historians elsewhere were calling \"history from below,\" turned out to be an idea more enthusiastically (i)__________ than (ii)__________. Some explanations are not hard to discover. Islander peoples have left few written sources, and these have often been in languages that Western historians did not (iii)__________.", "choices": null, "columns": [["disavowed", "advocated", "researched"], ["empirically realized", "persuasively undermined", "casually examined"], ["diminish", "comprehend", "resist"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i)(ii) 'more enthusiastically A than B': 열정적으로 주장됐지만 실제로 실현되지는 못했다.\n(i) advocated(옹호된), (ii) empirically realized(실증적으로 실현된).\n다음 문장들: 이유 = 섬 사람들의 문헌이 적고, 서양 역사가들이 그 언어를 ___하지 못했다 → comprehend(이해하다).\n정답: B, D, H", "trap": "(ii) persuasively undermined: '열렬히 옹호됐지만 반박되지는 않았다'도 가능해 보이나, 뒤에 실증 연구의 어려움(자료 부족, 언어)을 설명하므로 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"disavowed": "부인된", "advocated": "옹호된", "empirically realized": "실증적으로 실현된", "researched": "연구된", "persuasively undermined": "설득력 있게 약화된", "casually examined": "대충 검토된", "diminish": "줄이다", "comprehend": "이해하다", "resist": "저항하다"}, "src": "verbal21 Q3"}, {"id": "v11_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage would be most likely to agree with which of the following statements about Dumas as a novelist?", "choices": ["His use of non sequiturs detracts from the stylistic verve of his writing.", "His use of repetition has been overrated as effective novelistic technique.", "His reliance on humor results in one-dimensional characters.", "His novels, while technically well written, have predictable plots.", "His writing displays narrative skill despite certain technical flaws."], "columns": null, "pid": "v11_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 몬테크리스토 백작은 full of redundancies, repetitions, and non sequiturs(기술적 결점)이지만, 그 매력과 'narrative wisdom'은 sludgy prose와 분리할 수 없다.\n= 기술적 결점에도 불구하고 서사적 능력을 보여준다 → E.\n정답: E", "trap": "A: non sequitur가 verve(활기)를 해친다고 했지 않음, 오히려 'with all its verve and sparkle'로 공존한다고 함.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sludgy": "질척한, 둔탁한", "gasping": "숨이막히는", "verve": "활기, 열정", "non sequitur": "앞뒤가 맞지 않는 말", "redundancy": "중복, 군더더기"}, "src": "verbal11 Q4"}, {"id": "v11_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true regarding the novel 《Georges》?", "choices": ["Its authorship was widely questioned soon after its publication.", "Its characters are less interesting than those in most Dumas novels.", "It is marred by redundancies, repetitions, and non sequiturs.", "It presents unusual problems for translators.", "It has often been compared favorably to 《The Count of Monte Cristo》."], "columns": null, "pid": "v11_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: the characters of Georges are tiresomely earnest, while those from Dumas' well-known novels crack jokes and utter colorful oaths.\nGeorges의 인물은 지루하게 진지함 → 대표적 Dumas 소설 인물보다 덜 흥미로움 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "C: 중복·반복·비논리는 몬테크리스토 백작의 특징이며 Georges는 기술적으로 잘 쓰였다고 함 → 대상을 뒤바꾼 함정.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"earnest": "진지한", "oath": "욕설, 맹세", "tiresomely": "지루하게"}, "src": "verbal11 Q5"}, {"id": "v7_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Because it has usually been impossible to eradicate exotic species once they have become established, it is _____ to minimize introductions of species that have substantial probabilities of unwanted impacts.", "choices": ["prudent", "customary", "provident", "superfluous", "essential", "pointless"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Because(원인): 외래종은 일단 정착하면 제거가 거의 불가능하다.\n→ 원치 않는 영향을 줄 가능성이 큰 종의 도입을 최소화하는 것이 '현명하다'.\n빈칸 = 긍정적, '신중한, 현명한'이라는 뜻.\nprudent와 provident가 쌍.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "essential(필수적인)은 단독으로 자연스럽지만 짝이 되는 동의어가 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"prudent": "신중한, 현명한", "provident": "선견지명이 있는, 신중한", "superfluous": "불필요한", "customary": "관례적인", "essential": "필수적인", "pointless": "무의미한"}, "src": "verbal7 Q6"}, {"id": "v205_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The second group of volunteer excavators was far more _____ than the first, and consequently the obstructing material was removed much more rapidly during the second shift.", "choices": ["diligent", "incapacitated", "experienced", "punctual", "debilitated", "industrious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "consequently(결과): 두 번째 그룹이 더 ___해서 장애물을 훨씬 빨리 치웠다.\n빈칸 = 긍정적, '부지런한'이라는 뜻.\ndiligent와 industrious가 쌍.\n정답: A, F", "trap": "experienced도 빨리 치운 이유로 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없음. incapacitated/debilitated는 쌍이지만 반대 의미.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"diligent": "부지런한", "incapacitated": "무능력해진, 능력을 잃은", "experienced": "경험 많은", "punctual": "시간을 엄수하는", "debilitated": "쇠약해진", "industrious": "근면한"}, "src": "verbal205 Q6 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v229_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "During the Second World War, the substantial energy that industrial employers spent convincing workers to wear mandated safe attire suggests that compliance could not be _____.", "choices": ["countenanced", "monitored", "assumed", "counted on", "brought up", "sanctioned"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 고용주들이 근로자에게 안전복을 입히도록 설득하는 데 상당한 노력을 들였다 → 준수가 저절로 이루어질 거라 기대할 수 없었다.\n빈칸 = '당연시되다, 기대되다'라는 뜻.\nassumed와 counted on이 쌍.\n정답: C, D", "trap": "countenanced / sanctioned(용인되다, 승인되다)도 쌍이지만 '준수가 용인될 수 없었다'는 말이 안 됨.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"countenanced": "용인된, 묵인된", "assumed": "당연시된, 가정된", "counted on": "기대된, 믿어진", "monitored": "감시된", "brought up": "제기된, 길러진", "sanctioned": "승인된, 제재받은"}, "src": "verbal229 Q9 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v227_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "By the time they enter sixth grade, many children sleep so little during the school week that daytime drowsiness may _____ their ability to pay attention and learn.", "choices": ["compromise", "define", "highlight", "emphasize", "imperil", "destroy"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "so ... that(결과): 아이들이 너무 적게 자서 낮 졸음이 집중력·학습 능력을 ___할 수 있다.\n빈칸 = 부정적, '손상시키다, 위태롭게 하다'라는 뜻.\ncompromise(손상시키다)와 imperil(위태롭게 하다)이 쌍.\n정답: A, E", "trap": "destroy는 방향은 맞지만 'may ~'와 함께 쓰기엔 지나치게 극단적이고 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"compromise": "손상시키다, 위태롭게 하다", "imperil": "위태롭게 하다", "define": "정의하다", "highlight": "강조하다", "emphasize": "강조하다", "destroy": "파괴하다"}, "src": "verbal227 Q7 · 25년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v3_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["discuss evidence relevant to the frequency of co-orbiting asteroids near Earth and near Venus", "explain an unusual feature of the near-Venus asteroid population relative to the near-Earth asteroid population", "examine the effect of cratering as a factor that distinguishes Venus' surface from Earth's", "consider recent research on the ways in which Venus' atmosphere differs from Earth's", "evaluate recent studies of the relative frequency of impact craters on Earth and on Venus"], "columns": null, "pid": "v3_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문단: 지구의 이중 크레이터 → 동반 궤도 소행성이 상당수 존재한다는 증거.\n2문단: 금성에서도 찾아봄, 비율은 낮지만 대기 차폐 효과를 고려하면 비슷 → 결론: co-orbiting asteroids must be common among both.\n지구·금성 근처 동반 궤도 소행성의 빈도에 관한 증거를 논의 → A.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 금성 소행성 집단의 '특이한 특징'을 설명하는 게 아니라 결국 둘 다 흔하다는 결론. E: 충돌 크레이터 전체의 빈도가 아니라 이중 크레이터에 관한 글.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"doublet crater": "이중 크레이터", "co-orbiting": "함께 궤도를 도는", "screen out": "걸러내다, 차단하다"}, "src": "verbal3 Q10"}, {"id": "v3_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that one result of establishing the age of impact craters is that it enables researchers to", "choices": ["determine whether the screening effect of Earth's atmosphere may have diminished over time", "determine whether apparent doublet craters are simply chance associations", "determine whether erosion has wiped out the very oldest craters on Earth", "conclude that co-orbiting asteroids have become more common recently", "conclude that the doublet craters that exist on Earth are all roughly the same age"], "columns": null, "pid": "v3_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Kamensk crater ... partnered by the Gusev crater, ... of identical age.\n이중 크레이터는 두 소행성이 '거의 동시에' 충돌할 때 생김. 또한 금성은 크레이터 수가 '우연한 연관 가능성'이 높을 만큼 많지 않다고 언급.\n나이가 같으면 동시 충돌 → 우연히 가까이 있는 두 크레이터가 아님을 판별 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "E: 하나의 쌍 안에서 나이가 같다는 것이지 지구의 모든 이중 크레이터가 같은 나이라는 것이 아님.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"chance association": "우연한 연관", "simultaneously": "동시에", "partner crater": "짝 크레이터"}, "src": "verbal3 Q11"}, {"id": "v3_q12", "type": "RC_select", "blanks": null, "stem": "Select the sentence that proposes a possible explanation for a surprising discovery.", "choices": null, "columns": null, "pid": "v3_p2", "answer": "SENTENCE", "answer_sentence": "However, Venus' denser atmosphere may screen out the smaller member of some asteroid pairs.", "explanation": "놀라운 발견: Researchers found that the proportion of doublet craters on Venus is significantly smaller than on Earth.\n바로 다음 문장이 그 이유를 제시: However, Venus' denser atmosphere may screen out the smaller member of some asteroid pairs.\n'may'로 가능한 설명을 제안 → 정답 문장.\n정답: However, Venus' denser atmosphere may screen out the smaller member of some asteroid pairs.", "trap": "'If Earth had a similar screening effect...' 문장은 설명을 제안하는 게 아니라 그 설명을 적용해 비율을 비교하는 문장.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"denser": "더 밀도 높은", "screen out": "걸러내다", "within uncertainties": "오차 범위 내에서"}, "src": "verbal3 Q12"}], [{"id": "v210_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "There is no natural environment on Earth more _____ than a virgin rain forest: a plethora of rain forest species have developed remarkably sophisticated strategies to ensure that their voices are heard.", "choices": ["imperiled", "cacophonous", "fecund", "essential", "malleable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 빈칸을 설명.\n단서: species have developed sophisticated strategies to ensure that their voices are heard (소리가 들리게 하려는 전략).\n소리가 매우 많고 시끄러운 환경 → 빈칸 = '시끄러운, 불협화음의'라는 뜻.\ncacophonous가 정답.\n정답: B", "trap": "fecund(번식력 있는)는 '수많은 종(plethora of species)'에 끌리지만 핵심 단서인 voices(소리)와 연결되지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"imperiled": "위험에 처한", "cacophonous": "불협화음의, 시끄러운", "fecund": "비옥한, 다산의", "essential": "필수적인", "malleable": "유연한, 순응적인"}, "src": "verbal210 Q1 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v228_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "For a long time now, revenues from Broadway musicals have been (i) _____ with their quality: profits are higher than ever, but with few exceptions, the musicals are not (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["at odds", "stagnant compared", "fluctuating along"], ["insubstantial", "popular", "first-rate"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤 설명: profits are higher than ever, but ... the musicals are not ___.\n(ii) 수익은 최고인데 'but' → 품질이 좋지 않다 → first-rate(일류의).\n(i) 수익과 품질이 반대로 움직임 → at odds with(~와 상충하는).\n정답: A, F", "trap": "(ii) popular: 수익이 높다면 인기가 있는 것이므로 'not popular'는 모순. (i) stagnant compared는 수익이 최고라는 점과 모순.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"at odds": "상충하는, 불일치하는", "stagnant compared": "~에 비해 정체된", "fluctuating along": "~에 따라 변동하는", "insubstantial": "실체 없는, 빈약한", "popular": "인기 있는", "first-rate": "일류의"}, "src": "verbal228 Q2 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Sinden notes that in the face of warnings about the perils of climate change, the need to agree on strategies for reducing greenhouse-gas emissions is increasingly urgent. The question of who should reduce emissions is not (i) _____. Rather, according to Sinden, it is the question of who should bear the costs of these reductions that is (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["particularly vexed", "universally resolved", "politically innocuous"], ["redundant", "contentious", "prescient"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'not (i). Rather, ... it is the question of who should bear the costs that is (ii).'\nnot A, rather B 구조: (i)과 (ii)는 같은 성질이고, 문제의 초점만 옮겨짐.\n누가 줄일지는 '특히 골치 아픈' 문제가 아니라, 누가 비용을 부담할지가 '논쟁적'이다.\n(i) particularly vexed, (ii) contentious.\n정답: A, E", "trap": "(i) universally resolved: 'not universally resolved'는 '아직 논쟁 중'이라는 뜻이 되어 Rather 대조 구조와 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"particularly vexed": "특히 골치 아픈, 논란이 많은", "prescient": "선견지명이 있는", "universally resolved": "보편적으로 해결된", "politically innocuous": "정치적으로 무해한", "redundant": "불필요한, 중복된", "contentious": "논쟁적인"}, "src": "verbal200 Q2 · 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v218_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Climbing mountains in search of an awe-inspiring view can be (i) _____ experience. Too often, the peak seems forever out of reach, always disappearing over the next crest. It's a feeling that (ii) _____ physicists, who have spent much of the last century trudging up a seemingly endless slope in search of truly cosmic vistas. It is proving (iii) _____ climb.", "choices": null, "columns": [["a disappointing", "a breathtaking", "an unpredictable"], ["is sometimes baffling to", "must be shared by", "often inspires"], ["a difficult", "an exhilarating", "a productive"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AEG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 다음 문장 단서: Too often, the peak seems forever out of reach → 실망스러운 경험 → a disappointing.\n(ii) 끝없는 경사를 터벅터벅 올라온 물리학자들도 같은 느낌일 것 → must be shared by.\n(iii) 끝없이 오르는 중 → a difficult climb.\n정답: A, E, G", "trap": "(i) a breathtaking은 awe-inspiring view에 끌리지만, 정상이 늘 손에 닿지 않는다는 단서와 반대. (iii) an exhilarating도 같은 함정.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"a disappointing": "실망스러운", "a breathtaking": "숨이 멎을 듯한", "an unpredictable": "예측할 수 없는", "is sometimes baffling to": "~에게 때때로 당혹스럽다", "must be shared by": "~도 틀림없이 공유하는", "often inspires": "종종 영감을 주다", "a difficult": "어려운", "an exhilarating": "아주 신나는", "a productive": "생산적인"}, "src": "verbal218 Q4 · 25/11, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author would most likely agree that in early agricultural communities cats would have been", "choices": ["more tolerant than ferrets of contact with humans", "as incapable of performing directed tasks as ferrets", "less likely to be solitary than ferrets", "less useful than terrier dogs at controlling rodents", "more easily domesticated than terrier dogs"], "columns": null, "pid": "v224_p5", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: even as mousers, in this latter role, terrier dogs and ferrets are preferable.\n쥐 잡는 역할에서도 테리어와 페럿이 고양이보다 낫다 → 고양이는 테리어보다 설치류 퇴치에 덜 유용 → D.\n정답: D", "trap": "B: 페럿이 '지시된 일을 못한다'는 말은 없음, 고양이에 대해서만 언급.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"obligate carnivore": "절대 육식동물", "mouser": "쥐 잡는 동물", "domestication": "가축화"}, "src": "verbal224 Q5 · 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence in the context of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["It challenges a widely accepted theory presented in the passage.", "It explains a fact that has long puzzled researchers.", "It draws a conclusion from evidence presented in the passage.", "It presents new facts in support of a hypothesis.", "It formulates a new hypothesis from evidence presented in the passage."], "columns": null, "pid": "v224_p5", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 내용: 고양이는 가축화에 부적합(육식, 독립적, 유용성 낮음) → Accordingly, 일부러 선택했을 리 없다.\n강조 문장: Rather, the best inference is that... 사람이 단지 용인했고 점차 분화했다.\n앞서 제시한 증거에서 결론을 이끌어 냄 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "E: 'new hypothesis'는 그럴듯하지만, 'the best inference'로 앞 증거로부터 결론을 맺는 문장. A: 이 문장이 지문의 다른 이론에 도전하는 게 아님.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inference": "추론", "diverge": "갈라지다, 분화하다", "tolerate": "용인하다"}, "src": "verbal224 Q6 · 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v24_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["examine the origins of a particular style of painting", "analyze the paintings of a particular school", "point out the weakness that underlies a criticism", "compare two different approaches to the painting of objects", "rebut a criticism of a particular painter's integrity"], "columns": null, "pid": "v24_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 당시 비평가들이 Stubbs의 재산 그림을 비판 → 일반화된 그림을 사는 것이 취향과 시민적 덕의 증표.\nYet 이후: 이 '무관심한 취향' 개념 자체가 사적 이익(이미 재산을 충분히 가짐)에 근거.\n비판의 밑바탕에 깔린 약점을 지적 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "E: Stubbs의 '정직성'을 변호하는 것이 아니라 비판 논리의 모순을 지적하는 것. D: 두 화법 비교가 목적이 아님.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"materiality": "물질성", "disinterested": "사심 없는, 공평한", "avaricious": "탐욕스러운", "legitimate": "정당화하다"}, "src": "verbal24 Q5"}, {"id": "v24_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true about the painting of property as it is described in the passage?", "choices": ["It was typified in the work of George Stubbs.", "It was usually commissioned by persons who had great political power.", "It was regarded in the eighteenth century as a mark of good taste.", "It was at its most popular in eighteenth-century Britain.", "It was advocated primarily by those who owned a great deal of property."], "columns": null, "pid": "v24_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Paintings of property ... such as those created by eighteenth-century British painter George Stubbs.\nStubbs의 그림이 재산 그림의 대표적 예 → A.\n정답: A", "trap": "C: 좋은 취향의 증표로 여겨진 것은 '물질에 무관심한 일반화된 그림'이고 재산 그림은 비난받음 → 관계 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"typify": "전형적으로 보여주다", "commission": "의뢰하다", "condemn": "비난하다"}, "src": "verbal24 Q6"}, {"id": "v24_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "With which of the following statements about \"paintings displaying lofty unconcern with materiality\" would the author be most likely to agree?", "choices": ["Only the property-rich collector could appreciate paintings of this type.", "Such paintings demonstrated the collector's degree of taste and civic virtue.", "Such paintings were often collected by people who were quite property-rich.", "Collectors of such paintings often displayed them for the public's benefit.", "Collectors of such paintings were, as a class, the most avaricious members of their society."], "columns": null, "pid": "v24_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: it was because the 'public' man or woman already owned enough that he or she was presumed to be free from the urge to own more.\n이런 그림을 수집하는 사람들은 이미 재산이 충분한 사람들 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "B: 취향과 시민적 덕을 보여준다는 것은 당시 비평가들의 견해이지 저자는 이를 비판함. A: 'Only'는 지나치게 극단적.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lofty": "고상한, 초연한", "unconcern": "무관심", "civic virtue": "시민적 덕성", "property-rich": "재산이 많은"}, "src": "verbal24 Q7"}, {"id": "v8_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although both salinization and alkalinization impact water quality, they have generally been treated as _____ phenomena; however, new research proves that the processes, which impact most of the drainage area of the United States, are in fact closely linked.", "choices": ["unrelated", "insignificant", "unimportant", "reversible", "separate", "incremental"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "however 대조: 새 연구는 두 과정이 실제로는 closely linked라고 증명.\n→ 이전에는 '관련 없는' 현상으로 취급됨.\n빈칸 = '분리된, 관련 없는'이라는 뜻.\nunrelated와 separate가 쌍.\n정답: A, E", "trap": "insignificant / unimportant도 쌍이지만 대조 대상이 'closely linked'이므로 중요성이 아닌 연관성이 핵심.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unrelated": "관련 없는", "insignificant": "사소한", "unimportant": "중요하지 않은", "reversible": "되돌릴 수 있는", "separate": "별개의", "incremental": "점진적인"}, "src": "verbal8 Q9"}, {"id": "v214_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The writer's expression of _____ sentiments in fluid, vigorous prose is a strange blending of the high and the low, like an opera performed by sloppily dressed, unkempt musicians.", "choices": ["patriotic", "vile", "noble", "base", "tender", "lofty"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심: a strange blending of the high and the low.\n'fluid, vigorous prose'는 긍정적(high) → 빈칸의 감정은 low여야 고상함과 저속함의 혼합이 됨.\n빈칸 = 부정적, '저속한, 천한'이라는 뜻.\nvile과 base가 쌍.\n정답: B, D", "trap": "noble / lofty도 쌍이지만, 이 경우 감정·문체 모두 high가 되어 'high와 low의 혼합'이 성립하지 않음. 오페라 비유의 순서에 끌리면 틀리기 쉬움.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"vile": "비열한, 상스러운", "patriotic": "애국적인", "noble": "고귀한", "base": "천한, 저속한", "tender": "다정한", "lofty": "고상한"}, "src": "verbal214 Q11 · 25/1, 24/10, 24/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Accounts of early opera performances—both of the performances themselves and of their social milieu—indicate that the origins of the genre were anything but _____; it began at the peak.", "choices": ["lavish", "disreputable", "sumptuous", "decadent", "plebeian", "humble"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "EF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: it began at the peak (정점에서 시작했다). anything but = 결코 ~가 아닌.\n기원이 결코 ___하지 않았다 = 미천하지 않았다.\n빈칸 = '보잘것없는, 서민적인'이라는 뜻.\nplebeian과 humble이 쌍.\n정답: E, F", "trap": "lavish / sumptuous(호화로운)도 쌍이지만 'anything but lavish'는 '정점에서 시작'과 정반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lavish": "호화로운", "disreputable": "평판이 나쁜", "sumptuous": "호화로운", "decadent": "퇴폐적인", "plebeian": "서민의, 평민의", "humble": "미천한, 보잘것없는"}, "src": "verbal240 Q12 · 26/1, 25/10, 25/7, 25/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v22_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, would most help to explain the greater effect of zander on the native fish population?", "choices": ["The climate in Britain is very similar to the climate in regions to which zander are native.", "Most of the zander removed were fully grown, and fully grown zander eat large numbers of smaller zander.", "Every year a large number of zander are caught by sport fishers in Britain's waterways.", "Previous government programs designed to remove nonnative species from Britain's waterways have failed.", "Zander are just one of several nonnative fish that prey on the other fish found in Britain's waterways."], "columns": null, "pid": "v22_p3", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "역설: 정부가 상당수의 zander를 제거했는데 올해 토종 어류 손실이 오히려 증가.\nB: 제거된 것은 주로 다 자란 zander이고, 성체는 작은 zander를 많이 잡아먹음.\n→ 성체 제거로 어린 zander가 급증, 이들이 작은 토종 어류를 더 많이 먹음 → 역설 해결.\n정답: B", "trap": "C: 낚시꾼이 매년 zander를 잡는다는 것은 오히려 개체수 감소 요인으로, 손실 증가를 설명하지 못함.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"devastating": "파괴적인", "native": "토종의", "nonnative": "외래의"}, "src": "verbal22 Q13"}, {"id": "v226_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, in the era before phonographs, violinists probably", "choices": ["had greater difficulty maintaining intonation than later violinists did", "employed significantly less vibrato than later violinists did", "were unconcerned with others' subjective judgments of their playing", "were more skilled at sight-reading music than later violinists were", "did not understand how to use vibrato effectively"], "columns": null, "pid": "v226_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Early recordings of violinists suggest that vibrato ... was once used more sparingly than it is today.\n이후 1930년대에 continuous vibrato가 표준이 됨.\n축음기 이전 바이올리니스트는 비브라토를 훨씬 덜 사용 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "E: 비브라토를 덜 썼다고 해서 효과적으로 쓰는 법을 몰랐다는 뜻은 아님. A: 음정 문제는 축음기 이후 의식하게 된 것.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cover up": "숨기다", "vibrato": "비브라토(음을 떨리게 하는 기법)", "sparingly": "아껴서, 드물게", "intonation": "음정"}, "src": "verbal226 Q14 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v226_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies that after phonograph technology became widespread, which of the following occurred?", "choices": ["Violinists playing concerts applied a technique in a way that was first popularized in the recording studio.", "Conservatories taught violinists to play in a style that matched what was heard on the earliest phonograph recordings of violin playing.", "Violinists purged from their concert programs pieces of music that were poorly suited to recording."], "columns": null, "pid": "v226_p4", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A 근거: What worked in recording studios spread to concert stages. → 녹음실에서 먼저 유행한 기법(연속 비브라토)을 연주회에도 적용. 맞음.\nB: 음악원이 가르친 것은 연속 비브라토인데, 초기 녹음은 비브라토를 아껴 쓴 스타일 → 반대.\nC: 녹음에 맞지 않는 곡을 제외했다는 언급 없음.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 'phonograph recordings'와 'conservatories'라는 단어가 둘 다 지문에 나와 끌리지만, 초기 녹음 스타일(적은 비브라토)과 음악원 스타일(연속 비브라토)은 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"purged": "제거하다", "purge": "제거하다", "conservatory": "음악원", "self-conscious": "의식하는, 신경 쓰는"}, "src": "verbal226 Q15 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.3 / S2 2.5"}, {"set": 9, "sections": [[{"id": "v235_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Some experts now feel that exercise should not be regarded as _____ other treatments for depression: they believe that exercise can itself serve as an appropriate remedy for some forms of the mood disorder.", "choices": ["a model for", "a substitute for", "an improvement on", "an adjunct to", "an impediment to"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 앞 문장의 근거: 운동은 '그 자체로(itself)' 우울증의 적절한 치료법이 될 수 있다.\n앞 문장은 운동을 '___로 여겨서는 안 된다'고 하므로, 빈칸 = 운동을 단지 보조적인 것으로 보는 시각.\n즉 '다른 치료의 곁다리/보조 수단'이라는 뜻이 필요.\nan adjunct to(~의 부속물, 보조 수단)가 '그 자체로 치료'와 정확히 대조된다.\n정답: D (an adjunct to)", "trap": "B(a substitute for): '대체물'로 보지 말라는 건 '그 자체로 치료가 된다'는 뒷문장과 오히려 모순된다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"adjunct": "부속물", "a model for": "~의 본보기", "a substitute for": "~의 대체물", "an improvement on": "~보다 개선된 것", "an adjunct to": "~의 부속물, 보조 수단", "an impediment to": "~의 방해물"}, "src": "verbal235 Q1 · 26/1, 25/7, 24/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v213_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Despite the fact that the book promises a complete rethinking of the factors contributing to the conflict, the picture that the book paints is (i) _____; in identifying causes, it is more orthodox than (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["obscure", "detailed", "familiar"], ["restrictive", "revisionist", "enigmatic"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Despite → 대조: 책은 '완전한 재고(rethinking)'를 약속했지만 실제 그림은 그렇지 않다.\n빈칸(i) = 새롭지 않은, 익숙한 → familiar.\n빈칸(ii): 'more orthodox than ___' → orthodox(정통적)의 반대 = 기존 해석을 뒤엎는 → revisionist.\n세미콜론 뒤도 '새롭지 않다'는 같은 방향으로 이어진다.\n정답: C, E (familiar / revisionist)", "trap": "(i) obscure: '애매하다'도 부정적이지만, 약속(완전한 재고)과의 대조 포인트는 '새로움의 부재'이지 '불명확함'이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"obscure": "모호한, 잘 알려지지 않은", "detailed": "상세한", "familiar": "익숙한, 낯익은", "restrictive": "제한적인", "revisionist": "수정주의적인(기존 해석을 뒤엎는)", "enigmatic": "수수께끼 같은"}, "src": "verbal213 Q2 · 24/9, 23/3, 22/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v237_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Until recently, historians of science treated fundamental research as (i) _____ pure science—that is, both were taken to refer to scientific investigations (ii) _____ technological and/or commercial objectives. Now, however, historians have realized that in the mid-twentieth century the phrase \"fundamental research\" was sometimes (iii) _____ industrial scientists, who applied the phrase to their own work in order to distinguish it from that of applied scientists and thus elevate their status.", "choices": null, "columns": [["inimical to", "synonymous with", "more prestigious than"], ["mired in", "free from", "motivated by"], ["appropriated by", "confusing for", "objectionable to"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BEG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) '즉(that is), 둘 다(both) 같은 것을 가리킨다고 여겨졌다' → fundamental research = pure science → synonymous with.\n(ii) 순수 과학의 정의: 기술적/상업적 목적에서 '자유로운' 연구 → free from.\n(iii) Now, however → 반전: 산업 과학자들이 자기 지위를 높이려고 그 표현을 '가져다 썼다' → appropriated by.\n정답: B, E, G (synonymous with / free from / appropriated by)", "trap": "(ii) motivated by: 순수 과학을 '상업 목적에 의해 동기부여된' 것으로 정의하면 정반대다. (iii) objectionable to는 '자기 일에 적용했다'는 내용과 모순.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inimical to": "~에 적대적인", "synonymous with": "~와 동의어인", "more prestigious than": "~보다 더 권위 있는", "mired in": "~에 빠져 꼼짝 못하는", "free from": "~이 없는, ~에서 자유로운", "motivated by": "~에 의해 동기부여된", "appropriated by": "~에 의해 전용된(가져다 쓰인)", "confusing for": "~에게 혼란스러운", "objectionable to": "~에게 불쾌한, 반대할 만한"}, "src": "verbal237 Q3 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v215_q4", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, in which of the following ways did the underground economy of women in eighteenth-century colonial North America differ from other informal trade networks?", "choices": ["It continued after other informal trade networks had disappeared.", "It did not provide its participants with much economic power.", "It gave its participants a certain degree of control over how they spent their time."], "columns": null, "pid": "v215_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "질문은 '다른 비공식 거래망과 어떻게 달랐나(differ)'.\n근거: \"Unlike other informal local trade networks..., the economy of women never totally ceased to exist.\"\n→ 다른 망은 사라졌지만 여성 경제는 계속 존재 = A.\nB, C는 여성 경제의 특징으로 언급되긴 하지만 다른 거래망과의 '차이'로 제시되지 않았다.\n정답: A", "trap": "C: 시간 통제권을 준 건 사실이지만, 다른 거래망은 그렇지 않았다는 비교 근거가 없다(차이점이 아님).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"barter": "물물교환", "underrated": "과소평가된", "informal": "비공식적인", "cease": "중단되다"}, "src": "verbal215 Q4 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v215_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the context indicated, the word “underground” most nearly means", "choices": ["subversive", "secretive", "subterranean", "alternative", "antiestablishment"], "columns": null, "pid": "v215_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "문맥: 'underground economy' = 가정 내 생산·이웃 간 물물교환으로 이루어진 비공식 경제.\n앞 문장에서 이 활동이 '상업적이지 않다고' 간과되어 왔다고 함 → 공식 경제 밖의 '대안적' 경제라는 뜻.\n불법·비밀·반체제적 뉘앙스는 지문에 없다.\n정답: D (alternative)", "trap": "B(secretive)/A(subversive): 'underground'의 흔한 뜻(비밀의, 전복적인)이지만 지문에는 숨기거나 체제를 거스른다는 내용이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "underground", "glosses": {"alternative": "대안적인, 비주류의", "subversive": "전복적인", "subterranean": "지하의", "antiestablishment": "반체제적인"}, "src": "verbal215 Q5 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v29_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Price knew about how to do people favors, sometimes just from kindness, but often out of _____.", "choices": ["self-interest", "benevolence", "magnanimity", "opportunism", "disinterest", "mercy"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: 'sometimes just from kindness, but often out of ___' → but으로 kindness와 대조.\n빈칸 = 친절과 반대되는 동기, 즉 '자기 이익을 위한 계산'.\nself-interest(사리사욕)와 opportunism(기회주의)이 같은 뜻으로 짝을 이룬다.\n정답: A, D (self-interest, opportunism)", "trap": "benevolence/magnanimity/mercy는 kindness와 같은 방향이라 but 대조를 깨뜨린다. disinterest(사심 없음)도 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"self-interest": "사리사욕, 이기심", "benevolence": "자비심, 선의", "magnanimity": "관대함", "opportunism": "기회주의", "disinterest": "사심 없음(공평무사); 무관심", "mercy": "자비"}, "src": "verbal29 Q6"}, {"id": "v15_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to Panamanian composer Danilo Perez, the gravity of jazz pianist Randy Weston's performances is _____: you can copy one of his chords, but it doesn't sound the same.", "choices": ["elusive", "indelible", "unattainable", "estranging", "purposeful", "alienating"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤가 설명: 화음을 그대로 따라 쳐도 같은 소리가 나지 않는다.\n→ 그의 연주의 무게감은 복제·포착할 수 없는 것. 빈칸 = '붙잡기 어려운, 도달할 수 없는'.\nelusive(포착하기 어려운)와 unattainable(도달할 수 없는)이 짝.\n정답: A, C (elusive, unattainable)", "trap": "B(indelible): '지워지지 않는' 깊은 인상도 칭찬처럼 들리지만, '따라 해도 같지 않다'는 복제 불가능성과 무관하고 짝도 없다. estranging/alienating은 짝이지만 의미가 안 맞는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"indelible": "지울 수 없는", "elusive": "붙잡기 어려운, 포착하기 힘든", "unattainable": "도달할 수 없는", "estranging": "소원하게 만드는", "purposeful": "목적이 있는, 의도적인", "alienating": "멀어지게 하는, 소외시키는"}, "src": "verbal15 Q7"}, {"id": "v219_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "With Duncan's ambitious study, Chesnutt appears finally to have outgrown the _____ treatment he once received from literary historians and critics for whom he typically served as a merely transitional figure in the African American tradition.", "choices": ["cursory", "jocular", "heartfelt", "didactic", "fervent", "perfunctory"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 비평가들에게 그는 'merely transitional figure(단지 과도기적 인물)'였다 → 진지하게 다뤄지지 않았다.\nDuncan의 '야심찬(ambitious)' 연구로 그런 대우를 '벗어났다(outgrown)' → 빈칸 = 대충의, 피상적인.\ncursory(대충 하는)와 perfunctory(형식적인)가 짝.\n정답: A, F (cursory, perfunctory)", "trap": "didactic(교훈적인): 비평 맥락이라 그럴듯해 보이지만 '과도기적 인물로만 취급'과 연결되지 않고 짝도 없다. heartfelt/fervent는 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cursory": "대충 하는, 피상적인", "fervent": "열렬한", "perfunctory": "형식적인, 마지못해 하는", "jocular": "익살스러운", "heartfelt": "진심 어린", "didactic": "교훈적인, 가르치려 드는"}, "src": "verbal219 Q8 · 24년 10월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v25_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The _____ of native South American textiles at the time of the Spanish conquest should not be surprising: it represented the apogee of one of the world's oldest and most sophisticated weaving and dyeing traditions.", "choices": ["splendor", "eccentricity", "diversity", "brilliance", "practicality", "popularity"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤가 이유: 세계에서 가장 오래되고 '정교한' 직조·염색 전통의 정점(apogee)이었다.\n→ 놀랄 일이 아닌 것 = 직물의 뛰어남/화려함. 빈칸 = 긍정, '훌륭함'.\nsplendor(화려함)와 brilliance(탁월함, 광채)가 짝.\n정답: A, D (splendor, brilliance)", "trap": "C(diversity): 그럴듯하지만 '정교함의 정점'은 다양성이 아니라 수준의 높음을 뜻하고, 짝이 되는 단어가 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"splendor": "화려함, 장엄함", "eccentricity": "기이함", "diversity": "다양성", "brilliance": "탁월함, 광채", "practicality": "실용성", "popularity": "인기"}, "src": "verbal25 Q7"}, {"id": "v5_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author would be most likely to agree with which of the following statements about \"Current scholarship\"?", "choices": ["It underestimates the extent to which the American labor movement was affected by the decline in influence of the Knights of Labor.", "It tends to downplay the intensity of the tension between skilled and unskilled workers who belonged to the Knights of Labor.", "It offers a more accurate view of the factors that led to the decline of the Knights of Labor than was offered in earlier scholarship.", "It tends to characterize the organizational structure of the Knights of Labor in ways that obscure its effect on the organization's decline.", "It fails to identify a key factor that accounts for the decline in membership of the Knights of Labor."], "columns": null, "pid": "v5_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Current scholarship은 쇠퇴 원인을 두 가지(숙련/비숙련 노동자 간 긴장, 고용주 단체의 반대)로 본다.\n저자는 이후 핵심 요인으로 \"competition from rival trade and fraternal organizations lured members away\"를 제시하고,\n\"the profusion of organizational alternatives... induced mass defection\"이라고 강조한다.\n→ 기존 학설은 이 핵심 요인(경쟁 조직으로의 이탈)을 놓쳤다 = E.\n정답: E", "trap": "D: 저자가 조직 구조를 언급하긴 하지만, 기존 학설이 조직 구조를 '왜곡해서 묘사했다'는 근거는 없다. B는 기존 학설이 오히려 그 긴장을 원인으로 꼽았으므로 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Current scholarship", "glosses": {"calamitous": "재앙적인", "extralegal": "법의 테두리 밖의", "profusion": "풍부함, 다수", "defection": "이탈, 변절"}, "src": "verbal5 Q10"}, {"id": "v5_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, the rapid decline in the Knights of Labor membership resulted in which of the following?", "choices": ["Greater prominence of labor activists who advocated a relatively moderate approach to organizing workers", "Increasing tensions between labor activists who advocated a broad-based approach to organizing workers and those who advocated a less inclusive approach", "A decline in the number of workers who regarded labor organizing as an effective means of advancing their interests", "An increase in the aggressiveness with which employer associations sought to undermine workers' efforts to organize", "An increase in public concern over the use of extralegal means to undermine workers' efforts to organize"], "columns": null, "pid": "v5_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거(1단락): 쇠퇴의 결과로 \"subsequent worker organizations took a less active and less broad-based organizational approach\",\n그리고 \"empowering those who promoted a less inclusive strategy\".\n→ 덜 급진적·덜 포괄적인(=비교적 온건한) 접근을 주장한 활동가들이 힘을 얻었다 = A.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 두 진영 간 '긴장이 커졌다'는 내용은 없다. 한쪽이 약해지고 다른 쪽이 힘을 얻었을 뿐이다. C는 노동 조직 자체에 대한 신뢰 감소로 범위를 벗어난다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"fraternal order": "친목 단체", "demoralize": "사기를 꺾다", "inclusive": "포괄적인", "repercussion": "(간접적) 영향, 파장"}, "src": "verbal5 Q11"}, {"id": "v5_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author implies that the \"organizations\" highlighted in the passage were", "choices": ["strengthened by their adoption of the Knights' organizational structure", "weakened by their separation of skilled from unskilled workers", "more intent than the Knights had been on achieving radical political reforms", "more aggressive than the Knights had been in countering the extralegal strategies used by employer associations", "less committed than the Knights had been to including all workers"], "columns": null, "pid": "v5_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "highlight된 organizations = 회원을 빼앗아 간 'rival trade and fraternal organizations'(경쟁 직종·친목 단체).\n1단락: Knights는 노동자를 '하나의 계급(as a class)'으로 조직한 포괄적 단체였고, 그 뒤 \"less inclusive strategy\"가 득세했다.\ntrade organization(직종별 조직)은 특정 직종만 받아들이므로 Knights보다 덜 포괄적이라는 함의.\n→ 모든 노동자를 포함하는 데 Knights보다 덜 적극적 = E.\n정답: E", "trap": "C: 오히려 반대. 급진 개혁을 주장한 쪽은 Knights였고, 그 몰락으로 급진 개혁론자들이 사기를 잃었다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "rival trade and fraternal organizations", "glosses": {"rival": "경쟁하는", "factional": "파벌의", "dissension": "불화, 의견 충돌", "demise": "종말, 소멸"}, "src": "verbal5 Q12"}], [{"id": "v2_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "In the nineteenth century, geology became so respected among middle-class Britons that the science came to be seen as _____ a yardstick by which other disciplines measured their scientific rigor and imaginative power.", "choices": ["accessible", "derivative", "pragmatic", "empirical", "paradigmatic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 빈칸 뒤 동격 설명 'a yardstick by which other disciplines measured...'(다른 학문이 자신을 재는 잣대).\n'so respected' → 빈칸 = 긍정, '기준이 되는, 모범적인'.\nparadigmatic(모범이 되는, 전형적인)이 '잣대'와 정확히 맞는다.\n정답: E (paradigmatic)", "trap": "D(empirical): 지질학은 실증적이긴 하지만, '다른 학문의 잣대'라는 동격 설명과 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"paradigmatic": "모범이 되는, 전형적인", "accessible": "접근하기 쉬운", "derivative": "파생적인, 독창성 없는", "pragmatic": "실용적인", "empirical": "경험적인, 실증적인"}, "src": "verbal2 Q1"}, {"id": "v202_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Dr. Nicolelis believes that scientists are going to (i) _____ all the brain's information-processing mechanisms—or at least enough of them to yield improvements in neural medicine. Yet he also believes that certain aspects of our minds may remain (ii) _____ because our most meaningful thoughts are written in a code that is unique to each of us.", "choices": null, "columns": [["discount", "misunderstand", "ferret out"], ["inviolable", "perspicuous", "tractable"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'or at least enough of them to yield improvements' → 과학자들이 메커니즘을 '알아낼' 것이라는 긍정적 전망 → ferret out.\n(ii) Yet → 대조: 그래도 마음의 일부는 끝까지 알아낼 수 없을 것. 이유: 생각이 사람마다 고유한 코드로 쓰여 있음.\n→ 빈칸 = 침범·해독 불가능한 → inviolable.\n정답: C, D (ferret out / inviolable)", "trap": "(ii) perspicuous(명쾌한)/tractable(다루기 쉬운): '해독 가능하다'는 쪽이라 Yet 대조를 거스른다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ferret out": "찾아내다, 캐내다", "inviolable": "침범할 수 없는", "perspicuous": "명쾌한, 알기 쉬운", "discount": "무시하다, 경시하다", "misunderstand": "오해하다", "tractable": "다루기 쉬운"}, "src": "verbal202 Q3 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v214_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "High self-esteem has recently assumed a somewhat (i) _____ status in social psychology. On the one hand, high self-esteem is believed to confer a wide variety of adaptive and affective benefits; on the other hand, positive self-views have been linked to a number of intrapersonal and interpersonal strategies that can reasonably be described as (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["esoteric", "elevated", "paradoxical"], ["antisocial", "efficacious", "transparent"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'On the one hand(장점) ... on the other hand(단점)' 구조.\n(i) 장점과 단점이 공존 → 모순적인 지위 → paradoxical.\n(ii) adaptive/affective benefits와 반대되는 부정적 평가 → antisocial(반사회적).\n정답: C, D (paradoxical / antisocial)", "trap": "(ii) efficacious(효과적인): 긍정이라 on the other hand의 대조가 사라진다. (i) elevated는 장점만 반영.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"esoteric": "난해한, 소수만 아는", "elevated": "높은, 고상한", "paradoxical": "역설적인, 모순된", "antisocial": "반사회적인", "efficacious": "효과적인", "transparent": "투명한, 명백한"}, "src": "verbal214 Q3 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Statistics is the branch of applied mathematics that studies ways of drawing inferences from limited and imperfect data. Of course, if all data sources were totally (i) _____, statisticians could do little but (ii) _____ every conclusion with “but we could be wrong about this.” A mathematical science of statistics is possible because, although repeating an experiment numerous times may not yield uniform results, some results are more (iii) _____ than others.", "choices": null, "columns": [["empirical", "capricious", "defensible"], ["qualify", "affirm", "substantiate"], ["dubious", "unexpected", "common"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'Of course, if all data were totally ___' → 통계가 불가능해지는 가정 → 완전히 제멋대로 → capricious.\n(ii) 그러면 모든 결론에 '우리가 틀릴 수도 있다'는 단서를 달 수밖에 → qualify(단서를 달다, 제한하다).\n(iii) 반복 실험 결과가 균일하지 않아도 어떤 결과가 다른 것보다 더 '흔하기' 때문에 통계가 가능 → common.\n정답: B, D, I (capricious / qualify / common)", "trap": "(ii) affirm/substantiate: '틀릴 수 있다'는 말을 붙이는 건 확증이 아니라 유보다. (iii) unexpected는 통계의 근거가 되지 못한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"empirical": "경험적인", "capricious": "변덕스러운, 제멋대로인", "defensible": "옹호할 수 있는", "qualify": "단서를 달다, (진술을) 제한하다", "affirm": "단언하다", "substantiate": "입증하다", "dubious": "의심스러운", "unexpected": "예상치 못한", "common": "흔한"}, "src": "verbal230 Q4 · 25년 9월, 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v214_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["explain why certain scientists rejected a particular hypothesis", "show how a conventional theory was weakened by a new discovery", "discuss a shift in an approach to explaining a natural phenomenon", "account for the widespread influence of a scientific theory", "trace the origins of a scientific dispute"], "columns": null, "pid": "v214_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 초기 과학자들이 충돌설을 받아들이기 어려웠던 이유(원형 크레이터, 충돌체 부재, 규산염 용융물 → 화산설)\n→ \"The breakthrough in understanding crater origin was the recognition that the shock...\"\n즉 크레이터(자연 현상)의 기원 설명 방식이 화산설에서 충돌·충격파 이론으로 바뀐 과정 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 과학자들이 충돌 가설을 거부한 이유는 앞부분에만 해당하고, 후반의 '돌파구'를 빠뜨린다. B는 방향이 반대(기존 이론이 약화된 게 아니라 새 이해가 등장).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"elliptical": "타원형의", "silicate": "규산염", "vaporize": "기화시키다", "impactor": "충돌체"}, "src": "verbal214 Q5 · 24년 6월, 22년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v214_q6", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "What can be inferred from the passage about the silicate melt found around craters?", "choices": ["It was not caused exclusively by volcanic processes.", "It led early scientists to consider volcanic activity as a cause of crater formation.", "It can probably be explained by the intense heat caused by impact."], "columns": null, "pid": "v214_p1", "answer": "ABC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "B: \"there was often silicate melt around, suggesting that craters were caused by volcanic processes\" → 화산설을 떠올리게 함.\nC: 마지막 문장 \"The impact also generates enough heat to... melt the native rock\" → 충돌열로 설명 가능.\nA: 충돌열로도 생기므로 화산 활동만이 원인은 아니다 → 추론 가능.\n세 진술 모두 지문에서 뒷받침된다.\n정답: A, B, C", "trap": "A를 빼기 쉽다: 'not exclusively'는 C에서 바로 도출되는 약한 진술이므로 맞다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"silicate melt": "규산염 용융물", "native rock": "원래 그 자리의 암석", "exclusively": "오로지, 독점적으로"}, "src": "verbal214 Q6 · 24년 6월, 22년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v222_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["contrast two types of archaeological evidence", "explain why a particular finding is puzzling", "note an exception to a generalization", "question a particular interpretation", "evaluate two competing hypotheses"], "columns": null, "pid": "v222_p7", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "로마 고고학자들은 빗을 거의 항상 여성의 미·여성 세계와 연결했다(전통적 해석).\n저자는 다른 시대의 남성적 의미, 로마 군영지에서 나온 많은 빗을 근거로 \"make one feel uneasy about the strengths of the traditional interpretation\".\n결론: 병사들 스스로 빗을 썼을 수도 있다 → 특정 해석에 의문 제기 = D.\n정답: D", "trap": "B: 군영지의 빗이 '수수께끼'라고 설명하는 것이 목적이 아니라, 그것을 근거로 기존 해석을 의심하는 것이 목적이다. E는 두 가설을 대등하게 평가하지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"toilet articles": "세면·몸단장 용품", "ungendered": "성별 구분이 없는", "concubine": "첩", "grave furnishings": "부장품"}, "src": "verbal222 Q7 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v222_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions \"grave furnishings\" primarily to", "choices": ["account for a particular error made by some archaeologists and historians", "acknowledge the diversity of uses for combs in different historical periods", "establish a precedent for a particular assumption about the mundus muliebris", "suggest that combs may have had different meanings in funerary settings than in other settings", "substantiate a particular interpretation of the significance of recovered combs"], "columns": null, "pid": "v222_p7", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "\"grave furnishings\" 문장: 청동기~철기, 중세에 빗은 남성미의 상징이었고, 그래서 전사 무덤의 부장품이 되었다.\n바로 앞 문장의 주장(다른 시대에 빗은 남성 정체성의 표지였다)을 구체적 증거로 뒷받침하는 역할.\n→ 회수된 빗의 의미에 대한 특정 해석(남성적 상징)을 입증 = E.\n정답: E", "trap": "B: '다양한 용도'를 인정하려는 게 아니라 '남성적 의미'라는 한 가지 해석을 뒷받침한다. D: 장례 맥락과 다른 맥락의 의미 차이는 지문에 없다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "grave furnishings", "glosses": {"substantiate": "입증하다", "precedent": "선례", "funerary": "장례의", "furnishings": "부장품, 비품"}, "src": "verbal222 Q8 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v222_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies which of the following about Roman archaeologists and ancient historians?", "choices": ["They have tended to underestimate the significance of finds from ancient Roman army camps.", "They appear to have misconstrued the decorative function of combs found at sites of ancient Roman army camps.", "They diverge from researchers studying many other periods in the way they interpret combs recovered from historical sites.", "They make an assumption about the use of ancient combs based on evidence from later periods of history.", "They have generally assumed that combs were primarily used by women but that other toilet articles were used equally by both genders."], "columns": null, "pid": "v222_p7", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"Such an interpretation is in striking contrast with many other periods of the European past, when combs appear to have been either ungendered or tokens of an exclusive male identity.\"\n→ 로마 연구자들은 빗을 여성과 연결하는데, 다른 시대 연구에서는 무성별·남성적으로 본다.\n즉 빗 해석 방식이 다른 시대 연구자들과 다르다 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "D: 오히려 반대. 로마 연구자들은 다른 시대 증거와 '대조되는' 해석을 했지, 후대 증거에 근거하지 않았다. A는 '과소평가' 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"diverge": "갈라지다, 다르다", "misconstrue": "잘못 해석하다", "interpretation": "해석"}, "src": "verbal222 Q9 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v202_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In Roth’s fiction, politics is an element that does not naturally occur in _____ form but is always getting confused and mixed up with shame and anger, baseball and sex.", "choices": ["an unalloyed", "an unbiased", "an uncontroversial", "an objective", "a neat", "a tendentious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: but 뒤 '항상 수치·분노·야구·섹스와 뒤섞이고 혼동된다(confused and mixed up)'.\n→ 정치는 '순수한/깔끔하게 분리된' 형태로는 나타나지 않는다. 빈칸 = 뒤섞이지 않은.\nunalloyed(섞이지 않은, 순수한)와 neat(깔끔한, 다른 것이 섞이지 않은)가 짝.\n정답: A, E (an unalloyed, a neat)", "trap": "unbiased/objective는 서로 동의어라 짝처럼 보이지만, '편향'이 아니라 '뒤섞임'이 문맥의 핵심이라 틀렸다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unalloyed": "순수한", "neat": "깔끔한", "tendentious": "편향적인", "an unalloyed": "섞이지 않은, 순수한", "an unbiased": "편견 없는", "an uncontroversial": "논란이 없는", "an objective": "객관적인", "a neat": "깔끔한, 섞이지 않은", "a tendentious": "편향적인, 특정 주장을 내세우는"}, "src": "verbal202 Q11 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Lions are idiosyncratic animals that exhibit a remarkably wide range of behaviors, resisting our attempts to _____ them.", "choices": ["assess", "protect", "pigeonhole", "stereotype", "appreciate", "admire"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 사자는 'idiosyncratic(개성이 강한)' + '놀랍도록 넓은 범위의 행동'.\n→ 우리가 사자를 하나의 틀에 넣으려는 시도에 저항한다. 빈칸 = 범주화하다, 틀에 넣다.\npigeonhole(분류해 틀에 넣다)과 stereotype(정형화하다)이 짝.\n정답: C, D (pigeonhole, stereotype)", "trap": "A(assess): 평가하려는 시도에 저항한다는 것도 말은 되지만, '다양한 행동'과 직접 연결되는 건 '틀에 끼우기'이고 assess는 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pigeonhole": "(틀에) 분류하다, 정형화하다", "assess": "평가하다", "protect": "보호하다", "stereotype": "고정관념을 씌우다, 정형화하다", "appreciate": "진가를 알아보다", "admire": "감탄하다"}, "src": "verbal198 Q12 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v30_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In its few decades of existence, the field of technology assessment has undergone large changes: its original high ambitions to predict consequences of technology have been _____ if not discarded.", "choices": ["deferred", "subverted", "abandoned", "relinquished", "tempered", "modulated"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "EF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: '___ if not discarded' = '버려지지는 않았더라도 (적어도) ___되었다'.\n→ 빈칸은 discarded보다 약한 정도의 변화, 즉 '누그러지다, 완화되다'.\ntempered(누그러뜨려진)와 modulated(조절된, 완화된)가 짝. 콜론 앞 'large changes'와도 맞는다.\n정답: E, F (tempered, modulated)", "trap": "abandoned/relinquished는 동의어 짝이지만 discarded와 같은 뜻이라 'if not discarded' 구조가 무의미해진다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"deferred": "연기된", "subverted": "전복된", "abandoned": "버려진", "relinquished": "포기된", "tempered": "누그러진, 완화된", "modulated": "조절된, 완화된"}, "src": "verbal30 Q8"}, {"id": "v18_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "The information given, if accurate, most strongly supports which of the following hypotheses?", "choices": ["Fires in the habitat of E. penduliflora do not entirely destroy the plant's seeds even in the places where the fires burn most intensely.", "The nitrogen dioxide in automobile exhaust cannot harm plants of E. penduliflora after germination.", "If human intervention decreases the number of fires in the habitat of E. penduliflora, automobile exhaust can replicate the conditions the plant requires in order to thrive.", "Within the habitat of E. penduliflora, natural fires are significantly more frequent in areas with heavy automobile traffic than they are in other areas.", "Unless E. penduliflora seeds that have germinated can survive in the shade, automobile exhaust threatens the long-term survival of the plant in areas with heavy automobile traffic."], "columns": null, "pid": "v18_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "정상 경로: 불 → 연기 속 NO2로 발아 + 불이 덤불을 태워 햇빛 확보 → 빨리 자라 씨를 맺고 죽음.\n교통량 많은 곳: 불 없이 배기가스 NO2만으로 발아 → 덤불이 그대로라 햇빛이 없다.\n그늘에서 살아남지 못하면 발아한 씨는 씨를 맺기 전에 죽고, 휴면 씨앗 저장분만 소모된다.\n→ 그늘 생존이 불가능하다면 배기가스는 그 지역에서 식물의 장기 생존을 위협 = E.\n정답: E", "trap": "C: 배기가스가 발아는 대신할 수 있어도 '햇빛 확보(덤불 제거)'는 대신하지 못하므로 '번성 조건을 재현한다'는 틀렸다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dormant": "휴면 상태의", "germinate": "발아하다", "habitat": "서식지", "replicate": "재현하다"}, "src": "verbal18 Q11"}, {"id": "v210_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The argument anticipated in the highlighted sentence depends on which of the following assumptions?", "choices": ["The small craters on Europa's surface are possibly nonimpact craters.", "If leftover planetary building blocks exist, they must be larger than small comets.", "If small comets had formed in the Kuiper Belt, many would likely have impacted Europa.", "Europa was formed later than most other planetary bodies' solar system.", "If a planetary body is sparsely cratered, it cannot be formed in the Kuiper Belt."], "columns": null, "pid": "v210_p4", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "highlight 문장의 논리: 쿠이퍼 벨트에 잔여 물질이 있다면 → 소혜성이 형성됨 → 유로파는 수백만 년간 반복 충돌을 겪었을 것.\n이 기대가 성립하려면 '쿠이퍼 벨트에서 소혜성이 생겼다면 그중 다수가 실제로 유로파에 충돌했을 것'이라는 연결 고리가 필요.\n(실제로 지문 끝에서 '혜성이 태양열에 사라질 수도'라는 대안이 이 가정을 공격한다.)\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 작은 크레이터가 비충돌성일 수 있다는 건 오히려 논증을 약화하는 방향이지 필요한 가정이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"undermine": "약화시키다", "leftover": "남은, 잔여의", "impact crater": "충돌 크레이터", "sparsely": "드문드문"}, "src": "verbal210 Q14 · 24년 11월, 23년 7월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v210_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author suggests that if the traditional picture of planet formation were correct", "choices": ["Europa would likely be formed largely of material from the Kuiper Belt", "Europa would likely be formed from planetary building blocks left over from Jupiter's formation", "Europa would likely be unique in showing the impacts of small comets", "there would likely be many small comets originating from the Kuiper Belt", "there would likely be more large craters than small craters on Europa's surface"], "columns": null, "pid": "v210_p4", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"If this is correct, the Kuiper Belt... should hold leftover planetary building blocks.\"\n그리고 그 잔여 물질로부터 '소혜성(small comets)'이 형성된다는 전제가 이어진다.\n→ 전통적 그림이 맞다면 쿠이퍼 벨트에서 기원한 소혜성이 많아야 한다 = D.\n정답: D", "trap": "E: 큰 크레이터와 작은 크레이터의 비교는 지문에 없다. A/B: 유로파가 무엇으로 형성되었는지는 논의되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"Kuiper Belt": "카이퍼 벨트(해왕성 바깥 소천체 지대)", "building blocks": "구성 요소", "originate": "기원하다"}, "src": "verbal210 Q15 · 24년 11월, 23년 7월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.6 / S2 2.9"}, {"set": 10, "sections": [[{"id": "v227_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Some historians of science argue that chemistry had _____ scientific revolution in that seventeenth-century chemists failed to produce radical innovations parallel to those in other sciences at the time, and chemistry consequently matured later.", "choices": ["a mediated", "an oblique", "a postponed", "an inadvertent", "a surrogate"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "in that 이하가 이유: 17세기 화학자들은 다른 과학처럼 급진적 혁신을 내놓지 못했고, 그 결과 화학은 '더 늦게(later)' 성숙했다.\n빈칸 = 늦춰진, 지연된 과학혁명.\n정답: C (a postponed)", "trap": "B(an oblique, 간접적인): 혁명이 '돌려서' 일어났다는 뜻이라 'matured later'의 시간 지연 단서와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"a mediated": "매개된, 간접적인", "an oblique": "비스듬한, 간접적인", "a postponed": "연기된, 지연된", "an inadvertent": "의도치 않은", "a surrogate": "대리의"}, "src": "verbal227 Q1 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v27_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "She may have been (i) _____ when she was finance minister, fighting deficits, but now as prime minister she is marked by her (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["collaborative", "austere", "resourceful"], ["discretion", "largesse", "platitudes"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'may have been ... but now' → 과거와 현재 대조.\n(i) 재무장관으로 적자와 싸웠다 → 긴축적인 → austere.\n(ii) 대조로 지금은 돈을 후하게 쓰는 것으로 유명 → largesse(아낌없이 베풂).\n정답: B, E (austere / largesse)", "trap": "(ii) discretion(신중함): 그럴듯하지만 austere와의 '긴축 vs 씀씀이' 대조가 안 된다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"platitudes": "진부한 말", "collaborative": "협력적인", "austere": "긴축적인, 엄격한", "resourceful": "수완이 좋은", "discretion": "신중함, 재량", "largesse": "후한 베풂"}, "src": "verbal27 Q2"}, {"id": "v27_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "When learners are engaged in mathematical problem-solving, their activity does not have from the outset the structure of what will be considered a mathematical proof. Instead, a tangle of intuitions, know-how, factual knowledge, and a variety of other mental constructs allows learners to entertain choices and make decisions. Nonetheless, (i) _____ such mental activity (ii) _____ is (iii) _____: in many situations this process works, although it can prove to be wrong as a result of overgeneralizations.", "choices": null, "columns": [["concealing", "adapting", "describing"], ["from scrutiny", "as confused", "to the task"], ["uncommon", "unintentional", "uncharitable"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CEI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: 학습자의 문제풀이는 처음부터 증명 구조가 아니라 직관·지식이 '뒤엉킨(tangle)' 상태.\nNonetheless → 그렇다고 해서 이를 나쁘게 보면 안 된다. 콜론 뒤: 이 과정은 많은 경우 잘 작동한다.\n(i)(ii) 이런 정신 활동을 '혼란스럽다고 묘사하는 것' → describing ... as confused.\n(iii) 그렇게 묘사하는 건 '박하다, 공정하지 않다' → uncharitable.\n정답: C, E, I (describing / as confused / uncharitable)", "trap": "(i) adapting ... to the task: 그럴듯해 보이지만 'is ___'와 결합하면 '잘 작동한다'는 콜론 뒤 내용이 그 판단을 반박하는 구조가 안 된다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"concealing": "숨기는", "adapting": "적응시키는", "describing": "묘사하는", "from scrutiny": "면밀한 검토로부터", "as confused": "혼란스러운 것으로", "to the task": "그 과업에 맞게", "uncommon": "흔치 않은", "unintentional": "의도하지 않은", "uncharitable": "박한, 너그럽지 못한"}, "src": "verbal27 Q3"}, {"id": "v23_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies that its author would agree with which of the following statements about \"historical fiction, biography, court memoirs, and family history\"?", "choices": ["These genres had their origins primarily among pre-nineteenth-century British women writers.", "These genres were probably more reflective of women's views in pre-nineteenth-century Britain than they were in later periods.", "These genres can help scholars develop a comprehensive view of British women's historical writing.", "These genres have generally been regarded by scholars as more reliable sources of information about pre-nineteenth-century women than have other genres of historical writing.", "These genres are remarkably homogeneous in the way they represent the lives of pre-nineteenth-century women in Britain."], "columns": null, "pid": "v23_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"Isobel Grundy rightly argues that... scholars must define history broadly and include historical fiction, biography, court memoirs, and family history.\"\n'rightly'로 저자가 동의 → 이 장르들을 포함해야 여성 역사 서술을 폭넓게(포괄적으로) 볼 수 있다.\n→ 이 장르들이 포괄적 시각 형성에 도움이 된다 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "E: 저자는 오히려 개별 작가·텍스트의 다양성을 강조하므로 '동질적'은 반대다. D는 다른 장르와의 신뢰도 비교로 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "historical fiction, biography, court memoirs, and family history", "glosses": {"court memoir": "궁정 회고록", "homogeneous": "동질적인", "comprehensive": "포괄적인"}, "src": "verbal23 Q4"}, {"id": "v23_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following describes a difference between the author and Grundy regarding British women writers' engagement with historical discourse?", "choices": ["The author thinks the engagement was determined primarily in response to developing literary markets; Grundy thinks it had little to do with such markets.", "The author believes the engagement is reflected in numerous genres; Grundy thinks that one genre is specifically feminine.", "The author emphasizes the heterogeneity of factors that influenced the engagement; Grundy suggests that the engagement was unified by one particular factor.", "The author thinks the engagement was limited to women in certain social classes; Grundy thinks it was common to all classes.", "The author believes the engagement was just beginning in the late 1700s; Grundy thinks it reached its peak then."], "columns": null, "pid": "v23_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Grundy: 이 글들은 '전(前)19세기 여성적인(feminine)' 역사와의 관계를 구현한다 → 하나의 공통된 여성적 관계.\n저자: \"I do not believe there was a characteristic women's relationship to history\";\n관여 방식은 정치적 신념, 계층, 장르·시장 인식 등 여러 요인에 따라 달랐다.\n→ 저자는 요인의 이질성, Grundy는 하나의 통일 요인(여성성) = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 시장은 저자가 든 여러 요인 중 하나일 뿐, '주로' 시장에 의해 결정됐다고 하지 않았다. D: 계층은 요인이지 '특정 계층에 한정'이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"discourse": "담론", "heterogeneity": "이질성", "affiliation": "소속, 연계", "engagement": "관여"}, "src": "verbal23 Q5"}, {"id": "v215_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "This is a _____ book: it takes up and defends a position to which the current intellectual climate is generally hostile.", "choices": ["restrained", "plucky", "noteworthy", "temperate", "courageous", "subversive"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 설명: 현재 지적 분위기가 대체로 적대적인 입장을 받아들여 옹호한다.\n→ 그런 책은 '용감한' 책. 빈칸 = 긍정, 용기.\nplucky(대담한)와 courageous(용감한)가 짝.\n정답: B, E (plucky, courageous)", "trap": "F(subversive): 주류에 맞선다는 점에서 끌리지만 '전복적'이라는 뜻이고 짝이 없다. restrained/temperate는 짝이지만 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"plucky": "용감한, 대담한", "restrained": "절제된", "noteworthy": "주목할 만한", "temperate": "온건한, 절제된", "courageous": "용감한", "subversive": "전복적인"}, "src": "verbal215 Q7 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v11_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Jamie offered to loan her classmate a pencil on the condition that in three days he repay her with two boxes of brand-new pencils: who would have believed that such _____ would exist among the young?", "choices": ["largesse", "rapacity", "hedonism", "munificence", "exaction", "altruism"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "연필 하나 빌려주고 사흘 뒤 새 연필 두 상자로 갚으라는 조건 → 지나치게 많이 뜯어냄.\n'who would have believed' → 어린아이에게 이런 탐욕이 있다니 하는 놀라움. 빈칸 = 부정, 탐욕·착취.\nrapacity(탐욕)와 exaction(가혹한 요구, 착취)이 짝.\n정답: B, E (rapacity, exaction)", "trap": "largesse/munificence(후함)는 서로 짝이지만 상황과 정반대다. altruism도 같은 함정.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rapacity": "탐욕, 강탈", "largesse": "후한 베풂", "hedonism": "쾌락주의", "munificence": "아낌없이 줌, 후함", "exaction": "가혹한 요구, 착취", "altruism": "이타주의"}, "src": "verbal11 Q8"}, {"id": "v235_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Wilson is wont to emphasize the _____ of ants: how ants with full stomachs will regurgitate liquid food for those without, or how the old will fight so the young can survive.", "choices": ["beneficence", "altruism", "unpredictability", "intelligence", "fecundity", "fertility"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 예시: 배부른 개미가 굶은 개미에게 먹이를 토해 주고, 늙은 개미가 어린 개미를 위해 싸운다.\n→ 남을 위한 행동. 빈칸 = 이타성, 선행.\nbeneficence(선행, 자선)와 altruism(이타주의)이 짝.\n정답: A, B (beneficence, altruism)", "trap": "fecundity/fertility는 동의어 짝이지만 예시가 번식력이 아니라 남을 돕는 행동이다. intelligence도 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"emphasize": "강조하다", "beneficence": "선행, 자선", "altruism": "이타주의", "unpredictability": "예측 불가능성", "intelligence": "지능", "fecundity": "다산, 번식력", "fertility": "생식력, 비옥함"}, "src": "verbal235 Q6 · 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v35_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Upon realizing that the indicators of a stressful situation can be extremely _____, the psychologist reconsidered her claim that a reliable way of reducing stress is to recognize stressful situations and then avoid them.", "choices": ["acute", "exiguous", "persistent", "overstated", "tenuous", "unrelenting"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "심리학자의 주장: 스트레스 상황을 '알아차리고' 피하면 된다.\n그런데 그 지표가 극도로 ___하다는 걸 깨닫고 주장을 재고했다 → 지표가 알아차리기 어려울 만큼 미약하다는 뜻.\n빈칸 = 미미한, 희박한. exiguous(아주 적은, 빈약한)와 tenuous(희박한, 미약한)가 짝.\n정답: B, E (exiguous, tenuous)", "trap": "persistent/unrelenting은 짝이지만 지표가 '지속적'이면 오히려 알아차리기 쉬워 주장을 재고할 이유가 없다. acute(강렬한)도 같은 이유로 틀림.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"acute": "극심한, 예리한", "exiguous": "아주 적은, 빈약한", "persistent": "지속적인", "overstated": "과장된", "tenuous": "희박한, 미약한", "unrelenting": "수그러들지 않는"}, "src": "verbal35 Q8"}, {"id": "v227_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with", "choices": ["tracing the history of an art form in a particular culture", "identifying similarities between two different cultures' use of an art form", "examining an individual's views about a particular art form", "correcting a misconception about a particular culture's use of an art form", "refuting a theory about the development of a particular art form"], "columns": null, "pid": "v227_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문 전체가 루쉰(Lu Xun)이 서양 목판화를 어떻게 보았는지를 다룬다:\n선·흑백 대비의 진지함, 사회와의 연결, 기법보다 사회 정의 역할을 더 높이 평가, 교육 도구로서의 가능성.\n→ 한 개인의 특정 예술 형식에 대한 견해 검토 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 중국 목판화의 역사를 '추적'하지 않는다. 1920년대 루쉰 한 사람의 관점에 집중한다. B: 유사점이 아니라 차이점을 다룬다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"woodcut": "목판화", "linearity": "선적 특성", "consciousness": "의식"}, "src": "verbal227 Q10 · 25/8, 24/5, 23/10, 23/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v227_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the purpose of the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["To point out one of Lu Xun's concerns that was eventually outweighed by other considerations", "To rank the importance of the factors that influenced Lu Xun in making a decision", "To emphasize the complexity of the modern Western woodcut's effect on society", "To explain an apparently contradictory aspect of Western woodcuts", "To describe the ways in which Lu Xun succeeded in making modern Chinese woodcuts more like Western woodcuts"], "columns": null, "pid": "v227_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "highlight 문장: 'It is true that ... 기법에 깊은 인상을 받았다, but ... 결정은 기법보다(more ... than) 사회 정의 투쟁에서의 역할에 대한 감탄에서 나왔다.'\n두 요인을 모두 인정하면서 어느 쪽이 더 중요했는지 순위를 매긴다 = B.\n정답: B", "trap": "A: 기법은 '걱정(concern)'이 아니었고, 나중에 다른 고려에 밀려났다는 시간 순서도 없다. 동시에 비교했을 뿐이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"craftsmanship": "장인 솜씨", "prompted": "촉발된", "outweigh": "~보다 중요하다"}, "src": "verbal227 Q11 · 25/8, 24/5, 23/10, 23/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v227_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that Lu Xun believed which of the following about traditional Chinese woodcuts?", "choices": ["They were more similar in technique than in content to Western woodcuts.", "They were less successful than were other Chinese art forms in reshaping public consciousness.", "They were taken less seriously as an art form in Chinese society than they had once been.", "They were not aimed at furthering social and political justice.", "They had been used primarily to evoke human emotions."], "columns": null, "pid": "v227_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 서양 목판화의 가장 중요한 요소는 \"its close link to the broader society, an element missing in the Chinese woodcut tradition\".\n또 서양 작품은 사회·정치 정의를 위한 투쟁에서 역할을 했고, 중국 전통 목판화는 'largely decorative'였다.\n→ 중국 전통 목판화는 사회·정치 정의 증진을 목표로 하지 않았다 = D.\n정답: D", "trap": "E: 감정 환기는 서양 작가들의 기법에 대한 설명이다. 중국 목판화는 주로 '장식적'이었다고 했다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"decorative": "장식적인", "linearity": "선적 특성", "justice": "정의"}, "src": "verbal227 Q12 · 25/8, 24/5, 23/10, 23/9 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v4_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Since the fundamental frequency of an object's vibration is determined by its size and shape, a sequence of sounds having _____ pitch is perceived to have been produced by a single object.", "choices": ["discernible", "predictable", "unusual", "identical", "melodious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "인과 구조(Since): 기본 진동수는 물체의 크기와 형태로 결정된다 → 한 물체는 일정한 음높이를 낸다.\n따라서 음높이가 '같은' 소리들은 하나의 물체에서 나온 것으로 인식된다.\n빈칸 = 동일한.\n정답: D (identical)", "trap": "B(predictable): 예측 가능한 음높이는 변해도 될 수 있어 '하나의 물체'라는 추론의 근거가 되지 못한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"discernible": "식별할 수 있는", "predictable": "예측 가능한", "unusual": "특이한", "identical": "동일한", "melodious": "선율이 아름다운"}, "src": "verbal4 Q1"}, {"id": "v212_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Far from (i) _____ the actions taken by the newspaper's executives, Willes praised the executives' resistance to corruption—yet he doubted that their policies were practical enough to warrant (ii) _____ by other papers.", "choices": null, "columns": [["lionizing", "impugning", "surveying"], ["criticism", "admiration", "emulation"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'Far from ___, Willes praised' → praise의 반대 → impugning(비난하다, 의문을 제기하다).\n(ii) yet → 칭찬은 했지만 정책이 다른 신문이 '따라 할' 만큼 실용적이진 않다고 의심 → emulation(모방).\n'practical enough to warrant ___' → 실용적이어야 따라 하는 것.\n정답: B, F (impugning / emulation)", "trap": "(ii) admiration: Willes 자신이 이미 칭찬했으므로 '실용성이 있어야 받을 만한 것'은 칭찬이 아니라 모방이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lionizing": "치켜세우는", "impugning": "비난하는, 이의를 제기하는", "surveying": "조사하는, 살펴보는", "criticism": "비판", "admiration": "감탄, 칭찬", "emulation": "모방, 본받기"}, "src": "verbal212 Q2 · 25/7, 24/9, 22/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v12_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "It is not just Gelbspan's passionate advocacy that makes this, his second book, so compelling: it is also his (i) _____ analysis, made that much more (ii) _____ by his nine years of research on the subject.", "choices": null, "columns": [["voluble", "questionable", "penetrating"], ["spurious", "authoritative", "exciting"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'It is not just A that makes it compelling: it is also B' → B도 긍정적이어야 함.\n(i) 긍정적인 분석 → penetrating(통찰력 있는, 예리한).\n(ii) 9년간의 연구로 '더욱 ___해짐' → 신뢰할 만한, 권위 있는 → authoritative.\n정답: C, E (penetrating / authoritative)", "trap": "(ii) exciting: 긍정이지만 '오랜 연구'가 직접 높이는 것은 신뢰성/권위이지 흥미가 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"voluble": "말이 많은, 장황한", "questionable": "의심스러운", "penetrating": "통찰력 있는, 예리한", "spurious": "거짓된, 그럴듯한 가짜의", "authoritative": "권위 있는, 신뢰할 만한", "exciting": "흥미진진한"}, "src": "verbal12 Q2"}, {"id": "v220_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Extant manuscripts of sixteenth- and seventeenth-century plays were produced through the combined efforts of an author, one or more scribes, and various compositors. The blending of labors is so complete that some scholars (i) _____ that the author's contribution (ii) _____, a position that (iii) _____ the consideration of questions about authorial intention.", "choices": null, "columns": [["deny", "forget", "contend"], ["must be evaluated", "cannot be isolated", "should have priority"], ["requires", "precludes", "anticipates"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CEH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: 원고는 작가·필경사·식자공의 합작 → 노동이 '완전히 섞여 있어서(so complete that)'.\n(i)(ii) 결과: 일부 학자는 작가의 기여를 '분리해낼 수 없다'고 주장 → contend / cannot be isolated.\n(iii) 작가 기여를 분리할 수 없다면 작가 의도에 관한 질문은 따질 수 없다 → precludes(불가능하게 하다).\n정답: C, E, H (contend / cannot be isolated / precludes)", "trap": "(i) deny + (ii) should have priority 조합도 문법적으로 되지만, 'blending is so complete'의 결과로 나오는 건 '분리 불가'다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"deny": "부인하다", "forget": "잊다", "contend": "주장하다", "must be evaluated": "평가되어야 한다", "cannot be isolated": "분리될 수 없다", "should have priority": "우선해야 한다", "requires": "필요로 하다", "precludes": "불가능하게 하다, 배제하다", "anticipates": "예상하다, 앞서 고려하다"}, "src": "verbal220 Q4 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v4_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, certain African literatures have", "choices": ["undergone significant changes since the 1970s", "flourished as a result of governmental support", "been directed primarily at non-African audiences", "avoided openly discussing sensitive cultural issues", "achieved a degree of internal cohesiveness"], "columns": null, "pid": "v4_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"there has undoubtedly emerged a sense of corporate identity, often marked by clear thematic and formal progressions\"\n그리고 마지막 \"however abundant the corpus or coherent the internal configurations\".\n→ 일부 국민 문학은 내적 일관성을 어느 정도 이뤘다 = E.\n정답: E", "trap": "A: 1970년대 이후 변화한 것은 '아프리카 문학 연구의 흐름'이지 문학 자체가 크게 변했다는 진술이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incontrovertible": "논쟁의 여지가 없는", "indigenous": "토착의", "corpus": "(작품) 전체, 집적", "cohesiveness": "응집성"}, "src": "verbal4 Q14"}, {"id": "v4_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The highlighted portion (\"they ~ the word\") of the passage serves primarily to", "choices": ["support a conclusion stated later in the passage", "qualify an assertion presented earlier in the passage", "suggest an explanation for an anomaly mentioned in the passage", "offer a tentative answer to a question raised in the passage", "justify the use of a term introduced earlier in the passage"], "columns": null, "pid": "v4_p4", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "highlight 부분은 '유럽 언어는 공식적으로만 받아들여졌다'를 구체화: 토착어도 아니고 진정한 의미의 국어도 아니다.\n바로 다음 문장 \"This must limit the claims of any of these literatures to national significance\"의 근거가 된다.\n→ 뒤에 나오는 결론을 뒷받침 = A.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 앞의 주장(국민 문학 인정 흐름)을 제한하는 역할은 'But ...' 문장 전체가 하고, highlight 부분 자체는 뒤 결론의 근거로 기능한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"indigenous": "토착의", "impose": "강요하다, 부과하다", "qualify": "(진술을) 제한하다, 단서를 달다"}, "src": "verbal4 Q15"}, {"id": "v230_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["point out impediments to assessing the relative cost of books in eighteenth-century England", "explain why eighteenth-century England saw significant growth in the availability of used books", "identify means for evaluating the effects of used books on the book market in eighteenth-century England", "argue that the availability of used books lowered prices in the book market overall in eighteenth-century England", "show how the decreasing price of books in eighteenth-century England led to the diversification of the book market"], "columns": null, "pid": "v230_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: 정확한 통계는 불가능하지만 영향은 분명 있었다 → \"Fortunately, we can also call on extensive, independent price lists...\"\n→ 신간 정가 추이로 '중고 시장이 가격을 끌어내렸다'는 가설 검증, 신간·중고 가격 차를 물리적 품질의 대리 지표(proxy)로 활용.\n즉 중고책이 책 시장에 미친 영향을 평가할 수단을 제시 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 데이터 부족(장애물)은 첫 문장에만 해당. D: 가격을 낮췄다고 '주장'하지 않고 검증 방법을 제시할 뿐이라 너무 강하다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inferentially": "추론적으로", "proxy": "대리 지표", "differentiated": "세분화된", "drag": "억제 요인, 짐"}, "src": "verbal230 Q7 · 25/9, 25/6, 24/12, 24/9, 24/1, 23/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author cites “the standard behavior of markets\" primarily to", "choices": ["support a claim about differentiated classes of readers", "support a claim about the used book market", "account for certain marketing strategies on the part of booksellers", "account for an absence of a particular kind of data", "account for an increase in the cost of reading"], "columns": null, "pid": "v230_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "문장: \"Yet, it can hardly be doubted that such an impact occurred, not only through the standard behavior of markets but inferentially through...\"\n'such an impact' = 중고책 시장이 독서 비용에 미친 영향.\n'시장의 표준적 작동'은 그 영향이 있었다는 주장의 근거로 제시됨 → 중고책 시장에 관한 주장을 뒷받침 = B.\n정답: B", "trap": "D: 데이터 부재는 첫 문장의 내용이고, 시장 작동 원리로 그 부재를 설명하지 않는다. A: 세분화된 독자층은 packaging 전략과 연결된 내용이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "the standard behavior of markets", "glosses": {"standard": "표준적인", "impact": "영향", "inferentially": "추론적으로"}, "src": "verbal230 Q8 · 25/9, 25/6, 24/12, 24/9, 24/1, 23/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage mentions “innovative design and packaging strategies\" primarily to", "choices": ["note a way in which eighteenth-century English booksellers worked together to standardize book prices", "highlight evidence that suggests a response on the part of eighteenth-century English booksellers to shifting prices in the book market", "provide an example of how the presence of used books in the eighteenth-century English book market affected the average price of new book", "indicate one means by which eighteenth-century English booksellers tried to counteract a drop in the total number of books being sold", "discuss one strategy by which eighteenth-century English booksellers attempted to take advantage of an expansion in the number of readers"], "columns": null, "pid": "v230_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'innovative design and packaging strategies'는 중고책 시장의 영향이 있었다는 '추론적(inferentially)' 증거로 제시된다.\n1760년부터 런던 서적상들이 더 세분화된 독자층을 겨냥한 디자인·포장 전략에 의존 → 중고책 때문에 변한 가격 환경에 대한 서적상의 대응을 시사.\n→ 서적상들이 변화하는 가격에 반응했음을 보여주는 증거 = B.\n정답: B", "trap": "E: '독자 수 증가'를 이용했다는 내용은 없다. 독자층을 '세분화'한 것이지 확대된 것이 아니다. C: 신간 평균 가격에 미친 영향의 사례가 아니라 간접 증거다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "innovative design and packaging strategies", "glosses": {"packaging": "포장, 장정", "differentiated": "세분화된", "resort to": "~에 의존하다", "counteract": "대응하다, 상쇄하다"}, "src": "verbal230 Q9 · 25/9, 25/6, 24/12, 24/9, 24/1, 23/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v22_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "For all the __________ the new CEO has received from the press recently, her staff have a decidedly less rosy view of her.", "choices": ["encomiums", "tributes", "evaluations", "critiques", "attention", "publicity"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: 'For all the ___' = '~에도 불구하고'(양보) → 직원들은 '훨씬 덜 장밋빛인(less rosy)' 시각.\n→ 언론에게서 받은 것은 긍정적 평가. 빈칸 = 찬사.\nencomiums(찬사)와 tributes(헌사, 찬사)가 짝.\n정답: A, B (encomiums, tributes)", "trap": "attention/publicity는 짝이지만 중립적이라 'less rosy'와의 대조가 성립하지 않는다. critiques는 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"encomiums": "찬사", "tributes": "찬사, 헌사", "evaluations": "평가", "critiques": "비평, 비판", "attention": "관심", "publicity": "언론 노출, 홍보"}, "src": "verbal22 Q12"}, {"id": "v30_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "While the group's street protests assumed an assertory uncompromising tenor, once admitted to the halls of power to begin formal lobbying, the group's leadership wisely chose to _____ the stridency of their rhetoric.", "choices": ["metamorphose", "gild", "wane", "palliate", "succor", "damp"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "While → 대조: 거리 시위는 단호하고 타협하지 않는 어조였지만, 공식 로비를 시작하자 지도부는 '현명하게' 수사의 날카로움(stridency)을 ___.\n빈칸 = 누그러뜨리다, 완화하다.\npalliate(완화하다)와 damp(약하게 하다, 누그러뜨리다)가 짝.\n정답: D, F (palliate, damp)", "trap": "C(wane): 뜻은 '약해지다'로 맞아 보이지만 자동사라 목적어(the stridency)를 취할 수 없다. metamorphose는 방향 없는 '변형'.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"metamorphose": "변형시키다", "gild": "도금하다, 겉치레하다", "wane": "(스스로) 약해지다", "palliate": "완화하다", "succor": "구조하다, 돕다", "damp": "약하게 하다, 누그러뜨리다"}, "src": "verbal30 Q10"}, {"id": "v210_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The figure of the female orator, though indubitably _____, was far from unknown in fifteenth-century Italy.", "choices": ["controversial", "distrusted", "constrained", "self-effacing", "exotic", "anomalous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "EF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "though → 양보/대조: 확실히 ___했지만, 15세기 이탈리아에서 '결코 알려지지 않은 것은 아니었다(far from unknown)'.\n→ 빈칸 = '알려지지 않은'에 가까운 뜻, 즉 드문, 흔치 않은.\nexotic(이국적인, 낯선)과 anomalous(변칙적인, 이례적인)가 짝.\n정답: E, F (exotic, anomalous)", "trap": "controversial/distrusted는 그럴듯하지만 'unknown'과의 대조 축(희귀함 vs 존재함)에 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"controversial": "논란이 많은", "distrusted": "불신받는", "constrained": "제약을 받는", "self-effacing": "자기를 내세우지 않는", "exotic": "이국적인, 낯선", "anomalous": "변칙적인, 이례적인"}, "src": "verbal210 Q10 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "The argument depends on the assumption that", "choices": ["climate change is responsible for the decrease in water in many of the world's major rivers", "river water is the single largest source of water for crop irrigation worldwide", "none of the water from the rivers is reused after being initially used for irrigation of crops", "using the water of the rivers for personal hygiene is less important than using it to increase food supplies", "failure of the water to reach the sea does not decrease the production of fisheries at the outlets of the rivers enough to outweigh the increased crop yields"], "columns": null, "pid": "v232_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: (식량 수요에 대응한다는 점에서) 강의 고갈은 이롭다(beneficial).\n근거: 물을 관개에 돌려 식량 생산을 늘린다.\n'이롭다'고 하려면 물이 바다에 닿지 않아 생기는 손실(예: 하구 어업 감소)이 관개로 얻는 식량 증가를 상쇄하지 않아야 한다.\n부정 테스트: 어업 손실이 수확 증가보다 크다면 → 식량 측면에서도 이롭지 않음 → 논증 붕괴.\n정답: E", "trap": "B: 강물이 관개용수의 '최대' 공급원일 필요는 없다. C: 재사용 여부는 결론과 무관하다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"divert": "(물길을) 돌리다", "irrigation": "관개", "outweigh": "~보다 크다, 상쇄하다", "fisheries": "어업, 어장"}, "src": "verbal232 Q13 · 24/1, 23/10, 23/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v2_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with", "choices": ["outlining certain difficulties associated with the study of a particular species", "suggesting that the development of a phenomenon was not predicated upon a particular condition", "pointing out that a particular event is rarely known to occur", "detailing evidence that refutes a commonly held notion", "evaluating rival interpretations of a phenomenon"], "columns": null, "pid": "v2_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 통념 — 뉴질랜드에 토착 육상 포식자가 없었기 때문에 지상 생활(terrestriality)이 진화할 수 있었다.\nHowever → 지상 먹이활동이 포식자에 취약하게 만든다는 실제 위험에 대한 자료는 제한적이고,\n\"Indeed, Lloyd argues that... generally they would not be easy prey\"(재빠르고 청각·후각이 예민해 쉽게 잡히지 않음).\n→ 포식자가 있어도 지상 생활이 크게 위험하지 않다면, 그 진화가 '포식자 부재'라는 조건에 달려 있지 않았을 수 있다 = B.\n정답: B", "trap": "E(키 정답): '경쟁하는 해석들을 평가'한다고 보기 어렵다. 가설은 하나이고, 저자는 그것에 의문을 제기할 뿐 두 해석을 비교·평가하지 않는다. D는 'refute'가 너무 강함(자료가 제한적이라고 함).", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"terrestriality": "지상 생활성", "cryptic": "(보호색 등으로) 눈에 잘 띄지 않는", "predicated upon": "~에 근거한, ~을 전제로 한", "extant": "현존하는"}, "src": "verbal2 Q12", "note": "⚠ 원본 답안표 정답은 E이지만, 검토 풀이로는 B이(가) 더 타당해 보입니다. 채점은 원본 기준이며 아래 해설은 검토 풀이 기준입니다. 근거: Key says E, but the passage presents only one hypothesis (absence of predators facilitated terrestriality) and then undercuts it (risk data limited; Lloyd: not easy prey). It does not set out or evaluate rival interpretations. B (development of terrestriality not predicated on absence of predators) matches the 'However ... Indeed' structure. Fairly confident, so final_answer set to B; please double-check against the source key."}, {"id": "v2_q13", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred from the passage about Mystacina tuberculata?", "choices": ["It derives benefits from ground foraging that outweigh the risks of predation.", "Its flying ability is in some respects diminished in comparison with most other bat species.", "Its isolation in New Zealand has led to a misunderstanding regarding its abilities.", "It has developed keener hearing than most other bat species.", "It is not subject to predation by other bat species."], "columns": null, "pid": "v2_p3", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문 근거: 현존 개체는 지금도 지상에서 먹이를 찾는다(terrestrial foraging by extant M. tuberculata).\n외래 포식자에 취약할 '가능성'은 있지만 실제 위험 자료는 제한적이고, Lloyd는 \"generally they would not be easy prey\"라고 한다.\n→ 위험은 생각만큼 크지 않고 이 종은 여전히 지상 먹이활동을 유지 = 그로부터 얻는 이익이 포식 위험보다 크다는 추론(A)이 가장 무난.\n나머지는 지문에 근거가 전혀 없다(비행 능력 저하, 다른 박쥐와의 청각 비교, 다른 박쥐의 포식).\n정답: A", "trap": "D: 'acute hearing'은 언급되지만 '대부분의 다른 박쥐보다' 예민하다는 비교는 없다. B는 '빨리 날아오를 수 있다'와 반대.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"forage": "먹이를 찾다", "cryptic": "눈에 잘 띄지 않는", "olfaction": "후각", "predation": "포식"}, "src": "verbal2 Q13"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.7 / S2 3.0"}, {"set": 11, "sections": [[{"id": "v33_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The science community’s perennial lament over inadequate budgets has come to seem increasingly _____, because government support for science and engineering has never been greater.", "choices": ["vital", "hopeless", "poignant", "condescending", "disingenuous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: because + 'support has never been greater' → 예산이 부족하다는 불평이 사실과 맞지 않음.\n'perennial lament'(늘 하는 한탄)가 점점 어떻게 보이는가? → 빈칸 = 부정, '진실하지 않은/위선적인'.\n지원이 사상 최대인데도 예산 부족을 호소하면 속 보이는(솔직하지 못한) 불평이 된다.\ndisingenuous(솔직하지 못한, 위선적인)이 정확히 맞는다.\n정답: E (disingenuous)", "trap": "poignant(가슴 아픈)는 lament와 어울려 보이지만, 지원이 많다는 근거와 연결되지 않는다. hopeless도 '불평이 근거 없다'는 의미를 담지 못한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"vital": "필수적인, 생명의", "hopeless": "절망적인, 가망 없는", "poignant": "가슴 아픈, 통렬한", "condescending": "거들먹거리는, 깔보는", "disingenuous": "솔직하지 못한, 위선적인"}, "src": "verbal33 Q1"}, {"id": "v237_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The (i) _____ scientists─the notion that they are elitists scornful of the masses─is in no sense (ii) _____ the eighteenth century, since in our own time one does not have to look far to find such disdainful attitudes.", "choices": null, "columns": [["faith in", "contempt for", "apathy toward"], ["a monopoly of", "a mystery for", "an aspiration of"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 대시 뒤 동격 설명: 'the notion that they are elitists scornful of the masses' → 과학자에 대한 '경멸', contempt for.\n(ii) since 이하: 오늘날에도 그런 경멸적 태도를 쉽게 찾을 수 있다 → 18세기만의 '전유물'이 아니다 → a monopoly of.\n'in no sense a monopoly of the eighteenth century' = 18세기에만 있던 것이 결코 아니다.\n정답: B, D (contempt for / a monopoly of)", "trap": "(ii)의 a mystery for는 '18세기에게 수수께끼'라는 뜻이 되어 since 이하(지금도 흔하다)와 논리적으로 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"faith in": "~에 대한 믿음", "contempt for": "~에 대한 경멸", "apathy toward": "~에 대한 무관심", "a monopoly of": "~의 독점물, 전유물", "a mystery for": "~에게 수수께끼", "an aspiration of": "~의 열망"}, "src": "verbal237 Q2 · 26/1, 25/12, 24/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v203_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Like many composers of electronic music, this composer is a pianist by training, and one might be tempted to hypothesize that this (i) _____ is due to the fact that early electronic instruments, such as the synthesizer, were keyboard controlled. (ii) _____, the fact that, historically, most composers in any genre began as pianists (iii) _____ that hypothesis.", "choices": null, "columns": [["oddity", "correlation", "presumption"], ["Furthermore", "However", "Specifically"], ["clarifies", "challenges", "extends"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BEH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) '많은 전자음악 작곡가가 피아니스트 출신' + '건반식 초기 악기 때문'이라는 가설 → 두 사실 사이의 '상관관계'를 설명하려는 것 → correlation.\n(ii) 앞은 '그런 가설을 세우고 싶어진다(tempted)', 뒤는 반박 사실 → 역접 However.\n(iii) 어떤 장르든 역사적으로 대부분의 작곡가가 피아니스트 출신이었다 → 전자음악만의 특수 현상이 아님 → 가설을 '반박' challenges.\n'tempted to hypothesize'가 곧 뒤집힐 것을 예고하는 신호.\n정답: B, E, H (correlation / However / challenges)", "trap": "(i) oddity는 그럴듯하지만, 결국 모든 장르에서 흔한 일로 드러나므로 '특이한 현상'이 아니며, 문장은 두 사실의 연결(상관)을 설명하는 구조다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"oddity": "기이한 점, 특이함", "correlation": "상관관계", "presumption": "추정, 주제넘음", "Furthermore": "게다가", "However": "그러나", "Specifically": "구체적으로", "clarifies": "명확히 하다", "challenges": "이의를 제기하다, 반박하다", "extends": "확장하다"}, "src": "verbal203 Q3 · 25년 8월, 23년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v239_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, the equilibrium view of rangelands is defined in terms of the relationship between", "choices": ["distribution of rainfall and patterns of grazing", "predictability of rainfall and fluctuations in food distribution", "mobility of livestock and extent of land degradation", "livestock numbers and availability of food", "number of livestock species and variability of grazing resources"], "columns": null, "pid": "v239_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the equilibrium view of rangelands—that grazing-induced land degradation will occur if livestock numbers exceed the availability of food'.\n대시 뒤 정의가 '가축 수'와 '먹이 가용량'의 관계로 되어 있다.\nD는 이 정의를 그대로 옮긴 것.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(강우 예측성과 먹이 분포 변동)는 전통 목축 시스템/비평형 모델 쪽 내용으로, 평형론의 정의가 아니다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rangeland": "방목지", "equilibrium": "평형", "degradation": "황폐화, 저하", "arid": "건조한"}, "src": "verbal239 Q4 · 25/10, 25/8, 25/5, 25/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v239_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that proponents of \"nonequilibrium models\" would agree with which of the following statements about grazing-induced land degradation in arid zones?", "choices": ["Traditional pastoral systems of land use have caused land degradation.", "Land degradation will occur if livestock numbers exceed the availability of food.", "The employment of opportunistic methods of land use can help avoid land degradation."], "columns": null, "pid": "v239_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "비평형 모델: 'plant dynamics in arid zones are influenced more by rainfall than by grazing', 그리고 전통 목축 방식(opportunism, mobility)과 '유사한 접근'을 권장한다.\nC: 기회주의적(opportunistic) 토지 이용이 황폐화를 피하게 해 준다 → 비평형 모델이 권장하는 방식과 일치.\nA: 전통 목축이 황폐화를 일으켰다 → 오히려 더 적절하다고 했으므로 반대.\nB: 가축 수 > 먹이 → 황폐화 → 이것은 평형론의 주장.\n정답: C", "trap": "B는 지문에 그대로 나오는 문장이라 끌리지만, 비평형 모델이 아니라 비판받는 평형론(equilibrium view)의 정의다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "nonequilibrium models", "glosses": {"opportunism": "기회주의, 상황에 따른 유연한 대응", "pastoral": "목축의", "nonequilibrium": "비평형"}, "src": "verbal239 Q5 · 25/10, 25/8, 25/5, 25/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v199_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Personal computers have become so _____ that the use of digital evidence collected from them is now a common part of many criminal and civil investigations.", "choices": ["ubiquitous", "sophisticated", "affordable", "convenient", "elaborate", "omnipresent"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: so ~ that (결과) → 디지털 증거가 많은 수사에서 흔해졌다.\n빈칸 = '어디에나 있는, 매우 흔한'.\nubiquitous와 omnipresent가 같은 뜻(편재하는)으로 짝을 이룬다.\n정답: A, F (ubiquitous, omnipresent)", "trap": "affordable/sophisticated도 컴퓨터를 묘사할 수 있지만 '흔해졌다'는 결과를 직접 낳지 못하고 동의어 짝도 없다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ubiquitous": "어디에나 있는", "sophisticated": "정교한, 세련된", "affordable": "(가격이) 적당한", "convenient": "편리한", "elaborate": "정교한, 공들인", "omnipresent": "어디에나 있는, 편재하는"}, "src": "verbal199 Q6 · 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v19_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the wild, no other mammal __________ individuals from another species; badgers do not tend hares, deer do not nurture baby squirrels, and lions do not care for giraffes.", "choices": ["protects", "fosters", "aids", "cajoles", "adopts", "coaxes"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론 뒤 예시: 'do not tend hares', 'do not nurture baby squirrels', 'do not care for giraffes' → 다른 종의 새끼를 '돌보고 기르는' 행위.\n빈칸 = 다른 종을 데려다 기르다.\nfosters(양육하다)와 adopts(입양하다)가 같은 의미.\n정답: B, E (fosters, adopts)", "trap": "protects/aids도 '돕다'는 뜻으로 어울려 보이나, 예시의 핵심은 '키우는 것(nurture)'이며 두 단어는 서로 짝도 정확하지 않다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"adopts": "입양하다", "coaxes": "달래다, 구슬리다", "protects": "보호하다", "fosters": "(남의 아이를) 기르다, 육성하다", "aids": "돕다", "cajoles": "감언이설로 꾀다"}, "src": "verbal19 Q7"}, {"id": "v225_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The performer can be _____ in his comedy, but he is fundamentally a bighearted person who displays a core sweetness even at his most manic.", "choices": ["inflammatory", "pedestrian", "gloomy", "uninspired", "puerile", "provocative"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: can be ___ in his comedy, but fundamentally bighearted ... core sweetness → 역접.\n빈칸 = '착함/다정함'과 대조되는, 공격적이고 도발적인 면.\ninflammatory(선동적인)와 provocative(도발적인)가 짝.\n정답: A, F (inflammatory, provocative)", "trap": "puerile(유치한)·pedestrian(평범한)은 코미디 묘사로 가능하지만 'sweetness'와 대조되는 공격성이 아니고 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"bighearted": "마음이 넓은", "inflammatory": "선동적인, 분노를 일으키는", "uninspired": "영감 없는, 평범한", "provocative": "도발적인, 자극적인", "pedestrian": "평범한, 진부한", "gloomy": "우울한", "puerile": "유치한"}, "src": "verbal225 Q7 · 24년 4월, 23년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v11_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Recent advances in the study of desert varnish have been a boon to geologists, allowing them to date surface features and establish regional climate histories in _____ detail.", "choices": ["novel", "realistic", "unprecedented", "superfluous", "extraneous", "surprising"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: 'a boon to geologists'(큰 도움) + 'Recent advances' → 긍정, 전에 없던 수준의 정밀함.\n빈칸 = '이전에 없던, 새로운' 수준의 detail.\nnovel(새로운)과 unprecedented(전례 없는)가 짝.\n정답: A, C (novel, unprecedented)", "trap": "surprising도 긍정적으로 보이나 '전에 없던 새로움'이라는 의미 짝이 아니다. superfluous/extraneous는 서로 비슷하지만 'boon'과 모순(불필요한 detail).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"extraneous": "관련 없는, 외부의", "superfluous": "불필요한, 과잉의", "novel": "새로운, 참신한", "realistic": "현실적인", "unprecedented": "전례 없는", "surprising": "놀라운"}, "src": "verbal11 Q7"}, {"id": "v201_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage is primarily concerned with", "choices": ["confirming a theory", "supporting a statement", "presenting new information", "predicting future discoveries", "reconciling discrepant findings"], "columns": null, "pid": "v201_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문단: 1980년대 말 구름이 온난화를 도울지 해칠지 예측할 수 없었다는 진술.\n2문단: 'That clouds represented the weakest element in climate models was illustrated by a study' → 14개 모델 연구를 근거로 앞의 진술을 뒷받침.\n즉, 진술 하나를 제시하고 예시/연구로 지지하는 구조 → supporting a statement.\n정답: B", "trap": "C(새로운 정보 제시)는 너무 막연하고, E(상충되는 결과 조정)는 모델 간 불일치를 '언급'만 할 뿐 조정하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"discrepancy": "불일치", "stratocumulus": "층적운", "cirrus": "권운", "plague": "괴롭히다"}, "src": "verbal201 Q10 · 25/5, 25/4, 25/3, 24/9, 23/10, 23/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v201_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that one reason the fourteen models described in the passage failed to agree was that", "choices": ["they failed to incorporate the most up-to-date information about the effect of clouds on climate", "they were based on faulty information about factors other than clouds that affect climate", "they were based on different assumptions about the overall effects of clouds on climate", "their originators disagreed about the kinds of forecasts the models should provide", "their originators disagreed about the factors other than clouds that should be included in the models"], "columns": null, "pid": "v201_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 구름을 빼면 모델들이 'agreed quite well', 구름을 넣으면 'a wide range of forecasts'.\n또 1문단: 구름이 온난화를 도울지(층적운) 해칠지(권운) 알 수 없었다.\n→ 모델마다 구름의 전체적 효과에 대해 다른 가정을 했기 때문에 결과가 갈렸다고 추론 가능.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(최신 정보 미반영)는 지문 근거가 없다. B·E(구름 외 요인)는 구름을 빼면 잘 일치했다는 내용과 정반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incorporate": "포함하다", "forecast": "예측", "originator": "창안자"}, "src": "verbal201 Q11 · 25/5, 25/4, 25/3, 24/9, 23/10, 23/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v201_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the primary purpose of the models included in the study discussed in the second paragraph of the passage was to", "choices": ["predict future changes in the world's climate", "predict the effects of cloud systems on the world's climate", "find a way to prevent a disastrous planetwide temperature increase", "assess the percentage of the Earth's surface covered by cloud systems", "estimate by how much the amount of carbon dioxide in the Earth's atmosphere will increase"], "columns": null, "pid": "v201_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Comparing climate forecasts for a world with double the current amount of carbon dioxide' 그리고 'scientists could not easily predict how quickly the world's climate would change'.\n모델의 목적 = 미래 기후 변화 예측; 구름은 그 예측을 흔드는 변수일 뿐.\n정답: A", "trap": "B(구름의 영향 예측)가 가장 끌리지만, 구름은 모델에 넣거나 빼는 요소였을 뿐 모델의 주목적은 기후 전반의 변화 예측이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"atmospheric": "대기의", "drought": "가뭄", "monsoon": "몬순, 우기"}, "src": "verbal201 Q12 · 25/5, 25/4, 25/3, 24/9, 23/10, 23/9 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v200_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The science of astronomy was begun by amateurs and today remains dependent on their contributions, which are incisive by virtue of being _____ by the a priori assumptions that often vitiate the work of professional research scientists.", "choices": ["characterized", "unencumbered", "supported", "contradicted", "inspired"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: 'incisive by virtue of being ___ by the a priori assumptions that often vitiate the work of professionals'.\n선험적 가정은 전문가의 연구를 '망친다(vitiate)' → 아마추어의 기여가 예리한 이유는 그런 가정에 '얽매이지 않기' 때문.\n빈칸 = '~에 구애받지 않는'.\n정답: B (unencumbered)", "trap": "inspired/supported는 assumptions를 긍정적으로 만들어 vitiate(손상시키다)와 충돌한다. characterized도 가정에 영향받는다는 뜻이 되어 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incisive": "예리한", "vitiate": "손상시키다", "unencumbered": "방해받지 않는, 얽매이지 않은", "characterized": "특징지어진", "supported": "지지받는", "contradicted": "반박당한", "inspired": "영감을 받은"}, "src": "verbal200 Q1 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v222_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "In clinical research into new treatments or the causal factors of diseases, randomized, double-blind controlled clinical trials are seen as (i) _____, but, given their (ii) _____, often are not feasible.", "choices": null, "columns": [["a dead end", "the gold standard", "an unattainable ideal"], ["expense", "predictability", "appeal"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'seen as ___, but ... often are not feasible' → 역접 but: 앞은 긍정적 평가 → 최고 기준 the gold standard.\n(ii) given their ___ → 실행이 어려운 이유 → 비용 expense.\n무작위 이중맹검 시험은 최고의 기준이지만 비용 때문에 현실적으로 어렵다.\n정답: B, D (the gold standard / expense)", "trap": "(i) an unattainable ideal은 '실현 불가능'과 의미가 겹쳐 but의 대조가 사라진다(동어반복).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"a dead end": "막다른 길", "the gold standard": "최고 기준, 표준", "an unattainable ideal": "도달할 수 없는 이상", "expense": "비용", "predictability": "예측 가능성", "appeal": "매력, 호소력"}, "src": "verbal222 Q2 · 25/7, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v208_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Although weeds often (i) _____ and are (ii) _____ human activities, their cussedness and refusal to play by human rules makes them subversive and the very essence of wildness.", "choices": null, "columns": [["follow", "thwart", "ignore"], ["unaffected by", "impervious to", "dependent on"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: Although ... , their cussedness and refusal to play by human rules makes them subversive → 뒤는 '인간 규칙을 따르지 않는 야생성'.\n앞은 그와 대조: 잡초가 인간 활동을 '따라다니고' 인간 활동에 '의존한다'.\n(i) follow (ii) dependent on.\n정답: A, F (follow / dependent on)", "trap": "(i) thwart(방해하다), (ii) impervious to(영향받지 않는)는 뒤의 '반항적 야생성'과 같은 방향이라 Although의 대조가 성립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"impervious to": "~에 영향받지 않는", "follow": "따라가다, 뒤따르다", "thwart": "좌절시키다, 방해하다", "ignore": "무시하다", "unaffected by": "~의 영향을 받지 않는", "dependent on": "~에 의존하는"}, "src": "verbal208 Q3 · 25년 8월, 23년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "A minor criticism of the book, which is (i) _____ an understanding of the difficulty of doing direct research in Hong Kong politics, is that Soman relied on secondary sources to tell the story of Hong Kong’s political development, with previous histories of the period (ii) _____ his research. Given Soman’s (iii) _____ many of the players in Hong Kong politics, it is surprising that he did not use interviews and other forms of direct research to delve further into the motivations, strategies, and tactics of participants.", "choices": null, "columns": [["attributable to", "exacerbated by", "tempered by"], ["largely debunked by", "obviating the need for", "playing a large role in"], ["deference to", "estrangement from", "proximity to"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'A minor criticism ... which is ___ an understanding of the difficulty of direct research' → 사소한 비판이며, 직접 연구의 어려움을 이해하는 마음으로 '누그러뜨려진' 비판 → tempered by.\n(ii) 2차 자료에 의존 → 이전 역사서들이 그의 연구에서 '큰 역할' → playing a large role in.\n(iii) 'it is surprising that he did not use interviews' → 인터뷰가 쉬웠을 상황 → 정치인들과 '가까움' proximity to.\n정답: C, F, I (tempered by / playing a large role in / proximity to)", "trap": "(iii) deference to(존중)도 그럴듯하지만, 인터뷰를 안 한 것이 '놀랍다'려면 접근성이 좋았어야 하므로 proximity가 맞다. (ii) obviating the need for는 2차 자료 의존과 반대.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"attributable to": "~때문인", "exacerbated by": "~로 악화된", "tempered by": "~로 누그러진, 완화된", "largely debunked by": "~에 의해 대부분 반박된", "obviating the need for": "~의 필요를 없애는", "playing a large role in": "~에서 큰 역할을 하는", "deference to": "~에 대한 존중", "estrangement from": "~와의 소원함", "proximity to": "~와의 가까움"}, "src": "verbal200 Q4 · 24년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v10_q12", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage states which of the following about the Mesopotamian statues?", "choices": ["They lack mimetic resemblance to their historical subjects.", "They had a religious function for the individuals represented.", "Their uniformity makes it impossible to link the statues with specific individuals."], "columns": null, "pid": "v10_p3", "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'they do not mimetically imitate the individual's features' → 외형적 닮음이 없음, 맞음.\nB: 'placed in temples where they stood in for the individual as a worshipper' → 개인을 위한 종교적 기능, 맞음.\nC: 오히려 'they represent individuals'라고 했으므로 틀림(획일성 언급 없음).\n정답: A, B", "trap": "C는 '모방적 닮음이 없다'에서 '개인과 연결 불가'로 비약한 것; 지문은 닮지 않아도 개인을 표상한다고 말한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"mimetic": "모방적인", "portraiture": "초상화(법)", "agency": "행위 주체성, 작용력"}, "src": "verbal10 Q12"}, {"id": "v10_q13", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage mentions \"numerous ancient texts\" primarily in order to", "choices": ["support a contention about how Mesopotamians' attitude toward the statues differed from modern notions of portraiture", "identify the source of information about what kinds of images the Mesopotamians considered to be portraiture", "explain how modern scholars know that the statues were intended to be placed in temples", "argue that the standard Western division of genres is too recently developed for it to be applied appropriately to the statues", "defend the notion that the statues were made as representations of real, historical people"], "columns": null, "pid": "v10_p3", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'numerous ancient texts demonstrate that images ... had agency' 는 바로 앞의 주장 '현대의 초상 개념보다 더 밀접하게 개인과 연결되었다(the person's essence continued to exist in the image)'를 뒷받침하는 근거.\n즉 메소포타미아인의 태도가 현대 초상 개념과 어떻게 다른지에 대한 주장을 지지.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 '어떤 이미지를 초상으로 여겼는지'의 출처라고 하지만, 고대 문헌은 이미지의 힘(agency)을 보여 주는 근거로 쓰였다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "numerous ancient texts", "glosses": {"agency": "행위 주체성, 작용력", "essence": "본질", "contention": "주장"}, "src": "verbal10 Q13"}, {"id": "v32_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with", "choices": ["discussing shortsighted proposals to eliminate problems with mosquitoes", "outlining ways in which people can alleviate the problems caused by mosquitoes", "arguing that social traditions can perpetuate people's problems with mosquitoes", "discussing various ways in which people come into contact with mosquitoes", "suggesting how the breeding habits of mosquitoes create problems for people"], "columns": null, "pid": "v32_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심: 'Social tradition and habits ... do much to ensure continual contact between mosquitoes and people' 와 마지막 'until we accomplish ... understanding how our habits often perpetuate ... our problems, efforts ... will probably fail'.\n→ 사회적 전통이 모기 문제를 지속시킨다는 주장.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 '단순 박멸 캠페인'이 첫 문장에 나오지만 그것을 논의하는 것이 목적이 아니다. D는 '다양한 접촉 방식'을 나열하지 않고 예시 하나뿐.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"perpetuate": "영속시키다", "leaf axil": "잎겨드랑이", "advocate": "옹호하다"}, "src": "verbal32 Q5"}, {"id": "v32_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the organization of the passage?", "choices": ["A hypothesis is presented, weighed, and qualified, and then the modified hypothesis is reaffirmed.", "An argument is advanced, then it is refuted, and an alternative is suggested.", "A claim is made, a supporting example is provided, and then a conclusion is offered.", "Opposing views are presented, evaluated and then reconciled.", "A problem is identified, a solution is proposed, and potential difficulties with the solution are raised."], "columns": null, "pid": "v32_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 주장(사회적 전통·습관이 모기와의 접촉을 지속시킨다) → 예시(킬리만자로의 dracaena 울타리) → 결론(습관을 이해하지 않으면 노력이 실패할 것).\n'for example'과 마지막 'But until ...'이 각각 예시와 결론의 신호.\n정답: C", "trap": "E는 '해결책 제시 후 난점'이라 하지만, 저자는 해결책을 제안하지 않는다(살자고 하는 것도 아님).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"qualify": "단서를 달다, 제한하다", "refute": "반박하다", "reconcile": "조정하다, 화해시키다"}, "src": "verbal32 Q6"}, {"id": "v32_q7", "type": "RC_select", "blanks": null, "stem": "Select a sentence in which a potential misinterpretation of the author's position is addressed.", "choices": null, "columns": null, "pid": "v32_p1", "answer": "SENTENCE", "answer_sentence": "I am not advocating a policy of living with mosquitoes; we already know that living with them is very unpleasant.", "explanation": "저자는 인간 습관이 모기 문제를 지속시킨다고 주장하므로, '그럼 모기와 그냥 함께 살자는 말이냐'는 오해가 생길 수 있다.\n'I am not advocating a policy of living with mosquitoes' 가 바로 그 잠재적 오해를 차단하는 문장.\n정답: I am not advocating a policy of living with mosquitoes; we already know that living with them is very unpleasant.", "trap": "마지막 문장(But until ...)은 저자의 결론을 제시할 뿐, 오해를 해명하는 문장이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"advocate": "옹호하다", "misinterpretation": "오해, 잘못된 해석"}, "src": "verbal32 Q7"}, {"id": "v212_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Gilbert Blane confirmed in 1780 that citrus could cure scurvy, yet the British navy did not systematically treat afflicted sailors with citrus for another fifteen years, largely due to the _____ of the naval bureaucracy.", "choices": ["stubbornness", "ineffectiveness", "intransigence", "elusiveness", "imponderability", "contentiousness"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: yet → 1780년에 효과가 확인되었는데도 15년 동안 시행하지 않음.\nlargely due to the ___ of the naval bureaucracy → 변화를 거부하는 '고집'.\nstubbornness(완고함)와 intransigence(비타협성)가 짝.\n정답: A, C (stubbornness, intransigence)", "trap": "ineffectiveness(비효율)도 지연의 원인으로 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없고, '알면서도 안 바꿈'의 의미를 담지 못한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"intransigence": "비타협성, 완고함", "stubbornness": "완고함, 고집", "ineffectiveness": "비효율, 무능", "elusiveness": "파악하기 어려움", "imponderability": "헤아릴 수 없음", "contentiousness": "논쟁을 좋아함"}, "src": "verbal212 Q10 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The _____ of governmental subsidies to obscure airports that are rarely used underscores the political difficulties of cutting funds from even the most unnecessary projects.", "choices": ["paucity", "effectiveness", "durability", "persistence", "adequacy", "dearth"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'underscores the political difficulties of cutting funds from even the most unnecessary projects' → 불필요한 보조금도 끊기 어렵다.\n빈칸 = 보조금이 '계속 유지됨'.\ndurability(지속성)와 persistence(지속)가 짝.\n정답: C, D (durability, persistence)", "trap": "paucity/dearth(부족)는 서로 짝이지만 '삭감이 어렵다'는 내용과 반대(보조금이 적다는 뜻이 됨).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"paucity": "부족, 결핍", "effectiveness": "효과", "durability": "내구성, 지속성", "persistence": "지속, 끈기", "adequacy": "적절함, 충분함", "dearth": "부족, 결핍"}, "src": "verbal220 Q10 · 25년 7월, 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v34_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although many skeptics of the scientific theory _____ critiques that have long since been disproved, some of the doubters arguably bring up valid points.", "choices": ["overlook", "revise", "recycle", "utilize", "neglect", "rehash"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: Although many skeptics ___ critiques that have long since been disproved, some ... bring up valid points → 대조.\n앞은 부정: 이미 반박된 비판을 '재탕한다'.\nrecycle과 rehash가 짝(낡은 것을 다시 꺼내 씀).\n정답: C, F (recycle, rehash)", "trap": "utilize(활용하다)는 의미상 가능하나 '이미 반박된 것을 반복'이라는 부정 뉘앙스가 없고 짝이 없다. overlook/neglect는 짝이지만 논리가 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"overlook": "간과하다", "revise": "수정하다", "recycle": "재활용하다, 재탕하다", "utilize": "활용하다", "neglect": "소홀히 하다", "rehash": "(낡은 생각을) 재탕하다"}, "src": "verbal34 Q9"}, {"id": "v14_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, most seriously weakens the argument?", "choices": ["Most of the people who would take the special free buses are currently members of carpools.", "The city does not currently have enough buses to transport all of the commuters who normally commute by car.", "Buses that would be operating on hot, humid days would rarely, if ever, be filled to capacity.", "The amount of vehicle exhaust produced in the city is not significantly higher on hot, humid days.", "Not all commuter routes are used by enough people to warrant providing bus service for them."], "columns": null, "pid": "v14_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 버스가 절반 이상 차면 오존이 줄어든다.\n근거: 버스 1대(약 40명) = 자동차 약 20대분 배기가스 → 승객 1명이 자동차 1대를 대체한다고 가정.\nA: 버스 이용자가 대부분 이미 카풀을 하던 사람 → 버스 승객 수만큼 자동차가 줄지 않음 → 가정이 무너져 약화.\n정답: A", "trap": "C(정원을 거의 못 채운다)는 끌리지만, 논증은 '절반 이상'만 요구하므로 만석이 아니어도 결론은 유지된다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incentive": "유인책", "exhaust": "배기가스", "carpool": "카풀, 승용차 함께 타기"}, "src": "verbal14 Q11"}, {"id": "v208_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the highlighted portion of the passage, the author assumes that", "choices": ["consumers' attitude toward the assortment of choices they are presented with depends almost exclusively on the size of the range", "consumers who have clear preferences make their choices more quickly than those whose preferences are relatively vague", "consumers' anticipation of meeting specific expectations directly affects their satisfaction with a selected option", "consumers presented with an assortment of choices often adjust the preferences they had beforehand", "consumers presented with a larger assortment of choices often make their decisions too quickly"], "columns": null, "pid": "v208_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "강조 부분: 기대가 충족되지 않을 가능성이 커져 '더 큰 선택지에서 고른 것에 덜 만족한다'.\n이 결론은 '기대 충족 여부가 만족도에 영향을 준다'는 숨은 전제가 있어야 성립.\nC가 그 전제를 그대로 말한다.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 '거의 전적으로 크기에 달려 있다'는 극단적 표현이라 틀림. D(선호 조정)는 지문에 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"assortment": "구색, 모음", "anticipation": "기대, 예상", "preference": "선호"}, "src": "verbal208 Q5 · 25/7, 25/3, 24/12, 23/3, 23/1, 22/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v208_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the first sentence in the author's argument as a whole?", "choices": ["It states a premise on which the author's conclusion is based.", "It provides information to support the inference made in the following sentence.", "It introduces a concept that the author proves illogical.", "It summarizes a position that the author proceeds to dispute.", "It presents the phenomenon the argument is intended to explain."], "columns": null, "pid": "v208_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 선택지가 많으면 선호를 맞출 수 있다는 소비자의 '기대'가 커진다.\n저자는 이를 반박하지 않고 'seem logical'이라 인정한 뒤, 실제 만족스러운 매칭은 별로 늘지 않는다고 말한다.\n결론 'larger assortments can increase the likelihood that expectations will not be met'은 첫 문장(기대 상승)을 전제로 해야 성립.\n→ 결론의 근거가 되는 전제 = A.\n정답: A (교재 정답표는 D)", "trap": "D(저자가 반박하는 입장 요약): 저자가 반박하는 것은 '기대가 실제로 충족된다'는 생각이지, 기대가 커진다는 첫 문장 자체가 아니다. 'however'의 대상을 혼동하기 쉽다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "Having a larger assortment to choose from increases consumers’ expectations about matching their preferences.", "glosses": {"assortment": "구색, 모음", "premise": "전제", "envision": "상상하다, 마음에 그리다"}, "src": "verbal208 Q6 · 25/7, 25/3, 24/12, 23/3, 23/1, 22/4 중국후기", "note": "⚠ 원본 답안표 정답은 D이지만, 검토 풀이로는 A이(가) 더 타당해 보입니다. 채점은 원본 기준이며 아래 해설은 검토 풀이 기준입니다. 근거: Key says D, but the author never disputes the first sentence: he calls the heightened expectations 'logical' and his conclusion ('larger assortments can increase the likelihood that expectations will not be met') depends on expectations rising with assortment size. The first sentence is a premise of the conclusion, so A. ('however' contrasts with actual preference matches, not with sentence 1.)"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.2 / S2 2.5"}, {"set": 12, "sections": [[{"id": "v223_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Although most of her colleagues _____ that the science of ecology can be practiced without taking a stand on environmental issues, the scientist insists that certain ecological studies can be undertaken without adopting any particular position on such issues.", "choices": ["lament", "deny", "contend", "worry", "theorize"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: Although → 동료 대다수와 그 과학자의 입장이 대조.\n과학자: 특정 연구는 입장 없이도 수행할 수 있다고 주장(insists).\n→ 동료들은 '입장 없이 생태학을 할 수 있다'는 것을 부정해야 대조가 됨 → deny.\n정답: B (deny)", "trap": "contend(주장하다)는 동료와 과학자의 입장이 같아져 Although의 대조가 사라진다. lament/worry도 '그것이 가능하다'를 안타까워하는 뜻이라 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lament": "한탄하다", "deny": "부인하다", "contend": "주장하다", "worry": "걱정하다", "theorize": "이론화하다"}, "src": "verbal223 Q1 · 25년 7월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v201_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Her argument, though stimulating, is far from being proof against all reproach: several of its most crucial hypotheses are rather more (i) _____ than (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["simplistic", "provocative", "convincing"], ["sincere", "probable", "conventional"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: though stimulating, far from being proof against all reproach → 흥미롭지만 비판받을 여지가 있다.\n'rather more (i) than (ii)' → (i)은 stimulating과 같은 계열 provocative(자극적인), (ii)는 비판 받는 이유가 되는 부족한 점 = '그럴듯함' probable.\n가설들이 그럴듯하기보다 도발적이다.\n정답: B, E (provocative / probable)", "trap": "(i) simplistic도 비판처럼 보이지만 'stimulating'과 연결되지 않고, (ii) conventional과 짝지으면 오히려 칭찬에 가까워진다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"simplistic": "지나치게 단순화한", "provocative": "도발적인, 자극적인", "convincing": "설득력 있는", "sincere": "진실한", "probable": "개연성 있는, 그럴듯한", "conventional": "관습적인"}, "src": "verbal201 Q2 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v19_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "When a new scientific model emerges, research studies (i)__________ that paradigm tend to dominate in the scientific literature: the process of selecting articles for publication is tilted toward positive results. But once the paradigm (ii)__________, the academic incentives shift in the opposite direction: research results are more likely to be considered worthy of publication when they (iii)__________ what has become the established view.", "choices": null, "columns": [["tweaking", "affirming", "controverting"], ["is initially articulated", "has become entrenched", "is about to be attacked"], ["bolster", "circumvent", "undermine"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BEI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'the process of selecting articles ... is tilted toward positive results' → 새 패러다임을 '지지하는' 연구가 우세 → affirming.\n(ii) But once the paradigm ___ → 지배적 견해가 된 후 'what has become the established view' → has become entrenched(확고해지다).\n(iii) 'incentives shift in the opposite direction' → 이제는 기존 견해를 '약화시키는' 결과가 출판 가치 → undermine.\n정답: B, E, I (affirming / has become entrenched / undermine)", "trap": "(ii) is about to be attacked는 (iii)과 잘 이어지는 듯하지만 'established view'라는 표현과 맞지 않는다; 패러다임이 굳어진 상태여야 한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tweaking": "약간 수정하는", "affirming": "확증하는, 지지하는", "controverting": "반박하는", "is initially articulated": "처음 표명되다", "has become entrenched": "확고히 자리잡다", "is about to be attacked": "공격받기 직전이다", "bolster": "강화하다", "circumvent": "우회하다", "undermine": "약화시키다"}, "src": "verbal19 Q3"}, {"id": "v223_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which statement best expresses the author's main conclusion in the passage?", "choices": ["The second quarto version of Hamlet may have been performed in an indoor theater.", "The version of Hamlet that was originally performed must have had a considerably longer running time than did most other plays staged in Elizabethan theaters.", "The second quarto version of Hamlet may have been intended for readers rather than for theatrical performers.", "The second quarto version of Hamlet is far too long to have been performed on the Elizabethan stage.", "The version of Hamlet performed on the Elizabethan stage had to have been less than half the length of the second quarto version."], "columns": null, "pid": "v223_p4", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장이 결론: 'the second quarto version of Hamlet ... could not have been performed uncut'.\n이후는 근거(4시간 소요, 해 질 녘 문제, 다른 연극은 2시간).\nD가 '엘리자베스 시대 무대에서 공연되기엔 너무 길다'로 이를 바꿔 말함.\n정답: D", "trap": "E(절반 이하였어야 한다)는 '2시간' 언급에서 나온 계산이라 끌리지만 지문이 단정하지 않는 지나치게 구체적인 결론이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"quarto": "사절판(책 판형)", "uncut": "삭제되지 않은, 무삭제의", "rattle off": "술술 말하다"}, "src": "verbal223 Q4 · 25/6, 25/5, 24/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v223_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which statement best describes the function of the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["It summarizes the central claim of the author's argument.", "It underscores the importance of evidence previously presented in the passage.", "It supplies additional evidence to support the author's argument.", "It qualifies a point made earlier in the passage.", "It anticipates and refutes an objection to the author's claims."], "columns": null, "pid": "v223_p4", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "저자 주장: 2절판 햄릿은 무삭제 공연이 불가능했다.\n앞 근거: 분당 대사 속도·해 지는 시간 → 4시간 공연은 불가.\n강조 문장: 다른 연극들의 상연 시간이 2시간에 가까웠다 → 같은 결론을 지지하는 '추가 근거'.\n정답: C", "trap": "B(앞 근거의 중요성 강조)는 새로운 정보(다른 연극의 상연 시간)를 제시한다는 점을 놓친다. D(단서 달기)는 주장을 약화시키지 않으므로 틀림.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"contemporary": "동시대의", "running time": "상연 시간", "qualify": "단서를 달다"}, "src": "verbal223 Q5 · 25/6, 25/5, 24/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v7_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although some literary scholars may express disdain for words meant for popular audiences, only the most _____ proponent of so-called great literature could dismiss the works in a recent anthology of African science fiction as formulaic pulp.", "choices": ["radical", "pedantic", "oblivious", "hidebound", "illiberal", "charitable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: only the most ___ proponent of so-called great literature could dismiss ... as formulaic pulp → 그 작품들을 깎아내리는 사람은 극도로 '편협한/고루한' 사람뿐.\n빈칸 = 부정, 좁은 시야·전통에 갇힌.\nhidebound(편협한, 고루한)와 illiberal(편협한)이 짝.\n정답: D, E (hidebound, illiberal)", "trap": "pedantic(현학적인)은 문학 학자에게 그럴듯하지만 '좁은 시야'가 아닌 '지식 과시'의 뜻이라 짝이 없다. oblivious도 짝 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pedantic": "현학적인, 규칙에 얽매이는", "oblivious": "의식하지 못하는", "hidebound": "편협한, 고루한", "illiberal": "편협한, 관용 없는", "radical": "급진적인", "charitable": "너그러운, 자비로운"}, "src": "verbal7 Q9"}, {"id": "v225_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "A cure for the common cold has been so elusive that it has become a modern symbol of _____.", "choices": ["danger", "futility", "unease", "pointlessness", "sloth", "apathy"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: so elusive(너무 잡히지 않아서) → 감기 치료제를 찾는 일이 '헛된 노력'의 상징.\n빈칸 = 헛수고, 무의미함.\nfutility와 pointlessness가 짝.\n정답: B, D (futility, pointlessness)", "trap": "sloth(나태)와 apathy(무관심)는 '노력하지 않음'이라 서로 비슷해 보이지만, 문장은 노력해도 이루지 못함을 말한다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"danger": "위험", "futility": "헛됨, 무익함", "unease": "불안", "pointlessness": "무의미함", "sloth": "나태", "apathy": "무관심"}, "src": "verbal225 Q6 · 25/3, 24/12, 24/8, 23/10 중국후기"}, {"id": "v201_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Of the lizard species capable of traveling long distances beneath desert sands, most have very _____ limbs; by contrast, the sandfish lizard has well-developed limbs with which it propels itself through the sand.", "choices": ["modest", "unusual", "ungainly", "limited", "agile", "nimble"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: by contrast, the sandfish lizard has well-developed limbs → 대부분 다른 도마뱀은 다리가 '발달하지 않은/작은'.\n빈칸 = well-developed의 반대.\nmodest(작은, 대단치 않은)와 limited(제한된)가 짝.\n정답: A, D (modest, limited)", "trap": "agile/nimble은 짝이지만 'well-developed'와 대조되지 않는다. ungainly(어색한)는 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"modest": "대단치 않은, 작은", "ungainly": "볼품없는, 어색한", "limited": "제한된, 빈약한", "nimble": "날렵한, 민첩한", "unusual": "특이한", "agile": "민첩한"}, "src": "verbal201 Q9 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v9_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "A strong basic science program can be _____: the rate of return on capital invested in basic science is about three times that of capital invested in applied research and development.", "choices": ["idealistic", "remunerative", "lucrative", "transcendent", "feasible", "radical"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 설명: 기초과학에 투자한 자본의 수익률이 응용 연구의 약 3배.\n빈칸 = '돈이 되는, 수익성 있는'.\nremunerative와 lucrative가 짝.\n정답: B, C (remunerative, lucrative)", "trap": "feasible(실현 가능한)은 긍정적이지만 수익률과 직결되지 않고 짝이 없다. idealistic/transcendent는 '돈'과 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"remunerative": "수익성이 좋은, 보수가 많은", "idealistic": "이상주의적인", "lucrative": "수익성이 좋은", "transcendent": "초월적인", "feasible": "실현 가능한", "radical": "급진적인"}, "src": "verbal9 Q8"}, {"id": "v199_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["point out the parallel effects on jazz music of governmental actions in San Francisco and New Orleans", "offer an alternative to the standard explanation for the decline of San Francisco as a jazz center", "argue for the importance of Californian cities in the development of jazz", "present and refute an argument about the reasons for a demographic shift in jazz activity", "outline the factors that contributed to a change in the geographical locust of jazz activity"], "columns": null, "pid": "v199_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문단: 1921년 Barbary Coast 폐쇄가 LA를 서부 재즈 중심지로 만든 결정적 사건.\n2문단: 'Yet even before that closing' → LA의 흑인 공동체·영화·음반 산업, New Orleans Storyville 폐쇄 등 다른 요인.\n→ 재즈 중심지의 지리적 이동에 기여한 요인들을 개괄.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(논증 제시 후 반박)는 'Yet'에 끌리지만, 2문단은 1문단을 반박하지 않고 추가 요인을 보탤 뿐이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"venue": "장소, 무대", "premier": "최고의", "magnet": "끌어들이는 곳"}, "src": "verbal199 Q10 · 24/2, 23/10, 22/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v199_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage cites which of the following as a factor helping to explain San Francisco’s preeminence as a center for jazz music on the West Coast early in the twentieth century?", "choices": ["The number of job opportunities for musicians in San Francisco’s nightclub district", "The efforts by the government to enforce Prohibition in San Francisco", "The existence of venues for many different types of jazz in the San Francisco area", "The relative accessibility of San Francisco, as compared to Los Angeles, for musicians from elsewhere in the country", "The fact that San Francisco at that time had a larger African American population than Los Angeles"], "columns": null, "pid": "v199_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'an abundance of nightclubs provided ample work opportunities for local players and drew musicians'.\nA가 나이트클럽 지역의 일자리 수로 그대로 옮김.\n정답: A", "trap": "B(금주법 단속)는 오히려 San Francisco의 쇠퇴 원인이었다. E는 LA가 가장 큰 흑인 공동체였다는 지문과 반대.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"preeminence": "탁월함, 우위", "abundance": "풍부함", "ample": "충분한"}, "src": "verbal199 Q11 · 24/2, 23/10, 22/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v199_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that, for African American musicians, which of the following became an advantage of Los Angeles over San Francisco only after 1921?", "choices": ["It became easier to travel to Los Angeles than to San Francisco.", "Prohibition had less impact on the availability of work opportunities in Los Angeles.", "Nightclubs in Los Angeles offered better pay to jazz musicians than did nightclubs in San Francisco.", "The movie industry in Los Angeles became an important source of employment for jazz musicians.", "The African American community in Los Angeles began to expand rapidly."], "columns": null, "pid": "v199_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1921년 Barbary Coast 폐쇄(금주법 정책) → San Francisco에서 생계가 어려워져 LA로 이동.\n즉 1921년 이후에야 생긴 LA의 이점 = 금주법이 LA의 일자리에는 덜 영향을 줌.\nD(영화 산업), E(흑인 공동체 성장)는 'even before that closing' 이미 있던 요인.\n정답: B", "trap": "D·E는 LA의 장점이 맞지만 1921년 이전부터 존재했다고 지문이 명시하므로 'only after 1921' 조건에 어긋난다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"Prohibition": "(미국의) 금주법", "devastating": "파괴적인", "decisive": "결정적인"}, "src": "verbal199 Q12 · 24/2, 23/10, 22/12 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v238_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Some of the writers whose interviews with the Paris Review are included in this volume were caught in the final years of their lives, and these interviews thus lend _____ mood to the collection.", "choices": ["an autumnal", "a scintillating", "a liberal", "an apolitical", "a cosmopolitan"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'caught in the final years of their lives' → 인생 말년의 인터뷰 → 'thus' 결과로 모음집에 '황혼기의, 쓸쓸한' 분위기.\n빈칸 = 말년/노년을 떠올리게 하는 분위기.\nautumnal(가을의, 황혼기의)이 정답.\n정답: A (an autumnal)", "trap": "scintillating(재치 넘치는)은 인터뷰 모음집에 어울려 보이지만 '말년'이라는 단서와 관련이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"autumnal": "황혼기에 접어든", "an autumnal": "가을 같은, 황혼기의, 쓸쓸한", "a scintillating": "재기 넘치는, 번뜩이는", "a liberal": "자유주의적인, 관대한", "an apolitical": "정치에 무관심한", "a cosmopolitan": "국제적인, 세계적인"}, "src": "verbal238 Q1 · 25년 6월, 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v228_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Though it may not seem (i) _____, the fate of the grizzly bears, which have been both feared and revered throughout history, may hinge on something as (ii) _____ as a lowly moth.", "choices": null, "columns": [["plausible", "impressive", "incongruous"], ["widespread", "enduring", "unexceptional"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 'something as ___ as a lowly moth' → lowly(하찮은)와 같은 방향 → unexceptional(평범한).\n(i) Though it may not seem ___ → 거대한 회색곰의 운명이 하찮은 나방에 달려 있다는 건 '그럴듯해 보이지 않을' 수 있다 → plausible.\n정답: A, F (plausible / unexceptional)", "trap": "(i) incongruous(어울리지 않는)를 고르면 'not seem incongruous'가 되어 의미가 반대로 뒤집힌다(실제로는 어울리지 않아 보이는 상황).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"plausible": "그럴듯한", "impressive": "인상적인", "incongruous": "어울리지 않는, 부조화의", "widespread": "널리 퍼진", "enduring": "오래 지속되는", "unexceptional": "평범한, 특별할 것 없는"}, "src": "verbal228 Q3 · 25년 6월, 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v30_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Up to the 1970s, histories of science tended to be (i) _____, not least in their focus on discoveries and theories that could be read as anticipating later scientific orthodoxies, rather than on those deemed (ii) _____ in their own periods. Historians of science are now routinely far more sensitive on such scores.", "choices": null, "columns": [["anachronistic", "convoluted", "undogmatic"], ["major", "fallacious", "inessential"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'focus on discoveries ... that could be read as anticipating later scientific orthodoxies' → 과거를 현재 기준으로 해석 → anachronistic(시대착오적인).\n마지막 문장 '이제는 이런 점에 훨씬 민감하다' → (i)은 부정적 평가.\n(ii) rather than on those deemed ___ in their own periods → 당대에는 '중요하다'고 여겨진 것들을 소홀히 함 → major.\n정답: A, D (anachronistic / major)", "trap": "(ii) fallacious/inessential은 '당대에 틀렸거나 중요하지 않다고 여겨진 것'이 되어, 그것을 무시하는 게 왜 문제인지 설명하지 못한다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"anachronistic": "시대착오적인", "convoluted": "복잡한, 난해한", "undogmatic": "독단적이지 않은", "major": "주요한, 중요한", "fallacious": "잘못된, 오류가 있는", "inessential": "필수적이지 않은"}, "src": "verbal30 Q3"}, {"id": "v210_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Many perplexed observers find present-day museum design a choice between outlandishly sculptural structures that (i) _____ the proper display of art and neutral containers so (ii) _____ to art that all architectural presence is lost. But the New Museum persuasively demonstrates that honoring art and honoring architecture need not be (iii) _____ propositions.", "choices": null, "columns": [["ignore", "enhance", "honor"], ["submissive", "demeaning", "impervious"], ["carefully considered", "mutually exclusive", "entirely practical"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) outlandishly sculptural structures → 건축이 너무 튀어서 예술품의 적절한 전시를 '무시하는' → ignore.\n(ii) neutral containers so ___ to art that all architectural presence is lost → 예술에 너무 '순종적인/종속된' → submissive.\n(iii) But 뉴 뮤지엄은 예술 존중과 건축 존중이 '상호 배타적'일 필요가 없음을 보여 준다 → mutually exclusive.\n정답: A, D, H (ignore / submissive / mutually exclusive)", "trap": "(ii) demeaning(비하하는)은 '건축적 존재감이 사라진다'는 결과와 반대 방향이다(예술을 깎아내리는 것이 아님).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ignore": "무시하다", "enhance": "향상시키다", "honor": "존중하다", "submissive": "순종적인, 굴종적인", "demeaning": "비하하는", "impervious": "영향받지 않는", "carefully considered": "신중히 고려된", "mutually exclusive": "상호 배타적인", "entirely practical": "전적으로 실용적인"}, "src": "verbal210 Q4 · 25년 7월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author assumes which of the following about the emperor’s strategy of keeping “the taxes low and his bureaucracy small”?", "choices": ["It was implemented with little understanding of its consequences.", "It was a concession made to ameliorate an unacceptable situation", "It was an indication of the emperor’s refusal to compromise his principles", "It was a rare success in a policy area characterized by failure", "It was a choice of the common good over the emperor’s personal interests."], "columns": null, "pid": "v200_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Due to weak oversight, the emperor had to keep the taxes low and his bureaucracy small to mitigate this \"tyranny at the bottom\" effect'.\n'had to'와 'to mitigate' → 원해서가 아니라 관리들의 수탈(받아들일 수 없는 상황)을 완화하기 위한 어쩔 수 없는 양보.\n정답: B", "trap": "E(개인 이익보다 공익 선택)는 끌리지만, 황제 자신도 반란 예방이라는 이익을 위해 과세를 피했으므로 사익 희생으로 볼 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "the taxes low and his bureaucracy small", "glosses": {"ameliorate": "개선하다", "mitigate": "완화하다", "oversight": "감독", "preempt": "미연에 방지하다"}, "src": "verbal200 Q5 · 25/4, 24/4, 23/12, 23/11, 23/9, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that the Chinese emperor and the bureaucracy differed with respect to", "choices": ["the priority each placed on preventing popular rebellion", "the aversion of each to economic and bureaucratic reform", "the interest each showed in addressing the fiscal weakness of the state", "the willingness of each to encourage economic stability through large tax revenues", "the enthusiasm each had for the expansion of the Chinese economy"], "columns": null, "pid": "v200_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the emperor's interest in preempting rebellion militated against overtaxation, his agents had incentives to exploit the taxpayers' 그리고 관리들은 'shorter-term goals and narrower interests'.\n→ 황제는 반란 예방을 중시했지만 관리들은 그렇지 않음 → 반란 예방에 두는 우선순위가 달랐다.\n정답: A", "trap": "C(재정 약화 해결에 대한 관심)는 그럴듯하지만, 지문은 재정 약화에 대한 양측의 태도를 비교하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exploitation": "착취", "militate against": "~에 불리하게 작용하다", "exacerbate": "악화시키다"}, "src": "verbal200 Q6 · 25/4, 24/4, 23/12, 23/11, 23/9, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v20_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage cites \"evidence from the past\" in order to", "choices": ["Support a partial explanation", "Concede a potential objection", "Dismiss an apparent counterexample", "Highlight a scientific consensus", "Account for a historical anomaly"], "columns": null, "pid": "v20_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: 기후 변화로 산사태가 변하는 것은 놀랍지 않다 — 강수가 두 가지 촉발 요인 중 하나이기 때문.\n'Evidence from the past'는 산사태 주기가 기후 변동과 상관된다는 것을 보여 이 설명을 뒷받침.\n'partial'인 이유: 강수는 두 요인 중 하나이고, 2문단에서 인간 요인도 추가됨.\n정답: A", "trap": "D(과학적 합의 강조)는 'clearly indicates'에 끌리지만, 학계 합의를 말하는 것이 아니라 증거로 설명을 지지하는 역할이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Evidence from the past", "glosses": {"landsliding": "산사태", "precipitation": "강수", "seismic": "지진의", "anthropogenic": "인간이 초래한", "fluctuation": "변동"}, "src": "verbal20 Q5"}, {"id": "v20_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage makes which of the following claims?", "choices": ["A rise in precipitation resulting from human factors has increased the frequency and magnitude of landsliding.", "Human factors have led to greater changes in landsliding activity than have cyclical climate fluctuations.", "Decreases in landsliding activity have historically been accompanied by changes in climate.", "Slope stability is more influenced by seismic activity than it is by human factors.", "Changes in land-use patterns in mountain ecosystems are generally correlated with changes in climate."], "columns": null, "pid": "v20_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'cycles of elevated landslide activity have been followed by cycles of low activity, and that these are correlated with climate fluctuations'.\n산사태 감소(low activity) 주기도 기후 변동과 상관 → 감소가 기후 변화와 함께 일어났다 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "B(인간 요인이 기후 주기보다 더 큰 변화)는 비교 주장이 지문에 없다. A는 '인간에 의한 강수 증가'라는 근거 없는 인과를 만든다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"magnitude": "규모", "correlate": "상관관계가 있다", "slope stability": "사면 안정성"}, "src": "verbal20 Q6"}, {"id": "v20_q7", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage suggests which of the following about the role of human factors in landsliding activity?", "choices": ["Human factors can intensify or alter the effects of climate change on landsliding activity.", "It is likely that human factors affect landsliding activity more than climate change does.", "Until recently, human factors did not have much impact on landsliding activity."], "columns": null, "pid": "v20_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'anthropogenic factors, either acting alone or in concert with climate, which can further modify the process of landsliding' → 기후 변화의 효과를 강화·변형할 수 있음, 맞음.\nB: 인간 요인이 기후보다 더 크다는 비교는 없음.\nC: 'What sets current changes apart is the likely influence of anthropogenic factors'는 현재 변화의 특징을 말할 뿐, 과거 언제까지 영향이 미미했는지는 말하지 않음.\n정답: A", "trap": "C는 'What sets current changes ... apart'에서 추론하고 싶어지지만, 'until recently ... did not have much impact'는 지문이 다루지 않는 시점 주장으로 지나친 추론이다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"in concert with": "~와 함께, 협력하여", "anthropogenic": "인간이 초래한", "resilient": "회복력 있는", "deforestation": "삼림 벌채"}, "src": "verbal20 Q7"}, {"id": "v208_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Geologists' customary distinction between planetary mantle and core material appears increasingly _____: liquid oxides can be considered either molten mantle constituents or electrically conducting core components.", "choices": ["incontrovertible", "untenable", "dogmatic", "flawed", "contradictory", "confusing"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 액체 산화물은 맨틀 성분으로도, 핵 성분으로도 볼 수 있다 → 맨틀과 핵의 구분이 무너짐.\n빈칸 = 그 구분이 '유지될 수 없는, 결함 있는'.\nuntenable과 flawed가 짝.\n정답: B, D (untenable, flawed)", "trap": "confusing(혼란스러운)·contradictory(모순된)도 그럴듯하지만, 구분 자체가 '모순적'이거나 '헷갈리는' 것이 아니라 근거가 약해져 '타당성을 잃는' 것이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"untenable": "유지할 수 없는, 옹호할 수 없는", "incontrovertible": "논란의 여지가 없는", "dogmatic": "독단적인", "flawed": "결함이 있는", "contradictory": "모순된", "confusing": "혼란스러운"}, "src": "verbal208 Q10 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Critics have universally recognized Toni Morrison for _____ the limited perspectives of mainstream United States history by reclaiming the narratives of African American history, particularly from a female point of view.", "choices": ["defining", "correcting", "inferring", "espousing", "adopting", "redressing"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'the limited perspectives of mainstream history' + 'by reclaiming the narratives of African American history' → 한계를 '바로잡는' 행위로 인정받음.\n빈칸 = 결함을 고치다.\ncorrecting과 redressing(시정하다)이 짝.\n정답: B, F (correcting, redressing)", "trap": "espousing/adopting은 짝이지만 '편협한 관점을 채택했다'가 되어 칭찬받는 이유와 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"defining": "정의하다", "correcting": "바로잡다", "inferring": "추론하다", "espousing": "지지하다, 신봉하다", "adopting": "채택하다", "redressing": "바로잡다, 시정하다"}, "src": "verbal224 Q11 · 25/11, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Elizabethan actor Richard Tarlton was so _____ in appearance that a mere glimpse of his grinning face peeping through a curtain was enough to trigger prolonged peals of laughter.", "choices": ["animated", "risible", "comely", "ludicrous", "handsome", "anomalous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: so ___ in appearance that a mere glimpse ... trigger prolonged peals of laughter → 얼굴만 봐도 웃음이 터질 정도.\n빈칸 = '우스꽝스러운'.\nrisible과 ludicrous가 짝.\n정답: B, D (risible, ludicrous)", "trap": "animated(생기 있는)는 grinning face와 어울려 보이지만 '웃음을 유발하는' 의미가 아니고 짝이 없다. comely/handsome은 짝이지만 웃음과 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"risible": "웃음을 자아내는, 우스운", "ludicrous": "우스꽝스러운, 터무니없는", "animated": "생기 있는, 활발한", "comely": "잘생긴, 어여쁜", "handsome": "잘생긴", "anomalous": "변칙적인, 이례적인"}, "src": "verbal234 Q11 · 24년 3월, 22년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, most strengthens the argument?", "choices": ["The majority of nonviolent crimes committed by juveniles in Fiera occur between 3 P.M. and 8 P.M.", "The overall rate of violent crime in Fiera has gone up slightly over the past two years.", "After varying around an apparently stable average for several years, the number of violent crimes committed by juveniles in Fiera increased by twelve percent the year before the imposition of the curfew.", "Over the last two years, the city of Fiera has substantially increased the size of its police department and made some changes in the crime-fighting tactics the police use.", "Over the past two years, fewer juveniles have been arrested in Fiera for curfew violations than have been arrested for violent crimes."], "columns": null, "pid": "v240_p3", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 통금이 청소년 강력범죄 감소(약 10%)에 효과적이었다.\n약점: 범죄 전반이 줄어드는 추세였을 수도 있다(다른 원인).\nB: 같은 기간 도시 전체 강력범죄율은 오히려 약간 증가 → 전반적 추세 때문이 아님 → 통금 효과 지지.\n정답: B", "trap": "C는 통금 직전 해에 12% 급증했다는 내용 → 이후 감소가 평균 회귀일 수 있어 오히려 약화. D는 경찰 증원이라는 대안 원인으로 약화.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"curfew": "통행금지", "juvenile": "청소년", "impose": "부과하다, 시행하다"}, "src": "verbal240 Q13 · 24/2, 22/8, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v16_q14", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true regarding difficulties in measuring workers' talent?", "choices": ["These difficulties cannot fully explain the observed wage gap.", "These difficulties are greater in high-profit industry than in low-profit industries.", "These difficulties can be eliminated by controlling for education and tenure."], "columns": null, "pid": "v16_p4", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'it is unlikely that such measurement problems can explain everything' → 측정 문제로 임금 격차를 다 설명할 수 없음, 맞음.\nB: 고수익/저수익 산업 간 측정 어려움 차이는 언급 없음.\nC: 교육·근속을 통제해도 'still find big wage disparities' → 어려움이 제거된다는 말은 없음.\n정답: A", "trap": "C는 'control for those factors'라는 지문 표현과 겹쳐 끌리지만, 통제는 재능 측정 문제를 '우회'한 것이지 제거한 것이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tenure": "재직 기간, 근속", "disparity": "격차", "presumably": "아마, 추정컨대"}, "src": "verbal16 Q14"}, {"id": "v16_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence (\"Moreover, … the two.\") in the context of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["To analyze an unusual trend regarding measurement problems that was referred to earlier in the passage", "To offer a hypothesis that explains the measurement problems referred to earlier in the passage", "To cite an instance that supports an assumption about measurement problems that was made earlier in the passage", "To evaluate an assertion regarding the wage disparity that was mentioned in the preceding sentence", "To qualify the claim regarding workers doing identical jobs that was made in the first sentence"], "columns": null, "pid": "v16_p4", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "주장: 'it is unlikely that such measurement problems can explain everything' (측정 문제로 다 설명할 수 없다).\n근거1: 교육·근속을 통제해도 격차가 큼. 근거2(강조 문장, Moreover + for example): 접수원은 재능이 그대로인데 저수익 산업으로 옮기면 임금이 떨어짐.\n→ 앞서 나온 '측정 문제에 대한 주장(assumption)'을 뒷받침하는 사례 제시 = C.\nD처럼 앞 문장을 '평가'하는 것이 아니라 그와 나란히 추가 근거를 더한다.\n정답: C (교재 정답표는 D)", "trap": "D: 'evaluate'는 앞 문장을 검토·판단한다는 뜻인데, 강조 문장은 앞 문장을 평가하지 않고 'Moreover'로 같은 방향의 증거를 덧붙인다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tenure": "재직 기간, 근속", "disparity": "격차", "qualify": "단서를 달다, 제한하다", "in line with": "~에 맞춰, 비례하여"}, "src": "verbal16 Q15", "note": "⚠ 원본 답안표 정답은 D이지만, 검토 풀이로는 C이(가) 더 타당해 보입니다. 채점은 원본 기준이며 아래 해설은 검토 풀이 기준입니다. 근거: Key says D, but the highlighted sentence ('Moreover ... for example ...') adds a concrete instance (receptionists keep their talent yet their pay drops with the industry gap) supporting the earlier claim that measurement problems cannot explain everything. It does not evaluate the preceding sentence; it parallels it as additional evidence. Best answer C."}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.3 / S2 2.9"}, {"set": 13, "sections": [[{"id": "v15_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Drug companies rarely pursue new pharmacotherapies for rare disease because of the high failure rates and the cost of research, which make the companies' chances of recovering their investments _____.", "choices": ["tenable", "dubious", "invaluable", "sanguine", "expensive"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: because of the high failure rates and the cost of research (높은 실패율, 비용) → 원인-결과 관계.\n제약사가 희귀병 신약을 '거의 추진하지 않는다' → 투자금 회수 가능성이 낮다는 뜻.\n빈칸 = 부정, '불확실한/의심스러운'.\ndubious(불확실한, 의심스러운)가 정확히 들어맞는다.\n정답: B (dubious)", "trap": "tenable(유지 가능한)·sanguine(낙관적인)은 방향이 반대(긍정). expensive는 '비용'이란 단어에 끌린 함정으로, 회수 '가능성'을 수식할 수 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tenable": "타당한, 유지 가능한", "sanguine": "낙관적인", "dubious": "불확실한, 의심스러운", "invaluable": "매우 귀중한", "expensive": "비싼"}, "src": "verbal15 Q1"}, {"id": "v5_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "A sociological jurisprudence has a (i) _____ rather than (ii) _____ focus: it is concerned with what actually goes on in the legal system, not with what ought to go on.", "choices": null, "columns": [["humanitarian", "descriptive", "hypothetical"], ["an elitist", "a normative", "an applied"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 앞 문장을 풀어 설명한다.\n(i) 'what actually goes on'(실제로 일어나는 일) = 사실을 기술하는 → descriptive.\n(ii) 'what ought to go on'(일어나야 하는 일) = 당위·규범 → a normative.\nrather than 구조로 descriptive vs normative 대조가 완성된다.\n정답: B (descriptive), E (a normative)", "trap": "hypothetical은 '실제'와 반대처럼 보여 끌리지만, 콜론 뒤의 대조는 '사실 vs 당위'이지 '실제 vs 가정'이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"humanitarian": "인도주의적인", "descriptive": "기술적인, 사실을 서술하는", "hypothetical": "가설의, 가정의", "an elitist": "엘리트주의적인", "a normative": "규범적인, 당위의", "an applied": "응용의"}, "src": "verbal5 Q2"}, {"id": "v219_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Because the term \"memoir,\" unlike the term \"autobiography,\" can suggest subjectivity rather than objectivity, Barton, in choosing to call his book a memoir, (i) _____ the accusation that his story may be (ii) _____. As Barton himself has noted, memoir promises only to give the reader an account of the author's memory, and no one but the author can therefore (iii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["formulates", "deflects", "disavows"], ["untrue", "hackneyed", "unexceptional"], ["document its facts", "gauge its veracity", "explain its appeal"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "전제: memoir는 autobiography와 달리 '객관성'이 아닌 '주관성'을 암시한다.\n(ii) 주관적 기억이라면 '사실이 아닐 수 있다'는 비난이 문제 → untrue.\n(i) memoir라고 부름으로써 그 비난을 '피해 간다' → deflects.\n(iii) 회고록은 저자 기억의 기록일 뿐이므로 저자 외에는 그 '진실성을 판단할' 수 없다 → gauge its veracity.\n정답: B (deflects), D (untrue), H (gauge its veracity)", "trap": "disavows(부인하다)는 '비난을 부인한다'로 그럴듯하지만, 장르 선택이 비난 자체를 비켜 가게 만드는 것이지 적극적으로 부인하는 것이 아니다. (iii)의 document its facts도 '사실'에 끌리는 함정.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"formulates": "공식화하다, 만들어 내다", "deflects": "(비난 등을) 비켜 가게 하다", "disavows": "부인하다", "untrue": "사실이 아닌", "hackneyed": "진부한", "unexceptional": "평범한", "document its facts": "사실을 문서로 입증하다", "gauge its veracity": "진실성을 판단하다", "explain its appeal": "매력을 설명하다"}, "src": "verbal219 Q3 · 25/11, 25/7, 25/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v217_q4", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that which of the following statements about traditional ecological theories is true?", "choices": ["They are inadequate for studying the processes and dynamics of cities.", "They explain and predict the consequences of human interactions with nature.", "They exaggerate the negative effects human beings have on ecosystems."], "columns": null, "pid": "v217_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 마지막 문장 'The processes and dynamics within cities ... largely elude understanding based on traditional ecological theories.'\n도시의 과정·역학은 전통 이론으로 이해되지 않는다 = 전통 이론은 도시 연구에 부적절하다 → A.\nB: 인간-자연 상호작용을 설명·예측한다는 내용 없음(오히려 인간을 이론에 잘 못 맞춘다).\nC: 인간의 부정적 영향을 과장한다는 언급 없음.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 '이론'과 '인간'이라는 키워드가 지문에 있어 끌리지만, 지문은 인간이 이론에 '들어맞지 않는다'고 하므로 정반대다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exogenous": "외부에서 생긴, 외인성의", "perturbing": "교란하는", "pristine": "원시 그대로의, 오염되지 않은", "elude": "~을 피하다, (이해가) 안 되다"}, "src": "verbal217 Q4 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v217_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, human beings do not fit neatly into ecological theory for which of the following reasons?", "choices": ["Habitat change in cities happens more quickly than elsewhere.", "Human beings in cities deplete more nutrients than they mobilize.", "Human beings are a global force capable of affecting every ecosystem.", "Human beings create habitats that never before existed.", "Human beings are not viewed as a component of nature."], "columns": null, "pid": "v217_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Human beings ... fail to fit neatly into ecological theory—they are seen as an exogenous, perturbing force in nature.'\n대시(—) 뒤가 '이유': 인간은 자연 '외부의(exogenous)' 교란 요인으로 여겨진다.\n= 인간이 자연의 구성요소로 간주되지 않는다 → E.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(전 지구적 힘)·D(새 서식지 창조)는 지문에 실제로 있는 문장이지만, 이론에 안 맞는 '이유'가 아니라 오히려 'Yet'으로 이어지는 반박(인간이 중요한 생태적 요인임)이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exogenous": "외부에서 기인한", "mobilize": "동원하다, (영양분을) 순환시키다", "deplete": "고갈시키다"}, "src": "verbal217 Q5 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v239_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Since responsibility for content is often _____ in multiauthor papers, it is easy to suppose that such papers may contain more instances of questionable academic practices than do papers by a single author.", "choices": ["ignored", "diluted", "disputed", "weakened", "highlighted", "foregrounded"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Since(원인) → 다저자 논문에 '의심스러운 학술 관행'이 더 많을 것이라 추정하기 쉽다.\n그렇다면 책임이 여러 명에게 나뉘어 '희석/약화'된다는 뜻이어야 한다.\n빈칸 = 부정, '책임이 옅어지다'.\ndiluted(희석된)와 weakened(약해진)가 같은 의미 쌍.\n정답: B (diluted), D (weakened)", "trap": "ignored·disputed도 부정적이라 문장에 대충 맞지만 서로 동의어 짝이 없다. highlighted/foregrounded는 짝은 되지만 의미가 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ignored": "무시된", "diluted": "희석된", "disputed": "논란이 되는", "weakened": "약화된", "highlighted": "강조된", "foregrounded": "전면에 부각된"}, "src": "verbal239 Q9 · 25년 7월, 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v19_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Motorcycle riders in London have discovered an ingenious, albeit __________, way of parking illegally without getting a ticket.", "choices": ["inventive", "unscrupulous", "astute", "dishonest", "impractical", "shrewd"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: ingenious, albeit _____ → albeit(비록 ~이지만)는 양보·대조.\ningenious(기발한)는 긍정이므로 빈칸 = 부정.\n'불법 주차하면서 딱지를 피하는' 방법 → 비양심적/부정직한.\nunscrupulous와 dishonest가 같은 뜻 쌍.\n정답: B (unscrupulous), D (dishonest)", "trap": "inventive·astute·shrewd는 ingenious와 같은 방향(긍정)이라 albeit의 대조를 깨뜨린다. impractical은 부정이지만 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"astute": "영리한, 기민한", "unscrupulous": "비양심적인, 부도덕한", "inventive": "창의적인", "dishonest": "부정직한", "impractical": "비실용적인", "shrewd": "약삭빠른, 영리한"}, "src": "verbal19 Q9"}, {"id": "v223_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The simplicity of Ann Hamilton's sculpture, a single drop of water snaking its way down a vast white wall, _____ the elaborate technical apparatus hidden beneath its surface.", "choices": ["minimized", "undermined", "belied", "contradicted", "conjured", "evoked"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 조각의 '단순함(simplicity)' vs 표면 아래 숨겨진 '정교한 기술 장치(elaborate apparatus)'.\n겉모습이 실체와 반대되는 인상을 준다 → '실상을 감추다/모순되다'.\nbelie = 실제와 다른 인상을 주다, contradict = 모순되다.\n두 단어가 '겉의 단순함이 속의 복잡함과 어긋난다'는 의미를 공유.\n정답: C (belied), D (contradicted)", "trap": "conjured/evoked(떠올리게 하다)는 짝은 맞지만 단순함이 복잡함을 '연상시킨다'는 반대 의미. minimized·undermined는 짝이 되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"minimized": "최소화했다", "undermined": "약화시켰다", "belied": "(실상과) 다른 인상을 주었다, 감추었다", "contradicted": "모순되었다", "conjured": "(마음에) 떠올리게 했다", "evoked": "환기시켰다"}, "src": "verbal223 Q8 · 25년 3월, 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v25_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Sports stars are often _____ figures, regarded as representative of the city or country for which they compete.", "choices": ["totemic", "iconoclastic", "protean", "idealized", "irreverent", "emblematic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 콤마 뒤 'regarded as representative of the city or country' = 빈칸의 정의.\n빈칸 = '대표하는, 상징적인'.\ntotemic(상징물 같은)과 emblematic(상징적인)이 같은 뜻.\n정답: A (totemic), F (emblematic)", "trap": "idealized(이상화된)는 스타에 어울려 보이지만 '대표한다'는 의미가 아니고 짝도 없다. iconoclastic은 icon과 연결되는 착각을 노린 함정(실제 뜻은 '우상 파괴적인').", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"iconoclastic": "인습 타파적인", "protean": "변화무쌍한", "totemic": "상징적인, 토템 같은", "idealized": "이상화된", "irreverent": "불경한", "emblematic": "상징적인, 표상하는"}, "src": "verbal25 Q8"}, {"id": "v217_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author would most likely agree with which of the following statements about political acts performed by eighteenth-century women?", "choices": ["They had little influence on the outcome of elections.", "They were aimed largely at the expansion of the electorate.", "They probably were discouraged by men with political aspirations.", "They represented a new development in British society.", "They were sometimes perceived as being negative."], "columns": null, "pid": "v217_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Given the widespread hostility to “public” women in the eighteenth century, was female political activity quite so unproblematic...?' 및 'the nitpicking contemporary attacks on ... upper-class influence peddling'.\n당시 여성의 정치 활동은 적대·공격의 대상이기도 했다 = 때때로 부정적으로 인식되었다 → E.\nD는 'continuity and normalcy' 및 'long before the eighteenth' 와 모순.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(정치적 야심가인 남성들이 막았다)는 '적대'라는 분위기에 끌리지만, 남성 정치인이 막았다는 구체적 내용은 없고 오히려 귀족 여성은 남편의 대리인 역할을 기대받았다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"seditious": "선동적인", "aberrant": "일탈적인", "canvass": "선거운동하다, 유세하다", "patronage": "후원, 정치적 임명권", "machinations": "음모, 책략"}, "src": "verbal217 Q10 · 24/6, 24/3, 24/1, 23/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v217_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author suggested which of the following about the “expansion of the electorate to include women” in the eighteenth-century Britain?", "choices": ["It might have reduced women’s incentives to engage in such political activities as boycotts and riots.", "It might have reduced the political power of some people who had exerted great influence.", "It would have been unlikely to overturn the aristocracy’s political control of the country.", "It would likely have extended the vote only to aristocratic women.", "It was not an issue addressed by men who were engaged in politics."], "columns": null, "pid": "v217_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Patrician women had so much far-reaching political influence ... that they actually stood to lose by expansion of the electorate to include women.'\n막강한 영향력을 가진 귀족 여성들이 선거권 확대로 오히려 잃을 것이 있었다.\n= 큰 영향력을 행사하던 일부 사람들의 정치적 힘을 줄였을 수 있다 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "C(귀족의 정치 지배를 뒤집지 못했을 것)는 귀족과 관련되어 끌리지만, 지문은 귀족 여성의 '손실'을 말할 뿐 귀족 전체의 지배 유지 여부는 다루지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "expansion of the electorate to include women", "glosses": {"patrician": "귀족의", "electorate": "유권자 (전체)", "stood to lose": "잃을 처지였다", "far-reaching": "광범위한"}, "src": "verbal217 Q11 · 24/6, 24/3, 24/1, 23/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v217_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following statements best describes the function of the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["It reinterprets an explanation originated by historians who contributed to the “new historiography”.", "It questions the accuracy of evidence presented in the service of the “new historiography”.", "It identifies issues that have been overlooked by the “new historiography”.", "It highlights claims of the “new historiography” that have been neglected.", "It defends the “new historiography” against an unwarranted criticism."], "columns": null, "pid": "v217_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "하이라이트 문장: Anna Clark는 엘리트 정치 활동 찬양이 ① 평범한 여성들의 처지, ② 당시 상류층 영향력 행사에 대한 공격을 '무시한다(neglects)'고 지적.\n앞 문장 'criticized for its focus on ... high politics and its inattention to ideology'의 연장선 → 새 역사학이 간과한 문제들을 제시.\n= 'new historiography'가 간과한 쟁점을 확인한다 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "D는 'neglected'라는 단어로 유혹하지만, 방치된 것은 새 역사학의 '주장'이 아니라 새 역사학이 '놓친 쟁점'이다(주체가 뒤바뀜). E는 비판을 방어한다는 정반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"historiography": "역사 서술, 사학", "neglects": "등한시하다", "nitpicking": "트집 잡는", "influence peddling": "영향력 행사(이권 거래)"}, "src": "verbal217 Q12 · 24/6, 24/3, 24/1, 23/5 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v24_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "As British biochemist Joseph Needham became immersed in the study of China's history, he began to envision science as __________ endeavor, noting that \"the peoples of the whole world have all made their contributions.\"", "choices": ["an ecumenical", "a competitive", "a redemptive", "a misunderstood", "an underappreciated"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: noting that \"the peoples of the whole world have all made their contributions\" → 빈칸의 근거.\n전 세계 모든 민족이 기여한 노력 = 보편적·전 세계적인.\n빈칸 = '보편적인, 전 세계를 아우르는'.\necumenical(보편적인, 세계적인)이 정확.\n정답: A (an ecumenical)", "trap": "underappreciated는 '중국 과학의 공헌이 과소평가되었다'는 배경지식에 끌리지만, 인용문은 '모두가 기여했다'는 보편성을 말한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ecumenical": "보편적인", "an ecumenical": "보편적인, 세계 전체의", "a competitive": "경쟁적인", "a redemptive": "구원의, 속죄의", "a misunderstood": "오해받는", "an underappreciated": "과소평가된"}, "src": "verbal24 Q1"}, {"id": "v210_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Mowry believes that effective politics demands a synthesis of the practical and the visionary. He has never had much trouble coming up with (i) _____. But these days, he also thinks he has become better at relating that larger picture directly to (ii) _____ policies.", "choices": null, "columns": [["effective political strategies", "grand political ideas", "a dispassionate reading of the political mood"], ["inspired", "workable", "idealistic"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "전제: 효과적인 정치 = 실용적인 것(practical)과 비전적인 것(visionary)의 종합.\n(i) 'He has never had much trouble coming up with ___' + 다음 문장 'that larger picture' → (i)은 큰 그림 = visionary → grand political ideas.\n(ii) But also: 그 큰 그림을 '실용적' 정책에 연결 → workable.\n정답: B (grand political ideas), E (workable)", "trap": "(ii)의 inspired·idealistic은 visionary 쪽 단어라 '실용' 쪽 짝이 되지 못한다. (i)의 effective political strategies는 practical 쪽이라 'larger picture'와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"effective political strategies": "효과적인 정치 전략", "grand political ideas": "원대한 정치적 구상", "a dispassionate reading of the political mood": "정치 분위기에 대한 냉정한 판단", "inspired": "영감을 받은, 탁월한", "workable": "실행 가능한", "idealistic": "이상주의적인"}, "src": "verbal210 Q2 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "In spite of its rather (i) _____ subject matter, Brinkley's is (ii) _____ work, one that is moderated by grace and restraint and tempered by an economy that in no way suggests timidity.", "choices": null, "columns": [["coarse", "sophisticated", "endearing"], ["an indifferent", "a subtle", "an upsetting"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 근거: 'moderated by grace and restraint ... an economy that in no way suggests timidity' → 우아·절제·간결 = subtle(미묘한, 섬세한).\n(i) In spite of: 소재와 작품 성격이 대조 → 섬세한 작품과 반대되는 '거친' 소재 → coarse.\n정답: A (coarse), E (a subtle)", "trap": "(i)의 sophisticated는 작품 분위기와 같은 방향이라 In spite of 대조를 깨뜨린다. (ii)의 an indifferent는 restraint를 '무관심'으로 오해하게 만드는 함정.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"grace and restraint": "우아함과 절제미", "in no way": "결코 ~하지 않는", "coarse": "거친, 조잡한", "sophisticated": "세련된", "endearing": "사랑스러운", "an indifferent": "무관심한, 그저 그런", "a subtle": "미묘한, 섬세한", "an upsetting": "속상하게 하는"}, "src": "verbal232 Q2 · 24년 4월, 23년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v2_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Among chess aficionados, there have been many doomsday scenarios about people (i) _____ the game as a result of the superiority of computer chess programs over human players. Others have replied to this with variations on the theme of how we still hold footraces despite cars going much faster, but this analogy is (ii) _____ since cars do not help humans run faster while chess computers undoubtedly have an effect on the (iii) _____ of human chess.", "choices": null, "columns": [["losing interest in", "redoubling their efforts at", "struggling to master"], ["ineluctable", "transparent", "spurious"], ["popularity", "quality", "accessibility"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) doomsday scenarios(파멸 시나리오) + 컴퓨터가 인간보다 우월 → 사람들이 체스에 '흥미를 잃는다' → losing interest in.\n(ii) but this analogy is ___ since ~ : 비유가 성립하지 않는 이유가 이어짐 → spurious(그릇된).\n(iii) 차는 사람이 더 빨리 달리게 돕지 않지만, 체스 컴퓨터는 인간 체스의 '실력/수준'에 영향 → quality(빨리 달리기=실력과 대응).\n정답: A, F (spurious), H (quality)", "trap": "(iii)의 popularity는 (i)의 '흥미 상실'과 연결되어 끌리지만, since 절의 대응은 '달리기 속도(실력)'이므로 quality가 맞다. (ii)의 transparent는 부정 맥락에 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"aficionados": "광도", "ineluctable": "피할 수 없는", "spurious": "그릇된, 겉만 그럴듯한", "losing interest in": "~에 흥미를 잃는", "redoubling their efforts at": "~에 노력을 배가하는", "struggling to master": "숙달하려 애쓰는", "transparent": "명백한, 투명한", "popularity": "인기", "quality": "질, 수준", "accessibility": "접근성"}, "src": "verbal2 Q4"}, {"id": "v222_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions divorce rates in order to", "choices": ["suggest one possible reason for the number of unmarried women in the workplace", "Show one effect of the broadening of the definition of women's roles during the interwar period", "Identify a likely cause for the growing number of middle-class women in the workplace"], "columns": null, "pid": "v222_p5", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Divorce rates increased as work patterns and women's expectations of marriage changed.'\n이혼율 증가는 일하는 방식·결혼에 대한 기대 변화의 '결과'로 제시된다.\n이는 첫 문장의 'broadening of the definition of women's roles'의 한 효과 → B.\nA: 미혼 여성 수의 원인으로 제시되지 않음. C: 이혼율은 원인이 아니라 결과.\n정답: B", "trap": "C는 이혼율과 취업을 연결하지만 인과 방향이 뒤바뀌었다(지문은 취업 패턴 변화 → 이혼율 증가).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Divorce rates", "glosses": {"interwar": "양차 대전 사이의", "momentum": "기세, 추진력", "reasserting": "재천명하다, 다시 주장하다"}, "src": "verbal222 Q5 · 24/10, 24/4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v222_q6", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred from the passage about American women in the workplace during the interwar period?", "choices": ["Most middle-class women in the workplace were unmarried", "Most working-class women in the workplace were married", "Working-class women were active in the workplace from the beginning of the period"], "columns": null, "pid": "v222_p5", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Increasing numbers of middle-class women joined their working-class contemporaries in the workplace'\n중산층 여성이 이미 일터에 있던 노동계층 여성들에 '합류'했다 → 노동계층 여성은 기간 초부터 일하고 있었다 → C.\nB: 노동계층 여성의 결혼 여부에 대한 정보 없음.\nA: 'a small but growing minority of them continued working after marriage'는 중산층 여성 중 결혼 후에도 일한 비율을 말할 뿐, 일터의 중산층 여성 대다수가 미혼이었다고 확정하기엔 근거가 부족.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 'small minority ... after marriage'에서 쉽게 추론될 것 같아 가장 유혹적이지만, 지문이 말하는 비율의 기준(전체 중산층 여성인지, 일하는 여성인지)이 불분명해 확정할 수 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"contemporaries": "동시대 사람들", "minority": "소수", "interwar": "양차 대전 사이의"}, "src": "verbal222 Q6 · 24/10, 24/4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v226_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["argue that intellectual property policies are often unwarranted", "show how a particular criterion can be used to evaluate an intellectual property policy", "summarize the costs and benefits of introducing intellectual property policies", "approve the reasoning that was used to justify a particular intellectual property policy", "challenge a claim that the benefits of intellectual property policies outweigh the costs"], "columns": null, "pid": "v226_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 지적재산권 정책은 비용-편익(cost-benefit)으로 평가해야 한다는 기준 제시.\n이후 1998년 저작권 연장 사례에 그 기준을 적용: 비용(책값 상승)은 있고 편익(저자 동기 부여)은 없다 → 부당.\n= 특정 기준이 특정 정책 평가에 어떻게 쓰이는지 보여준다 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 '지적재산권 정책이 흔히(often) 부당하다'로 일반화가 지나치다. 지문은 한 가지 사례만 비판한다. E는 누군가의 '편익>비용' 주장을 반박하는 구조가 지문에 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"countervailing": "상쇄하는", "retroactively": "소급하여", "unwarranted": "부당한, 정당화되지 않는", "royalties": "인세, 저작권료"}, "src": "verbal226 Q7 · 25/1, 24/6, 23/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v226_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions “royalties” primarily in order to identify", "choices": ["a benefit that is likely to motivate authors", "a way in which publishers compete with one another", "a factor that contributes to a negative effect of copyright", "a reason underlying Congress, actions regarding copyright", "an unintended effect of extending the term of copyright"], "columns": null, "pid": "v226_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'A book's price is higher under copyright because the publisher continues to owe royalties to the author's heirs...'\n인세는 책값 상승의 원인 → 책값 상승은 'Book buyers are harmed'라는 저작권의 부정적 효과.\n= 저작권의 부정적 효과에 기여하는 요인 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(저자에게 동기를 주는 편익)는 인세가 저자 측 수입이라 끌리지만, 지문은 사후 50년 넘어 오는 수입은 동기가 되지 않는다고 하므로 반대. E는 '의도치 않은' 효과라는 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "royalties", "glosses": {"royalties": "인세, 저작권 사용료", "heirs": "상속인", "countervailing": "상쇄하는"}, "src": "verbal226 Q8 · 25/1, 24/6, 23/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v226_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that which of the following assumptions underlies the statement in the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["Concern for their heirs is not a factor that motivates authors to publish.", "Authors are motivated by factors other than the prospect of financial gain.", "Sales of a book are unlikely to change after its author's death.", "Publishers tend to act in their own best interest rather than in the author's.", "The earnings of most authors tend to decline over time."], "columns": null, "pid": "v226_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "하이라이트 문장: 사후 50년 이후의 수입 전망은 저자에게 동기가 되지 않는다.\n그런데 그 수입은 상속인(heirs)에게 간다. 이 주장이 성립하려면 '상속인을 위한 마음'이 저자 동기가 아니어야 한다.\n= 숨은 가정: 상속인에 대한 관심은 저자의 출판 동기가 아니다 → A.\n(부정 테스트: 저자가 상속인을 위해 쓴다면 연장된 저작권도 동기가 되어 주장이 무너짐)\n정답: A", "trap": "B(금전 외 요인으로 동기 부여)는 그럴듯하지만, 저자는 금전에 동기 부여될 수 있다고 해도 주장은 성립한다. 핵심은 '사후 수입=상속인 몫'이라는 점이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incentive": "유인, 동기", "heirs": "상속인", "underlies": "~의 기저에 있다"}, "src": "verbal226 Q9 · 25/1, 24/6, 23/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v28_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author's point is not that people should be _____ science; he is careful to point out that what science is discovering about humans, for example, is certainly important and worthy of careful consideration.", "choices": ["skeptical toward", "dismissive of", "ignorant of", "zealous regarding", "scornful of", "passionate about"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 'not that people should be ___ science; ... science is certainly important and worthy of careful consideration.'\n세미콜론 뒤에서 저자는 과학이 중요하고 진지하게 고려할 가치가 있다고 강조 → 빈칸은 그 반대 태도.\n빈칸 = 부정, '과학을 무시/경시하는'.\ndismissive of와 scornful of가 같은 의미.\n정답: B (dismissive of), E (scornful of)", "trap": "skeptical toward(회의적인)도 부정이지만 '중요성'을 부정하는 것과 의미가 다르고 짝이 없다. zealous/passionate는 짝이지만 방향이 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dismissive of": "~을 무시하는, 일축하는", "ignorant of": "~을 모르는", "scornful of": "~을 경멸하는", "skeptical toward": "~에 회의적인", "zealous regarding": "~에 열성적인", "passionate about": "~에 열정적인"}, "src": "verbal28 Q8"}, {"id": "v10_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Many people perceive an unearned grandiosity at work in the news business, and given that perception, it should be no surprise that they have such a strong _____ for the business.", "choices": ["preference", "passion", "esteem", "disdain", "fervor", "contempt"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: unearned grandiosity(받을 자격 없는 거드름)를 느낀다 → given that perception, 놀랍지 않다.\n그렇다면 사람들은 언론에 대해 강한 '경멸'을 가질 것.\n빈칸 = 부정.\ndisdain과 contempt가 같은 뜻.\n정답: D (disdain), F (contempt)", "trap": "passion/fervor는 짝이 되지만 긍정 방향. 'strong ___ for'라는 표현이 preference·passion과 잘 어울려 보이는 것이 함정.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unearned grandiosity": "부당한 거드름/과장", "preference": "선호", "passion": "열정", "esteem": "존경", "disdain": "경멸", "fervor": "열렬함", "contempt": "경멸"}, "src": "verbal10 Q9"}, {"id": "v34_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The current _____ of repackaged music under Miles Davis’ name might prompt any reasonable person to conclude that the recording vault has been plundered bare.", "choices": ["glut", "revival", "hodgepodge", "surfeit", "modicum", "dearth"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'the recording vault has been plundered bare'(음반 보관고가 싹 털렸다)고 결론 내릴 정도.\n→ 재포장 음반이 '넘쳐난다'.\n빈칸 = '과잉, 과다'.\nglut과 surfeit가 같은 뜻.\n정답: A (glut), D (surfeit)", "trap": "revival(부활)은 '재포장'에 어울려 보이지만 '털렸다'고 할 만큼의 양을 의미하지 않고 짝도 없다. modicum·dearth는 '소량/부족'으로 반대.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"glut": "과잉, 공급 과다", "revival": "부활, 재유행", "hodgepodge": "뒤죽박죽", "surfeit": "과다, 과잉", "modicum": "소량", "dearth": "부족, 결핍"}, "src": "verbal34 Q8"}, {"id": "v234_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following most logically completes the argument?", "choices": ["archaeologists cannot determine the actual identity of the individual portrayed just from the likeness that appears on the coins", "it cannot be established with certainty that Carthagian artists were on the whole less skillful at portraying human face than artists of other cultures", "none of the other designs of Carthagian coins that have been discovered features a face with a mole on it", "in ancient times it was quite common for the money circulated in a city or country to include coins that originated in other jurisdictions", "the relatively soft metal used for Carthagian coin molds sometimes resulted in the production of series of coins with unintended bumps"], "columns": null, "pid": "v234_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론(고고학자): 동전의 '점'은 일반화된 얼굴에 넣지 않을 세부 → 실제 인물을 묘사한 것.\n저자는 이 결론이 부당하다고 함 → 점이 '의도된 묘사'가 아닐 수 있음을 보여야 한다.\nE: 무른 주형 금속 때문에 의도치 않은 돌기가 생겼다 → 점이 예술가의 선택이 아닌 제조상 결함일 수 있다 → 대안 설명.\n정답: E", "trap": "A(실제 신원은 알 수 없다)는 그럴듯하지만, 결론은 '누구인지'가 아니라 '실제 인물인지 아닌지'이므로 반박이 되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hoard": "(숨겨 둔) 비축물, 무더기", "idealized": "이상화된", "unwarranted": "부당한", "jurisdictions": "관할 구역"}, "src": "verbal234 Q13 · 24년 4월, 23년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v12_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following typically distinguishes soil nourished exclusively by N-P-K fertilizers from unfertilized soils?", "choices": ["Lower average yields", "Higher earthworm populations", "Slower crop growth", "Less microbial activity", "Increased resistance to pests"], "columns": null, "pid": "v12_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Chemical fertilizers such as N-P-K depress this activity' – this activity = 'biological activity provided by ... soil microbes, earthworms, and Mycorrhizal fungi'.\nN-P-K 비료만 쓴 토양은 미생물 활동이 줄어든다 → D.\nB(지렁이 증가)·E(해충 저항 증가)는 정반대.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(수확량 감소)·C(성장 속도 저하)는 비료의 부정적 효과로 그럴듯하지만 지문에 언급이 없다(오히려 육종이 수확량을 위해 선택됨).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"macronutrients": "다량 영양소", "agronomists": "농학자", "depress": "억제하다, 저하시키다", "Mycorrhizal fungi": "균근균"}, "src": "verbal12 Q12"}, {"id": "v12_q13", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage would most likely agree that the widespread use of N-P-K fertilizers", "choices": ["has encouraged plant breeders to select for yield rather than other characteristics", "caused early agronomists to ignore the importance of biological activity in soils", "has diverted attention away from the nutritional value of crops", "spurred attempts to reproduce the effect of microbial activity in the soil", "has resulted in plants that are less hardy"], "columns": null, "pid": "v12_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Chemical fertilizers ... depress this activity, increasing plants' vulnerability to pests and diseases.'\n해충·질병에 취약해짐 = 덜 강건한(less hardy) 식물 → E.\nA: 육종가의 수확량 선택은 영양 감소의 '다른 설명'일 뿐, 비료 사용이 원인이라는 말은 없음.\nB: 농학자들의 간과가 비료 사용 때문이라는 인과는 없음.\n정답: E", "trap": "B는 지문에 'overlooked the importance of biological activity'가 있어 끌리지만, 비료 사용이 그 간과를 '야기했다'는 인과가 없다(순서상 간과가 먼저).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"vulnerability": "취약성", "hardy": "강건한, 내한성이 있는", "agronomists": "농학자", "spurred": "자극했다, 촉진했다"}, "src": "verbal12 Q13"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.2 / S2 2.2"}, {"set": 14, "sections": [[{"id": "v207_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "To write convincing fiction about the tedium of ordinary life may be one of the hardest challenges facing a novelist, who must find a way to engage the reader despite a focus on _____ events.", "choices": ["distressing", "dubious", "quotidian", "unwonted", "nebulous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'the tedium of ordinary life'(평범한 삶의 지루함) + 'despite a focus on ___ events'.\n독자를 사로잡기 어려운 이유 = 다루는 사건이 평범하고 일상적이라서.\n빈칸 = '일상적인'.\nquotidian(일상의, 평범한)이 정확.\n정답: C (quotidian)", "trap": "unwonted(이례적인)는 wonted(익숙한)와 혼동시키는 함정으로, 실제로는 '평범함'의 반대다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"distressing": "괴로운", "dubious": "의심스러운", "quotidian": "일상적인, 평범한", "unwonted": "이례적인, 보기 드문", "nebulous": "모호한"}, "src": "verbal207 Q1 · 25/9, 24/12, 24/11, 24/1, 23/10, 22/8, 22/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v223_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "All of these writers rely on (i) _____ and (ii) _____ to make their argument; they take a single idea and illustrate it with endless, rather overblown examples while avoiding any genuinely nuanced analysis.", "choices": null, "columns": [["fabrication", "equivocation", "simplification"], ["exaggeration", "speculation", "prevarication"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론 뒤가 앞을 설명.\n'take a single idea' + 'avoiding any genuinely nuanced analysis' → 복잡한 걸 단일 아이디어로 축소 → (i) simplification.\n'endless, rather overblown examples' → 과장 → (ii) exaggeration.\n정답: C (simplification), D (exaggeration)", "trap": "(ii)의 prevarication(얼버무림)·(i)의 equivocation(모호한 말)·fabrication(날조)은 부정적 수사법이라 끌리지만, 지문은 거짓말이 아닌 '축소'와 '과장'을 묘사한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"fabrication": "날조", "equivocation": "얼버무림, 모호한 말", "simplification": "단순화", "exaggeration": "과장", "speculation": "추측", "prevarication": "얼버무림, 발뺌"}, "src": "verbal223 Q2 · 24년 11월, 23년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v29_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "During the Harlem Renaissance, Alain Locke (i) _____ the first flourishing of a self-consciously racial art movement in America and was widely credited with providing the philosophical basis for its emergence. His importance as a critic of African America art and as an art theorist is (ii) _____ if controversial, yet he has received (iii) _____ attention for his unique insight into the broad forces that shaped American modernism and cultural nationalism in the visual arts.", "choices": null, "columns": [["forestalled", "presided over", "seethed over"], ["undisputed", "misleading", "questionable"], ["undeserved", "meticulous", "insufficient"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'widely credited with providing the philosophical basis for its emergence' → 그 운동을 이끌었다 → presided over.\n(ii) '___ if controversial' : if = 비록 ~일지라도(양보) → 논란은 있지만 중요성은 '확실한' → undisputed.\n(iii) yet: 중요성은 확실하지만 그의 독특한 통찰은 '부족한' 관심을 받았다 → insufficient.\n정답: B (presided over), D (undisputed), I (insufficient)", "trap": "(ii)의 questionable은 controversial과 같은 방향이라 if(양보)의 대조를 깨뜨린다. (iii)의 undeserved는 '부당한 관심'이라 yet 대조와 그의 '독특한 통찰'과 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"presided over": "주도했다, 이끌었다", "forestalled": "미연에 막았다", "seethed over": "~에 분노로 들끓었다", "undisputed": "논란의 여지가 없는", "misleading": "오해를 불러일으키는", "questionable": "의심스러운", "undeserved": "부당한, 받을 자격 없는", "meticulous": "꼼꼼한", "insufficient": "불충분한"}, "src": "verbal29 Q3"}, {"id": "v233_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage implies which of the following about the political importance of the type of urban water management system described in the passage?", "choices": ["Because the system was centralized, it allowed political control over a widely scattered population.", "The knowledge required to design and maintain the system became the pretext for Maya elites' political authority.", "By selectively limiting access to water, Maya elites used the system to curb challenges to their authority.", "The system is not sufficient to explain the sources of centralized political power in all parts of the Maya region.", "The system’s continued maintenance required political authorities to exert control over an increasing proportion of economic resources."], "columns": null, "pid": "v233_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Such an argument is plausible; however, it is less useful for understanding ... other, water-rich parts of the Maya region.'\n물 통제가 정치권력의 원천이라는 주장은 물이 풍부한 다른 지역에는 덜 유용 → 이 시스템만으로 모든 지역의 중앙 권력을 설명할 수 없다 → D.\n정답: D", "trap": "C(물 접근을 선택적으로 제한해 도전을 억눌렀다)는 'controlled water access'와 비슷해 보이지만 지문은 그런 구체적 사용 방식을 말하지 않으며, '일부 학자'의 주장일 뿐이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"perennial": "연중 지속되는", "plausible": "그럴듯한", "sociopolitical": "사회정치적인", "pretext": "구실"}, "src": "verbal233 Q4 · 24/10, 24/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v233_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true of the water management systems in the central and southern Maya Lowlands?", "choices": ["They were implemented in part because of the prevailing pattern of rainfall.", "They were an integral part of lowland cities' architecture.", "They were needed because of insufficient resources such as ponds, rivers, and lakes in the lowlands."], "columns": null, "pid": "v233_p1", "answer": "ABC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'due to the scarcity of perennial surface water and the seasonal availability of rainfall'.\nA: 계절적인 강우 패턴 때문 → 맞음.\nC: 연중 지표수(연못·강·호수) 부족 때문 → 맞음.\nB: 'the urban architecture of some cities was used to divert rainfall runoff' → 도시 건축 자체가 물 관리 시스템의 일부 → 맞음.\n정답: A, B, C", "trap": "B는 지문이 'some cities'라고 하여 일반화처럼 보여 빼기 쉽지만, 저지대 물 관리 시스템이 도시 건축과 통합되어 있었다는 지문 내용과 일치한다. C의 'ponds, rivers, and lakes'는 'perennial surface water'의 바꿔 말하기.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"perennial": "연중 지속되는", "reservoirs": "저수지", "runoff": "(빗물 등의) 유출수", "gravity-fed": "중력식의"}, "src": "verbal233 Q5 · 24/10, 24/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v207_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the early twentieth century, some _____ the environmental benefits of a motor designed to harness the power of the ocean's waves, pointing out that the motor did not create the smoke or soot associated with burning oil.", "choices": ["apprehended", "countenanced", "extolled", "predicted", "exaggerated", "touted"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: pointing out that the motor did not create the smoke or soot → 환경적 이점을 긍정적으로 강조.\n빈칸 = 긍정, '칭찬하다, 홍보하다'.\nextolled(극찬했다)와 touted(선전했다)가 같은 의미.\n정답: C (extolled), F (touted)", "trap": "exaggerated(과장했다)는 '이점을 내세운다'는 맥락에 맞아 보이지만 부정적 함의가 있고 짝이 없다. predicted도 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"apprehended": "체포했다, 이해했다", "countenanced": "묵인했다, 승인했다", "extolled": "극찬했다", "predicted": "예측했다", "exaggerated": "과장했다", "touted": "선전했다, 치켜세웠다"}, "src": "verbal207 Q9 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v7_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The decision to rely on mechanical biological treatment to process the two million tons of waste that the region produces annually was _____ to experts, who had long been aware that this approach had several shortcomings.", "choices": ["alarming", "infuriating", "perplexing", "humiliating", "baffling", "surprising"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'experts, who had long been aware that this approach had several shortcomings' → 단점을 알던 전문가들에게 그 결정은 이해하기 어려움.\n빈칸 = '당혹스러운, 이해 안 되는'.\nperplexing과 baffling이 같은 뜻.\n정답: C (perplexing), E (baffling)", "trap": "surprising·alarming도 문맥에 맞아 보이지만 짝이 없다. 특히 '오래전부터 단점을 알았다'면 '놀라운' 것보다 '왜 그런 결정을?'이라는 당혹감이 핵심.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"alarming": "걱정스러운", "infuriating": "격분하게 하는", "perplexing": "당혹스러운", "humiliating": "굴욕적인", "baffling": "이해할 수 없는, 당혹스러운", "surprising": "놀라운"}, "src": "verbal7 Q8"}, {"id": "v207_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Methane that is oxidized to diamond is thought to originate from reduced fluids in Earth's upper mantle; the ultimate origin of carbon in diamonds, however, is _____.", "choices": ["obscure", "mysterious", "contentious", "crucial", "forgotten", "intriguing"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: however → 대조.\n앞: 메탄의 기원은 '~로 생각된다'(어느 정도 알려짐) vs 뒤: 탄소의 궁극적 기원은 ___ → 잘 알려지지 않음.\n빈칸 = '불분명한, 알 수 없는'.\nobscure와 mysterious가 같은 뜻.\n정답: A (obscure), B (mysterious)", "trap": "contentious(논쟁적인)도 '불확실'과 비슷해 보이지만 '논쟁'이 있다는 근거가 없고 짝이 없다. intriguing은 흥미롭다는 뜻일 뿐.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"obscure": "불분명한", "mysterious": "불가사의한", "contentious": "논쟁을 불러일으키는", "crucial": "결정적인", "forgotten": "잊혀진", "intriguing": "흥미로운"}, "src": "verbal207 Q8 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v23_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Meteorology is one of the few fields of applied science that demands prediction; since prediction involves considerable uncertainty and uncertainty is __________ scientists, meteorology will continue to exist in a fraught intellectual space.", "choices": ["mysterious to", "anathema to", "discredited by", "pivotal for", "repellent to", "familiar to"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 기상학은 예측 → 불확실성이 큼 → 그래서 'fraught intellectual space'(긴장된 지적 공간)에 있다.\n그러려면 불확실성이 과학자들에게 '혐오스러운' 것이어야 한다.\n빈칸 = 부정, '아주 싫어하는'.\nanathema to와 repellent to가 같은 의미.\n정답: B (anathema to), E (repellent to)", "trap": "mysterious to·discredited by도 부정적이지만 짝이 없다. familiar to는 오히려 긴장을 해소하는 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"mysterious to": "~에게 불가사의한", "anathema to": "~가 몹시 싫어하는 것", "discredited by": "~에 의해 신빙성을 잃은", "pivotal for": "~에 중추적인", "repellent to": "~에게 혐오감을 주는", "familiar to": "~에게 익숙한"}, "src": "verbal23 Q8"}, {"id": "v215_q10", "type": "RC_select", "blanks": null, "stem": "Select the sentence that presents an illustration of Clements' superorganism concept.", "choices": null, "columns": null, "pid": "v215_p2", "answer": "SENTENCE", "answer_sentence": "Thus, forests, for example, if undisturbed by humans, will evolve toward a stable community of old-growth trees.", "explanation": "Clements의 superorganism 개념: 식물 공동체가 시간에 따라 예측 가능한 단계를 거쳐 'climax' 형태로 발달.\n'Thus, forests, for example, ...' 문장이 숲이라는 구체적 예시(for example)로 이를 보여준다.\n다른 문장들은 개념의 정의이거나 반론(Gleason, botanists).\n정답: Thus, forests, for example, if undisturbed by humans, will evolve toward a stable community of old-growth trees.", "trap": "'while pine forests and hardwood forests might appear to constitute two distinct superorganisms' 문장도 예시처럼 보이지만, 이는 개념을 반박하는 비판의 일부다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"superorganisms": "초유기체", "succession": "(생태) 천이", "climax": "극상", "imperceptibly": "감지할 수 없을 만큼"}, "src": "verbal215 Q10 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v215_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following statements about Clements' theory is true?", "choices": ["The reason for its initial rejection by most scientists was that it challenged established scientific views.", "It received its widest support long after its inception.", "It heightened popular awareness of certain threats to the environment.", "It has influenced the views of nature held by many nonscientists.", "It can be usefully applied to forests but not to other kinds of plant communities."], "columns": null, "pid": "v215_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: '...has continued to influence popular conceptions of nature.'\n대중의 자연관에 계속 영향 = 많은 비과학자들의 자연관에 영향 → D.\nA: 초기 반대 이유가 기존 견해에 도전했기 때문이라는 내용 없음.\nB·C·E: 지문 근거 없음.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 'challenged by scientists from its inception'에 끌리지만, 지문은 반대 이유가 '기존 견해에 도전해서'라고 하지 않으며 '대부분의' 과학자라는 말도 없다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inception": "시작, 발단", "popular conceptions": "대중적 인식", "succession": "천이"}, "src": "verbal215 Q11 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v215_q12", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage makes which of the following claims about the scientific reaction to Clements' theory?", "choices": ["Some scientists began to dispute the theory as soon as it was proposed.", "Scientists in the late twentieth century had mostly come to accept the theory.", "Some early-twentieth-century scientists accepted Clements' view of succession but challenged his view of superorganisms."], "columns": null, "pid": "v215_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'while challenged by scientists from its inception' 및 'many botanists immediately pointed out...'\nA: 제안 직후부터 일부 과학자가 반박 → 맞음.\nB: 20세기 후반 과학자 대다수가 수용했다는 내용 없음.\nC: Gleason은 오히려 천이(succession) 개념도 비판(양방향 진행) → 틀림.\n정답: A", "trap": "C는 botanists가 superorganism의 경계를 비판한 부분에 끌리지만, 천이를 '받아들였다'는 진술이 없고 Gleason은 천이도 비판했다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inception": "시작", "imperceptibly": "알아차릴 수 없게", "succession": "천이"}, "src": "verbal215 Q12 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v234_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Archaeopteryx had feathers on its hind limbs that helped stabilize it and acted as air brakes, allowing the otherwise _____ creature to turn more adeptly and fly steadily.", "choices": ["docile", "ungainly", "unpredictable", "torpid", "reckless"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'allowing the otherwise ___ creature to turn more adeptly and fly steadily.'\notherwise(그렇지 않았다면) → 깃털이 없었다면 민첩하지 못했을 동물.\n빈칸 = adeptly(능숙하게)·steadily의 반대, '어설픈, 둔한'.\nungainly(어색한, 볼품없는)가 정확.\n정답: B (ungainly)", "trap": "torpid(무기력한)·unpredictable도 부정적이지만, '능숙하게 회전하고 안정적으로 난다'의 반대는 '움직임이 서툰'이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ungainly": "어설픈, 동작이 서툰", "torpid": "무기력한, 휴면 상태의", "docile": "온순한", "unpredictable": "예측할 수 없는", "reckless": "무모한"}, "src": "verbal234 Q1 · 25/7, 25/6, 25/4, 23/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v32_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "It was fine to be (i) _____ in the old days when papers were still not losing readers and advertisement revenue was not tough to come by, but many editors today are uneasy about bludgeoning their readers with the inherently (ii) _____ work of cartoonists.", "choices": null, "columns": [["comprehensive", "opinionated", "profligate"], ["unbalanced", "flawed", "vacuous"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 'bludgeoning their readers'(독자를 몽둥이로 때리듯) + 만평가의 작업은 'inherently' ___ → 본질적으로 편향된 → unbalanced.\n(i) 예전엔 ___해도 괜찮았다 → 만평처럼 한쪽 입장을 강하게 내세우는 것 → opinionated.\n두 빈칸이 '편향/강한 주장'으로 연결.\n정답: B (opinionated), D (unbalanced)", "trap": "(i)의 profligate(낭비하는)는 '광고 수입이 넉넉했던 시절'과 연결되어 끌리지만, 뒤 내용은 돈이 아니라 만평의 성격(편향)에 관한 것이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"opinionated": "독선적인, 자기주장이 강한", "profligate": "낭비하는, 방탕한", "vacuous": "공허한, 멍청한", "comprehensive": "포괄적인", "unbalanced": "편향된, 불균형한", "flawed": "결함이 있는"}, "src": "verbal32 Q2"}, {"id": "v204_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The company's chief executive is (i) _____ the desire to postpone action until a consensus has been reached. Instead she makes a brief for instinctive decision making, treating extensive deliberation as something to (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["intrigued by", "comfortable with", "skeptical of"], ["shun", "implement", "put off"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Instead → 앞과 반대.\n'she makes a brief for instinctive decision making'(직관적 결정을 옹호) → 합의까지 미루려는 욕구에 대해 (i) 회의적 → skeptical of.\n(ii) 긴 숙고를 '피해야 할' 것으로 여김 → shun.\n정답: C (skeptical of), D (shun)", "trap": "(ii)의 put off(미루다)는 '연기'와 연결되어 끌리지만, 숙고를 '미룬다'는 말은 숙고를 결국 한다는 뜻이 되어 직관적 결정 옹호와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"intrigued by": "~에 흥미를 느끼는", "comfortable with": "~을 편하게 여기는", "skeptical of": "~에 회의적인", "shun": "피하다", "implement": "실행하다", "put off": "미루다"}, "src": "verbal204 Q2 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The flood of new candidates, including newcomers, party veterans, and the first female candidate, is a startling (i) _____ Japan's (ii) _____ political successions. The crowded field means that the selection of the new prime minister, instead of being the customary (iii) _____, backroom affair, has become a source of intense public excitement.", "choices": null, "columns": [["abbreviation of", "illustration of", "departure from"], ["scripted", "chaotic", "prolonged"], ["conspicuous", "celebrated", "dry"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CDI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(iii) 'instead of being the customary ___, backroom affair, has become a source of intense public excitement' → 흥미 없고 밀실의 → dry.\n(ii) 관례적으로 밀실에서 정해지는 승계 → 짜여진 → scripted.\n(i) 후보의 대거 출마는 그런 관례에서 '벗어난' 것 → departure from.\n정답: C (departure from), D (scripted), I (dry)", "trap": "(i)의 illustration of는 '관례의 예시'가 되어 startling(놀라운)·instead of와 모순된다. (iii)의 conspicuous·celebrated는 backroom(밀실)과 충돌.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"scripted": "짜여진, 각본대로의", "abbreviation of": "~의 축약", "illustration of": "~의 예시", "departure from": "~에서의 이탈", "chaotic": "혼란스러운", "prolonged": "장기화된", "conspicuous": "눈에 띄는", "celebrated": "유명한, 축하받는", "dry": "무미건조한"}, "src": "verbal206 Q4 · 25년 8월, 23년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies that Du Bois attributed which of the following beliefs to Spencerian sociologists?", "choices": ["Theorizing is important to the understanding of human actions", "Vast generalizations have limited value.", "Data gathering is a relatively unimportant part of sociological research.", "Sociology should focus on the living elements of society rather than cultural artifacts.", "Particulars are more important than universals."], "columns": null, "pid": "v206_p4", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Du Bois는 Spencerian 사회학자들이 'their work examined not deeds but theories'이고 'gathered data not to affect social progress but merely to theorize'라고 봄.\n이들은 데이터를 이론화를 위해 모았다 → 그들은 이론화가 인간 행위 이해에 중요하다고 믿었다 → A.\nB·E: Du Bois 자신의 입장(일반화보다 개별). C: 데이터를 모았으므로 반대. D: Du Bois의 목표.\n정답: A", "trap": "B·E는 Du Bois의 견해를 Spencerian 학자들에게 잘못 귀속시킨 함정(관점 뒤바꾸기).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"Spencerian": "스펜서 학파의", "generalizations": "일반화", "theorize": "이론화하다", "artifacts": "문화적 유물, 인공물"}, "src": "verbal206 Q14 · 25/2, 24/9, 24/8, 24/2, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that Du Bois believed which of the following statements about the artifacts he included in his exhibit?", "choices": ["They tended to support an established view of African American history and culture.", "They documented the contributions of particular African Americans to American social structure.", "They were chosen to encourage Spencerian sociologists to form useful generalizations."], "columns": null, "pid": "v206_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Du Bois sought to present cultural artifacts that would shift the focus ... to 'the working contributions of individual people to a vast functioning social structure.'\nB: 특정 아프리카계 미국인들의 사회 구조에 대한 기여를 기록 → 일치.\nA: 그의 작업은 기존 학계에 '도전(challenged)'했으므로 기존 견해 지지라는 근거 없음.\nC: 오히려 '거대한 일반화'로부터 초점을 옮기려 함 → 반대.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 '전시가 아프리카계 미국인 역사를 보여줬다'는 점에 끌리지만, 지문은 '확립된 견해'를 지지한다는 말이 없고 오히려 기존 학문에 도전했다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exhibit": "전시회", "Spencerian": "스펜서 학파의", "artifacts": "유물, 인공물"}, "src": "verbal206 Q15 · 25/2, 24/9, 24/8, 24/2, 23/2 중국후기", "note": "원본 답안표가 회차마다 달랐던 문항입니다(AB / B). 지문 근거로 B를 정답으로 확정했습니다. 중복본 키 충돌(AB vs B): A는 근거가 없고(작업은 기존 학계에 도전함) 지문과 부합하지 않으므로 B로 확정."}, {"id": "v238_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["explore an analogy between aspects of the geology of Mars and the geology of Earth", "describe how a certain feature of Mars's surface formed", "point out the effect that new data has had on a scientific investigation", "summarize potential explanations of a large-scale geological feature", "present the rationale for a scientist's theory and expose some of its weakness"], "columns": null, "pid": "v238_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 1단락 화성 북부 저지대 질문 + 지구형 판구조 설명, 2단락 McGill의 함몰 가설, 3단락 'The third possibility' 충돌 가설.\n하나의 대규모 지질 특성(북부 저지대)에 대한 여러 가능한 설명을 정리 → D.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(형성 과정 설명)는 하나의 결론을 내리는 것처럼 표현되어 틀리다. 지문은 세 가지 가설을 나열할 뿐 결론을 내리지 않는다. E는 McGill 한 사람에 국한되어 범위가 좁다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"plate tectonics": "판구조론", "bedrock": "기반암", "postulate": "가정하다, 상정하다", "predate": "~보다 앞서다"}, "src": "verbal238 Q7 · 24/10, 23/1, 22/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v238_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred from the passage about geological features on Earth?", "choices": ["The relative elevation of the lowest-lying regions of the crust arises in part from forces generated within the planet.", "The difference in elevation between the ocean basins and their surroundings is greater than the difference between Mars's northern basin and its surroundings.", "The formation of low-lying areas proceeds by a different process than the one that created Mars's northern basin.", "The weight of the oceans does not affect the depth of the ocean basins.", "The proportions of the crust that is oceanic crust is increasing."], "columns": null, "pid": "v238_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 지구의 저지대 해양 지각은 얇고 밀도가 높아 중력에 의해 지구 중심으로 더 강하게 당겨지고, 'The processes that generate this oceanic crust drive plate tectonics.'\n가장 낮은 지역의 상대적 고도는 내부 힘(중력·지각 생성 과정)에서 일부 비롯된다 → A.\nB: 고도 차이 비교 없음. C: 일부 연구자는 화성도 같은 과정으로 봄 → 단정 불가. D: 물의 무게 언급 없음. E: 해양 지각 비율 증가 언급 없음.\n정답: A", "trap": "C는 McGill이나 충돌 가설을 근거로 그럴듯해 보이지만, 지문은 화성 분지 형성 과정을 확정하지 않으므로 '다르다'고 추론할 수 없다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dense": "밀도가 높은", "oceanic crust": "해양 지각", "elevation": "고도", "basin": "분지"}, "src": "verbal238 Q8 · 24/10, 23/1, 22/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v238_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "As presented in the passage, McGill's account of the formation of Mars's northern basin differs from the other mentioned in that it alone", "choices": ["explains the formation of certain northern bedrock features", "does not specify the force that caused the northern basin to be lower than its surroundings", "takes the northern basin to be a landform that is not analogous to any found on Earth", "denies that features around the northern basin are the result of tectonic activity", "attributes the creation of the northern lowlands to processes occurring within the planet"], "columns": null, "pid": "v238_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'McGill instead believes that through some novel mechanism the ancient surface sank to its current depth as a single unit.'\n'some novel mechanism'(어떤 새로운 메커니즘) → 무엇이 가라앉혔는지 구체적 힘을 명시하지 않는다.\n다른 가설은 판구조(새 지각 형성), 충돌(소행성)이라는 원인을 명시 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "E(내부 과정에 의한 형성)는 그럴듯하지만, 판구조 가설도 내부 과정이므로 McGill만의 특징이 아니다. A는 기반암 구조를 McGill이 '설명'한 것이 아니라 근거로 '지적'한 것.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"novel": "새로운", "bedrock": "기반암", "predate": "~보다 먼저 존재하다", "analogous": "유사한"}, "src": "verbal238 Q9 · 24/10, 23/1, 22/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Local seawater acidification caused by carbon dioxide bubbling from the Pacific Ocean floor above a buried volcano _____ projected levels of climate-change-induced ocean acidification and so provides insight into likely future reef ecosystem effects.", "choices": ["alleviates", "emulates", "mitigates", "induces", "intensifies", "mirrors"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: and so provides insight into likely future reef ecosystem effects → 이 국지적 산성화가 미래 상황의 '모델'이 된다.\n그러려면 예상되는 기후변화 산성화 수준을 '흉내 내다/반영하다'.\nemulates와 mirrors가 같은 의미.\n정답: B (emulates), F (mirrors)", "trap": "alleviates/mitigates(완화하다)는 짝이 되지만, 미래 효과에 대한 통찰을 준다는 결과와 맞지 않는다. intensifies도 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"alleviates": "완화하다", "emulates": "모방하다, 흉내 내다", "mitigates": "완화하다", "induces": "유도하다", "intensifies": "강화하다", "mirrors": "반영하다, 그대로 보여주다"}, "src": "verbal206 Q11 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Though the progress of the reform legislation was _____, it was surprisingly steady, and there never seemed any reasonable doubt that it would eventually be enacted into law.", "choices": ["unwieldy", "erratic", "hindered", "snail-like", "ponderous", "unreliable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Though ___, it was surprisingly steady → 빈칸은 '꾸준함'과 대조되지만 공존할 수 있는 성질.\n'결국 법으로 통과될 것에 의심이 없었다' → 진행은 느렸지만 꾸준했다.\n빈칸 = '느린'.\nsnail-like(달팽이처럼 느린)와 ponderous(느릿느릿한, 둔중한)가 짝.\n정답: D (snail-like), E (ponderous)", "trap": "erratic/unreliable은 짝이 되지만 steady와 정면으로 모순되어 'though ~ surprisingly steady'가 성립하지 않는다. 가장 흔한 함정.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unwieldy": "다루기 힘든", "erratic": "변덕스러운, 불규칙한", "hindered": "방해받은", "snail-like": "달팽이처럼 느린", "ponderous": "느릿느릿한, 둔중한", "unreliable": "신뢰할 수 없는"}, "src": "verbal206 Q12 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Between 1975 and 2005, water use in the United States declined just as the population rose, showing the old assumption that total water consumption is positively correlated with population growth to be _____.", "choices": ["ubiquitous", "specious", "fallacious", "controversial", "unequivocal", "commonplace"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 인구는 늘었는데 물 사용량은 감소 → 'showing the old assumption ... to be ___'.\n기존 가정(물 소비량과 인구 증가는 양의 상관)이 반증됨.\n빈칸 = '틀린'.\nspecious(그럴듯하지만 틀린)와 fallacious(잘못된)가 짝.\n정답: B (specious), C (fallacious)", "trap": "controversial(논쟁적인)은 '오래된 가정'과 어울려 보이지만, 데이터가 가정을 반증했으므로 '틀렸다'가 핵심이다. ubiquitous/commonplace는 짝이 되지만 의미가 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"fallacious": "잘못된, 오류의", "specious": "그럴듯하나 틀린", "ubiquitous": "어디에나 있는", "controversial": "논란이 많은", "unequivocal": "명백한", "commonplace": "흔한"}, "src": "verbal232 Q10 · 25년 6월, 23년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v4_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the argument in the editorial, the part (\"the project ~ population\") that is highlighted plays which of the following roles?", "choices": ["stating the conclusion toward which the argument is directed", "describing a circumstance that the argument seeks to explain", "introducing the position to be refuted by the argument", "serving as an intermediate conclusion that supports a further conclusion stated in the argument", "introducing an explanation that is called into question by the argument"], "columns": null, "pid": "v4_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "하이라이트 부분: 반대자들의 주장(지하철 연장은 소수만 이득).\n바로 뒤 'These opponents are misguided.'가 결론 → 하이라이트는 논증이 반박하려는 입장.\n'After all ...' 이후는 반박 근거.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(결론)는 하이라이트가 주장 형태라 끌리지만, 실제 결론은 'These opponents are misguided.'이다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"misguided": "잘못 생각한", "editorial": "사설", "refuted": "반박된"}, "src": "verbal4 Q11"}, {"id": "v20_q14", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "Life on Europa in the form suggested in the passage would be dependent on", "choices": ["the protection Europa's icy crust gives against the harmful components of sunlight", "the existence of water on Europa", "the motion of Europa around Jupiter"], "columns": null, "pid": "v20_p4", "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'life such as the microbes that flourish deep within earth may still be possible' – 이런 생명은 액체 물을 필요로 한다.\nB: 'observations suggest liquid water exists beneath Europa's icy crust' → 물 필요.\nC: 그 물은 공전하며 휘어짐(flexing) → 마찰열 → 얼음이 녹아 생김 → 공전 운동에 의존.\nA: 햇빛 차단은 언급 없음(햇빛이 없어서 광합성 불가일 뿐).\n정답: B, C", "trap": "A는 '얼음 지각'과 '햇빛'이 지문에 있어 끌리지만, 지문은 얼음이 해로운 햇빛을 막는다고 하지 않는다. C는 인과 사슬이 길어 놓치기 쉽다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"refuted": "반박했다", "flexes": "휘어지다", "photosynthetic": "광합성의", "friction": "마찰"}, "src": "verbal20 Q14"}, {"id": "v20_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The highlighted sentence \"Take Jupiter's moon Europa\" serves to introduce", "choices": ["an instance that allows a hypothesis to be tested", "speculation grounded in empirical discovery", "a deduction from a newly advanced hypothesis", "a large-scale effect of an apparently insignificant contingency", "the derivation of a contradiction to refute a claim"], "columns": null, "pid": "v20_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 지하 생명의 '발견(empirical discovery)'이 지구 밖 생명의 가능성을 높였다.\n'Take Jupiter's moon Europa.' 이후: 관측에 근거해 유로파에 지하 생명이 '가능할 수 있다(may still be possible)'는 추측을 전개.\n= 경험적 발견에 근거한 추측 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "A(가설 검증 사례)는 그럴듯하지만, 유로파는 가설을 '검증'하는 사례가 아니라 가능성을 추측하는 대상이다. C는 '새로 제시된 가설'로부터의 연역이 아니라 발견에서 나온 추측이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"empirical": "경험적인, 관찰에 근거한", "speculation": "추측", "deduction": "연역, 추론", "contingency": "우발적 사건"}, "src": "verbal20 Q15"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.1 / S2 2.7"}, {"set": 15, "sections": [[{"id": "v197_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Astronomers affiliated with larger scientific institutions are often seen by their peers as _____; successful practice of astronomy today is contingent upon easy access to sizeable and costly instruments.", "choices": ["assiduous", "collegial", "pedantic", "privileged", "hypocritical"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론(;) 뒤 문장이 앞 문장의 이유를 설명한다.\n오늘날 천문학의 성공은 '크고 비싼 장비에 쉽게 접근하는 것'에 달려 있다.\n큰 기관 소속 천문학자는 그런 장비를 쉽게 쓸 수 있으므로 동료들에게 '혜택받은, 유리한 위치에 있는' 사람으로 보인다.\n빈칸 = 유리한 조건을 가진, 특권을 누리는.\n정답: D (privileged)", "trap": "assiduous(근면한)는 긍정적 평가지만 세미콜론 뒤 근거는 노력이 아니라 '장비 접근성'이라는 조건이므로 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"assiduous": "근면한, 끈기 있는", "collegial": "동료 간 협력적인", "pedantic": "현학적인, 사소한 것에 얽매이는", "privileged": "특권을 가진, 혜택받은", "hypocritical": "위선적인"}, "src": "verbal197 Q1 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v11_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Humans can have (i) _____ tastes: crab brains and squeezable cheese are delicacies to many people, even as others find them repulsive. The preference for sweet and abhorrence of bitter is (ii) _____, however.", "choices": null, "columns": [["self-indulgent", "refined", "idiosyncratic"], ["explicable", "strong", "universal"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 콜론 뒤 설명: 게 뇌·짜 먹는 치즈를 어떤 사람은 별미로, 어떤 사람은 역겹게 여긴다 → 사람마다 다른 취향.\n빈칸 (i) = 개인마다 다른 → idiosyncratic.\n(ii) however로 대조: 단 것을 좋아하고 쓴 것을 싫어하는 것은 사람마다 다르지 않다 → 모두에게 공통.\n빈칸 (ii) = universal.\n정답: C, F (idiosyncratic, universal)", "trap": "(ii)의 strong은 그럴듯해 보이지만 however의 대조 축은 '개인차 vs 공통성'이므로 strong은 대조가 되지 않는다. (i)의 refined는 '세련된'으로 역겹게 여기는 사람도 있다는 다양성을 담지 못한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"idiosyncratic": "특이한, 개인 특유의", "self-indulgent": "제멋대로 하는, 방종한", "refined": "세련된, 정제된", "explicable": "설명 가능한", "strong": "강한", "universal": "보편적인"}, "src": "verbal11 Q2"}, {"id": "v201_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "One disadvantage of reading (i) _____ accounts of historical events is that the textual (ii) _____ often lead to abrupt transitions and (iii) _____ references.", "choices": null, "columns": [["straightforward", "condensed", "lucid"], ["additions", "alterations", "redundancies"], ["explicit", "copious", "unexplained"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BEI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "역사 기록을 읽을 때의 '단점'을 말하는 문장 → 빈칸은 모두 부정적 결과로 이어져야 한다.\n(i) 갑작스러운 전환(abrupt transitions)이 생기는 원인 → 내용을 줄인 condensed(축약된) 기록.\n(ii) 축약 과정에서 생긴 텍스트상의 '변경' → alterations. (additions는 축약과 반대, redundancies는 갑작스러운 전환을 낳지 않음)\n(iii) 축약 때문에 설명이 빠진 참조 → unexplained references.\n정답: B, E, I (condensed, alterations, unexplained)", "trap": "(i) straightforward/lucid는 긍정적 성질이라 '단점' 문맥과 충돌한다. (iii) explicit은 abrupt transitions와 나란히 나올 부정적 결과가 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"straightforward": "단순명료한", "condensed": "요약된, 압축된", "lucid": "명쾌한", "additions": "추가(된 것)", "alterations": "변경, 수정", "redundancies": "중복, 불필요한 반복", "explicit": "명시적인", "copious": "풍부한, 많은", "unexplained": "설명되지 않은"}, "src": "verbal201 Q3 · 25/7, 23/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v211_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with", "choices": ["examining how a phenomenon affected a particular group", "critiquing a historical explanation for a particular change", "describing innovations that led to the development of a new technology", "explaining the success of a strategy", "defending the viability of a political position"], "columns": null, "pid": "v211_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문 전체: 유성영화(talkies)의 등장 → 3,200명 이상의 뉴욕 극장 연주자 실직 → 노조 파업 실패 → 실패 이유(노동계급의 선호, 싼 티켓 가격).\n즉 '어떤 현상(유성영화)'이 '특정 집단(극장 연주자)'에 어떤 영향을 미쳤는지 살펴보는 글.\n정답: A", "trap": "D(전략의 성공 설명)는 반대다. 노조의 캠페인은 'utter disaster'로 실패했다. B는 지문이 기존의 역사적 설명을 비판하지 않으므로 오답.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"talkies": "유성영화", "culminating in": "결국 ~로 끝나다", "inevitable tide": "피할 수 없는 흐름"}, "src": "verbal211 Q4 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v211_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that before the introduction of sound films, movie theater owners", "choices": ["did not question the control the musicians' union exercised over wages and hours", "invested in technology that the advent of sound films made redundant", "catered primarily to an audience that was not working class", "had less flexibility in scheduling", "made less profit per film showing"], "columns": null, "pid": "v211_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Freed from paying wages and from union regulations governing musicians' hours, theater owners could show films all day.'\n유성영화 이후 연주자 근무시간 규정에서 '해방'되어 하루 종일 상영할 수 있었다 → 그 전에는 상영 시간 편성이 노조 규정에 묶여 있었다.\n즉 이전에는 스케줄 유연성이 더 적었다.\n정답: D", "trap": "E(상영당 이윤이 더 적었다)는 임금 부담에서 그럴듯하지만, 티켓 가격도 더 비쌌으므로 상영당 이윤 비교는 지문으로 알 수 없다. A는 노조 통제에 의문을 갖지 않았다는 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pit musicians": "극장 오케스트라석 연주자", "Depression-era": "대공황 시대의", "redundant": "불필요해진, 쓸모없어진"}, "src": "verbal211 Q5 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v11_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Unsurprisingly, the novelist's new work has not been without its critics, drawing particular attention from those who have _____ the vapidity of other novels of the same genre in a number of acerbic reviews.", "choices": ["reprehended", "questioned", "ignored", "overlooked", "decried", "relished"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'not without its critics', 'acerbic reviews(신랄한 비평)', 'vapidity(무미건조함)'.\n같은 장르 다른 소설들의 무미건조함을 신랄한 비평으로 '비난해 온' 사람들이 이 신작에도 주목했다.\n빈칸 = 강하게 비난하다.\nreprehended(질책하다)와 decried(공개적으로 비난하다)가 같은 뜻.\n정답: A, E (reprehended, decried)", "trap": "questioned(의문을 제기하다)는 부정적이긴 하지만 acerbic(신랄한)에 비해 너무 약하고 짝이 없다. ignored/overlooked는 짝이 있지만 '신랄한 비평'을 쓴 것과 모순된다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"relished": "즐기다, 음미하다", "reprehended": "꾸짖다, 질책하다", "questioned": "의문을 제기하다", "ignored": "무시하다", "overlooked": "간과하다", "decried": "공공연히 비난하다"}, "src": "verbal11 Q6"}, {"id": "v1_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "On stage, jazz artist James Carter often veers dangerously close to the _____: he becomes a man possessed, his tenor saxophone wailing and whimpering with a musicality so muscular it threatens to consume him.", "choices": ["lugubrious", "doleful", "intemperate", "excessive", "idiosyncratic", "sublime"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 설명: 사로잡힌 사람처럼 되고, 색소폰이 울부짖으며, 너무 강렬한 음악성이 그를 집어삼킬 듯하다.\n'veers dangerously close to(위험할 정도로 ~에 가까워진다)'와 함께 → 빈칸 = 지나침, 절제가 없음.\nintemperate(무절제한)와 excessive(과도한)가 같은 뜻.\n정답: C, D (intemperate, excessive)", "trap": "lugubrious/doleful(슬픈)은 'wailing and whimpering'에 끌리지만, 핵심은 슬픔이 아니라 '통제를 벗어난 과잉'이다. sublime은 긍정적이라 dangerously와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lugubrious": "침울한, 애처로운", "doleful": "슬픈, 애절한", "intemperate": "무절제한, 지나친", "idiosyncratic": "특이한", "sublime": "숭고한", "excessive": "과도한"}, "src": "verbal1 Q7"}, {"id": "v199_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The early universe was _____ but no longer: galaxies, galaxy clusters, and stars punctuate the expanse of empty space, staking their uneven distribution throughout the firmament.", "choices": ["compact", "symmetrical", "uniform", "inhospitable", "homogeneous", "impenetrable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'but no longer'로 대조: 지금은 은하·성단·별이 'uneven distribution(고르지 않은 분포)'을 이룬다.\n그렇다면 초기 우주는 그 반대 → 빈칸 = 고르게 퍼진, 균일한.\nuniform과 homogeneous가 같은 뜻.\n정답: C, E (uniform, homogeneous)", "trap": "compact(조밀한)는 '빈 공간의 확장'과 대조처럼 보이지만 콜론 뒤 핵심어는 uneven distribution이므로 대조 짝은 '균일함'이다. symmetrical도 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"compact": "조밀한, 빽빽한", "symmetrical": "대칭적인", "uniform": "균일한", "inhospitable": "살기 힘든, 불친절한", "homogeneous": "균질한, 동질의", "impenetrable": "꿰뚫을 수 없는, 이해할 수 없는"}, "src": "verbal199 Q7 · 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v29_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Benjamin Franklin’s reputation is so much one of appearing scientific investigation with common sense empiricism that it is somewhat startling to realize how _____ the great experiment’s mentor truly was.", "choices": ["reasonable", "speculative", "pragmatic", "conjectural", "careless", "judicious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 프랭클린의 평판은 '상식적 경험주의(common sense empiricism)'인데, 실제로 그가 얼마나 ___였는지 알면 놀랍다(startling).\n'startling'이 대조 신호 → 빈칸 = 경험주의와 반대, 즉 추측에 의존하는.\nspeculative와 conjectural이 같은 뜻.\n정답: B, D (speculative, conjectural)", "trap": "pragmatic/reasonable/judicious는 '상식적 경험주의'와 같은 방향이라 놀랄 이유가 없다. careless는 부정적이지만 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"reasonable": "합리적인", "speculative": "사변적인, 추측에 근거한", "pragmatic": "실용적인", "conjectural": "추측의, 억측에 의한", "careless": "부주의한", "judicious": "분별 있는, 신중한"}, "src": "verbal29 Q9"}, {"id": "v225_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["consider similarities in several studies of Charlotte Bronte's life", "defend a particular view of Charlotte Bronte's life", "discuss a change in perspective on Charlotte Bronte's life", "depict the social environment in which Charlotte Bronte lived", "portray Charlotte Bronte as an early feminist writer"], "columns": null, "pid": "v225_p10", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: Gaskell의 낭만적 관점(사회와 단절된 시골 출신) → Gerin도 그 관점을 버리지 못함 → 페미니스트들의 새 해석 → 'it is primarily Juliet Barker who takes into account the larger world'.\n즉 브론테 삶을 보는 관점이 오래 지속되다가 바뀌는 과정을 다룬다.\n정답: C", "trap": "D(사회 환경 묘사)는 마지막 문장에만 언급된 세부라 글 전체 목적이 아니다. E는 페미니스트 해석이 한 번 언급될 뿐 브론테를 페미니스트 작가로 그리는 글이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"irreproachably": "나무랄 데 없이", "at variance with": "~와 상충하는", "subversive": "전복적인", "discern": "식별하다, 알아보다", "impinge on": "~에 영향을 미치다"}, "src": "verbal225 Q10 · 25년 9월, 24년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v225_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggest that Matthew Arnold disapproved of Charlotte Bronte's fiction insofar as he believed that it", "choices": ["overly romanticized the English countryside", "contained dangerous ideas buried within it", "perpetuated outmoded social distinctions", "failed to represent industrialized society realistically", "reflected an excessive concern with propriety"], "columns": null, "pid": "v225_p10", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the subversive spirit Matthew Arnold accurately discerned, albeit with distance, deep within Bronte's fiction'.\n'albeit with distance(거리를 두고는 있지만)'가 Arnold의 불편함·불찬성을 암시하고, 그가 본 것은 소설 깊숙이 있는 '전복적 정신'.\n→ 소설 속에 위험한 생각이 묻혀 있다고 봤다.\n정답: B", "trap": "E(예의범절에 지나치게 집착)는 Gaskell이 묘사한 브론테 이미지(irreproachably proper)이며 Arnold가 본 것과 정반대다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"subversive": "체제 전복적인", "albeit": "비록 ~이지만", "propriety": "예의범절, 적절성", "outmoded": "구식의"}, "src": "verbal225 Q11 · 25년 9월, 24년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v225_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggest that Gaskell's biography of Charlotte Bronte advanced the idea that Bronte was", "choices": ["one of the most celebrated of the romantic novelists", "an outspoken advocate of the social change", "opposed to the industrialization of England", "strongly influenced by the social upheaval of the times", "chiefly the product of a rustic environment"], "columns": null, "pid": "v225_p10", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Gaskell은 브론테를 산업화 사회와 무관하게 'sprung naturally, like so much purple heather, out of the English countryside'한 존재로 그렸다.\n시골에서 자연스럽게 피어난 존재 = 주로 전원적 환경의 산물.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(사회적 격변의 강한 영향)는 정반대다. Gaskell은 브론테가 산업화 혼란과 'no connection'이라고 했다. A는 'most celebrated'가 브론테가 아니라 그 전기에 대한 수식어다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"heather": "헤더(황야에 피는 보라색 꽃)", "rustic": "시골의, 전원적인", "upheaval": "격변", "turbulence": "격동, 혼란"}, "src": "verbal225 Q12 · 25년 9월, 24년 9월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v208_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Bridges are often offered as _____ examples of engineering, given that a bridge's structure is out in the open for all to see.", "choices": ["intelligible", "collaborative", "elementary", "undervalued", "serendipitous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'given that ~(~을 고려하면)'은 이유 신호.\n다리 구조가 모두에게 훤히 드러나 있다 → 누구나 보고 이해할 수 있는 공학의 예.\n빈칸 = 이해하기 쉬운.\n정답: A (intelligible)", "trap": "elementary(기초적인)는 '쉬운 예'처럼 보이지만 구조가 드러나 있다는 것은 다리가 단순하다는 뜻이 아니라 '이해 가능하다'는 뜻이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"intelligible": "이해할 수 있는", "serendipitous": "우연히 발견된, 뜻밖의", "collaborative": "협력적인", "elementary": "기초적인, 초보의", "undervalued": "과소평가된"}, "src": "verbal208 Q1 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v238_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "As a general rule, the larger a governmental jurisdiction is, the (i) _____ its personnel system will be. Since a large percentage of the more than 80 thousand public jurisdictions in the United States are quite small, much human-resource management is conducted in (ii) _____ manner.", "choices": null, "columns": [["more expensive", "more formal", "less stratified"], ["a unilateral", "an ad hoc", "an equable"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) '관할 구역이 클수록 인사 시스템이 더 ___하다' — 두 번째 문장과 연결해야 함.\n(ii) 대부분의 관할 구역이 작다 → 인사 관리가 (작은 곳의 특징대로) ___한 방식으로 이루어진다.\n크다 ↔ 공식적, 작다 ↔ 임시변통적이라는 짝이 성립 → (i) more formal, (ii) an ad hoc.\n정답: B, E (more formal, an ad hoc)", "trap": "(i) more expensive는 크기와 그럴듯하게 연결되지만 (ii)에서 '싸게'에 해당하는 선택지가 없어 두 빈칸이 이어지지 않는다. less stratified는 방향이 반대(클수록 계층화가 더 많다).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"more expensive": "더 비싼", "more formal": "더 공식적인, 격식 있는", "less stratified": "덜 계층화된", "a unilateral": "일방적인", "an ad hoc": "임시변통의, 그때그때의", "an equable": "차분한, 균등한"}, "src": "verbal238 Q3 · 25/12, 25/9, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v218_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "While offering important insights into supernova remnants, Finch's paper is often rather (i) _____: it is (ii) _____ unexplained concepts and details.", "choices": null, "columns": [["impenetrable", "unoriginal", "trivial"], ["replete with", "free from", "purged of"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'While offering important insights'로 양보 → 뒤에는 부정적 평가.\n(ii) 콜론 뒤 설명: 설명되지 않은 개념과 세부로 '가득하다' → replete with.\n(i) 설명 안 된 개념이 많으면 이해하기 어렵다 → impenetrable.\n정답: A, D (impenetrable, replete with)", "trap": "trivial/unoriginal은 부정적이지만 '중요한 통찰을 준다'는 앞부분과 모순되고, 설명 부족과도 연결되지 않는다. (ii) free from/purged of는 부정적 평가를 만들지 못한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"impenetrable": "이해할 수 없는, 난해한", "unoriginal": "독창적이지 않은", "trivial": "사소한", "replete with": "~로 가득 찬", "free from": "~이 없는", "purged of": "~이 제거된"}, "src": "verbal218 Q2 · 25/7, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Ironically, contemporary critics who celebrate the Victorian novel for its intellectual depth describe the (i) _____ effects of newer media—film, television, digital technology—in precisely the same terms that earlier critics had used to (ii) _____ the novel itself: as piecemeal entertainments that (iii) _____ mental effort on the part of the consumer.", "choices": null, "columns": [["salubrious", "numbing", "inflammatory"], ["lambast", "lionize", "legitimate"], ["entail", "obviate", "presage"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'Ironically'가 핵심: 오늘날 빅토리아 소설을 칭찬하는 비평가들이 새 매체를 비판하는 말이, 예전 비평가들이 소설 자체를 비판할 때 쓴 말과 똑같다.\n(i) 새 매체의 (부정적) 효과 → numbing(마비시키는).\n(ii) 예전 비평가들이 소설을 '혹평'했다 → lambast.\n(iii) 단편적 오락이 정신적 노력을 '불필요하게 만든다' → obviate.\n정답: B, D, H (numbing, lambast, obviate)", "trap": "(ii) lionize(치켜세우다)를 고르면 아이러니가 사라진다. (iii) entail(수반하다)은 '노력을 요구한다'는 뜻이라 numbing 효과와 반대다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"piecemeal": "단편적인", "presage": "예고하다, 전조가 되다", "obviate": "불필요하게 하다, 제거하다", "salubrious": "건강에 좋은, 유익한", "numbing": "마비시키는, 둔하게 만드는", "inflammatory": "선동적인, 염증성의", "lambast": "혹평하다", "lionize": "떠받들다, 치켜세우다", "legitimate": "정당화하다", "entail": "수반하다, 필요로 하다"}, "src": "verbal234 Q4 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary function of the highlighted sentence is to", "choices": ["provide evidence that helps explain the success of the red fire ant in the United States", "identify a feature of red fire ant colonies in the United States that makes them appealing to researchers", "suggest why red fire ant colonies have been so damaging in many regions of the United States", "explain why researchers feel that studying the territoriality of red fire ants in the United States may yield problematic results", "suggest a reason for the absence of competitors to the red fire ant in the United States"], "columns": null, "pid": "v200_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문 주장: 미국의 붉은불개미 영역성 연구는 'distinct advantages'가 있다.\n강조 문장(땅이 불개미 영역으로 거의 연속해서 덮여 있어 모든 경계가 다른 불개미 군체와 맞닿음)은 그 장점을 보여주는 특징이다.\n다음 문장 'without the complicating influences of other competitors'로 연구자에게 매력적인 이유가 이어진다.\n정답: B", "trap": "A(미국에서 불개미가 성공한 이유)는 그럴듯하지만 지문은 개미의 성공이 아니라 '연구상의 장점'을 말한다. D는 'problematic results'로 방향이 반대다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"territoriality": "영역성, 세력권 행동", "blanketed": "뒤덮인", "generalizable": "일반화할 수 있는"}, "src": "verbal200 Q14 · 25/7, 24/1, 22/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author implies that red fire ants in the United States differ from red fire ants in South America in the extent to which ants in the two environments", "choices": ["dominate their habitat", "interact with other red fire ant colonies", "have had their territorial behavior studied by researchers"], "columns": null, "pid": "v200_p4", "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 남미에서는 'shares habitat with many ant competitors', 미국에서는 땅이 불개미 영역으로 거의 연속해서 덮여 있고 'all territorial boundaries are with other fire ant colonies'.\nA: 미국에서는 서식지를 거의 독점, 남미에서는 경쟁자와 공유 → 지배 정도가 다름. O\nB: 미국에서는 모든 경계가 다른 불개미 군체와 맞닿아 있고(밀도도 높음) 남미는 다른 종과도 맞닿음 → 동종 군체와의 상호작용 정도가 다름. O\nC: 두 지역에서 연구가 얼마나 이루어졌는지는 언급이 없다. X\n정답: A, B", "trap": "C는 지문이 미국에서 연구하기 좋은 장점을 말할 뿐, 실제로 어느 쪽이 더 많이 연구되었는지는 말하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"colonizable": "정착·군체 형성이 가능한", "densities": "밀도", "competitors": "경쟁자"}, "src": "verbal200 Q15 · 25/7, 24/1, 22/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v228_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage as a whole is to", "choices": ["analyze a philosophical theory", "describe the doctrines of a noted thinker", "trace the evolution of a noted philosopher's thinking", "reevaluate a body of work", "defend a philosophical doctrine"], "columns": null, "pid": "v228_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문단: Peirce는 업적이 크지만 현대 철학에서 'largely ignored'되며 그 이유를 설명.\n2문단: 'Certainly(인정)' 상당 부분이 역사적 가치뿐임을 인정 → 'Still(반전)' 누구보다 넓은 관심·깊은 지식을 가졌고, 인내하는 독자에게는 큰 폭과 복잡성을 준다.\n→ 무시된 작업 전체를 다시 평가하는 글.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(사상가의 학설 설명)는 Peirce의 구체적 학설을 설명하지 않는다. E는 특정 학설을 옹호하는 것이 아니라 작업 전체의 가치를 재평가하는 것이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"voluminous": "방대한", "dissonance": "불일치, 부조화", "erudition": "박식함", "slapdash": "엉성한, 되는 대로의", "anticipation": "예견, 선취"}, "src": "verbal228 Q7 · 24년 5월, 23년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v228_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author suggests that which of the following was a flaw in Peirce's work?", "choices": ["A rigidity in his attitudes", "An inability to delve deeply into any one subject", "A failure to organize his views", "A propensity to romanticize his views", "A tendency to appropriate others' theories"], "columns": null, "pid": "v228_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Peirce never welded his views into a system', 'the chaotic state of his voluminous writings'.\n자신의 견해를 체계로 묶지 못했다 = 견해를 정리·조직하지 못했다.\n정답: C", "trap": "B(한 주제를 깊이 파고들지 못함)는 오히려 'deeper knowledge', 'immense erudition'과 반대다. A(경직성)도 'refusal to oversimplify'와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"weld": "결합하다, 용접하다", "propensity": "성향", "appropriate": "도용하다, 전유하다", "rigidity": "경직성"}, "src": "verbal228 Q8 · 24년 5월, 23년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v228_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions Peirce's theory of “evolutionary love” most likely in order to", "choices": ["provide an illustration of Peirce's immense erudition", "demonstrate Peirce's command of the scientific culture of his time", "illustrate the dissonance among Peirce's various doctrines", "suggest that Peirce has integrated theories about evolution into his philosophical system", "demonstrate the broad range of Peirce's expertise"], "columns": null, "pid": "v228_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the dissonance of his doctrines, which range from an insistence on rigorous scientific methodology to a cosmological metaphysics of evolutionary love'.\n엄격한 과학 방법론부터 '진화적 사랑'이라는 우주론적 형이상학까지 → 학설들 사이의 부조화를 보여주는 예.\n정답: C", "trap": "E(폭넓은 전문성)나 A(박식함)는 2문단 내용이라 끌리지만, 'evolutionary love'는 1문단에서 무시당하는 이유 중 '부조화'의 예로 나온다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "evolutionary love", "glosses": {"cosmological": "우주론적인", "metaphysics": "형이상학", "doctrine": "학설, 교리"}, "src": "verbal228 Q9 · 24년 5월, 23년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v206_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Researchers comparing test subjects' abilities to interpret others' facial expressions found that while some expressions were easy to interpret, others were difficult because they were so _____ the person making the expression.", "choices": ["habitual for", "customary for", "peculiar to", "idiosyncratic to", "opaque to", "inoffensive to"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'while'로 대조: 어떤 표정은 해석이 쉽지만, 다른 표정은 표정 짓는 사람에게 너무 ___해서 해석이 어렵다.\n남이 해석하기 어려운 이유 → 그 사람에게만 고유한 표정.\n빈칸 = ~에게 특유한.\npeculiar to와 idiosyncratic to가 같은 뜻.\n정답: C, D (peculiar to, idiosyncratic to)", "trap": "opaque to(~에게 불투명한)는 '어렵다'와 연결돼 보이지만, 표정이 그 표정을 짓는 사람 본인에게 불투명하다는 것은 말이 안 된다. habitual for/customary for는 짝이지만 습관적이라는 이유만으로는 해석이 어렵지 않다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"habitual for": "~에게 습관적인", "customary for": "~에게 관례적인", "peculiar to": "~에게 특유한", "idiosyncratic to": "~에게 고유한, 특이한", "opaque to": "~에게 불투명한, 이해되지 않는", "inoffensive to": "~에게 불쾌감을 주지 않는"}, "src": "verbal206 Q10 · 25/9, 25/8, 23/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v236_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The firm's startling admission of bookkeeping irregularities called into question the _____ of the oversight that government exercises over the financial health of private businesses.", "choices": ["sufficiency", "efficacy", "authenticity", "legitimacy", "propriety", "constitutionality"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "기업이 회계 부정을 인정했다 → 정부의 감독이 이를 잡아내지 못했다는 뜻.\n그러므로 의문이 제기되는 것은 감독의 '충분함·효과'.\n빈칸 = 효과적으로 작동하는지.\nsufficiency(충분함)와 efficacy(효과)가 같은 방향.\n정답: A, B (sufficiency, efficacy)", "trap": "legitimacy/propriety/constitutionality는 감독할 '권한·적법성'에 관한 것인데, 회계 부정 발생은 감독이 정당한지가 아니라 잘 작동하는지를 문제 삼는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"bookkeeping irregularities": "회계의 불규칙성들", "legitimacy": "정당성, 합법성", "propriety": "적절성, 예의범절", "constitutionality": "합헌성", "sufficiency": "충분함, 적절한 양", "efficacy": "효능, 효과", "authenticity": "진정성, 진짜임"}, "src": "verbal236 Q12 · 25/9, 25/7, 25/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Judge Jones brought some welcome levity to the often tense, though sometimes _____, proceedings.", "choices": ["humorous", "tedious", "stressful", "inconsequential", "fraught", "tiresome"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'often tense, though sometimes ___'에서 though는 tense와 대조.\n그런데 판사가 'welcome levity(반가운 가벼움)'를 가져왔으므로 빈칸도 가벼움이 필요한 부정적 상태여야 한다.\n긴장과 대조되면서도 부정적인 것 = 지루함.\ntedious와 tiresome이 같은 뜻.\n정답: B, F (tedious, tiresome)", "trap": "humorous는 tense와 대조되지만, 이미 유머러스하다면 levity가 'welcome'할 이유가 없다. stressful/fraught는 tense와 같은 방향이라 though와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"levity": "가벼움", "humorous": "유머러스한", "tedious": "지루한, 싫증 나는", "stressful": "스트레스가 많은", "inconsequential": "중요하지 않은, 사소한", "fraught": "(문제·긴장 등으로) 가득한, 걱정스러운", "tiresome": "지루한, 성가신"}, "src": "verbal230 Q12 · 25/8, 25/7, 25/4, 25/2, 24/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is an assumption on which the argument relies?", "choices": ["Industrial pollution is the principal source of heavy metals in marine sediments.", "Harpacticoids are the only crustaceans that feed on microorganisms by ingesting sediment particles.", "Harpacticoids are more susceptible to poisoning by heavy metals than are other marine organisms.", "The microorganisms that harpacticoids feed on are not killed by pollutants that are harmless to harpacticoids.", "The microorganisms that harpacticoids feed on absorb heavy metals."], "columns": null, "pid": "v220_p13", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 하르팍티코이드의 농도는 그 해역에 중금속이 있는지를 잘 보여주는 지표다.\n근거: 중금속에는 중독되지만 다른 오염물질에는 영향을 받지 않는다.\n빈틈: 다른 오염물질이 '먹이'인 미생물을 죽이면, 중금속이 없어도 하르팍티코이드가 굶어서 줄어든다 → 개체 수 감소가 중금속 때문인지 알 수 없다.\nD는 이 가능성을 배제한다(부정하면 논증 붕괴).\n정답: D (주어진 키 E와 다름)", "trap": "E는 그럴듯하지만, 중금속은 퇴적 입자 자체에 붙고 하르팍티코이드는 그 입자를 삼키므로 미생물이 중금속을 흡수하지 않아도 중독된다. C는 다른 생물과의 비교라 논증과 무관하다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"harpacticoids": "하르팍티코이드(저서성 요각류)", "crustaceans": "갑각류", "sediment": "퇴적물", "adhere to": "~에 달라붙다", "susceptible": "~에 취약한"}, "src": "verbal220 Q13 · 25/7, 24/2, 23/12 중국후기", "note": "⚠ 원본 답안표 정답은 E이지만, 검토 풀이로는 D이(가) 더 타당해 보입니다. 채점은 원본 기준이며 아래 해설은 검토 풀이 기준입니다. 근거: 주어진 키는 E이지만 D가 정답으로 판단됨. 하르팍티코이드는 미생물이 붙은 퇴적 입자를 통째로 삼키고, 중금속은 그 퇴적 입자에 달라붙으므로 미생물이 중금속을 흡수할 필요가 없다(E를 부정해도 논증 유지). 반면 다른 오염물질이 먹이 미생물을 죽이면 중금속이 없어도 개체 수가 줄어 지표로서의 신뢰성이 무너지므로 D가 필요한 가정이다. 이 문제의 원 출처(GMAT 공식 문제)에서도 정답은 D로 알려져 있다."}, {"id": "v26_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage mentions \"protoplanetary disks\" because", "choices": ["the computer modeling techniques used to study them were later applied to Saturn's rings", "conclusions about them might reasonably be applied to Saturn's rings", "the accepted understanding of them is challenged by observations of Saturn's rings", "the material of which Saturn's rings are composed must at one time have been in a protoplanetary disk around the Sun", "observations of Saturn's rings may serve as a substitute for observations of protoplanetary disks"], "columns": null, "pid": "v26_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'An analogous process occurs around young stars in the disks ... and these protoplanetary disks do vanish that quickly, computer models show.'\n토성 고리와 '유사한 과정'이 일어나는 원시행성원반도 실제로 그만큼 빨리 사라진다 → 토성 고리가 빨리 붕괴한다는 예측을 뒷받침.\n즉 원반에 대한 결론을 토성 고리에도 합리적으로 적용할 수 있다는 취지.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 같은 모델링 기법이 '나중에' 토성 고리에 적용되었다는 시간 순서·인과가 지문에 없다. C는 반대로 원반이 토성 고리 예측을 지지한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"protoplanetary disk": "원시행성원반", "angular momentum": "각운동량", "analogous": "유사한"}, "src": "verbal26 Q14"}, {"id": "v26_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about the \"energy transfer\"?", "choices": ["Its effects are obscured by the angular momentum of Saturn's moons.", "It is part of a process that also imparts angular momentum to at least some of Saturn's moons.", "It proceeds more slowly than does an analogous energy transfer that occurs in the vicinity of young stars."], "columns": null, "pid": "v26_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the particles constituting Saturn's rings are giving up angular momentum to moons of the planet ... the related energy transfer will cause the rings' collapse.'\nA: 위성 각운동량이 그 효과를 가린다는 말은 없다. X\nB: 에너지 전달은 고리 입자가 위성에 각운동량을 넘겨주는 과정의 일부. O\nC: 원시행성원반도 'vanish that quickly'로 같은 속도이지, 더 느리다고 하지 않았다. X\n정답: B", "trap": "C는 비교 방향을 지어낸 것이다. 지문은 두 과정이 비슷한 속도(그만큼 빨리)라고 말한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "energy transfer", "glosses": {"angular momentum": "각운동량", "collapse": "붕괴", "obscure": "가리다, 모호하게 하다", "impart": "전하다, 부여하다"}, "src": "verbal26 Q15"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.4 / S2 2.8"}, {"set": 16, "sections": [[{"id": "v219_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Many readers today consider the moral sentiments expressed in the ancient writers' work to be quite vapid, and in the seventeenth century they were similarly regarded as _____.", "choices": ["jejune", "didactic", "dogmatic", "tendentious", "arcane"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'similarly(마찬가지로)' → 빈칸은 앞의 vapid(무미건조한, 내용 없는)와 같은 뜻.\n오늘날 독자들도, 17세기 사람들도 그 도덕적 정서를 시시하게 여겼다.\n빈칸 = 무미건조한, 유치한.\n정답: A (jejune)", "trap": "didactic(교훈적인)은 '도덕적 정서'와 잘 어울려 보이지만 vapid와 같은 뜻이 아니다. 'similarly'가 요구하는 것은 동의어다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"jejune": "무미건조한, 유치한", "tendentious": "편향된, 특정 입장을 옹호하는", "didactic": "교훈적인, 가르치려 드는", "dogmatic": "독단적인", "arcane": "난해한, 비밀스러운"}, "src": "verbal219 Q1 · 25/11, 25/8, 25/3, 23/4, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v231_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The priorities at astronomical observatories changed dramatically in the period. A major reason was the (i) _____ government funding for solar system research: the national government, eager to bolster the sense that the country was a supportive place for scientists, made a concerted effort to (ii) _____ studies of the moon, the planets, and near space.", "choices": null, "columns": [["curb on", "spate of", "continuation of"], ["stymie", "maintain", "accelerate"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "관측소 우선순위가 '극적으로' 바뀐 주요 이유 → 태양계 연구에 대한 정부 자금의 변화.\n콜론 뒤: 정부는 과학자를 지원하는 나라라는 인식을 강화하려고 달·행성 연구를 '___하려는' 공동 노력을 했다 → 촉진.\n(ii) accelerate, (i) 자금의 급증 → spate of.\n정답: B, F (spate of, accelerate)", "trap": "continuation of/maintain은 짝을 이루지만 '극적인 변화'의 원인이 될 수 없다. curb on/stymie는 'supportive place for scientists'와 모순된다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"curb on": "~의 억제", "spate of": "~의 급증, 쇄도", "continuation of": "~의 지속", "stymie": "방해하다, 좌절시키다", "maintain": "유지하다", "accelerate": "가속하다, 촉진하다"}, "src": "verbal231 Q2 · 25/12, 25/5, 24/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v33_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "When potentially disruptive change appears on the horizon, managers’ approach should be to assemble the capabilities to (i) _____ that change before it affects the mainstream business. The (ii) _____ to run two businesses, one with processes attuned to the existing business model and another geared toward the new model. While apparently onerous, this parallel operation is far less dangerous than either (iii) _____ innovation irrevocably or remaining committed to tried-and-true methods that are threatened with obsolescence.", "choices": null, "columns": [["obstruct", "stimulate", "handle"], ["competition might have", "requirement is", "mistaken approach is"], ["jumping into", "exploring", "rejecting"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CEG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 파괴적 변화가 다가올 때 관리자는 그것이 주력 사업에 영향을 주기 전에 '대처할' 역량을 갖춰야 한다 → handle.\n(ii) 두 개의 사업(기존 모델용·새 모델용)을 운영하는 것이 해법으로 제시됨 → 'requirement is'.\n(iii) 병행 운영이 '두 극단'보다 덜 위험하다: 혁신에 '돌이킬 수 없이 뛰어드는 것' vs 기존 방식에 머무는 것 → jumping into.\n정답: C, E, G (handle, requirement is, jumping into)", "trap": "(iii) rejecting은 '기존 방식 고수'와 같은 쪽이라 either A or B의 대조가 성립하지 않는다. (ii) mistaken approach is는 뒤에서 이 병행 운영을 '덜 위험하다'고 권하는 것과 모순.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"obstruct": "방해하다", "stimulate": "자극하다", "handle": "다루다, 대처하다", "competition might have": "경쟁자들이 ~해야 할 수도 있다", "requirement is": "필요한 것은 ~이다", "mistaken approach is": "잘못된 접근은 ~이다", "jumping into": "~에 뛰어들기", "exploring": "탐색하기", "rejecting": "거부하기"}, "src": "verbal33 Q3"}, {"id": "v201_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["It states a viewpoint about Franklin with which the author disagrees.", "It introduces new evidence about Franklin’s role in the collaborative process.", "It explains Franklin’s reputation in terms of a broad scholarly phenomenon.", "It emphasizes the extent to which Franklin relied on others in his workshop.", "It describes Franklin’s approach to writing scientific results."], "columns": null, "pid": "v201_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "강조 문장: 프랭클린이 개인 연구자로 유명한 것은 부분적으로 '한 사람이 집단의 발견을 글로 쓰면 역사가 집단의 노력을 한 사람의 공으로 돌리는' 관행 때문이다.\n→ 프랭클린 개인의 명성을 보다 일반적인 학술적·역사적 현상으로 설명.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 이 문장이 저자 자신의 견해이므로 틀리다. D는 앞 문장들(Syng, Hopkinson)의 역할이지 이 문장의 기능이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"quintessential": "전형적인", "shorthand": "약칭, 간편한 관행", "singular credit": "단독 공로"}, "src": "verbal201 Q4 · 25/8, 25/5, 24/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v201_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "“Emerson” is mentioned in the passage primarily to", "choices": ["Identify the origin of a particular understanding of Franklin", "Elaborate on a view of Franklin that the author takes issue with", "Point to a controversial claim about Franklin’s historical legacy", "Introduce the question of what Franklin’s main scientific influences were", "Suggest that Franklin was resistant to collaboration with other scientists"], "columns": null, "pid": "v201_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: 프랭클린은 '자수성가형 인물'로 그려진다 → Emerson의 'Where is the master who could have instructed Franklin?'(누가 프랭클린을 가르칠 수 있었겠는가) → 'In fact'로 반박: 그는 널리 배웠고 연구는 협력적이었다.\nEmerson 인용은 저자가 반대하는 견해를 구체적으로 보여준다.\n정답: B", "trap": "A(그 견해의 기원)는 Emerson이 그 견해의 출처라는 근거가 없다. 하나의 예일 뿐이다. D는 영향 관계가 아니라 협력이 논점이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Emerson", "glosses": {"quintessential": "전형적인", "self-made": "자수성가한", "take issue with": "~에 이의를 제기하다"}, "src": "verbal201 Q5 · 25/8, 25/5, 24/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v237_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "We tend to think of plants as _____, yet in a sense, some move with spectacular speed as they propel their reproductive particles—seeds and spores, pollen and sperm as far as they can.", "choices": ["hardy", "stationary", "innocuous", "mundane", "inert", "harmless"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'yet'으로 대조: 어떤 식물은 놀라운 속도로 '움직인다'.\n그러므로 우리가 식물에 대해 흔히 생각하는 것 = 움직이지 않는.\nstationary와 inert가 같은 뜻.\n정답: B, E (stationary, inert)", "trap": "innocuous/harmless는 짝이지만 대조 축이 '움직임'이므로 맞지 않는다. hardy, mundane은 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hardy": "강인한, 잘 견디는", "stationary": "정지된, 움직이지 않는", "innocuous": "무해한", "mundane": "평범한, 세속적인", "inert": "움직이지 않는, 비활성의", "harmless": "무해한"}, "src": "verbal237 Q8 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v233_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "There is a vast disparity of computational power between mathematical _____ like many of us and a mathematical prodigy like Ramanujan.", "choices": ["dullards", "enthusiasts", "virtuosos", "tyros", "geniuses", "novices"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "대조: '우리 대부분 같은 수학 ___' vs '라마누잔 같은 수학 천재(prodigy)' 사이의 큰 격차.\n빈칸 = 천재의 반대, 즉 초보자.\ntyros와 novices가 같은 뜻.\n정답: D, F (tyros, novices)", "trap": "dullards(둔한 사람)도 대조는 되지만 짝이 없고, '우리 대부분'을 바보라고 하는 것은 지나치다. virtuosos/geniuses는 짝이지만 대조가 없어진다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"virtuosos": "거장, 대가", "dullards": "둔한 사람, 바보", "enthusiasts": "애호가, 열성팬", "tyros": "초보자, 풋내기", "geniuses": "천재들", "novices": "초보자"}, "src": "verbal233 Q6 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v229_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The series of paintings, as a whole, is remarkably _____ despite the distinctive character of each canvas.", "choices": ["interconnected", "challenging", "comprehensive", "homogenous", "provocative", "uniform"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'despite the distinctive character of each canvas(각 작품의 뚜렷한 개성에도 불구하고)'로 대조.\n전체로서는 놀랍도록 ___하다 → 개성의 반대 = 통일된, 균일한.\nhomogenous와 uniform이 같은 뜻.\n정답: D, F (homogenous, uniform)", "trap": "interconnected(상호 연결된)는 그럴듯하지만 '개별적 개성'의 반대말이 아니고 짝도 없다. challenging/provocative는 짝이지만 despite 대조와 무관하다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"interconnected": "서로 연결된", "challenging": "도전적인, 어려운", "comprehensive": "포괄적인", "homogenous": "동질적인", "provocative": "도발적인", "uniform": "균일한, 한결같은"}, "src": "verbal229 Q6 · 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the northeastern United States, beaver populations had been critically reduced or even _____ in large areas at the end of nineteenth century; as a result, several states instituted prohibitions on beaver trapping.", "choices": ["diminished", "extirpated", "eliminated", "devalued", "weakened", "underrated"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'critically reduced or even ___'에서 or even은 더 강한 정도로 나아가는 신호.\n심각하게 줄어든 것보다 더 심한 것 = 완전히 사라짐 → 그래서 덫 사냥을 금지했다.\nextirpated(근절된)와 eliminated(제거된)가 같은 뜻.\n정답: B, C (extirpated, eliminated)", "trap": "diminished/weakened는 짝이지만 'reduced'와 같은 정도라 'or even'의 강조가 성립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"diminished": "줄어든", "extirpated": "(특정 지역에서) 근절된", "eliminated": "제거된", "devalued": "가치가 떨어진", "weakened": "약해진", "underrated": "과소평가된"}, "src": "verbal221 Q7 · 24/11, 23/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v21_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["provide an example of the dangers of a recent discovery based on faulty data", "illustrate the difficulty of explanation concerning a recent discovery", "assess the credibility of recent findings concerning the as yet unverified existence of a class of objects", "argue that a certain hypothesis fails to account for a seemingly contradictory phenomenon", "demonstrate how difficult it might be to find out the reality of a phenomenon"], "columns": null, "pid": "v21_p3", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문단: 펄서 주위 행성 발견은 잘못된 데이터였고, 확인되었더라도 설명이 어려웠을 것.\n2문단: 'But newer evidence of a different pulsar with planets is more promising' — 그런 행성이 생길 수 있는 이론적 경로를 제시.\n→ 아직 확인되지 않은 '펄서 행성'이라는 대상에 관한 최근 발견들의 신빙성을 평가.\n정답: C", "trap": "B(설명의 어려움)는 1문단에만 해당하고, 2문단의 '더 유망한' 증거를 담지 못한다. A의 '위험'은 지문에서 다루지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pulsar": "펄서(맥동성)", "supernova": "초신성", "coalesce": "합쳐지다, 응집하다", "remnant": "잔해"}, "src": "verbal21 Q10"}, {"id": "v21_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the organization of the passage?", "choices": ["Two sets of research findings relating to similar phenomenon are mentioned, and the theoretical implications of each are discussed.", "A theoretical explanation of a phenomenon is presented and rejected, and a more attractive alternative is offered.", "Two independent and divergent interpretations of a set of observational data are compared and one is favored over the other.", "An example of careless scientific research is introduced and contrasted with a more rigorous analysis of the same material.", "The state of knowledge of an unexplainable phenomenon is outlined and an approach to further investigation is recommended."], "columns": null, "pid": "v21_p3", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문단: 첫 번째 펄서 행성 발견 → 이론적 함의(존재를 설명하기 어려웠을 것).\n2문단: 다른 펄서 행성의 새 증거 → 이론적 함의(남은 가스나 증발한 동반성으로 행성 형성 가능).\n비슷한 현상에 관한 두 연구 결과와 각각의 이론적 함의 → A.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 '이론적 설명이 제시되고 기각된다'고 하지만, 1문단에서 기각되는 것은 설명이 아니라 데이터다. D의 'careless research'는 지문에 없는 비난이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"millisecond pulsar": "밀리초 펄서", "faulty data": "잘못된 데이터", "divergent": "갈라지는, 서로 다른"}, "src": "verbal21 Q11"}, {"id": "v21_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred regarding the pulsar discussed in the first paragraph?", "choices": ["Theorists initially doubted its existence.", "If its existence had been confirmed, astronomers would have turned their attention to the pulsar discussed in the second paragraph.", "If the supernova explosion that created it had been more powerful, the resulting radiation would have preceded the subsequent formation of a planet.", "If it had interacted with a nearby star since the supernova explosion, it would rotate faster than it does.", "Astronomers' interest in it ultimately led to a new theory of planetary formation."], "columns": null, "pid": "v21_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'it rotates relatively slowly, implying that it has not interacted with any nearby star since the supernova'.\n느리게 회전 → 주변 별과 상호작용하지 않았다는 추론이 성립하려면, 상호작용했다면 더 빨리 회전했을 것.\n2문단의 '이웃 별에서 가스를 끌어와 회전 속도가 빨라졌다'도 이를 뒷받침.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 이론가들이 의심한 것은 펄서가 아니라 그 펄서 주위 '행성'의 존재다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rotational speed": "회전 속도", "preexisting": "이전부터 존재하던", "vaporize": "증발시키다"}, "src": "verbal21 Q12"}], [{"id": "v20_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "In general, the relationship between neural activity and behavioral output is __________: multiple behaviors can be associated with activation of the same neurons and multiple neurons can trigger the same behavior.", "choices": ["deterministic", "hardwired", "random", "complicated", "cumulative"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 설명: 같은 뉴런이 여러 행동과 연결되고, 여러 뉴런이 같은 행동을 유발한다 → 일대일이 아닌 다대다 관계.\n빈칸 = 단순하지 않은, 복잡한.\n정답: D (complicated)", "trap": "random(무작위의)은 일대일이 아니라는 점에서 끌리지만, 연관이 있다는 것 자체는 무작위가 아니다. deterministic/hardwired는 단순 대응을 뜻해 반대다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"deterministic": "결정론적인", "hardwired": "고정된, 타고난", "random": "무작위의", "complicated": "복잡한", "cumulative": "누적되는"}, "src": "verbal20 Q1"}, {"id": "v18_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "When in 1980 the father and son pair of Louis and Walter Alvarez and their colleagues linked the end-Cretaceous extinction to a catastrophic extraterrestrial impact, they were met with skepticism by most paleontologists, which was (i)__________ given that geological training since the mid-1800s had emphasized the primacy of (ii)__________.", "choices": null, "columns": [["unsurprising", "unwarranted", "prescient"], ["discernible causes", "gradual processes", "reversible changes"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Alvarez 부자는 대멸종을 '파국적' 외계 충돌과 연결 → 고생물학자들은 회의적.\n'given that'(이유): 1800년대 중반부터 지질학 교육은 ___의 우위를 강조해 왔다.\n(ii) 파국적 사건과 대립하는 것 = gradual processes(점진적 과정).\n(i) 그렇게 교육받았으니 회의적인 것은 당연 → unsurprising.\n정답: A, E (unsurprising, gradual processes)", "trap": "(i) unwarranted(부당한)는 결과적으로 Alvarez가 옳았다는 배경지식에 끌리지만, given that 절은 회의의 '이유'를 설명하므로 놀랍지 않다는 쪽이다. (ii) discernible causes는 catastrophic과 대비되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unsurprising": "놀랍지 않은", "unwarranted": "부당한, 근거 없는", "prescient": "선견지명이 있는", "discernible causes": "식별 가능한 원인", "gradual processes": "점진적 과정", "reversible changes": "되돌릴 수 있는 변화"}, "src": "verbal18 Q3"}, {"id": "v30_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "As cheaper imports drove most California potteries out of business during the 1950s, one company (i) _____. The substantial size and weight of the specialized products produced by Architectural Pottery helped (ii) _____ the company, because it was uneconomical for foreign companies to ship similarly large objects to California.", "choices": null, "columns": [["stagnated", "diversified", "flourished"], ["transform", "insulate", "finance"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'As cheaper imports drove most potteries out of business' — 대부분 망할 때 한 회사는 ___했다 → 대조로 번창했다(flourished).\n(ii) 크고 무거운 제품은 외국 회사가 배송하기에 비경제적 → 수입 경쟁으로부터 회사를 '보호했다' → insulate.\n정답: C, E (flourished, insulate)", "trap": "(i) diversified(다각화)는 생존 전략처럼 보이지만 지문은 특화된 대형 제품 덕분이라고 하므로 반대 방향. (ii) finance는 '수입품과의 경쟁 차단' 논리와 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"stagnated": "정체되었다", "diversified": "다각화했다", "flourished": "번창했다", "transform": "변모시키다", "insulate": "보호하다, 격리하다", "finance": "자금을 대다"}, "src": "verbal30 Q2"}, {"id": "v228_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Proposed technological innovations aimed at removing carbon dioxide from the atmosphere would likely be more (i) _____ than transitioning to clean energy sources. Still, according to some energy experts, given the political barriers to emissions reductions and the scale of reductions needed, it is (ii) _____ that some carbon-capture technology will (iii) _____ some of the worst effects of warming.", "choices": null, "columns": [["realistic", "costly", "effective"], ["unlikely", "puzzling", "inevitable"], ["succeed in countering", "appear to exacerbate", "be required to avoid"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BFI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 탄소 제거 기술은 청정에너지 전환보다 더 ___할 것 → 'Still'로 양보·반전되므로 단점 → costly.\n(ii) 'Still' 이후: 배출 감축의 정치적 장벽과 필요한 감축 규모를 고려하면, 어떤 탄소 포집 기술이 ___하는 것은 피할 수 없다 → inevitable.\n(iii) 감축만으로 부족하므로 최악의 영향을 피하려면 탄소 포집이 '필요하게 될 것' → be required to avoid.\n정답: B, F, I (costly, inevitable, be required to avoid)", "trap": "(iii) succeed in countering은 '반드시 성공한다'는 낙관적 예측이라 inevitable과 어울리지 않고, 근거(감축의 어려움)는 성공이 아니라 필요성을 뒷받침한다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"realistic": "현실적인", "costly": "비용이 많이 드는", "effective": "효과적인", "unlikely": "~할 것 같지 않은", "puzzling": "당혹스러운", "inevitable": "불가피한", "succeed in countering": "대응하는 데 성공하다", "appear to exacerbate": "악화시키는 것처럼 보이다", "be required to avoid": "피하기 위해 필요하게 되다"}, "src": "verbal228 Q4 · 25년 6월, 23년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies that the \"ingredients\" associated with soul food", "choices": ["were rarely included as components of the recipes that Edna Lewis published in her cookbooks", "may have been less representative of any particular United States regional cuisine than has sometimes been assumed", "were differently prepared by African Americans in the South than by other southerners", "were probably consumed less often by African Americans in the South than by African Americans in the North or the West", "would have been largely unavailable to most consumers outside the southern United States before the 1960s"], "columns": null, "pid": "v230_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: soul food는 다양한 공동체를 결속하려고 만든 'simplified narrative', 'invented tradition'이며, Lewis에게는 남부 음식의 'limited and static rendition'.\n즉 그 재료들은 실제 남부 지역 음식의 다양성을 대표하지 못한 단순화된 것.\n→ 어떤 특정 지역 음식을 대표한다고 여겨져 온 것보다 덜 대표적일 수 있다.\n정답: B", "trap": "A(Lewis의 요리책에 거의 없었다)는 Lewis가 soul food에 반발했다는 내용에서 지나치게 나아간 추론이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "ingredients", "glosses": {"strictures": "제약, 구속", "rendition": "해석, 표현", "proponent": "지지자", "static": "정적인, 변화 없는"}, "src": "verbal230 Q14 · 24년 2월, 23년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage mentions \"Americans who first encountered the cuisine in the North or the West\" primarily to", "choices": ["shed light on a divergence of opinions about the origins of soul food", "challenge the idea that soul food reflected the diet of a particular region", "explain why some typical southern foods but not others came to be identified with soul food", "point out the culturally specific nature of Lewis's perspective on soul food", "undermine Lewis's view about soul food by highlighting an inherent contradiction"], "columns": null, "pid": "v230_p4", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'For Lewis, soul food constituted a limited and static rendition of southern food; however, Americans who first encountered the cuisine in the North or the West lacked the same regional frame of reference.'\nLewis의 비판은 남부에서 자란 그녀의 '지역적 관점'에서 나온 것이며, 북부·서부 사람들은 그 관점이 없었다.\n→ Lewis 시각이 문화적으로 특정한 배경에 기반함을 지적.\n정답: D", "trap": "E(Lewis의 견해를 모순을 들어 약화)는 너무 강하다. 저자는 관점의 차이를 지적할 뿐 Lewis를 반박하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Americans who first encountered the cuisine in the North or the West", "glosses": {"frame of reference": "준거 틀, 관점", "culturally specific": "문화적으로 특정한", "divergence": "차이, 분기"}, "src": "verbal230 Q15 · 24년 2월, 23년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v204_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["illustrate the processes through which a particular phenomenon takes place", "introduce additional information in order to qualify a particular explanation for a phenomenon", "explain an apparent contradiction in the results of an experiment concerning a particular phenomenon", "describe two experiments concerning a particular phenomenon in order to compare opposing theories about that phenomenon", "outline the types of evidence that are typically used to support particular theory about a phenomenon"], "columns": null, "pid": "v204_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1문단: TV 뉴스가 더 잘 기억된다 → Paivio의 이중부호화 가설로 설명.\n2문단: 'However' 그림이 말과 같은 의미를 전달할 때(redundant)만 학습이 향상되고, 아니면 오히려 덜 기억한다 → 제한된 주의 용량 이론.\n즉 추가 정보를 제시해 기존 설명에 단서·조건을 단다(qualify).\n정답: B", "trap": "D는 '두 실험'을 묘사해 '상반된 이론'을 비교한다고 하지만, 지문은 실험을 구체적으로 묘사하지 않고 두 이론을 대립시키기보다 첫 설명을 보완·제한한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"qualify": "(주장에) 단서를 달다, 제한하다", "redundant": "(의미가) 중복되는", "retrieval cue": "인출 단서", "attentional capacity": "주의 용량"}, "src": "verbal204 Q7 · 25/9, 25/8, 24/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v204_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, Paivio's dual-coding hypothesis suggests that the difference between viewers' ability to recall television news stories and their ability to recall print versions of the same stores is primarily the result of the fact that viewers can do which of the following?", "choices": ["Reduce information conveyed in two different forms to a single type of memory code.", "Remain within their attentional capacity by avoiding the storage of redundant information.", "Translate text-only information into both verbal-memory and visual-memory codes.", "Determine whether the pictures and words in a television news story coincide.", "Retrieve information through the use of more than one memory code."], "columns": null, "pid": "v204_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 시청각 정보는 언어 부호와 시각 부호 두 가지로 저장되고, 'During recall, the visual-memory code serves as an extra retrieval cue'.\n→ 하나 이상의 기억 부호를 통해 정보를 인출할 수 있다.\n정답: E", "trap": "C는 방향이 반대다. 텍스트만 있는 정보는 언어 부호로만 저장된다. B는 제한된 주의 용량 이론의 내용이지 Paivio 가설이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dual-coding": "이중 부호화", "retrieval cue": "인출 단서", "associated": "연관된"}, "src": "verbal204 Q8 · 25/9, 25/8, 24/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v204_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "If theories of limited attentional capacity, as described in the passage, are correct, which of the following is most likely to be true of the news stories used in the \"studies comparing children's memory\"?", "choices": ["The main message in the television news stories was provided through visual images.", "The effort required to process the print versions of the news stories exceeded the attentional capacity of the children in the studies.", "The visual component of the television news stories provide information that was redundant with the spoken commentary.", "The difficulty of the print versions of the news stories prevent the children from storing the information presented in the studies comparing as a verbal code.", "The television news stories included less verbal information than did the print versions of the stories."], "columns": null, "pid": "v204_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "그 연구들은 TV 뉴스가 더 잘 기억된다는 결과를 보였다.\n제한된 주의 용량 이론에 따르면 시각·언어 정보가 일치하지 않으면 정보가 손실되어 기억이 나빠진다. 학습 향상은 'redundant' 그림일 때만 일어난다.\n따라서 TV 쪽이 더 잘 기억되었다면 그 영상은 음성 해설과 같은 의미를 전달했을(중복된) 것이다.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(주 메시지가 영상으로 전달)는 그럴듯하지만, 지문은 보통 주 메시지가 'spoken commentary'에 있다고 하며, 이 이론으로 TV 우위를 설명하는 핵심은 '중복성'이다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "Studies comparing children's memory", "glosses": {"nonredundant": "중복되지 않는, 서로 다른 의미를 전달하는", "posit": "가정하다, 상정하다", "hinder": "방해하다", "commentary": "해설"}, "src": "verbal204 Q9 · 25/9, 25/8, 24/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v26_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Because the political situation seriously impeded international communication, French scientific research was at that time uncharacteristically _____.", "choices": ["biased", "insular", "competitive", "misleading", "deceptive", "parochial"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'Because' 인과: 정치 상황이 국제 교류를 심각하게 방해함 → 프랑스 과학 연구가 평소와 달리 ___했다.\n국제 교류 단절의 결과 = 고립되고 편협한.\ninsular와 parochial이 같은 뜻.\n정답: B, F (insular, parochial)", "trap": "biased(편향된)는 부정적 뉘앙스로 끌리지만 교류 단절의 직접 결과인 '고립성'과 다르다. misleading/deceptive는 짝이지만 원인과 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"parochial": "편협한, 지역적인", "biased": "편향된", "insular": "고립된, 편협한", "competitive": "경쟁적인", "misleading": "오해를 낳는", "deceptive": "기만적인"}, "src": "verbal26 Q8"}, {"id": "v200_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "There is very little _____ in culture: an art form or a practice (or a language or an institution) can become extinct in a generation if it does not evolve.", "choices": ["inertia", "homogeneity", "symbiosis", "stasis", "cooperation", "waste"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 설명: 예술 형식이나 관습은 진화하지 않으면 한 세대 안에 사라질 수 있다.\n즉 문화에서는 변하지 않고 머물러 있는 것이 거의 불가능하다.\n빈칸 = 정체, 변하지 않음.\ninertia와 stasis가 같은 뜻.\n정답: A, D (inertia, stasis)", "trap": "homogeneity(동질성)는 '변화가 아닌' 느낌이 있지만 콜론 뒤의 핵심은 진화(변화) vs 정체이며, 동질성과는 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inertia": "관성, 정체", "homogeneity": "동질성", "symbiosis": "공생", "stasis": "정체, 정지 상태", "cooperation": "협력", "waste": "낭비"}, "src": "verbal200 Q10 · 25/2, 23/8 중국후기"}, {"id": "v16_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Scientists are finding that the adult brain is far more _____ than they once thought: our behavior and environment can cause substantial rewiring of the brain or a reorganization of its functions and where they are located.", "choices": ["reparable", "heterogeneous", "malleable", "variegated", "complex", "plastic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 설명: 행동과 환경이 뇌의 상당한 재배선이나 기능 재조직을 일으킬 수 있다.\n빈칸 = 변형될 수 있는, 유연한.\nmalleable과 plastic(가소성 있는)이 같은 뜻.\n정답: C, F (malleable, plastic)", "trap": "heterogeneous/variegated는 '다양한'이라는 짝이지만 변화 가능성이 아니라 구성의 다양성이다. complex도 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"reparable": "수리할 수 있는", "heterogeneous": "이질적인, 다양한", "malleable": "가단성 있는, 유연한", "variegated": "다채로운, 얼룩덜룩한", "complex": "복잡한", "plastic": "가소성 있는, 변형 가능한"}, "src": "verbal16 Q10"}, {"id": "v210_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is an assumption on which the argument depends?", "choices": ["Nearby cultures in North and Central America used iron tools for carving stone.", "The Mayans did not use tools made from softer metals than iron for other purposes.", "The stone from which these carvings are made is no softer than the stone used in the carvings of other Central American peoples.", "The stone tools that have been found are among the hardest stone tools used by the Maya.", "Iron tools were found at the same Mayan sites at which the stone tools were found."], "columns": null, "pid": "v210_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 마야인은 조각에 철제 도구를 썼음이 틀림없다.\n근거: 돌 또는 철 도구만 가능했고, 발견된 돌 도구는 충분히 단단하지 않다.\n빈틈: 발견된 돌 도구가 마야의 '가장 단단한' 돌 도구가 아니라면, 발견되지 않은 더 단단한 돌 도구로 조각했을 수 있다.\nD를 부정하면 논증이 무너진다.\n정답: D", "trap": "E(철 도구도 같은 장소에서 발견됨)는 결론을 강화하지만 필요한 가정은 아니다. B는 '돌 또는 철만 가능'이라는 전제가 이미 다른 금속을 배제한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"elaborate": "정교한", "deeply cut": "깊게 새겨진", "assumption": "가정"}, "src": "verbal210 Q13 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v14_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence in the context of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["It suggests why a technique discussed in the passage is becoming outmoded.", "It confirms the existence of dimmer stars in the Milky Way outer halo.", "It explains a shortcoming of a commonly used technique.", "It supports the arguments of astronomers who challenge Heber's conjecture.", "It bolsters the passage's claim that larger telescopes need to be built."], "columns": null, "pid": "v14_p3", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: 분광 분석은 가까운 별에는 쉽지만 은하 바깥 헤일로의 먼 별에는 훨씬 어렵다.\n강조 문장 'Even large telescopes can't gather enough of their light.'는 왜 어려운지 이유를 설명한다.\n→ 흔히 쓰이는 기법(분광 분석)의 한계를 설명.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(기법이 구식이 되고 있다)는 지문에 없다. 가까운 별에는 여전히 straightforward하다. E는 더 큰 망원경이 필요하다는 주장이 지문에 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"radial velocity": "시선 속도", "spectrum": "스펙트럼", "outer halo": "바깥 헤일로", "outmoded": "구식의"}, "src": "verbal14 Q12"}, {"id": "v14_q13", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that Heber would be most likely to agree with which statement about low-mass hypervelocity stars?", "choices": ["The spectral lines of low-mass hypervelocity stars are subject to constant fluctuation.", "Methods other than spectral analysis have failed to confirm the existence of low-mass hypervelocity stars.", "Low-mass hypervelocity stars are more numerous in the Milky Way than B-type stars.", "There are more low-mass hypervelocity stars than currently available methods are capable of detecting.", "The light from low-mass hypervelocity stars cannot be distinguished from the light of brighter B-type stars."], "columns": null, "pid": "v14_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'For this reason, astronomer Ulrich Heber conjectures that there are probably several low-mass hypervelocity stars yet to be discovered.'\n먼 별은 빛이 부족해 분광 분석이 어렵고, 저질량 별은 빛을 훨씬 덜 낸다 → 현재 방법으로 감지하지 못한 별이 더 있다.\n정답: D", "trap": "C(B형 별보다 더 많다)는 '수가 많다'는 비교로 끌리지만, 지문은 B형 별과 수명·밝기만 비교했지 개수를 비교하지 않았다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hypervelocity": "초고속의", "conjecture": "추측하다", "diminutive": "아주 작은", "luminous": "밝은, 빛나는"}, "src": "verbal14 Q13"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.8 / S2 2.7"}, {"set": 17, "sections": [[{"id": "v5_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Astronomy dominated ancient science partly because it was _____ in a way that the physics and biology of the time were not: even in prehistory, people probably used the apparent motion of the Sun, for example, as a crude clock, calendar, and compass.", "choices": ["precise", "exciting", "practical", "lucrative", "provocative"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 빈칸의 근거(부연 설명)이다.\n선사시대에도 사람들이 태양의 움직임을 시계, 달력, 나침반으로 '사용했다(used ... as a crude clock, calendar, and compass)'.\n즉 천문학은 당시 물리학·생물학과 달리 '실제로 쓸모가 있었다'는 뜻 → 빈칸 = 실용적인.\npractical이 '사용'이라는 단서와 정확히 맞는다.\n정답: C (practical)", "trap": "precise(정확한)는 천문학 이미지와 어울려 보이지만, 근거 문장은 '정확성'이 아니라 '쓰임새(used as)'를 말한다. crude(조잡한) clock이라는 표현은 오히려 정밀함과 반대다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"precise": "정확한, 정밀한", "exciting": "흥미진진한", "practical": "실용적인, 쓸모 있는", "lucrative": "수익성이 좋은", "provocative": "도발적인, 자극적인"}, "src": "verbal5 Q1"}, {"id": "v217_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "In the discussions on international patent law, many (i) _____ issues will probably be pushed far into the future. This cautious approach makes diplomatic sense, since attempts over the past 15 years to reach international agreements on patents have (ii) _____ just such sensitive issues.", "choices": null, "columns": [["contentious", "stimulating", "subjective"], ["approached", "articulated", "foundered on"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 뒤 문장의 'just such sensitive issues(바로 그런 민감한 문제들)'가 (i)을 다시 가리킨다 → 빈칸 = 민감한, 논란이 되는 → contentious.\n(ii) 이런 문제를 미래로 미루는 것이 '외교적으로 현명한(cautious approach makes diplomatic sense)' 이유는, 과거 합의 시도가 그 문제들 때문에 '실패했기' 때문 → foundered on(~에 걸려 좌초하다).\napproached/articulated는 실패의 이유가 되지 못한다.\n정답: A (contentious), F (foundered on)", "trap": "(ii)의 approached(다루었다)는 문법상 자연스럽지만, 그것만으로는 왜 지금 문제를 미루는 게 현명한지 설명이 안 된다. 미루는 이유 = 과거의 실패.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"foundered on": "~때문에 좌초(실패)했다", "contentious": "논쟁적인, 논란이 많은", "stimulating": "자극적인, 고무적인", "subjective": "주관적인", "approached": "접근했다, 다루었다", "articulated": "명확히 표현했다"}, "src": "verbal217 Q2 · 25/8, 24/9, 23/6, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v197_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Computers’ triumph in chess had been engineered not by creating machines that (i) _____ human thought, as most experts in artificial intelligence had expected, but by perfecting machines that played like machines. The analogy with flight is (ii) _____: as long as people tried to fly by imitating birds, attaching wings to their arms and flapping madly, they were (iii) _____ to fail. Once engineering escaped the paradigm of the familiar, however, people were soon flying much faster than birds.", "choices": null, "columns": [["aped", "shelved", "subverted"], ["disingenuous", "instructive", "narrow"], ["expected", "likely", "doomed"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AEI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) not A but B 구조: '기계처럼 두는 기계(played like machines)'와 대조 → 인간 사고를 '흉내 낸' 기계 → aped.\n(ii) 콜론 뒤에서 비행의 예가 체스 이야기와 같은 교훈을 준다(새를 흉내 내면 실패, 패러다임을 벗어나야 성공) → 비유가 '교훈적이다' → instructive.\n(iii) 팔에 날개를 달고 퍼덕이는 한 실패할 수밖에 없었다 → doomed to fail(실패할 운명).\n정답: A (aped), E (instructive), I (doomed)", "trap": "(iii)의 likely/expected도 'to fail'과 결합은 되지만, 새 흉내로는 절대 날 수 없다는 강한 의미에는 doomed가 가장 정확하다. (ii) narrow는 비유를 깎아내리는 말로 문맥과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"aped": "흉내 냈다, 모방했다", "shelved": "보류했다", "subverted": "전복시켰다, 훼손했다", "disingenuous": "솔직하지 못한, 위선적인", "instructive": "교훈적인, 유익한", "narrow": "편협한, 좁은", "expected": "예상된", "likely": "~할 것 같은", "doomed": "(실패할) 운명인"}, "src": "verbal197 Q3 · 25/2, 24/9, 22/8 중국후기"}, {"id": "v19_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["It casts doubt on the accuracy of earlier observations of seasonal breeding among shrimp species living near hydrothermal vents.", "It undermines the explanation proposed for seasonal breeding among some shrimp species living near hydrothermal vents.", "It suggests that alternative theories are needed to explain seasonal breeding among shrimp species living near hydrothermal vents.", "It describes the survival benefits to shrimp of mating in parts of the ocean where algae blooms rain down abundantly.", "It supports the explanation proffered for the seasonal breeding observed among some shrimp species living near hydrothermal vents."], "columns": null, "pid": "v19_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞에서 제시된 설명: 유생이 이동 중 먹이를 먹어야 하므로, 봄철 조류(algae)가 쏟아질 때 방출되도록 계절 번식을 한다.\n강조 문장: 새끼에게 난황(yolk)을 주는 종, 또는 계절성 조류 번식이 없는 지역의 종에서는 계절 번식이 발견되지 않았다.\n즉 '먹이가 필요 없거나, 계절성 먹이가 없으면 → 계절 번식도 없다'는 사실로, 조류-먹이 설명을 뒷받침한다.\n정답: E", "trap": "B(설명을 약화)는 정반대. 'no evidence'라는 부정 표현 때문에 약화로 착각하기 쉽지만, 예외 사례가 없다는 것은 오히려 가설과 일치하는 증거다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hydrothermal vent": "열수 분출구", "larval": "유생의", "yolk": "난황, 노른자", "proffered": "제시된, 제안된"}, "src": "verbal19 Q4"}, {"id": "v19_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following statements about hydrothermal vents can be inferred from the passage?", "choices": ["They can propel newly released shrimp larvae toward other vents that are nearby.", "Some of them are found in areas of the ocean with no seasonal algae blooms.", "The food they provide for species living near them does not become seasonally scarce."], "columns": null, "pid": "v19_p1", "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "B: 'vent-dwelling species found in areas of the ocean with no seasonal algae blooms' → 계절성 조류 번식이 없는 해역에도 열수구가 있다는 뜻. 맞음.\nC: 'with food abundant around the vents all year round' → 열수구 주변 먹이는 계절적으로 부족해지지 않는다. 맞음.\nA: 유생을 운반하는 것은 '해류(currents)'이지 열수구가 아니며, 다른 열수구가 '가까이' 있다는 내용도 없다.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "A는 'drift in the currents to colonize new vents'를 비틀어 열수구가 유생을 밀어낸다고 바꾼 오답(주체 왜곡 + nearby는 근거 없음).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"propel": "추진하다, 밀어내다", "colonize": "군체를 이루다, 정착하다", "abundant": "풍부한"}, "src": "verbal19 Q5"}, {"id": "v231_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "While traditional Chinese historiography ostensibly described events in a neutral manner, early historians did not always _____ tendentiousness, sometimes offering moral judgments about the historical figures they discussed.", "choices": ["eschew", "forgo", "denounce", "descry", "defend", "justify"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "While(대조): 겉으로는(ostensibly) 중립적으로 서술했지만 → 실제로는 편향(tendentiousness)을 항상 '피하지는' 않았다.\n뒤의 근거: 때때로 인물에 대해 도덕적 판단을 내렸다 = 편향을 드러냄.\n빈칸 = 피하다, 삼가다 → eschew, forgo.\n정답: A (eschew), B (forgo)", "trap": "denounce(비난하다)는 '편향을 항상 비난하지는 않았다'로 그럴듯하지만, 짝이 되는 동의어가 없고 문장은 역사가 '자신의' 서술 태도를 말한다. descry(발견하다)는 describe와 혼동 유도.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"eschew": "피하다, 삼가다", "forgo": "포기하다, 삼가다", "denounce": "비난하다, 고발하다", "descry": "(멀리서) 발견하다, 알아보다", "defend": "옹호하다", "justify": "정당화하다", "tendentiousness": "편향성"}, "src": "verbal231 Q8 · 25/9, 25/8, 25/5, 25/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v17_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Citing the corruption and intrigue that pervaded politics in the city, my colleague __________ the newspaper's trove of journalism prizes, declaring that finding great stories in the city must be effortless.", "choices": ["slighted", "ignored", "lauded", "disparaged", "confounded", "commended"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "동료는 도시 정치에 부패와 음모가 만연하다는 점을 들어, 이 도시에서 좋은 기사를 찾는 건 '식은 죽 먹기'라고 말했다.\n즉 신문사의 많은 언론상을 대단치 않은 것으로 '깎아내린' 것 → 빈칸 = 부정적 평가.\nslighted(무시하다, 얕보다)와 disparaged(폄하하다)가 같은 의미.\n정답: A (slighted), D (disparaged)", "trap": "lauded/commended(칭찬하다)는 서로 짝이 되지만 'effortless'라는 비꼬는 근거와 반대 방향. ignored는 '언급하며 평가했다'는 문맥과 맞지 않고 짝도 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"slighted": "얕보았다, 경시했다", "ignored": "무시했다(언급하지 않음)", "lauded": "칭찬했다", "disparaged": "폄하했다, 깎아내렸다", "confounded": "혼란스럽게 했다", "commended": "칭찬했다"}, "src": "verbal17 Q7"}, {"id": "v5_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "It is easy to see why the aspiring singer was _____ the awareness of her lack of talent: her shaky voice notwithstanding, she was a kindly woman with a genuine appreciation for music.", "choices": ["surprised by", "insulated from", "humbled by", "appreciative of", "guided to", "buffered against"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 목소리는 떨렸지만(notwithstanding) 그녀는 친절하고 음악을 진심으로 사랑했다.\n'쉽게 이해된다(It is easy to see why)' → 주변 사람들이 그녀에게 재능이 없다는 사실을 굳이 말하지 않았을 것 → 그녀는 그 깨달음으로부터 '보호받았다'.\n빈칸 = 차단·보호되다 → insulated from, buffered against.\n정답: B (insulated from), F (buffered against)", "trap": "humbled by(겸손해지다)나 surprised by는 '재능 없음을 알게 되었다'는 방향이라 근거(착한 사람이라 주변이 감싸줌)와 연결되지 않고 짝도 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"surprised by": "~에 놀란", "insulated from": "~로부터 차단된, 보호된", "humbled by": "~로 겸손해진", "appreciative of": "~을 고마워하는", "guided to": "~로 인도된", "buffered against": "~로부터 완충·보호된"}, "src": "verbal5 Q8"}, {"id": "v233_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Leaders within the Native American culture known as Fort Ancient differed from those of the neighboring Mississippian groups, whose authority was often _____; indeed, one expert has described the Fort Ancient society as intensely egalitarian.", "choices": ["quixotic", "dubious", "uncertain", "coercive", "efficacious", "imperious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Fort Ancient 지도자들은 이웃 미시시피 집단 지도자들과 '달랐다(differed)'.\nindeed 뒤: Fort Ancient 사회는 '매우 평등주의적(intensely egalitarian)'.\n따라서 미시시피 집단의 권위는 그 반대, 즉 강압적·위압적 → coercive, imperious.\n정답: D (coercive), F (imperious)", "trap": "dubious/uncertain(불확실한)은 서로 짝이 되지만 '평등주의'의 반대 개념이 아니다. 대조 대상은 권위의 '강도'이지 '확실성'이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"quixotic": "비현실적인, 공상적인", "dubious": "의심스러운", "uncertain": "불확실한", "coercive": "강압적인", "efficacious": "효과적인", "imperious": "오만한, 고압적인", "egalitarian": "평등주의의"}, "src": "verbal233 Q8 · 25년 1월, 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v11_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions \"studies of lake and shallow ocean sediments\" primarily in order to", "choices": ["describe the results of a novel study", "identify the source of evidence that suggested a hypothesis", "undermine a conventional explanation", "highlight the importance of one type of evidence", "clarify the value of a particular undertaking"], "columns": null, "pid": "v11_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "해당 문장: 'evidence of droughts ... based on studies of lake and shallow ocean sediments has led many researchers to suspect that climate was responsible for the Classic Maya collapse.'\n호수·얕은 바다 퇴적물 연구 = 가뭄의 증거가 나온 출처 → 이것이 '기후가 붕괴의 원인'이라는 가설을 낳았다.\n즉 가설을 제시하게 만든 증거의 출처를 밝힌다.\n정답: B", "trap": "D(한 종류 증거의 중요성 강조)는 그럴듯하지만, 저자는 이 증거를 다른 증거와 비교하거나 중요성을 강조하지 않고 단지 가설의 출처로 언급만 한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "studies of lake and shallow ocean sediments", "glosses": {"sediment": "퇴적물", "susceptible": "~에 취약한", "collapse": "붕괴", "cenote": "세노테(천연 우물)"}, "src": "verbal11 Q10"}, {"id": "v11_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about the reservoirs at Tikal?", "choices": ["They may have been designed by people from northern Yucatan.", "They may have hastened the Classic Maya collapse.", "They were insufficient to protect the Maya against some lingering droughts.", "They were more effective than the cenotes found in northern Yucatan.", "They formed a basis for certain Mayan cultural traditions."], "columns": null, "pid": "v11_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Tikal 저수지는 약 9,600명에게 6~18개월 물을 공급할 수 있었다.\n그러나 'susceptible to frequent or prolonged droughts that approached or exceeded the capacity of their reservoirs' → 저수지 용량을 넘는 장기 가뭄에는 대비가 안 되었다.\nC '일부 오래 지속된 가뭄을 막기에 불충분했다'가 이를 그대로 바꿔 말한 것.\n정답: C", "trap": "B(붕괴를 앞당겼다)는 너무 나감. 저수지가 충분하지 않았다는 것이지 저수지가 붕괴를 '촉진'했다는 근거는 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"reservoir": "저수지", "prolonged": "장기화된", "capacity": "용량", "hasten": "앞당기다, 재촉하다"}, "src": "verbal11 Q11"}, {"id": "v11_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about cenotes?", "choices": ["They allowed people in northern Yucatan to avoid dependence on artificial reservoirs.", "They were less capacious than the artificial reservoirs found in the Maya Lowlands.", "They helped protect people in the Maya Lowlands from prolonged droughts.", "They allowed the Maya to store excess water for times of need.", "They were an important Mayan social innovation."], "columns": null, "pid": "v11_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'In northern Yucatan, the permanent water table is sufficiently shallow that it can be accessed by natural wells known as cenotes.'\n'However, over much of the Maya Lowlands ... too deep ... In response, they constructed artificial reservoirs.'\n즉 인공 저수지는 지하수가 깊은 곳의 대응책이고, 북부 유카탄은 세노테로 지하수에 접근할 수 있어 인공 저수지에 의존할 필요가 없었다.\n정답: A", "trap": "D/E: 세노테는 '자연' 우물이므로 '물을 저장하는 사회적 혁신(social innovation)'이 아니다. 혁신은 인공 저수지 쪽.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"water table": "지하수면", "capacious": "용량이 큰", "artificial": "인공의", "runoff": "빗물 유출수"}, "src": "verbal11 Q12"}], [{"id": "v232_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The fanciful notion that the legislative initiative would bring unlimited social benefits has soured into an equally _____ mood of skepticism and distrust.", "choices": ["valid", "pessimistic", "unanticipated", "pragmatic", "baseless"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심 단서는 'equally': 앞의 생각과 '똑같이' 어떤 성질을 가진 분위기.\n앞의 생각 = fanciful notion(공상적인 생각, 무한한 사회적 이익) → 근거 없는 낙관.\n그것이 회의·불신으로 변질(soured into)되었는데, 이 역시 '똑같이 근거 없다' → baseless.\n정답: E (baseless)", "trap": "pessimistic(비관적인)은 skepticism and distrust와 잘 어울려 보이지만, equally는 앞의 fanciful과 공통점을 요구한다. 앞의 생각은 비관적이지 않았으므로 '똑같이 비관적'은 성립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"soured into": "A가 B로 변질되었다", "valid": "타당한", "pessimistic": "비관적인", "unanticipated": "예상치 못한", "pragmatic": "실용적인", "baseless": "근거 없는", "fanciful": "공상적인, 비현실적인"}, "src": "verbal232 Q1 · 25/7, 25/4, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "When the United States government created the Post Office at the founding of the republic, it didn't invite rival postal firms to compete; in fact, it created a monopoly. That monopoly, however, was (i) _____ free expression because of the policies Congress adopted, which (ii) _____ the circulation of newspapers irrespective of their viewpoint and spread postal service throughout the country.", "choices": null, "columns": [["conducive to", "threatened by", "dependent on"], ["subsidized", "limited", "trivialized"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "however: 경쟁을 허용하지 않은 독점이었지만(부정적 이미지), 그럼에도 표현의 자유에 '도움이 되었다' → (i) conducive to.\n그 이유 = 의회의 정책: 관점과 무관하게 신문 유통을 (ii) 하고, 전국에 우편 서비스를 확산 → 신문 유통을 '지원했다' → subsidized.\nlimited/trivialized는 표현의 자유를 돕는 정책이 될 수 없다.\n정답: A (conducive to), D (subsidized)", "trap": "(i) threatened by는 '독점=자유 위협'이라는 상식적 연상을 노린 함정. however가 그 예상을 뒤집는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"conducive to": "~에 도움이 되는", "threatened by": "~에 의해 위협받는", "dependent on": "~에 의존하는", "subsidized": "보조금을 주어 지원했다", "limited": "제한했다", "trivialized": "하찮게 만들었다"}, "src": "verbal198 Q3 · 25/7, 24/3, 23/5, 22/12 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Maddox presents a more (i) _____ view of Franklin than the stereotyped rendering of her as the martyr whose data were stolen. By focusing substantial attention on Franklin's achievements working on the molecular structure of coal and on virus research, Maddox (ii) _____ reducing Franklin's legacy to her involvement in the (admittedly central) scientific story of DNA.", "choices": null, "columns": [["conventional", "facile", "complex"], ["resists", "deplores", "invites"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'stereotyped rendering(정형화된 묘사, 데이터를 도둑맞은 순교자)'보다 '더 ~한' 관점 → 정형화의 반대 = 복잡하고 다면적인 → complex.\n(ii) 석탄 분자구조·바이러스 연구 등 다른 업적에 상당한 관심을 기울임으로써 → 프랭클린의 유산을 DNA 이야기로만 축소하는 것에 '저항한다' → resists.\n정답: C (complex), D (resists)", "trap": "(ii) deplores(개탄하다)는 방향은 맞지만, 다른 업적에 '초점을 맞추는' 행동은 축소를 비난하는 것이 아니라 축소를 피하는/거부하는 것이다. (i) facile은 stereotyped와 같은 쪽이라 오답.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"conventional": "관습적인, 틀에 박힌", "facile": "피상적인, 안이한", "complex": "복잡한, 다면적인", "resists": "저항하다, 거부하다", "deplores": "개탄하다", "invites": "초래하다, 불러오다"}, "src": "verbal220 Q3 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v28_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Although Uruk in southern Mesopotamia has been (i) _____ as being both the first city and the model for later ones, at least two sites in northern Mesopotamia have yielded clear evidence of urbanization long before the existing evidence from Uruk, and other discoveries indicate that some of the (ii) _____ early urbanism were invented not in southern Mesopotamia but in the north. These findings have led some archaeologists to (iii) _____ a serious reconsideration about when and where the first cities arose.", "choices": null, "columns": [["established", "contested", "presented"], ["defining features of", "derivative aspects of", "traditional theories about"], ["evaluate", "ignore", "propose"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) Although: 우루크가 최초의 도시이자 이후 도시의 모델로 '인정되어 왔지만' ↔ 북부에서 더 이른 도시화 증거가 나왔다 → 기존 통념을 나타내는 말 → established.\n(ii) 초기 도시화의 '핵심적 특징(defining features)' 중 일부가 남부가 아니라 북부에서 발명되었다 → 우루크가 '모델'이라는 주장에 대한 반박. derivative(파생적) 특징이면 반박 효과가 없다.\n(iii) 이런 발견으로 일부 고고학자들이 최초 도시의 시기와 장소에 대한 심각한 재고를 '제안했다' → propose.\n정답: A (established), D (defining features of), I (propose)", "trap": "(i) contested(이의가 제기된)는 Although 대조를 무너뜨린다(이미 반박되고 있었다면 뒤의 새 증거와 대조가 안 됨). (iii) evaluate a reconsideration은 어색하다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"established": "확립된, 인정된", "contested": "이의가 제기된", "presented": "제시된", "defining features of": "~의 핵심적 특징", "derivative aspects of": "~의 파생적 측면", "traditional theories about": "~에 대한 전통적 이론", "evaluate": "평가하다", "ignore": "무시하다", "propose": "제안하다"}, "src": "verbal28 Q4"}, {"id": "v214_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about art collectors in antiquity", "choices": ["They were largely ignorant about who created the artworks they owned.", "They did not consider originality a quality that made an artwork more collectible.", "They had a unique understanding of the notion of art forgery.", "They were more concerned about the subject matter of an artwork than about the identity of its creator.", "They did not view their art purchases as investments, as do some art collectors today."], "columns": null, "pid": "v214_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'There were many collectors, but they seem to have found copies as desirable as originals.'\n고대 수집가들은 복제품을 원본만큼 원했다 → 원본성(originality)을 수집 가치를 높이는 요소로 보지 않았다.\nB가 이를 정확히 바꿔 말함.\n정답: B", "trap": "A(누가 만들었는지 몰랐다)는 '서명도 작가 제작의 증거로 여겨지지 않았다'에서 끌어낸 과잉 추론. 신경을 안 썼다는 것이지 '무지했다'는 것이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"forgery": "위조(품)", "antiquity": "고대", "collectible": "수집 가치가 있는", "expertise": "전문 지식"}, "src": "verbal214 Q14 · 24/5, 23/9, 23/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v214_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions “many collectors\" primarily to", "choices": ["describe an exception to an artistic trend in antiquity", "underscore the universality of the appreciation of works of art", "provide an example of a disputable claim about art forgery in antiquity", "dispel a misconception about art culture in antiquity", "cite a factor that might be expected to promote art forgery in antiquity"], "columns": null, "pid": "v214_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 위조는 미술품 '수요(demand)'가 존재한 만큼 오래되었다는 통념이 있다.\n'There were many collectors, but ...' → 수집가가 많았다 = 수요가 있었다 = 위조를 부추길 만한 요인.\n하지만(but) 그들은 복제품도 원본만큼 원했기 때문에 위조라는 개념이 생기지 않았다.\n즉 '많은 수집가'는 위조를 촉진할 것으로 예상되는 요인을 제시한 것.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(위조에 관한 논쟁적 주장의 예)는 '수집가가 많았다'를 통념 자체로 착각하게 만든다. 논쟁적 주장은 첫 문장의 통념이고, many collectors는 사실(fact)로 제시된다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "many collectors", "glosses": {"underscore": "강조하다", "dispel": "(오해를) 없애다", "universality": "보편성", "disputable": "논란의 여지가 있는"}, "src": "verbal214 Q15 · 24/5, 23/9, 23/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v12_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following most accurately describes the organization of the passage?", "choices": ["A theory is proposed, refuted, and then amended.", "The thesis of the passage is stated and several views for and against that thesis are compared and contrasted.", "Opposing views are presented, classified, and then reconciled.", "An assertion is made and an elaboration of that assertion is provided.", "An argument is advanced and evidence is presented to refute it."], "columns": null, "pid": "v12_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장(주장): 진보주의는 역사가들에 의해 여러 차례 상당한 재평가를 거쳤다.\n이후 1960년대 → 1970~80년대 → 1990년대 초의 평가 변화를 차례로 설명 = 그 주장의 상술(elaboration).\n저자가 어느 견해를 반박하거나 화해시키지 않는다.\n정답: D", "trap": "C(대립 견해 제시 후 화해)는 여러 견해가 나오기 때문에 끌리지만, 저자는 견해들을 분류하거나 화해시키지 않고 시간 순서대로 나열할 뿐이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"amorphous": "형태가 없는, 모호한", "reevaluation": "재평가", "reactionary": "반동적인", "coherence": "일관성"}, "src": "verbal12 Q5"}, {"id": "v12_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, the term \"progressive minimum\" is used by scholars who have", "choices": ["determined the quintessential elements of reform movements in general", "claimed that progressivism was a movement grounded in a set of common beliefs", "underrated the impact and historical significance of progressivism", "defined progressivism as a unified effort led by a core of proponents", "questioned the basic motivation underlying the inception of progressivism"], "columns": null, "pid": "v12_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'they insisted that there is an identifiable “progressive minimum”, a core of belief and action that lends coherence to the concept.'\n'progressive minimum'을 쓰는 학자들은 진보주의에 일관성을 주는 공통 신념과 행동의 핵심이 있다고 주장했다.\nB '공통 신념에 기반한 운동이라고 주장했다'가 이를 바꿔 말함.\n정답: B", "trap": "D(핵심 지지자들이 이끈 통일된 운동)는 'core'를 '핵심 인물 집단'으로 바꿔치기한 오답. 지문의 core는 '신념과 행동의 핵심'이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "progressive minimum", "glosses": {"quintessential": "전형적인, 본질적인", "inception": "시작, 발단", "coherence": "일관성", "diverse": "다양한"}, "src": "verbal12 Q6"}, {"id": "v12_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["analyze the early-twentieth-century sociopolitical environment of the United States", "affirm the profound differences among reformist groups contending for power in the early-twentieth-century United States", "explain a radical approach to promoting democracy in the early twentieth-century United States", "argue that the results achieved by several decades of reform activity begun in the early-twentieth-century United States were paradoxical", "trace the course of inquiry over time regarding an aspect of early twentieth-century United States history"], "columns": null, "pid": "v12_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문은 진보주의라는 20세기 초 미국사의 한 측면에 대해 학자들의 평가가 1960년대 → 이후 20년 → 1990년대 초로 어떻게 변해 왔는지 추적한다.\nE '시간에 따른 탐구 흐름을 추적한다'가 정확한 요약.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(개혁 결과가 역설적이었다고 주장)는 마지막 문장의 'conservative and even reactionary results'만 확대한 부분 정보. 저자는 이를 논증하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sociopolitical": "사회정치적인", "paradoxical": "역설적인", "trace": "추적하다", "contend": "경쟁하다, 다투다"}, "src": "verbal12 Q7"}, {"id": "v234_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Jimi Hendrix was a pivotal figure in the visionary aesthetic movement known as Afrofuturism, which is steeped in African American musical tradition yet _____ technological innovation, from synthesizers to spaceships.", "choices": ["circumspect about", "indebted to", "enthralled by", "wary of", "captivated by", "heedful of"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'steeped in African American musical tradition yet ___ technological innovation': 전통에 뿌리박고 있지만(yet) 기술 혁신에는 ~하다.\n'visionary aesthetic movement', 신시사이저부터 우주선까지 → 기술 혁신에 매료된 긍정적 태도.\n빈칸 = 매혹되다 → enthralled by, captivated by.\n정답: C (enthralled by), E (captivated by)", "trap": "yet을 '부정 전환'으로만 보면 wary of/circumspect about(경계하는)을 고르기 쉽다. 여기서 yet은 '전통 vs 미래 기술'의 대비이지 긍정 vs 부정이 아니다. indebted to는 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"steeped in": "뿌리박고 있다", "circumspect about": "~에 신중한", "indebted to": "~에 빚진", "enthralled by": "~에 매료된", "wary of": "~을 경계하는", "captivated by": "~에 사로잡힌", "heedful of": "~에 주의하는"}, "src": "verbal234 Q12 · 24년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v20_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Even though the man was reserved in his speech, he thoroughly understood his mother, which made him far from __________ as people usually thought.", "choices": ["comprehensive", "ingenuous", "sophisticated", "foolish", "simple", "sententious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Even though: 그는 말수가 적었지만(→ 사람들은 그를 단순하다고 여김), 어머니를 깊이 이해했다.\n그래서 사람들이 생각한 것처럼 '~한 사람과는 거리가 멀다(far from ___)' → 빈칸 = 사람들이 잘못 생각한 부정적 성질 = 어리석은, 단순한.\nfoolish, simple이 짝.\n정답: D (foolish), E (simple)", "trap": "ingenuous(순진한)는 simple과 비슷해 보이지만 '솔직하고 순진한'이라는 뜻으로 지적 이해력 부족을 뜻하지 않는다. sophisticated는 방향이 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ingenuous": "순진한, 솔직한", "sententious": "훈계조의, 격언을 늘어놓는", "comprehensive": "포괄적인", "sophisticated": "세련된, 정교한", "foolish": "어리석은", "simple": "단순한, 우둔한"}, "src": "verbal20 Q9"}, {"id": "v208_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Smil's analysis of climate change is even more _____ than that supplied by most well-informed writers, and thus deserves serious consideration.", "choices": ["nuanced", "unoriginal", "complex", "derivative", "partisan", "compelling"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'even more ___ than ... most well-informed writers, and thus deserves serious consideration'\n빈칸은 진지하게 고려할 가치가 있는 이유 → 긍정적 성질.\n잘 아는 저자들보다 '더' 뛰어난 점 = 세밀하고 복잡한 분석 → nuanced, complex.\n정답: A (nuanced), C (complex)", "trap": "compelling(설득력 있는)도 긍정이라 들어갈 것 같지만 짝이 없다. unoriginal/derivative는 서로 짝이지만 부정적이라 thus deserves와 모순.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"nuanced": "미묘한 차이를 살린, 섬세한", "unoriginal": "독창적이지 않은", "complex": "복잡한", "derivative": "모방한, 독창성 없는", "partisan": "당파적인", "compelling": "설득력 있는"}, "src": "verbal208 Q12 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v8_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, most seriously undermines the hypothesis?", "choices": ["When a power station near which manatees usually gather is shut down for even a few hours, manatees move elsewhere.", "Other marine animals that feed on vegetation also congregate in large numbers in the vicinity of power stations.", "All of the species of vegetation that grow near the power stations also grow elsewhere in the coastal waters of southern Florida, though not nearly as abundantly.", "Even more manatees than usual gather near power stations during the winter months, when vegetation growth away from power stations slows.", "Manatees also tend to gather in waters where high levels of nutrients support especially abundant vegetation."], "columns": null, "pid": "v8_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "가설: 매너티는 따뜻한 물이 키운 '풍부한 먹이(식물)' 때문에 발전소 근처에 모인다.\nA: 발전소가 몇 시간만 멈춰도 매너티가 떠난다. 식물은 몇 시간 만에 사라지지 않으므로, 매너티를 끄는 것은 먹이가 아니라 '따뜻한 물 자체'라는 대안 설명이 된다 → 가설 약화.\nD, E는 먹이를 따라간다는 가설을 오히려 강화한다.\n정답: A", "trap": "C(같은 식물이 다른 곳에도 자라지만 덜 풍부)는 약화처럼 보이지만, 발전소 근처가 더 풍부하다는 점에서 오히려 가설과 일치한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"congregate": "모이다", "vicinity": "부근", "undermine": "약화시키다", "abundantly": "풍부하게"}, "src": "verbal8 Q11"}, {"id": "v240_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the sentence highlighted in the passage?", "choices": ["It suggests a direction for future research regarding, a theory presented earlier in the passage.", "It presents evidence that will support a theory that is introduced in the following sentence.", "It questions the usefulness of a particular version of a theory.", "It clarifies an ambiguous statement made earlier in the passage.", "It presents a general rule to which the passage will identify the exception"], "columns": null, "pid": "v240_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "강조 문장: 'Consequently, ecological theory is rarely directly relevant to the practice of conservation biology.' → 생태 이론은 보전생물학에 거의 직접 관련이 없다는 일반 규칙.\n바로 다음 문장: 'One notable exception is MacArthur's theory of island biogeography' → 그 규칙의 예외를 제시.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(특정 버전의 이론의 유용성 의문)는 rarely relevant를 보고 고르기 쉽지만, 이 문장은 생태 이론 '전반'에 대한 일반론이지 특정 버전에 대한 것이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"idealized": "이상화된", "biogeography": "생물지리학", "exception": "예외", "consequently": "결과적으로"}, "src": "verbal240 Q14 · 24년 1월, 22년 10월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that the author would probably agree with which of the following statements?", "choices": ["The practice of conservation biology may be directly affected by MacArthur's theory of island biogeography.", "Undisturbed systems surrounded by biologically distinct areas may be helpful in estimating birth and death rate parameters more accurately.", "The similarity between nature preserves and the islands studies in MacArthur's biogeography theory may help predict species richness in nature preserves."], "columns": null, "pid": "v240_p4", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 생태 이론은 보전생물학에 '거의' 직접 관련 없지만 MacArthur 이론은 'notable exception' → 직접 영향을 줄 수 있다. 맞음.\nC: 이론은 섬의 크기·고립 정도로 종 풍부도를 예측하고, 자연보호구역은 섬과 유사할 수 있다 → 보호구역의 종 풍부도 예측에 도움. 맞음.\nB: 출생·사망률 추정이 어렵다는 말은 있지만, 고립된 생태계가 추정에 도움이 된다는 내용은 없다.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "B는 지문의 두 부분(출생·사망률 추정의 어려움 + 비교적 교란되지 않은 생태계)을 억지로 이어 붙인 오답.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"species richness": "종 풍부도", "analogous": "유사한", "parameter": "변수, 매개변수", "isolation": "고립"}, "src": "verbal240 Q15 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.8 / S2 2.8"}, {"set": 18, "sections": [[{"id": "v231_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Monumental changes taking place in the structures of world business match some equally _____ changes taking place in the relations of international companies to the governments with which they deal.", "choices": ["ill-advised", "magnanimous", "portentous", "discreet", "overblown"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'Monumental changes ... match some equally ___ changes': equally가 핵심 → 앞의 monumental(엄청난, 기념비적인)과 같은 성질.\n빈칸 = 중대한, 엄청난 → portentous(중대한, 앞날을 예고하는).\n다른 선택지는 '규모·중요성'과 관계가 없다.\n정답: C (portentous)", "trap": "overblown(과장된)은 '크다'는 느낌이 있지만 '실제보다 부풀려진'이라는 부정적 의미라 monumental과 동등하지 않다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"magnanimous": "관대한, 도량이 넓은", "ill-advised": "경솔한, 무분별한", "portentous": "중대한, 전조가 되는", "discreet": "신중한, 조심스러운", "overblown": "과장된, 부풀려진"}, "src": "verbal231 Q1 · 25년 5월, 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v215_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "A long-running philosophical debate in the field of stratigraphy—the study of sequences of sedimentary rocks—is whether the sedimentary record represents mainly (i) _____ happenings (e.g., waves and tides) or their opposite, (ii) _____ events (e.g., hurricanes and flash floods).", "choices": null, "columns": [["measurable", "everyday", "discrete"], ["destructive", "extraordinary", "unclassifiable"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "괄호 속 예시가 결정적 단서.\n(i) 예: 파도와 조수(waves and tides) → 늘 일어나는 일 → everyday.\n(ii) 'their opposite(그 반대)', 예: 허리케인, 돌발 홍수 → 드문 사건 → extraordinary.\n정답: B (everyday), E (extraordinary)", "trap": "(ii) destructive(파괴적인)는 허리케인·홍수와 잘 어울리지만 everyday의 '반대'가 아니다. their opposite가 반의어를 요구한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"measurable": "측정 가능한", "everyday": "일상적인", "discrete": "별개의, 분리된", "destructive": "파괴적인", "extraordinary": "비범한, 이례적인", "unclassifiable": "분류할 수 없는", "stratigraphy": "층서학"}, "src": "verbal215 Q2 · 25/11, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v239_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Until recentily, superhero comics were seen as irredeemably (i) _____; they were widely disparaged for being so (ii) _____ in conception and execution, and anyone who was a fan was given plenty of reasons to be (iii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["puerile", "innocuous", "facetious"], ["lowbrow", "shrewd", "moralistic"], ["heartened", "emulated", "abashed"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'irredeemably(구제불능으로) ___', 이어서 widely disparaged(널리 폄하됨) → 부정적 → puerile(유치한).\n(ii) 기획과 실행이 너무 ~해서 폄하됨 → 부정적 → lowbrow(저급한).\n(iii) 팬들은 ~할 이유가 많았다 → 무시당하는 취미 → abashed(부끄러운).\n정답: A (puerile), D (lowbrow), I (abashed)", "trap": "(i) innocuous(무해한)는 비판의 근거가 되기 약하다. (ii) moralistic(교훈적인)도 비판 이유가 될 수는 있지만 puerile과 일관된 '유치·저급' 흐름에는 lowbrow가 맞다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"puerile": "유치한", "lowbrow": "저급한, 교양 없는", "innocuous": "무해한", "facetious": "경박한, 우스갯소리의", "shrewd": "영리한, 빈틈없는", "moralistic": "교훈적인, 도덕주의적인", "heartened": "격려받은", "emulated": "모방된", "abashed": "부끄러운, 무안한"}, "src": "verbal239 Q3 · 25/9, 25/8, 25/7, 25/5, 25/3, 24/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v219_q4", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage indicates which of the following about firewood?", "choices": ["Its use has a damaging effect on the quality of soil.", "Its advantages over coal as a fuel have been exaggerated.", "Its effect on human health is partly a result of the conditions under which it is burned."], "columns": null, "pid": "v219_p4", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'Firewood use results in deforestation, loss of ecosystems, and degradation of soil quality.' → 토양의 질 저하. 맞음.\nC: 'firewood is generally burned in homes with poor ventilation and poses a greater health risk' → 건강 영향은 환기 나쁜 곳에서 태우는 조건 때문이기도 하다. 맞음.\nB: 지문은 장작의 '장점이 과장되었다'고 말하지 않는다.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "B는 지문이 장작보다 석탄이 낫다고 하니 그럴듯해 보이지만, 장작의 장점이 과장되었다는 주장 자체는 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"deforestation": "삼림 벌채", "degradation": "저하, 악화", "particulate": "미립자", "ventilation": "환기"}, "src": "verbal219 Q4 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v219_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions arsenic and lead primarily in order to", "choices": ["identify some of the factors that might support a particular conclusion", "challenge an assertion about the toxicity of various sources of fuel", "establish the grounds for a recommendation concerning future energy use", "acknowledge a weakness of the hypothesis proposed by the author", "question the advantages of switching from one source of fuel to another"], "columns": null, "pid": "v219_p4", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'Because coal contains toxic materials such as arsenic and lead ... one might therefore conclude that no good case could be made for burning it.'\n비소와 납은 '석탄을 태울 이유가 없다'는 결론을 뒷받침할 수 있는 요인의 예시.\n저자는 이어서 'But that depends on where one is starting from'으로 반론한다.\n정답: A", "trap": "D(저자 가설의 약점 인정)는 함정. 비소·납은 저자의 주장이 아니라 저자가 반박하려는 반대 측 결론의 근거다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "arsenic and lead", "glosses": {"arsenic": "비소", "acid rain": "산성비", "toxic": "유독한", "reflectivity": "반사율"}, "src": "verbal219 Q5 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v31_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Agencies responsible for protecting natural resources too often issue permits allowing exploitation of those resources, a process that remains _____ given that agencies have become experts at masking their decisions in the scientific terms.", "choices": ["controversial", "exacting", "obscure", "onerous", "opaque", "misleading"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "given that(~을 고려하면): 기관들이 결정을 과학 용어로 '가리는(masking)' 데 전문가가 되었다.\n그래서 허가 과정이 계속 '불투명·이해하기 어렵다' → 빈칸 = 불분명한.\nobscure, opaque가 짝.\n정답: C (obscure), E (opaque)", "trap": "misleading(오해를 일으키는)은 masking과 어울려 보이지만 짝이 없고, 과학 용어로 가리는 것의 직접 결과는 '이해하기 어려움'이다. controversial은 근거와 무관.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"controversial": "논란이 많은", "exacting": "까다로운, 엄격한", "obscure": "모호한, 불분명한", "onerous": "부담스러운, 성가신", "opaque": "불투명한, 이해하기 어려운", "misleading": "오해의 소지가 있는"}, "src": "verbal31 Q8"}, {"id": "v217_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "\"Revolutionary\" and \"unique\" are words that have become _____: every century in human history is described as unique, and every year, somewhere in the world, some event is characterized as revolutionary.", "choices": ["overused", "interchangeable", "confused", "distorted", "trite", "contentious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 모든 세기가 unique하다고 묘사되고, 매년 어딘가의 사건이 revolutionary라고 불린다.\n즉 두 단어가 너무 자주 쓰여 의미가 닳았다 → 빈칸 = 남용된, 진부한.\noverused, trite가 짝.\n정답: A (overused), E (trite)", "trap": "interchangeable(서로 바꿔 쓸 수 있는)은 두 단어가 함께 나와 끌리지만, 근거는 두 단어가 서로 대체된다는 것이 아니라 '남발된다'는 것이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"overused": "남용된", "interchangeable": "서로 바꿀 수 있는", "confused": "혼동된", "distorted": "왜곡된", "trite": "진부한", "contentious": "논쟁적인"}, "src": "verbal217 Q8 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v13_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The twentieth-century Chinese painter Fu Baoshi was an impassioned advocate of ink-and-brush painting, a form that was often dismissed by his contemporaries as _____ a relic of the old imperialist elite.", "choices": ["fusty", "conventional", "constricted", "retrograde", "effete", "sentimental"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "동시대인들은 수묵화를 '___ 한, 옛 제국주의 엘리트의 유물(a relic of the old imperialist elite)'이라고 무시했다.\n빈칸은 relic(유물)과 같은 방향 → 낡고 시대에 뒤떨어진.\nfusty(케케묵은), retrograde(퇴행적인)가 짝.\n정답: A (fusty), D (retrograde)", "trap": "conventional(관습적인)은 '오래된'과 연관되지만 비난조의 '시대착오'까지는 아니고 짝이 없다. effete(쇠약한, 퇴폐적인)도 엘리트와 어울려 보이지만 '낡음'과는 다르다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"fusty": "케케묵은, 낡은", "retrograde": "퇴보적인, 시대에 역행하는", "effete": "쇠약한, 기력 없는, 퇴폐적인", "conventional": "관습적인", "constricted": "제한된, 답답한", "sentimental": "감상적인"}, "src": "verbal13 Q9"}, {"id": "v219_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In many branches of science, our knowledge and technology have advanced so rapidly that new studies carried out with improved instruments and techniques may well _____ research done just twenty years earlier.", "choices": ["confirm", "supplant", "elaborate", "supersede", "question", "validate"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "so ... that 인과 구조: 지식과 기술이 매우 빠르게 발전했으므로 → 개선된 장비로 한 새 연구가 불과 20년 전 연구를 '대체'할 수 있다.\n빈칸 = 대신하다, 낡은 것으로 만들다 → supplant, supersede.\n정답: B (supplant), D (supersede)", "trap": "confirm/validate(확인하다)는 서로 짝이지만 '급속한 발전'이라는 원인과 연결되지 않는다. question도 가능해 보이지만 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"confirm": "확인하다", "supplant": "대체하다, 밀어내다", "elaborate": "상술하다, 정교하게 하다", "supersede": "대신하다, 대체하다", "question": "의문을 제기하다", "validate": "입증하다"}, "src": "verbal219 Q6 · 24년 3월, 23년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v27_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author suggests which of the following about motivated reasoning?", "choices": ["It allows judges to take into consideration a wide range of views beyond those that they themselves hold.", "It has a greater impact on the decisions of judges with certain kinds of policy preferences than on the decisions of judges with other preferences.", "It is unlikely to result in ideologically biased judicial decisions in cases where the law is open to multiple interpretations.", "Its effects on a decision may be mitigated by exposure to compelling arguments that challenge the decision maker's biases.", "Its impact on judicial decision-making may be more evident in decisions rendered by the United States Supreme Court than in decisions rendered by other courts."], "columns": null, "pid": "v27_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'The presence of stronger arguments contrary to preferences reduces the influence of motivations.'\n선호와 반대되는 강한 논증이 있으면 동기화된 추론의 영향이 줄어든다.\nD '편향에 도전하는 설득력 있는 논증에 노출되면 효과가 완화될 수 있다'가 그대로 바꿔 말한 것.\n정답: D", "trap": "C는 정반대. 지문은 법이 덜 확정적일 때(여러 해석이 가능할 때) 동기화된 추론의 영향이 '최고조(apex)'라고 한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"mitigate": "완화하다", "apex": "정점", "determinate": "확정적인", "predisposition": "성향"}, "src": "verbal27 Q10"}, {"id": "v27_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author uses \"the United States Supreme Court\" to illustrate the argument because of a belief that", "choices": ["the Supreme Court is obligated to render its decisions without regard to its members' ideological predispositions", "the record of the Supreme Court shows it to be roughly similar to other courts in the frequency with which its decisions reflect particular policy preferences", "the extent to which decisions made by the Supreme Court are affected by reasonableness constraints is relatively easy to determine", "the unanimous decisions sometimes handed down by the Supreme Court would be unlikely to come from an ideologically diverse court if motivated reasoning were unchecked", "the members of the Supreme Court provide clear and extended explanations of the reasoning that has informed their decisions"], "columns": null, "pid": "v27_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'The limitations of the power of motivated reasoning are apparent from the numerous unanimous opinions of the United States Supreme Court (whose members generally represent a range of ideological predispositions)'.\n이념적으로 다양한 대법관들이 만장일치 판결을 많이 낸다 → 동기화된 추론이 제약 없이 작동한다면 이런 만장일치는 나오기 어렵다.\n그래서 대법원은 동기화된 추론의 한계를 보여주는 예.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(대법원은 이념과 무관하게 판결할 '의무'가 있다)는 규범적 주장으로 지문에 없다. 저자는 의무가 아니라 실제 판결 결과(만장일치)를 근거로 든다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unanimous": "만장일치의", "ideological": "이념적인", "predisposition": "성향, 경향", "render": "(판결을) 내리다"}, "src": "verbal27 Q11"}, {"id": "v27_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author suggests which of the following about the \"circumstances\" mentioned in the passage?", "choices": ["They allow decision makers to rationalize lapses in their objectivity.", "They tend to undermine the efficacy of reasonableness constraints.", "They may weaken the effect of policy preferences on decisions.", "They are insufficiently distinguished from one another by attitudinalists.", "They can disguise the extent to which a decision has been influenced by motivated reasoning."], "columns": null, "pid": "v27_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'circumstances' = 바로 앞의 조건들: 결정의 이해관계가 클 때, 결정을 정당화해야 할 때, 결정이 공개될 때 → 이때 'accuracy of decision-making is enhanced'.\n이것들은 동기화된 추론에 대한 '합리성 제약(reasonableness constraints)'의 예다.\n따라서 이런 상황은 정책 선호가 결정에 미치는 영향을 약화시킬 수 있다.\n정답: C", "trap": "B(합리성 제약의 효과를 약화)는 정반대. 이 상황들 자체가 합리성 제약의 예시다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "circumstances", "glosses": {"rationalize": "합리화하다", "efficacy": "효력", "lapse": "실수, 일탈", "constraint": "제약"}, "src": "verbal27 Q12"}], [{"id": "v214_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Bone is a physiologically _____ tissue: it can change size and shape to meet the body's needs during the various stages of an animal's life.", "choices": ["rigid", "vulnerable", "active", "permeable", "lightweight"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 뼈는 동물의 일생 동안 몸의 필요에 맞춰 크기와 모양을 바꿀 수 있다.\n변화하고 반응한다 → 생리적으로 '활동적인' 조직 → active.\n정답: C (active)", "trap": "rigid(단단한)는 뼈에 대한 상식적 이미지라 끌리지만, 근거(크기와 모양이 변한다)와 정반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"permeable": "투과성의", "rigid": "단단한, 경직된", "vulnerable": "취약한", "active": "활동적인", "lightweight": "가벼운"}, "src": "verbal214 Q1 · 25년 6월, 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v226_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "There has been a noticeable reversal from the time when (i) _____ was accepted as the essential characteristic of genuine science: now the role of (ii) _____ in scientific research is generating a great deal of interest.", "choices": null, "columns": [["disciplinary specialization", "long apprenticeship", "dispassionate inquiry"], ["speculation", "emotion", "technology"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심 단서: 'noticeable reversal(눈에 띄는 반전)' → (i)과 (ii)는 서로 반대 개념이어야 한다.\n(i) 과거에 진정한 과학의 본질적 특징으로 받아들여진 것 → dispassionate inquiry(냉정한 탐구).\n(ii) 이제 과학 연구에서 관심을 받는 것 → 그 반대인 emotion(감정).\n정답: C (dispassionate inquiry), E (emotion)", "trap": "(ii) speculation(추측)도 '엄밀한 과학'과 대조되어 보이지만, (i)의 dispassionate(감정 없는)의 정확한 반대는 emotion이다. 짝을 맞춰 풀어야 한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"disciplinary specialization": "학문 분야의 전문화", "long apprenticeship": "긴 수습 기간", "dispassionate inquiry": "냉정한(감정 없는) 탐구", "speculation": "추측, 사변", "emotion": "감정", "technology": "기술"}, "src": "verbal226 Q2 · 24/8, 23/8, 22/6, 22/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v202_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Literary salons and coffeehouses (i) _____ the class-based systems of social hierarchies prevalent at the time. Meritocratic appreciation of wit and brilliance, wherever it might issue, replaced (ii) _____ to establish power.", "choices": null, "columns": [["reaffirmed", "broke down", "anticipated"], ["indifference", "deference", "affronts"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 두 번째 문장: 출신과 관계없이(wherever it might issue) 재치와 탁월함을 존중하는 능력주의가 권력을 세우던 ~을 대체했다 → 계급 사회에서 권력을 세우는 방식 = 윗사람에 대한 경의·복종 → deference.\n(i) 능력주의가 계급적 존중을 대체했으므로, 살롱과 커피하우스는 계급 위계 체제를 '무너뜨렸다' → broke down.\n정답: B (broke down), E (deference)", "trap": "(i) reaffirmed(재확인했다)는 정반대. (ii) affronts(모욕)는 권력을 세우는 수단이 아니며, indifference도 계급 위계와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"affronts": "모욕", "reaffirmed": "재확인했다", "broke down": "무너뜨렸다", "anticipated": "예상했다, 앞서 나타냈다", "indifference": "무관심", "deference": "경의, 존중, 복종", "meritocratic": "능력주의의"}, "src": "verbal202 Q2 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v30_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Vaccine denial has all the hallmarks of a belief system that is not (i) _____. The notion that childhood vaccines are driving autism rates has been (ii) _____ by multiple epidemiological studies. Yet the true believers are (iii) _____, critiquing each new study that challenges their views, and rallying to the defense of disgraced researchers whose work was retracted.", "choices": null, "columns": [["amenable to refutation", "susceptible to fashion", "open to criticism"], ["resuscitated", "documented", "upended"], ["indignant", "persistent", "phlegmatic"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 아래 내용(반박하는 연구를 계속 비판, 철회된 연구자 옹호)은 반박을 받아들이지 않는 신념 체계를 보여준다 → not amenable to refutation(반박을 받아들이지 않는).\n(ii) 백신이 자폐를 유발한다는 생각은 여러 역학 연구에 의해 '뒤집혔다' → upended. Yet과 이어지려면 반박된 상태여야 한다.\n(iii) Yet: 반박되었는데도 신봉자들은 새 연구마다 비판하며 '끈질기다' → persistent.\n정답: A (amenable to refutation), F (upended), H (persistent)", "trap": "(i) open to criticism도 비슷해 보이지만, 이들은 오히려 새 연구를 활발히 '비판'한다. 문제는 자신들이 '반박'당하는 것을 받아들이지 않는 점이다. (iii) indignant(분개한)는 rallying to the defense와 어울려 보이지만 핵심은 '버팀'이다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"amenable to refutation": "반박을 받아들이는", "susceptible to fashion": "유행에 휩쓸리기 쉬운", "open to criticism": "비판에 열려 있는", "resuscitated": "되살려진", "documented": "기록된, 입증된", "upended": "뒤집힌", "indignant": "분개한", "persistent": "끈질긴, 집요한", "phlegmatic": "침착한, 무덤덤한"}, "src": "verbal30 Q4"}, {"id": "v228_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage would agree with which of the following statements about the United States Endangered Species Act?", "choices": ["It has become outdated as a result of critical scientific advances.", "It suffered as a result of a lack of input from scientists.", "It was overly influenced by the interests of industry.", "It should have focused more on short-term, single-species demographic viability.", "Its primary goal is the preservation of strongly interactive species."], "columns": null, "pid": "v228_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 'Among the scientific anachronisms in the United States Endangered Species Act is the absence of specific reference to interactions among species'.\n'It is now understood' → 종간 상호작용의 중요성은 이제야 이해된 과학적 진보.\n따라서 법이 과학의 발전으로 시대에 뒤떨어지게 되었다(anachronism) → A.\n정답: A", "trap": "B(과학자 의견 부족)는 너무 나감. 법이 제정될 때 과학자 의견이 없었다는 것이 아니라, 이후 과학이 발전했다는 것이 요점이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"anachronism": "시대착오", "decimation": "대량 살상, 격감", "circumscribed": "제한된, 한정된", "demographic viability": "인구학적 생존 가능성"}, "src": "verbal228 Q5 · 24년 7월, 22년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v228_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author alludes to functional extinction primarily in order to imply that", "choices": ["functional extinction is a more common form of extinction than is the death of a species", "the extinction of a species serves an important ecological function", "population level and geographic range are not the only predictors of species extinction", "in order to maintain species interactions, more is required than that interactive species do not die out", "in order to avoid extinction, species must interact with other species"], "columns": null, "pid": "v228_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'may render a species functionally extinct in terms of its interactions well before the species itself has completely disappeared'.\n개체 수와 분포 범위가 줄면, 종이 완전히 사라지기 훨씬 전에 상호작용 측면에서 '기능적으로 멸종'할 수 있다.\n즉 종 간 상호작용을 유지하려면 단지 그 종이 멸종하지 않는 것 이상(충분한 개체 수와 범위)이 필요하다 → D.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(기능적 멸종이 더 흔하다)는 빈도 비교로 지문에 근거 없음. C는 '멸종 예측 변수'로 화제를 바꾼 오답.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "Decreased numbers and reduced geographic range may render a species functionally extinct in terms of its interactions well before the species itself has completely disappeared.", "glosses": {"functionally extinct": "기능적으로 멸종한", "allude to": "넌지시 언급하다", "geographic range": "지리적 분포 범위", "interactive species": "상호작용하는 종"}, "src": "verbal228 Q6 · 24년 7월, 22년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v208_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Regarding the evidence collected by the Society for Psychical Research, which of the following can properly be concluded from the passage?", "choices": ["The society's attempts to confirm paranormal phenomena using controlled scientific methodology have all been frustrated.", "The society collected stories of paranormal phenomena with the intent of demonstrating the limitations of scientific methodology.", "The society has not documented cases of people apparently able to produce paranormal effects dispassionately and under any given conditions.", "Because the society scrupulously examines and documents the stories it reports, few charlatans attempt to convince the society's members with fraudulent phenomena.", "When investigation discredits what was claimed to be a paranormal phenomenon, the society does not publicly document the fact."], "columns": null, "pid": "v208_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'One fact that emerges clearly from the stories is that paranormal events occur, if they occur at all, only when people are experiencing strong emotion.'\n학회가 수집한 이야기에서 초자연 현상은 강한 감정 상태에서'만' 일어났다.\n따라서 학회는 감정 없이(dispassionately), 아무 조건에서나 초자연 효과를 내는 사람의 사례를 기록한 적이 없다 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(통제된 과학적 방법으로 확인하려는 시도가 모두 좌절)는 그럴듯하지만, 학회가 그런 실험을 시도했다는 말은 지문에 없다. 학회는 이야기를 수집·기록했을 뿐이다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"paranormal": "초자연적인", "anecdotal": "일화적인", "dispassionately": "감정 없이, 냉정하게", "charlatan": "사기꾼"}, "src": "verbal208 Q7 · 25/9, 25/8, 25/3, 24/11, 24/9, 24/1, 23/7, 22/12, 22/8, 22/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v208_q8", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage would agree with which of the following descriptions of the evidence collected by the Society for Psychical Research?", "choices": ["Carefully recorded", "Unscientific", "Credible"], "columns": null, "pid": "v208_p2", "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'the society took great trouble to interview first-hand witnesses and to document the stories carefully' → 신중하게 기록됨. 맞음.\nB: 'Entirely anecdotal, this evidence has nothing to do with science, since it cannot be reproduced under controlled conditions' → 비과학적. 맞음.\nC: 저자는 'apparently demonstrating', 'if they occur at all'처럼 유보적 표현을 쓴다. 증거가 '신빙성 있다'고 단정하지 않는다.\n정답: A, B", "trap": "C(Credible)는 첫 문장 'supported by considerable evidence'에 끌려 고르기 쉽지만, 저자는 증거의 양과 기록의 꼼꼼함을 말할 뿐 사실로 믿을 만하다고 보증하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"anecdotal": "일화적인", "first-hand": "직접 겪은", "credible": "믿을 만한", "inherently": "본질적으로"}, "src": "verbal208 Q8 · 25/9, 25/8, 25/3, 24/11, 24/9, 24/1, 23/7, 22/12, 22/8, 22/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v208_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the role played in the passage by the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["It states the main conclusion of the author's argument.", "It provides a basis for a recommended course of action.", "It articulates a principle that supports the claim made in the preceding sentence.", "It is intended to undermine the credibility of apparent evidence that the author has mentioned earlier in the passage.", "It serves to emphasize a limitation of the evidence collected by the Society for Psychical Research."], "columns": null, "pid": "v208_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장(주장): 초자연 현상이 강한 감정에서만 일어난다는 사실이 '왜 통제된 과학 실험에서 관찰되지 않는지를 즉시 설명한다'.\n강조 문장: 'Strong emotion is inherently incompatible with controlled scientific procedures.' → 강한 감정과 통제된 실험은 본질적으로 양립 불가라는 일반 원칙.\n이 원칙이 있어야 앞 문장의 설명이 성립 → 앞 주장을 뒷받침하는 원칙.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(주요 결론)는 함정. 주요 결론은 첫 문장(초자연 현상은 실재하지만 과학의 한계 밖에 있다)이고, 강조 문장은 그 논증을 위한 근거 원칙이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incompatible": "양립할 수 없는", "inherently": "본질적으로", "articulate": "명확히 표현하다", "credibility": "신뢰성"}, "src": "verbal208 Q9 · 25/9, 25/8, 25/3, 24/11, 24/9, 24/1, 23/7, 22/12, 22/8, 22/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v216_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "What differentiates this book from more traditional works on grammar is that it reserves its _____ not for students of writing, but for teachers who harbor unduly restrictive views.", "choices": ["mockery", "skepticism", "scolding", "approbation", "admonishment", "commendation"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "not A but B 구조: 이 책은 ~을 학생이 아니라 '지나치게 제한적인 견해를 가진 교사들'에게 돌린다.\n'unduly restrictive views(지나치게 제한적인 견해)'는 비판 대상 → 빈칸 = 꾸짖음, 비판.\n전통 문법책은 학생을 꾸짖지만 이 책은 교사를 꾸짖는다 → scolding, admonishment.\n정답: C (scolding), E (admonishment)", "trap": "mockery(조롱)도 부정적이라 들어갈 수 있어 보이지만 짝이 없다. 전통 문법서가 학생을 '조롱'한다기보다 '훈계'한다는 의미가 자연스럽다. approbation/commendation은 칭찬으로 방향이 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"mockery": "조롱", "skepticism": "회의론", "scolding": "꾸짖음", "approbation": "승인, 칭찬", "admonishment": "훈계, 질책", "commendation": "칭찬"}, "src": "verbal216 Q10 · 25/8, 24/9, 24/6, 23/9, 23/5, 22/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v238_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "When published Native American autobiographies derive from a Native subject's oral narration transcribed and edited by a non-Native collaborator, some consider the term \"autobiography\" _____ since the final work may largely reflect the editor's choices.", "choices": ["misappropriated", "inauspicious", "unwarranted", "inexpedient", "inapplicable", "unpropitious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "since 이유: 최종 작품이 대부분 (비원주민) 편집자의 선택을 반영할 수 있기 때문.\n'자서전(autobiography)'은 '자기가 쓴 자기 이야기'인데, 편집자의 선택이 크게 반영되면 이 용어가 '맞지 않는다/정당하지 않다'.\n빈칸 = 부적절한, 적용할 수 없는 → unwarranted, inapplicable.\n정답: C (unwarranted), E (inapplicable)", "trap": "misappropriated(도용된)는 원주민 이야기를 비원주민이 편집한다는 맥락에서 매우 끌리지만, '용어'가 도용되었다는 말은 어색하고 짝도 없다. inauspicious/unpropitious(불길한)는 서로 짝이지만 문맥과 무관.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"misappropriated": "도용된, 부정하게 사용된", "inapplicable": "적용할 수 없는, 부적절한", "unwarranted": "부당한, 근거 없는", "inauspicious": "불길한, 상서롭지 못한", "inexpedient": "부적당한, 불리한", "unpropitious": "불길한, 형편이 나쁜"}, "src": "verbal238 Q11 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Individuals interested in longevity have sought to fine-tune their bodies with all kinds of _____ diets: only raw foods, only plants, only the flesh, fruit, and nuts that prehistoric humans would have hunted and foraged.", "choices": ["eccentric", "meager", "salutary", "proscriptive", "trendy", "exacting"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 예시: 생식만, 식물만, 선사인들이 사냥·채집했을 고기·과일·견과류만 → 반복되는 'only'.\n즉 먹을 수 있는 것을 엄격히 제한하는 식단 → 빈칸 = 제한적인, 엄격한.\nproscriptive(금지하는), exacting(엄격한, 까다로운)이 짝.\n정답: D (proscriptive), F (exacting)", "trap": "eccentric(별난)과 trendy(유행하는)는 이 식단들의 이미지와 어울리지만 서로 동의어가 아니고, 'only'라는 핵심 단서(제한)를 반영하지 못한다. meager(빈약한)는 양이 적다는 뜻이라 다르다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"proscriptive": "금지하는, 제한하는", "eccentric": "별난, 기이한", "meager": "빈약한, 불충분한", "salutary": "건강에 좋은, 유익한", "trendy": "유행하는", "exacting": "엄격한, 까다로운"}, "src": "verbal200 Q11 · 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v10_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is an assumption on which the argument depends?", "choices": ["Costs incurred from smoking-related health problems account for a greater portion of the Belnovian government's overall health expenditures now than they did five years ago.", "The average cost of treatment for smoking-related health problems in Belnovia has not increased significantly over the past five years.", "Overall health expenditures account for a greater portion of the Belnovian government's annual expenditures now than they did five years ago.", "Belnovia's annual government expenditures are not significantly lower now than they were five years ago.", "Smoking-related health problems usually persist long after a person has quit smoking."], "columns": null, "pid": "v10_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 캠페인은 흡연 관련 비용을 줄이는 데 실패했다.\n근거: 그 비용이 정부 지출에서 차지하는 '비율'이 5% → 6%로 올랐다.\n비율 = 흡연 비용(분자) / 총 정부 지출(분모). 분모가 크게 줄었다면 흡연 비용 자체가 줄어도 비율은 오를 수 있다.\n따라서 논증은 '총 정부 지출이 크게 줄지 않았다'는 가정에 의존 → D.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(치료 평균 비용이 크게 늘지 않았다)는 관련 있어 보이지만, 결론은 비용이 '줄지 않았다'는 것이라 원인(단가 상승)을 배제할 필요가 없다. A, C는 분모를 '보건 지출'로 바꿔 범위를 벗어났다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"expenditure": "지출", "incur": "(비용을) 발생시키다", "assumption": "가정", "persist": "지속되다"}, "src": "verbal10 Q11"}, {"id": "v210_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["It points out a difficulty involved in studying pen flourishing.", "It restates an assertion about the first printed books.", "It corrects a misconception regarding the decoration of manuscripts.", "It provides support for a claim about the dating of printed books.", "It summarized an argument about how to interpret certain type of penwork."], "columns": null, "pid": "v210_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "바로 앞 문장: 인쇄본의 장식 연구는 날짜 측정에는 도움이 되지만 'It is of less help in localizing the flourishing'(장소 파악에는 덜 도움).\n강조 문장: 인쇄본은 장식 없이 팔린 뒤 구매자의 주문에 따라 '다른 곳에서(elsewhere)' 장식되는 경우가 많았다.\n→ 인쇄 장소와 장식 장소가 달라 위치 파악이 어렵다는 이유 = 펜 장식 연구의 어려움.\n정답: A", "trap": "D(인쇄본의 연대 측정에 관한 주장 뒷받침)는 앞부분 '날짜 측정' 이야기에 끌리게 하지만, 강조 문장은 '장소(localizing)' 문제에 대한 설명이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pen flourishing": "펜 장식(필사본 테두리 장식)", "localize": "(장소를) 특정하다", "unadorned": "장식되지 않은", "commission": "주문하다, 의뢰하다"}, "src": "verbal210 Q5 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v210_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, pen flourishing in manuscripts can provide historians with valuable information about", "choices": ["who commissioned the manuscript", "the source from which the manuscript was copied", "the value placed on the contents of the manuscript", "where the manuscript was produced", "the collaborative process used to produce the manuscript"], "columns": null, "pid": "v210_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'The regional variants in form that evolved make flourishing a useful tool for localizing and roughly dating manuscripts.'\n지역별로 다른 형태 → 필사본이 '어디서' 만들어졌는지(localizing)와 대략적인 시기를 알려준다.\nD '필사본이 제작된 장소'가 localizing을 바꿔 말한 것.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(누가 의뢰했는지)는 강조 문장의 'commissioned by their buyers'를 끌어온 오답으로, 그것은 인쇄본에 대한 이야기다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"regional variant": "지역적 변형", "manuscript": "필사본", "flourishing": "(펜) 장식", "collaborative": "공동의, 협력적인"}, "src": "verbal210 Q6 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.7 / S2 3.3"}, {"set": 19, "sections": [[{"id": "v17_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The membership of the two clubs being __________, no one had a member's perspective on both.", "choices": ["selective", "extensive", "mutual", "restricted", "disjoint"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'no one had a member's perspective on both' = 두 클럽에 동시에 속한 사람이 없다.\n분사구문(being ~)이 원인을 나타냄 → 빈칸 = 두 회원 집단이 겹치지 않는다는 뜻.\ndisjoint(서로 겹치지 않는, 교집합이 없는)가 정확히 이 의미.\n정답: E (disjoint)", "trap": "selective/restricted는 '가입이 까다로운'이라는 뜻일 뿐, 두 클럽 회원이 겹치지 않는다는 결과를 설명하지 못함. mutual은 정반대(공유하는).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"selective": "선별적인, 까다로운", "extensive": "광범위한", "mutual": "상호의, 공유하는", "restricted": "제한된", "disjoint": "서로 겹치지 않는, 분리된"}, "src": "verbal17 Q1"}, {"id": "v233_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Those who knew the senator well were convinced that in spite of his (i) _____ in larger political matters, there was no (ii) _____ in his expressions of feeling for his constituents.", "choices": null, "columns": [["candor", "cooperation", "duplicity"], ["dissemblance", "compassion", "fervency"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호어: in spite of → (i)과 (ii)가 대조.\n(ii) 'there was no ___ in his expressions of feeling' = 감정 표현은 진심이었다 → 빈칸 = 거짓, 위선 → dissemblance.\n(i) 그런데 큰 정치 문제에서는 그 반대(거짓, 표리부동)였다 → duplicity.\n정치에서는 이중적이지만 유권자에 대한 감정은 진실했다는 대조가 완성됨.\n정답: C (duplicity), D (dissemblance)", "trap": "(i)에 candor를 넣으면 in spite of의 대조가 사라짐. (ii)에 compassion을 넣으면 '감정 표현에 연민이 없었다'가 되어 사람들이 확신한 내용과 어긋남.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dissemblance": "거짓, 위장", "fervency": "열렬함, 뜨거움", "candor": "솔직함", "cooperation": "협조", "duplicity": "표리부동, 이중성", "compassion": "연민"}, "src": "verbal233 Q2 · 25/10, 24/11, 23/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v209_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Engineers have become (i) _____ constructing static objects such as buildings and bridges, and the vehicles they design, from aircraft to automobiles, are sleek and impressive. Robots and other imitations of organic life, by contrast, always seem (ii) _____. Even in science fiction fantasies, robots lack the (iii) _____ that is typical of a living creature.", "choices": null, "columns": [["weary of", "notorious for", "adept at"], ["complicated", "finicky", "clumsy"], ["ability to learn", "ease of motion", "need for interaction"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 뒤에 'sleek and impressive' → 엔지니어는 정적인 구조물 제작에 능숙하다 → adept at.\n(ii) by contrast → 로봇은 반대로 어설프다 → clumsy.\n(iii) 로봇에게 없는 것 = 생명체의 전형적 특징 중 '어설픔'의 반대 → ease of motion(움직임의 자연스러움).\n(ii)의 clumsy와 (iii)의 ease of motion이 서로 맞물림.\n정답: C (adept at), F (clumsy), H (ease of motion)", "trap": "(ii)의 complicated/finicky는 'sleek'과의 대조로 그럴듯하지만, 셋째 문장의 움직임 문제와 연결되지 않음. (iii)의 ability to learn은 앞 문맥(외형, 움직임)과 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"weary of": "~에 싫증 난", "notorious for": "~로 악명 높은", "adept at": "~에 능숙한", "complicated": "복잡한", "finicky": "까다로운, 세심한 조작이 필요한", "clumsy": "어설픈, 서투른", "ability to learn": "학습 능력", "ease of motion": "움직임의 자연스러움", "need for interaction": "상호작용의 필요"}, "src": "verbal209 Q3 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v229_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies which of the following about Irish American women in the nineteenth century?", "choices": ["At least some would have worked outside the home for wages even if they had not needed to.", "Few desired to become labor activists and organizers in the industrial labor movement.", "Few who were immigrants would have preferred to stay in Ireland, even if they had been able to.", "Many were motivated to return to Ireland after facing difficulties in the United States.", "Many were pleasantly surprised by the working conditions they encountered in New England's textile towns."], "columns": null, "pid": "v229_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 첫 문장 'domesticity ... was an unrealistic and unwelcome ideal'.\nunrealistic(경제적으로 불가능)뿐 아니라 unwelcome(원하지도 않음)이라고 했으므로, 돈이 필요 없더라도 일부는 바깥에서 일하기를 원했을 것이라고 추론 가능.\n또 'embraced occupations like teaching as careers'도 자발적 직업 선택을 뒷받침.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 지문의 'participated in boycotts, strikes'와 반대 방향. C, D, E는 아일랜드로의 귀환 의사나 노동 환경에 대한 반응 등 지문에 없는 내용.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"domesticity": "가정 중심성, 가사 전념", "occupational mobility": "직업적 이동성(지위 상승)", "boycott": "불매 운동"}, "src": "verbal229 Q4 · 25년 7월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v229_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions \"Irish families\" primarily in order to", "choices": ["challenge a stereotype concerning the economic role played by Irish American women", "emphasize the importance of Irish American women's paid labor", "suggest the difficulty of economic conditions in Ireland during the nineteenth century", "contrast the career paths open to American-born Irish women with those open to Irish-born immigrants", "indicate the closeness of nineteenth-century ties between Ireland and the United States"], "columns": null, "pid": "v229_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "해당 문장: 'Women's wages were crucial to the economic health of Irish American households and helped support Irish families in the United States and Ireland.'\n여성의 임금이 미국과 아일랜드 양쪽 가족까지 부양했다고 말해 그 임금 노동의 중요성을 강조함.\n이는 '가정에만 머무는 삶은 현실이 아니었다'는 결론으로 이어짐.\n정답: B", "trap": "E(아일랜드와 미국의 긴밀한 관계)는 표면적으로 그럴듯하지만, 저자의 목적은 두 나라 관계가 아니라 여성 임금의 중요성. A는 고정관념에 '도전'한다는 점에서 혼동되지만 'Irish families'의 직접 기능은 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Irish families", "glosses": {"crucial": "결정적으로 중요한", "household": "가구, 가정", "wage labor": "임금 노동"}, "src": "verbal229 Q5 · 25년 7월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v213_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "When Kim Dae Jung was decisively elected South Korea's president in December 1997, he was considered something of _____ but nevertheless the right man for the time and the job.", "choices": ["an unknown", "an expert", "a maverick", "a nonconformist", "a dilettante", "an authority"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호어: but nevertheless → 빈칸은 '적임자'라는 평가와 대조되는 다소 부정적/의외의 특성.\n빈칸 = 주류에서 벗어난 사람, 독자 노선을 걷는 사람.\nmaverick(이단아, 독불장군)과 nonconformist(비순응주의자)가 같은 뜻.\n정답: C (a maverick), D (a nonconformist)", "trap": "an unknown(무명인)도 대조로 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없고, 압도적으로 당선된 사람에게는 어색함. expert/authority는 짝이지만 but nevertheless의 대조가 성립하지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"an unknown": "무명인", "an expert": "전문가", "a maverick": "이단아, 독자적인 사람", "a nonconformist": "비순응주의자", "a dilettante": "아마추어 애호가, 딜레탕트", "an authority": "권위자"}, "src": "verbal213 Q7 · 25/1, 24/1, 22/8 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Curry did not necessarily agree with the criticisms about her research paper, but rather than _____ them, as many scientists might have done, she began to engage with the critics.", "choices": ["dismissing", "refuting", "acknowledging", "recognizing", "ignoring", "attacking"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: rather than ___ them, she began to engage with the critics → 빈칸은 engage(적극적으로 상대하다)의 반대.\n빈칸 = 비판을 무시하고 상대하지 않다.\ndismissing(일축하다)과 ignoring(무시하다)이 짝.\n정답: A (dismissing), E (ignoring)", "trap": "refuting/attacking도 많은 과학자가 할 법한 반응이지만 이것들은 오히려 비판에 '대응'하는 것이라 engage의 반대가 아님. acknowledging/recognizing은 짝이지만 방향이 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dismissing": "일축하는, 묵살하는", "refuting": "반박하는", "acknowledging": "인정하는", "recognizing": "인정하는, 알아보는", "ignoring": "무시하는", "attacking": "공격하는"}, "src": "verbal221 Q8 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v205_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In contrast to today, when many readers consider the moral sentiments expressed in the ancient writer's work to be quite sophomoric, in the writer's own time, these sentiments were regarded as remarkably _____.", "choices": ["abstruse", "misguided", "insightful", "ill-conceived", "sagacious", "sanguine"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호어: In contrast to today → 오늘날 평가(sophomoric, 유치한)와 정반대.\n빈칸 = 긍정, '성숙하고 지혜로운'이라는 뜻.\ninsightful(통찰력 있는)과 sagacious(현명한)가 짝.\n정답: C (insightful), E (sagacious)", "trap": "sanguine은 '낙관적인'이라는 뜻으로 sagacious와 철자가 비슷해 헷갈리지만 의미가 다름. abstruse(난해한)는 sophomoric의 반대처럼 보이지만 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sophomoric": "유치한", "sagacious": "현명한, 지혜로운", "sanguine": "낙관적인, 쾌활한", "abstruse": "난해한", "misguided": "잘못 판단된", "insightful": "통찰력 있는", "ill-conceived": "잘못 구상된"}, "src": "verbal205 Q9 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v211_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "He was one of the most powerful chess players ever and one of the most _____: at the height of his fame he all but dropped out of chess, entering into a self-imposed exile.", "choices": ["perplexing", "creative", "troubled", "infuriating", "enigmatic", "imaginative"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 빈칸의 설명: 명성의 정점에서 체스를 거의 그만두고 스스로 은둔 → 이해하기 어려운 행동.\n빈칸 = 수수께끼 같은, 이해할 수 없는.\nperplexing(당혹스럽게 하는)과 enigmatic(수수께끼 같은)이 짝.\n정답: A (perplexing), E (enigmatic)", "trap": "troubled(괴로워하는)는 은둔과 연결될 듯하지만 짝이 없음. creative/imaginative는 짝이지만 콜론 뒤 설명과 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"perplexing": "당혹스럽게 하는, 이해하기 어려운", "creative": "창의적인", "troubled": "괴로워하는, 문제가 많은", "infuriating": "몹시 화나게 하는", "enigmatic": "수수께끼 같은", "imaginative": "상상력이 풍부한"}, "src": "verbal211 Q7 · 24/7, 23/2, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v35_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with doing which of the following?", "choices": ["Presenting an objection to a claim", "Accounting for an apparent anomaly", "Outlining an alternative interpretation", "Correcting a particular misconception", "Questioning the validity of a comparison"], "columns": null, "pid": "v35_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 일부 고고학자의 주장(4만~2만5천 년 전 아메리카 정착).\n'However, to support this theory it is necessary to explain the absence...' 이후 호주와 비교하며 유적이 없는 것을 해명하기 어렵다는 근거를 나열.\n마지막 문장: 그때 사람이 있었다면 호주보다 기록에 남을 가능성이 더 컸을 것 → 그 주장에 대한 반론.\n정답: A", "trap": "B(이상 현상 설명)는 '유적 부재'라는 이상 현상을 설명하려는 것처럼 보이지만, 저자는 이를 해명하는 것이 아니라 해명이 어렵다고 지적해 주장을 반박함. E는 저자가 호주 비교를 오히려 근거로 사용하므로 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"colonize": "정착하다, 식민지화하다", "aridity": "건조함", "postglacial": "빙하기 이후의", "deplete": "고갈시키다, 감소시키다"}, "src": "verbal35 Q10"}, {"id": "v35_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage implies which of the following about 25,000 years ago?", "choices": ["The coastline of the region that is now the United States is longer than it was 40,000 years ago.", "Rivers in what is now the United States were numerous than they are now.", "Australia was less densely populated at that time than was the region that is now the United States.", "Australia’s climate was significantly drier than it is now.", "Global sea level was lower than it is now."], "columns": null, "pid": "v35_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'land area has been lost from the coastal regions ... because of postglacial sea-level rise'.\n빙하기 이후 해수면이 상승해 해안 땅이 사라졌다 → 2만5천 년 전(빙하기)에는 해수면이 지금보다 낮았다는 함축.\n정답: E", "trap": "A는 해안선 '길이' 변화로 지문이 말하지 않은 내용. D는 지문의 aridity가 현재 호주의 건조함을 말할 뿐 과거와 비교하지 않음. C의 인구밀도도 현재에 대한 진술.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sea-level rise": "해수면 상승", "density": "밀도", "imply": "함축하다, 암시하다"}, "src": "verbal35 Q11"}, {"id": "v35_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage implies that, in what is now the United States, archaeological evidence of inhabitation in the period from 40,000 to 25,000 years ago is lacking because that region", "choices": ["had its oldest habitation sites inundated following a postglacial rise in sea level", "has many resource-rich rivers that facilitated the dispersal of early inhabitants from an initial concentration in coastal areas", "was sparsely populated until about 25,000 years ago", "was colonized less than 25,000 years ago", "was inhabited only by hunter-gatherers until 25,000 years ago"], "columns": null, "pid": "v35_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "저자의 논지: 사람이 있었다면 미국이 호주보다 유적이 남을 조건이 더 좋았다('the chances ... would seem to be greater than for Australia').\n그런데도 유적이 없다 → 가장 그럴듯한 설명은 그 시기에 아직 사람이 살지 않았다는 것, 즉 2만5천 년 전 이후에 정착.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(해수면 상승으로 유적 침수)는 저자가 호주도 같은 정도로 영향을 받았다며 배제한 설명. B는 저자가 강을 '해안에만 머물렀을 리 없다'는 근거로 쓴 것이지 유적 부재의 원인이 아님.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inundate": "범람시키다, 침수시키다", "dispersal": "분산", "habitation site": "거주 유적지", "hunter-gatherer": "수렵채집인"}, "src": "verbal35 Q12"}], [{"id": "v204_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Pearl millet possesses the unique genetic predisposition to withstand environmental stress and produce appreciable yield, cultivation on _____ soils notwithstanding.", "choices": ["arable", "fertilized", "marginal", "native", "choice"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: notwithstanding(~에도 불구하고) + 'withstand environmental stress'.\n빈칸 = 부정, 열악한 토양이라는 뜻 → 그런 토양에서 재배되더라도 상당한 수확을 낸다.\nmarginal(척박한, 경작에 부적합한)이 정답.\n정답: C (marginal)", "trap": "arable, fertilized, choice는 모두 좋은 토양이라 notwithstanding의 양보 의미가 성립하지 않음. marginal을 '가장자리의'로만 알면 놓치기 쉬움.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"arable": "경작 가능한", "choice": "고급의, 최상의", "fertilized": "비료를 준", "marginal": "척박한, 생산성이 낮은", "native": "토착의, 원래의"}, "src": "verbal204 Q1 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "I did not begin work on my biography of Mary Somerville as Somerville’s (i) _____. When I first began studying her, I saw Somerville and the esteem in which her contemporaries held her as (ii) _____. Over time, however, I have come to understand what she accomplished and why it was justly valued.", "choices": null, "columns": [["counterpart", "adversary", "advocate"], ["a boon", "a puzzle", "an inspiration"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "마지막 문장: 'Over time, however, I have come to understand what she accomplished and why it was justly valued.'\n(ii) 처음엔 그녀와 그녀가 받은 존경을 이해하지 못했다 → a puzzle.\n(i) 따라서 시작할 때는 그녀의 지지자가 아니었다 → advocate (not ~ as her advocate).\n정답: C (advocate), E (a puzzle)", "trap": "(i)에 adversary를 넣고 싶지만 not이 있어 '적으로서 시작하지 않았다'가 되어 논리가 뒤틀림. (ii)의 boon/inspiration은 긍정이라 however 이후의 변화와 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"counterpart": "상대, 대응하는 사람", "adversary": "적, 반대자", "advocate": "옹호자, 지지자", "a boon": "혜택, 이로운 것", "a puzzle": "수수께끼", "an inspiration": "영감을 주는 존재"}, "src": "verbal200 Q3 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v26_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Because the currents that flow back and forth between the Galapagos Islands and the Ecuadoran mainland create connections, the evolutionary (i) _____ of the sea creatures in the two areas, compared with that of the land dwellers, has been (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["association", "sophistication", "separateness"], ["disguised", "derailed", "diminished"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "원인: 해류가 두 지역을 오가며 '연결'을 만든다.\n결과: 바다 생물의 진화적 '분리됨'은 육상 생물과 비교해 줄어들었다.\n(i) separateness, (ii) diminished가 인과를 완성.\n정답: C (separateness), F (diminished)", "trap": "(i)에 association을 넣으면 (ii)가 '증가'여야 하는데 그 선택지가 없음. derailed는 부정적 어감만 맞을 뿐 의미가 어긋남.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"association": "연관, 결합", "sophistication": "정교함", "separateness": "분리됨, 별개성", "disguised": "위장된", "derailed": "탈선된, 좌절된", "diminished": "줄어든"}, "src": "verbal26 Q3"}, {"id": "v222_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "When we forgive a person, we (i) _____ our (ii) _____ his or her transgression but (iii) _____ certain punitive responses that we would ordinarily be justified in taking on the basis of that person's objectionable conduct.", "choices": null, "columns": [["relinquish", "regret", "retain"], ["leniency toward", "uncertainty about", "condemnation of"], ["disguise", "forgo", "initiate"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심 구조: we (i) our (ii) his transgression BUT (iii) certain punitive responses.\nbut 때문에 (i)+(ii)와 (iii)이 대조: 잘못을 여전히 나쁘다고 여기지만 처벌은 하지 않는다.\n(i) retain + (ii) condemnation of = 비난은 유지.\n(iii) forgo = 정당한 처벌적 대응을 포기.\n정답: C (retain), F (condemnation of), H (forgo)", "trap": "'용서 = 비난을 버림'이라는 직관 때문에 relinquish를 고르기 쉽지만, 그러면 but 이후의 forgo와 대조가 사라짐. 용서는 판단은 유지하되 처벌만 포기하는 것.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"relinquish": "포기하다, 내려놓다", "regret": "후회하다", "retain": "유지하다", "leniency toward": "~에 대한 관대함", "uncertainty about": "~에 대한 불확실함", "condemnation of": "~에 대한 비난", "disguise": "숨기다, 위장하다", "forgo": "포기하다, 삼가다", "initiate": "시작하다"}, "src": "verbal222 Q4 · 25년 8월, 23년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Why does the author note that people \"make inconsistent choices\"?", "choices": ["To account for why people's stated intentions and their actual behavior often do not coincide", "To explain why most economists no longer adhere to standard model of the rational economic agent", "To identify a prevailing theory among economists about people's behavior", "To cast doubt on a particular assumption about people's revealed preferences", "To suggest that economists should draw more heavily from behavioral economics and psychology"], "columns": null, "pid": "v224_p14", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "경제학자들은 실제 선택(revealed preferences)이 진짜 선호를 보여준다고 가정함.\n'Yet people's choices often bear a mixed relationship to their own happiness' 이후 비합리적 선택의 예로 'make inconsistent choices'를 제시.\n결론: 선택이 진짜 선호를 반영하지 않을 수 있으므로 선택에만 의존하는 방법은 매력을 잃는다.\n즉 revealed preferences에 관한 가정을 의심하기 위한 예시.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 '말한 의도 vs 실제 행동'의 불일치로, 첫 문장의 stated intentions 언급과 섞어 만든 함정. B는 '대부분의 경제학자가 더 이상 따르지 않는다'는 지문에 없는 과장.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "make inconsistent choices", "glosses": {"revealed preference": "현시 선호(실제 선택으로 드러난 선호)", "bounded rationality": "제한된 합리성", "utility": "효용", "infer": "추론하다"}, "src": "verbal224 Q14 · 24/11, 23/8, 22/10, 22/6, 22/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the context in which it appears, \"mixed\" most nearly means", "choices": ["ambiguous", "combined", "associated", "convoluted", "adulterated"], "columns": null, "pid": "v224_p14", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "문장: 'people's choices often bear a mixed relationship to their own happiness'.\n선택이 행복을 높이기도 하고 아니기도 하다 → 관계가 일관되지 않고 불분명하다.\n뒤에서 선택이 진짜 선호를 '반드시' 반영하지는 않는다고 함 → ambiguous(애매한, 일관되지 않은).\n정답: A (ambiguous)", "trap": "combined는 mixed의 사전적 1차 의미(섞인)라 끌리지만 '관계'를 수식할 때 의미가 통하지 않음. adulterated(불순물이 섞인)도 같은 함정.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "mixed", "glosses": {"ambiguous": "애매한, 불분명한", "convoluted": "복잡하게 얽힌", "adulterated": "불순물이 섞인", "associated": "연관된"}, "src": "verbal224 Q15 · 24/11, 23/8, 22/10, 22/6, 22/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v212_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with", "choices": ["resolving a dispute", "defending a practice", "summarizing a dilemma", "delineating a difference", "explaining an anomaly"], "columns": null, "pid": "v212_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1단락: 수집 과학에서 원자료는 공동 재산(intellectual commons).\n2단락: 'The moral economy of facts is quite different in sciences that generate facts artificially' → 실험 과학에서 원자료는 사적 재산.\n두 분야의 데이터 취급 방식 차이를 설명하는 글.\n정답: D (delineating a difference)", "trap": "E(이상 현상 설명)는 저자가 각 차이의 이유(I think ...)를 설명하기 때문에 끌리지만, 설명 대상은 '이상 현상'이 아니라 두 분야 간 차이.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"delineate": "묘사하다, 윤곽을 그리다", "commons": "공유지, 공동 자원", "irreplaceable": "대체 불가능한"}, "src": "verbal212 Q7 · 25년 9월, 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v212_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage would most likely agree with which of the following statements about manufactured data?", "choices": ["They are essential to the common good.", "They cannot be easily replicated.", "They can play a key role in career advancement.", "They cannot be adequately interpreted until they have been published.", "They are often manipulated to support specific hypotheses."], "columns": null, "pid": "v212_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 출판은 'impelled more by ambition and career imperatives than by moral obligation', 'Individuals may perish professionally if they neglect to publish'.\n제조된 데이터를 출판하는 것이 경력에 결정적이라는 의미 → 경력 발전에 핵심 역할.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 반대: 'there is no loss to the common good'. B도 반대: 'can be produced again', 'someone else can always produce equivalent data'.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"imperative": "필수 사항, 요구", "impel": "몰아대다, 강요하다", "perish": "소멸하다, 끝장나다"}, "src": "verbal212 Q8 · 25년 9월, 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v212_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the context of the passage as a whole, the highlighted sentence serves to", "choices": ["warn of the consequences of overlooking a point made in the first sentence of the passage", "cite an exception to a principle described in the preceding sentence", "present a conditional scenario that is confirmed in the subsequent sentence", "provide a rationale for an assertion made in the final sentence of the passage", "predict an outcome that is refuted in the final sentence of the passage"], "columns": null, "pid": "v212_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "강조 문장: 출판을 안 하면 개인은 경력상 손해를 보지만 다른 사람이 같은 데이터를 만들 수 있으므로 공익 손실이 없다.\n마지막 문장: 'The experimental sciences operate more in a market economy than a moral one.'\n개인의 이익(경력)이 동기이고 도덕적 의무가 없다는 강조 문장이 '시장 경제'라는 결론의 근거가 됨.\n정답: D", "trap": "C는 다음 문장('Raw data are not an intellectual commons')이 '확인'한다고 하지만 강조 문장은 조건적 시나리오를 제시해 확인받는 구조가 아님. B는 앞 문장의 원칙에 대한 예외가 아니라 그 연장선.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rationale": "근거, 논리적 이유", "conditional": "조건부의", "refute": "반박하다"}, "src": "verbal212 Q9 · 25년 9월, 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v218_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "At the core of science fiction is the notion of _____, of asking, \"If this phenomenon continues, where will it lead?\"", "choices": ["generalization", "extrapolation", "projection", "compensation", "reparation", "theorization"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콤마 뒤 동격 설명: 'If this phenomenon continues, where will it lead?' = 현재 추세를 미래로 연장해 예측하는 것.\n빈칸 = 추정, 미래 예측.\nextrapolation(외삽, 추정)과 projection(예측, 투사)이 짝.\n정답: B (extrapolation), C (projection)", "trap": "theorization과 generalization은 과학적 사고와 관련돼 그럴듯하지만 '계속되면 어디로 가는가'라는 미래 연장 의미가 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"generalization": "일반화", "extrapolation": "외삽, 추정(연장 예측)", "projection": "예측, 추정", "compensation": "보상", "reparation": "배상", "theorization": "이론화"}, "src": "verbal218 Q12 · 25/10, 25/8, 25/7, 25/5, 25/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v228_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "This novel is not great literature; there are too many characters, too many subplots, and no clearly defined protagonist, making for _____ story.", "choices": ["a banal", "a diffuse", "a mawkish", "an innocuous", "an amorphous", "a hackneyed"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론 뒤 근거: 인물이 너무 많고, 서브플롯이 너무 많고, 명확한 주인공이 없다 → 초점과 형태가 없는 이야기.\n빈칸 = 산만하고 형체가 없는.\ndiffuse(산만한, 초점 없는)와 amorphous(형태가 없는)가 짝.\n정답: B (a diffuse), E (an amorphous)", "trap": "banal과 hackneyed(진부한)는 '훌륭한 문학이 아니다'와 어울리는 짝이지만, 근거로 제시된 것은 진부함이 아니라 구조의 산만함.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"diffuse": "장황한, 산만한", "amorphous": "형태가 없는", "mawkish": "매우 감상적인", "innocuous": "해가 없는", "a banal": "진부한", "a diffuse": "산만한, 장황한", "a mawkish": "지나치게 감상적인", "an innocuous": "무해한, 무난한", "an amorphous": "형태가 없는", "a hackneyed": "진부한, 낡은"}, "src": "verbal228 Q12 · 24/10, 23/10, 22/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v236_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Coral reefs are often referred to as the rain forests of the sea, _____ comparison, given that only tropical rain forests can compete with the sheer concentration of biodiversity found in coral reefs.", "choices": ["a factitious", "an imaginative", "a fitting", "an artificial", "an apposite", "a common"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: given that only tropical rain forests can compete with ... → 두 생태계의 생물다양성이 실제로 비슷하다는 근거.\n빈칸 = 긍정, '적절한 비유'라는 뜻.\nfitting과 apposite(적절한)가 짝.\n정답: C (a fitting), E (an apposite)", "trap": "factitious와 artificial(인위적인)은 짝이지만 근거가 비유를 지지하므로 부정어는 맞지 않음. common도 의미상 가능하지만 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rain forests": "열대우림", "compete with": "필적하다", "a factitious": "인위적인, 꾸며낸", "an imaginative": "상상력이 풍부한", "a fitting": "적절한", "an artificial": "인위적인", "an apposite": "적절한, 적합한", "a common": "흔한"}, "src": "verbal236 Q10 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v30_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "The conclusion of the argument above depends on which of the following assumptions?", "choices": ["In the 1950’s only sixty percent of cancer patients received treatment, whereas now a substantially higher percentage does.", "Free medical treatment is more likely to be available now to people who have no health insurance than it was in the 1950’s.", "Detection of cancer does not now take place, on average, significantly earlier in the progression of the disease than it did in the 1950’s.", "Physicians now usually predict a longer life for cancer patients after detection of the disease than did physicians in the 1950’s.", "The number of cancer patients now is approximately the same as it was in the 1950’s."], "columns": null, "pid": "v30_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 치료법이 좋아져서 환자들이 발병 후 더 오래 산다.\n근거: 진단(detection) 후 생존 기간이 5년 → 7년으로 늘어남.\n허점: 진단이 더 일찍 이루어지면 실제 수명이 같아도 '진단 후 생존 기간'은 길어 보임.\n따라서 진단 시점이 크게 앞당겨지지 않았다는 가정이 필요.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 치료받은 환자 비율 이야기로, 지문의 60%는 치료받은 환자 중 생존 비율이라 혼동을 노림. D는 의사의 예측일 뿐 실제 생존과 무관.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"detection": "발견, 진단", "progression": "진행", "assumption": "가정"}, "src": "verbal30 Q11"}, {"id": "v212_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Duprat would most likely agree that certain nineteenth-century French female societies", "choices": ["sometimes took unfair advantage of their charitable status", "hoped to change public perceptions of the activities of dames decharite", "strategically misled government officials about their activities", "were not consistent in representing their members' values", "conducted themselves in a way that contributed to their neglect by government officials"], "columns": null, "pid": "v212_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'she suggests that their official silence ... as well as their careful cultivation of the traditional, nonthreatening image ... kept these associations largely out of public view.'\n총회나 출판을 하지 않고 조용한 이미지를 유지한 그들의 행동이 주목받지 못한 원인 → 정부의 무관심에 기여.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(정부를 전략적으로 속였다)는 'careful cultivation'에서 의도성을 과장한 선택지. 지문은 기만이 아니라 조용한 이미지 유지만 말함. B는 전통적 이미지를 '유지'했으므로 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"garner": "얻다, 모으다", "cultivation": "조성, 함양", "municipal": "시의, 지방 자치의"}, "src": "verbal212 Q14 · 25/1, 24/10, 23/8, 22/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v212_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "As represented in the passage, the views of which of the following scholars are consistent with one another with regard to the official notice received by women's associations?", "choices": ["Harrison and most historians", "Harrison and Grange", "Grange and most historians"], "columns": null, "pid": "v212_p4", "answer": "ABC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Harrison: 행정가들이 여성 단체 활동을 대체로 무시했다.\n대부분 역사가: 여성 단체는 당국의 주목을 거의 받지 못한 것 같다 → Harrison과 일치(A).\nGrange: 'this may be because so few female associations existed' → '주목받지 못했다'는 사실 자체는 받아들이고 그 이유만 제시 → Harrison, 대부분 역사가와 모두 일치(B, C).\n'공식적 주목' 측면에서 세 견해 모두 '거의 받지 못함'으로 일치함 (Duprat만 다름).\n정답: A, B, C", "trap": "Grange 문장이 While로 시작해 대립처럼 보이므로 B, C를 빼기 쉬움. 하지만 While은 Grange와 Duprat의 대조이고, Grange는 무관심이라는 사실 자체에는 동의함.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"administrator": "행정가", "garner": "얻다, 모으다", "counterpart": "상대, 대응되는 것"}, "src": "verbal212 Q15 · 25/1, 24/10, 23/8, 22/11 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.3 / S2 3.0"}, {"set": 20, "sections": [[{"id": "v225_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "In theory, when water freezes, ice crystals grow only from pure water, while any impurities are _____ the ice structure and are eventually swept away.", "choices": ["dispersed throughout", "incorporated into", "rejected from", "trapped in", "concealed by"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 얼음 결정은 순수한 물에서만 자란다 (while: 대조) + 불순물은 결국 'swept away'된다.\n빈칸 = 불순물이 얼음 구조에서 밀려난다는 뜻.\nrejected from(배제되다)이 정답.\n정답: C (rejected from)", "trap": "incorporated into, trapped in, dispersed throughout은 모두 불순물이 얼음 '안에' 남는 것이라 '순수한 물에서만 자란다', 'swept away'와 모순.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dispersed throughout": "~전체에 흩어진", "incorporated into": "~에 통합된", "rejected from": "~에서 배제된", "trapped in": "~에 갇힌", "concealed by": "~에 의해 감춰진"}, "src": "verbal225 Q1 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v35_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The building affairs minister rightly recognizes that the current planning system—under which the government controls every aspect of construction—creates disastrous developments, but she is wrong to propose the opposite: the wholesale (i) _____ of the building market. Such a complete (ii) _____ of responsibility on the part of the state can hardly be in the public’s interest.", "choices": null, "columns": [["liberalization", "preservation", "regulation"], ["abnegation", "recapitulation", "accretion"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 현재 체계 = 정부가 모든 것을 통제 → 'the opposite' = 시장의 전면적 자유화 → liberalization.\n(ii) 'Such a complete ___ of responsibility on the part of the state' = 국가가 책임을 완전히 내려놓는 것 → abnegation(포기, 방기).\n정답: A (liberalization), D (abnegation)", "trap": "(i)의 regulation은 현재 체계와 같은 방향이라 'opposite'에 어긋남. (ii)의 accretion(증가, 축적)은 국가 책임이 커진다는 반대 의미.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"liberalization": "자유화, 규제 완화", "preservation": "보존", "regulation": "규제", "abnegation": "포기, 방기", "recapitulation": "요약, 반복", "accretion": "증가, 축적"}, "src": "verbal35 Q2"}, {"id": "v11_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The advance of medical knowledge is not always (i) _____; on the contrary, it is often the result of (ii) _____. In the 1830s, groups of doctors began to question long-enshrined treatments such as bleeding, cupping, and purging, eventually discovering that many ailments were more effectively treated by nothing more than bed rest, nutrition, and observation. This news must have been (iii) _____ to those with a vested interest in the medical orthodoxy of the time.", "choices": null, "columns": [["scientific", "experimental", "cumulative"], ["patient repetition", "heretical departures", "chance discoveries"], ["unsurprising", "welcome", "jarring"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CEI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i)-(ii): 'not always ___; on the contrary, ... the result of ___' → 대조.\n예시: 오래된 치료법(사혈 등)을 의심하고 버린 것 → 기존 정설에서 벗어난 것 → (ii) heretical departures.\n그 반대 = 기존 지식 위에 차곡차곡 쌓이는 것 → (i) cumulative.\n(iii) 기존 의학 정설에 이해관계가 있는 사람들에게 이 소식은 충격적 → jarring.\n정답: C (cumulative), E (heretical departures), I (jarring)", "trap": "(i)에 scientific을 넣으면 '과학적이지 않다'가 되어 의사들의 체계적 관찰과 맞지 않음. (ii)의 chance discoveries는 예시가 '우연'이 아니라 의도적 의심이므로 오답.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"heretical departures": "이단적인 이탈", "jarring": "충격적인, 거슬리는", "scientific": "과학적인", "experimental": "실험적인", "cumulative": "누적되는, 점진적으로 쌓이는", "patient repetition": "끈기 있는 반복", "chance discoveries": "우연한 발견", "unsurprising": "놀랍지 않은", "welcome": "반가운"}, "src": "verbal11 Q3"}, {"id": "v207_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author would most likely agree with which of the following claims about Australian Dunatothrips?", "choices": ["Their offspring survival rates increase when large groups cooperate to modify nests.", "Their effect on the leaves used to support their tent-like structures is not necessarily permanent.", "They expend as much energy to create tent-like structures as they do to produce broods.", "They exhibit an effect from collective activity that is also found in certain other insect species.", "They modify nests in different ways depending on what other species are present in their vicinity."], "columns": null, "pid": "v207_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Several studies of other species of nest-building insects have concluded that foundress associations are beneficial to all parties.'\nDunatothrips도 집단으로 둥지를 만들면 생존 및 산란 가능성이 높아짐 → 다른 곤충에서도 발견되는 집단 활동의 이점.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 '자손'의 생존율이 증가한다고 했지만 지문은 창립 암컷(foundress)의 생존을 말하고, 개체당 산란은 오히려 감소함. 또 '큰 집단'도 지문에 없는 표현.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"desiccation": "건조, 탈수", "foundress": "(군집의) 창립 암컷", "per capita": "1인당, 개체당"}, "src": "verbal207 Q4 · 25년 8월, 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v207_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions \"desiccation” primarily to", "choices": ["describe an environment suitable for one species’ reproduction", "characterize a stage in an insect species' developmental cycle", "analyze an environmental challenge faced by some insect species", "exemplify a changing feature of a particular climate", "identify the purpose served by a particular behavior"], "columns": null, "pid": "v207_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "문장: 암컷이 텐트 구조물을 만드는 이유 = 'to protect themselves and their eggs and larvae from desiccation'.\ndesiccation은 텐트를 만드는 행동의 목적(건조 방지)을 밝혀줌.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(환경적 어려움 분석)는 건조가 도전이긴 하지만 저자는 이를 '분석'하지 않고 행동의 목적을 밝히는 데 그침. A는 건조한 환경을 '번식에 적합한' 환경이라 해 방향이 틀림.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "desiccation", "glosses": {"desiccation": "건조, 탈수", "arid": "건조한", "larvae": "유충(larva의 복수)"}, "src": "verbal207 Q5 · 25년 8월, 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v31_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Debate rages on between proponents of corporal punishment and the death penalty and their detractors, though even the most rabid supporter agrees that punishments must be _____ and the justice system evenhanded and thorough.", "choices": ["meet", "clement", "delimited", "condign", "tantamount", "merciful"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'even the most rabid supporter agrees' + 'evenhanded and thorough' → 양측 모두 동의할 만한 원칙.\n열성 지지자도 '처벌은 관대해야 한다'고 하지는 않으므로 빈칸 = 공정한, 마땅한(죄에 상응하는).\nmeet(적절한, 마땅한)와 condign(합당한, 죄에 걸맞은)이 짝.\n정답: A (meet), D (condign)", "trap": "clement와 merciful(관대한)은 완벽한 짝이지만, 체벌·사형 열성 지지자(rabid supporter)가 동의할 내용이 아님. meet의 형용사 뜻(적절한)을 모르면 놓치기 쉬움.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"meet": "(형용사) 적절한, 마땅한", "clement": "관대한, 온화한", "delimited": "범위가 정해진", "condign": "(벌이) 합당한, 응당한", "tantamount": "~와 동등한", "merciful": "자비로운"}, "src": "verbal31 Q9"}, {"id": "v223_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "To keep the museum’s admission lines moving, security inspections are considerably _____.", "choices": ["thorough", "annoying", "cursory", "casual", "irritating", "methodical"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: To keep the admission lines moving → 줄이 빨리 줄어들게 하려면 검사가 빨라야 함.\n빈칸 = 대충 하는, 간단한.\ncursory(대충의, 피상적인)와 casual(가벼운, 형식적인)이 짝.\n정답: C (cursory), D (casual)", "trap": "annoying과 irritating은 짝이지만 목적(줄을 빨리 움직이게)과 무관. thorough/methodical은 정반대 짝.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"thorough": "철저한", "annoying": "짜증나게 하는", "cursory": "대충의, 피상적인", "casual": "가벼운, 형식적인", "irritating": "짜증나게 하는", "methodical": "체계적인"}, "src": "verbal223 Q6 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v217_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the realm of science and mathematics, ambiguity is generally seen as something that arises from erroneous understanding and must be overcome, yet ambiguity has often _____ developments in science and mathematics.", "choices": ["preceded", "scotched", "stimulated", "hindered", "accompanied", "spurred"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호어: yet → 앞의 '모호함은 극복해야 할 것'이라는 일반적 시각과 반대.\n빈칸 = 긍정, 모호함이 발전을 촉진했다는 뜻.\nstimulated와 spurred(촉진하다)가 짝.\n정답: C (stimulated), F (spurred)", "trap": "scotched/hindered는 일반적 시각과 같은 방향이라 yet과 충돌. preceded/accompanied는 중립적이라 대조의 힘이 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"scotched": "좌절시켰다, 억눌렀다", "preceded": "~에 앞섰다", "stimulated": "자극했다, 촉진했다", "hindered": "방해했다", "accompanied": "동반했다", "spurred": "박차를 가했다, 촉진했다"}, "src": "verbal217 Q7 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v35_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "After many years of feeling _____ by his senior managers, Clark was becoming hopeful of advancement..", "choices": ["vilified", "stymied", "hindered", "aggrieved", "circumvented", "overlooked"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 수년간 상사들에게 ___ 느낌을 받은 후 이제 승진(advancement)에 희망을 갖게 됨.\n빈칸 = 승진이 막혔다는 뜻 (advancement의 반대).\nstymied(방해받은, 가로막힌)와 hindered(방해받은)가 짝.\n정답: B (stymied), C (hindered)", "trap": "overlooked(간과된)는 단독으로 완벽히 어울리지만 짝이 없음. vilified(비방받은)와 aggrieved(억울한)도 부정적이지만 서로 의미가 다르고 승진과 직접 연결되지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"vilified": "비방받은", "stymied": "방해받은, 가로막힌", "hindered": "방해받은", "aggrieved": "억울한, 피해를 입은", "circumvented": "우회당한, 회피된", "overlooked": "간과된, 무시당한"}, "src": "verbal35 Q7"}, {"id": "v13_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following occurs as a result of cooling in the upper layers of the ocean?", "choices": ["The concentration of oxygen in the air above the ocean's surface decreases.", "The concentration of DMS in the air above the ocean's surface increases.", "The nutrient supply at the surface of the ocean is replenished.", "Cloud formation increases over the ocean.", "Marine algae make more efficient use of nutrients."], "columns": null, "pid": "v13_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'it allows the cooled upper layers of the ocean to sink, and then the circulating water carries nutrients upward from the depths below.'\n냉각된 표층수가 가라앉고 순환하는 물이 깊은 곳의 영양분을 위로 운반 → 표층의 영양분이 보충됨.\n정답: C", "trap": "B, D는 기후가 '따뜻할 때' 일어나는 일(DMS 증가, 구름 증가)로, 냉각 후에는 오히려 감소함. E는 영양분 '이용 효율'로 지문에 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"replenish": "다시 채우다, 보충하다", "condense": "응결하다", "circulate": "순환하다"}, "src": "verbal13 Q10"}, {"id": "v13_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is most similar to the role played by marine algae in the global climate control system proposed by Lovelock?", "choices": ["A fan that continually replaces stale air in a room with fresh air from outside.", "A thermostat that automatically controls an air-conditioning system.", "An insulating blanket that retains heat.", "A filter used to purify water.", "A dehumidifier that constantly removes moisture from the air in a room."], "columns": null, "pid": "v13_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Lovelock의 체계: 따뜻해지면 조류 활동, DMS 증가 → 구름 증가 → 냉각; 냉각되면 조류 활동 감소 → 순환.\n즉 온도를 감지해 자동으로 냉각을 켜고 끄는 피드백 장치.\n온도 조절기(thermostat)가 에어컨을 자동 제어하는 것과 같은 구조.\n정답: B", "trap": "C(단열 담요)는 열을 '보존'하는 단방향 장치이고, A, E는 '지속적으로' 한 방향 작용만 하므로 온도에 따른 조절(피드백) 특성이 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"thermostat": "온도 조절 장치", "feedback": "되먹임", "super organism": "초유기체"}, "src": "verbal13 Q11"}, {"id": "v13_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage mentions \"benefit from nitrogen\" most likely in order to", "choices": ["provide support for Lovelock's response to an objection mentioned in the passage", "suggest that the climatic effects of DMS production have been underestimated", "acknowledge that Lovelock's hypothesis is based in part on speculation", "demonstrate that DMS production alters the planet in more than one way", "assert that algae are the sole beneficiaries of DMS production"], "columns": null, "pid": "v13_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "반론: 생물학자들은 이기적인 생물이 어떻게 지구 전체에 이익이 되도록 진화했는지 묻는다.\nLovelock의 답: 냉각이 조류 자신에게도 이익이 된다(영양분 공급).\n'Algae may also benefit from nitrogen' = 조류가 얻는 추가 이익을 제시해 Lovelock의 답변을 보강.\n정답: A", "trap": "D는 DMS가 지구를 여러 방식으로 바꾼다는 내용이지만 질소 언급의 초점은 지구가 아니라 '조류 자신의 이익'. E는 'sole beneficiaries'가 지나친 과장.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "benefit from nitrogen", "glosses": {"objection": "반론, 이의", "selfish ends": "이기적인 목적", "speculation": "추측"}, "src": "verbal13 Q12"}], [{"id": "v212_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The novel contains long, boring expository tangents designed to _____ readers, encouraging them to think they are reading a serious and important book, not just a thriller.", "choices": ["stymie", "placate", "amuse", "flatter", "reprove"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 콤마 뒤 'encouraging them to think they are reading a serious and important book' = 빈칸의 구체적 설명.\n독자에게 자신이 진지한 책을 읽는 수준 높은 독자라고 느끼게 함 → 빈칸 = 우쭐하게 하다.\nflatter(추켜세우다)가 정답.\n정답: D (flatter)", "trap": "placate(달래다)는 긍정적 어감이 비슷하지만 '화를 누그러뜨리다'라는 뜻이라 맞지 않음. amuse는 boring과 모순.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"flatter": "아첨하다, 우쭐하게 하다", "stymie": "방해하다, 좌절시키다", "placate": "달래다, 진정시키다", "amuse": "즐겁게 하다", "reprove": "꾸짖다"}, "src": "verbal212 Q1 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v24_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "While writers on Parker often present her as an avaricious stick figure, thus making her an object of (i)__________, Nash, by contrast, gives a more (ii)__________ and sympathetic portrait of the woman.", "choices": null, "columns": [["adulation", "praise", "opprobrium"], ["intense", "polemical", "nuanced"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'avaricious stick figure'(탐욕스러운 평면적 인물)로 묘사 → 비난의 대상 → opprobrium.\n(ii) by contrast + 'stick figure'(단순한 인물)의 반대 → 미묘하고 입체적인 → nuanced.\nsympathetic도 opprobrium의 반대로 연결됨.\n정답: C (opprobrium), F (nuanced)", "trap": "(ii)의 intense는 강한 어감만 줄 뿐 stick figure(단순함)의 반대가 아님. polemical(논쟁적)은 sympathetic과 어울리지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"adulation": "과찬, 아첨", "praise": "칭찬", "opprobrium": "비난, 오명", "intense": "강렬한", "polemical": "논쟁적인", "nuanced": "미묘한 차이를 살린, 섬세한"}, "src": "verbal24 Q2"}, {"id": "v216_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Among geophysicists there was considerably less (i) _____ the proposed environment measure than the (ii) _____ media accounts of the conference would suggest; the debate was often animated but never uncivil.", "choices": null, "columns": [["ambivalence toward", "satisfaction with", "rancor over"], ["sanitized", "sensationalized", "poignant"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 세미콜론 뒤 'the debate was often animated but never uncivil' = 실제로는 무례하지 않았다.\n(i) 실제로는 ___가 훨씬 적었다 → 적대감 → rancor over.\n(ii) 언론 보도는 실제보다 과장해 적대감이 있는 것처럼 보이게 함 → sensationalized.\n정답: C (rancor over), E (sensationalized)", "trap": "(ii)의 sanitized(순화된)는 오히려 갈등을 줄여 보도하는 것이라 'considerably less ... than media would suggest' 구조와 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ambivalence toward": "~에 대한 양가감정", "satisfaction with": "~에 대한 만족", "rancor over": "~에 대한 원한, 적대감", "sanitized": "순화된, 불쾌한 부분을 뺀", "sensationalized": "선정적으로 과장된", "poignant": "가슴 아픈, 통렬한"}, "src": "verbal216 Q2 · 25/5, 25/4, 24/11, 24/8, 23/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v26_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Our contemporary preference for natural expression over artifice is (i) _____ the traditional Western view that the skill with which you expressed a position corresponded closely to the credibility of your argument. Rhetorical styles might vary, but style itself was never a matter of (ii) _____. And \"style\" was not just a well-turned sentence: poor expression, it was believed, (iii) _____ poor thought.", "choices": null, "columns": [["a departure from", "a reflection on", "an endorsement of"], ["substance", "indifference", "intention"], ["ameliorated", "elevated", "betrayed"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AEI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 현대: 기교보다 자연스러운 표현 선호 vs 전통: 표현 기술이 논증의 신뢰도와 직결 → 현대 선호는 전통으로부터의 이탈 → a departure from.\n(ii) 스타일은 다양할 수 있지만 스타일 자체는 결코 '무관심의 문제(중요하지 않은 문제)'가 아니었다 → indifference.\n(iii) 나쁜 표현은 나쁜 사고를 드러낸다 → betrayed(무심코 드러내다).\n정답: A (a departure from), E (indifference), I (betrayed)", "trap": "(ii)에 substance를 넣으면 '스타일은 실질의 문제가 아니었다'가 되어 전통 시각과 반대. (iii)의 betrayed를 '배신하다'로만 알면 놓치기 쉬움.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"betrayed": "(무심코) 드러냈다", "a departure from": "~로부터의 이탈", "a reflection on": "~에 대한 성찰", "an endorsement of": "~에 대한 지지", "substance": "실질, 내용", "indifference": "무관심, 중요하지 않음", "intention": "의도", "ameliorated": "개선했다", "elevated": "높였다"}, "src": "verbal26 Q4"}, {"id": "v14_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following claims about Lamarque can be inferred from the passage?", "choices": ["She considered herself to be primarily a tango singer rather than a movie actor.", "By the end of her movie career, she was exercising considerable control over the writing and direction of her films.", "Her personality differed greatly from those of the characters she portrayed in films.", "Her popularity as a tango singer preceded her popularity as an actor.", "She continued to act in movies after she had ceased performing as a tango singer."], "columns": null, "pid": "v14_p4", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 관객 다수가 'were drawn to her early movies precisely because of her fame as a tango singer.'\n초기 영화 시절 이미 탱고 가수로 유명했다 → 가수로서의 인기가 배우로서의 인기보다 먼저.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 그녀 자신의 인식으로 지문에 근거 없음. E는 가수 활동을 그만둔 시점에 대한 정보가 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"melodrama": "멜로드라마", "transgressive": "위반하는, 금기를 깨는", "elitist": "엘리트주의적인"}, "src": "verbal14 Q14"}, {"id": "v14_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the author of the passage, which of the following is true about the tango?", "choices": ["By the time Lamarque starred in films as a tango singer, the tango was socially acceptable.", "Outside Argentina the tango's reputation was quite different from what prevailed in Argentina.", "The tango began to gain popularity in Argentina once it became an element in melodramatic films.", "By the 1930s, no one in Argentina associated the tango with criminality and vice.", "Until the 1930s, the tango was primarily thought of as a dance form rather than as a genre of song."], "columns": null, "pid": "v14_p4", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Despite its widespread social acceptance by the 1930s, tango continued to be associated in film melodramas with criminality and vice.'\n1930년대에 탱고는 이미 사회적으로 널리 수용됨 = Lamarque가 탱고 가수 역할로 출연하던 시기.\n정답: A", "trap": "D는 'no one'이 과장이며, 영화에서는 여전히 범죄와 연결되었다고 했으므로 틀림. B, E는 지문에 없는 내용.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"vice": "악덕", "criminality": "범죄성", "widespread": "널리 퍼진"}, "src": "verbal14 Q15"}, {"id": "v218_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following gives the most accurate definition of the trader's dilemma, as it is presented in the passage?", "choices": ["The impossibility of both remaining a part of the village's social structure and maintaining economic relations outside the village", "The conflict involved in sharing profits with both fellow villagers and people outside the village", "The difficulty of fulfilling both social obligations to neighbors and the economic imperatives of business", "The conflict between the need as a buyer to keep prices low and the need as a seller to have customers who can afford imported goods", "The difficulty of maintaining a distance from clients and customers while remaining part of their community"], "columns": null, "pid": "v218_p7", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the trader confronts the risk of either losing working capital or losing the respect and moral support of neighbors and kinfolk.'\n좋은 값을 쳐주거나 외상으로 팔아야 하는 도덕적 의무 vs 운영 자금 유지라는 사업상 요구.\n= 이웃에 대한 사회적 의무와 사업의 경제적 요구를 동시에 충족하기 어려움.\n정답: C", "trap": "D는 구매자/판매자 역할을 언급해 그럴듯하지만, 딜레마는 가격 문제 자체가 아니라 사회적 의무와 경제적 필요의 충돌. A는 '불가능'이라는 과장과 마을 밖 관계로 초점이 엇나감.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"working capital": "운영 자금", "kinfolk": "친척", "imperative": "필요, 의무"}, "src": "verbal218 Q7 · 25/11, 25/7, 25/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v218_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, the \"sociocultural change\" alluded to in the passage would occur as a result of", "choices": ["outside influences being brought to the village by villagers who travel as traders", "a rejection of individual economic interests in favor of communal political interests as a motive for action", "the recognition by peasant farmers that their interests were aligned with those of traders", "some villagers adopting cultural practices that imitate those of migrant traders", "a social segmentation within a village that reflects differentiated economic roles"], "columns": null, "pid": "v218_p7", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'a resident trading minority itself creates cultural distance in order to find a solution for the trader's dilemma, which thus may drive sociocultural change.'\n마을 내 상인과 농민이 '두 개의 별개 도덕 공동체'로 분화 → 경제적 역할에 따른 사회적 분리.\n정답: E", "trap": "B는 '경제적 이익보다 정치적 이익'으로 지문('economically rather than politically motivated')과 정반대. D는 이주 상인을 모방한다는 내용으로 지문에 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "sociocultural change", "glosses": {"differentiation": "분화", "segmentation": "분할, 구분", "migrant": "이주자"}, "src": "verbal218 Q8 · 25/11, 25/7, 25/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v218_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the \"way out of the dilemma\" described by Evers works by allowing", "choices": ["prices to be set by a market in which there are many buyers and many sellers", "people from outside the village to play the role of economic intermediary between the village and the outside world", "traders to fill dissociated roles as buyers and sellers on one hand and as neighbors and members of the village's moral community on the other", "villagers a greater range of options when they are selling their produce or buying supplies", "a weakening of the social and cultural bonds between traders and the people from whom they buy and to whom they sell"], "columns": null, "pid": "v218_p7", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'sociocultural differentiation of peasants and traders into two separate, locally coexisting moral communities', 'creates cultural distance'.\n상인이 농민과 다른 도덕 공동체가 되면 이웃으로서의 도덕적 의무(좋은 값, 외상)에서 벗어남.\n즉 상인과 고객 간 사회적, 문화적 유대를 약화시켜 딜레마를 해소.\n정답: E", "trap": "C는 상인이 여전히 '마을 도덕 공동체의 일원'으로 남는다고 해 함정. 지문은 상인이 별개의 도덕 공동체가 된다고 했으므로 틀림. B는 외부인 상인이 역할을 맡는 경우로, Evers의 요점(마을 내부 상인의 분화)과 다름.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "way out of the dilemma", "glosses": {"dissociated": "분리된", "intermediary": "중개자", "coexist": "공존하다"}, "src": "verbal218 Q9 · 25/11, 25/7, 25/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v10_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Whether the film is _____ adaptation of the legend is debatable; the author of the screenplay claims that it was based on the original tale, but admits taking some interpretive license with the story.", "choices": ["an inspired", "a rigorous", "an unsentimental", "a successful", "a sober", "a faithful"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 원작에 기반했다고 주장하지만 'admits taking some interpretive license' (해석상의 자유를 취함) → 원작에 충실했는지 논란.\n빈칸 = 원작에 충실하고 정확한.\nrigorous(엄격한, 정확한)와 faithful(충실한)이 짝.\n정답: B (a rigorous), F (a faithful)", "trap": "inspired(영감 받은)와 successful(성공적인)은 '논란의 여지가 있다'와 어울리지만 '해석의 자유'라는 근거와 연결되지 않고 서로 짝도 아님.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rigorous": "철저한", "sober": "침착한", "faithful": "충실한", "an inspired": "영감 받은, 탁월한", "a rigorous": "엄격한, 정확한", "an unsentimental": "감상적이지 않은", "a successful": "성공적인", "a sober": "냉정한, 절제된", "a faithful": "충실한"}, "src": "verbal10 Q10"}, {"id": "v210_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The legislators didn't merely sell out to business; they retreated to _____ style of governing whereby the interest group that is currently lobbying the hardest on an issue determines the party's position.", "choices": ["a reckless", "a rigid", "a craven", "an unyielding", "an arrogant", "a cowardly"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 가장 강하게 로비하는 이익 단체가 당의 입장을 결정하는 통치 방식 = 압력에 굴복하는 줏대 없는 방식.\n'didn't merely sell out' → 단순 매수보다 더 나쁜, 비겁한 후퇴.\ncraven(비겁한)과 cowardly(겁 많은)가 짝.\n정답: C (a craven), F (a cowardly)", "trap": "rigid와 unyielding(완고한)은 짝이지만, 로비에 따라 입장이 바뀌는 방식이므로 정반대 의미.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"a reckless": "무모한", "a rigid": "경직된", "a craven": "비겁한", "an unyielding": "굽히지 않는", "an arrogant": "오만한", "a cowardly": "겁 많은, 비겁한"}, "src": "verbal210 Q11 · 25년 7월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v28_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "For parents, the pleasure of letting children choose which book to read aloud together is not always _____; I well remembered my inner groans when my child would constantly pick my least favorite book from the shelf.", "choices": ["intangible", "enduring", "impalpable", "unalloyed", "ephemeral", "unqualified"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론 뒤 근거: 아이가 내가 제일 싫어하는 책을 고를 때마다 속으로 신음 → 즐거움에 불쾌함이 섞여 있다.\n빈칸 = 즐거움이 '항상 순수하고 완전하지는 않다'는 뜻.\nunalloyed(섞이지 않은, 순수한)와 unqualified(무조건적인, 완전한)가 짝.\n정답: D (unalloyed), F (unqualified)", "trap": "enduring(지속되는)은 not always와 어울려 보이지만 근거는 즐거움의 지속이 아니라 '불순물'에 관한 것. intangible/impalpable(무형의)은 짝이지만 문맥과 무관.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unalloyed": "섞이지 않은, 순수한", "ephemeral": "일시적인", "unqualified": "무조건적인, 완전한", "intangible": "무형의, 만질 수 없는", "enduring": "지속되는", "impalpable": "만질 수 없는, 감지하기 어려운"}, "src": "verbal28 Q9"}, {"id": "v20_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, most strongly supports the scientists' conclusion?", "choices": ["Volcanoes massive enough to generate high concentrations of iridium are very rare.", "Massive volcanic eruptions occurred frequently 80 million years ago.", "Most scientists support the hypothesis that a cosmic impact wiped out the dinosaurs.", "The massive extinction that occurred 70 million years ago killed not only the dinosaurs but also 70 percent of all life on Earth.", "A comet struck the earth some 120 million years ago, but no widespread extinction occurred."], "columns": null, "pid": "v20_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 높은 이리듐 농도 → 운석/혜성 충돌이 원인.\n근거상 이리듐 고농도의 원인은 두 가지(거대 화산 폭발, 운석).\n대안 원인(화산)이 가능성 낮다는 것을 보여주면 결론 강화.\nA: 그 정도 규모의 화산은 매우 드물다 → 화산 가능성 약화 → 운석 결론 지지.\n정답: A", "trap": "C는 '대부분 과학자가 지지한다'는 권위 호소로 논리적 근거가 아님. B는 8천만 년 전 화산이 잦았다는 것으로 6천5백만 년 전 지층과 무관하거나 오히려 화산 가능성을 열어줌.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"stratum": "지층", "meteorite": "운석", "extinction": "멸종"}, "src": "verbal20 Q11"}, {"id": "v24_q12", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, would challenge the hypothesis presented in the passage concerning Enceladus and Saturn's E ring?", "choices": ["Enceladus is not the only moon orbiting Saturn.", "Enceladus's lack of craters is not due to erasure by water.", "No impact has occurred on Enceladus in the past few tens of thousands of years."], "columns": null, "pid": "v24_p3", "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "가설: 최근 천 년 내 Enceladus 충돌로 액체 물이 우주로 분출 → 얼음 결정 → E 고리.\n근거 중 하나: 크레이터가 없음 = 최근 내부 액체 물이 표면을 덮었다.\nB: 크레이터 부재가 물 때문이 아니라면 액체 물의 존재 근거가 약해짐 → 도전.\nC: 수만 년간 충돌이 없었다면 '최근 천 년 내 충돌'이라는 핵심 전제가 무너짐 → 도전.\nA: 다른 위성이 있다는 것만으로는 Enceladus 가설을 반박하지 못함.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "A는 다른 위성이 원인일 가능성을 떠올리게 하지만, 단순히 다른 위성이 '존재'한다는 사실만으로는 가설에 도전하지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"solar radiation pressure": "태양 복사압", "disperse": "흩뜨리다", "preexisting": "기존의"}, "src": "verbal24 Q12"}, {"id": "v24_q13", "type": "RC_select", "blanks": null, "stem": "Select the sentence that points out the significance of the fact that the particles that make up Saturn's E ring are susceptible to dispersion.", "choices": [], "columns": null, "pid": "v24_p3", "answer": "SENTENCE", "answer_sentence": "That the ring exists today suggests, therefore, that it originated in the relatively recent past—but how?", "explanation": "첫 문장: 입자가 매우 작아 수만 년 안에 흩어진다(분산되기 쉬움)는 사실.\n둘째 문장: 'That the ring exists today suggests, therefore, that it originated in the relatively recent past' → 그 사실이 갖는 의미(고리가 최근에 생겼다는 것)를 짚어줌.\ntherefore가 '의미, 함의'를 나타내는 신호어.\n정답: That the ring exists today suggests, therefore, that it originated in the relatively recent past—but how?", "trap": "첫 문장은 분산되기 쉽다는 '사실' 자체를 진술할 뿐 그 의미를 말하지 않음. 이후 Enceladus 관련 문장은 원인 가설이지 분산의 의미가 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"susceptible": "~에 영향받기 쉬운", "dispersion": "분산", "originate": "생겨나다, 비롯되다"}, "src": "verbal24 Q13"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.7 / S2 2.9"}, {"set": 21, "sections": [[{"id": "v201_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The regulatory agency’s attempts to impose new and harsher restrictions on the business community were met with such _____ that the agency finally opted to maintain its existing rules.", "choices": ["impunity", "probity", "recalcitrance", "indemnity", "approbation"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 규제 기관이 더 가혹한 규제를 시도했으나 결국 기존 규칙을 유지하기로 함(finally opted to maintain).\n→ 업계의 반응이 강한 '저항'이어서 물러섰다는 인과 관계.\n빈칸 = 부정적 반응, '말을 듣지 않음/저항'이라는 뜻.\nrecalcitrance(반항, 고집스러운 저항)가 정확히 들어맞음.\n정답: C (recalcitrance)", "trap": "approbation(승인)은 반응을 나타내는 단어지만 방향이 반대 — 승인받았다면 규제를 포기할 이유가 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"impunity": "처벌받지 않음, 면책", "probity": "정직성, 청렴", "recalcitrance": "반항, 완강한 저항", "indemnity": "보상, 손해 배상(보장)", "approbation": "승인, 찬성"}, "src": "verbal201 Q1 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v229_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Ancient cart ruts found on Malta were created in soft limestone that begins to dissolve when exposed to rainfall. Their forms thus necessarily become (i) _____ over time and their original features are (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["solidified", "degraded", "conspicuous"], ["refined", "replicated", "obscured"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 석회암이 빗물에 녹기 시작함 → thus(결과).\n(i) 시간이 지나며 형태가 '손상/풍화'되어야 함 → degraded.\n(ii) 원래 특징이 '흐려지고 알아보기 어렵게' 됨 → obscured.\n녹아내림 → 마모 → 원형 불분명이라는 일관된 흐름.\n정답: B (degraded), F (obscured)", "trap": "solidified/conspicuous는 녹는다는 내용과 정반대. refined(정교해진)도 '녹아서 다듬어졌다'로 착각하기 쉽지만 원래 특징이 사라지는 문맥과 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"solidified": "굳어진, 단단해진", "degraded": "열화된, 손상된", "conspicuous": "눈에 띄는", "refined": "정제된, 세련된", "replicated": "복제된", "obscured": "흐려진, 가려진"}, "src": "verbal229 Q2 · 24년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v215_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "There are two opposing theories about mountain formation and climate over the past 40 million years: either the surge of mountain building (i) _____ the global cooling, or vice versa. The first of these two theories asserts that widespread mountain building cooled the earth as a result of the (ii) _____ mountains and climate. For example, mountain glaciers tend to be (iii) _____: once established, they increase the reflectivity of the surface, thus lowering temperatures and allowing more ice to form.", "choices": null, "columns": [["superseded", "halted", "caused"], ["disparity between", "feedback between", "complexity of"], ["unpredictable", "static", "self-perpetuating"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CEI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'either A ___ B, or vice versa' → 두 이론은 인과 방향이 반대. 산맥 형성이 냉각을 '일으켰다' → caused.\n(ii) 첫 이론: 산맥 형성이 지구를 냉각시킴. 예시에서 빙하가 반사율을 높여 기온을 낮추고 더 많은 얼음 형성 → 산과 기후의 상호 작용, 즉 feedback between.\n(iii) 'once established, ... allowing more ice to form' → 스스로 계속 강화되는 = self-perpetuating.\n정답: C (caused), E (feedback between), I (self-perpetuating)", "trap": "(ii)의 complexity of는 그럴듯하지만, 뒤 예시가 보여주는 것은 '복잡성'이 아니라 순환적 상호 강화(피드백). (iii) static은 '한번 생기면 유지된다'로 오해하기 쉽지만 '더 많은 얼음'이 생기는 확장을 설명 못함.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"superseded": "대체했다", "halted": "멈추게 했다", "caused": "일으켰다", "disparity between": "~사이의 불균형", "feedback between": "~사이의 되먹임(상호 작용)", "complexity of": "~의 복잡성", "unpredictable": "예측할 수 없는", "static": "정적인, 변화 없는", "self-perpetuating": "스스로 지속/강화되는"}, "src": "verbal215 Q3 · 25/8, 24/10, 24/9, 23/10, 23/8 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is an assumption that may be invalidated by recent seismological evidence?", "choices": ["Earthquakes are caused by stresses building up in faults within Earth’s crust.", "Most major earthquakes can be predicted with reasonable accuracy.", "Faults are highly responsive to even minor stresses in neighboring faults.", "Most major earthquakes are followed by predictable aftershocks.", "A fault that has resulted in a major earthquake becomes quiet for a long period."], "columns": null, "pid": "v221_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 첫 문장 'Most seismologists assume that following a major earthquake ..., the fault ... will remain quiet until stresses have time to rebuild, typically over hundreds or thousands of years.'\n둘째 문장 'Recent evidence ... may overturn this assumption' → 뒤집힐 수 있는 가정이 바로 이것.\nE '큰 지진을 일으킨 단층은 오랫동안 조용해진다'가 정확한 paraphrase.\n정답: E", "trap": "C는 새 가설(stress-triggering)의 내용이지 뒤집힐 가정이 아님 — 관계를 거꾸로 뒤집은 선택지.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"fault": "단층", "aftershock": "여진", "dissipate": "흩어지다, 소멸하다", "invalidate": "무효화하다"}, "src": "verbal221 Q4 · 24/3, 23/9, 22/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that most seismologists believe which of the following about fault stresses?", "choices": ["They are dissipated when they result in an earthquake.", "They are transferred between neighboring faults.", "They will not cause a major earthquake along the same fault in the space of a few years."], "columns": null, "pid": "v221_p4", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'Rather than simply dissipating, stress relieved during an earthquake travels...' → 새 가설이 반박하는 기존 통념은 '응력이 그냥 소멸된다'는 것 → 다수 지진학자의 믿음으로 추론 가능.\nC: 기존 가정 'remain quiet until stresses have time to rebuild, typically over hundreds or thousands of years' → 몇 년 안에 같은 단층에서 큰 지진은 없다.\nB는 stress-triggering 가설의 주장이며, 'scientists have long viewed such subtle interactions as nonexistent'와 반대.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "B(이웃 단층 간 응력 전달)는 지문에 나오는 내용이라 고르기 쉽지만, 다수 학자가 아니라 새 가설의 입장임.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"stress-triggering": "응력 유발(촉발)", "dissipate": "소멸하다", "subtle": "미묘한", "overturn": "뒤집다"}, "src": "verbal221 Q5 · 24/3, 23/9, 22/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v7_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the Old Southwest, only writers who showed exceptional _____ were likely to become widely known, because the region's weak infrastructure inhibited the development of publishing beyond local newspapers that served small towns.", "choices": ["prescience", "foresightedness", "optimism", "resolve", "patience", "determination"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: because 이하 — 기반 시설이 약해 지역 신문 외에는 출판이 발달하지 못함.\n→ 이런 열악한 조건을 뚫고 유명해지려면 '끈기/결단력'이 필요.\n빈칸 = 어려움을 이겨내는 의지.\nresolve와 determination은 둘 다 '결의, 결단력'으로 동의어 쌍.\n정답: D (resolve), F (determination)", "trap": "prescience/foresightedness도 '선견지명'으로 짝을 이루지만, 장애물을 극복하는 문맥에 맞지 않음. patience는 단독으로 그럴듯하나 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"prescience": "선견지명", "foresightedness": "선견지명, 앞을 내다봄", "optimism": "낙관주의", "resolve": "결의, 결단력", "patience": "인내심", "determination": "결단력, 투지"}, "src": "verbal7 Q7"}, {"id": "v33_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Ancient cave painters explored every surface, and although they bypassed certain walls that to us seem just as suitable for decoration as ones they chose, the placement of the art apparently wasn’t _____.", "choices": ["inconsequential", "capricious", "strenuous", "undisclosed", "arduous", "impulsive"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: although — 똑같이 적합해 보이는 벽을 건너뛰었지만, 그럼에도 → 배치가 '아무렇게나' 한 것은 아니었다.\n건너뛴 벽이 있다는 사실이 의도적 선택을 암시.\n빈칸 = '무작위, 변덕스러운'이라는 뜻(앞에 wasn't가 있으므로).\ncapricious와 impulsive가 '변덕스러운/충동적인'으로 짝.\n정답: B (capricious), F (impulsive)", "trap": "inconsequential(중요하지 않은)은 단독으로 말이 되는 듯하지만 짝이 없음. strenuous/arduous는 '힘든'으로 짝은 맞지만 문맥과 무관.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inconsequential": "중요하지 않은, 사소한", "capricious": "변덕스러운", "strenuous": "몹시 힘든, 격렬한", "undisclosed": "공개되지 않은", "arduous": "몹시 힘든", "impulsive": "충동적인"}, "src": "verbal33 Q8"}, {"id": "v203_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The use of temperature records for the period from 1880 to 1899 as the favored baseline for measuring global warming is _____ because the 1880s were particularly cold after the eruption of the Krakatoa volcano.", "choices": ["injudicious", "unnecessary", "ill-advised", "controversial", "commonplace", "widespread"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: because — 1880년대는 크라카토아 화산 폭발 이후 특히 추웠음.\n→ 비정상적으로 추운 시기를 기준선으로 쓰면 온난화가 과장됨 → 그 선택은 '현명하지 못하다'.\n빈칸 = 부정적 평가, '부적절한/분별없는'.\ninjudicious와 ill-advised가 동의어 쌍.\n정답: A (injudicious), C (ill-advised)", "trap": "controversial은 단독으로 그럴듯하지만 이유절이 '논란'이 아니라 '잘못된 선택'을 뒷받침하며 짝도 없음. commonplace/widespread는 짝이지만 because절과 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"injudicious": "분별없는, 현명하지 못한", "unnecessary": "불필요한", "ill-advised": "현명하지 못한, 경솔한", "controversial": "논란이 많은", "commonplace": "흔한", "widespread": "널리 퍼진"}, "src": "verbal203 Q8 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although ants and humans have _____ lifestyles, they fight their foes for many of the same economic reasons, including access to dwelling spaces, to territory, and to food.", "choices": ["complex", "divergent", "atypical", "conflicting", "disparate", "complicated"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Although — 개미와 인간이 '같은' 경제적 이유로 싸운다는 내용과 대조.\n빈칸 = 생활 방식이 '서로 다르다'는 뜻.\ndivergent와 disparate가 '이질적인, 서로 다른'으로 동의어 쌍.\n정답: B (divergent), E (disparate)", "trap": "complex/complicated는 짝을 이루지만 'same reasons'와 대조를 만들지 못함. conflicting은 '충돌하는'으로 차이와 다름.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"complex": "복잡한", "divergent": "서로 다른, 갈라지는", "atypical": "비전형적인", "conflicting": "상충하는", "disparate": "이질적인, 서로 다른", "complicated": "복잡한"}, "src": "verbal221 Q6 · 25년 3월, 25년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v239_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that Leonardo Bruni most likely believed which of the following?", "choices": ["The private sphere was superior to the public sphere.", "Formal education was unnecessary for women in Renaissance Italy.", "Rhetoric was useful primarily in the public sphere rather than in the private sphere.", "Women in Renaissance Italy had less desire to study rhetoric than did men.", "Most liberal arts were of little utility in the public sphere."], "columns": null, "pid": "v239_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Bruni는 여성이 남성처럼 교양 과목을 배우되 rhetoric은 'lies wholly outside the province of women'라고 함.\n이어서 이것이 'women's province was the private sphere rather than the public sphere'라는 인문주의 가정과 연결됨.\n→ 여성의 영역 = 사적 영역이므로 수사학은 여성 영역 밖 = 공적 영역에 속하는 기술이라고 Bruni가 생각했음을 추론.\n정답: C", "trap": "D는 '여성이 수사학을 원하지 않았다'로 바꿔치기 — Bruni의 주장은 여성의 '영역'에 관한 것이지 욕구에 관한 것이 아님. B는 교양 과목 학습을 권장했으므로 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pedagogic": "교육학의", "imperative": "명령, 필수 사항", "rhetoric": "수사학, 웅변술", "relegation": "격하, 밀어냄"}, "src": "verbal239 Q10 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v239_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is a crticism the author of the passage makes of Burckhardt's work?", "choices": ["Burckhardt's discussion of women's roles overemphasizes certain social and economic factors at the expense of other factors.", "Burckhardt failed to conduct a detailed study of all of the works of Bruni.", "Burckhardt was overly influenced by nineteenth-century assumptions about women's roles.", "Burckhardt relied heavily on sixteenth-century Italian pedagogic works; thus, his work was narrowly focused.", "Burckhardt overlooked important evidence because he shared an assumpton contained in that evidence."], "columns": null, "pid": "v239_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Bruni의 지시가 'went unnoticed by Burckhardt because he shared the humanist assumption that women's province was the private sphere'.\n→ Burckhardt는 증거(인문주의 텍스트) 속 불평등을 보지 못했는데, 그 이유가 그 증거에 담긴 가정을 자신도 공유했기 때문.\nE가 이를 정확히 일반화함.\n정답: E", "trap": "C는 그럴듯하지만 지문은 '19세기' 가정이 아니라 '인문주의자(르네상스)'의 가정을 공유했다고 말함 — 출처를 바꿔치기한 선택지.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"elite": "엘리트의, 소수 정예의", "humanist": "인문주의자", "province": "영역, 분야", "assumption": "가정"}, "src": "verbal239 Q11 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v239_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, would cast the most serious doubt on the position taken by the author of the passage regarding Burckhardt's evaluation of historical evidence?", "choices": ["Burckhardt's scholarly works focus almost exclusively on sixteenth-century European humanists.", "Burckhardt had read Bruni's pedagogic works and had admired them.", "Margaret King's work has received considerable scholarly acclaim.", "Many of Bruni's colleagues felt that women should be excluded from instruction in all of the liberal arts.", "Margaret King's evidence is based largely on Bruni's work, which was not representative of humanist texts."], "columns": null, "pid": "v239_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "저자의 입장: Burckhardt는 인문주의자와 동일시해 증거를 잘못 평가했고, King이 보였듯 인문주의 텍스트는 실제로 남녀 불평등을 반영함(Bruni를 예로 듦).\n약화: King의 증거가 대부분 Bruni에 기반하고 Bruni의 글이 인문주의 텍스트를 대표하지 않는다면, '인문주의 텍스트는 불평등을 반영한다'는 근거가 무너짐 → Burckhardt의 평가가 옳았을 수도.\n정답: E", "trap": "B(Burckhardt가 Bruni의 글을 읽고 감탄했다)는 오히려 '그가 불평등을 알아채지 못했다'는 저자 주장과 양립하거나 강화함. D는 인문주의자들이 더 차별적이었다는 것으로 저자를 강화.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cast doubt on": "~에 의문을 제기하다", "representative": "대표적인", "acclaim": "찬사"}, "src": "verbal239 Q12 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v220_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The character whose fate dominates the film's plot appears only briefly onscreen, a bit of narrative slyness that we might welcome as _____ the sensory overload more characteristic of this director.", "choices": ["a consequence of", "an intensification of", "an incorporation of", "an allusion to", "a palliative to"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: '이 감독의 특징인 sensory overload(감각 과부하)'와 '주인공이 잠깐만 등장하는 절제된 서술(slyness)'이 대비됨.\nwelcome(반가워하다) → 과부하에 대한 '해독제/완화책'으로 반길 수 있다.\n빈칸 = 과부하를 '덜어주는 것'.\na palliative to = ~에 대한 완화책.\n정답: E (a palliative to)", "trap": "an intensification of(강화)는 반대 방향. an allusion to는 형식상 가능해 보이나 '환영할 만한' 대비 관계를 설명하지 못함.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"slyness": "교묘함", "a palliative to": "~에 대한 완화책, 진정제", "a consequence of": "~의 결과", "an intensification of": "~의 강화", "an incorporation of": "~의 통합, 편입", "an allusion to": "~에 대한 암시, 언급"}, "src": "verbal220 Q1 · 25년 7월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The committee (i) _____ their praise for the proposal with several (ii) _____ remarks pointing out flaws in the document; in fact, one committee member referred to a trivial typographical error as \"unpardonable.”", "choices": null, "columns": [["underscored", "tempered", "augmented"], ["captious", "adroit", "propitious"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'in fact' 이하 — 사소한 오타를 '용서할 수 없다'고까지 함 → 지나친 트집.\n(ii) 결함을 지적하는 지나치게 까다로운 발언 → captious(트집 잡는).\n(i) 칭찬을 그런 비판으로 '누그러뜨렸다' → tempered.\n정답: B (tempered), D (captious)", "trap": "(i) underscored/augmented는 칭찬을 '강화'하는 뜻이라 비판적 발언과 함께 쓰기 어려움. (ii) propitious(유리한)는 결함 지적과 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"captious": "트집 잡기 좋아하는, 흠잡는", "adroit": "능숙한, 솜씨 좋은", "propitious": "유리한, 길조의", "underscored": "강조했다", "tempered": "누그러뜨렸다, 완화했다", "augmented": "증대시켰다"}, "src": "verbal234 Q2 · 24년 2월, 23년 7월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v10_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The enlightenment philosophers of the eighteenth century acknowledged that unrestricted freedom to publish could (i) _____ motivated by envy or hatred, but they hoped that any such (ii) _____ enabled by expanded liberties would suffer from being publicly exposed.", "choices": null, "columns": [["encourage blandishments", "facilitate calumny", "constrain vituperation"], ["evasion", "defamation", "prurience"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'motivated by envy or hatred' → 시기·증오에서 나온 것 = 비방. 무제한 출판의 자유가 비방을 '조장할 수 있다' → facilitate calumny.\n(ii) 'any such ___' → 앞의 calumny를 다시 가리키는 말 = defamation(명예 훼손).\nbut they hoped ... suffer from being publicly exposed → 그런 비방은 공개되면 타격을 입으리라 기대.\n정답: B (facilitate calumny), E (defamation)", "trap": "constrain vituperation은 '혹평'이 시기·증오와 어울리지만 constrain(억제하다)이 acknowledged(우려를 인정)와 방향이 반대. blandishments(감언)는 증오와 무관.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"blandishments": "감언이섧", "calumny": "비방", "vituperation": "혹평", "prurience": "음란함, 호색", "encourage blandishments": "감언이설을 조장하다", "facilitate calumny": "비방을 용이하게 하다", "constrain vituperation": "혹평을 억제하다", "evasion": "회피", "defamation": "명예 훼손, 중상"}, "src": "verbal10 Q2"}, {"id": "v226_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Although Dostoyevsky was not the (i) _____ portrayed by some biographers, at least implicitly guilty of the terrible crimes he depicted in his novels, he was notoriously (ii) _____. Indeed, his attitude toward people who questioned him about his work was anything but friendly. No such problems bother students of Chekhov. On the contrary, it is difficult to think of a writer of equal fame and importance who, on close inspection, proves to be such a (iii) _____ human being.", "choices": null, "columns": [["monster", "malcontent", "pedant"], ["vain", "diffident", "prickly"], ["sympathetic", "self-assured", "talented"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'at least implicitly guilty of the terrible crimes he depicted' → 끔찍한 범죄를 저지른 듯 그려진 인물 = monster.\n(ii) 'Indeed, his attitude toward people who questioned him ... was anything but friendly' → 까칠하고 성마른 = prickly.\n(iii) 'On the contrary' → 체호프는 도스토옙스키와 반대로 호감 가는 인간 = sympathetic.\n정답: A (monster), F (prickly), G (sympathetic)", "trap": "(ii) vain(허영심 많은)은 부정적이라 끌리지만 '질문하는 사람에게 불친절함'을 직접 설명하지 못함. (iii) talented는 '명성과 중요성이 같은 작가'와 비교하는 문맥에서 인간적 성품과 무관.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"vain": "허영심 많은", "monster": "괴물, 극악한 사람", "malcontent": "불평분자", "pedant": "현학자", "diffident": "자신감 없는, 소심한", "prickly": "성미가 까다로운, 까칠한", "sympathetic": "호감 가는, 인정 많은", "self-assured": "자신감 있는", "talented": "재능 있는"}, "src": "verbal226 Q4 · 25년 6월, 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v12_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage mentions \"orangutans in other habitats where Neesia grows\" primarily in order to", "choices": ["explain why orangutans living in dry forests apparently do not use tools to obtain foods", "propose an alternative to the environmental explanation for Suaq orangutans' tool use", "demonstrate how environment may influence orangutan populations' brain capacity", "contrast the food preferences of the Suaq orangutans with those of orangutans living in other habitats", "suggest that the Suaq orangutans' tool use cannot be explained merely by the availability of certain foods in their habitat"], "columns": null, "pid": "v12_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: 도구 사용의 설명 후보 ① 지능 → 부정 ② 환경(곤충·Neesia가 풍부한 늪지) 제시.\n마지막 문장 'However, orangutans in other habitats where Neesia grows do harvest the seeds, but without tools'.\n→ Neesia가 있는 다른 곳의 오랑우탄은 도구 없이 수확함 → 먹이의 존재만으로는 도구 사용을 설명할 수 없다.\n정답: E", "trap": "B는 '환경적 설명에 대한 대안을 제시'한다고 하지만, 지문은 환경 설명의 한계를 지적할 뿐 대안을 내놓지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "orangutans in other habitats where Neesia grows", "glosses": {"intrinsically": "본질적으로", "extract": "추출하다, 빼내다", "flourish": "번성하다"}, "src": "verbal12 Q14"}, {"id": "v12_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about orangutans that live mostly in dry forests?", "choices": ["They probably use some tools, though this tool use has not been observed by researchers.", "They dislike the foods that the orangutans living near Suaq Balimbing prefer.", "They probably have the same capacity for tool use as have orangutans living near Suaq Balimbing."], "columns": null, "pid": "v12_p4", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'captive orangutans have demonstrated that the species has the brain capacity to use tools' → 종(species) 전체가 도구 사용 능력을 가짐.\n따라서 건조림에 사는 오랑우탄도 Suaq 오랑우탄과 같은 능력이 있다고 추론 가능 → C.\nA: 관찰되지 않았다는 사실만 있을 뿐 '아마 사용한다'는 근거 없음. B: 먹이 선호에 관한 언급 없음.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 '관찰되지 않았다'를 '사용하지만 못 봤다'로 비약 — 근거 없는 추측.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"captive": "사로잡힌, 사육되는", "brain capacity": "뇌 능력", "habitat": "서식지"}, "src": "verbal12 Q15"}, {"id": "v18_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, village sketches written by women in the United States in the 1830s and 1840s typically reflected", "choices": ["the negotiations that characterized trade relationships between villages", "the fact that these women did not often travel very far beyond their own village", "the plurality of experiences and ideas that existed among the residents of a village"], "columns": null, "pid": "v18_p1", "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "B: 'These women's geographical mobility was restricted ..., and their subject matter reflected this fact' → 멀리 이동하지 못한 사실이 작품에 반영됨.\nC: 'depicted the diversity', 'divergent histories, positions, expectations, and beliefs' → 주민들 사이 경험·생각의 다양성.\nA: negotiation은 공동체 '내부'의 관계에 대한 것이지 마을 간 '무역'이 아님.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "A는 지문의 'negotiated'를 그대로 가져와 마을 간 무역 관계로 바꿔치기한 함정.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"homogeneous": "동질적인", "circumscribed": "제한된", "divergent": "서로 다른", "plurality": "다양성, 복수성"}, "src": "verbal18 Q5"}, {"id": "v18_q6", "type": "RC_select", "blanks": null, "stem": "Select the sentence in the passage that contrasts how men and women depicted life in village communities.", "choices": [], "columns": null, "pid": "v18_p1", "answer": "SENTENCE", "answer_sentence": "Buell's study of village sketches (a type of fiction popular in the United States in the 1830s and 1840s) provides a valuable summary of sketches that portray the community as homogeneous and fixed, but it ignores those by women writers, which typically depicted the diversity that increasingly characterized actual village communities at that time.", "explanation": "남성/여성 작가의 묘사 대조를 찾아야 함.\n첫 문장: Buell이 정리한 (주로 남성 작가의) 스케치는 'portray the community as homogeneous and fixed', 반면 여성 작가의 것은 'depicted the diversity'.\n→ 동질적·고정적 vs 다양성의 대조가 이 문장에 있음.\n정답: 첫 번째 문장(Buell's study of village sketches ...)", "trap": "'all stress differences among men and among women ... as well as differences between the sexes' 문장은 남녀 '사이의 차이를 묘사'한다는 내용일 뿐, 남녀 작가의 묘사 방식을 대조하지 않음.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"homogeneous": "동질적인", "summary": "요약", "diversity": "다양성"}, "src": "verbal18 Q6"}, {"id": "v18_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage indicates that when Gilligan spoke of \"the ability to attend to voices other than one's own,\" she", "choices": ["did not consider that ability to be a desirable psychological characteristic", "did not believe that individuals differ greatly with respect to that ability", "was implying that that ability enhances a sense of belonging in communities", "was assuming that good writers are able to depict diverse characters", "was not discussing the women who wrote village sketches"], "columns": null, "pid": "v18_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'what Gilligan, writing in a different context, has called the ability to attend to voices other than one's own'.\n'in a different context' → Gilligan은 마을 스케치를 쓴 여성 작가들에 대해 말한 것이 아님.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(좋은 작가는 다양한 인물을 그릴 수 있다고 가정)는 저자가 그 개념을 여성 작가에 적용한 것을 Gilligan의 의도로 착각하게 만드는 함정.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "the ability to attend to voices other than one's own", "glosses": {"attend to": "~에 귀 기울이다, 주의를 기울이다", "context": "맥락", "enriched": "풍부해진"}, "src": "verbal18 Q7"}, {"id": "v220_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In her early years as a theater critic, Willa Cather was _____, veering between ecstatic raves and brutal takedowns.", "choices": ["bellicose", "enigmatic", "mercurial", "pugnacious", "volatile", "voluble"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 쉼표 뒤 설명 'veering between ecstatic raves and brutal takedowns' → 극찬과 혹평 사이를 오락가락.\n빈칸 = '변덕스러운, 기복이 심한'.\nmercurial과 volatile이 동의어 쌍.\n정답: C (mercurial), E (volatile)", "trap": "bellicose/pugnacious(호전적인)는 짝을 이루며 brutal takedowns에 끌리지만, ecstatic raves(극찬)까지 포함한 '오락가락'을 설명하지 못함.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"mercurial": "변덕스러운", "bellicose": "호전적인", "enigmatic": "수수께끼 같은", "pugnacious": "싸우기 좋아하는", "volatile": "변덕스러운, 불안정한", "voluble": "말이 많은, 유창한"}, "src": "verbal220 Q11 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v30_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The laboratory maze has grown ever less _____ since it was invented; instead of hoping to lose a rodent in a labyrinth, today’s scientists design mazes to elicit a few simple, easily measurable behaviors.", "choices": ["intricate", "extensive", "effective", "convoluted", "useful", "prevalent"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: instead of hoping to lose a rodent in a labyrinth → 예전에는 쥐를 잃어버릴 만큼 복잡했음.\n현재는 'a few simple, easily measurable behaviors' → 단순해짐 → 'ever less ___' = 덜 복잡해짐.\n빈칸 = '복잡한'.\nintricate와 convoluted가 동의어 쌍.\n정답: A (intricate), D (convoluted)", "trap": "effective/useful은 짝이지만 '덜 유용해졌다'는 지문 어디에도 없음. extensive는 크기와 관련되어 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"intricate": "복잡한, 정교한", "extensive": "광범위한, 대규모의", "effective": "효과적인", "convoluted": "뒤얽힌, 복잡한", "useful": "유용한", "prevalent": "널리 퍼진"}, "src": "verbal30 Q9"}, {"id": "v214_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "My colleagues _____ the journalist's vaunted expertise at securing high-profile interviews, declaring that, given her family's connections to celebrities, obtaining such interviews must be no more difficult than asking a friend out for coffee.", "choices": ["confounded", "disparaged", "dismissed", "envied", "thwarted", "sanctioned"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: declaring that ... 가족 인맥 덕분에 인터뷰는 친구에게 커피 마시자는 것만큼 쉬울 것이다 → 그녀의 실력을 깎아내림.\nvaunted(과시된, 자랑하는) 전문성을 '폄하/일축'했다.\n빈칸 = 부정적, '대수롭지 않게 여기다'.\ndisparaged와 dismissed가 짝.\n정답: B (disparaged), C (dismissed)", "trap": "envied는 유명인 인맥에 대한 질투로 읽힐 수 있지만, 동료들이 '쉬운 일'이라 말하는 것은 깎아내림이며 짝도 없음. thwarted는 실제 방해 행위를 뜻해 발언과 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"thwarted": "좌절시켰다, 방해했다", "sanctioned": "승인했다; 제재했다", "confounded": "혼란스럽게 했다, 좌절시켰다", "disparaged": "폄하했다", "dismissed": "일축했다, 묵살했다", "envied": "부러워했다"}, "src": "verbal214 Q10 · 25년 9월, 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v32_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following most logically completes the argument?", "choices": ["The fruits of the domesticated varieties are too large for birds to swallow.", "C.chinense grows in the Caribbean islands under climatic conditions very similar to those under which the wild variety grows.", "The peppers are an important part of the Caribbean islands’ characteristic cooking.", "Most of the plant species in the Caribbean islands originated is South America.", "Many of the species of birds that are found in the Caribbean islands spend only the winter there."], "columns": null, "pid": "v32_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: C. chinense가 카리브 제도에 들어온 것은 아마 인간 활동 때문이다.\n자연 전파 경로는 새가 열매를 통째로 삼켜 씨를 퍼뜨리는 것뿐.\n카리브에 있는 것은 재배종(domesticated) → 재배종 열매가 너무 커서 새가 삼킬 수 없다면 새에 의한 전파는 불가능 → 인간이 옮겼다는 결론을 뒷받침.\n정답: A", "trap": "E(겨울에만 머무는 철새)는 새의 이동을 언급해 끌리지만 오히려 새가 남미에서 씨를 옮겼을 가능성을 열어줌. C(요리에 중요)는 인간과의 관계를 말할 뿐 도입 원인은 증명 못함.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"domesticated": "재배된, 길들여진", "distributing": "퍼뜨리는", "introduction": "도입, 유입"}, "src": "verbal32 Q11"}, {"id": "v204_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author implies which of the following about “certain basic biological characteristics”?", "choices": ["They are less applicable to invasive species than many scientists think.", "They suggest that invasive species are more destructive than they really are.", "They are just as prevalent among noninvasive species as among invasive species.", "They can help distinguish invasive from noninvasive species.", "They may help explain why invasive species are successful in some habitats but not in others."], "columns": null, "pid": "v204_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'They all share certain basic biological characteristics ... but these merely describe, rather than explain, their power.'\n→ 이 특성들은 침입종의 '설명'은 못 하지만 침입종을 '묘사'하는 공통 특징이므로, 침입종을 식별·구별하는 데는 쓸 수 있다.\n정답: D", "trap": "E는 '설명하는 데 도움이 될 수 있다'고 해 'merely describe, rather than explain'과 정면으로 모순. C(비침입종에도 똑같이 흔하다)는 지문에 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "certain basic biological characteristics", "glosses": {"opportunism": "기회주의", "voraciousness": "탐욕, 게걸스러움", "ascribe": "~의 탓으로 돌리다", "tempered": "단련된"}, "src": "verbal204 Q5 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v204_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author notes that invaders are “not necessarily dominant in their original habitats” primarily to", "choices": ["demonstrate the limitations of a theory", "highlight an alternative point of view", "elaborate on the central point of an argument", "explain the outcome of a process", "question the validity of a hypothesis"], "columns": null, "pid": "v204_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "주장(고전적 설명): 침입종은 오랜 경쟁으로 단련된 강인함을 지님.\n'They are not necessarily dominant in their original habitats' → 원래 서식지에서는 적과 경쟁 때문에 우세하지 않았음.\n이어서 'When they find new territory, they escape competitors and predators' → 새 지역에서 잠재력을 발휘.\n즉 같은 논지를 구체적으로 부연함 = 논증의 중심 요점을 상술.\n정답: C", "trap": "A/E는 이 문장을 이론의 한계·반론으로 오해한 것 — 실제로는 같은 이론의 일부. B도 대안적 관점이 아님.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "not necessarily dominant in their original habitats", "glosses": {"tempered": "단련된", "unleash": "풀어놓다", "marauding": "약탈하는, 휩쓰는", "dominant": "우세한"}, "src": "verbal204 Q6 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.4 / S2 3.1"}, {"set": 22, "sections": [[{"id": "v215_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Accustomed to the author's ponderous prose, readers will likely be startled by the _____ that characterizes his new work.", "choices": ["prolixity", "jocularity", "abstruseness", "predictability", "pessimism"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Accustomed to ponderous prose(무겁고 지루한 문체)에 익숙한 독자가 'startled(놀라다)'.\n→ 새 작품은 그와 정반대 특징이어야 함.\n빈칸 = 가볍고 재미있는 = jocularity.\n정답: B (jocularity)", "trap": "prolixity/abstruseness는 ponderous와 비슷한 성질이라 놀랄 이유가 없음. pessimism은 무거움과 대조되지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"ponderous prose": "무겁고 단단한 문체", "prolixity": "장황함", "jocularity": "익살, 쾌활함", "abstruseness": "난해함", "predictability": "예측 가능성", "pessimism": "비관주의"}, "src": "verbal215 Q1 · 25/9, 25/8, 23/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "In years prior to the Civil War, Philadelphia’s African American press encouraged readers to be vaccinated against the smallpox. This journalistic campaign was initially (i) _____, appealing to readers’ sense of communal duty, and became even more (ii) _____ once the war started, as smallpox outbreaks began to occur on Philadelphia’s city skirts.", "choices": null, "columns": [["hortatory", "ineffective", "widespread"], ["controversial", "urgent", "inopportune"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'appealing to readers' sense of communal duty' → 공동체 의무감에 호소하는 = 권고하는 = hortatory.\n(ii) 'became even more ___ once the war started, as smallpox outbreaks began to occur' → 발병이 가까이 생기며 더 '긴박'해짐 = urgent.\n정답: A (hortatory), E (urgent)", "trap": "(i) widespread는 단독으로 그럴듯하지만 쉼표 뒤 '의무감에 호소'라는 동격 설명과 맞지 않음. (ii) controversial은 발병 확산이 논란을 키운다는 근거가 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hortatory": "권고하는, 장려하는", "ineffective": "효과 없는", "widespread": "널리 퍼진", "controversial": "논란이 많은", "urgent": "긴급한", "inopportune": "시기가 좋지 않은"}, "src": "verbal221 Q2 · 24/12, 22/10 중국후기"}, {"id": "v15_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Books about humor are rarely funny. Their goal, after all, is to (i) _____ the workings of that which we find comic, not to (ii) _____ laughter, and understanding why jokes are funny is not in itself (iii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["celebrate", "analyze", "improve"], ["explain", "occasion", "recall"], ["amusing", "helpful", "admirable"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BEG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 유머에 관한 책은 거의 재미없다 → 그 이유 설명.\n(i) 목표는 우스운 것의 작동 원리를 '분석'하는 것 → analyze.\n(ii) 'not to ___ laughter' → 웃음을 '일으키는' 것이 아님 → occasion.\n(iii) 농담이 왜 웃긴지 이해하는 것 자체는 '재미있지' 않다 → amusing (첫 문장 'rarely funny'와 연결).\n정답: B (analyze), E (occasion), G (amusing)", "trap": "(ii) explain은 (i)의 analyze와 겹치며 'not to'와 대조를 만들지 못함. (iii) helpful은 그럴듯하지만 '재미없다'는 주제와 무관.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"occasion": "일으키다, 유발하다", "celebrate": "찬양하다", "analyze": "분석하다", "improve": "개선하다", "explain": "설명하다", "recall": "상기하다", "amusing": "재미있는", "helpful": "도움이 되는", "admirable": "감탄할 만한"}, "src": "verbal15 Q3"}, {"id": "v27_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that biologists who say egg production in birds is biologically highly costly would agree that clutch size is determined primarily by", "choices": ["the nutritional and energy demands of egg production", "the number of young that the parents can rear successfully", "reproductive limitations operating during chick rearing", "the availability of food for newly hatched chicks", "the differences between altricial and precocial species"], "columns": null, "pid": "v27_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'some theorizing that egg production is energetically or nutritionally demanding'.\n알 생산이 비용이 크다고 보는 학자들은 산란 수가 알 생산의 영양·에너지 부담으로 결정된다고 볼 것.\n정답: A", "trap": "B/C는 Lack의 견해(키울 수 있는 새끼 수, 양육 단계의 제약)로, 비용이 크다고 보는 학자들과 대립하는 입장.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"clutch size": "한 번에 낳는 알의 수", "altricial": "만성성(부모가 먹이는)", "precocial": "조성성(스스로 먹는)"}, "src": "verbal27 Q4"}, {"id": "v27_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that Lack would agree with which of the following statements about factors affecting clutch size in birds?", "choices": ["In altricial species, clutch size is determined primarily by factors operating after eggs are laid.", "In precocial species, clutch size is determined primarily by factors operating after eggs are laid.", "In many bird species, clutch size generally remains well below the potential limit of egg production."], "columns": null, "pid": "v27_p1", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: Lack은 산란 수가 '부모가 성공적으로 키울 수 있는 새끼 수'에 따라 진화했다고 봄 → 만성성 종은 알을 낳은 뒤(양육 단계)의 요인이 결정적.\nC: 'clutch size ... is far below the potential limit of egg production'.\nB: 조성성 종은 'availability of food for egg-laying females' 즉 알을 낳기 '전' 요인으로 설명될 수 있다고 봄 → 반대.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "B는 A와 형태가 같아 둘 다 고르기 쉬우나, Lack은 조성성 종에는 '다른 요인'(산란 암컷의 먹이)이 작용한다고 인정함.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"clutch size": "한배 산란 수", "altricial": "만성성의", "precocial": "조성성의", "potential limit": "잠재적 한계"}, "src": "verbal27 Q5"}, {"id": "v15_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "While the coauthors of the new guide to the American artistic experience have received accolades for their wide-ranging work, they do not _____ that the publication is exhaustive in content.", "choices": ["hope", "care", "assert", "insist", "doubt", "question"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: While — 폭넓은 작업으로 찬사를 받았지만, 그래도 저자들은 그 책이 내용상 완벽하다고 '주장하지는' 않는다(겸손).\n빈칸 = '주장하다'.\nassert와 insist가 짝.\n정답: C (assert), D (insist)", "trap": "doubt/question은 짝이지만 'do not doubt'가 되면 '완전하다고 확신한다'는 뜻이 되어 While의 양보 관계가 깨짐. hope는 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hope": "바라다", "care": "신경 쓰다, 원하다", "assert": "주장하다", "insist": "주장하다, 고집하다", "doubt": "의심하다", "question": "의문을 제기하다"}, "src": "verbal15 Q6"}, {"id": "v209_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The public memorial in Pretoria's Freedom Park presents _____ view of South Africa's history, with the names on it representing all those who died in conflicts that contributed to the shaping of the country.", "choices": ["an inclusive", "a comprehensive", "a definitive", "a coherent", "an empowering", "a conventional"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'with the names on it representing all those who died' → 모든 사망자를 망라함.\n빈칸 = '포괄적인, 모두를 아우르는'.\ninclusive와 comprehensive가 짝.\n정답: A (an inclusive), B (a comprehensive)", "trap": "definitive(결정적인)는 '완결된'이라는 느낌으로 끌리지만 '모두를 포함함'과 다르며 짝이 없음. coherent도 짝 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"an inclusive": "포괄적인, 모두를 아우르는", "a comprehensive": "종합적인, 포괄적인", "a definitive": "결정적인, 최종적인", "a coherent": "일관성 있는", "an empowering": "힘을 실어 주는", "a conventional": "관례적인"}, "src": "verbal209 Q7 · 25년 6월, 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v3_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The concept of the Hellenistic period in ancient history has proved useful but also _____, with scholars disagreeing on the dates when the period began and ended.", "choices": ["slippery", "elusive", "fruitless", "deceptive", "futile", "compelling"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: useful but also ___ → but으로 부정적 측면. 이유 'scholars disagreeing on the dates' → 시작·끝이 불분명.\n빈칸 = '규정하기 어려운, 붙잡기 힘든'.\nslippery와 elusive가 짝.\n정답: A (slippery), B (elusive)", "trap": "fruitless/futile(쓸모없는)은 짝이지만 앞의 'useful'과 모순. deceptive는 '오해를 부르는'이라 그럴듯하나 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"slippery": "파악하기 어려운, 애매한", "elusive": "규정하기 힘든, 잡히지 않는", "fruitless": "결실 없는", "deceptive": "기만적인, 현혹하는", "futile": "헛된", "compelling": "설득력 있는"}, "src": "verbal3 Q9"}, {"id": "v31_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Mark Messina’s book The Simple Soybean and Your Health exudes recognition much less unrestrained in the description of the soy's medical efficiency than its versatility, but the author’s cautions arrest soy to be a _____.", "choices": ["cure-all", "solitude", "efficacy", "effectuality", "panacea", "placebo"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문 문장이 원문에서 깨져 있지만 요지: 저자는 콩의 다양한 쓰임새에 비해 의학적 효능에 대해서는 훨씬 절제된 태도를 보이며, 그의 경고는 콩이 '만병통치약'이라는 생각을 막는다.\n빈칸 = 지나친 기대의 대상 = 만병통치약.\ncure-all과 panacea가 동의어 쌍.\n정답: A (cure-all), E (panacea)", "trap": "efficacy/effectuality는 '효능'으로 짝이지만 'a ___'로 콩 자체를 지칭하기 어렵고, 경고가 막는 대상은 과장된 만능 이미지임. placebo는 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cure-all": "만병통치약", "solitude": "고독", "efficacy": "효능", "effectuality": "효과, 유효성", "panacea": "만병통치약", "placebo": "위약"}, "src": "verbal31 Q7"}, {"id": "v231_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following does the author mention as an important condition thought by border identity theorists to support their view?", "choices": ["The persistence of ethnic loyalties despite globalization", "Populations that are very mobile on a global scale", "The renewed interest in national origins and ethnic heritage", "Tensions between ethnic groups within national boundaries", "Marginalization based on mobility between economic classes"], "columns": null, "pid": "v231_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: border identity theorists는 'individual identity is influenced by the various cultures with which one interacts, especially in a mobile global society'.\n→ 전 지구적으로 이동성이 큰 사회가 그들의 견해를 뒷받침하는 중요한 조건.\n정답: B", "trap": "A/C(민족적 충성심·출신 관심의 지속)는 오히려 국경 기반 정체성을 강조하는 쪽이라 이 이론가들과 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"arbitrariness": "자의성", "border identity": "경계 정체성", "mobile": "이동성 있는"}, "src": "verbal231 Q10 · 26/1, 25/11, 25/2, 24/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v231_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, Kingston and the border identity theorists would be most likely to disagree over which of the following?", "choices": ["The extent to which specific national origin plays a part in identity formation", "The extent to which individual identity determines economic status", "Whether or not cultural diversity plays a role in identity formation", "Whether or not the term \"American\" has any definable contemporary meaning", "Whether or not global mobility is becoming an economic necessity today"], "columns": null, "pid": "v231_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Kingston: 'acknowledges the importance of ethnicity (the national origins of one's ancestors ...)' + 'counters border theorists' emphasis on ... disconnection from specific countries'.\nBorder theorists: 'challenge the arbitrariness of ethnic identities based on national boundaries'.\n→ 특정 국가적 기원이 정체성 형성에 얼마나 작용하는가에서 의견이 갈림.\n정답: A", "trap": "C(문화적 다양성의 역할)는 양쪽 모두 인정하는 부분(Kingston도 다른 문화와의 상호 작용을 중시) — 불일치가 아니라 공통점.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"aside from": "~ 이외의", "Even so": "그렇다고 해도", "counter": "반박하다", "redefinition": "재정의"}, "src": "verbal231 Q11 · 26/1, 25/11, 25/2, 24/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v231_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the main purpose of the final sentence of the passage?", "choices": ["It demonstrates how Kingston's ideas contradict those of border identity theorists.", "It summarizes Kingston's views of the process of Chinese American identity formation.", "It raises objections to certain elements of Kingston's worldview.", "It further elucidates Kingston's understanding of American identity.", "It suggests an alternative interpretation of Kingston's ideas about the relationship between geography and identity."], "columns": null, "pid": "v231_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "마지막 문장: 'Even so, to belong to America in Kingston's world is not to have a set identity, but rather to have the opportunity to reconstruct identity through group interactions.'\n앞 문장에서 Kingston이 '소속감'을 강조한다고 했고, 마지막 문장은 그 소속이 고정된 정체성이 아니라 재구성의 기회라고 덧붙여 미국인 정체성에 대한 그녀의 생각을 더 명확히 함.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 '경계 이론가와 모순'을 보여준다고 하지만, 'Even so'로 시작하는 마지막 문장은 오히려 Kingston과 경계 이론가의 공통점(고정되지 않은 정체성)을 드러냄. B는 '요약'이라 범위 과다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Even so, to belong to America in Kingston's world is not to have a set identity, but rather to have the opportunity to reconstruct identity through group interactions.", "glosses": {"elucidate": "명료하게 설명하다", "reconstruct": "재구성하다", "set identity": "고정된 정체성"}, "src": "verbal231 Q12 · 26/1, 25/11, 25/2, 24/11 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v228_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The growth of kelp in the kelp bed communities of the North Pacific Ocean is _____ sea otters: the otters prey on kelp-eating sea urchins, keeping the urchin population in check.", "choices": ["impeded by", "detected by", "invisible to", "facilitated by", "disruptive for"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 콜론 뒤 설명 — 해달이 켈프를 먹는 성게를 잡아먹어 성게 개체 수를 억제함.\n→ 해달 덕분에 켈프 성장이 '촉진됨'.\n빈칸 = 긍정, '도움을 받는'.\n정답: D (facilitated by)", "trap": "impeded by(방해받는)는 '해달이 포식자'라는 점만 보고 고를 수 있으나, 해달이 먹는 것은 켈프가 아니라 성게임.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"impeded by": "~에 의해 방해받는", "detected by": "~에 의해 감지되는", "invisible to": "~에게 보이지 않는", "facilitated by": "~에 의해 촉진되는", "disruptive for": "~에 지장을 주는"}, "src": "verbal228 Q1 · 25/11, 25/6, 25/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v24_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Movies based on the lives of popular musicians constitute a durable genre in Hollywood, but also a fairly unambitious one. While there are very few that manage to be completely (i)__________, not many of them rise to the level of (ii)__________.", "choices": null, "columns": [["unwatchable", "stellar", "accurate"], ["difficulty", "greatness", "mediocrity"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 이 장르는 durable(오래가는)하지만 unambitious(야심이 없는) → 평범함.\nWhile 대조: 완전히 '형편없는' 것도 드물지만, '위대함'에 이르는 것도 많지 않다.\n(i) unwatchable, (ii) greatness → 양 극단을 모두 피한 '그저 그런' 장르.\n정답: A (unwatchable), E (greatness)", "trap": "(ii) mediocrity를 고르면 '평범함 수준에도 못 미친다'가 되어 unambitious(평범)라는 요지와 어긋남. (i) stellar를 고르면 두 절이 같은 말이 되어 While 대조가 사라짐.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unwatchable": "볼 수 없을 만큼 형편없는", "stellar": "뛰어난", "accurate": "정확한", "difficulty": "어려움", "greatness": "위대함", "mediocrity": "평범함, 범작"}, "src": "verbal24 Q3"}, {"id": "v220_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Among historians, conjecture and grand vision have given way to (i) _____, an intensified focus on ever smaller units of time and space, and a (ii) _____ to build analytical frames that can fully articulate the broad sweep of history.", "choices": null, "columns": [["abstraction", "specialization", "polemicism"], ["pervasive reluctance", "heedless scramble", "grudging willingness"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: conjecture and grand vision(추측과 거대한 비전)이 ~에 자리를 내줌 → 그 반대 경향.\n(i) 'an intensified focus on ever smaller units of time and space'와 나란히 → 세분화·전문화 = specialization.\n(ii) 역사 전체를 아우르는 분석틀을 만드는 것을 '꺼림' = pervasive reluctance(grand vision을 버렸으므로).\n정답: B (specialization), D (pervasive reluctance)", "trap": "(ii) grudging willingness는 '마지못해 하려 함'이라 큰 틀 구축을 여전히 시도한다는 뜻이 되어 grand vision의 퇴조와 모순. (i) abstraction은 오히려 grand vision에 가까움.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"abstraction": "추상화", "specialization": "전문화, 세분화", "polemicism": "논쟁적 태도", "pervasive reluctance": "만연한 꺼림", "heedless scramble": "무분별한 쟁탈", "grudging willingness": "마지못한 의향"}, "src": "verbal220 Q2 · 25/11, 25/10, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v208_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The latest encyclopedia (i) _____ the (ii) _____ made by many other books on how things work—giving (iii) _____ for every device, no matter how complicated—by taking just as long as is needed to explain things.", "choices": null, "columns": [["repeats", "exposes", "avoids"], ["assumption", "mistake", "compromise"], ["a brief historical background", "an equal number of words", "at least one illustration"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심: 마지막 'by taking just as long as is needed to explain things' → 필요한 만큼 길게 설명함.\n(iii) 다른 책들은 그 반대 = 아무리 복잡해도 모든 기기에 '같은 분량'을 할애 → an equal number of words.\n(ii) 지면 제약 때문에 분량을 똑같이 맞추는 타협 = compromise.\n(i) 이 백과사전은 그 타협을 '피한다' → avoids.\n정답: C (avoids), F (compromise), H (an equal number of words)", "trap": "(ii) mistake도 '다른 책들의 실수를 피한다'로 자연스러워 보여 가장 헷갈리지만, 균등 분량은 명백한 오류라기보다 공간과 설명의 균형을 맞춘 절충(타협)이라는 점에서 compromise가 정답 키. (i) exposes는 비판하는 것일 뿐, 'by taking ...'(방법)과 연결되지 않음.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"compromise": "타협, 절충", "repeats": "반복하다", "exposes": "폭로하다", "avoids": "피하다", "assumption": "가정", "mistake": "실수", "a brief historical background": "간단한 역사적 배경", "an equal number of words": "같은 분량의 단어", "at least one illustration": "최소 한 개의 삽화"}, "src": "verbal208 Q4 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following statements about the development of the piano can be inferred from the passage?", "choices": ["Pianos continued to be made by artisans well into the nineteenth century.", "The use of steam-powered tools in piano making led to a decline in tone quality.", "Prior to the Industrial Revolution, the framing in pianos was made entirely of wood."], "columns": null, "pid": "v240_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'Even long after factories had taken over the manufacture of other commodities' + 'fully handcrafted artwork in wood' → 다른 상품이 공장 생산으로 넘어간 뒤에도 피아노는 장인 수공 전통이 이어졌음을 추론 가능.\nB: 증기 동력 도구가 음질을 떨어뜨렸다는 언급 없음 — 음질 우려는 '철제 프레임'에 대한 것.\nC: 산업혁명 이전에 프레임이 '전적으로' 나무였다는 것은 지문이 말하지 않음.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 'ruin the tone'을 증기 도구에 잘못 연결한 함정. 지문은 증기 도구 사용과 철제 프레임을 'one thing ... quite another'로 명확히 구분함.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"commodity": "상품", "framing": "골격, 틀", "artisan": "장인", "vigorous": "격렬한"}, "src": "verbal240 Q5 · 25/8, 25/7, 25/3, 24/4, 23/9, 23/6, 23/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the context in which it appears, “tone” most exactly means", "choices": ["interval", "mood", "timbre", "pitch", "shade"], "columns": null, "pid": "v240_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'many feeling certain that iron in the piano would ruin the tone'.\n피아노 줄의 장력·소리 이야기 → 철이 망칠 수 있는 것은 소리의 '음색(질감)'.\ntimbre = 음색.\n정답: C (timbre)", "trap": "pitch(음 높이)도 소리 관련어지만, 철제 프레임 논쟁은 음의 높낮이가 아니라 소리의 질에 관한 것. mood/shade는 tone의 다른 의미(분위기, 색조)를 이용한 함정.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "tone", "glosses": {"timbre": "음색", "pitch": "음 높이", "interval": "음정", "shade": "색조, 미묘한 차이"}, "src": "verbal240 Q6 · 25/8, 25/7, 25/3, 24/4, 23/9, 23/6, 23/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v10_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage mentions \"Earth\" primarily in order to", "choices": ["stress the massive size of a hot Jupiter", "emphasize the proximity of a hot Jupiter to its parent star", "imply that hot Jupiters are unlikely to harbor extraterrestrial life", "point out differences between Earth and Jupiter with regard to their orbital distance from the Sun", "illustrate how hot Jupiters might fit into the standard theory of planetary formation"], "columns": null, "pid": "v10_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'orbits its parent star at a fraction of the distance at which Earth, let alone Jupiter, orbits the Sun'.\nlet alone(~는 말할 것도 없고) → 지구 궤도 거리보다도 훨씬 가깝다 → hot Jupiter가 모항성에 얼마나 가까운지 강조.\n정답: B", "trap": "D는 지구와 목성의 궤도 거리 차이를 말하지만, 그것은 목적이 아니라 강조를 위한 수단일 뿐. A는 질량 비교 대상이 목성이지 지구가 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Earth", "glosses": {"let alone": "~는 말할 것도 없고", "a fraction of": "~의 일부(극히 적은)", "parent star": "모항성"}, "src": "verbal10 Q5"}, {"id": "v10_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following elements is part of one but not both of the hypotheses discussed in the passage?", "choices": ["An interplay of gravitational forces", "A loss of orbital momentum", "A protoplanetary disk composed of dust and gas", "A protoplanetary disk divided into two regions", "The movement direction of hot Jupiters"], "columns": null, "pid": "v10_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "가설 1: 행성 중력이 원시행성 원반을 당김 → 상호 작용으로 궤도 운동량 상실 → 나선형으로 안쪽 이동.\n가설 2: 중력이 원반에 groove를 만들어 'partitioning it into inner and outer regions' → 운동량 상실 → 안쪽 이동.\n두 영역으로 나뉜 원반은 가설 2에만 있음.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(중력 상호 작용)는 가설 1에만 'interplay of forces'로 명시돼 끌리지만, 가설 2에도 'gravitational interactions'가 있어 둘 다 해당.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"protoplanetary disk": "원시행성 원반", "momentum": "운동량", "partition": "분할하다", "groove": "홈, 틈"}, "src": "verbal10 Q6"}, {"id": "v10_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that the \"attempts\" share which of the following goals?", "choices": ["to explain how a Jupiter-sized planet could form so close to its parent star", "to explain what prevents a hot Jupiter from colliding with its parent star", "to determine whether a hot Jupiter is formed from a protoplanetary disk of dust and gas", "to determine whether a hot Jupiter's gravitational field is strong enough to create a groove in its protoplanetary disk", "to account for hot Jupiters in a way that is not inconsistent with the standard theory of planetary formation"], "columns": null, "pid": "v10_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'In the standard ... theory ..., such a massive planet could not form so close to a star. So most attempts ... envision it forming farther away, then migrating inward.'\n→ 표준 이론과 충돌하지 않도록 '먼 곳에서 형성 후 이동'으로 설명하려는 것.\n정답: E", "trap": "A는 '그렇게 가까이에서 형성되는 방법'을 설명한다고 하지만, 시도들은 오히려 가까이서 형성되지 않았다고 봄 — 관계를 뒤집음. B는 지문 마지막의 '남은 질문'.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "attempts", "glosses": {"migrate": "이동하다", "envision": "상정하다, 구상하다", "inconsistent": "모순되는"}, "src": "verbal10 Q7"}, {"id": "v204_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "At their most _____, memoirs are about more than the story of someone' s life: they are about the function of memory itself, its narrative power to create and destroy, sweeten and obliterate the past in the service of the present.", "choices": ["perceptive", "polemical", "disputatious", "loquacious", "eloquent", "astute"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 콜론 뒤 — 최고의 회고록은 단순한 인생 이야기를 넘어 기억 자체의 기능과 서사적 힘까지 다룸.\n→ 깊은 통찰을 보여줄 때 = 빈칸은 '통찰력 있는'.\nperceptive와 astute가 짝.\n정답: A (perceptive), F (astute)", "trap": "eloquent(웅변적인)는 단독으로 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없고, 콜론 뒤는 표현력이 아니라 사유의 깊이를 설명함. polemical/disputatious는 짝이지만 '논쟁'과 무관.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"At their most": "가장 ~한 순간에", "perceptive": "통찰력 있는, 예리한", "astute": "기민한, 통찰력 있는", "polemical": "논쟁적인", "disputatious": "논쟁을 좋아하는", "loquacious": "말이 많은", "eloquent": "웅변적인, 유창한"}, "src": "verbal204 Q11 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v12_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although Duke Ellington's musicians owed their fame to him, they also recognized his debt to them; as such, many _____ the fact that their improvisations became subsumed into the Ellingtonian canon unacknowledged.", "choices": ["overlooked", "resented", "lamented", "disregarded", "begrudged", "denied"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 음악가들은 자기들 명성이 Ellington 덕분이지만, 동시에 Ellington도 자신들에게 빚졌다고 인식함 → as such(그러므로).\n→ 자신들의 즉흥 연주가 인정받지 못한 채(unacknowledged) Ellington 작품에 흡수된 것을 '분하게 여겼다'.\n빈칸 = 부정적 감정, '원망하다'.\nresented와 begrudged가 짝.\n정답: B (resented), E (begrudged)", "trap": "lamented(한탄했다)도 부정적 감정이라 끌리지만 '빚을 인식함 → 억울함'의 감정과 결이 다르고 짝이 없음. overlooked/disregarded는 짝이지만 '빚을 인식했다'와 모순.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unacknowledged": "인정받지못한채", "resented": "분개했다", "begrudged": "못마땅해했다, 시기했다", "overlooked": "간과했다", "lamented": "한탄했다", "disregarded": "무시했다", "denied": "부인했다"}, "src": "verbal12 Q10"}, {"id": "v32_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The recent exhibition on Dadaism is nothing if not _____, for the visual arts are currently awash in Dadaist gestures and gambits of one variety or another.", "choices": ["sensational", "timely", "daunting", "ill-advised", "opportune", "misguided"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'nothing if not ___' = 무엇보다도 ~하다(매우 ~하다). for 이하 이유: 현재 시각 예술계에 다다이즘적 제스처가 넘쳐남.\n→ 다다이즘 전시는 시의적절하다.\ntimely와 opportune이 짝.\n정답: B (timely), E (opportune)", "trap": "ill-advised/misguided는 짝이지만 '지금 다다이즘이 넘쳐난다'는 이유와 맞지 않음. sensational은 단독으로 그럴듯하나 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sensational": "선풍적인, 선정적인", "timely": "시기적절한", "daunting": "벅찬, 위압적인", "ill-advised": "현명하지 못한", "opportune": "시의적절한", "misguided": "잘못 판단한"}, "src": "verbal32 Q8"}, {"id": "v16_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is an assumption on which the argument depends?", "choices": ["Whooping cough is more difficult to diagnose in adults than in children.", "Adults with whooping cough do not readily transmit the disease to children.", "Most adults who contract whooping cough get the disease from children with whom they are in close contact.", "A disease poses no significant public health threat unless it is life-threatening.", "Under comparable conditions of exposure, adults contract whooping cough more readily than do children."], "columns": null, "pid": "v16_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 성인의 백일해 발병은 공중 보건에 중대한 위협이 아니다.\n근거: 성인에게는 기침 정도로 심각하지 않다(아이에게는 생명을 위협함).\n숨은 가정: 성인 환자가 아이에게 병을 쉽게 옮기지 않는다 — 만약 쉽게 옮긴다면 성인 감염은 아이를 통해 심각한 위협이 됨.\n부정 테스트: B를 부정하면 결론이 무너짐.\n정답: B", "trap": "D는 '생명을 위협하지 않으면 공중 보건 위협이 아니다'로 그럴듯하지만 너무 강한 일반화 — 논증은 이 정도의 절대적 원칙까지 필요로 하지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incidence": "발생률", "persistent": "지속적인", "transmit": "전염시키다", "contract": "(병에) 걸리다"}, "src": "verbal16 Q11"}, {"id": "v30_q12", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage indicates that Peterson identifies which of the following as obstacles faced by the women included in her study?", "choices": ["The attitudes of Black male intellectuals toward female intellectual work", "The discriminatory attitudes faced by Black women in nineteenth-century America as a whole", "Disagreements among Black women speakers and writers themselves about the impact of the Black intelligentsia"], "columns": null, "pid": "v30_p3", "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Peterson은 여성들이 'fundamentally estranged from the nation by a dominant culture unsympathetic to Black women, and by a Black intelligentsia whose male view of race concerns left little room for Black female intellect'라고 봄.\nA = 흑인 남성 지식인들의 태도, B = 19세기 미국 주류 문화의 차별적 태도 → 둘 다 장애물.\nC: 흑인 여성들 사이의 의견 불일치는 언급 없음.\n정답: A, B", "trap": "C는 'Black intelligentsia'라는 지문 단어를 재활용했지만, 여성들 내부의 '불일치'는 지문에 없는 내용.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"estranged": "소외된", "intelligentsia": "지식인 계층", "polity": "정치 공동체", "unsympathetic": "냉담한, 공감하지 않는"}, "src": "verbal30 Q12"}, {"id": "v30_q13", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that Peterson’s study and Foster’s study are similar with respect to which of the following?", "choices": ["the writers that each takes up for examination", "the degree to which each has influenced other scholars", "the assumptions that each brings to nineteenth-century African American literature", "their analysis of the nineteenth-century Black intelligentsia", "their interpretation of nineteenth-century America’s dominant culture"], "columns": null, "pid": "v30_p3", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Its scope resembles that of Frances Smith Foster's 1993 study, but its approach is quite different.'\n범위(scope)가 비슷 = 다루는 대상(1830-1880 흑인 여성 연사·작가)이 같음 → 다루는 작가들이 유사.\n정답: A", "trap": "C/E는 접근 방식·해석에 관한 것으로, 지문은 바로 이 점에서 두 연구가 'quite different'하다고 말함.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"scope": "범위", "approach": "접근 방식", "enlightened": "계몽된"}, "src": "verbal30 Q13"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.8 / S2 2.8"}, {"set": 23, "sections": [[{"id": "v29_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Although Emily Bronte is impassioned about gender equality, she is anything but _____ to endorse more privileges endowed to women.", "choices": ["zealous", "apathetic", "abhorrent", "stubborn", "lethargic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although(대조) 신호: 앞절 '양성평등에 열정적(impassioned)'과 뒷절이 반대 방향이어야 함.\nanything but ___ = 결코 ~하지 않다 → 빈칸에는 '열정적으로 지지하는'이 들어가야 '여성 특권 확대를 지지하는 데는 전혀 열성적이지 않다'가 됨.\n빈칸 = 긍정(열심인, 열성적인) 뜻.\nzealous(열성적인)가 정확히 맞음. 평등은 원하지만 '특권'은 원하지 않는다는 구분.\n정답: A (zealous)", "trap": "apathetic/lethargic(무관심한, 무기력한)는 anything but과 결합하면 '매우 열심'이 되어 Although의 대조가 사라짐.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"impassioned": "열정적인", "anything but": "결코 ~않는", "zealous": "열성적인", "apathetic": "무관심한", "abhorrent": "혐오스러운", "stubborn": "고집 센", "lethargic": "무기력한"}, "src": "verbal29 Q1"}, {"id": "v203_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Biologist Catherine Graham, studying toucans in Mexico, predicted that because toucans prefer relatively large forest patches and feed on fruit, they would fly more often to (i) _____ patches and to patches with abundant fruit resources than to small patches or those that had (ii) _____ fruit resources.", "choices": null, "columns": [["sizable", "nearby", "dense"], ["dislocated", "unusual", "scant"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "병렬 구조: 'relatively large forest patches'를 선호 + 'feed on fruit'.\n(i) small patches와 대비 → 큰 패치 = sizable.\n(ii) 'abundant fruit resources'와 대비 → 열매가 적은 = scant.\n정답: A (sizable), F (scant)", "trap": "nearby/dense는 '크기'와 무관, dislocated/unusual은 abundant의 반대가 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sizable": "상당히 큰", "nearby": "근처의", "dense": "빽빽한", "dislocated": "제자리를 벗어난", "unusual": "특이한", "scant": "부족한, 빈약한"}, "src": "verbal203 Q2 · 25년 10월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v9_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Although the (i) _____ and the not infrequent appearance of terms like synaptogenesis and N-methyl-D-aspartate glutamate receptor can be (ii) _____ in a book aimed at the general reader, Konner's overall style is (iii) _____ enough that you feel as though you are in the company of a helpful and hopeful teacher who is eager to share what he's found.", "choices": null, "columns": [["occasional glimpses of humor", "deft deployment of examples", "repeated use of jargon"], ["placating", "galvanizing", "daunting"], ["disputatious", "conversational", "baroque"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'and the not infrequent appearance of terms like synaptogenesis...'와 병렬 → 어려운 전문용어 계열 = repeated use of jargon.\n(ii) 일반 독자용 책에서 전문용어는 부담스러움 → daunting(위압적인).\n(iii) Although 대조 + 'in the company of a helpful teacher' → 친근하고 대화체 = conversational.\n정답: C (repeated use of jargon), F (daunting), H (conversational)", "trap": "(ii) galvanizing(활기를 주는)은 긍정이라 Although 대조가 깨짐. (iii) baroque/disputatious는 '친절한 선생님' 느낌과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"galvanizing": "활기를 불어넣는", "baroque": "지나치게 화려한", "occasional glimpses of humor": "가끔 보이는 유머", "deft deployment of examples": "능숙한 예시 활용", "repeated use of jargon": "전문용어의 반복 사용", "placating": "달래는", "daunting": "위압적인, 벅찬", "disputatious": "논쟁적인", "conversational": "대화체의, 친근한"}, "src": "verbal9 Q3"}, {"id": "v199_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that one factor that has made it difficult to account for the temperatures once reached by asteroids is", "choices": ["a miscalculation of the frequency of asteroid collisions", "a misconception about asteroids’ density", "a mistaken assumption about what the heat source of the asteroids was", "an underestimation of the rate at which small bodies lose heat", "an erroneous view of how asteroids were formed"], "columns": null, "pid": "v199_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'these objections assumed that asteroids are dense, solid bodies. A recent discovery that asteroids are highly porous...'\n회의론자들이 '밀도 높은 고체'라고 잘못 가정해서 충돌로 인한 가열 설명(Rubin)이 그럴듯해 보이지 않았음.\n→ 고온을 설명하기 어렵게 만든 요인 = 밀도에 대한 오해.\n정답: B", "trap": "C: 열원이 '알려지지 않았다(unknown)'고 했을 뿐 잘못 가정했다는 말은 없음. D: 작은 천체가 빨리 식는다는 건 사실로 제시됨.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"porous": "구멍이 많은, 다공성의", "dissipate": "흩뜨리다, 소산시키다", "plausible": "그럴듯한"}, "src": "verbal199 Q4 · 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v199_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that Rubin disagrees with skeptics mentioned in the passage about which of the following?", "choices": ["Whether porous bodies generate less debris when struck than do solid bodies", "The temperatures asteroids would have to reach for their rocks to have melted", "The likely effect of impacts on asteroids’ temperatures"], "columns": null, "pid": "v199_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Rubin: 충돌이 소행성의 열원일 수 있다.\nSkeptics: 'a single impact would raise an asteroid's overall temperature very little' → 충돌의 온도 효과에 대해 의견 불일치.\nA: 다공성 천체의 파편 감소는 최근 발견으로 소개된 것이지 둘의 논쟁점이 아님. B: 녹는 온도 자체는 언급 없음.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 지문에 나오는 내용이라 고르기 쉽지만, 회의론자가 이에 반대했다는 근거가 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"skeptic": "회의론자", "debris": "파편, 잔해", "insulating": "단열하는"}, "src": "verbal199 Q5 · 24년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v235_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Astute and incisive, the essayist's work was nevertheless civil and polite: the essayist either had no gift of _____ or else never felt any.", "choices": ["vitriol", "clairvoyance", "theatricality", "prescience", "mimicry", "obloquy"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'Astute and incisive'(날카로움)인데 nevertheless 'civil and polite' → 날카롭지만 공격적이지 않았다.\n'had no gift of ___ or else never felt any' → 빈칸 = 신랄한 비난, 독설(정중함의 반대).\nvitriol(독설)과 obloquy(비난, 욕설)가 같은 뜻.\n정답: A (vitriol), F (obloquy)", "trap": "clairvoyance/prescience(예지력)도 짝이 되지만 'civil and polite'와 대비되지 않고 'never felt any'와도 안 맞음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"vitriol": "독설, 신랄한 비판", "clairvoyance": "투시력, 통찰력", "prescience": "예지력, 선견지명", "obloquy": "비난, 악평", "theatricality": "연극조, 과장됨", "mimicry": "흉내"}, "src": "verbal235 Q8 · 25/12, 25/9, 25/5, 25/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v231_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Those familiar with the insular conditions that once prevailed in Russia may be surprised by the _____ of eighteenth-century Russian composer Natalia Kurakina, who translated novels from French into Italian and composed songs in both languages.", "choices": ["versatility", "worldliness", "dedication", "ingenuity", "cosmopolitanism", "industriousness"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'insular conditions'(폐쇄적·고립된 환경)을 아는 사람들이 'be surprised by' → 빈칸은 insular의 반대.\n근거: 프랑스어→이탈리아어 번역, 두 언어로 작곡 → 국제적 감각.\nworldliness(세상 물정에 밝음, 세련됨)와 cosmopolitanism(세계주의적 교양)이 짝.\n정답: B (worldliness), E (cosmopolitanism)", "trap": "versatility(다재다능)는 혼자 그럴듯하지만 insular와의 대비가 없고 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"versatility": "다재다능함", "worldliness": "세상 물정에 밝음, 세련됨", "dedication": "헌신", "ingenuity": "독창성, 재주", "cosmopolitanism": "세계주의, 국제적 교양", "industriousness": "근면함"}, "src": "verbal231 Q9 · 25년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v13_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Despite the rather _____ conditions required for its preservation, the evidence for glaciation during the late Proterozoic is found on every continent, suggesting that ice sheets were present throughout the globe.", "choices": ["unusual", "hostile", "drastic", "stringent", "exacting", "complex"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Despite(대조): 보존 조건이 까다로운데도 증거가 모든 대륙에서 발견됨.\n빈칸 = '보존되기 어려운, 엄격한' 조건.\nstringent와 exacting(엄격한, 까다로운)이 짝.\n정답: D (stringent), E (exacting)", "trap": "unusual/complex도 혼자는 그럴듯하지만 서로 동의어가 아님. hostile은 조건이 '적대적'이라 보존과 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unusual": "특이한", "hostile": "적대적인", "drastic": "극단적인, 과감한", "stringent": "엄격한", "exacting": "까다로운, 엄한", "complex": "복잡한"}, "src": "verbal13 Q8"}, {"id": "v203_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The rate of sediment deposition may be _____ desertification in Central Asia: data from a Tajik site show the rate to have increased during Pleistocene glacial periods as aridity increased.", "choices": ["a restraint on", "a gauge of", "an indicator of", "a factor in", "a hedge against", "a consequence of"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 건조함(aridity)이 증가할 때 퇴적률도 증가 → 퇴적률은 사막화를 '나타내는' 지표.\n상관관계만 제시되어 인과 방향은 언급 없음 → '측정 지표'가 가장 안전.\na gauge of와 an indicator of가 짝.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "a consequence of / a factor in은 인과 방향이 서로 반대라 짝이 안 됨. a restraint on / a hedge against는 방향 자체가 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"a hedge against": "~에 대한 방어수단", "a restraint on": "~에 대한 억제", "a gauge of": "~의 척도", "an indicator of": "~의 지표", "a factor in": "~의 요인", "a consequence of": "~의 결과"}, "src": "verbal203 Q9 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v235_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage would most likely agree with which of the following statements regarding the effect of marketing gender-differentiated furniture?", "choices": ["It introduced new ideas of femininity and masculinity to consumers.", "It was more successful than was the marketing of age-differentiated furniture.", "It undermined conventional ideas of masculine importance.", "It contributed to an increase in custom-designed furniture.", "It promulgated a limited definition of femininity."], "columns": null, "pid": "v235_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 마지막 부분 'conventional ideas of masculine importance and feminine delicacy were amplified and fixed. In the process, femininity was expressed in a specific and narrowly defined aesthetic register.'\n'narrowly defined' = limited definition → E가 정확한 패러프레이즈.\n정답: E", "trap": "A: 새로운 관념을 '도입'한 것이 아니라 기존(conventional) 관념을 증폭·고정함. C: 남성의 중요성을 약화시킨 것이 아니라 강화함.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"promulgate": "널리 퍼뜨리다", "amplify": "증폭시키다", "register": "(표현의) 범위, 영역"}, "src": "verbal235 Q10 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v235_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true about furniture prior to the 1760s?", "choices": ["Some furniture made specifically for women already existed.", "Most furniture design was already influenced by women's preferences.", "Custom-designed furniture was small.", "The range of available furniture was small.", "Advertising had rarely been used to generate consumer demand for furniture."], "columns": null, "pid": "v235_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the idea of furniture suited to female needs is not unprecedented (think of birthing stools)'.\n1760년대 카탈로그 이전에도 여성용 가구(출산 의자)가 있었음 → A.\n정답: A", "trap": "D: 가구 '범위'가 작았다는 말은 없음(범위의 확장을 언급할 뿐). B: '대부분'의 디자인이 여성 선호의 영향을 받았다는 건 과장.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unprecedented": "전례 없는", "birthing stool": "출산용 의자", "diffusion": "확산"}, "src": "verbal235 Q11 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v235_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following statements best describes the function of the highlighted sentence in the context of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["It mitigates a claim that was presented in the first sentence of the passage.", "It interprets an example that was introduced in the first sentence of the passage.", "It provides historical context for the phenomenon that is analyzed in the remainder of the passage.", "It introduces a distinction between two historical approaches that the remainder of the passage elaborates on.", "It gives an overview of a historical development that the rest of the passage explores in more detail."], "columns": null, "pid": "v235_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 여성 수요를 상정한 마케팅이 획기적인 변화였다(전체 주제 = 역사적 전개).\n강조 문장: 1600년대 서적상부터 1770년 잡지까지 그 전개의 초기 흐름을 시대순으로 훑음(overview).\n이후: 'The leap to objects...' 가구로의 확장과 그 효과(성 고정관념 강화)를 자세히 다룸 → 같은 전개를 더 깊이 탐구.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(역사적 배경 제공)가 가장 헷갈림. 하지만 강조 문장은 '배경'이 아니라 첫 문장이 말한 현상 자체의 개척자들(pioneers)을 보여주는 일부임. A/B: 첫 문장의 주장을 완화하거나 예시를 해석하지 않음.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"an overview of a historical development": "역사적 전개의 개요", "mitigate": "완화하다", "pioneer": "개척자", "proliferation": "급증, 확산"}, "src": "verbal235 Q12 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v240_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The depletion of soil and trees in southern West Virginia has resulted in frequent flash floods, since when the mountain slopes are _____, storms cause torrents of water to pour down them unimpeded.", "choices": ["riven", "fecund", "denuded", "withered", "mutable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "원인 신호 since: 흙과 나무가 고갈(depletion) → 홍수.\n빈칸 = 산비탈이 '헐벗은' 상태여서 물이 막힘없이(unimpeded) 흘러내림.\ndenuded(벌거벗겨진, 덮개가 제거된)가 정확.\n정답: C (denuded)", "trap": "withered(시든)는 나무가 시든 것일 뿐 흙·나무가 '없어진' 상태가 아님. riven(갈라진)도 흙 고갈과 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unimpeded": "막힘없이", "denuded": "벌거벗겨진, 제거된", "riven": "갈라진, 찢긴", "fecund": "비옥한, 다산의", "withered": "시든", "mutable": "변하기 쉬운"}, "src": "verbal240 Q1 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v22_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Historians have been (i)__________ African American fraternal organizations, in part due to the (ii)__________ historical evidence: the relevant records are scarce and difficult to obtain.", "choices": null, "columns": [["hindered in studying", "confident in assessing", "eager to categorize"], ["discrepancies in", "insufficiency of", "approach to"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 'records are scarce and difficult to obtain' → 자료 부족.\n(ii) scarce = insufficiency of(부족).\n(i) 자료가 부족하니 연구에 방해를 받음 = hindered in studying.\n정답: A (hindered in studying), E (insufficiency of)", "trap": "(ii) discrepancies in(불일치)은 '부족하다'와 다른 문제. (i) confident/eager는 긍정이라 자료 부족과 모순.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hindered in studying": "연구에 방해를 받은", "confident in assessing": "평가에 자신 있는", "eager to categorize": "분류하고 싶어하는", "discrepancies in": "~의 불일치", "insufficiency of": "~의 부족", "approach to": "~에 대한 접근법"}, "src": "verbal22 Q2"}, {"id": "v28_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The (i) _____ current-generation solar cells are (ii) _____: although experimental cells have reached efficiencies greater than 40 percent, most commercially available cells in the early part of the twenty-first century still struggle to get past about 20 percent.", "choices": null, "columns": [["attractions of", "limitations of", "improvements in"], ["clear", "unmatched", "misunderstood"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 실험용 셀은 40% 이상인데 상용 셀은 20%를 넘기 힘들다 → 한계가 뚜렷함.\n(i) limitations of(한계).\n(ii) 콜론 뒤에서 수치로 분명히 보여줌 → clear(명확한).\n정답: B (limitations of), D (clear)", "trap": "(ii) misunderstood는 오해받고 있다는 근거 없음. (i) attractions/improvements는 '20% 넘기 힘들다'와 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"attractions of": "~의 매력", "limitations of": "~의 한계", "improvements in": "~의 향상", "clear": "분명한", "unmatched": "필적할 것이 없는", "misunderstood": "오해받는"}, "src": "verbal28 Q2"}, {"id": "v204_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Filler claims that after the social welfare programs of the 1960s, belief that the government has an obligation to provide decent housing for citizens who cannot afford it was (i) _____ in the United States by the notion that providing suitable shelter for everyone should be (ii) _____. Thus, today in the (iii) _____ of taxpayer-sponsored initiatives, we have volunteer home-construction programs, honorable in intent but pitifully limited in scope.", "choices": null, "columns": [["supplanted", "promulgated", "corroborated"], ["a shared civic responsibility", "an act of private charity", "a profit-oriented enterprise"], ["absence", "name", "mold"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AEG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 정부의 의무라는 믿음이 다른 생각에 의해 '대체'됨 → supplanted.\n(ii) 결과: 'volunteer home-construction programs' → 민간 자선 행위 = an act of private charity.\n(iii) 납세자 지원 사업이 '없는' 상황에서 자원봉사 프로그램 → in the absence of.\n정답: A (supplanted), E (an act of private charity), G (absence)", "trap": "(ii) a shared civic responsibility도 그럴듯하지만 '자원봉사'와 정부 의무의 대체를 정확히 설명하지 못함. (iii) in the name of(~라는 명목으로)는 의미가 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"supplanted": "대체된", "promulgated": "공표된, 널리 알려진", "corroborated": "확증된", "a shared civic responsibility": "공동의 시민적 책임", "an act of private charity": "민간 자선 행위", "a profit-oriented enterprise": "영리 사업", "absence": "부재(in the absence of: ~이 없는 상황에서)", "name": "이름(in the name of: ~의 명목으로)", "mold": "틀(in the mold of: ~의 유형으로)"}, "src": "verbal204 Q4 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v236_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred from the passage regarding the period in which Bulosan immigrated to the United States?", "choices": ["Legal restrictions on Filipinos who wished to immigrate to the United States were tighter then than they have been since 1965.", "Filipinos generally had different reasons for immigrating to the United States then than they have had since 1965.", "Relatively few of the Filipinos who immigrated to the United States then were women.", "No one was then working to factually document the lives of Filipino immigrants in the United States.", "During that period, the movement to advance civil rights for Filipino Americans attempted to ease legal restrictions on immigration."], "columns": null, "pid": "v236_p4", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Filipino American women, who were scarce among immigrants before the 1934 American curb' + Bulosan은 'a member of the first substantial wave of immigrants'(1934 이전).\n→ Bulosan 시기 이민자 중 여성은 적었다 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "D: Bulosan 자신이 'personal testimony'로 삶을 기록했으므로 '아무도 기록하지 않았다'는 극단적이고 틀림. A: 1934년의 제한은 Bulosan 이민 '이후'에 생김.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hiatus": "공백, 중단", "curb": "제한, 억제", "liberalization": "자유화"}, "src": "verbal236 Q14 · 24년 2월, 23년 9월 중국후기", "note": "원본 답안표가 회차마다 달랐던 문항입니다(C / D). 지문 근거로 C를 정답으로 확정했습니다. Conflicting keys C/D resolved to C: passage says women were scarce among pre-1934 immigrants (Bulosan's wave); D is unsupported/contradicted since Bulosan himself documented immigrant life."}, {"id": "v236_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "Regarding Espiritu's work, the passage implies which of the following?", "choices": ["Her work attempts to give expression to the experiences of a number of Filipino Americans.", "Her work documents how some people's lives were affected by the 1965 liberalization of immigration.", "Her work represents the experiences of Filipino women in the United States more than does Bulosan's."], "columns": null, "pid": "v236_p4", "answer": "ABC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'recovering life histories of Filipino Americans' → 경험을 표현하려 함.\nB: 'generation following the 1934-1965 immigration hiatus' + 1965 자유화 이후 이민자 → 1965 자유화가 삶에 미친 영향 기록.\nC: 'A special strength is the representation of Filipino American women' + Bulosan 시기엔 여성이 적었음 → Bulosan보다 여성 경험을 더 많이 다룸.\n정답: A, B, C", "trap": "C를 빼기 쉬움: 직접 비교 문장은 없지만 '특별한 강점'과 Bulosan 시대 여성 희소성을 결합하면 추론 가능.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"has set herself the task": "그녀 스스로를 과제로 삼았다", "hiatus": "공백", "testimony": "증언", "graphically": "생생하게"}, "src": "verbal236 Q15 · 24년 2월, 23년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions “Medea” primarily in order to", "choices": ["give an example of a play in which references to certain authors can be used to determine when the Marci Lucii Annei Senecae Tragoediae were composed", "acknowledge the possibility that the Marci Lucii Annei Senecae Tragoediae may have been written by Quintilian rather than Seneca", "suggest that certain of the Marci Lucii Annei Senecae Tragoediae may have been written near the end of Seneca's lifetime", "argue that Marci may have been one of the last of the eight plays in the Marci Lucii Annei Senecae Tragoediae to be written", "indicate how the latest possible date for the time period during which the Marci Lucii Annei Senecae Tragordiae were composed might be established"], "columns": null, "pid": "v234_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the plays must have been written by 96 C.E., when Quintilian quotes Medea'.\nQuintilian이 Medea를 인용한 시점 → 작품이 그 이전에 쓰였어야 함 → 작성 시기의 가장 늦은 한계 시점(terminus ante quem)을 정함.\n정답: E", "trap": "A: 다른 작가(Ovid)에 대한 언급은 '가장 이른 날짜'를 정하는 근거이지 Medea의 역할이 아님. C: Seneca 말년에 쓰였다는 주장은 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Medea", "glosses": {"extant": "현존하는", "terminus": "한계 시점", "prudence": "신중함"}, "src": "verbal234 Q7 · 25/6, 24/10, 22/4 중국후기", "note": "원본 답안표가 회차마다 달랐던 문항입니다(C / E). 지문 근거로 E를 정답으로 확정했습니다. Conflicting keys C/E resolved to E: Medea is cited because Quintilian's quotation of it in 96 C.E. sets the latest possible composition date; nothing suggests late-life composition (C)."}, {"id": "v234_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage makes which of the following claims about the eight extant Latin tragedies?", "choices": ["There is only circumstantial evidence that the plays were all written by the same author.", "Scholars have persistently attributed the plays to Seneca despite evidence that some of them may have been composed prior to his lifetime.", "Evidence in the manuscripts of the plays identifies them as having been written by Lucius Annaeus Seneca the Younger.", "The plays contain some lines that have been construed as being directed against the emperor.", "The plays contain material that could illustrate certain aspects of Seneca’s philosophy."], "columns": null, "pid": "v234_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'there are certainly passages in them that could be used to illustrate points of his philosophy'.\nE가 거의 그대로 패러프레이즈.\n정답: E", "trap": "A: 'circumstantial'은 Seneca가 작가라는 증거에 대한 말이지 '모두 같은 작가'에 대한 말이 아님. D: 반황제 대사로 처벌받은 건 일반 극작가 이야기이지 이 작품들에 그런 대사가 있다는 주장은 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"circumstantial": "정황적인", "construe": "해석하다", "extant": "현존하는"}, "src": "verbal234 Q8 · 25/6, 24/10, 22/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v234_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage would most likely agree that if Seneca had in fact written the tragedies, then Seneca probably would have", "choices": ["used the plays as platforms for his philosophical ideas", "referred to the plays in some of his other writings", "been in danger of exile or execution for certain line in the plays", "avoided attaching his name to be the plays out of modesty", "written the plays during the latter portion of his lifetime"], "columns": null, "pid": "v234_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "저자는 Herrmann의 '겸손' 설명을 반박: 'Seneca is not averse to referring to his other writings'.\n→ 정말 Seneca가 썼다면 다른 글에서 이 극들을 언급했을 것이라고 저자는 생각함.\n정답: B", "trap": "D: 겸손해서 이름을 붙이지 않았다는 건 Herrmann의 견해이고 저자는 이를 반박함. C: 저자는 황제의 스승이라 안전했을 것이라 봄.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"averse": "싫어하는, 꺼리는", "prudence": "신중함", "modesty": "겸손"}, "src": "verbal234 Q9 · 25/6, 24/10, 22/4 중국후기", "note": "원본 답안표가 회차마다 달랐던 문항입니다(B / D). 지문 근거로 B를 정답으로 확정했습니다. Conflicting keys B/D resolved to B: the author rejects the modesty explanation (D is Herrmann's view) by noting Seneca readily refers to his other writings."}, {"id": "v2_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "If satellite images predicting outbreaks of Rift Valley fever in the Horn of Africa were to lead to vaccination campaigns five months in advance, monitoring of such images could potentially _____ epidemics of both livestock and people.", "choices": ["avert", "initiate", "anticipate", "obliterate", "forecast", "forestall"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "조건문: 위성 이미지가 5개월 전 '예방접종 캠페인'으로 이어진다면 → 전염병을 '막을' 수 있다.\n빈칸 = 예방하다, 미연에 방지하다.\navert와 forestall이 짝.\n정답: A (avert), F (forestall)", "trap": "anticipate/forecast도 짝이지만, 예측은 이미 이미지가 하고 있는 일(predicting)이고 '예방접종'이 추가되는 의미(예방)를 반영하지 못함.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"obliterate": "완전히 없애다, 지우다", "avert": "피하다, 막다", "initiate": "시작하다", "anticipate": "예상하다", "forecast": "예측하다", "forestall": "미연에 방지하다"}, "src": "verbal2 Q9"}, {"id": "v226_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Azarenka's descriptions are not _____: they grow organically from the themes that animate her writing.", "choices": ["derivative", "gratuitous", "sophomoric", "original", "arbitrary", "novel"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 'they grow organically from the themes' → 묘사가 주제에서 자연스럽게 나옴.\n그러니 묘사는 '불필요하거나 제멋대로'인 것이 아님 → 빈칸 = 근거 없는, 불필요한.\ngratuitous와 arbitrary가 짝.\n정답: B (gratuitous), E (arbitrary)", "trap": "original/novel은 짝이지만 '독창적이지 않다'는 콜론 뒤 내용과 연결되지 않음. derivative는 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"gratuitous": "불필요한, 이유 없는", "sophomoric": "미숙한, 유치한", "derivative": "모방한, 독창성 없는", "original": "독창적인", "arbitrary": "임의적인, 제멋대로인", "novel": "새로운"}, "src": "verbal226 Q11 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v238_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Sea turtles' grazing on sea grass is less _____ near Bermuda than elsewhere: Bermuda protects sea turtles as an endangered species but does not protect their predators, tiger sharks.", "choices": ["consistent", "pervasive", "inhibited", "destructive", "damaging", "constrained"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 버뮤다는 바다거북은 보호하지만 포식자(뱀상어)는 보호하지 않음 → 상어 감소 + 거북 보호.\n→ 거북의 먹이활동이 덜 '제약받음'.\ninhibited와 constrained가 짝.\n정답: C (inhibited), F (constrained)", "trap": "destructive/damaging도 짝이지만 방향이 반대: 포식 압력이 줄면 거북의 해초 피해는 오히려 더 커짐.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"consistent": "일관된", "pervasive": "만연한", "inhibited": "억제된", "destructive": "파괴적인", "damaging": "해로운", "constrained": "제약받는"}, "src": "verbal238 Q10 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v34_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following most logically completes the passage?", "choices": ["experts who knew the results of the pigment analyses reexamined these paintings and found no previously unnoticed stylistic similarities between the Altamira paintings and the paintings in the third group", "there are certain stylistic features that the Altamira paintings share with all known paintings of their period and do not share with the El Castillo paintings", "before dating by pigment analysis was widely practiced, stylistic similarities were the only means of determining whether two prehistoric cave paintings dated from the same period", "determining the age of a prehistoric cave painting simply by reference to the age of the pigments used in that painting substitutes technology for artistic judgment", "there are experts who maintain that the results of the recent pigment analyses leave the striking stylistic similarities between the El Castillo paintings and the Altamira paintings unexplained"], "columns": null, "pid": "v34_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 이 사례가 '양식 유사성은 연대의 지표가 될 수 없다'를 증명하지는 않는다.\n필요한 것: 양식으로도 올바른 연대를 알아낼 수 있었다는 근거.\nB: Altamira 그림은 같은 시대 모든 그림과 공유하고 El Castillo와는 공유하지 않는 양식 특징이 있음 → 더 세밀한 양식 분석이었다면 정확히 연대를 맞혔을 것.\n정답: B", "trap": "E: 유사성이 설명되지 않는다는 전문가 의견은 양식의 신뢰성을 지지하지 못함. A: 오히려 양식이 연대 지표로 실패했다는 쪽을 지지.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pigment": "안료", "reliable": "신뢰할 수 있는", "indicator": "지표"}, "src": "verbal34 Q11"}, {"id": "v216_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about grasshoppers?", "choices": ["In the absence of certain predators, they are more likely to eat Kentucky bluegrass than to eat goldenrod.", "When many predators are present, they typically eat only the most nutritious plants available.", "When their population density is reduced, they tend to eat less nutritious plants.", "They are the preferred prey of nursery-web spiders.", "They prefer to eat plants located near ground level."], "columns": null, "pid": "v216_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'In systems where the spiders are present, grasshoppers shift their feeding activity toward ground level, thereby increasing the relative consumption of goldenrod over Kentucky bluegrass.'\n거미가 없으면 그 반대 → 상대적으로 bluegrass를 더 먹음.\n정답: A", "trap": "E: 지면 근처로 이동하는 건 거미가 있을 때의 행동 변화일 뿐 원래 선호가 아님(관계 역전). C: 밀도 감소 효과와 행동 효과를 혼동.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"herbivore": "초식동물", "refuge": "피난처", "canopy": "덮개층, 윗부분"}, "src": "verbal216 Q5 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v216_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about predators that modify herbivore behavior?", "choices": ["They are typically better hunters than density-reducing predators.", "They often cause their prey to consume only the most nutritious foods available.", "Their presence can cause plants to change their relative use of available nutrients.", "Their effect on an ecosystem is usually less noticeable than that of density-reducing predators.", "Their presence can affect some plant species more than others."], "columns": null, "pid": "v216_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'behavioral effects... can lead to a redistribution of herbivore damage on different plant species'.\n행동을 바꾸는 포식자 → 일부 식물 종이 다른 종보다 더 큰 영향을 받음 = E.\n정답: E", "trap": "B: 오히려 '덜 영양가 있는(less nutritious)' 식물로 옮겨감(반대). C: 식물이 아니라 초식동물이 서식지 사용을 바꿈.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"density-mediated": "개체 밀도로 매개된", "redistribution": "재분배", "nutritious": "영양가 높은"}, "src": "verbal216 Q6 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.9 / S2 2.9"}, {"set": 24, "sections": [[{"id": "v205_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The research institute publishes new material on its Web site well in advance of its appearance in print; inevitably, there is a lot of dross, but fortunately, much of the material is both _____ and free.", "choices": ["speculative", "specious", "copious", "valuable", "perplexing"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "inevitably 'dross'(쓰레기 같은 자료)가 많지만 fortunately(but 대조) → 빈칸 = dross의 반대, 긍정.\n빈칸 = 가치 있는.\n정답: D (valuable)", "trap": "copious(풍부한)는 긍정처럼 보이지만 dross(질 낮음)와 대비되는 것은 '양'이 아니라 '질'.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dross": "찌꺼기", "speculative": "추측에 근거한", "specious": "그럴듯하지만 거짓인", "copious": "풍부한", "valuable": "가치 있는", "perplexing": "당혹스러운"}, "src": "verbal205 Q1 · 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v239_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "In managing the economy, there is always tension between (i) _____ and (ii) _____. People want less government regulation, but not when it means firms can hire cheap child labor. People want open markets, but not so when bankers can deceive investors.", "choices": null, "columns": [["equality", "freedom", "cooperation"], ["transparency", "innovation", "fairness"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "뒤 예시가 단서: '규제를 줄이길 원하지만(자유) 아동 노동은 안 된다(공정)', '시장 개방을 원하지만(자유) 은행가의 사기는 안 된다(공정)'.\n(i) freedom, (ii) fairness 사이의 긴장.\n정답: B (freedom), F (fairness)", "trap": "(ii) transparency(투명성)는 은행가 사기 예시엔 맞지만 아동 노동 예시엔 안 맞음. (i) equality는 '규제 완화, 시장 개방'과 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"equality": "평등", "freedom": "자유", "cooperation": "협력", "transparency": "투명성", "innovation": "혁신", "fairness": "공정성"}, "src": "verbal239 Q2 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v7_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Because leadership in the computer hacker group is extremely (i) _____, when law enforcement agencies arrested several prominent members, taking them offline, the group (ii) _____. Instead, it continues to operate, sometimes under its own name, sometimes under other names. The names are (iii) _____, as are the members of the group: anyone, anywhere, is free to work behind its mask.", "choices": null, "columns": [["fluid", "efficient", "hierarchical"], ["adopted new practice", "replaced its leadership", "did not collapse"], ["idiosyncratic", "fungible", "misleading"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'anyone, anywhere, is free to work behind its mask' → 리더십이 고정되지 않음 = fluid.\n(ii) 'Instead, it continues to operate' → 지도부 체포에도 무너지지 않음 = did not collapse.\n(iii) 'as are the members' + 이름을 바꿔가며 활동 → 이름도 서로 바꿔 쓸 수 있음 = fungible.\n정답: A (fluid), F (did not collapse), H (fungible)", "trap": "(i) hierarchical은 정반대(위계적이면 지도부 체포로 붕괴). (ii) replaced its leadership은 Instead와 연결이 어색.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"idiosyncratic": "특이한", "fungible": "대체 가능한", "fluid": "유동적인", "efficient": "효율적인", "hierarchical": "위계적인", "adopted new practice": "새 관행을 채택했다", "replaced its leadership": "지도부를 교체했다", "did not collapse": "무너지지 않았다", "misleading": "오해를 일으키는"}, "src": "verbal7 Q3"}, {"id": "v1_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that which of the following was true of \"early scholars\"?", "choices": ["They downplayed the African influence on traditional English dance forms.", "They overlooked the importance of migration in Appalachian history.", "They may have been unaware of the complexity of Appalachia's musical traditions.", "They underestimated the prominence of the fiddle in Appalachian dance music.", "They neglected the social context in which Appalachian square dances were performed."], "columns": null, "pid": "v1_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: early scholars는 스퀘어 댄스를 영국 춤이 '변함없이 보존된' 것이라 봄. However 이후 저자는 음악적 다양성(reels, breakdowns, rags, blues, banjo)을 제시하며 'it would be naive to think...purely English'.\n→ 초기 학자들은 애팔래치아 음악 전통의 복잡성을 몰랐을 수 있음 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "B: 이주(immigration)가 언급되지만 초기 학자들의 문제를 '이주의 중요성 간과'로 특정하기엔 범위 밖. A: 영국 춤에 대한 아프리카 영향이 아니라 애팔래치아 문화에 대한 것.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Early scholars", "glosses": {"repertoire": "레퍼토리, 연주 목록", "naive": "순진한", "iconic": "상징적인"}, "src": "verbal1 Q4"}, {"id": "v1_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, Appalachian square dancing differs from English country dancing in that Appalachian square dancing", "choices": ["is closely associated with the banjo", "is particularly common in rural settings", "can be performed to the tune of a reel", "developed in isolation from outside influences", "has changed significantly since it first emerged"], "columns": null, "pid": "v1_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'not to mention the iconic presence of the banjo, an instrument with African roots—it would be naive to think the accompanying dances are purely English forms.'\nbanjo는 애팔래치아 춤 음악의 상징적 요소이며, 순수 영국식이 아니라는 근거 → 애팔래치아 스퀘어 댄스는 banjo와 밀접 = A.\n정답: A", "trap": "E: 새로운 요소가 계속 유입됐다는 언급은 있지만, 그것이 영국 춤과의 '차이점'으로 제시되진 않음. D: isolation은 지문이 반박하는 견해.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"breakdown": "브레이크다운(빠른 춤곡)", "reel": "릴(스코틀랜드식 춤곡)", "rural": "시골의"}, "src": "verbal1 Q5"}, {"id": "v215_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Pre-Columbian peoples had a significant impact on Amazonian forest diversity; at least 8,000 years ago, they must have begun domesticating plants recently found to be _____ around sites once occupied by humans.", "choices": ["hybridized", "abundant", "uncommon", "preserved", "harvested", "dominant"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론 앞: 선사시대 사람들이 숲의 다양성에 큰 영향 → 그들이 기른 식물이 인간 거주지 주변에 '많이' 발견됨.\n빈칸 = 풍부한, 우세한.\nabundant와 dominant가 짝.\n정답: B (abundant), F (dominant)", "trap": "harvested/preserved/hybridized는 혼자 그럴듯해도 짝이 없음. uncommon은 '큰 영향'과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hybridized": "잡종 교배된", "abundant": "풍부한", "uncommon": "드문", "preserved": "보존된", "harvested": "수확된", "dominant": "우세한"}, "src": "verbal215 Q9 · 25/11, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v19_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Since it was committed to the idea of science as an international, politically neutral enterprise, the Royal Society of London refused to __________ members from enemy nations during world wars of the twentieth century.", "choices": ["betray", "expel", "endorse", "oust", "sanction", "condemn"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "원인 Since: 과학은 국제적·정치적으로 중립이라는 이념 → 적국 출신 회원을 '쫓아내길' 거부함.\n빈칸 = 축출하다.\nexpel과 oust가 짝.\n정답: B (expel), D (oust)", "trap": "sanction/condemn은 '제재·비난'으로 혼자 그럴듯하지만 서로 정확한 동의어가 아니고 sanction은 '승인'이라는 반대 뜻도 있음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"oust": "몰아내다", "betray": "배신하다", "expel": "추방하다", "endorse": "지지하다", "sanction": "제재하다; 승인하다", "condemn": "비난하다"}, "src": "verbal19 Q8"}, {"id": "v23_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "__________ the idea that attention is a limited resource, scientists have repeatedly observed that drivers using mobile phones are slower to react and more apt to miss important details than are drivers focused solely on the road.", "choices": ["Extending", "Bolstering", "Obscuring", "Buttressing", "Eclipsing", "Complicating"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'주의력은 한정된 자원'이라는 생각과, 휴대전화 사용 운전자가 반응이 느리다는 관찰 → 관찰이 그 생각을 '뒷받침'.\n빈칸 = 지지하다, 강화하다.\nBolstering과 Buttressing이 짝.\n정답: B, D", "trap": "Extending(확장)은 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없고 관찰은 기존 생각을 '지지'하는 것이지 확장하는 것이 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"Extending": "확장하는", "Bolstering": "강화하는, 지지하는", "Obscuring": "모호하게 하는", "Buttressing": "뒷받침하는", "Eclipsing": "가리는, 능가하는", "Complicating": "복잡하게 하는"}, "src": "verbal23 Q7"}, {"id": "v5_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The adipose tissue in which our bodies store fat from the food we eat has traditionally been thought of as _____, but in reality, this tissue constitutes a dynamic organ, not a mere repository.", "choices": ["capacious", "deleterious", "inert", "detrimental", "passive", "inessential"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "but in reality 대조: 실제로는 'a dynamic organ, not a mere repository' → 전통적 생각은 그 반대.\n빈칸 = dynamic의 반대 = 비활성의, 수동적인.\ninert와 passive가 짝.\n정답: C (inert), E (passive)", "trap": "deleterious/detrimental(해로운)도 짝이지만 'dynamic'과 대조되지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"capacious": "용량이 큰", "deleterious": "해로운", "inert": "비활성의, 움직이지 않는", "detrimental": "해로운", "passive": "수동적인", "inessential": "필수적이지 않은"}, "src": "verbal5 Q9"}, {"id": "v15_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following statements regarding medieval astronomers can be inferred from the passage?", "choices": ["They were skeptical of the idea that certain astronomical configurations could produce high flood tides.", "They had an understanding of the effect of the Sun and Moon on ocean tides.", "They could calculate lunar positions with some accuracy, but not the positions of the Sun and Earth.", "Although they were highly skilled in celestial calculations, they were unlikely to apply this knowledge to predictions of events on Earth.", "They possessed the mathematical skills for performing only the simplest of astronomical calculations."], "columns": null, "pid": "v15_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'a clerk uses medieval astronomical tables, calculating lunar and solar positions, to predict an extraordinarily high flood tide'.\n해·달의 위치로 조수를 예측 → 중세 천문학자들이 해와 달이 조수에 미치는 영향을 이해했음.\nOlson의 분석으로 그 묘사가 실제 천문 현상과 일치함도 확인.\n정답: B", "trap": "D: 천체 지식을 지구의 사건 예측에 적용하지 않았다는 건 지문(조수 예측)과 정반대. C/E: 근거 없는 제한.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"astrolabe": "아스트롤라베(천체 관측기)", "configuration": "배치", "treatise": "논문"}, "src": "verbal15 Q10"}, {"id": "v15_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that Hodgson would agree with which of the following statements about the clerk's astronomical calculations?", "choices": ["The clerk's calculations do not add artistic merit to \"The Franklin's Tale.\"", "Chaucer's purpose in describing the clerk's calculations is to instruct readers in the rudiments of astronomy.", "Chaucer's intent in using technical material was not to provide a scientifically valid discussion.", "The clerk's ability to predict a high flood tide is implausible, given the level of scientific knowledge in the late fourteenth century.", "The technical language that Chaucer uses in describing the calculations does not reflect the scientific terminology of the time."], "columns": null, "pid": "v15_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Hodgson은 'Chaucer's purpose here is artistic, not scientific' + 'need not be taken too seriously'.\n→ 과학적으로 타당한 논의를 제공하려는 의도가 아님 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 목적이 '예술적'이라 했으니 예술적 가치를 더하지 않는다는 건 반대. D: 예측이 불가능했다는 주장은 Hodgson이 하지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rudiments": "기초", "plausible": "그럴듯한", "artistic": "예술적인"}, "src": "verbal15 Q11"}, {"id": "v15_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["explain how fourteenth-century astronomers used complicated astronomical calculations to predict unusually high tides", "show how medieval and modern methods predict similar effects of astronomical configurations on tides", "argue that modern literary scholars should take Chaucer's scientific references throughout 《The Canterbury Tales》 more seriously", "describe Chaucer's fascination with astronomy in general and with horoscopes in particular", "present an explanation that supports the scientific veracity of a particular passage in 《The Canterbury Tales》"], "columns": null, "pid": "v15_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: Hodgson(과학적 진지함 없음) → However, Olson(실제 1340년 천문 현상 묘사) → Chaucer가 자기 별자리 계산 중 알았을 가능성으로 설명.\n→ 특정 구절의 과학적 정확성을 뒷받침하는 설명 제시 = E.\n정답: E", "trap": "D: 별점(horoscope) 언급은 설명의 일부일 뿐 주목적이 아님. C: Canterbury Tales 전체(throughout)로 일반화하는 것은 범위 초과.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"veracity": "진실성, 정확성", "horoscope": "별점, 천궁도", "plot device": "줄거리 장치"}, "src": "verbal15 Q12"}], [{"id": "v32_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The stars’ attitudes toward their glowing press are diametrically opposed: some think it _____ and others take the adulation seriously.", "choices": ["flummery", "consequential", "fanatical", "coincidental", "sincere"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'diametrically opposed'(정반대): 어떤 이들은 ___라 여기고, 다른 이들은 찬사를 진지하게 받아들임.\n빈칸 = '진지하게 받아들이다'의 반대 = 헛소리, 허튼 아첨.\nflummery(허튼소리, 빈말)가 정확.\n정답: A (flummery)", "trap": "sincere(진실한)는 진지하게 받아들이는 쪽과 같은 방향이라 대조가 없음. consequential(중요한)도 같은 방향.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"flummery": "허튼소리, 빈말 아첨", "consequential": "중요한, 결과로 생기는", "fanatical": "광신적인", "coincidental": "우연의", "sincere": "진실한"}, "src": "verbal32 Q1"}, {"id": "v6_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Many elected officials have (i) _____ into believing that the new reforms represent a solution rather than (ii) _____ of the problem. Unfortunately, such self-deception is not uncommon among politicians.", "choices": null, "columns": [["conned others", "deluded themselves", "persuaded some"], ["an elucidation", "a resolution", "an exacerbation"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "둘째 문장 'such self-deception' → (i) 자기 자신을 속임 = deluded themselves.\n(ii) 'a solution rather than ___ of the problem' → 해결책의 반대 = 문제의 악화 = an exacerbation.\n정답: B (deluded themselves), F (an exacerbation)", "trap": "(i) conned others는 '남을' 속인 것이라 self-deception과 어긋남. (ii) a resolution은 solution과 같은 뜻이라 rather than 대조가 성립하지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"conned": "속이다", "elucidation": "명쾌한 설명", "conned others": "남을 속였다", "deluded themselves": "스스로를 속였다", "persuaded some": "일부를 설득했다", "an elucidation": "명쾌한 설명", "a resolution": "해결", "an exacerbation": "악화"}, "src": "verbal6 Q2"}, {"id": "v230_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Feeling that Francisco Suarez’s views on early modern philosophy had received an amount of attention (i) _____ their great importance, the scholar decided to write a paper about Suarez to help (ii) _____ that neglect.", "choices": null, "columns": [["consonant with", "independent of", "incommensurate with"], ["codify", "redress", "corroborate"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 'that neglect' → 관심이 부족했음 → (i) 큰 중요성에 비해 관심이 '걸맞지 않게 적음' = incommensurate with.\n(ii) 그 소홀함을 '바로잡기' 위해 논문을 씀 = redress.\n정답: C (incommensurate with), E (redress)", "trap": "(i) consonant with(~과 일치하는)는 neglect와 모순. (ii) corroborate(확증하다)는 소홀함을 확증하는 셈이라 목적과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"consonant with": "~과 일치하는", "independent of": "~과 무관한", "incommensurate with": "~에 걸맞지 않은", "codify": "성문화하다", "redress": "바로잡다, 시정하다", "corroborate": "확증하다"}, "src": "verbal230 Q2 · 24년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v16_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "During Nigeria's colonial period, the country's Igbo societies had (i) _____ sense of gender distinctions, but the idea of a strict division of labor along gender lines (ii) _____. Indeed, the social roles of women and men were quite (iii) _____, based on what people did rather than on existential categories like gender.", "choices": null, "columns": [["an elastic", "a well-developed", "a diminishing"], ["did not exist", "was emerging", "hardly changed"], ["fluid", "dissimilar", "traditional"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) but 대조: 성별 구분 의식은 있었지만 엄격한 성별 분업은 없었다 → 성별 구분 의식은 '잘 발달된' = a well-developed.\n(ii) 'Indeed' 이후 역할이 행동에 따라 정해졌다 → 엄격한 분업은 존재하지 않음 = did not exist.\n(iii) 성별이 아니라 하는 일에 따라 정해짐 → 유동적 = fluid.\n정답: B (a well-developed), D (did not exist), G (fluid)", "trap": "(i) an elastic(유연한)은 (iii)과 같은 방향이라 but 대조가 사라짐. (ii) was emerging은 Indeed 이후 내용과 불일치.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"an elastic": "유연한", "a well-developed": "잘 발달된", "a diminishing": "줄어드는", "did not exist": "존재하지 않았다", "was emerging": "생겨나고 있었다", "hardly changed": "거의 변하지 않았다", "fluid": "유동적인", "dissimilar": "다른", "traditional": "전통적인"}, "src": "verbal16 Q4"}, {"id": "v22_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that Auffenberg regarded the bacteria in Komodo dragon saliva as \"beneficial\" because he believed that these bacteria", "choices": ["play an important role in helping the lizards digest their food", "play an important role in maintaining the lizards' immune systems", "are a weapon used by the lizards to incapacitate their prey", "are transmitted directly from parent lizards to their offspring", "deter larger predators from attacking the lizards"], "columns": null, "pid": "v22_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Auffenberg proposed that the bacteria are beneficial to the lizards; in essence a slow-acting venom facilitates prey capture'.\n→ 박테리아는 먹이를 무력화하는 무기 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "D: 부모에서 자식으로의 전달은 Auffenberg가 메커니즘을 '제시하지 않았다'는 부분과 관련, 그의 견해 아님. A/B: 소화·면역은 언급 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "beneficial", "glosses": {"pathogenic": "병원성의", "sepsis": "패혈증", "incapacitate": "무력화하다"}, "src": "verbal22 Q5"}, {"id": "v22_q6", "type": "RC_select", "blanks": null, "stem": "Select a sentence in the passage that highlights a gap in an explanation.", "choices": [], "columns": null, "pid": "v22_p1", "answer": "SENTENCE", "answer_sentence": "He offered no mechanism by which the bacteria are acquired by lizards, however.", "explanation": "'gap in an explanation' = 설명의 빈틈.\nAuffenberg의 설명(박테리아는 먹이 사냥을 돕는 독)에 대해 'He offered no mechanism by which the bacteria are acquired by lizards, however.'\n→ 박테리아를 어떻게 얻는지 메커니즘이 빠져 있음 = 빈틈.\n정답: He offered no mechanism by which the bacteria are acquired by lizards, however.", "trap": "Fry et al. 문장은 대안 설명 제시이지 빈틈 지적이 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"mechanism": "메커니즘, 작용 방식", "acquire": "획득하다", "passively": "수동적으로"}, "src": "verbal22 Q6"}, {"id": "v16_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["explore the interplay between two professional disciplines", "discuss the personal qualities needed to succeed in a particular endeavor", "consider what qualities give aesthetic appeal to structures of a particular kind", "present the evolution of a relationship between competing goals", "explain how apparently disparate goals actually support each other"], "columns": null, "pid": "v16_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1단락: 엔지니어가 혼자 기능과 미를 모두 달성(Telford, Roebling).\n2단락: 덜 자신 있는 엔지니어는 건축가에게 자문(Ammann과 Gilbert, Le Corbusier).\n→ 공학과 건축 두 직업 분야의 상호작용을 탐구 = A.\n정답: A", "trap": "E: 첫 문장의 'seemingly unrelated aims'에 끌리지만, 지문은 두 목표가 어떻게 서로 돕는지 설명하지 않음. C: 미적 매력의 '요소'를 분석하지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"facade": "건물 정면, 외관", "anchorage": "고정부, 정착장치", "disparate": "이질적인"}, "src": "verbal16 Q5"}, {"id": "v16_q6", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies that Othmar Ammann was", "choices": ["responsible for a design that became an aesthetic touchstone for later bridges", "financially constrained from hiring the architects he wished for the George Washington Bridge", "less certain of his aesthetic design abilities than Telford and Roebling were of theirs"], "columns": null, "pid": "v16_p1", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: GWB의 맨 강철 탑 → 'bare steel became the new aesthetic standard for monumental bridge towers' → 이후 다리의 미적 기준(touchstone).\nC: 'Engineers less artistically confident than Telford and Roebling have engaged consulting architects' + Ammann은 'often sought the help of famous architects' → 덜 자신 있었음.\nB: 돈이 부족해 영향받은 건 탑 마감(stone)이지 건축가 고용이 아님.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "B: 'money was tight'를 건축가 고용 제약으로 잘못 연결하기 쉬움. Gilbert는 실제로 고용됨.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"touchstone": "시금석, 기준", "consulting": "자문의", "constrained": "제약받는"}, "src": "verbal16 Q6"}, {"id": "v16_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true of Cass Gilbert's ideas for finishing the towers of the George Washington Bridge?", "choices": ["They had to be abandoned during construction.", "They impressed Le Corbusier.", "They were judged to be too costly when the project was initially proposed.", "They derived from themes Gilbert had explored in the Woolworth Building.", "They started a fashion that was followed in later bridge towers."], "columns": null, "pid": "v16_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Gilbert는 탑을 석재로 마감하는 모습을 그렸지만 'Since money was tight when the bridge was being completed, however, the steel-framed towers were left bare'.\n→ 건설 중 아이디어가 포기됨 = A.\n정답: A", "trap": "C: 비용 문제는 '처음 제안될 때'가 아니라 '완공 시점'에 발생. B/E: Le Corbusier가 좋아하고 유행이 된 건 맨 강철 모습이지 Gilbert의 안이 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"depict": "묘사하다", "bare": "드러난, 맨", "aesthetic": "미적인"}, "src": "verbal16 Q7"}, {"id": "v232_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "For every _____ reader of 《Vestiges》, there were many more who became vocal critics, and the book aroused heated opposition from a broad range of British society.", "choices": ["outspoken", "meticulous", "sympathetic", "well-disposed", "unenthusiastic", "candid"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'For every ___ reader, there were many more who became vocal critics' → 빈칸은 critics의 반대.\n빈칸 = 호의적인, 지지하는.\nsympathetic과 well-disposed가 짝.\n정답: C (sympathetic), D (well-disposed)", "trap": "outspoken/candid(솔직한)는 짝이지만 vocal critics와 대비되지 않음(비평가도 솔직할 수 있음).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"well-disposed": "호의적인", "outspoken": "거리낌 없이 말하는", "meticulous": "꼼꼼한", "sympathetic": "공감하는, 호의적인", "unenthusiastic": "열의 없는", "candid": "솔직한"}, "src": "verbal232 Q11 · 25/11, 25/6, 25/3, 24/9, 24/8, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v204_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Because video game users control their character's actions, the distinction between media user and character is not as _____ in video games as it is in traditional media, where audience members simply witness characters' actions.", "choices": ["fluid", "salient", "fraught", "elusive", "palpable", "charged"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "원인 Because: 게임 사용자는 캐릭터의 행동을 직접 조종 → 사용자와 캐릭터의 구분이 흐려짐.\n'not as ___ in video games as in traditional media' → 빈칸 = 뚜렷한, 분명한.\nsalient와 palpable이 짝.\n정답: B (salient), E (palpable)", "trap": "fluid/elusive(흐릿한)는 짝이지만 방향이 반대: 'not as fluid'면 게임에서 구분이 더 분명하다는 뜻이 됨. fraught/charged도 짝이지만 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"salient": "두드러진", "palpable": "뚜렷한, 손에 잡힐 듯한", "charged": "감정이 격앙된", "fluid": "유동적인", "fraught": "긴장된, ~로 가득한", "elusive": "파악하기 어려운"}, "src": "verbal204 Q10 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v222_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Scientists are finding that the adult brain is for more _____ than they once thought: our behavior and environment can cause substantial rewiring of the brain or a reorganization of its functions and where they are located.", "choices": ["reparable", "heterogeneous", "malleable", "variegated", "complex", "plastic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 행동과 환경이 뇌를 'substantial rewiring', 기능의 재조직을 일으킴 → 뇌가 변형 가능함.\n빈칸 = 유연한, 변형 가능한.\nmalleable과 plastic이 짝.\n정답: C (malleable), F (plastic)", "trap": "heterogeneous/variegated(다양한)도 짝이지만 '재배선, 재조직'이라는 변화 가능성과 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"reparable": "수리 가능한", "heterogeneous": "이질적인, 다양한", "malleable": "유연한, 변형 가능한", "variegated": "다채로운, 잡색의", "complex": "복잡한", "plastic": "가소성 있는, 유연한"}, "src": "verbal222 Q10 · 25/9, 25/6, 24/5, 23/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v6_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following most logically completes the argument?", "choices": ["there are no historical records of any state burial of foot soldiers in that location around that period", "none of the other gravesites in the area contain the bones of women, who were not permitted to be soldiers in ancient Athens", "few Athenian men who lived during that period rode horses frequently", "none of the bones at the gravesite are those of horses", "ancient historians do not provide specific enough descriptions to enable archaeologists to pinpoint the burial's exact location"], "columns": null, "pid": "v6_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 이 뼈는 기병의 것일 가능성이 높다. 근거: 뼈 주인들이 말을 자주 탔다.\n가정: 말을 자주 타는 사람 = 기병일 가능성이 높아야 함(다른 사람들은 말을 잘 안 탐).\nC: 당시 아테네 남성 중 말을 자주 탄 사람은 드물었다 → 다른 무덤의 남성일 가능성을 배제.\n정답: C", "trap": "B: 다른 무덤에 여성이 없다는 건 말 타기 근거와 무관. A: 보병 국장 기록이 없다는 건 보조 정보일 뿐 '말 타기' 증거를 연결하지 못함.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cavalry": "기병", "excavate": "발굴하다", "pinpoint": "정확히 짚다"}, "src": "verbal6 Q11"}, {"id": "v18_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best expresses the main idea of the passage?", "choices": ["Increasing the space devoted to parks in urban areas would not necessarily make cities seem less man-made.", "Because they are densely populated, cities tend to have a disproportionately negative impact on the environment.", "Although densely populated cities are relatively energy efficient, they are still the largest contributors to environmental pollution.", "Decreasing the density of urban populations might in some respects worsen their environmental impact.", "The extraordinary energy efficiency of cities suggests that concerns about the environment in urban areas may be unwarranted."], "columns": null, "pid": "v18_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 도시는 오염 위기 지역으로 여겨짐 → But 공원 확대, 개발 강도 완화 같은 변화는 도시의 에너지 효율을 해친다 → 면적당은 나쁘지만 1인당은 반대.\n→ 도시 밀도를 낮추면 오히려 환경 영향이 악화될 수 있다 = D.\n정답: D", "trap": "E: '우려가 부당하다'는 과장(극단적). C: 1인당 기준으로는 가장 큰 기여자가 아님. B: 저자가 반박하는 통념.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"undermine": "약화시키다", "per capita": "1인당", "unwarranted": "부당한, 근거 없는"}, "src": "verbal18 Q12"}, {"id": "v18_q13", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies that in the United States relatively sparsely populated areas exceed cities in per capita rate of", "choices": ["solid-waste production", "intensity of development", "greenhouse-gas emissions"], "columns": null, "pid": "v18_p3", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 면적당 도시는 'generate more greenhouse gases, use more energy, and produce more solid waste'이지만 'If you plotted the same negative impacts by resident or household, however, the reverse would hold.'\n→ 1인당 기준으로는 다른 지역이 고형 폐기물(A), 온실가스(C)에서 도시를 초과.\nB: 개발 강도는 1인당 '비율'로 언급된 항목이 아님.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "B: 'intensity of development'가 지문에 나와 고르기 쉽지만 per capita 역전 대상 목록에 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"per capita": "1인당", "intensity": "강도", "comparable": "비슷한, 비교할 만한"}, "src": "verbal18 Q13"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.6 / S2 2.9"}, {"set": 25, "sections": [[{"id": "v27_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Massive geological changes do not always happen gradually; for example, asteroid and comet impacts and volcanic eruptions cause _____ changes in Earth's environment.", "choices": ["transitory", "precipitate", "predictable", "inconspicuous", "incalculable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 절: 거대한 지질 변화가 '항상 점진적으로(gradually)' 일어나는 것은 아니다.\n세미콜론 + for example → 앞 내용의 예시(연속 관계).\n따라서 소행성 충돌·화산 폭발은 '점진적'의 반대, 즉 갑작스러운 변화를 일으킨다.\n빈칸 = gradual의 반대 = '급격한, 갑작스러운'.\nprecipitate(형용사) = 갑작스러운, 성급한 → 정확히 일치.\n정답: B (precipitate)", "trap": "transitory(일시적인)는 '짧게 지나가는'이라는 뜻이라 '점진적'의 반대 축(속도)이 아니라 지속 기간에 관한 말이다. incalculable(헤아릴 수 없는)도 그럴듯하지만 gradual과의 대비가 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"precipitate": "갑작스러운, 성급한", "transitory": "일시적인, 덧없는", "predictable": "예측 가능한", "inconspicuous": "눈에 띄지 않는", "incalculable": "헤아릴 수 없는, 막대한"}, "src": "verbal27 Q1"}, {"id": "v235_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Considering that experimental treatments that are (i) _____ one mouse population are, nonetheless, ineffectual with other mice, we might reasonably conclude that many rodent studies are not (ii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["extreme for", "successful for", "unpredictable in"], ["conceptually innovative", "methodologically rigorous", "scientifically controversial"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Considering that ... nonetheless ineffectual with other mice: '그럼에도 불구하고' 다른 쥐에게는 효과가 없다 → (i)은 ineffectual의 반대.\n(i) = 효과가 있는 → successful for (어떤 쥐 집단에는 성공적).\n한 집단에선 되고 다른 집단에선 안 된다 = 결과가 재현·일반화되지 않음.\n(ii) 그러므로 많은 설치류 연구는 '엄밀하지' 않다고 결론 → methodologically rigorous.\n정답: B (successful for), E (methodologically rigorous)", "trap": "(ii)의 conceptually innovative는 '혁신적이지 않다'는 결론이 되어 재현성 문제와 연결되지 않는다. (i)의 unpredictable in은 nonetheless의 대비를 만들지 못한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"extreme for": "~에 극단적인", "successful for": "~에 성공적인(효과 있는)", "unpredictable in": "~에서 예측 불가능한", "conceptually innovative": "개념적으로 혁신적인", "methodologically rigorous": "방법론적으로 엄밀한", "scientifically controversial": "과학적으로 논란이 많은"}, "src": "verbal235 Q2 · 25년 10월, 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v217_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The notion of popular science or of the public understanding of science is very much a concern in today's world, where we can see (i) _____ between science and nonscience. But in the nineteenth century, there was still an enviable mixing and cross-fertilization between seemingly (ii) _____ subjects, and there was no (iii) _____ what counted as science, let alone how a public understanding might differ from any other sort of understanding.", "choices": null, "columns": [["very permeable boundaries", "a historical synergy", "a clear demarcation"], ["disparate", "redundant", "resurgent"], ["foreknowledge of", "candor about", "consensus on"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CDI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 오늘날(today) vs. 19세기(But in the nineteenth century) 대비.\n19세기에는 '혼합과 교류(mixing and cross-fertilization)'가 있었다 → 오늘날은 그 반대: 과학/비과학 사이의 분명한 경계 → (i) a clear demarcation.\n(ii) 교류가 '부러울 만한' 이유: 겉보기에는 서로 이질적인(disparate) 분야들 사이에서도 섞였기 때문 → disparate.\n(iii) 무엇이 과학인지조차 정해지지 않았다 = 합의가 없었다 → consensus on. let alone(하물며)과도 자연스럽게 연결.\n정답: C (a clear demarcation), D (disparate), I (consensus on)", "trap": "(i)의 very permeable boundaries(투과적 경계)는 오히려 19세기의 상황을 묘사하므로 대비가 깨진다. (iii)의 foreknowledge of는 '미리 아는 것'이라 '과학의 정의'와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"very permeable boundaries": "매우 투과적인(쉽게 넘나드는) 경계", "a historical synergy": "역사적 상승작용", "a clear demarcation": "분명한 경계 구분", "disparate": "이질적인, 서로 다른", "redundant": "불필요한, 중복되는", "resurgent": "부활하는, 재기하는", "foreknowledge of": "~에 대한 예지", "candor about": "~에 대한 솔직함", "consensus on": "~에 대한 합의"}, "src": "verbal217 Q3 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v235_q4", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage mentions which of the following as effects of exotic pests on forest ecosystems?", "choices": ["Decreased vitality in trees", "Defoliation of trees", "Change in forest structure"], "columns": null, "pid": "v235_p1", "answer": "ABC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거 문장: Short-term effects ... \"may cause the defoliation, loss of vigor, or death of trees.\"\nA Decreased vitality = loss of vigor의 패러프레이즈 → O.\nB Defoliation of trees = defoliation 그대로 → O.\nC 장기 효과: \"consequent alternations of forest structure\" → Change in forest structure → O.\n세 가지 모두 본문에 명시되어 있다.\n정답: A, B, C", "trap": "C가 '단기 효과' 목록에 없다고 빼기 쉽지만, 질문은 단기/장기를 구분하지 않고 '효과'를 묻는다. 장기 효과 문장에 forest structure가 있다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"defoliation": "낙엽화, 잎이 떨어짐", "vigor": "활력, 생기", "abiotic": "비생물적인", "ramify": "파급되다, 가지를 치다"}, "src": "verbal235 Q4 · 26/1, 24/2, 23/10, 22/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v235_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage mentions the “unique properties” of tree species primarily in order to help explain", "choices": ["why pests tend to target specific tree species", "why pests can have long-term effects on entire ecosystems", "how pests contribute to shifts in forest species composition", "how pests are able to become established in an ecosystem", "how some tree species are able to withstand the effects of pests"], "columns": null, "pid": "v235_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"Shifts in forest species composition ramify through the ecosystem in many ways because tree species have different, often unique properties.\"\nunique properties는 because절로, '종 구성의 변화가 왜 생태계 전체로 파급되는가'를 설명한다.\n이 문장은 앞의 장기 효과(Long-term effects ... changes in species composition) 논의를 마무리한다.\n즉 해충 → 종 구성 변화 → (나무마다 고유한 특성이 있으므로) 생태계 전체에 장기적 영향.\nB 'why pests can have long-term effects on entire ecosystems'가 이 역할을 정확히 담는다.\n정답: B", "trap": "C(how pests contribute to shifts in species composition)가 가장 헷갈린다. unique properties는 종 구성 변화가 '일어나는 이유'가 아니라 그 변화가 '생태계 전체로 퍼지는 이유'를 설명한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "unique properties", "glosses": {"ramify": "파급되다, 가지를 치다", "composition": "구성", "mediate": "매개하다", "permanent component": "영구적 구성 요소"}, "src": "verbal235 Q5 · 26/1, 24/2, 23/10, 22/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v21_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "For certain economists, \"pure\" economic theory, that is, economic theory __________ a specific social structure, is impossible, much like a concept of anatomy that investigates no specific species.", "choices": ["attuned to", "abstracted from", "derived from", "divorced from", "sensitive to", "analyzed in"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "\"pure\" economic theory, that is(즉) ~ : 빈칸 부분은 '순수' 이론의 정의다.\n뒤의 비유: 특정 종을 조사하지 않는 해부학 개념 → 특정 대상에서 떨어져 나온 것.\n빈칸 = 특정 사회 구조로부터 '분리된, 추상화된'.\nabstracted from(~에서 추상화된)과 divorced from(~와 분리된)이 같은 의미.\n정답: B (abstracted from), D (divorced from)", "trap": "derived from(~에서 파생된)은 '분리'가 아니라 '근거함'이라 반대 의미. attuned to / sensitive to도 서로 짝이 되지만 '특정 구조에 맞춘'이라 '순수'와 반대다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"attuned to": "~에 맞춰진, 조화된", "abstracted from": "~에서 추상화된(떼어낸)", "derived from": "~에서 파생된", "divorced from": "~와 분리된", "sensitive to": "~에 민감한", "analyzed in": "~에서 분석된"}, "src": "verbal21 Q8"}, {"id": "v207_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Many people remember a time when cutting-edge architects, who are these days treated like celebrities, had _____ relationship with the public: for much of the 1960s, big new buildings in cities were often cause for hostility, not celebration.", "choices": ["an antagonistic", "an inimical", "an autocratic", "a symbiotic", "an indifferent", "an apathetic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 콜론 뒤 설명 — 1960년대 대형 신축 건물은 축하가 아니라 적대감(hostility)의 원인이었다.\n또 '요즘은 셀럽 대접' vs '예전에는'의 대비.\n빈칸 = 대중과의 관계가 '적대적인'.\nantagonistic(적대적인)과 inimical(적대적인, 해로운)이 같은 의미.\n정답: A (an antagonistic), B (an inimical)", "trap": "indifferent / apathetic(무관심한)도 서로 짝이지만, hostility는 무관심이 아니라 적극적인 적대이므로 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"antagonistic": "적대적인", "inimical": "적대적인, 해로운", "autocratic": "독재적인", "symbiotic": "공생의", "indifferent": "무관심한", "apathetic": "무관심한, 냉담한"}, "src": "verbal207 Q6 · 24년 3월, 22년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v205_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although it is premature to say whether nanomotors would _____ conventional methods, Wang believes that the most promising applications for nanomotors lie in fast drug delivery or low-cost cleanup of environmental pollutants.", "choices": ["replicate", "complement", "eliminate", "supplant", "supersede", "exacerbate"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although it is premature to say whether nanomotors would ___ conventional methods: '기존 방법을 ~할지 말하기는 이르다'.\n뒤 절: 그래도 가장 유망한 응용 분야는 약물 전달·오염 정화라는 것 → 새로운 기술이 기존 기술을 '대체할지'가 자연스러운 질문.\n빈칸 = '대체하다'.\nsupplant와 supersede가 모두 '대체하다, 밀어내다'.\n정답: D (supplant), E (supersede)", "trap": "eliminate(제거하다)는 짝이 없고 '기존 방법을 없앤다'는 과한 표현. complement(보완하다)는 그럴듯하지만 동의어 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"supplant": "대체하다, 밀어내다", "replicate": "복제하다, 재현하다", "complement": "보완하다", "eliminate": "제거하다", "supersede": "대체하다, 대신하다", "exacerbate": "악화시키다"}, "src": "verbal205 Q7 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v219_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Though initially presented in a blaze of hyperbole, the thesis is repeated even more _____ in the ensuing paragraphs.", "choices": ["vehemently", "pragmatically", "soberly", "emphatically", "pretentiously", "sensibly"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Though(양보) → 앞과 뒤가 대비된다.\n앞: 처음에는 과장(hyperbole)의 불길 속에서 제시됨.\n뒤: 그 논지가 이후 문단에서는 '과장과 반대로' 반복됨 → 차분하게, 분별 있게.\n빈칸 = hyperbole의 반대 = '절제된, 냉정한'.\nsoberly(냉정하게, 절제하여)와 sensibly(분별 있게)가 같은 방향.\n정답: C (soberly), F (sensibly)", "trap": "vehemently / emphatically(격렬하게, 강조하여)가 서로 짝이고 'even more'와 붙어 매력적이지만, Though의 대비 신호를 무시한 답이다(과장 → 더 과장이면 양보가 성립 안 함).", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hyperbole": "반대 (handwritten note 'hyperbole반대': blank is the opposite of hyperbole)", "vehemently": "격렬하게, 열렬히", "pragmatically": "실용적으로", "soberly": "냉정하게, 절제하여", "emphatically": "강조하여, 단호히", "pretentiously": "허세 부리며", "sensibly": "분별 있게, 현명하게"}, "src": "verbal219 Q9 · 25/10, 25/7, 25/6, 25/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v33_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["explain why 《Dust Tracks》 has been less well received than other similarly structured works by Hurston", "argue that a supposed deficiency in 《Dust Tracks》 actually contributes to the work’s presentation of its subject", "compare the critical reaction to 《Dust Tracks》 with the critical reaction to 《Their Eyes Were Watching God》", "point out specific similarities between the structure of 《Dust Tracks》 and the structure of Hurston’s other works", "suggest that some critics’ evaluations of 《Dust Tracks》 is influenced by their rejection of certain conventions of autobiography"], "columns": null, "pid": "v33_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1~2문장: 비평가들이 《Dust Tracks》의 '파편적 성격(fragmentary nature)'을 비판한다.\n3문장: 그 비판은 자서전의 관습을 고집할 때만 타당하다(valid if one insists on...).\n4~5문장: But 이 작품은 하나로 통합되지 않는 페르소나를 그리며, \"In order to correspond better to this persona\" 파편적 구성을 택했다.\n즉 '결점으로 여겨지는 점(파편성)'이 실제로는 주제(페르소나) 표현에 기여한다는 주장.\n정답: B", "trap": "E는 비평가들이 자서전 관습을 '거부'해서 평가했다고 하지만, 실제로는 관습을 '고수'해서 비판한 것이므로 방향이 반대다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"fragmentary": "단편적인, 파편적인", "conspicuous": "눈에 띄는, 두드러진", "cardinal": "기본적인, 가장 중요한", "persona": "(작품 속) 인물상, 페르소나"}, "src": "verbal33 Q10"}, {"id": "v33_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage suggests that critics’ complaints about the structure of 《Dust Tracks》 are", "choices": ["not valid, because 《Dust Tracks》 should not be judged by the standards of conventional autobiography", "unjustified, because they have not been directed at other Hurston texts that are similarly structured", "justified, given the extent to which 《Dust Tracks》 is autobiographical", "inexplicable, given the critical response to 《Their Eyes Were Watching God》", "compelling, because Huston’s warmest admirers have complained the most strenuously"], "columns": null, "pid": "v33_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"The complaints ... are valid if one insists on the cardinal conventions of autobiography.\"\n이어서 But으로, 이 작품은 통일되지 않는 페르소나에 맞추기 위해 파편적 구조를 택했다고 설명한다.\n즉 관습적 자서전 기준으로 판단할 때만 비판이 성립 → 그 기준으로 판단하면 안 되므로 비판은 타당하지 않다.\nA가 이를 그대로 패러프레이즈한다.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 '다른 작품에는 같은 비판이 없었다'는 이유를 대지만, 본문은 그런 비교로 비판을 반박하지 않는다(《Their Eyes》 언급은 파편성이 다른 작품에도 있다는 사실 제시일 뿐).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cardinal": "기본적인, 핵심적인", "conventions": "관습, 관례", "strenuously": "격렬하게, 열심히", "inexplicable": "설명할 수 없는"}, "src": "verbal33 Q11"}, {"id": "v33_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the organization of the passage?", "choices": ["A situation is presented and an explanation of how that situation developed is offered.", "Two opposing points of view are contrasted and their relative merits are evaluated.", "An orthodox view is discussed, a challenge to it is analyzed, and the original view is affirmed.", "A point of view is described and an analysis challenging that point of view follows.", "A dispute is analyzed and several points of agreement between the two sides are identified."], "columns": null, "pid": "v33_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞부분: 비평가들의 관점(파편적 구성에 대한 부정적 비판)을 소개.\n\"The complaints ... are valid if ...\" 이후 But으로 그 관점에 도전하는 분석이 이어진다.\n작품의 페르소나와 구성의 관계를 분석하며 비판을 반박한다.\n= '한 관점이 서술되고, 그 관점에 도전하는 분석이 뒤따른다'.\n정답: D", "trap": "C는 정통 견해가 결국 '재확인(affirmed)'된다고 하므로 결론이 반대다. B는 두 관점의 장단점을 '평가'한다고 하지만 저자는 한쪽을 분명히 반박한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"orthodox": "정통의, 일반적으로 인정된", "affirm": "확인하다, 단언하다", "merits": "장점, 가치"}, "src": "verbal33 Q12"}], [{"id": "v14_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "If we admire Winslow Homer as he wished to be admired, for his avoidance of claptrap and sentimentality, we may fear that Wood has done him a disservice by introducing _____ note into his discussion of the painter.", "choices": ["an acerbic", "a supercilious", "an austere", "a maudlin", "an ironic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Homer가 원한 방식 = 허튼 과장(claptrap)과 감상주의(sentimentality)를 피한 점으로 존경받는 것.\nWood가 '해를 끼쳤다(disservice)'는 것은 Homer가 피한 바로 그것을 끌어들였다는 뜻.\n빈칸 = sentimentality와 같은 계열 = '감상적인'.\nmaudlin(지나치게 감상적인, 눈물짜는)이 정확히 일치.\n정답: D (a maudlin)", "trap": "acerbic(신랄한)이나 ironic(반어적인)도 '부정적 어조'라 끌리지만, Homer가 피한 것은 감상주의이므로 해(disservice)의 내용과 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"claptrap": "허튼 과장, 해", "acerbic": "신랄한, 독설적인", "supercilious": "거만한, 남을 깔보는", "austere": "엄격한, 꾸밈없는", "maudlin": "지나치게 감상적인", "ironic": "반어적인, 아이러니한"}, "src": "verbal14 Q1"}, {"id": "v22_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "While catalogs of record labels that specialize in Native American music are useful indices of Native American consumers' preferences, their (i)__________ are also (ii)__________: some genres of Native American music have been deemed inappropriate to record because of their special cultural significance.", "choices": null, "columns": [["strategies", "omissions", "inconsistencies"], ["telling", "misleading", "surprising"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "While(양보): 카탈로그는 소비자 선호를 보여주는 유용한 지표이지만, 그것들의 (i)도 (ii)하다.\n콜론 뒤 근거: 일부 장르는 문화적 의미 때문에 녹음하기 부적절하다고 여겨졌다 → 카탈로그에서 '빠진 것'.\n(i) = omissions(누락).\n(ii) 그 누락은 문화적 의미를 드러내 준다 → telling(많은 것을 드러내는, 의미심장한). also가 '역시 정보를 준다'는 흐름.\n정답: B (omissions), D (telling)", "trap": "(ii)의 misleading(오해를 부르는)은 누락이 '정보를 왜곡'한다는 뜻이 되어, 누락 이유가 문화적 의미를 드러낸다는 콜론 뒤 설명과 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"strategies": "전략", "omissions": "누락, 빠진 것", "inconsistencies": "비일관성, 모순", "telling": "의미심장한, 많은 것을 드러내는", "misleading": "오해를 부르는", "surprising": "놀라운"}, "src": "verbal22 Q3"}, {"id": "v212_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The only way to definitively test a large civil engineering structure such as a bridge is to build it in anticipation of possible challenges from nature and then let nature take its course. That is not to say that every new large structure is a (i) _____. Engineers understand a great deal about the behavior and limitations of their structures' components. Furthermore, it is the (ii) _____ structure that is built more than 10 or 20 percent larger than its predecessors, thus allowing engineers to move (iii) _____ into unknown territory.", "choices": null, "columns": [["success", "gamble", "mistake"], ["conventional", "unusual", "outstanding"], ["incrementally", "unchecked", "enthusiastically"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BEG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 다리는 지어놓고 자연에 맡겨봐야만 확실히 검증된다 → '그렇다고 모든 신축 구조물이 (i)인 것은 아니다': 엔지니어는 많은 것을 안다 → (i) = gamble(도박).\n(ii) Furthermore: 위험을 줄이는 추가 근거. 이전 것보다 10~20% 이상 크게 짓는 구조물은 '드물다' → unusual.\n(iii) 그래서 미지의 영역으로 '조금씩' 나아갈 수 있다 → incrementally.\n정답: B (gamble), E (unusual), G (incrementally)", "trap": "(ii)의 conventional은 '크게 짓는 게 일반적'이라는 뜻이 되어 위험을 줄인다는 논지와 반대. (iii)의 unchecked(제지받지 않고)는 신중함의 흐름에 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"success": "성공", "gamble": "도박, 모험", "mistake": "실수", "conventional": "관습적인, 일반적인", "unusual": "드문, 특이한", "outstanding": "뛰어난, 두드러진", "incrementally": "조금씩, 점진적으로", "unchecked": "억제되지 않은 채로", "enthusiastically": "열정적으로"}, "src": "verbal212 Q4 · 25년 8월, 23년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v6_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "It appears that the terrestrial biosphere has been absorbing a significant fraction of anthropogenic CO2, thereby slowing down the rate of global climate change. However, the (i) _____ of this (ii) _____ is not (iii) _____: if pushed too far, the biosphere might become a net source of CO2, thereby accelerating climate change and causing a positive feedback loop.", "choices": null, "columns": [["complexity", "actuality", "continuation"], ["additional information", "formidable challenge", "compensatory mechanism"], ["imminent", "surprising", "guaranteed"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 육지 생물권이 인위적 CO2를 흡수해 기후 변화를 늦춰 왔다 → 이것은 '보상(완충) 메커니즘'.\nHowever + 콜론 뒤: 너무 밀어붙이면 생물권이 오히려 CO2 순배출원이 될 수 있다 → 이 흡수가 계속된다는 보장이 없다.\n(i) continuation(지속), (ii) compensatory mechanism(보상 메커니즘), (iii) guaranteed(보장된).\n= '이 보상 메커니즘의 지속은 보장되지 않는다'.\n정답: C, F, I", "trap": "(iii)의 imminent(임박한)는 '지속이 임박하지 않다'는 어색한 말이 된다. (ii)의 formidable challenge는 흡수 작용을 '도전'으로 보는 것이라 첫 문장의 긍정적 효과와 어긋난다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"complexity": "복잡성", "actuality": "실재, 현실성", "continuation": "지속, 계속", "additional information": "추가 정보", "formidable challenge": "만만치 않은 도전", "compensatory mechanism": "보상(완충) 메커니즘", "imminent": "임박한", "surprising": "놀라운", "guaranteed": "보장된"}, "src": "verbal6 Q3"}, {"id": "v8_q12", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage would agree with which of the following descriptions of the evidence collected by the Society for Psychical Research?", "choices": ["carefully recorded", "unscientific", "credible"], "columns": null, "pid": "v8_p3", "answer": "ABC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A carefully recorded: \"took great trouble to interview first-hand witnesses and to document the stories carefully\" → O.\nB unscientific: \"this evidence has nothing to do with science, since it cannot be reproduced under controlled conditions\" → O.\nC credible: 저자는 가설이 \"supported by considerable evidence\"라 하고, But 이하로 증거의 신빙성을 옹호한다 → 믿을 만하다고 본다 → O.\n비과학적이지만 신빙성 있다는 것이 저자 논지의 핵심.\n정답: A, B, C", "trap": "'unscientific'이면 'credible'일 수 없다고 생각해 C를 빼기 쉽다. 저자는 과학적이지 않아도(통제 재현 불가) 꼼꼼히 기록되었으므로 믿을 만하다고 본다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"anecdotal": "일화적인, 개인 경험담에 근거한", "paranormal": "초자연적인", "first-hand": "직접 경험한", "inherently": "본질적으로"}, "src": "verbal8 Q12"}, {"id": "v8_q13", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the role played in the passage by the highlighted sentence (the final sentence)?", "choices": ["It states the main conclusion of the author's argument.", "It provides a basis for a recommended course of action.", "It articulates a principle that supports the claim made in the preceding sentence.", "It is intended to undermine the credibility of apparent evidence that the author has mentioned earlier in the passage.", "It serves to emphasize a limitation of the evidence collected by the Society for Psychical Research."], "columns": null, "pid": "v8_p3", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "직전 문장: 초자연 현상이 강한 감정 상태에서만 일어난다는 사실이 '왜 통제된 실험에서 관찰되지 않는지'를 설명해 준다.\n마지막 문장: \"Strong emotion is inherently incompatible with controlled scientific procedures.\"\n이는 직전 문장의 설명이 성립하기 위한 일반 원리(전제)를 제시한다.\n= 앞 문장의 주장을 뒷받침하는 원칙.\n정답: C", "trap": "A(main conclusion)가 가장 매력적이지만, 주 결론은 첫 문장(초자연 현상은 실재하지만 과학의 한계 밖)이고 마지막 문장은 그것을 받치는 전제다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inherently": "본질적으로", "incompatible": "양립할 수 없는", "articulate": "명확히 표현하다", "undermine": "약화시키다"}, "src": "verbal8 Q13"}, {"id": "v216_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author refers to the Huron attitude toward coercion primarily in order to", "choices": ["weaken the claim that the desire to avoid dishonor and criticism influenced behavior in Huron society", "weaken the claim that vigorous protection of clan privileges caused clashes among the clans", "support the claim that the Hurons valued conformity more than independence", "support the contention that the clan was important in shaping the customs governing personal independence", "support the view that Huron culture respected an individual's personal freedom"], "columns": null, "pid": "v216_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞부분: 휴런 문화는 순응을 중시했다. However, 개인의 특이 행동에 대한 불관용을 개인 존엄성 무시와 동일시하는 건 오류다.\n이를 뒷받침하는 사례로 \"Overt attempts to coerce anyone were strongly opposed.\"가 나온다.\n강압에 대한 반대 태도 → 개인의 독립·자유를 존중했다는 견해를 지지.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(씨족이 관습 형성에 중요)는 씨족 이야기가 뒤에 나와 끌리지만, 강압 태도 언급의 목적은 개인 자유 존중을 보여주는 것이지 씨족의 관습 형성 역할이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Overt attempts to coerce anyone were strongly opposed.", "glosses": {"coercion": "강압, 강제", "idiosyncratic": "특이한, 별난", "affront": "모욕", "contention": "주장, 논쟁"}, "src": "verbal216 Q7 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v216_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, Huron custom in the seventeenth century did all of the following EXCEPT", "choices": ["encourage personal independence", "preserve the independence of each clan", "discourage idiosyncratic actions", "foster respect for individual dignity", "curb public criticism of individuals"], "columns": null, "pid": "v216_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "EXCEPT 문제: 본문에서 휴런 관습이 한 일이 아닌 것.\nA personal independence remained highly important / reinforced by Huron custom → O.\nB \"the vigor with which each clan guarded its independence\" → O.\nC \"strongly discouraged idiosyncratic behavior\" → O. D 개인 존엄성 존중 → O.\nE: 오히려 \"public criticism was often used effectively as a strong pressure for conformity\" → 공개 비판을 억제하지 않았다.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(존엄성 존중)는 '순응 중시'와 모순되어 보여 고르기 쉽지만, 본문은 바로 그 둘을 동일시하는 것이 오류라고 명시한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"curb": "억제하다", "foster": "육성하다, 조장하다", "idiosyncratic": "특이한, 별난", "conformity": "순응"}, "src": "verbal216 Q8 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v216_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that if the behavior of an individual member of Huron society was strikingly out of the ordinary, the individual would most likely be", "choices": ["punished by the society for setting a bad example for his or her clan", "pressured by family and friends to follow the society's code of behavior", "punished by his or her clan only if the behavior adversely affected other members of the clan", "encouraged by members of clans other than the individual's clan to continue his or her independent behavior", "praised by fellow clan members for being an individualist whose independence was admirable"], "columns": null, "pid": "v216_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"public criticism was often used effectively as a strong pressure for conformity\" — 특이 행동을 하면 비판이라는 순응 압력을 받는다.\n또 \"Custom did not permit society as a whole to punish offenders\" → 사회가 처벌하지는 않는다.\n따라서 가장 가능성 높은 결과는 처벌이 아닌 '순응하라는 압력'.\nB '주변 사람들로부터 사회 규범을 따르라는 압력'이 이를 패러프레이즈한다.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 '사회에 의해 처벌'된다고 하는데, 본문은 사회 전체가 처벌하는 것을 관습이 허용하지 않았다고 명시한다. D·E는 특이 행동을 장려·칭찬한다고 하여 순응 중시와 반대다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"idiosyncratic": "특이한, 별난", "reproach": "비난, 질책", "conformity": "순응", "offender": "위반자"}, "src": "verbal216 Q9 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v208_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the nineteenth century, the dish known as lobster Newburg was sometimes associated with the culinary accessory known as the chafing dish, but Welsh rarebit was considered the truly _____ chafing dish recipe.", "choices": ["indigenous", "sumptuous", "ubiquitous", "paradigmatic", "newfangled", "archetypal"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "대비 구조: lobster Newburg는 '때때로(sometimes)' chafing dish와 연관되었다, but Welsh rarebit은 '진정으로(truly)' ___ 요리였다.\nsometimes ↔ truly 대비 → 빈칸 = chafing dish 요리의 '대표적인, 전형적인' 예.\nparadigmatic(전형적인, 모범적인)과 archetypal(원형적인, 전형적인)이 같은 의미.\n정답: D (paradigmatic), F (archetypal)", "trap": "ubiquitous(어디에나 있는)는 '흔하다'는 뜻이라 '그 요리 장르를 대표한다'는 의미와 다르고 짝도 없다. indigenous(토착의)도 맥락과 무관하다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"indigenous": "토착의, 고유한", "sumptuous": "호화로운", "ubiquitous": "어디에나 있는", "paradigmatic": "전형적인, 모범이 되는", "newfangled": "새로 유행하는(부정적)", "archetypal": "원형적인, 전형적인"}, "src": "verbal208 Q11 · 25/9, 25/8, 24/6, 23/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v224_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Despite the critic's assertion that Willa Cather's place in the literary canon is now so entrenched that it scarcely matters if she were really a modernist, her reputation arguably remains _____.", "choices": ["flawless", "uncertain", "impressive", "tenuous", "consequential", "steadfast"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Despite(양보): 비평가는 Cather의 문학 정전 내 위치가 '확고하다(entrenched)'고 주장한다.\n그럼에도 그녀의 평판은 여전히 ___ → entrenched의 반대.\n빈칸 = '불확실한, 불안정한'.\nuncertain(불확실한)과 tenuous(미약한, 확고하지 않은)가 같은 의미.\n정답: B (uncertain), D (tenuous)", "trap": "steadfast(확고한)는 entrenched와 같은 쪽이라 Despite의 대비를 깨뜨린다. flawless / impressive도 긍정 방향이라 오답.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tenuous": "미약한, 확고하지 않은", "flawless": "흠 없는", "uncertain": "불확실한", "impressive": "인상적인", "consequential": "중대한, 결과적인", "steadfast": "확고한, 변함없는"}, "src": "verbal224 Q12 · 25/8, 25/7, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v22_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Because archaeology explores the most profound changes in human history by means of a grossly incomplete record, it has invited the sort of bold, imaginative interpretation in which speculation too easily becomes __________ evidence.", "choices": ["replaced by", "constrained by", "untethered from", "divorced from", "substituted for", "constricted by"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Because: 고고학은 '매우 불완전한 기록'으로 큰 변화를 탐구한다 → 대담하고 상상력 넘치는 해석을 불러왔다.\n그런 해석에서는 추측(speculation)이 너무 쉽게 증거로부터 '떨어져 나간다'.\n빈칸 = 증거와 '분리된, 근거 없는'.\nuntethered from(~에서 풀려난)과 divorced from(~와 분리된)이 같은 의미.\n정답: C (untethered from), D (divorced from)", "trap": "replaced by / substituted for가 짝처럼 보이지만 방향이 다르다: 'speculation becomes replaced by evidence'는 추측이 증거로 대체된다는 긍정적 의미이고, substituted for는 '증거를 대신한다'로 서로 의미가 반대다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"replaced by": "~으로 대체된", "constrained by": "~에 제약된", "untethered from": "~에서 풀려난(매이지 않은)", "divorced from": "~와 분리된", "substituted for": "~을 대신하는", "constricted by": "~에 의해 조여진, 제한된"}, "src": "verbal22 Q10"}, {"id": "v228_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following hypotheses is most strongly supported by the information given?", "choices": ["Wolves were the first animals to be domesticated.", "Dogs were first domesticated in an area other than Europe.", "The modern dog is not actually a distinct species form the wolf.", "Once dogs had become a distinct species from wolves, prehistoric humans no longer domesticated wolves.", "There were no wolves in Europe much earlier than 14,000 years ago."], "columns": null, "pid": "v228_p3", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "겉보기 모순: 고고학적 증거 → 유럽에는 1만 4천 년 전보다 훨씬 이전에는 개가 없었다.\n유전적 분기 이론 → 개는 13만 5천 년 전부터 별개 종이 되기 시작했고, 그러려면 가축화가 필요했다.\n두 진술이 모두 참이려면: 개는 이미 오래전에 가축화되었지만 '유럽이 아닌 곳'에서였다.\nB가 두 사실을 동시에 만족시킨다(유럽 한정 증거라는 점이 핵심).\n정답: B", "trap": "A(늑대가 최초의 가축)는 다른 동물과의 비교 정보가 전혀 없어 범위를 벗어난다. E는 늑대 존재 여부라 본문 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"domesticate": "가축화하다, 길들이다", "genetic divergence": "유전적 분기", "distinct species": "별개의 종", "archaeological": "고고학적인"}, "src": "verbal228 Q13 · 24년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, after the 1440s, Timurid paintings of court scenes", "choices": ["generally followed well-established formulas", "are more likely to have survived than Timurid textiles", "were greatly influenced by the painter Behzad", "are frequently found in Timurid manuscripts", "sometimes showed rugs with geometric patterns"], "columns": null, "pid": "v232_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"the occasional presence of geometric rugs in similar paintings after the 1440s\"\n1440년대 이후 비슷한 그림들에 기하학 문양 러그가 가끔(occasional) 등장한다.\nE 'sometimes showed rugs with geometric patterns' = occasional presence의 패러프레이즈.\n정답: E", "trap": "A(일반적으로 정형화된 공식을 따랐다)는 본문의 'painters simply followed a well-established formula'를 가져왔지만, 그것은 아직 열린 질문(open question)인 하나의 가능성일 뿐이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"geometric": "기하학적인", "occasional": "가끔의", "formula": "정형화된 방식, 공식", "manuscript": "필사본"}, "src": "verbal232 Q14 · 25/7, 25/3, 22/10, 22/8 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies which of the following about the introduction of floral-patterned rugs in Timurid royal courts?", "choices": ["It explains the absence of any surviving geometric-patterned rugs.", "It predates any influence wielded by the painter Behzad.", "It occurred earlier than scholars have long thought."], "columns": null, "pid": "v232_p4", "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "C: 학자들은 플로럴 러그가 1400년대 말에야 도입되었다고 오래 가정했다. 그러나 1440년대 필사본에 이미 등장 → 생각보다 일찍 도입 → O.\nB: Behzad는 circa 1455년생 → 1440년대에는 그의 영향이 있을 수 없다 → 도입이 Behzad 영향보다 앞선다 → O.\nA: 기하학 러그가 남아있지 않은 이유를 설명한다는 내용은 없다(본문은 Timurid 직물 전반이 적게 남았다고만 함) → X.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "B는 연도(1440s vs Behzad 1455년생)를 직접 계산해야 해서 놓치기 쉽다. A는 첫 문장(직물이 별로 남지 않았다)과 엮어 끌리지만 인과관계는 언급되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"predate": "~보다 앞서다", "wield": "(영향력을) 행사하다", "floral-patterned": "꽃무늬의", "survive": "현존하다, 남아있다"}, "src": "verbal232 Q15 · 25/7, 25/3, 22/10, 22/8 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.8 / S2 3.1"}, {"set": 26, "sections": [[{"id": "v199_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "It is ironic that the scientist’s work was criticized recently for its _____ research methodology, since other researchers have argued for years that this same methodology was based absolutely on impeccable logic.", "choices": ["fastidious", "esoteric", "abstruse", "impervious", "specious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "It is ironic that ~, since ~: 아이러니 = 두 평가가 정반대.\n다른 연구자들은 수년간 이 방법론이 '흠잡을 데 없는 논리(impeccable logic)'에 기반한다고 했다.\n그런데 최근에는 그 반대, 즉 '논리가 그럴듯하지만 틀린' 방법론이라고 비판받음.\n빈칸 = impeccable logic의 반대 = '겉만 그럴듯한, 허울만 좋은'.\nspecious(그럴듯하지만 틀린)가 정확히 일치.\n정답: E (specious)", "trap": "esoteric / abstruse(난해한)도 비판처럼 들리지만, '어렵다'는 것은 논리적 결함이 아니므로 impeccable logic과 반대가 되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"impeccable": "흠잡을 데 없는", "fastidious": "꼼꼼한, 까다로운", "esoteric": "난해한, 소수만 이해하는", "abstruse": "난해한", "impervious": "영향받지 않는, 불침투성의", "specious": "그럴듯하지만 틀린, 허울만 좋은"}, "src": "verbal199 Q1 · 25/1, 24/11, 23/2, 22/8 중국후기"}, {"id": "v207_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Once Plowright's research is complete, she will be prepared to talk about it (i) _____, but for now, because she is discussing theories rather than facts and does not want to commit herself to an unsubstantiated claim, she prefers to make only the most (ii) _____ comments.", "choices": null, "columns": [["authoritatively", "tentatively", "extemporaneously"], ["provisional", "prescient", "germane"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 연구가 끝나면(Once ... complete) vs 지금은(but for now) 대비.\n지금은 사실이 아닌 이론을 논하고 있고, 입증되지 않은 주장에 얽매이고 싶지 않다 → (ii) 아주 '잠정적인' 발언만 → provisional.\n연구가 끝나면 그 반대로 '권위 있게, 확신을 갖고' 말할 수 있다 → (i) authoritatively.\n정답: A (authoritatively), D (provisional)", "trap": "(i)의 tentatively(잠정적으로)는 '지금'의 태도라 대비를 깨뜨린다. (ii)의 germane(적절한)은 '조심스러움'과 무관하다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"authoritatively": "권위 있게, 확신을 갖고", "tentatively": "잠정적으로, 머뭇거리며", "extemporaneously": "즉흥적으로", "provisional": "잠정적인, 임시의", "prescient": "선견지명이 있는", "germane": "관련 있는, 적절한"}, "src": "verbal207 Q2 · 25/8, 22/9, 22/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v229_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Throughout human history, religion and other areas of culture have always been (i) _____. Secularized cultural domains have often (ii) _____ religious symbols for expressing values, while religion has often drawn its symbols from (iii) _____, whether social, political, or economic.", "choices": null, "columns": [["indistinguishable", "interchangeable", "interdependent"], ["critiqued", "disguised", "adopted"], ["alien peoples", "worldly contexts", "aligned sources"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "2번째 문장이 1번째 문장을 설명한다: 세속 영역은 종교 상징을 가져다 쓰고, 종교는 세속 맥락에서 상징을 가져온다 → 서로 의존.\n(i) interdependent(상호의존적).\n(ii) 세속 문화 영역이 가치를 표현하기 위해 종교 상징을 '채택했다' → adopted.\n(iii) whether social, political, or economic → 세속적인 맥락 → worldly contexts.\n정답: C (interdependent), F (adopted), H (worldly contexts)", "trap": "(i)의 interchangeable(교환 가능한)은 상호 차용과 비슷해 보이지만 '서로 대체 가능하다'는 뜻이라 지나치다. (iii)의 alien peoples는 social/political/economic과 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"indistinguishable": "구별할 수 없는", "interchangeable": "교환 가능한", "interdependent": "상호의존적인", "critiqued": "비평했다", "disguised": "위장했다", "adopted": "채택했다", "alien peoples": "이질적인 민족", "worldly contexts": "세속적 맥락", "aligned sources": "제휴된(같은 편의) 출처"}, "src": "verbal229 Q3 · 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v227_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence within the context of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["It calls into question a distinction made in the previous sentence.", "It responds to a criticism made in the previous sentence.", "It helps explain an assertion made in the previous sentence.", "It introduces a problem that is discussed later in the passage.", "It anticipates a dispute that is discussed later in the passage."], "columns": null, "pid": "v227_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "직전 문장: 지역 규모에서는 침입이 종 구성을 바꾸지만, 다양성에 대한 영향은 '덜 확실하다'.\n강조 문장: \"Changes in diversity within a region depend on the number of extinctions of native species.\"\n→ 왜 불확실한가? 다양성 변화는 토착종 멸종 수에 달려 있기 때문(멸종이 많으면 감소, 없으면 증가).\n즉 직전 문장의 주장을 설명하는 역할.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 앞 문장의 '전 지구 vs 지역' 구분을 의문시한다고 하지만, 강조 문장은 구분을 문제 삼지 않고 지역 차원의 불확실성 이유를 설명한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"species composition": "종 구성", "nonnative": "외래의, 비토착의", "coincident": "동시에 일어나는", "extinction": "멸종"}, "src": "verbal227 Q4 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v227_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage would be likely to agree with which of the following statements about the effects of invasions by nonnative species on species diversity?", "choices": ["Invasions of nonnative species have led to an overall reduction in global species diversity.", "In regions where several native species have become extinct following the invasion of a nonnative species, the diversity of those regions has decreased.", "In regions where invasions of nonnative species have not led to extinctions of native species, the diversity of those regions has increased."], "columns": null, "pid": "v227_p1", "answer": "ABC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: \"Invasions of nonnative species are clearly reducing species diversity on a global scale.\" → O.\nB: 지역 다양성은 토착종 멸종 수에 달려 있다. 외래종 1종이 들어와 여러 토착종이 멸종하면 순감소 → 감소 (예: 괌의 갈색나무뱀과 여러 조류 멸종 \"broad losses\") → O.\nC: 마지막 문장 \"in regions where many nonnative species have become established without coincident extinctions, diversity has increased.\" → O.\n정답: A, B, C", "trap": "B는 '종 수 = 들어온 종 - 멸종 종'을 따져야 해서 놓치기 쉽다. 'a nonnative species(1종)'가 들어오고 'several(여러)' 종이 멸종했으니 순감소가 확실하다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"nonnative": "외래의", "coincident": "동시에 일어나는", "flora and fauna": "식물상과 동물상", "establishment": "정착"}, "src": "verbal227 Q5 · 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v15_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although, in spirit at least, solar panels _____ nature and the way our biosphere harnesses the energy of our sun, the actual photosynthetic process by which plants convert sunlight into chemical energy is far more complex than solar power generation is.", "choices": ["streamline", "enhance", "imitate", "exploit", "simplify", "mimic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although(양보): 정신적으로는(in spirit at least) 태양광 패널이 자연을 ___하지만, 실제 광합성은 태양광 발전보다 훨씬 복잡하다.\n'적어도 취지상으로는 자연을 따라 하지만 실제로는 훨씬 단순하다'는 대비.\n빈칸 = '모방하다'.\nimitate와 mimic이 같은 의미.\n정답: C (imitate), F (mimic)", "trap": "simplify / streamline(단순화하다)은 뒤의 '광합성이 더 복잡하다'와 연결되어 끌리지만, Although의 대비(취지는 같지만 실제는 다르다)를 만들지 못하고 서로도 완전한 동의어 짝이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"streamline": "간소화하다, 효율화하다", "enhance": "향상시키다", "imitate": "모방하다", "exploit": "이용하다, 착취하다", "simplify": "단순화하다", "mimic": "흉내 내다, 모방하다"}, "src": "verbal15 Q8"}, {"id": "v3_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Those who initially recorded American Indian oral stories often _____ them when they wrote them down; the subsequent publishers of American Indian stories, therefore, are not the first to affect the meaning.", "choices": ["modified", "preserved", "misconstrued", "circulated", "adapted", "promulgated"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 세미콜론 + therefore → 이후 출판사들이 의미에 영향을 준 '최초'가 아니다.\n즉 처음 기록한 사람들도 이미 의미에 영향을 주었다 → 기록하면서 이야기를 '바꿨다'.\n빈칸 = '변경하다, 각색하다'.\nmodified와 adapted가 같은 의미.\n정답: A (modified), E (adapted)", "trap": "misconstrued(오해하다)는 '의미에 영향'과 연결되어 끌리지만, 짝이 되는 동의어가 없고 '잘못 이해함'은 '바꿔 적음'과 다르다. circulated / promulgated(유포하다)는 짝이지만 의미 변경과 무관하다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"modified": "수정했다, 변경했다", "preserved": "보존했다", "misconstrued": "오해했다, 잘못 해석했다", "circulated": "유포했다", "adapted": "각색했다, 조정했다", "promulgated": "공표했다, 널리 퍼뜨렸다"}, "src": "verbal3 Q6"}, {"id": "v25_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although collisions between the largest planetesimals in a planetesimal belt are _____, they can release large amounts of debris when they occur.", "choices": ["risky", "exceptional", "irregular", "violent", "rare", "powerful"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although(양보): 가장 큰 미행성끼리의 충돌은 ___하지만, '일어날 때는(when they occur)' 많은 파편을 방출한다.\nwhen they occur가 핵심 → 충돌이 '드물다'는 뜻이 대비를 이룬다.\n빈칸 = '드문'.\nexceptional(예외적인, 드문)과 rare(드문)가 같은 의미.\n정답: B (exceptional), E (rare)", "trap": "violent / powerful(격렬한)이 짝이지만, '격렬하지만 많은 파편을 방출한다'는 대비가 아니라 같은 방향이라 Although가 성립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"risky": "위험한", "exceptional": "예외적인, 드문", "irregular": "불규칙한", "violent": "격렬한", "rare": "드문", "powerful": "강력한"}, "src": "verbal25 Q6"}, {"id": "v233_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Like the detective, the biographer applies his or her powers of deduction and analysis to uncover new facts and to _____ known ones.", "choices": ["renounce", "reconstrue", "regiment", "reinterpret", "reject", "repudiate"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Like the detective: 탐정처럼 전기 작가는 추론과 분석을 적용해 새로운 사실을 밝히고, 알려진 사실을 ___한다.\n분석력으로 알려진 사실을 다루는 것 = '다시 해석하다'.\nreconstrue와 reinterpret가 같은 의미.\n정답: B (reconstrue), D (reinterpret)", "trap": "reject / repudiate / renounce는 '거부하다' 계열로 서로 비슷하지만, 탐정의 추론·분석은 사실을 거부하는 것이 아니라 새롭게 해석하는 것이다(또한 세 개라 정답 짝이 될 수 없다).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"renounce": "포기하다, 단념하다", "reconstrue": "재해석하다", "regiment": "엄격히 통제하다, 조직화하다", "reinterpret": "재해석하다", "reject": "거부하다", "repudiate": "부인하다, 거부하다"}, "src": "verbal233 Q7 · 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v9_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage would be most likely to agree with which of the following statements about Windes' argument?", "choices": ["It relies on evidence that is irrelevant to the examination of structures as large as Pueblo Bonito.", "It fails to acknowledge crucial evidence from great houses other than Pueblo Bonito.", "It fails to incorporate crucial evidence from excavations before the 1920s.", "It is based on a false notion about the significance of hearths.", "It is based on evidence that may be incomplete."], "columns": null, "pid": "v9_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Windes의 주장: 상층 화로가 3개뿐 → 상층은 주거용이 아니었다.\n저자: \"It is possible, however, that the collapse of upper-story floors disturbed evidence of upper-story hearths...\"\n또 초기 발굴이 바닥을 걷어내지 않아 \"may have concealed evidence of hearths in upper-story rooms.\"\n즉 Windes의 근거(화로 수)가 불완전할 수 있다는 것.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(화로의 의미에 대한 잘못된 생각)는 Windes의 전제를 공격하지만, 저자는 '주거엔 화로가 필요하다'는 전제는 문제 삼지 않고 증거의 불완전성만 지적한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"paucity": "부족, 결핍", "hearth": "화로, 난로", "remodeling": "개조", "disinclination": "내키지 않음, 꺼림"}, "src": "verbal9 Q10"}, {"id": "v9_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that Windes would be most likely to agree with which of the following statements about room usage in Pueblo Bonito?", "choices": ["Upper-story rooms were rarely used as storage areas.", "Rooms that were remodeled were most likely to have been residential rooms.", "The majority of residential rooms were located on the ground floor.", "Early excavations of Pueblo Bonito disturbed much of the evidence indicating room usage.", "Upper-story rooms with hearths were probably used for different purposes than were lower story rooms with hearths."], "columns": null, "pid": "v9_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Windes의 근거: 상층 화로 3개 vs 1층 화로 59개, \"habitation rooms would have required hearths for cooking and heat.\"\n주거실에는 화로가 필요 → 화로가 대부분 1층에 있다 → 주거실 대부분이 1층에 있었다.\nC가 이 추론을 그대로 담는다.\n정답: C", "trap": "D(초기 발굴이 증거를 훼손)는 저자의 반론 내용이지 Windes의 견해가 아니다. 그렇게 생각했다면 Windes는 화로 수를 근거로 쓰지 않았을 것이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"habitation": "거주", "hearth": "화로", "paucity": "부족", "excavation": "발굴"}, "src": "verbal9 Q11"}, {"id": "v9_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred about the excavation work performed by Judd's field crew?", "choices": ["It did not unearth many room features that existed prior to Chacoan remodeling.", "It did not unearth any evidence of upper-story hearths.", "It revealed only habitation rooms.", "It resulted in the collapse of some room features and upper-story floors.", "It confirmed traditional population estimates for Pueblo Bonito."], "columns": null, "pid": "v9_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"reliance on room features ... is complicated by the Chacoan's later remodeling, especially given Judd's disinclination to destroy later structures and features to expose earlier ones.\"\nJudd는 나중 구조물을 부수고 이전 구조를 드러내는 것을 꺼렸다 → 개조 이전의 방 특징들을 많이 발굴하지 못했다.\nA가 이를 정확히 패러프레이즈한다.\n정답: A", "trap": "B(상층 화로 증거를 하나도 못 찾았다)는 '숨겨졌을 수 있다'는 내용과 연결되어 끌리지만, 상층 화로 3개가 발견되었고 그것이 누구의 발굴인지 본문은 말하지 않으므로 'any'는 과하다. D는 붕괴의 원인을 발굴로 돌려 인과를 왜곡한다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"disinclination": "꺼림, 내키지 않음", "remodeling": "개조", "unearth": "발굴하다", "intact": "온전한"}, "src": "verbal9 Q12"}], [{"id": "v34_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Studies of hermaphroditic plants may exhibit sampling bias against self-fertilizing and cross-fertilizing species, thus inflating the frequency of species using a mixed mating system (both self-fertilizing and cross-fertilizing); nevertheless, the number of mixed-system species is not _____.", "choices": ["self-evident", "static", "trivial", "relevant", "calculable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 절: 표본 편향 때문에 혼합 교배 체계 종의 빈도가 '부풀려졌을(inflating)' 수 있다.\nnevertheless(그럼에도) → 부풀려졌다는 점을 감안해도, 그 수가 '무시할 정도는 아니다'.\n빈칸 = '하찮은, 사소한' (not ___ = 상당하다).\ntrivial이 정확히 들어맞는다.\n정답: C (trivial)", "trap": "static(정적인)이나 calculable(계산 가능한)은 '부풀려짐'과의 대비를 만들지 못한다. self-evident(자명한)도 nevertheless의 논리와 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"self-evident": "자명한", "static": "정적인, 고정된", "trivial": "사소한, 하찮은", "relevant": "관련 있는", "calculable": "계산 가능한"}, "src": "verbal34 Q1"}, {"id": "v206_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "It is often the case that a certain intellectual advantage may be found by being (i) _____ an established field of knowledge, but even if you accept the argument about the importance of (ii) _____ thinking, it is hardly the only significant thinking there is.", "choices": null, "columns": [["aware of trends in", "deeply indebted to", "on the periphery of"], ["intuitive", "arbitrary", "outsider"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 어떤 지적 이점은 기존 지식 분야의 (i)에 있음으로써 얻어진다 + but even if you accept the argument about the importance of (ii) thinking...\n(ii)는 (i)의 입장을 요약한 말이어야 한다 → 바깥에 있는 사람의 사고 = outsider thinking.\n그러면 (i)은 분야의 '주변부에' 있는 것 → on the periphery of.\n정답: C (on the periphery of), F (outsider)", "trap": "(i)의 deeply indebted to(크게 빚진)는 '내부자'의 위치라 outsider와 연결되지 않는다. (ii)의 intuitive(직관적)는 그럴듯하지만 (i)과의 논리적 연결이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"aware of trends in": "~의 동향을 아는", "deeply indebted to": "~에 크게 빚진", "on the periphery of": "~의 주변부에 있는", "intuitive": "직관적인", "arbitrary": "임의적인", "outsider": "외부자의"}, "src": "verbal206 Q2 · 25/8, 24/11, 24/9 중국후기"}, {"id": "v26_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Although the system for collecting data about user needs is called a \"customer capture method,\" this scientific-sounding terminology connotes greater (i) _____ than the method can deliver. While this terminology de-emphasizes the (ii) _____ aspects of knowledge management processes, such elements abound in the actual data collection.", "choices": null, "columns": [["neutrality", "range", "flexibility"], ["interpretive and evaluative", "innovative and economical", "frank and impartial"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'customer capture method'라는 과학적으로 들리는 용어는 방법이 실제로 제공하는 것보다 더 큰 ___을 암시한다.\n'과학적으로 들린다' → 객관성, 중립성을 연상시킴 → (i) neutrality.\n(ii) 이 용어는 ___ 측면을 덜 강조하지만, 실제 데이터 수집에는 그런 요소가 가득하다 → 중립성의 반대인 주관적 요소 → interpretive and evaluative(해석적이고 평가적인).\n정답: A (neutrality), D (interpretive and evaluative)", "trap": "(ii)의 frank and impartial(솔직하고 공정한)은 오히려 과학적 용어가 '강조하는' 측면이므로 de-emphasizes와 반대다. (i)의 range / flexibility는 '과학적'이라는 어감과 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"neutrality": "중립성", "range": "범위", "flexibility": "유연성", "interpretive and evaluative": "해석적이고 평가적인", "innovative and economical": "혁신적이고 경제적인", "frank and impartial": "솔직하고 공정한"}, "src": "verbal26 Q2"}, {"id": "v238_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "As theories, quantum field theory and theory of general relativity have been astonishingly (i) _____, in that no experiment yet has shown a crack in either of them, even though both of them (ii) _____ wildly counterintuitive properties in physical reality. And yet even proponents note that the two theories are (iii) _____, a fact that has disallowed theorists—at least so far—from incorporating both into a self-consistent theory of quantum gravity.", "choices": null, "columns": [["successful", "popular", "implausible"], ["downplay", "result in", "posit"], ["difficult for laypeople to understand", "deeply at odds with each other", "similar to earlier physical theories"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) in that 이하: 어떤 실험도 두 이론에 균열을 보여주지 못했다 → 놀라울 만큼 '성공적' → successful.\n(ii) even though: 반직관적인 성질을 '상정함'에도 불구하고 → 이론이 그런 성질을 가정한다 → posit.\n(iii) And yet + 두 이론을 하나의 자기일관적 이론으로 통합하지 못했다 → 서로 '근본적으로 충돌한다' → deeply at odds with each other.\n정답: A (successful), F (posit), H (deeply at odds with each other)", "trap": "(ii)의 result in(초래하다)은 '이론이 물리적 실재에 성질을 만들어낸다'가 되어 어색하다. (iii)의 difficult for laypeople to understand는 통합 불가의 이유가 될 수 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"successful": "성공적인", "popular": "인기 있는", "implausible": "믿기 어려운", "downplay": "경시하다", "result in": "초래하다", "posit": "상정하다, 가정하다", "difficult for laypeople to understand": "일반인이 이해하기 어려운", "deeply at odds with each other": "서로 근본적으로 상충하는", "similar to earlier physical theories": "이전 물리 이론과 유사한"}, "src": "verbal238 Q4 · 25년 8월, 24년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v22_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, those who challenge \"Meltzoff's interpretation\" do so on the basis that it", "choices": ["implies inaccurate predictions", "lacks testable consequences", "assumes a discredited theory", "leaves an unexplained gap", "involves circular reasoning"], "columns": null, "pid": "v22_p4", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Meltzoff의 해석: 신생아 모방이 이후(8~12개월) 모방의 기원이다.\n반론 근거: \"the neonatal imitative response disappears or is lessened at approximately two months.\"\n2개월에 사라졌다가 8~12개월에 다시 나타나므로, 그 사이의 공백이 설명되지 않는다.\n= 설명되지 않는 간극(unexplained gap).\n정답: D", "trap": "A(부정확한 예측)는 반론이 '예측이 틀렸다'고 보는 것 같아 끌리지만, 반론은 연속성의 단절(공백)을 문제 삼는다. 두 번째 반론(탐색 행동일 뿐)은 '해석' 자체가 아니라 모방 여부에 대한 것이다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "Meltzoff's interpretation", "glosses": {"neonatal": "신생아의", "protruding": "돌출된, 내민", "exploratory": "탐색적인", "stimuli": "자극(복수)"}, "src": "verbal22 Q14"}, {"id": "v22_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies which of the following about the experimental results reported by Meltzoff and Moore?", "choices": ["They were, at best, only partially borne out by subsequent studies.", "They cast doubt on the validity of a particular claim about newborns.", "They formed the basis for revised interpretation of other behaviors of newborns.", "They derived from a methodology that turned out to be flawed.", "They challenged the distinction between imitative and nonimitative behavior in newborns."], "columns": null, "pid": "v22_p4", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Meltzoff와 Moore: 신생아가 혀 내밀기, 입 벌리기 등 여러 표정을 모방할 수 있다고 보고.\n근거: \"in follow-up studies only one type of imitative response ... (that is, tongue protrusion) was observed\"\n후속 연구에서 한 가지만 확인됨 → 원래 결과는 기껏해야 부분적으로만 입증되었다.\n정답: A", "trap": "D(방법론이 결함이 있었다)는 너무 나간 진술이다. 본문은 후속 연구에서 일부만 재현되었다고 할 뿐, 방법론 결함을 말하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"borne out": "입증된, 뒷받침된", "follow-up": "후속의", "protrusion": "돌출, 내밀기", "neonatal": "신생아의"}, "src": "verbal22 Q15"}, {"id": "v220_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["discuss the defining characteristics of chondrites", "compare the spectrums of light reflected by chondrites and S-type asteroids", "chronicle changes in the accepted interpretation of data concerning the chemical composition of asteroids", "weigh evidence for and against a particular hypothesis on the origin of meteorites", "question a current theory on the chemical composition of the most common type of meteorite"], "columns": null, "pid": "v220_p7", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "가설: 운석은 소행성 조각이며, 특히 S형 소행성에서 온다.\n찬성 근거: S형은 콘드라이트와 같은 규산염을 포함하고, 지구로 오기 쉬운 내부 소행성대에 가장 많다.\n반대 근거: However, S형은 금속 함량이 더 높아 보인다 → 다른 소행성 기원설.\n재반박: However, 우주 풍화 때문에 그렇게 보일 수 있다.\n= 특정 가설에 대한 찬반 증거를 저울질함.\n정답: D", "trap": "C(해석의 변화를 연대기적으로 서술)는 가설-반론-재반론 흐름 때문에 끌리지만, 본문은 시간 순 변화가 아니라 증거의 찬반을 따진다. E는 콘드라이트 성분 이론을 의문시한다고 하여 초점이 틀렸다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"chondrite": "콘드라이트(운석의 한 종류)", "spectrum": "스펙트럼", "silicate": "규산염", "weathered": "풍화된"}, "src": "verbal220 Q7 · 25년 7월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage most likely mentions that the inner asteroid belt is \"the part of the asteroid belt from which objects are most likely to escape and travel to Earth\" in order to", "choices": ["distinguish between two important sources of meteorites that travel to Earth", "suggest that S-type asteroids are likely to be a source of meteorites", "call into question an assumption about the compounds that dominate chondrites", "explain why S-type asteroids do not reflect green, blue, and violet light as well as they reflect red and infrared light", "provide evidence to support an assertion about the abundance of S-type asteroids"], "columns": null, "pid": "v220_p7", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "이 구절은 S형 소행성이 '내부 소행성대에서 가장 많다'는 문장 안에 있다.\n내부 소행성대 = 지구로 오기 가장 쉬운 곳 → 그곳에 가장 많은 S형이 운석의 출처일 가능성이 높다.\n앞 문장(S형이 콘드라이트와 같은 성분)과 함께 S형 기원설을 지지하는 근거.\n정답: B", "trap": "E(S형의 풍부함을 뒷받침하는 증거)는 같은 문장에 abundant가 있어 끌리지만, 이 구절은 풍부함의 근거가 아니라 그 풍부함이 왜 운석 기원과 관련되는지를 보여준다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "the part of the asteroid belt from which objects are most likely to escape and travel to Earth", "glosses": {"asteroid belt": "소행성대", "escape": "벗어나다", "abundant": "풍부한", "S-type": "S형(규산염질)"}, "src": "verbal220 Q8 · 25년 7월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that one reason for considering S-type asteroids to be likely sources of meteorites is that S-type asteroids", "choices": ["are brighter than other types of asteroids", "are the most common type of asteroid throughout the asteroid belt", "reflect red and infrared light better than they reflect green, blue, and violet light", "contain the same silicates and other compounds that dominate chondrites", "are the only type of asteroid found in the inner asteroid belt"], "columns": null, "pid": "v220_p7", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: \"most of the brighter asteroids contain the same silicates and other compounds that dominate chondrites. These silicaceous, or S-type, asteroids...\"\n가장 흔한 운석(일반 콘드라이트)과 같은 성분 → S형이 운석의 출처일 가능성.\nD가 그대로 패러프레이즈한다.\n정답: D", "trap": "B는 '소행성대 전체에서' 가장 흔하다고 하지만 본문은 '내부 소행성대'에서 가장 흔하다고 한정한다. C의 빛 반사 특성은 오히려 반대 근거(금속 함량 차이)로 쓰였다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"silicaceous": "규산질의", "compound": "화합물", "dominate": "주를 이루다", "infrared": "적외선"}, "src": "verbal220 Q9 · 25년 7월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although automated agricultural technology boosts yields and profits, its high degree of prescriptiveness diminishes the role of individual farmers by making their _____ almost irrelevant.", "choices": ["diligence", "integrity", "judgment", "foresight", "discretion", "honesty"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although(양보): 자동화 농업 기술은 수확량·이익을 높이지만, 높은 '처방성(prescriptiveness)' 때문에 개별 농부의 역할이 줄어든다.\n기계가 무엇을 할지 다 정해 준다 → 농부의 '판단, 재량'이 거의 무의미해진다.\n빈칸 = 스스로 결정하는 능력.\njudgment와 discretion(재량, 분별)이 같은 의미.\n정답: C (judgment), E (discretion)", "trap": "integrity / honesty(정직)가 짝이지만, prescriptiveness(처방성)가 없애는 것은 도덕성이 아니라 결정 권한이다. foresight(선견지명)는 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"diligence": "근면, 성실", "integrity": "진실성, 고결함", "judgment": "판단력", "foresight": "선견지명", "discretion": "재량, 분별", "honesty": "정직"}, "src": "verbal220 Q12 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v202_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Researchers studying India's monsoon weather have evaluated more than 100 years of rain gauge data; _____ such information, South American scientists are forced to reconstruct centuries of monsoon history by analyzing lake-bottom sediment cores.", "choices": ["verifying", "lacking", "utilizing", "employing", "wanting", "confirming"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "대비: 인도 연구자들은 100년 이상의 우량계 데이터를 활용했다; 남미 과학자들은 퇴적물 코어 분석으로 '억지로(are forced to)' 몬순 역사를 재구성해야 한다.\nforced to → 그런 데이터가 '없어서'.\n빈칸 = '~이 없는, 부족한'.\nlacking과 wanting(형용사/분사: ~이 결여된)이 같은 의미.\n정답: B (lacking), E (wanting)", "trap": "utilizing / employing(활용하는)이 짝이지만 forced to(어쩔 수 없이)와 반대 논리다. wanting을 '원하는'으로만 알면 놓친다 — 여기서는 '~이 부족한'.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"verifying": "검증하는", "lacking": "~이 없는, 부족한", "utilizing": "활용하는", "employing": "사용하는", "wanting": "~이 결여된, 부족한", "confirming": "확인하는"}, "src": "verbal202 Q10 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v222_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although technically their members were hunter-gatherers, many early Native California communities exhibited traits more typically associated with well-developed agrarian societies and, therefore, are often presented in the ethnographic literature as _____.", "choices": ["archaic", "pragmatic", "anomalous", "exemplary", "exceptional", "utilitarian"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although technically 수렵채집인이었지만, 발달한 농경사회의 특징을 보였다 → 그러므로(therefore) 민족지 문헌에서 ___으로 소개된다.\n수렵채집 사회인데 농경사회 특징 → 일반 범주에서 벗어난 '예외적, 변칙적' 사례.\nanomalous(변칙적인)와 exceptional(예외적인)이 같은 의미.\n정답: C (anomalous), E (exceptional)", "trap": "exemplary(모범적인)는 exceptional과 비슷해 보이지만 '본보기가 될 만한'이라는 긍정 평가이지 '예외'가 아니다. archaic(고대의)도 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"archaic": "고대의, 낡은", "pragmatic": "실용적인", "anomalous": "변칙적인, 이례적인", "exemplary": "모범적인", "exceptional": "예외적인", "utilitarian": "실용적인, 공리주의의"}, "src": "verbal222 Q11 · 25/9, 25/8, 25/7, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v24_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true about Stanton, most seriously weakens the argument?", "choices": ["The number of automobile accidents has been declining in recent years.", "Since taxicabs are driven more miles annually than most other vehicles, they are more likely to be in an accident during any given year than is the average vehicle.", "There are more taxicabs in operation, relative to the overall number of motor vehicles, than there are in most cities of Stanton's size.", "The number of people, including the driver, who occupy a vehicle is generally greater for taxicabs than for other vehicles.", "Not all passengers in automobiles other than taxicabs use seat belts."], "columns": null, "pid": "v24_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 택시 승객에게 안전벨트를 의무화하면 사고당 부상자 수가 다른 차와 같아질 것이다.\n가정: 택시 사고의 부상자 수가 더 많은 이유는 (오직) 안전벨트 미착용 때문이다.\nD: 택시는 원래 탑승 인원(운전자 포함)이 더 많다 → 안전벨트와 무관하게 사고당 부상자 수가 많을 수 있다 → 대안 원인 제시로 결론 약화.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(택시는 사고 확률이 높다)는 '사고 횟수'에 관한 것이라 '사고당 부상자 수'라는 결론의 기준과 무관하다. E는 다른 차도 착용률이 100%가 아님을 말하지만 차이를 설명하지 못한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"weaken": "약화시키다", "occupy": "(차량에) 타다, 차지하다", "per accident": "사고당", "consistently": "일관되게"}, "src": "verbal24 Q11"}, {"id": "v202_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to Parker, when Hymes and Tedlock argued for the value of the Native American narratives, they based that claim on the value that the European tradition places on", "choices": ["poetry", "truth", "literature", "ideas", "narratives"], "columns": null, "pid": "v202_p4", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Hymes와 Tedlock은 \"by claiming to discover poetry as the true nature of Native American narrative and asserting the value of such narrative on that ground\"\n즉 원주민 서사가 '시(poetry)'라는 근거로 그 가치를 주장했다.\nParker는 이것이 유럽 전통의 가치 관념에 의존한 것이라 비판한다.\n정답: A (poetry)", "trap": "C(literature)는 Parker 자신의 입장(원주민 문학은 정전 문학에 필적)과 연결되어 헷갈리지만, Hymes와 Tedlock이 근거로 삼은 것은 '시'다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"oral narrative": "구전 서사", "canonical": "정전의", "validate": "인정하다, 정당화하다", "misconstrue": "잘못 이해하다"}, "src": "verbal202 Q14 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v202_q15", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage suggests that Parker would agree with which of the following statements about the work done by Hymes and Tedlock?", "choices": ["It made a significant contribution toward making Native Amenican narratives accessible to a broader readership.", "Some of its features might have been more vigorously questioned if it had appeared at a different time.", "It creates a misleading impression of Native American oral narratives in general because of the selections on which they chose to work."], "columns": null, "pid": "v202_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "B: Parker는 그들의 작업이 \"Romanticized ideas ... converged to create a surprisingly uncritical reception\"인 시기에 나왔다고 지적 → 다른 시기였다면 더 비판적으로 검토되었을 것 → O.\nA: 원주민 서사를 더 많은 독자에게 접근 가능하게 했다는 기여는 언급되지 않는다(groundbreaking만으로 독자층 확대를 추론할 수 없다) → X.\nC: 작품 '선정(selections)' 문제는 본문에 없다. Parker의 비판은 장르·가치 판단 방식에 대한 것 → X.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 'groundbreaking work'를 존중한다는 말 때문에 끌리지만, '더 넓은 독자층'이라는 구체적 기여는 본문 범위를 벗어난다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"groundbreaking": "획기적인", "uncritical": "무비판적인", "converge": "모이다, 수렴하다", "misconstrue": "잘못 해석하다"}, "src": "verbal202 Q15 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.8 / S2 3.0"}, {"set": 27, "sections": [[{"id": "v31_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The chairman, faced with the need to forge a consensus on a number of proposals, acknowledged that it would be difficult to reconcile the push for a radical overhaul with the stance of those who want _____ change.", "choices": ["deliberate", "indiscriminate", "genuine", "immediate", "wholesale"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심 단서: 'reconcile A with B' — A(radical overhaul, 급진적 전면 개혁)와 B가 조화시키기 어렵다 = 서로 반대 입장.\n빈칸 = radical의 반대, 즉 '천천히, 신중하게 진행되는' 변화.\ndeliberate는 '신중한, 서두르지 않는'이라는 뜻으로 급진적 개혁과 정확히 대비된다.\n정답: A (deliberate)", "trap": "wholesale(전면적인)·indiscriminate는 radical overhaul과 같은 방향이라 '조화시키기 어려운' 대립 구도가 성립하지 않는다. immediate도 급진 쪽에 가깝다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"deliberate": "신중한, 서두르지 않는; 의도적인", "indiscriminate": "무차별적인", "genuine": "진정한", "immediate": "즉각적인", "wholesale": "전면적인, 대대적인"}, "src": "verbal31 Q1"}, {"id": "v1_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "It is possible that the earliest terrestrial plants were (i) _____ natural enemies, such as herbivores. By the mid-Carboniferous period, however, there was abundant evidence—in the form of fossil leaves with signs of bite marks—that plants were (ii) _____ animal attack.", "choices": null, "columns": [["free from", "influenced by", "overwhelmed by"], ["experiencing", "avoiding", "exploiting"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'However, by the mid-Carboniferous...' — however로 초기와 후기를 대비. 후기에는 물린 자국(공격의 증거)이 있으므로, 초기 식물은 천적이 없었을 것 → free from.\n(ii) 잎의 bite marks = 식물이 동물의 공격을 '겪고 있었다'는 증거 → experiencing.\noverwhelmed by는 증거(물린 자국 있음)와 맞지만 however 대비가 깨지고, 지나치게 강하다.\n정답: A, D (free from / experiencing)", "trap": "(ii) avoiding은 bite marks라는 증거와 정반대. (i) influenced by는 however 대비 구조를 무너뜨린다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"free from": "~이 없는", "influenced by": "~의 영향을 받은", "overwhelmed by": "~에 압도된", "experiencing": "겪고 있는", "avoiding": "피하고 있는", "exploiting": "이용하고 있는"}, "src": "verbal1 Q2"}, {"id": "v31_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The perennial problem for critics of nineteenth-century novelist Charlotte Yonge is the relationship of her realism to her (i) _____. While admiring her complex psychological portraits and detailed descriptions of quotidian family life, readers since her own time have tended to fault her improbable manipulation of plot to teach a moral lesson. Indeed, many critics (ii) _____ her because of her willingness to (iii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["pessimism", "didacticism", "eclecticism"], ["dismiss", "applaud", "underestimate"], ["squander suspense", "sacrifice credibility", "deflate pretension"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 둘째 문장이 풀이: 사실적 묘사(realism)는 칭찬하지만 'manipulation of plot to teach a moral lesson'은 비판 → 교훈을 주려는 경향 = didacticism.\n(ii) 'readers... tended to fault her' + Indeed(강조·연속) → 부정적 평가 = dismiss(무시·일축하다).\n(iii) 교훈을 위해 '있을 법하지 않은(improbable)' 플롯 조작 → 사실성(credibility)을 희생 = sacrifice credibility.\n정답: B, D, H", "trap": "(ii) underestimate도 부정적이지만 '과소평가'는 그녀의 결함을 지적하는 맥락(fault)과 맞지 않는다. (iii) squander suspense는 단서(improbable)와 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pessimism": "비관주의", "didacticism": "교훈주의", "eclecticism": "절충주의", "dismiss": "일축하다, 무시하다", "applaud": "칭찬하다", "underestimate": "과소평가하다", "squander suspense": "긴장감을 낭비하다", "sacrifice credibility": "신빙성을 희생하다", "deflate pretension": "허세를 꺾다"}, "src": "verbal31 Q3"}, {"id": "v5_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author suggests that according to historical demographers, the birth rate in early-modern German cities", "choices": ["was affected by sanitary conditions", "increased as a result of in-migration", "was lower than the annual death rate", "decreased as population density increased", "was lower than the rate in communities with fewer than 10,000 inhabitants"], "columns": null, "pid": "v5_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'extremely high mortality rates in cities... meant that their populations could not be sustained by reproduction alone' (law of natural decrease).\n출생만으로 인구가 유지되지 못한다 = 출생률 < 사망률.\n또 'in-migration sufficient to overcome the population losses'도 같은 내용을 뒷받침.\n정답: C", "trap": "E: 소도시는 출생 ≥ 사망이라고만 했지 도시와 소도시의 출생률 자체를 비교한 적은 없다. B: 이민은 '인구'를 늘린 것이지 '출생률'을 높인 게 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"in-migration": "(국내) 인구 유입", "mortality": "사망률", "parish register": "교구 기록부", "sustain": "유지하다"}, "src": "verbal5 Q4"}, {"id": "v5_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that historical demographers generally believe which of the following about communities of fewer than 10,000 people in early-modern Germany?", "choices": ["Mortality rates were lower than those in cities of over 10,000 inhabitants.", "In-migrations were not a significant factor in population trends.", "Population levels remained quite stable for extended periods."], "columns": null, "pid": "v5_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "도시: 사망률이 극도로 높아 출생만으로 유지 불가(natural decrease 적용).\n소도시: 'the annual number of births usually equaled or exceeded that of deaths' → natural decrease가 적용되지 않는다고 봄.\n도시의 문제가 '극도로 높은 사망률'이었으므로, 학자들은 소도시의 사망률이 도시보다 낮았다고 본다고 추론 가능 → A.\nB(이민이 중요하지 않음), C(인구가 오래 안정)는 지문에 근거 없음.\n정답: A", "trap": "C: 출생 ≥ 사망이면 인구가 안정적일 것 같지만, 출생이 사망을 '초과'할 수도 있고 이주 등 다른 요인도 있어 '안정'까지는 추론 불가.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"law of natural decrease": "자연 감소의 법칙", "demographer": "인구통계학자", "sanitary": "위생의", "interrelated": "상호 연관된"}, "src": "verbal5 Q5"}, {"id": "v29_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although the claim that no one knows what dark matter is remains _____, some scientists dispute the parallel assertion that dark matter has not been detected.", "choices": ["contentious", "sound", "questionable", "unassailable", "unverifiable", "prominent"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although로 대비: 앞 주장은 ___한 상태로 남아 있지만, 뒤 '평행한 주장(parallel assertion)'은 일부 과학자들이 반박한다.\n따라서 빈칸 = '반박되지 않는, 타당한'이라는 긍정 의미.\nsound(타당한)와 unassailable(공격 불가한, 확고한)이 짝.\n정답: B, D (sound / unassailable)", "trap": "contentious·questionable은 dispute와 같은 방향이라 Although 대비가 사라진다. prominent는 혼자 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"contentious": "논쟁적인", "sound": "타당한, 건전한", "questionable": "의심스러운", "unassailable": "반박할 수 없는, 확고한", "unverifiable": "검증할 수 없는", "prominent": "두드러진, 저명한"}, "src": "verbal29 Q8"}, {"id": "v21_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "It's hardly __________ the committee calls for: rudimentary competence would be an improvement on the current chaos.", "choices": ["accountability", "disarray", "unruliness", "faultlessness", "loyalty", "perfection"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 앞 내용을 설명: '기초적인 능력만 있어도 현재의 혼란보다 나을 것'.\n즉 위원회가 요구하는 것은 '완벽함'이 아니라 최소한의 능력 → It's hardly ___ = 거창한 수준의 것이 아니다.\n빈칸 = 최고 수준, 흠잡을 데 없음 → faultlessness, perfection.\n정답: D, F", "trap": "disarray·unruliness는 'current chaos'와 연결되어 눈에 띄지만, 위원회가 '혼란'을 요구할 리 없다(짝은 되지만 의미가 반대). accountability는 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"competence": "능력", "disarray": "혼란, 무질서", "unruliness": "제멋대로임, 무질서", "accountability": "책임(성)", "faultlessness": "흠잡을 데 없음", "loyalty": "충성", "perfection": "완벽"}, "src": "verbal21 Q6"}, {"id": "v33_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "People enjoy listening to the governor’s inspiring speeches, and his eloquence lulls his adversaries into underestimating his _____, the tempered steel beneath the sleek suits.", "choices": ["tenacity", "resolve", "resourcefulness", "kindness", "compassion", "frankness"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "빈칸 뒤 동격 표현 'the tempered steel beneath the sleek suits'(매끈한 정장 밑의 단련된 강철)가 빈칸을 정의한다.\n유창한 연설(eloquence)에 속아 상대가 과소평가하는 것 = 강인한 의지, 끈기.\ntenacity(끈기)와 resolve(결의)가 짝.\n정답: A, B", "trap": "resourcefulness(수완)는 '얕보이는 장점'으로 그럴듯하지만 '강철' 이미지(굳셈, 굴하지 않음)와 맞지 않고 짝도 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tenacity": "끈기, 집요함", "resolve": "결의, 결단력", "resourcefulness": "수완, 기지", "kindness": "친절", "compassion": "연민", "frankness": "솔직함"}, "src": "verbal33 Q7"}, {"id": "v211_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The _____ of the folktales in this collection does not inhibit the conveyance of important lessons; indeed, the didactic effect would be lost if the stories were more protracted.", "choices": ["gaiety", "simplicity", "whimsy", "brevity", "sobriety", "economy"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'the didactic effect would be lost if the stories were more protracted(더 길어지면)'.\n세미콜론 + indeed로 앞 내용을 강화 → 빈칸 = protracted의 반대 = 짧음, 간결함.\nbrevity(짧음)와 economy(간결함, 절약)가 짝.\n정답: D, F", "trap": "simplicity(단순함)는 혼자 그럴듯하지만 '길이'에 대한 단서와 정확히 맞지 않고 짝도 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"gaiety": "명랑함", "simplicity": "단순함", "whimsy": "엉뚱함, 기발함", "brevity": "간결함, 짧음", "sobriety": "진지함, 냉철함", "economy": "(표현의) 간결함, 절약"}, "src": "verbal211 Q6 · 25년 6월, 23년 10월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v209_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["describe some adaptations of birds to environmental changes caused by humans", "challenge the role of brain size in birds' behavioral responses to potential threats", "argue that cognitive ability may be more useful than measures of escape behavior in predicting the survival of birds", "examine the link between brain size and escape behavior in birds", "explore a possible correlation between escape behavior and survival of birds encountering humans"], "columns": null, "pid": "v209_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문 흐름: FID 정의 → 새가 FID를 조정(인지 관여) → 'cognitive buffer' 가설(큰 뇌 = 적응 잘함) → 'negative association between FID and brain size' 예측.\n즉 뇌 크기와 도주 행동(escape behavior)의 관련성을 다루는 글.\n정답: D", "trap": "E: 도주 행동과 '생존'의 상관관계는 배경일 뿐 중심 초점은 '뇌 크기'다. B: 뇌 크기의 역할에 '도전'하는 게 아니라 그 역할을 제시한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"anthropogenic": "인간이 초래한", "habituate": "익숙해지다", "sensitize": "민감하게 하다", "stimulus": "자극"}, "src": "verbal209 Q10 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v209_q11", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following statements, if true, would confirm the prediction made in the final sentence of the passage?", "choices": ["Birds with larger brains tend to allow humans to approach more closely before fleeing than do smaller-brained birds.", "Birds of the same species tend to have the same FID regardless of brain size.", "Birds with smaller brains become habituated more quickly to the presence of humans than do larger-brained birds."], "columns": null, "pid": "v209_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "예측: FID와 뇌 크기의 '음의 상관관계' → 뇌가 클수록 FID(도망치는 거리)가 짧다.\nA: 큰 뇌의 새가 사람을 더 가까이 오도록 허용 = FID가 짧음 → 예측 확인.\nB: 같은 종 안에서 뇌 크기와 무관 → 'within species' 예측과 반대.\nC: 작은 뇌가 더 빨리 적응 → 가설과 반대.\n정답: A", "trap": "C: habituate라는 지문 단어를 써서 끌리지만, 큰 뇌가 더 잘 학습한다는 가설과 방향이 반대다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "If so, one would predict that there would be a negative association between FID and brain size within and across species.", "glosses": {"negative association": "음의 상관관계", "flee": "도망치다", "habituated": "익숙해진"}, "src": "verbal209 Q11 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v209_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that birds with an invariably long FID are", "choices": ["likely to adapt effectively to anthropogenic landscape change", "less likely to accurately judge risk in anthropogenic environments", "unlikely to flee approaching humans so long as the humans approach slowly", "more likely to flee an approaching vehicle than a person on foot", "likely to benefit from interactions with humans"], "columns": null, "pid": "v209_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문: 큰 뇌의 새는 위험을 정확히 판단하고, 경험에 따라 반응을 'adjust responses appropriately' 조정한다.\n'invariably long FID'(항상 먼 거리에서 도망) = 상황에 따라 FID를 조정하지 못함 = 위험 판단이 부정확.\n따라서 인간이 만든 환경에서 위험을 정확히 판단할 가능성이 낮다.\n정답: B", "trap": "A: 조정 못하는 새는 오히려 적응을 잘 못한다(반대). D: 차량 vs 보행자 구분은 '항상 같은 FID'와 모순된다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"invariably": "변함없이, 항상", "discriminate": "구별하다", "mediation": "조절, 중재"}, "src": "verbal209 Q12 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v28_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Among the Meakambut people of Papua New Guinea, legends are associated with specific caves in the Sepik region, and these legends are _____: only the cave owner can share its secrets.", "choices": ["impenetrable", "immutable", "proprietary", "didactic", "self-perpetuating"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 설명: 'only the cave owner can share its secrets'(동굴 주인만 비밀을 공유할 수 있다).\n빈칸 = 특정 사람에게 소유권이 있는 → proprietary.\n정답: C (proprietary)", "trap": "impenetrable(이해할 수 없는)은 '비밀'과 연결돼 끌리지만, 핵심은 '소유자만 공유 가능'이라는 소유 관계다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"proprietary": "소유권이 있는, 독점적인", "impenetrable": "이해할 수 없는, 뚫을 수 없는", "immutable": "불변의", "didactic": "교훈적인", "self-perpetuating": "자기 영속적인"}, "src": "verbal28 Q1"}, {"id": "v198_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The enthusiasm for dancing in New Zealand during the 1920s and 1930s to some extent (i) _____ in both the United States and Britain, where new dance halls (ii) _____ in response to customer demand, although the rampant commercialization associated with larger populations in the United States was not so apparent in New Zealand.", "choices": null, "columns": [["heralded its decline", "bucked trends", "mirrored its popularity"], ["foundered", "burgeoned", "rebounded"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 뉴질랜드의 춤 열풍이 'in both the US and Britain'에서의 상황과 '어느 정도(to some extent)' 같았다 → mirrored its popularity. 뒤의 'although ... not so apparent in New Zealand'가 '부분적 유사, 일부 차이'를 확인.\n(ii) 'in response to customer demand' → 댄스홀이 급증 = burgeoned.\n정답: C, E", "trap": "(i) bucked trends는 although 뒤 차이점에 끌리지만 그건 상업화의 차이일 뿐 열풍 자체는 같았다. (ii) rebounded는 이전 쇠퇴에 대한 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"bucked trends": "흐름을 거슬렀다", "heralded its decline": "쇠퇴를 예고했다", "mirrored its popularity": "인기를 그대로 반영했다", "foundered": "실패했다, 무너졌다", "burgeoned": "급증했다, 번성했다", "rebounded": "회복했다, 반등했다"}, "src": "verbal198 Q2 · 25/2, 24/7, 24/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "It is true that with too much exposure, one can weary of visionary poems; their rhetoric can become (i) _____. And yet, there are few among us who are completely (ii) _____ visionary rhetoric for the obvious reason that we do, on rare occasions, have an experience that (iii) _____ and leaves us baffled, deeply moved, and ready to believe things we hadn't dreamed of.", "choices": null, "columns": [["engaging", "insufferable", "prescient"], ["immune to", "immersed in", "comfortable with"], ["passes by unnoticed", "lifts us out of the ordinary", "fits all expectations"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'with too much exposure, one can weary of' → 과하면 싫증 → 수사가 참을 수 없게 됨 = insufferable.\n(ii) 'And yet' 반전 → 그래도 완전히 영향을 받지 않는 사람은 거의 없다 = immune to.\n(iii) 그 이유: 드물게 우리를 당황시키고 깊이 감동시키는 경험 → 일상에서 벗어나게 함 = lifts us out of the ordinary.\n정답: B, D, H", "trap": "(ii) comfortable with는 앞의 '싫증'과 연결돼 끌리지만, 'few among us are completely ___' 구조에서 의미가 맞지 않는다. (iii) fits all expectations는 'baffled'와 모순.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"weary of": "싫증이 나다", "insufferable": "참을 수 없는", "prescient": "선견지명이 있는", "engaging": "매력적인", "immune to": "~에 영향을 받지 않는", "immersed in": "~에 몰두한", "comfortable with": "~이 편한", "passes by unnoticed": "눈치채지 못하게 지나가다", "lifts us out of the ordinary": "일상에서 벗어나게 하다", "fits all expectations": "모든 기대에 부합하다"}, "src": "verbal232 Q4 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v14_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "A certain (i) _____ governs the way most of us think about routines. A routine is sometimes conceived as constraining—a self-made prison of inflexible habits that prevent people from changing their lives. But routine is also seen as (ii) _____: activities that become routine (iii) _____, allowing us to expend energy on other things.", "choices": null, "columns": [["pessimism", "misunderstanding", "polarity"], ["liberating", "alterable", "unintentional"], ["are often tedious", "demand less attention", "encourage personal discipline"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CDH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 뒤에서 루틴을 두 가지 정반대로 봄: 'constraining'(구속) vs 'But... also' 다른 관점 → 양극성 = polarity.\n(ii) constraining(감옥)의 반대 → liberating(해방시키는).\n(iii) 'allowing us to expend energy on other things' → 루틴이 된 활동은 주의를 덜 요구 = demand less attention.\n정답: C, D, H", "trap": "(i) misunderstanding은 그럴듯하지만, 지문은 두 관점을 '오해'로 평가하지 않고 대립만 제시한다. (iii) encourage personal discipline은 '에너지를 다른 데 쓴다'와 연결되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pessimism": "비관주의", "misunderstanding": "오해", "polarity": "양극성, 정반대 성향", "liberating": "해방시키는", "alterable": "바꿀 수 있는", "unintentional": "의도치 않은", "are often tedious": "종종 지루하다", "demand less attention": "주의를 덜 요구하다", "encourage personal discipline": "자기 단련을 장려하다"}, "src": "verbal14 Q3"}, {"id": "v228_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about Chopin?", "choices": ["He wrote more scherzos and sonatas than did other composers of his generation.", "He has a better reputation today than he had prior to the twentieth century.", "He was less interested in such genres as nocturnes, mazurkas, and waltzes than was once assumed.", "His reputation as a miniaturist was regarded by other composers of his time as misleading.", "His ability to write large works declined after the age of twenty-one."], "columns": null, "pid": "v228_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'This view of Chopin (miniaturist), which remained orthodox into the later twentieth century, is now largely discredited.'\n20세기 이전부터 그를 '소품 작곡가'로 낮게 보던 견해가 이제는 부정됨 → 오늘날 평판이 더 좋다.\n정답: B", "trap": "D: '당대 다른 작곡가들'이 그 평가를 오해라고 봤다는 말은 없다(현재의 평가). A: 다른 작곡가보다 '더 많이' 썼다는 수치 비교는 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"facile": "안이한, 깊이 없는", "miniaturist": "소품 작곡가(작가)", "orthodox": "정설의", "discredited": "신빙성을 잃은", "efficacy": "효과"}, "src": "verbal228 Q14 · 24년 7월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v228_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author would most likely agree with which of the following statements about Berlioz and Liszt?", "choices": ["Their longer works are generally less successful than their shorter ones.", "Their works rarely achieve the elegance of Chopin's best nocturnes.", "Their large works are not as consistent as are the large works of Chopin.", "Their compositions show that they borrowed from Chopin but not very successfully.", "Their compositions have more in common with music that has been considered miniaturist than many critics have recognized."], "columns": null, "pid": "v228_p4", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'deserts with few oases in a number of works of Berlioz; not many works of Liszt are completely exempt from some facile pages.'\n즉 그들의 큰 작품에는 약한 부분이 섞여 있음 → 고르지 않다.\n반면 Chopin은 'never... wrote a long piece that was ineffective' → 대형 작품이 일관되게 성공적.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 그들의 긴 작품이 '짧은 작품보다' 못하다는 비교는 지문에 없다. B: 녹턴과의 비교도 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exempt from": "~에서 면제된", "facile": "안이한, 피상적인", "oasis": "오아시스(좋은 부분)", "consistent": "일관된"}, "src": "verbal228 Q15 · 24년 7월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary concern of the passage is to", "choices": ["articulate objections to a new hypothesis", "support widely held hypotheses with new evidence", "reconcile seemingly incompatible hypotheses", "provide evidence against some widely held hypotheses", "summarize the evidence for a long-held hypothesis"], "columns": null, "pid": "v240_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "지문은 두 가설을 반박: (1) 'widely held hypothesis that lichen-forming fungi are a closely knit, peripheral group' — DNA 결과 서로보다 비지의류 곰팡이와 더 가까움. (2) 'long-standing hypothesis' 공생이 해로움→상호이익 순서로 진화 — 'These considerations undermine'.\n= 널리 받아들여진 가설들에 반하는 증거 제시.\n정답: D", "trap": "A: 반박 대상은 '새로운' 가설이 아니라 오래되고 널리 받아들여진 가설이다. B는 방향이 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"symbiotic": "공생의", "peripheral": "주변적인", "closely knit": "긴밀하게 결합된", "undermine": "약화시키다", "benign": "무해한"}, "src": "verbal240 Q7 · 25/8, 25/7, 25/5, 25/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author refers to \"harmful parasites on lichens themselves\" in order to", "choices": ["suggest the effects of lichen-forming fungi on algae with which they live symbiotically", "indicate the prevalence of symbiotic relationships across a wide variety of species", "describe the evolutionary origins of lichen-forming fungi", "provide evidence against the hypothesis described in the second sentence of the passage", "provide evidence against the hypothesis described in the final sentence of the passage"], "columns": null, "pid": "v240_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "마지막 문장의 가설: 공생은 '해로운 관계 → 상호 이익 관계' 순서로 진화한다.\n그런데 지의류 형성 곰팡이(상호 이익 공생)가 지의류에 '해로운 기생체'를 낳은 것으로 보임 → 이익→해로움 방향의 진화도 존재.\n그래서 'These considerations undermine...' 마지막 문장 가설에 대한 반증.\n정답: E", "trap": "D: 둘째 문장 가설(긴밀한 주변 그룹)은 DNA 비교로 반박되며, 기생체 이야기는 진화 '방향'에 관한 것이라 마지막 가설에 해당한다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "harmful parasites on lichens themselves", "glosses": {"parasite": "기생체", "orderly progression": "질서 있는 진행", "give rise to": "~을 낳다", "malignant": "해로운, 악성의"}, "src": "verbal240 Q8 · 25/8, 25/7, 25/5, 25/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following statements about lichen-forming fungi can be inferred from the passage?", "choices": ["Some of the evolutionary ancestors of these kinds of fungi probably were involved in symbiotic relationships that were not mutually beneficial.", "Some of these kinds of fungi are now involved in symbiotic relationships that are harmful to lichens themselves.", "These kinds of fungi probably are relatively distant relations of certain disease-causing fungi.", "These kinds of fungi probably have evolved from fungi that are parasitic on lichens themselves.", "These kinds of fungi are probably more closely related to each other than to non-lichen-forming fungi."], "columns": null, "pid": "v240_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'lichen-forming fungi probably evolved from various species whose effects on associated organisms ranged from benign to malignant'.\n조상 중 일부는 연관 생물에 해를 끼쳤음(malignant) → 상호 이익이 아닌 공생 관계에 있었다.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 지의류에 해로운 것은 지의류 형성 곰팡이에서 '생겨난 다른 곰팡이'이지 그들 자신이 아니다. D는 진화 방향을 거꾸로 했고, E는 지문과 정반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"benign": "무해한, 이로운", "malignant": "해로운", "evolutionary ancestor": "진화상의 조상", "mutually beneficial": "상호 이익의"}, "src": "verbal240 Q9 · 25/8, 25/7, 25/5, 25/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v2_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The rebellion was _____ one, driven less by ardor than by reason and calculation.", "choices": ["a cerebral", "a dispassionate", "a rash", "an idealistic", "a cautious", "a reckless"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "쉼표 뒤 설명: 'driven less by ardor(열정) than by reason and calculation(이성과 계산)'.\n빈칸 = 감정이 아닌 이성 중심 → cerebral(지적인, 이성적인), dispassionate(냉정한).\n정답: A, B", "trap": "cautious(신중한)는 'calculation'과 연결돼 끌리지만, 핵심은 '감정 vs 이성' 대비이지 '신중함'이 아니며 짝도 없다. rash·reckless는 서로 짝이지만 의미가 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cerebral": "지적인, 이성적인", "dispassionate": "냉정한, 감정에 치우치지 않는", "rash": "경솔한", "idealistic": "이상주의적인", "cautious": "신중한", "reckless": "무모한"}, "src": "verbal2 Q10"}, {"id": "v200_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The museum's display of bandolier bags made by Ojibwa artists of the Mille Lacs community reinforces the idea that this community's culture is _____ one: early twentieth-century bandolier bags are displayed alongside others made recently.", "choices": ["a historic", "an inventive", "an unfolding", "a living", "a resourceful", "a unique"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 근거: 20세기 초 가방과 '최근에 만든' 가방을 함께 전시.\n→ 이 문화가 과거에 멈춘 것이 아니라 지금도 계속 이어지고 발전 중 = 살아 있는, 전개 중인.\nunfolding과 living이 짝.\n정답: C, D", "trap": "historic은 '20세기 초' 가방에 끌리지만, 최근 작품이 함께 있다는 점(현재 진행)을 반영하지 못한다. inventive·resourceful은 짝처럼 보이나 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"historic": "역사적인", "inventive": "창의적인", "unfolding": "전개되고 있는", "living": "살아 있는, 현존하는", "resourceful": "수완 있는", "unique": "독특한"}, "src": "verbal200 Q12 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v18_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Family photos of the author suggest that she was __________ child: she seemed to wear a permanent frown.", "choices": ["a sullen", "an amiable", "a surly", "a beautiful", "a prudent", "a stunning"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론 뒤 설명: 'she seemed to wear a permanent frown(늘 찡그린 얼굴)'.\n빈칸 = 시무룩하고 뚱한 성격 → sullen, surly.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "beautiful·stunning은 사진이라는 맥락에 끌리는 짝이지만 frown 단서와 무관하다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sullen": "시무룩한, 뚱한", "surly": "퉁명스러운, 무뚝뚝한", "amiable": "상냥한", "beautiful": "아름다운", "prudent": "신중한", "stunning": "매우 아름다운"}, "src": "verbal18 Q8"}, {"id": "v202_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following is an assumption on which the editorial’s argument depends?", "choices": ["The unemployment rate is higher in Torre City than in Glanville.", "The unemployment rate in Torre City is higher now than it has ever been.", "Since making the prediction a year ago, the government of Portran has taken no steps to improve job growth in the country.", "Few, if any, unemployed people moved to Torre City from Glanville during the year.", "Government predictions about the economy in Portran are generally not reliable."], "columns": null, "pid": "v202_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 정부 예측(Torre City 순고용 증가)은 틀렸다. 근거: Torre City의 실업자 '수'가 1년 전보다 늘었다.\n빈틈: 실업자 수는 일자리 감소가 아니라 '실업자 유입'으로도 늘 수 있다.\nD: Glanville에서 Torre City로 실업자가 거의 이주하지 않았다 → 이 대안 설명을 차단하는 필수 가정(부정하면 논증 붕괴).\n정답: D", "trap": "A: 두 도시의 실업률 '수준' 비교는 논증과 무관하다(논증은 각 도시의 변화량에 대한 것). E: 예측 전반의 신뢰성은 필요 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"net job growth": "순 일자리 증가", "assumption": "가정", "unemployment rate": "실업률"}, "src": "verbal202 Q13 · 24년 10월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v226_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies that Turner's conclusion regarding the origins of most Native American populations is based in part on which of the following findings?", "choices": ["The presence of Sundadonty among prehistoric American populations", "The prevalence of shovel-shaped incisors among Native Americans", "The absence of Sinodonty among people from southern Asia, Africa, and Europe"], "columns": null, "pid": "v226_p1", "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Turner의 결론: 대부분 아메리카 원주민의 기원은 북동아시아. 근거: Sinodonty(삽 모양 앞니 포함)가 대부분 원주민과 북동아시아인에게 공유됨.\nB: 'shovel-shaped incisors'는 Sinodonty의 특징 → 근거.\nC: 'not found in people who originated in southern Asia, Africa, or Europe' → 다른 지역 기원을 배제하는 근거.\nA: Sundadonty는 오히려 결론에 불리한 사실('but Turner believes...').\n정답: B, C", "trap": "A: 지문에 나온 사실이지만 'but'로 Turner가 그것에도 불구하고 결론을 유지했음을 보여주므로 근거가 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dentition": "치열", "incisor": "앞니", "molar": "어금니", "prehistoric": "선사 시대의"}, "src": "verbal226 Q5 · 24년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v226_q6", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, Sinodonty and Sundadonty differ from one another in that Sinodonty", "choices": ["has been found among prehistoric Native American populations, while Sundadonty has not", "is a more complex dental pattern than Sundadonty is", "occurs frequently in modern Native American populations, while Sundadonty does not"], "columns": null, "pid": "v226_p1", "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "B: Sundadonty는 'Another less complex pattern' → Sinodonty가 더 복잡 (명시).\nC: Sinodonty는 'shared among most Native Americans'인 반면, Sundadonty는 동남아시아인에게 공유되고 '선사 시대' 아메리카 집단에서 발견된다고만 함 → 현대 원주민에게는 흔하지 않다는 대비.\nA: Sundadonty도 'also found in prehistoric American populations' → 틀림.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "A: Sinodonty가 선사 시대 원주민에게 있다는 점은 맞지만, 'Sundadonty는 없다'는 부분이 지문과 정면으로 모순된다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"complex": "복잡한", "prevalence": "널리 퍼짐", "originate": "기원하다"}, "src": "verbal226 Q6 · 24년 6월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.8 / S2 3.0"}, {"set": 28, "sections": [[{"id": "v237_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Solitary birds must be more _____ than those in a flock, constantly interrupting valuable feeding time to scan for predators.", "choices": ["omnivorous", "aggressive", "vocal", "vigilant", "peripatetic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "쉼표 뒤 설명: 'constantly interrupting valuable feeding time to scan for predators'(포식자를 살피려 계속 먹이 활동을 중단).\n빈칸 = 늘 경계하는 → vigilant.\n정답: D (vigilant)", "trap": "peripatetic(돌아다니는)이나 aggressive는 새의 행동처럼 들리지만 '포식자를 살핀다'는 단서와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"omnivorous": "잡식성의", "aggressive": "공격적인", "vocal": "소리를 많이 내는", "vigilant": "경계하는, 방심하지 않는", "peripatetic": "여기저기 돌아다니는"}, "src": "verbal237 Q1 · 25년 12월, 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v197_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The overall message of this book on neuroscience is (i) _____: the brain is quite (ii) _____, and therefore damaged brains can be healed, aging brains can be rejuvenated, and even ordinarily healthy brains can be made faster and better.", "choices": null, "columns": [["enigmatic", "cautious", "upbeat"], ["malleable", "fragile", "complex"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 'and therefore damaged brains can be healed, aging brains can be rejuvenated...' → 뇌가 변화·개선 가능해야 함 = malleable(가소성 있는).\n(i) 치유·회춘·향상이 가능하다는 메시지 = 낙관적 → upbeat.\n정답: C, D", "trap": "(ii) complex는 뇌에 대해 흔히 쓰지만 '그러므로 치유 가능하다'는 결과로 이어지지 않는다. (i) cautious는 낙관적 내용과 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"enigmatic": "수수께끼 같은", "cautious": "신중한", "upbeat": "낙관적인, 긍정적인", "malleable": "가소성 있는, 잘 변하는", "fragile": "취약한", "complex": "복잡한"}, "src": "verbal197 Q2 · 24/2, 23/8, 23/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v205_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Scholars and journalists interested in the ideology of rock music have rightly noted that Romanticism and Modernism provided rock with an aesthetic morality (i) _____ commercialism. However, while openly expressing (ii) _____ mass culture, rock has exhibited a remarkable capacity to (iii) _____ it, calling the genre's subversive image into question.", "choices": null, "columns": [["deeply opposed to", "largely determined by", "generally compatible with"], ["interest in", "solidarity with", "disdain for"], ["grow without", "thrive in", "rail against"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 낭만주의·모더니즘이 준 '미학적 도덕' + 뒤의 'subversive image' → 상업주의에 반대 = deeply opposed to.\n(ii) 'openly expressing ___ mass culture' → 같은 반상업적 태도 = disdain for.\n(iii) 'while... however'로 대비 + 'calling the genre's subversive image into question' → 겉으로는 경멸하지만 실제로는 대중문화 속에서 번성 = thrive in.\n정답: A, F, H", "trap": "(iii) rail against(비난하다)는 disdain과 같은 방향이라 while의 대비가 사라지고 '전복적 이미지에 의문'이 생기지 않는다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"deeply opposed to": "~에 깊이 반대하는", "largely determined by": "~에 의해 크게 좌우되는", "generally compatible with": "~와 대체로 양립하는", "interest in": "~에 대한 관심", "solidarity with": "~와의 연대", "disdain for": "~에 대한 경멸", "grow without": "~없이 성장하다", "thrive in": "~속에서 번성하다", "rail against": "~을 맹비난하다"}, "src": "verbal205 Q3 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v231_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The highlighted sentence performs which of the following function in the passage?", "choices": ["It helps explain how tunnels built for trains differ from those built primarily for automobiles.", "It points out some of the advantages of bored tunnel technology.", "It lists several attributes of immersed tube tunnels that support the previous sentence's assertion.", "It emphasizes the extent to which unanticipated delays can add to a project's cost.", "It introduces evidence that challenges certain claims about bored tunnels made earlier in the passage."], "columns": null, "pid": "v231_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: immersed tubes는 'generally faster and less expensive to build than traditional bored tunnels'.\n하이라이트 문장은 'To begin with'로 시작해 그 근거를 나열: 한 구간 문제로 전체가 지연되지 않음(더 빠름), 사각 단면이 더 효율적.\n= 앞 문장의 주장을 뒷받침하는 immersed tube의 특성 나열.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 철도 노선 언급이 있지만 기차용 vs 자동차용 터널 비교는 없다. B: bored tunnel이 아니라 immersed tube의 장점이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"immersed": "물속에 잠긴", "bored tunnel": "굴착 터널", "prefabricated": "미리 제작된", "cross-section": "단면", "gradient": "경사"}, "src": "verbal231 Q4 · 25/9, 24/11, 22/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v231_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that which of the following is characteristic of bored tunnels?", "choices": ["They are the preferred option for crossing shallower spans of water.", "Their stability suffers if they are not built deeply enough.", "The shape of their cross-sections cannot be rectangular."], "columns": null, "pid": "v231_p1", "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "B: 'bored tunnels are usually considered stable only if their depth under the seabed at least equals their diameter' → 충분히 깊지 않으면 안정성이 떨어진다.\nC: 'because immersed tubes CAN have a rectangular cross-section, they are a more efficient shape than circular tunnels' → 사각 단면이 immersed tube만의 장점 = bored tunnel은 원형(사각 불가).\nA: 얕은 곳에서는 오히려 immersed tube가 유리(shallower approach gradients).\n정답: B, C", "trap": "A: 지문의 마지막 문장은 얕은 곳에서 immersed tube가 유리하다는 뜻이므로 정반대다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"stability": "안정성", "diameter": "지름", "span": "(다리·터널의) 구간, 폭"}, "src": "verbal231 Q5 · 25/9, 24/11, 22/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v217_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Despite much _____ the country's political system, the fact that supporters failed in their attempts to change the constitution to allow the President to run again speaks well of the system's fundamental strengths.", "choices": ["faith in", "confidence in", "frustration regarding", "skepticism regarding", "hesitation toward", "doubt about"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Despite로 대비: 체제의 근본적 강점을 보여주는 사실 '에도 불구하고' → 빈칸 = 체제에 대한 부정적 태도.\n'강점'과 대비되려면 체제가 튼튼한지 '의심'하는 것 → skepticism regarding, doubt about.\n정답: D, F", "trap": "frustration regarding(좌절)도 부정적이지만 '강점이 있다'와 논리적으로 대비되는 것은 '의심'이며 frustration은 짝이 없다. faith·confidence는 짝이지만 Despite와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"faith in": "~에 대한 신뢰", "confidence in": "~에 대한 확신", "frustration regarding": "~에 대한 좌절", "skepticism regarding": "~에 대한 회의", "hesitation toward": "~에 대한 망설임", "doubt about": "~에 대한 의심"}, "src": "verbal217 Q6 · 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v227_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Fungi are a basic component of every ecosystem, and their importance cannot be _____, but mycologists generally lack an understanding of which fungi are present in oceans and what roles they play.", "choices": ["gainsaid", "underestimated", "calculated", "disputed", "exaggerated", "matched"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞: 곰팡이는 모든 생태계의 기본 요소 → 그 중요성은 ___할 수 없다 = 부정할 수 없다.\nbut 이하(해양 곰팡이 이해 부족)는 중요성과 대비되는 현실.\ngainsaid(부인되다)와 disputed(반박되다)가 짝.\n정답: A, D", "trap": "underestimated와 exaggerated는 각각 'cannot be ~ed'로 관용적으로 쓰이지만 서로 반대 의미라 짝이 되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"gainsaid": "부인된, 반박된", "underestimated": "과소평가된", "calculated": "계산된", "disputed": "반박된, 이의가 제기된", "exaggerated": "과장된", "matched": "필적된"}, "src": "verbal227 Q8 · 24년 3월, 23년 2월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v17_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The campaign official argued that the large swings in the candidate's approval ratings were a result not of the ___________ of the electorate but rather of the polls' margins of error and divergent methodologies.", "choices": ["exactitude", "resurgence", "capriciousness", "volatility", "partisanship", "scrupulousness"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'not of A but rather of B' 구조: 지지율의 큰 변동(large swings)은 유권자의 A 때문이 아니라 여론조사 오차 때문.\nA = 큰 변동을 설명할 수 있는 유권자의 특성 = 변덕스러움.\ncapriciousness(변덕)와 volatility(변동성)가 짝.\n정답: C, D", "trap": "partisanship(당파성)은 선거 맥락에 그럴듯하지만 '급격한 변동'을 설명하지 못한다. exactitude·scrupulousness는 짝이지만 의미가 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"resurgence": "부활, 재기", "scrupulousness": "꼼꼼함, 양심적임", "exactitude": "정확성", "capriciousness": "변덕스러움", "volatility": "변동성, 변덕", "partisanship": "당파성"}, "src": "verbal17 Q8"}, {"id": "v213_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Because the chemical and physical properties of a material are a function of its structure, the enhanced three-dimensional results derived from a crystallographic study have become _____ the overall characterization of any new material.", "choices": ["consistent with", "dependent on", "determined by", "peripheral to", "indispensable to", "vital to"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "EF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Because절: 물질의 성질은 구조의 함수다 → 구조를 밝히는 결정학 연구 결과는 물질 특성 분석에 '필수적'이 됨.\n빈칸 = 매우 중요한 → indispensable to, vital to.\n정답: E, F", "trap": "dependent on·determined by는 짝처럼 보이지만 인과 방향이 반대(결과가 특성 분석에 의존하는 게 아니라 특성 분석이 결과에 의존). peripheral to는 반대 의미.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"consistent with": "~와 일치하는", "dependent on": "~에 의존하는", "determined by": "~에 의해 결정되는", "peripheral to": "~에 주변적인", "indispensable to": "~에 필수적인", "vital to": "~에 매우 중요한"}, "src": "verbal213 Q8 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v203_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["argue that Manet was relatively slow to adopt the newest approaches to painting", "illustrate the authority that Manet's example had with the artists of his time", "situate Manet's choice of subject within the context of contemporary trends", "compare the poses used in Manet's 《Le Bain》 with those found in two of his earlier paintings", "emphasize the influence of Manet's teacher on nineteenth-century painting"], "columns": null, "pid": "v203_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "글의 흐름: Le Bain의 '현대 복장' 논란 → 당시 현대인 그림은 드묾(Stendhal의 권고, Meissonier의 과거 장면) → 스승 Couture의 권고 → Manet가 점차 현대 주제로 전환.\n= Manet의 주제 선택을 당대 경향 속에 위치시키는 글.\n정답: C", "trap": "E: Couture의 영향은 맥락 설명의 일부일 뿐, 19세기 회화 전반에 대한 영향을 강조하지 않는다. A: '느렸다'는 평가적 주장은 하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tableau": "(극적인) 장면 그림", "convert": "전향자", "appropriate": "차용하다, 도용하다", "idyllic": "목가적인"}, "src": "verbal203 Q10 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v203_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The \"advice\" referred to in the passage is to", "choices": ["avoid idealized subjects", "develop one's technique by copying approved works", "draw inspiration from works of old masters", "choose subjects contemporary with the artist", "use one's artistic imagination"], "columns": null, "pid": "v203_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'Manet had begun paying heed to the advice of his teacher' — 그 앞 문장: Couture가 학생들에게 'take as the subjects of their own paintings contemporary sights such as workmen, public holidays...'를 권고.\n= 동시대의 주제를 선택하라.\n정답: D", "trap": "B·C: Couture가 옛 거장 작품을 '모사하게' 한 것도 사실이지만, 그것은 '요구(required)'였고 Manet가 새로 따르기 시작한 advice는 현대 주제 쪽이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "advice", "glosses": {"pay heed to": "~에 주의를 기울이다", "contemporary": "동시대의", "idealized": "이상화된"}, "src": "verbal203 Q11 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v203_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies which of the following about Thomas Couture's painting 《The Romans of the Decadence》?", "choices": ["Its renown had faded by the time Manet began to study with Couture.", "It was admired less than some of Meissonier's paintings and probably was not idyllic.", "Its subject probably would not have been recommended by Stendhal.", "It was studied by Couture's students as a required part of their instruction.", "It was a work that Couture rejected in later life."], "columns": null, "pid": "v203_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Stendhal은 'the men of today and not those who probably never existed'를 그리라고 촉구.\nThe Romans of the Decadence는 'historical tableau of Roman times' → 현대가 아닌 과거 로마 주제.\n따라서 Stendhal이 권했을 주제가 아님.\n정답: C", "trap": "D: Couture가 학생들에게 모사시킨 것은 'old masters'의 작품이지 자신의 작품이 아니다. B: Meissonier와의 비교는 지문에 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"renown": "명성", "decadence": "퇴폐, 쇠퇴", "urge": "촉구하다"}, "src": "verbal203 Q12 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v202_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Other company insiders have recently offered testimony that _____ several of the more lurid anecdotes found in Belmer's account, though that testimony hardly minimizes the company's culture of malfeasance and mismanagement.", "choices": ["tempers", "corroborates", "outdoes", "exploits", "foreshadows"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심 단서: 'though that testimony hardly minimizes the company's culture of malfeasance'.\nthough(양보) → 증언이 무언가를 '약화'시키긴 하지만 회사의 비리 문화 자체를 축소하지는 못한다는 뜻.\n빈칸 = 일부 선정적(lurid) 일화를 '누그러뜨리다, 완화하다' → tempers.\n정답: A (tempers)", "trap": "corroborates(입증하다)가 가장 매력적이지만, 입증이라면 'though... hardly minimizes'라는 양보 구조가 필요 없다. 양보절은 빈칸이 '축소' 방향임을 알려준다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"tempers": "완화하다, 누그러뜨리다", "corroborates": "입증하다, 확증하다", "outdoes": "능가하다", "exploits": "이용하다", "foreshadows": "예시하다, 전조가 되다"}, "src": "verbal202 Q1 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v18_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The novel's heroine shows a remarkable (i)__________ to worship at the altar of youth; in her world, youth is (ii)__________, while age, by contrast, confers competence and wisdom.", "choices": null, "columns": [["disinclination", "desire", "tendency"], ["incredulous", "sagacious", "callow"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 'while age, by contrast, confers competence and wisdom' → 나이와 대조되는 젊음 = 미숙함 → callow.\n(i) 젊음을 미숙하다고 보므로 젊음을 숭배하지 '않으려는' 태도 → disinclination.\n정답: A, F", "trap": "(i) desire·tendency는 'worship at the altar of youth'와 자연스럽게 붙지만, 젊음 = 미숙이라는 그녀의 관점과 모순된다. (ii) sagacious는 'by contrast'를 무시한 선택.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"callow": "미숙한, 풋내기의", "sagacious": "현명한", "disinclination": "내키지 않음, 싫어함", "desire": "욕구", "tendency": "경향", "incredulous": "믿지 않는, 회의적인"}, "src": "verbal18 Q2"}, {"id": "v236_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "The notion that scientists consider the work they do to be (i) _____ contradicts popular stereotypes that depict the work of scientists (and the scientists themselves) as being formal and rigid, following lockstep procedures in which the (ii) _____ elements of researchers' personalities fail to enter their labors.", "choices": null, "columns": [["socially useful", "emotionally satisfying", "intellectually demanding"], ["affective", "cognitive", "conjectural"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 과학자들의 생각(i)이 대중의 고정관념(형식적·경직적, 성격의 (ii) 요소가 작업에 들어가지 않음)과 '모순'된다.\n(ii) 경직된 절차 때문에 연구에 반영되지 않는 성격 요소 = 감정적 요소 → affective.\n(i) 그것과 모순되려면 과학자들이 일을 감정적으로 만족스럽다고 여겨야 함 → emotionally satisfying.\n정답: B, D", "trap": "(ii) cognitive는 과학 작업과 연결돼 끌리지만, 인지적 요소는 경직된 절차에서도 당연히 들어간다. (i) intellectually demanding은 고정관념과 모순되지 않는다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"following lockstep procedures": "정해진 절차를 따르는", "socially useful": "사회적으로 유용한", "emotionally satisfying": "감정적으로 만족스러운", "intellectually demanding": "지적으로 까다로운", "affective": "정서적인, 감정의", "cognitive": "인지적인", "conjectural": "추측에 의한"}, "src": "verbal236 Q2 · 24/1, 23/10 중국후기"}, {"id": "v12_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "As a matter of good practice, members of the scientific community tend to be (i) _____ when it comes to affirming received opinion. They constantly question whatever is offered as accepted truth. Science (ii) _____ when its practitioners hew to (iii) _____ approach.", "choices": null, "columns": [["coy", "chary", "ambivalent"], ["regresses", "founders", "thrives"], ["pragmatic", "skeptical", "circuitous"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 다음 문장 'They constantly question whatever is offered as accepted truth' → 통념을 인정하는 데 조심스러움 = chary.\n(ii)(iii) 'As a matter of good practice' → 과학은 그런 태도를 고수할 때 번창한다: thrives + skeptical(회의적) 접근.\n정답: B, F, H", "trap": "(i) ambivalent(양가적)는 '늘 의문을 제기한다'보다 약하고 방향성이 없다. coy는 '수줍어하는 척하는'이라 맥락에 안 맞는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"coy": "수줍어하는(척하는)", "chary": "조심하는, 신중한", "hew": "고수하다", "ambivalent": "양가적인", "regresses": "퇴보하다", "founders": "실패하다, 좌초하다", "thrives": "번창하다", "pragmatic": "실용적인", "skeptical": "회의적인", "circuitous": "우회적인"}, "src": "verbal12 Q4"}, {"id": "v6_q12", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage would probably agree with which of the following statements about ballet's lack of a written tradition?", "choices": ["This lack is one reason that ballet has shallow roots in American culture.", "This lack makes it imperative that a ballet be performed regularly for it to remain alive.", "This lack makes it more difficult to preserve a particular ballet in the public's consciousness."], "columns": null, "pid": "v6_p3", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'dance has no written tradition and disappears easily from collective memory'.\n→ 글로 된 전통이 없으니 특정 발레를 대중의 기억 속에 보존하기 어렵다 = C.\nA: 'shallow roots'는 별개의 이유('In part this is because...')로 제시될 뿐, 기록 전통 부재가 그 원인이라고 하지 않는다.\nB: 'unless... alive and interesting now'는 생생하고 흥미로워야 한다는 것이지 '정기 공연이 필수'라는 주장까지는 아니다.\n정답: C", "trap": "B: 'alive'라는 표현 때문에 끌리지만 'imperative'·'performed regularly'는 지문보다 강하고 구체적이다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"collective memory": "집단 기억", "imperative": "필수적인", "vaudeville": "보드빌(버라이어티 쇼)", "legacy": "유산"}, "src": "verbal6 Q12"}, {"id": "v6_q13", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that at the time of Balanchine's death, many people thought which of the following about Balanchine's work?", "choices": ["There was little danger that Balanchine's work would be forgotten.", "It was unlikely that Balanchine's body of work would ever be equaled.", "Balanchine's work had only shallow roots in American culture.", "Balanchine's work was difficult to understand due to the lack of a written balletic tradition.", "Balanchine's work made work by other American choreographers look like a vaudeville act."], "columns": null, "pid": "v6_p3", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: '...laying a foundation for generations to come—or so it was thought at the time of his death.'\n당시에는 그의 업적이 다음 세대들의 토대가 될 것(지속될 것)이라 생각됨 → 잊힐 위험이 거의 없다고 생각했다.\n'or so it was thought'는 그 생각이 지금은 의심스럽다는 함의.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: '필적할 수 없다'는 평가는 지문에 없다. C·D: 저자의 현재 분석이지 그 당시 사람들의 생각이 아니다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"choreographer": "안무가", "body of work": "작품 전체", "foundation": "토대"}, "src": "verbal6 Q13"}, {"id": "v210_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["consider the consequences of a scholarly oversight", "question the ideological consistency of certain literary critics", "show the shortcomings of a critical propensity", "discuss the contradictions inherent in a literary movement", "demonstrate certain difficulties involved in unearthing obscure literary works"], "columns": null, "pid": "v210_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 두 문장이 주제: 일부 페미니스트 학자들의 '현재 이념 기준으로 평가하는 경향(tendency)'에는 'certain pitfalls'가 있으며, Female Wits 사례가 이를 보여준다.\n= 비평적 성향(critical propensity)의 단점 제시. tendency → propensity, pitfalls → shortcomings로 패러프레이즈.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: Pix의 업적 간과(oversight)는 언급되지만, 그 '결과'를 고찰하는 글이 아니라 그런 경향의 문제점을 보여주는 사례다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"propensity": "성향, 경향", "pitfall": "함정, 위험", "unearth": "발굴하다", "ideological": "이념적인"}, "src": "verbal210 Q7 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v210_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, feminist literary scholars of the Female Wits have a tendency to", "choices": ["overlook the originality of certain features of Pix's plays", "exaggerate the stereotypically feminine characteristics of Pix's heroines", "dwell on the progressive nature of Pix's views on social issues", "downplay the villainous nature of some of Manley's heroines", "misinterpret Trotter's insistence on feminine virtue"], "columns": null, "pid": "v210_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: Pix는 'more formally innovative than Manley's', 'broke new ground regarding subject matter' — 'However, these acts are rarely acknowledged by scholars of the Female Wits.'\n= Pix 작품의 독창적 특징을 간과한다.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 학자들이 Pix의 '여성적' 묘사를 근거로 그녀를 무시한 것이지 그것을 '과장'했다는 말은 없다. D·E는 지문에 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"formally innovative": "형식적으로 혁신적인", "break new ground": "새로운 영역을 개척하다", "dismiss": "무시하다, 일축하다"}, "src": "verbal210 Q8 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v210_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author's reference to Pix's \"addressing contemporary social issues such as class upheaval\" serves primarily to", "choices": ["suggest that Pix's political and social views were stereotypically \"feminine\"", "identify a Pixian subject that feminist scholars have consistently misinterpreted", "help explain why Pix's plays proved to be more successful than either Manley's or Trotter's", "support the claim that Pix's plays pursued previously unexplored topics", "identify a factor that contributed to the formal innovativeness of Pix's plays"], "columns": null, "pid": "v210_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "해당 문장: 'She also broke new ground regarding subject matter, addressing contemporary social issues such as class upheaval.'\n'broke new ground regarding subject matter'(주제 면에서 새 영역 개척)의 구체적 예시로 사회 문제를 다룬 점을 든다.\n= 이전에 탐구되지 않은 주제를 다뤘다는 주장을 뒷받침.\n정답: D", "trap": "E: 'formally innovative'(형식적 혁신)는 앞 문장의 별개 장점이고, 이 예시는 '주제(subject matter)'에 관한 것이다. C: 성공의 원인으로 제시되지 않았다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "addressing contemporary social issues such as class upheaval", "glosses": {"class upheaval": "계급 격변", "subject matter": "주제, 소재", "unexplored": "탐구되지 않은"}, "src": "verbal210 Q9 · 24년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v26_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "If aging is merely an avoidable by-product of life rather than a necessary progression, it is possible that we might eventually forestall _____.", "choices": ["senescence", "dynamism", "decrepitude", "privation", "ennui", "vitality"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "If절: 노화(aging)가 필연이 아니라 피할 수 있는 부산물이라면 → 결국 ___을 막을(forestall) 수 있다.\n빈칸 = 노화와 관련된 쇠퇴 → senescence(노화), decrepitude(노쇠).\n정답: A, C", "trap": "dynamism·vitality는 짝이지만 '막는다'의 대상으로는 정반대 의미다. ennui·privation은 노화와 무관.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"senescence": "노화, 노쇠", "decrepitude": "노쇠, 쇠약", "privation": "궁핍, 결핍", "ennui": "권태", "dynamism": "역동성", "vitality": "활력"}, "src": "verbal26 Q9"}, {"id": "v218_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "While there is no evidence that Bigfoot is real, several well-known species were once thought to be _____; the okapi, for instance, was known as the “African unicorn” until explorers obtained proof of its existence.", "choices": ["threatened", "fabulous", "extinct", "defunct", "legendary", "secretive"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론 뒤 예시: 오카피는 존재 증거가 나오기 전까지 'African unicorn'(상상 속 동물)으로 불렸다.\n앞의 'no evidence that Bigfoot is real'과 연결 → 빈칸 = 실재하지 않는, 전설 속의.\nfabulous(전설상의)와 legendary가 짝.\n정답: B, E", "trap": "extinct·defunct는 서로 짝이지만 '존재 증거를 얻었다'는 단서는 멸종이 아니라 '실존 여부'에 관한 것이다. fabulous는 '멋진'이 아니라 '전설상의' 뜻.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"fabulous": "전설상의, 우화에 나오는", "threatened": "멸종 위기의", "extinct": "멸종한", "defunct": "더 이상 존재하지 않는", "legendary": "전설적인", "secretive": "비밀스러운"}, "src": "verbal218 Q11 · 25/10, 25/8, 25/1, 24/9, 24/6, 24/1 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "By 1600, France's sense of itself as a nation bound by a shared destiny was _____, but over the course of the seventeenth century, French culture regained the strength it had had in the Middle Ages.", "choices": ["absent", "innocuous", "benign", "unique", "precarious", "uncertain"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "EF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "but으로 대비: 17세기 동안 프랑스 문화는 중세의 힘을 '되찾았다(regained)'.\n→ 1600년의 국가 정체성은 약하고 불안정했다 = 빈칸 부정적, '흔들리는'.\nprecarious(불안정한)와 uncertain(불확실한)이 짝.\n정답: E, F", "trap": "absent(없는)는 혼자 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없고, '되찾다'는 완전 부재보다 '약화'에 가깝다. innocuous·benign은 짝이지만 의미가 안 맞는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"absent": "없는, 부재한", "innocuous": "무해한", "benign": "온화한, 무해한", "unique": "독특한", "precarious": "불안정한, 위태로운", "uncertain": "불확실한"}, "src": "verbal240 Q11 · 25/7, 25/4, 24/2, 23/10, 22/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v222_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following most logically completes the argument?", "choices": ["very few languages are as difficult to learn as a second language as Torvic is", "of all the people in the world who speak several languages, only a small minority speak Torvic", "few people who live in Torvia actually speak Torvic", "few people who live in Torvia have ever lived outside Torvia", "some of the languages taught in Torvia's public schools are not spoken in any of the countries with which Torvia trades"], "columns": null, "pid": "v222_p13", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "사실: Torvic 사용자는 거의 모두 Torvia에 산다 / Torvia 거주자 대부분은 여러 언어를 쓴다.\n추론하면 안 되는 것: 'Torvic 사용자 대부분이 여러 언어를 쓴다'.\n이 추론은 Torvia 거주자 대부분이 Torvic을 쓸 때만 성립. 만약 Torvia 거주자 중 Torvic 사용자가 소수라면, 다언어 사용자 다수가 Torvic 비사용자일 수 있다.\nC가 이 빈틈을 정확히 지적.\n정답: C", "trap": "B: 전 세계 다언어 사용자 중 Torvic 사용자가 소수라는 것은 'Torvic 사용자 중' 다언어 사용자 비율과 무관하다(방향이 뒤집힘).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"infer": "추론하다", "minority": "소수"}, "src": "verbal222 Q13 · 25/9, 25/3, 25/1, 24/9, 23/1, 22/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v236_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that many historians in the nineteenth century believed that the French chroniclers", "choices": ["overly praised Richard II during his reign", "were less meticulous than their English counterparts", "distorted their accounts of the events of 1399 because of antipathy toward England", "refused requests by those in power to have their chronicles inspected", "willfully ignored events in England in favor of recording happenings closer to home"], "columns": null, "pid": "v236_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'For most of the nineteenth and twentieth centuries, this discrepancy was attributed to French Anglophobia'.\nAnglophobia(영국 혐오) = antipathy toward England. 즉 19세기 역사가들은 프랑스 연대기가 영국에 대한 반감 때문에 1399년 사건을 왜곡했다고 봤다.\n정답: C", "trap": "B: '덜 꼼꼼했다'는 정확성 문제이지만, 지문은 원인을 '반감(Anglophobia)'으로 명시한다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"usurped": "찬탈하다", "usurp": "찬탈하다", "Anglophobia": "영국 혐오", "antipathy": "반감", "discrepancy": "불일치", "reappraise": "재평가하다"}, "src": "verbal236 Q5 · 26년 1월, 24년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v236_q6", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage mentions which of the following as evidence suggesting censorship on the part of Henry IV?", "choices": ["Henry's request to inspect the chronicles", "The uniformity of those chronicles' criticism of Henry's predecessor", "The disparity between accounts offered in English and French chronicles"], "columns": null, "pid": "v236_p1", "answer": "ABC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "A: 'one chronicler mentions that Henry ordered all chronicles inspected' → 검열의 증거.\nB: 'the single voice with which the English chronicles praise Henry and defame Richard' + 비판적 연대기가 하나도 없음 → 획일성 = 증거.\nC: 'Moreover... is challenged by the contrary version of events recorded in the French chronicles' → Moreover로 추가 증거 제시.\n정답: A, B, C", "trap": "C를 빼기 쉽다: 불일치가 과거에 Anglophobia로 설명됐다는 점 때문에 증거가 아닌 것처럼 보이지만, Moreover로 추가 근거로 제시되고 프랑스 연대기는 재평가되었다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"predecessor": "전임자", "censor": "검열하다", "defame": "명예를 훼손하다", "disparity": "차이, 불일치", "uniformity": "획일성"}, "src": "verbal236 Q6 · 26년 1월, 24년 3월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.8 / S2 3.1"}, {"set": 29, "sections": [[{"id": "v217_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The deep water realm was once assumed to be _____, but we now know that submerged currents of cold water flowing from high latitudes toward the equator may generate high-energy eddies that reshape the seafloor.", "choices": ["virtually inaccessible", "relatively peaceful", "geologically active", "completely lifeless", "ecologically important"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "신호: 'was once assumed to be ___, but we now know ...' → 과거의 가정과 현재 지식이 대조됨.\n현재 사실: 차가운 해류가 고에너지 소용돌이(high-energy eddies)를 만들어 해저를 재형성함 = 역동적·격렬함.\n빈칸 = 그 반대, '조용하고 평온하다'는 뜻.\nrelatively peaceful(비교적 평온한)이 정확히 대조를 이룸.\n정답: B (relatively peaceful)", "trap": "geologically active는 'we now know' 쪽 내용과 같은 방향이라 대조가 성립하지 않음. inaccessible/lifeless는 에너지·지형 변화와 대조 축이 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"virtually inaccessible": "사실상 접근 불가능한", "relatively peaceful": "비교적 평온한", "geologically active": "지질학적으로 활발한", "completely lifeless": "생명체가 전혀 없는", "ecologically important": "생태학적으로 중요한"}, "src": "verbal217 Q1 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v9_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Their remote jungle habitat and their extreme shyness have (i) _____ any thorough investigation of orangutans except in the (ii) _____ conditions of captivity.", "choices": null, "columns": [["subsumed", "simplified", "precluded"], ["primitive", "heightened", "unnatural"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 서식지가 외진 정글이고 극도로 수줍음 → 철저한 조사를 '불가능하게 만들었다' → precluded.\n'except in the (ii) ___ conditions of captivity' → 사육 상태는 자연 서식지와 다른 조건.\n(ii) = 부자연스러운 → unnatural.\n즉 야생에서는 연구가 막혀서 부자연스러운 사육 환경에서만 연구가 가능했다는 논리.\n정답: C (precluded), F (unnatural)", "trap": "(ii)의 primitive는 '정글=원시적'이라는 연상에 끌리는 함정. 사육 환경은 원시적인 것이 아니라 자연과 다른 '인위적' 조건.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"subsumed": "포함시킨, 포섭한", "simplified": "단순화한", "precluded": "불가능하게 한, 막은", "primitive": "원시적인", "heightened": "고조된, 강화된", "unnatural": "부자연스러운, 인위적인"}, "src": "verbal9 Q2"}, {"id": "v223_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "One of the fundamental problems with learning mathematics is that while the number sense may be (i) _____, exact calculation requires cultural tools—symbols and algorithms—that are relatively new and must therefore be absorbed by areas of the brain designed for other purposes, which is easier when what we are learning (ii) _____ our built-in circuitry. With an understanding of it, we can at least (iii) _____ our teaching methods by reflecting on the constraints it imposes.", "choices": null, "columns": [["innate", "modern", "complex"], ["harmonizes with", "intrudes on", "goes beyond"], ["preserve", "discard", "adapt"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'while number sense may be ___, exact calculation requires cultural tools ... relatively new' → while 대조. 문화적 도구는 '새로 배운 것' ↔ 수 감각은 '타고난 것' → innate. 뒤의 'built-in circuitry'도 단서.\n(ii) 다른 용도로 설계된 뇌 영역이 새 도구를 흡수해야 함 → 배우는 것이 내장 회로와 '조화를 이룰 때' 더 쉬움 → harmonizes with.\n(iii) 이 원리를 이해하면 그것이 부과하는 제약을 고려해 교수법을 '조정할' 수 있음 → adapt.\n정답: A (innate), D (harmonizes with), I (adapt)", "trap": "(i) modern은 'relatively new'와 대조가 깨짐. (iii) discard는 너무 극단적—제약을 '반영'한다는 말과 맞는 것은 수정·조정.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"innate": "타고난, 선천적인", "modern": "현대적인", "complex": "복잡한", "harmonizes with": "~와 조화를 이루다", "intrudes on": "~을 침해하다", "goes beyond": "~을 넘어서다", "preserve": "보존하다", "discard": "버리다", "adapt": "조정하다, 맞추다"}, "src": "verbal223 Q3 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v13_q4", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true of Han dynasty writers' attitudes toward women and cloth production?", "choices": ["These writers presented cloth production as a woman's most important job.", "These writers believed that women who devoted significant time to tasks other than cloth production were irresponsible.", "These writers linked cloth production with the concept of successful womanhood."], "columns": null, "pid": "v13_p1", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'writers during the Han dynasty ... singling out cloth production as the most important job and linking it to the concept of successful womanhood.'\nA: 'most important job' 그대로 → 참.\nC: 'linking it to the concept of successful womanhood' 그대로 → 참.\nB: 'irresponsible' 평가는 실제(In reality) 사회가 '옷감만 만들고 다른 일을 무시한 여성'에게 내렸을 평가이지, 한나라 작가들의 생각이 아님.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "B는 지문의 'irresponsible'이라는 단어를 가져왔지만 주체(작가 → 현실 사회)와 대상(옷감만 만드는 여성 → 다른 일을 하는 여성)을 모두 뒤집음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"idealized": "이상화된", "single out": "특별히 골라내다", "gendered": "성별로 구분된", "womanhood": "여성다움, 여성으로서의 삶"}, "src": "verbal13 Q4"}, {"id": "v13_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage would be most likely to agree with which of the following evaluations of Han dynasty writers' views of labor?", "choices": ["These writers assumed that labor was more divided along gender lines than was in fact the case.", "These writers failed to distinguish the variety of tasks included in men's labor.", "These writers overestimated the role of household labor in the Chinese economy.", "These writers underestimated the contribution of men's labor to the Chinese economy.", "These writers exaggerated the prominence of cloth production in women's labor."], "columns": null, "pid": "v13_p1", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "현대 학자: 여성은 매우 다양한 일을 했음.\n한나라 작가: 그 다양성 대신 옷감 생산을 '가장 중요한 일'로 이상화.\n'In reality, however' 옷감만 만드는 여성은 무책임하다고 여겨졌을 것 → 옷감 생산의 비중이 실제보다 과장되었다는 평가.\nE 'exaggerated the prominence of cloth production in women's labor'가 정확한 paraphrase.\n정답: E", "trap": "A는 '성별 분업'이라는 말에 끌리지만 지문은 현대 학자도 gendered tasks를 인정함—작가들이 성별 분업을 과장했다는 근거는 없음. B/D는 남성 노동 이야기로 범위 밖.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"prominence": "두드러짐, 중요성", "exaggerate": "과장하다", "overestimate": "과대평가하다"}, "src": "verbal13 Q5"}, {"id": "v213_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Yoshiko Yamaguchi was a remarkably _____ public figure: she was not only an actress but also a journalist, a prominent politician in the Japanese parliament, and the wife of a diplomat.", "choices": ["protean", "sporadic", "prolific", "pedestrian", "versatile", "prosaic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 빈칸의 설명: 배우이자 기자, 국회의원, 외교관의 아내 → 여러 역할을 소화함.\n빈칸 = '다재다능한, 다양한 역할을 하는'이라는 뜻.\nprotean(변화무쌍한, 다재다능한)과 versatile(다재다능한)이 같은 의미의 쌍.\n정답: A (protean), E (versatile)", "trap": "prolific(다작의)는 '많이 생산함'이지 '여러 분야'가 아님—짝도 없음. pedestrian/prosaic은 '평범한'으로 짝은 맞지만 remarkably와 문맥에 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"protean": "변화무쌍한, 다재다능한", "sporadic": "산발적인", "prolific": "다작의, 다산의", "pedestrian": "평범한, 진부한", "versatile": "다재다능한", "prosaic": "평범한, 지루한"}, "src": "verbal213 Q9 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v13_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The book captures the _____ of several politicians who spoke publicly of old-time virtues in order to mask private vices.", "choices": ["probity", "dissemblance", "opportunism", "rectitude", "ingenuousness", "duplicity"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 공개적으로는 옛 미덕을 말하면서(spoke publicly of old-time virtues) 사적인 악덕을 감춤(mask private vices).\n빈칸 = 겉과 속이 다름, '위선·기만'이라는 뜻.\ndissemblance(위장, 시치미)와 duplicity(표리부동, 이중성)가 같은 의미.\n정답: B (dissemblance), F (duplicity)", "trap": "probity/rectitude는 '정직'으로 짝은 맞지만 정반대 의미. opportunism(기회주의)은 부정적이지만 '감춤'의 의미가 없고 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"probity": "정직, 청렴", "rectitude": "도덕적 올바름, 정직", "dissemblance": "위장, 본심을 숨김", "opportunism": "기회주의", "ingenuousness": "순진함, 솔직함", "duplicity": "이중성, 표리부동"}, "src": "verbal13 Q7"}, {"id": "v229_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The hypothesis that the moon formed from a planetary impact could account for the _____ of water and other volatiles on the Moon since such an impact would have caused volatiles to escape into space.", "choices": ["condensation", "paucity", "nullity", "ephemerality", "dearth", "occurrence"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "since 이하가 원인: 충돌로 휘발성 물질이 우주로 빠져나갔을 것.\n그 결과 달에는 물·휘발성 물질이 '부족함' → 빈칸 = 부족, 결핍.\npaucity(부족)와 dearth(결핍)가 같은 의미.\n정답: B (paucity), E (dearth)", "trap": "nullity는 '무효, 존재하지 않음'이라 비슷해 보이지만 '양이 적음'의 의미가 아니고 짝이 없음. occurrence는 '존재'로 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"condensation": "응결, 압축", "paucity": "부족, 소량", "nullity": "무효, 무(無)", "ephemerality": "덧없음, 일시성", "dearth": "결핍, 부족", "occurrence": "발생, 존재"}, "src": "verbal229 Q7 · 25년 1월, 24년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v201_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In his discussion of art, Ramachandran makes no distinction between the arousal value of a stimulus and its aesthetic value; he takes the emotional power of an artwork to be _____ that work's aesthetic quality.", "choices": ["predictive of", "tantamount to", "subordinate to", "dependent on", "commensurate with", "derived from"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'makes no distinction between the arousal value ... and its aesthetic value' + 세미콜론(;) → 뒤 문장은 같은 내용 재진술.\n빈칸 = 감정적 힘을 미적 가치와 '같은 것/동등한 것'으로 본다는 뜻.\ntantamount to(~와 같은)와 commensurate with(~에 상응하는, 대등한)가 '동등함'의 쌍.\n정답: B (tantamount to), E (commensurate with)", "trap": "dependent on/derived from은 의미상 짝이지만 '하나가 다른 것에서 나온다'는 구분(인과)을 전제함—'구분하지 않는다'와 충돌.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"predictive of": "~을 예측하게 하는", "tantamount to": "~와 마찬가지인", "subordinate to": "~에 종속된", "dependent on": "~에 의존하는", "commensurate with": "~에 상응하는, 대등한", "derived from": "~에서 유래한"}, "src": "verbal201 Q7 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v19_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["compare two explanations for a recurring problem", "summarize evidence relevant to a hypothesis", "point out inconsistencies in a set of findings", "account for the persistence of a point of view", "reconsider the origins of an ongoing issue"], "columns": null, "pid": "v19_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "가설: 'increasing-disadvantage model'(여성이 위로 갈수록 불이익 증가).\n지문 전체가 이 가설과 관련된 연구 결과들을 나열: 'most research to date has failed to support', 민간·공공 부문 연구, Baxter와 Wright의 연구.\n마지막에 'Taken together, these findings suggest...'로 정리 → 가설 관련 증거를 요약.\n정답: B", "trap": "D(관점의 지속을 설명)는 'continued widespread public acceptance'에 끌리지만 지문은 왜 대중이 믿는지 설명하지 않음. C는 연구 결과들이 대체로 일관됨.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"proposition": "명제, 주장", "cumulative": "누적되는", "cross-sectional": "횡단적인(한 시점의)", "hierarchy": "위계"}, "src": "verbal19 Q10"}, {"id": "v19_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Based on the passage, which of the following is true of the \"limited evidence\" from Sweden and Australia?", "choices": ["It lends support to the increasing-disadvantage model.", "It correlates with findings on women's mobility from most other countries.", "It suggests important cultural similarities between these countries.", "It points to a phenomenon not widely recognized in these countries.", "It helps explain the persistence of the glass ceiling."], "columns": null, "pid": "v19_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'only limited evidence in Sweden and Australia, that women's probability of being located in a higher ... level declined relative to men's at higher levels.'\n즉 '높은 직급일수록 여성의 상대적 불리함이 커진다'는 증거 = increasing-disadvantage model을 (제한적으로) 뒷받침.\nA 'lends support to the increasing-disadvantage model'이 정확.\n정답: A", "trap": "E는 '유리천장을 설명'으로 그럴듯하지만 'persistence'(지속)를 설명하는 것은 아님; 저자는 오히려 유리천장이 myth일 수 있다고 결론. B는 다른 나라와의 비교가 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "limited evidence", "glosses": {"probability": "확률", "hierarchical": "위계적인", "glass ceiling": "유리천장"}, "src": "verbal19 Q11"}, {"id": "v19_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage and those accepting the \"proposition\" would most likely agree with which of the following?", "choices": ["Lower down on the organizational ladder, women tend to experience fewer disadvantages than they do at higher levels.", "Women experience no more disadvantages in moving up the organizational ladder than do men.", "The degree of disadvantage experienced by women remains constant as women move up the organizational ladder.", "The obstacles to women's advancement vary significantly from country to country.", "Women face some disadvantage at each stage of the organizational ladder."], "columns": null, "pid": "v19_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'proposition' = increasing-disadvantage model: 위로 갈수록 여성의 불이익이 증가.\n저자: 'cumulative effect of a constant—or even decreasing—disadvantage at successive hierarchical levels' → 각 단계마다 불이익은 있지만 일정하거나 줄어듦.\n공통점: 두 입장 모두 '각 단계에서 여성이 어느 정도 불이익을 겪는다'는 데는 동의.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(불이익이 일정)는 저자 쪽 주장일 뿐 proposition 지지자는 '증가'를 주장하므로 동의 불가. A는 proposition만의 입장. B는 둘 다 반대.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "proposition", "glosses": {"proposition": "명제", "successive": "연속적인", "cumulative": "누적의", "mobility": "(지위) 이동성"}, "src": "verbal19 Q12"}], [{"id": "v10_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Historically, it has been unusual for scientific terms, once coined, to enter common usage with much _____; \"scientist\" and \"dinosaur\" (coined in 1833 and 1842, respectively), for instance, were rarely used before the late nineteenth century.", "choices": ["recognition", "dispatch", "accuracy", "controversy", "acclaim"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론 뒤 예시: 'scientist'(1833), 'dinosaur'(1842)는 19세기 후반 전까지 거의 쓰이지 않음 → 일반 용어가 되기까지 '오래 걸렸다'.\n'unusual ... to enter common usage with much ___' → 빈칸 = 시간적 '빠름'이라는 뜻.\ndispatch = 신속함. 'with dispatch' = 신속하게.\n정답: B (dispatch)", "trap": "recognition/acclaim은 '잘 쓰이지 않았다'에 끌리지만, 예시의 핵심은 coined 연도와 late nineteenth century 사이의 '시간 간격'임.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"dispatch": "신속함; 발송", "recognition": "인정, 인식", "accuracy": "정확성", "controversy": "논란", "acclaim": "찬사"}, "src": "verbal10 Q1"}, {"id": "v34_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Since he had demonstrated (i) _____ talent as an amateur, several of his acquaintances (ii) _____ a career on the stage, but he followed his parents’ wishes, becoming an engineer.", "choices": null, "columns": [["an innocuous", "an unremarkable", "the requisite"], ["aided him in pursuing", "badgered him to pursue", "swayed him into pursuing"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'Since he had demonstrated ___ talent' → 무대 경력을 권한 이유이므로 긍정 → the requisite(필요한 만큼의) talent.\n(ii) 'but he followed his parents' wishes, becoming an engineer' → 결국 배우가 되지 않음.\n→ 지인들이 무대 경력을 하도록 '졸랐다'(badgered him to pursue)가 맞음.\n정답: C (the requisite), E (badgered him to pursue)", "trap": "(ii) swayed him into pursuing은 실제로 그 길로 '이끌었다'는 결과를 포함해 but 이하(엔지니어가 됨)와 모순. aided도 실제로 추구했다는 전제.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"an innocuous": "무해한, 무난한", "an unremarkable": "평범한", "the requisite": "필요한, 필수의", "aided him in pursuing": "추구하도록 도왔다", "badgered him to pursue": "추구하라고 졸랐다", "swayed him into pursuing": "설득해 추구하게 만들었다"}, "src": "verbal34 Q2"}, {"id": "v214_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "This collection is something of a (i) _____. The connections between sections are largely ephemeral, and the differences in the styles of the chapters often (ii) _____: some appear to be in entirely the wrong section. Nonetheless, there are many high-quality chapters here, and the issues addressed are important and timely. Readers will therefore find much of interest in parts of this book, especially if prepared to take individual chapters in isolation, although when the book is taken as a whole, they will experience a certain amount of conceptual (iii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["call to arms", "missed opportunity", "tour de force"], ["jarring", "fascinating", "inadequate"], ["brilliance", "fog", "integrity"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 장 간 연결이 미약하고 스타일 차이가 큼, 그러나 좋은 장도 많음 → 전체로서는 '아쉬운 책' → missed opportunity.\n(ii) 콜론 뒤 'some appear to be in entirely the wrong section' → 스타일 차이가 '거슬린다' → jarring.\n(iii) 'although when the book is taken as a whole' → 전체로 보면 개념적 '혼란' → fog.\n정답: B (missed opportunity), D (jarring), H (fog)", "trap": "(i) tour de force(걸작)는 'many high-quality chapters'에 끌리지만 첫 문장은 전체 구성의 결함을 말함. (iii) integrity/brilliance는 although 대조와 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"call to arms": "행동 촉구, 궐기 호소", "missed opportunity": "놓친 기회", "tour de force": "역작, 걸작", "jarring": "거슬리는, 삐걱거리는", "fascinating": "매혹적인", "inadequate": "불충분한", "brilliance": "탁월함", "fog": "혼란, 모호함", "integrity": "통합성, 온전함"}, "src": "verbal214 Q4 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v8_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The newly discovered fossil skeletons have the fins, scales, and other attributes of a giant fish, but also the telling anatomical traits of (i) _____ creature, such as the beginnings of digits, protowrists, and joints resembling elbows on the forward fins. The specimen is a fish with features that (ii) _____ the emergence of land animals and is thus a (iii) _____ of amphibians, reptiles, dinosaurs, and mammals.", "choices": null, "columns": [["a diurnal", "a marine", "a transitional"], ["anticipate", "impede", "supersede"], ["derivative", "predator", "predecessor"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CDI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 물고기 특징 + 손가락·손목·팔꿈치의 시초 → 물고기와 육상동물 사이 '과도기적' 생물 → a transitional.\n(ii) 육상동물의 출현을 '예고하는' 특징 → anticipate.\n(iii) thus → 그래서 양서류·파충류·공룡·포유류의 '조상' → predecessor.\n정답: C (a transitional), D (anticipate), I (predecessor)", "trap": "(i) a marine은 '물고기'에서 연상되지만 'but also' 대조 뒤에는 육상 특성이 와야 함. (iii) derivative는 시간 순서를 뒤집음(후손).", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"a diurnal": "주행성의", "a marine": "바다의", "a transitional": "과도기적인", "anticipate": "예고하다, 앞서 나타내다", "impede": "방해하다", "supersede": "대체하다", "derivative": "파생물", "predator": "포식자", "predecessor": "전신, 조상"}, "src": "verbal8 Q4"}, {"id": "v28_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage implies that many nineteenth-century American women chose to remain single because they", "choices": ["believed that marriage required them to give up much of their autonomy", "had attitudes toward marriage that were influenced by contemporary reform movements", "wanted to take advantage of increasing opportunities to distinguish themselves as professionals", "doubted that their own marriage would live up to their notion of what a marriage ought to be", "had a negative view of marriage fostered by a change in social attitudes during the nineteenth century"], "columns": null, "pid": "v28_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 결혼은 '사랑에 의한 결혼'이라는 영적 이상으로 격상됨 → 'socially acceptable for women not to marry if such an ideal marriage could not be realized with an available suitor.'\n결론: 'not a negative view of marriage but a highly idealistic one.'\nD '자신의 결혼이 이상에 못 미칠 것이라 의심했다'가 정확한 paraphrase.\n정답: D", "trap": "A·E는 결혼을 부정적으로 본다는 내용 → 저자가 반박하는 페미니스트 학자들의 견해. B·C는 개혁운동·전문직 언급을 끌어온 범위 밖 인과.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"elect to": "~하기로 선택하다", "autonomy": "자율성", "suitor": "구혼자", "idealistic": "이상주의적인"}, "src": "verbal28 Q12"}, {"id": "v28_q13", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage suggests that the feminist scholars mentioned in the first sentence distort the meaning of certain nineteenth-century American women’s choices by", "choices": ["ascribing those choices to a particular attitude toward marriage", "ignoring evidence about single women’s motives for becoming writers or professionals", "overestimating the number of nineteenth-century American women who were single by choice"], "columns": null, "pid": "v28_p3", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "페미니스트 학자들: 미혼 여성 = 결혼을 '억압적 제도'로 비판한 사람들.\n저자: 'Yet this view ... tends to distort the meaning of their choices' → 실제로는 부정적이 아닌 '이상주의적' 결혼관 때문.\n즉 학자들은 그 선택을 특정한(부정적) 결혼관 탓으로 돌려 왜곡 → A.\nB·C: 동기 증거 무시나 숫자 과대평가는 지문에 없음.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 'writers and professionals' 단어를 재활용한 함정—저자는 그 증거를 학자들이 무시했다고 말하지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "Feminist scholars", "glosses": {"ascribe": "~의 탓으로 돌리다", "distort": "왜곡하다", "oppressive": "억압적인"}, "src": "verbal28 Q13"}, {"id": "v236_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["describe a complex situation that evolved over time", "trace the development of a popular conception", "highlight similarities among different points of view regarding an issue", "present a hypothesis that challenges a commonly held perception", "introduce evidence that explains a puzzling phenomenon"], "columns": null, "pid": "v236_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "통념: 'popular consensus characterizes the intensive grazing ... as overgrazing'.\n저자: 'such intensive grazing is not necessarily destructive' → 통념에 도전.\n근거로 intermediate-disturbance hypothesis(중간 정도 교란에서 다양성 최대)를 제시하고 Papageorgiou 연구로 뒷받침.\nD '통념에 도전하는 가설을 제시'가 정확.\n정답: D", "trap": "E는 '과잉 방목된 섬에 종이 더 많다'는 결과를 '수수께끼 현상'으로 보게 만드는 함정—그건 마지막 근거일 뿐 글 전체의 목적이 아님. B는 통념의 '발달 과정'을 추적하지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rangelands": "목초지", "rangeland": "방목지, 목초지", "herbivore": "초식동물", "encroachment": "잠식, 침범", "consensus": "합의, 통념"}, "src": "verbal236 Q7 · 24년 7월, 23년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v236_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that which of the following would most likely take place in the Mediterranean shrublands if the intensity of grazing decreased significantly?", "choices": ["The dominance of woody vegetation would be reduced.", "The relative success of plant species would not be modified.", "The diversity of plant species would diminish.", "The most destructive plants would be eradicated.", "Conditions would be created that would require a rethinking of the intermediate-disturbance hypothesis."], "columns": null, "pid": "v236_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'low-intensity to moderate-intensity grazing is often ineffective in preventing the encroachment and dominance of woody vegetation.'\n→ 방목 강도가 크게 줄면 목본 식물이 잠식·우세해짐 → 다른 종이 밀려남.\n또한 방목이 경쟁적인 종을 억제해 다른 종이 살아남는다(Crawley) → 방목이 줄면 다양성 감소.\n정답: C", "trap": "A는 정반대(목본 우세가 '증가'함). E는 오히려 가설과 부합하는 결과이므로 가설을 재고할 필요 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"intensity": "강도", "woody vegetation": "목본 식물", "dominance": "우세, 지배"}, "src": "verbal236 Q8 · 24년 7월, 23년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v236_q9", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that supporters of the intermediate-disturbance hypothesis would most likely agree with which of the following claims?", "choices": ["An intermediate level of disturbance affects plant species diversity primarily when certain species are eaten to extinction.", "An intermediate level of disturbance promotes greater plant variety.", "The likelihood of survival of certain plant species increases with an intermediate level of disturbance."], "columns": null, "pid": "v236_p2", "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "가설 정의: 'biodiversity is higher with moderate disturbance' → B(중간 교란이 식물 다양성을 높임) 참.\n메커니즘: 'some species can survive because competition from more aggressive species that have been grazed is reduced' → C(특정 종의 생존 가능성 증가) 참.\nA: 'not by eating plants to extinction but by selective feeding' → 정반대이므로 거짓.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "A는 지문 표현 'eating plants to extinction'을 그대로 가져왔지만 not ... but 구조에서 부정된 쪽임.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"selective feeding": "선택적 섭식", "disturbance": "교란", "biodiversity": "생물다양성"}, "src": "verbal236 Q9 · 24년 7월, 23년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v4_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "If it is wrong to justify human selfishness on the basis of the alleged selfishness of nature, then it is equally mistaken to espouse _____ merely because some animals happily assist each other.", "choices": ["pragmatism", "moderation", "restraint", "altruism", "benevolence", "permissiveness"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 'If it is wrong to justify human selfishness on ... nature, then it is equally mistaken to espouse ___ merely because some animals happily assist each other.'\n앞의 selfishness와 대칭 → 빈칸 = 이기심의 반대, 서로 돕는 것 = '이타심'.\naltruism(이타주의)과 benevolence(자비, 선의)가 같은 방향의 쌍.\n정답: D (altruism), E (benevolence)", "trap": "moderation/restraint는 '절제'로 짝은 이루지만 'assist each other'(서로 도움)와 연결되지 않고 selfishness의 대칭어가 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pragmatism": "실용주의", "moderation": "절제, 중용", "restraint": "자제, 억제", "altruism": "이타주의", "benevolence": "자비심, 선의", "permissiveness": "관대함, 방임"}, "src": "verbal4 Q9"}, {"id": "v20_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "California's building codes are more __________ than those elsewhere in the United States to ensure that structures are capable of protecting people from frequent seismic events.", "choices": ["circuitous", "exacting", "controversial", "stringent", "convoluted", "extensive"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "목적: 잦은 지진에서 사람을 보호할 수 있는 건물 보장.\n→ 건축 규정이 다른 곳보다 '더 엄격하다'.\nexacting(엄격한, 까다로운)과 stringent(엄격한)가 같은 의미.\n정답: B (exacting), D (stringent)", "trap": "extensive(광범위한)는 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없음. circuitous/convoluted는 '복잡한·우회적인'으로 짝이지만 안전 목적과 무관하고 부정적.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"circuitous": "우회적인", "exacting": "엄격한, 까다로운", "controversial": "논란이 많은", "stringent": "엄격한", "convoluted": "복잡한, 난해한", "extensive": "광범위한"}, "src": "verbal20 Q8"}, {"id": "v18_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Monarch butterflies sequester toxins in their skin to discourage predators, but black-backed orioles (Icterus abeillei) __________ the defense: they consume only the soft insides of the butterfly.", "choices": ["anticipate", "disable", "ignore", "skirt", "circumvent", "disregard"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "but 대조: 나비가 피부에 독을 저장해 포식자를 막지만, 꾀꼬리는 그 방어를 ___.\n콜론 뒤: 부드러운 내부만 먹음 → 독이 있는 피부를 '피해 감' = 방어를 우회함.\nskirt(피해 가다)와 circumvent(우회하다)가 같은 의미.\n정답: D (skirt), E (circumvent)", "trap": "ignore/disregard는 짝이지만 '무시한다'면 독을 그냥 먹는다는 뜻—실제로는 독을 피해서 먹으므로 부적합. disable은 독을 무력화한다는 뜻이라 틀림.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"anticipate": "예상하다", "disable": "무력화하다", "ignore": "무시하다", "skirt": "피해 가다, 회피하다", "circumvent": "우회하다, 피하다", "disregard": "무시하다"}, "src": "verbal18 Q9"}, {"id": "v2_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "The statements given, if true, most strongly support which of the following?", "choices": ["Some members of the nobility in fourteenth-century Europe abandoned other activities in order to become professional musicians.", "There were styles of music performed in the fourteenth century for which no written scores survive.", "Professional musicians in fourteenth-century Europe had more highly developed skills than do the most skilled professional musicians today.", "The fourteenth-century European accounts that describe members of the nobility as excelling in musical performance do not specify the amount of time these members devoted to music.", "Professional musicians in fourteenth-century Europe did not perform for gatherings of members of the nobility."], "columns": null, "pid": "v2_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "전제1: 악보가 남아 있는 14세기 음악은 모두 너무 어려워 연주에만 평생을 바친 음악가만 연주 가능.\n전제2: 많은 귀족이 음악 연주에 뛰어났고 동시에 춤·시·그림에도 뛰어남(= 음악에만 전념하지 않음, 기록은 정확).\n→ 귀족들이 연주한 음악은 악보가 남은 그 어려운 음악이 아닌 다른 음악 → 악보가 남지 않은 음악 양식이 있었다.\n정답: B", "trap": "D(기록이 연습 시간을 명시하지 않음)는 모순을 해소하려는 듯 보이지만 지문은 기록이 'accurate'하다고 하므로 지지 근거가 없음. A는 귀족이 다른 활동을 포기했다는 것으로 전제와 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"notation": "기보법", "nobility": "귀족", "excel": "뛰어나다"}, "src": "verbal2 Q11"}, {"id": "v198_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about the “contradiction” mentioned in the highlighted sentence?", "choices": ["It was not generally addressed by critics before the 1970s.", "It is apparent in only a small number of Fern’s writings", "It has troubled many feminist critics who study Fern."], "columns": null, "pid": "v198_p1", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'contradiction' = Fern의 신랄한 사회 비판 vs 관습적 가치에 대한 열렬한 찬양 사이의 모순.\nA: 1970년대 이전 비평가들은 Fern을 '감상주의의 전형, 관습적 아이콘'으로만 봄 → 비판적 면모를 보지 못했으니 모순 자체를 다루지 않았음 → 참.\nC: 'Most feminist scholars find it difficult to reconcile' → 많은 페미니스트 비평가를 곤란하게 함 → 참.\nB: 일부 작품에만 나타난다는 근거 없음.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "A는 직접 진술이 아니라 추론이라 놓치기 쉬움. B는 근거 없는 범위 제한.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sardonic": "냉소적인, 비꼬는", "effusive": "과장된, 감정이 넘치는", "reconcile": "조화시키다", "insipid": "무미건조한"}, "src": "verbal198 Q5 · 25/2, 24/12, 24/6, 22/12, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that Tompkins would be most likely to agree with which of the following about the “critics” mentioned in the passage?", "choices": ["They accurately characterize the overall result Fern is aiming to achieve.", "They are not as dismissive of Fern as some feminist critics have suggested.", "They exaggerate the extent to which Fern intended her writing to serve a social purpose.", "They wrongly assume that sentimentalism must be a pejorative term.", "They fail to recognize that sentimental rhetoric plays to reader’s emotions."], "columns": null, "pid": "v198_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'critics' = 1970년대 이전 Fern을 'weepy sentimentalism', 'pious, insipid icon of conventional culture'로 본 비평가들 → 감상주의를 경멸적(무미건조·보수적)으로 사용.\nTompkins: 'sentimental writing could serve radical, rather than only conservative, ends' → 감상주의가 반드시 부정적·보수적인 것은 아님.\n→ Tompkins는 비평가들이 감상주의를 '반드시 경멸적 용어'로 잘못 가정했다고 볼 것 → D.\nE는 틀림: 비평가들은 'weepy'(눈물 짜는)라고 했으므로 감상적 수사가 감정에 호소한다는 점은 이미 인식함.\n정답: D", "trap": "E는 Tompkins의 'swaying readers emotionally'를 연상시키는 함정—Tompkins의 핵심은 감정 호소가 '급진적 사회 변화'로 이어질 수 있다는 것이지, 비평가들이 감정 호소 자체를 몰랐다는 것이 아님.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "most critics", "glosses": {"pejorative": "경멸적인", "sentimentalism": "감상주의", "insipid": "무미건조한", "pious": "경건한, 독실한"}, "src": "verbal198 Q6 · 25/2, 24/12, 24/6, 22/12, 22/6 중국후기", "note": "원본 답안표가 회차마다 달랐던 문항입니다(D / E). 지문 근거로 D를 정답으로 확정했습니다. Conflicting keys D/E (this copy says E, verbal34 copy says D). Chose D: the pre-1970s critics treated sentimentalism as a put-down (weepy, insipid, conventional), while Tompkins argues sentimental writing can serve radical ends, so she would say they wrongly assume sentimentalism is necessarily pejorative. E fails because calling Fern 'weepy' shows the critics did recognize the emotional appeal."}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.5 / S2 2.7"}, {"set": 30, "sections": [[{"id": "v211_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The effect of the film's expansive, darkly mournful opening sequence was magnified by a score that was similarly _____ and unrelenting.", "choices": ["iridescent", "volatile", "equivocal", "plangent", "blithe"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'similarly ___ and unrelenting' → similarly = 앞의 오프닝 장면과 같은 성격.\n오프닝: 'darkly mournful'(어둡고 애절한) → 빈칸 = '슬픈, 애절한'이라는 뜻.\nplangent = 구슬프게 울려 퍼지는, 애절한(소리·음악에 씀).\n정답: D (plangent)", "trap": "volatile(변덕스러운)은 'unrelenting'(끊임없는)과 오히려 상충. blithe(쾌활한)는 정반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"iridescent": "무지갯빛의", "plangent": "구슬픈, 애절하게 울리는", "volatile": "변덕스러운, 불안정한", "equivocal": "모호한", "blithe": "쾌활한, 태평한"}, "src": "verbal211 Q1 · 25/9, 25/8, 23/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v209_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Few consumers think of food as having a production history. Rather, our food seems (i) _____ those who grow, process, and serve it. Our food supply system encourages us to ignore connections between what we eat and its past, and, until recently, such (ii) _____ scarcely impacted consumer health.", "choices": null, "columns": [["disconnected from", "reflective of", "overwhelming to"], ["insistence", "unawareness", "ambivalence"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'Few consumers think of food as having a production history. Rather, ...' → 음식은 재배·가공·제공하는 사람들과 '단절된' 것처럼 보임 → disconnected from.\n(ii) 'encourages us to ignore connections' → such ___ = 그런 무시·모름 → unawareness.\n정답: A (disconnected from), E (unawareness)", "trap": "(ii) ambivalence(양가감정)는 '무시'가 아니라 '이중적 감정'이라 부적합. insistence는 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"disconnected from": "~와 단절된", "reflective of": "~을 반영하는", "overwhelming to": "~에게 압도적인", "insistence": "고집, 주장", "unawareness": "인식하지 못함", "ambivalence": "양가감정, 반대 감정 공존"}, "src": "verbal209 Q2 · 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v207_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Native American art is not a (i) _____ enterprise: it reflects differences among artists' personal, community, and tribal experience. As Native American artists continue to create the art that is valid for them, however, the (ii) _____ in Native American art between traditional and modern styles (primarily promulgated by non-Native American critics) has become outmoded. There is heightened recognition that placing Native American art in these two opposing categories has had a (iii) _____ effect on both artists and viewers.", "choices": null, "columns": [["fatalistic", "monolithic", "celebrated"], ["supposed distinction", "indispensable connection", "considerable overlap"], ["transient", "deleterious", "propitious"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 콜론 뒤 '작가 개인·공동체·부족 경험의 차이를 반영' → 획일적인 것이 아님 → not a monolithic enterprise.\n(ii) 'between traditional and modern styles' + 'has become outmoded' + 뒤 'two opposing categories' → 전통/현대의 '이른바 구분' → supposed distinction.\n(iii) 이 이분법이 구식이 되었다는 흐름 → 작가와 관객 모두에게 '해로운' 영향 → deleterious.\n정답: B (monolithic), D (supposed distinction), H (deleterious)", "trap": "(iii) propitious(유리한)는 outmoded라는 비판적 흐름과 반대. (ii) considerable overlap은 'opposing categories'와 모순.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"fatalistic": "숙명론적인", "monolithic": "획일적인, 단일한", "celebrated": "유명한, 칭송받는", "supposed distinction": "이른바 구분", "indispensable connection": "필수적 연결", "considerable overlap": "상당한 중첩", "transient": "일시적인", "deleterious": "해로운", "propitious": "유리한, 길조의"}, "src": "verbal207 Q3 · 25년 6월, 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v209_q4", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author indicates that the shift in attitudes about childhood involved which of the following?", "choices": ["Increased interest in child psychology", "Increased parental participation in children's development", "Increased emphasis on schooling"], "columns": null, "pid": "v209_p1", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Children were increasingly studied, regulated, and protected through the rise of pediatrics, child psychology, ..., compulsory schooling, ...'\nA: child psychology의 부상 → 아동 심리에 대한 관심 증가 → 참.\nC: compulsory schooling → 학교 교육 강조 증가 → 참.\nB: 'whose development would preoccupy parents'는 부모의 '관심·염려'이지 아이 발달에 '참여'가 늘었다는 직접 진술이 아님.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "B는 'preoccupy parents', 'scientific parenting regimes'에 끌리기 쉬우나, 지문은 부모의 실제 참여 증가를 말하지 않음(관심의 대상이 바뀌었다는 것).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"compulsory": "의무적인", "pediatrics": "소아과학", "preoccupy": "몰두하게 하다", "commoditization": "상품화"}, "src": "verbal209 Q4 · 25년 7월, 22년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v209_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies the author's agreement with which of the following statements about changes in how childhood was viewed?", "choices": ["The newly sentimental view of children did not preclude the commercial exploitation of children's wishes.", "The removal of children from the labor force was seen by advertisers as likely to reduce children's buying power.", "Parents felt compelled to resort to so-called scientific child-rearing regimes in order to counteract what they viewed as a harmful rise in consumerism.", "Increased study and regulation of children resulted from increased public attention to what was considered typical childhood development.", "Changing attitudes about child labor and the importance of children's education may have contributed to declines in agricultural production."], "columns": null, "pid": "v209_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'The redefinition of childhood served not to separate children from the commercial realm, but, rather, to advance the commoditization of childhood'.\n또 광고주들이 아이를 내세우고 결국 아이에게 직접 호소(appeal to directly)함.\n→ 감상적 아동관이 아이의 욕구를 상업적으로 이용하는 것을 막지 않았다 = A.\n정답: A", "trap": "D는 인과를 뒤집음: 지문은 연구·규제 증가가 공적 관심을 '발달하는 아이'로 옮겼다(These changes shifted public attention)고 하지, 관심이 연구를 낳았다고 하지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"instrumental": "도구적인, 실용적인", "commercial realm": "상업 영역", "exploitation": "이용, 착취", "preclude": "막다, 불가능하게 하다"}, "src": "verbal209 Q5 · 25년 7월, 22년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v23_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The philosopher contended that society had defeated individuality to the extent that the danger threatening human progress was no longer the __________ but, on the contrary, the deficiency of personal impulses and preference.", "choices": ["failure", "absence", "presence", "lack", "surfeit", "excess"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "EF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 'no longer the ___ but, on the contrary, the deficiency of personal impulses' → on the contrary로 deficiency(결핍)와 정반대.\n빈칸 = '과잉, 넘침'이라는 뜻.\nsurfeit(과잉)와 excess(과다)가 같은 의미.\n정답: E (surfeit), F (excess)", "trap": "absence/lack은 짝이 맞지만 deficiency와 같은 뜻이라 'on the contrary' 대조가 깨짐.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"failure": "실패", "absence": "부재", "presence": "존재", "lack": "부족", "surfeit": "과잉, 과다", "excess": "과다, 지나침"}, "src": "verbal23 Q6"}, {"id": "v21_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although the employees' union and company management, entering into contract negotiations, both issued statements encouraging __________, acrimony between the two sides continued unabated.", "choices": ["pertinacity", "compromise", "patience", "civility", "comity", "steadfastness"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although 대조: 양측이 ___을 장려하는 성명을 냈지만 'acrimony(신랄한 적대감)'가 계속됨.\n빈칸 = acrimony의 반대, '정중함·상호 예의'라는 뜻.\ncivility(정중함)와 comity(상호 예의, 우호)가 같은 의미.\n정답: D (civility), E (comity)", "trap": "compromise(타협)는 협상 문맥에 잘 어울리지만 짝이 없고 acrimony(감정·태도)와의 직접 대비가 약함. pertinacity/steadfastness는 '끈질김' 짝이지만 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pertinacity": "끈질김, 집요함", "compromise": "타협", "patience": "인내", "civility": "정중함, 예의", "comity": "상호 예의, 우호", "steadfastness": "확고함, 불굴"}, "src": "verbal21 Q7"}, {"id": "v203_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Because Earth's atmosphere distorts astronomical observations, whatever tends to _____ its influence is dismaying to the astronomer.", "choices": ["amplify", "sustain", "alter", "adjust", "revive", "strengthen"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "대기가 관측을 왜곡하므로, 그 영향을 ___ 하는 것은 천문학자에게 실망스러움(dismaying).\n빈칸 = 대기 영향을 '증가시키다'라는 뜻.\namplify(증폭하다)와 strengthen(강화하다)이 같은 의미.\n정답: A (amplify), F (strengthen)", "trap": "alter/adjust는 '바꾸다'로 짝이지만 변화가 줄이는 쪽일 수도 있어 반드시 실망스러운 것은 아님. sustain(유지)은 증가가 아니고 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"amplify": "증폭하다", "sustain": "유지하다", "alter": "바꾸다", "adjust": "조정하다", "revive": "되살리다", "strengthen": "강화하다"}, "src": "verbal203 Q7 · 25년 10월, 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v201_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "When urged to give up his place in line, the child initially _____ but eventually acquiesced.", "choices": ["retaliated", "capitulated", "commiserated", "remonstrated", "complied", "protested"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 'initially ___ but eventually acquiesced(결국 묵묵히 따랐다)' → but 대조.\n빈칸 = 처음에는 '반대·항의했다'.\nremonstrated(항의했다)와 protested(항의했다)가 같은 의미.\n정답: D (remonstrated), F (protested)", "trap": "capitulated/complied는 '굴복·응했다'로 짝이지만 acquiesced와 같은 뜻이라 but 대조가 깨짐. retaliated(보복했다)는 지나치고 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"remonstrated": "항의했다", "retaliated": "보복했다", "capitulated": "굴복했다", "commiserated": "동정했다", "complied": "따랐다", "protested": "항의했다"}, "src": "verbal201 Q6 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v211_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about the \"commentators\"?", "choices": ["They are partly responsible for Aristotle's reputation as a particularly clear writer.", "They considered the 《Poetics》 to be the most cryptic of Aristotle's works.", "They admired the writing that Aristotle prepared for publication more than they admired his lecture notes.", "Their intellectual interests are reflected in the Aristotelian works available to readers today.", "Their efforts helped clarify some of the more obscure passages in Aristotle's lecture notes."], "columns": null, "pid": "v211_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the Aristotelian works available to us are the ones that intellectually sophisticated commentators in late antiquity ... found philosophically most rewarding.'\n→ 오늘날 우리가 읽는 아리스토텔레스 저작은 그 주석가들이 가장 가치 있다고 본 것들 = 그들의 지적 관심이 반영됨.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 '명료한 문체' 명성이 출판용 저작에서 나온 것이라 주석가와 무관. E는 주석가가 난해한 부분을 해명했다는 언급이 없음—오히려 지금도 해석 논쟁 중.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "intellectually sophisticated commentators in late antiquity", "glosses": {"commentator": "주석가", "late antiquity": "고대 후기", "concession": "양보, 배려", "rewarding": "보람 있는, 가치 있는"}, "src": "verbal211 Q10 · 24년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v211_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage indicates which of the following about the highlighted \"writings\"?", "choices": ["They were intended to be read primarily by philosophers.", "They were admired in the ancient world for their lucidity.", "They included some material added by Aristotle's editors.", "They are primarily responsible for Aristotle's reputation today.", "They are the writing that scholars of late antiquity preferred."], "columns": null, "pid": "v211_p2", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'writings' = 'the writings that earned him this esteem' → 이 존경(esteem)은 앞 문장의 'admired in the ancient world for the clarity of his style'.\n→ 그 저작들은 고대에 명료함으로 찬사받았음 = B (lucidity = clarity).\n정답: B", "trap": "E는 함정: 고대 후기 학자들이 선호한 것은 '현존하는 강의 노트'이지 이 출판용 writings가 아님. D도 오늘날 명성의 근거는 현존 텍스트임.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"lucidity": "명료함", "esteem": "존경, 높은 평가", "lay readership": "일반 독자층"}, "src": "verbal211 Q11 · 24년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v211_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage mentions \"editorial activity\" primarily in order to", "choices": ["suggest that the texts Aristotle originally prepared for publication may not have been significantly less obscure than the texts available today", "help account for the rise in influence of the 《Poetics》 among literary critics during the Renaissance", "explain why currently available texts by Aristotle have certain advantages over the texts that Aristotle prepared for publication", "question the extent to which currently available texts by Aristotle reflect Aristotle's ideas accurately", "illustrate a point about the process by which Aristotle's surviving texts took their present form"], "columns": null, "pid": "v211_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "문맥: 'The process by which they took their present form is unclear: in some cases, there are signs of editorial activity ...'\n콜론 앞 진술(현재 형태가 된 과정이 불분명)을 콜론 뒤에서 예시로 보여줌.\n→ 현존 텍스트가 현재 형태를 갖추게 된 과정에 대한 요점을 예시 = E.\n정답: E", "trap": "D는 '아이디어를 정확히 반영하는지 의문'으로 그럴듯하지만, 지문은 텍스트의 형성 과정이 불분명하다는 것을 말할 뿐 내용의 정확성을 문제 삼지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "editorial activity", "glosses": {"editorial": "편집의", "splice": "이어 붙이다", "cryptic": "난해한, 수수께끼 같은", "allusive": "암시적인"}, "src": "verbal211 Q12 · 24년 6월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v222_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "In its literature and its political discourse, the nation has created various narratives about itself that tend to _____ intractable social divisions in the interest of perpetuating a dubious myth of unity.", "choices": ["denounce", "obscure", "corroborate", "anatomize", "explicate"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'in the interest of perpetuating a dubious myth of unity' → 통합이라는 의심스러운 신화를 유지하기 위해.\n그러려면 다루기 힘든 사회적 분열을 '가리고 감춰야' 함 → 빈칸 = 숨기다.\nobscure = 모호하게 하다, 감추다.\n정답: B (obscure)", "trap": "anatomize(상세히 분석하다)/explicate(설명하다)/denounce(비난하다)는 모두 분열을 드러내는 방향이라 통합 신화 유지와 모순.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"denounce": "비난하다", "obscure": "모호하게 하다, 감추다", "corroborate": "확증하다", "anatomize": "상세히 분석하다", "explicate": "설명하다"}, "src": "verbal222 Q1 · 24년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v20_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "At first glance, each of the stories in the anthology seemed (i)__________. Upon closer inspection of their protagonists, implied morals, and fantasy elements, however, subtle similarities among the stories emerged to (ii)__________ this initial observation.", "choices": null, "columns": [["compelling", "implausible", "idiosyncratic"], ["impugn", "bolster", "explain"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'At first glance ... However, ... subtle similarities among the stories emerged' → 처음에는 각 이야기가 '독특해/제각각으로' 보였음 → idiosyncratic.\n(ii) 유사점이 드러나 그 첫인상(초기 관찰)을 '반박·의문시'함 → impugn.\n정답: C (idiosyncratic), D (impugn)", "trap": "(ii) bolster는 '강화'로 however 대조와 반대. (i) compelling/implausible은 'similarities'와의 대조 축(독특함 vs 유사성)이 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"impugn": "의문을 제기하다, 반박하다", "compelling": "설득력 있는, 강렬한", "implausible": "믿기 어려운", "idiosyncratic": "특이한, 독특한", "bolster": "강화하다, 지지하다", "explain": "설명하다"}, "src": "verbal20 Q3"}, {"id": "v224_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Wald's decision to tell Rosetta Tharpe's story to a wider audience in 《Shout, Sister, Shout!》 (i) _____ the rigor of the book's scholarship or the acuity of its theory. The scholarly quality of the work is (ii) _____ on every page, and yet it is not a dry, specialist academic tome.", "choices": null, "columns": [["is not reflected in", "does not compromise", "does little to enhance"], ["evident", "diluted", "veiled"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 대중에게 이야기를 전하기로 한 결정 → 흔히 학문적 엄밀성이 떨어질 우려. 뒤의 'and yet it is not a dry, specialist academic tome'로 보아 학문성은 유지됨.\n→ 그 결정이 엄밀성과 이론의 날카로움을 '해치지 않는다' → does not compromise.\n(ii) 학문적 질이 모든 페이지에 '분명하다' → evident. 'and yet ... not dry'와 자연스러운 대조.\n정답: B (does not compromise), D (evident)", "trap": "(i) does little to enhance/is not reflected in은 부정적 평가로, (ii) evident와 함께 쓰면 모순. (ii) diluted/veiled는 and yet 대조와 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"does not compromise": "손상시키지 않다", "is not reflected in": "~에 반영되지 않다", "does little to enhance": "거의 향상시키지 않다", "evident": "분명한", "diluted": "희석된", "veiled": "가려진"}, "src": "verbal224 Q3 · 25/7, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v240_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The theater's stately production certainly does keep (i) _____ and the high praise it has received for its (ii) _____ could thus be called justified. But perhaps the performance goes too far in that direction. The (iii) _____ story line that makes this one of Shakespeare's most wayward (and least performed) plays has been smoothed into a well-drilled parade of avowals and betrayals, plots and counterplots, deaths and resurrections.", "choices": null, "columns": [["confusion at bay", "fidelity in view", "impropriety in check"], ["lucidity", "subtlety", "authenticity"], ["convoluted", "familiar", "facile"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(iii) 'makes this one of Shakespeare's most wayward (and least performed) plays' → 줄거리가 '복잡하게 뒤얽힌' → convoluted. 그것이 'smoothed into a well-drilled parade'(잘 정돈된 행렬로 매끄럽게 됨).\n(i) 위엄 있는 연출이 그 복잡성을 정돈 → '혼란을 막아 둔다' → confusion at bay.\n(ii) thus → 칭찬받은 것은 '명료함' → lucidity. 'But perhaps the performance goes too far in that direction'(너무 정돈함)과 연결.\n정답: A (confusion at bay), D (lucidity), G (convoluted)", "trap": "(ii) subtlety/authenticity는 '너무 매끈하게 정리했다'는 비판의 방향과 맞지 않음. (iii) facile(얄팍한)은 'wayward'(제멋대로인) 줄거리 설명으로 부적합.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"confusion at bay": "혼란을 막아 둔", "lucidity": "명료함", "impropriety in check": "부적절함을 억제한", "facile": "피상적인, 손쉬운", "fidelity in view": "충실함을 염두에 둔", "subtlety": "미묘함", "authenticity": "진정성, 원전 충실성", "convoluted": "뒤얽힌, 복잡한", "familiar": "익숙한"}, "src": "verbal240 Q4 · 26/2, 25/8, 25/4, 25/1 중국후기"}, {"id": "v34_q14", "type": "RC_select", "blanks": null, "stem": "Select the sentence in the passage that offers a possible explanation for a trend?", "choices": null, "columns": null, "pid": "v34_p4", "answer": "SENTENCE", "answer_sentence": "This shift in focus from gender inequality in political participation may be due to the finding in several studies of voting behavior in the United States that since 1980, differences in rates of registration and voting between men and women are not statistically significant after controlling for traditional predictors of participation.", "explanation": "trend(경향): 최근 연구가 등록·투표율보다 후보 선택에 초점을 두는 '초점의 이동'(shift in focus).\n두 번째 문장 'This shift in focus ... may be due to the finding ... that since 1980, differences ... are not statistically significant' → 'may be due to'로 이 경향의 가능한 원인을 제시.\n정답: 두 번째 문장 (This shift in focus ... may be due to ...)", "trap": "마지막 문장(남부에서 성별 격차가 지속되다 1970년대에 감소)은 '추세' 자체를 서술할 뿐 설명이 아님. Fullerton and Stern 문장은 반론.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"turnout": "투표율", "statistically significant": "통계적으로 유의한", "predictor": "예측 변수"}, "src": "verbal34 Q14"}, {"id": "v34_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true about recent studies of the gender gap in the United States politics?", "choices": ["They accurately depict voter participation in the South prior to 1980.", "They have been unduly influenced by changes in voter participation.", "They fail to recognize important factors affecting levels of voter participation.", "They do not pay sufficient attention to the effect regional differences have on voter participation.", "They are more concerned with the choices that male and female voters make than with the frequency with which they vote."], "columns": null, "pid": "v34_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Recent studies ... tend to focus on candidate choice rather than on registration and turnout.'\ncandidate choice = 유권자가 하는 선택, registration and turnout = 투표하는 빈도.\nE가 첫 문장의 직접 paraphrase.\n정답: E", "trap": "D(지역 차이에 충분히 주의를 기울이지 않음)는 Fullerton and Stern의 주장이지, 지문이 사실로 진술한 '최근 연구'의 특징이 아님. 'According to the passage' 문제는 직접 진술을 고를 것.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"registration": "(유권자) 등록", "turnout": "투표율", "unduly": "지나치게, 부당하게"}, "src": "verbal34 Q15"}, {"id": "v232_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["suggest that growers' selection for gigantism in plants may have certain unexpected long-term benefits", "account for a previously overlooked correlation between insectivore egg-laying on flowers and flower size", "examine some findings regarding the effects of domestication on sunflowers' interactions with insect herbivores", "challenge the idea that domestication of certain crops may contribute to changes in species that depend on those crops", "consider whether the plant vigor hypothesis might explain recent research findings concerning the parasitization of certain herbivorous moths"], "columns": null, "pid": "v232_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "1단락: 작물화로 인한 거대화(gigantism).\n2단락: plant vigor hypothesis → 재배 해바라기의 꽃 크기 증가와 나방 산란, 종자 크기와 기생자 접근성, 두 나방 종 비교 → 작물화가 해바라기-초식곤충 상호작용에 미치는 영향에 대한 연구 결과 검토.\nC 'examine some findings regarding the effects of domestication on sunflowers' interactions with insect herbivores'가 정확.\n정답: C", "trap": "E는 plant vigor hypothesis가 '기생 현상'을 설명하는지를 따지는 것이라 범위가 어긋남(가설은 산란 위치에 관한 것). D는 저자 입장과 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sunflower moths": "해바라기 나방 = 초식곤충", "parasitoid": "포식기생자", "progenitor": "조상, 원종", "oviposit": "산란하다", "gigantism": "거대화"}, "src": "verbal232 Q7 · 25년 8월, 23년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions \"maize (Zea mays)\" primarily in order to", "choices": ["acknowledge that domesticated crops with certain features in common likely originated in similar ecosystems", "emphasize that domestication of wild plants has resulted in a wide range of now-common food crops", "cite a species that differs from its wild progenitor in the size of some of its plant structures", "illustrate a claim about the reason that certain plant species have been favored for domestication", "provide evidence that certain traits shared by many domesticated plants are advantageous"], "columns": null, "pid": "v232_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "문맥: 'Striking examples of gigantism can be found by comparing crops such as tomato, maize ... with their wild ancestors.'\nmaize는 거대화(특정 구조의 확대)의 예시 → 야생 조상과 일부 식물 구조의 크기가 다른 종.\n정답: C", "trap": "B는 '다양한 식용 작물'이라는 나열 형태에 끌리는 함정—목적은 다양성이 아니라 '크기 확대'의 예시. E는 그 특징이 유리하다는 주장이 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "maize (Zea mays)", "glosses": {"progenitor": "조상", "morphological": "형태학적인", "domestication": "작물화, 가축화"}, "src": "verbal232 Q8 · 25년 8월, 23년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about organisms that parasitize the larvae of H. electelhum?", "choices": ["They tend to be more successful in habitats with natural sunflowers than in those with domesticated sunflowers.", "They have been observed to reproduce most prolifically in ecosystems where sunflowers have relatively large seeds.", "They appear to interfere with H. electellum egg-laying effort on domesticated sunflowers but not on natural sunflowers.", "They create a problem for growers of domesticated sunflowers for which innovative solutions are being sought.", "They have been found to be more diverse in areas where Cochylis hospes are more numerous than H. electellum."], "columns": null, "pid": "v232_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'increased seed size is negatively associated with parasitoid accessibility to H. electellum larvae' → 재배 해바라기에서는 기생자가 유충에 접근하기 어려움.\n그래서 'H. electellum is parasitized less frequently in sunflower agroecosystems than in natural sunflower ecosystems.'\n→ 기생자는 자연 해바라기 서식지에서 더 성공적 = A.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 반대(큰 종자 = 기생자 접근성 저하). C는 기생자가 산란을 방해한다는 내용이 없음—산란은 꽃 크기와 관련.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"parasitize": "기생하다", "larvae": "유충(larva의 복수)", "agroecosystem": "농업 생태계", "accessibility": "접근성"}, "src": "verbal232 Q9 · 25년 8월, 23년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v212_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Although extreme and singular events occur in a black hole, its event horizon boundary is _____: space travelers crossing it would be subject to the same physical laws that apply anywhere else.", "choices": ["illusory", "obscure", "unremarkable", "immutable", "unchanging", "commonplace"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Although 대조: 블랙홀 내부엔 극단적·특이한 사건이 일어나지만, 사건의 지평선 경계는 ___.\n콜론 뒤: 통과하는 여행자는 다른 곳과 같은 물리 법칙을 적용받음 → '특별할 것 없다'.\n빈칸 = 평범한. unremarkable과 commonplace가 같은 의미.\n정답: C (unremarkable), F (commonplace)", "trap": "immutable/unchanging은 '불변의'로 짝이지만 '같은 법칙이 적용됨 = 평범함'이지 경계가 변하지 않는다는 뜻이 아님. illusory도 그럴듯하나 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"illusory": "환상의, 실체 없는", "obscure": "모호한", "unremarkable": "평범한, 특별할 것 없는", "immutable": "불변의", "unchanging": "변하지 않는", "commonplace": "흔한, 평범한"}, "src": "verbal212 Q11 · 25년 6월, 23년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v24_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "A clever form of diplomacy involves subtly inducing the other party to propose your preference so that your __________ their requests appear as the gratifying of concession.", "choices": ["accession to", "inattention to", "subversion of", "abnegation of", "repudiation of", "acquiescence to"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "전략: 상대가 '당신이 원하는 것'을 제안하도록 유도 → 그러면 당신이 상대 요청을 ___ 하는 것이 '양보를 베푸는 것'처럼 보임.\n빈칸 = 상대 요청을 '받아들임/동의함'이라는 뜻.\naccession to(동의, 수락)와 acquiescence to(묵인, 따름)가 같은 의미.\n정답: A (accession to), F (acquiescence to)", "trap": "subversion of/repudiation of는 거부·전복으로 반대 방향. abnegation of(포기, 자기 부정)는 '양보'와 연상되지만 '요청을 수락'의 뜻이 아니고 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"accession to": "~에 동의, 수락", "inattention to": "~에 대한 부주의", "subversion of": "~의 전복", "abnegation of": "~의 포기, 자기희생", "repudiation of": "~의 거부, 부인", "acquiescence to": "~에 대한 묵인, 따름"}, "src": "verbal24 Q8"}, {"id": "v216_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The scientific study of laughter faces a frustrating paradox: ideal experiments take place in rigidly controlled environments with all but the most salient variables eliminated, but such sterile settings are often _____ laughter.", "choices": ["inimical to", "devoid of", "subverted by", "adverse to", "replete with", "rife with"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "역설(paradox) + but 대조: 이상적 실험은 엄격히 통제된 환경에서 이뤄지지만, 그런 무균적 환경은 웃음에 ___.\n빈칸 = 웃음 연구에 '불리하다, 웃음을 억제한다'는 뜻.\ninimical to(~에 해로운)와 adverse to(~에 불리한)가 같은 의미.\n정답: A (inimical to), D (adverse to)", "trap": "devoid of(~이 없는)는 문맥상 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없음. replete with/rife with는 짝이지만 정반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inimical to": "~에 해로운, 적대적인", "devoid of": "~이 없는", "subverted by": "~에 의해 전복된", "adverse to": "~에 불리한, 반하는", "replete with": "~로 가득한", "rife with": "~이 만연한"}, "src": "verbal216 Q12 · 25년 5월, 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following would it be most useful to establish in order to evaluate the argument?", "choices": ["Whether symptoms of amatrox are experienced only when the virus is detectable", "Whether there is a drug that is more effective than vericol in treating the symptoms of amatrox", "Whether by taking vericol someone who has never been infected by the amatrox virus can be protected from becoming infected", "Whether a person who has had amatrox in the past can be reinfected with the virus", "Whether a person who is being treated with vericol can transmit the amatrox virus"], "columns": null, "pid": "v198_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: vericol은 바이러스를 검출 불가 수준으로 억제할 뿐 완전히 제거하지는 못함.\n근거: 치료 중단 후 몇 달 내 증상과 바이러스가 다시 나타남.\n가정: 다시 나타난 바이러스는 '원래 남아 있던 것'이지 '새로 감염된 것'이 아님(열대지방의 전염성 높은 질병!).\n→ 재감염이 가능한지 확인하면 논증 평가 가능 = D.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(증상은 바이러스가 검출될 때만 나타나는가)는 그럴듯하지만, 증상과 검출이 함께 돌아온 상황이라 어느 쪽 답이든 '남아 있던 바이러스 vs 재감염' 문제를 해결하지 못함.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"suppress": "억제하다", "detectable": "검출 가능한", "discontinue": "중단하다", "reinfect": "재감염시키다"}, "src": "verbal198 Q13 · 24년 10월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following can be inferred from the passage about \"large-scale voter studies\"?", "choices": ["They are not well suited for drawing conclusions about certain population groups.", "They are insufficiently concerned with producing valid and generalizable results.", "They have helped give rise to political science's focus on decision-making in a narrow range of contexts.", "They remain unappealing to mainstream journals.", "They are becoming less popular among political scientists."], "columns": null, "pid": "v220_p5", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'pressure to do large-scale voter studies ... placed those interested in African American politics at a disadvantage, because the relevant empirical data on the Black population were insufficient to render findings that were externally valid and generalizable.'\n→ 대규모 유권자 연구는 특정 인구 집단(흑인)에 대해 결론을 내리기에 적합하지 않음 = A.\n정답: A", "trap": "B는 정반대: 대규모 연구는 일반화 가능성을 '요구'하며, 문제는 흑인 데이터 부족. D는 오히려 주류 학계가 대규모 연구를 선호함.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "large-scale voter studies", "glosses": {"empirical": "경험적인, 실증적인", "externally valid": "외적 타당성이 있는", "generalizable": "일반화 가능한"}, "src": "verbal220 Q5 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v220_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, Wilson has proposed that political science's \"lagging behind\" can be explained in part by", "choices": ["the greater number of mainstream journals in both history and sociology as compared with political science", "the tendency for political scientists to focus on relatively recent events", "a narrow emphasis within political science on particular levels of decision-making", "a shift in emphasis in mainstream political science journals away from African American topics", "misinterpretations by political scientists of relevant data on African American voters"], "columns": null, "pid": "v220_p5", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Wilson의 두 번째 설명: 'the discipline's traditional focus on politics and decision-making processes at levels to which African Americans have historically had limited access—a narrow focus'.\n→ 특정 수준의 의사결정에 대한 좁은 강조 = C.\n정답: C", "trap": "E는 '흑인 유권자 데이터'를 끌어왔지만 지문은 데이터가 '불충분'하다고 했지 '잘못 해석'했다고 하지 않음. A는 학술지 수 비교가 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "lagging behind", "glosses": {"methodological": "방법론적인", "discipline": "학문 분야", "mainstream": "주류의"}, "src": "verbal220 Q6 · 25년 5월 중국후기"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.5 / S2 2.7"}, {"set": 31, "sections": [[{"id": "v25_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The _____ repeating real-time climatological measurements largely prevents correcting inaccurate readings made in the past.", "choices": ["need for", "impossibility of", "history of", "consensus about", "approach to"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "핵심: 빈칸 ___ repeating measurements가 '과거의 부정확한 측정값 수정을 막는다(prevents correcting)'.\n실시간(real-time) 측정은 그 순간에만 가능하므로 다시 반복할 수 없다 → 그래서 과거 값을 고칠 수 없음.\n빈칸 = '반복할 수 없음'이라는 뜻.\nimpossibility of(~의 불가능성)가 인과관계를 정확히 완성.\n정답: B (impossibility of)", "trap": "need for: '반복할 필요'는 수정을 '막는' 원인이 될 수 없음. 오히려 수정을 돕는 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"need for": "~의 필요성", "impossibility of": "~의 불가능성", "history of": "~의 역사", "consensus about": "~에 대한 합의", "approach to": "~에 대한 접근법"}, "src": "verbal25 Q1"}, {"id": "v19_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Seemingly to compensate for the (i)__________ nature of her subject, in her review the theater critic (ii)__________ a casual chatty style.", "choices": null, "columns": [["undemanding", "rarefied", "well-defined"], ["opted for", "misused", "invited"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'to compensate for(~을 보완하려고)' → 주제의 성격과 문체가 반대여야 함.\n(ii) 비평가가 casual chatty style을 '선택했다' → opted for. (misused/invited는 문체에 어색)\n(i) 가볍고 수다스러운 문체로 보완해야 할 주제 = 어렵고 전문적인 주제 → rarefied.\n정답: rarefied / opted for (B, D)", "trap": "undemanding: 주제가 쉬우면 굳이 가벼운 문체로 '보완'할 이유가 없음 — 방향이 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"undemanding": "쉬운, 힘들지 않은", "rarefied": "난해한, 소수만 아는, 고상한", "well-defined": "명확히 정의된", "opted for": "~을 택했다", "misused": "오용했다", "invited": "초래했다, 초대했다"}, "src": "verbal19 Q2"}, {"id": "v233_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Why Zona Gale—a Pulitzer Prize-winning writer whose novels were both a critical and popular success—has fallen so far out of the literary canon is the fascinating subject of Deborah Lindsay Williams' recent book. Williams concludes that Gale's embrace of literary (i) _____ accounts for her eventual decline in reputation. Gale sought professional affiliation with other women writers of many stripes, and Williams contends that she has therefore been (ii) _____ by a later literary paradigm that favors (iii) _____ as a marker of artistic prowess.", "choices": null, "columns": [["fame", "conservatism", "sisterhood"], ["marginalized", "studied", "overrated"], ["sociological accuracy", "bold risk-taking", "individual exceptionalism"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CDI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 다음 문장 'sought professional affiliation with other women writers' = 여성 작가들과의 연대 → sisterhood.\n(ii) 문맥: 정전(canon)에서 밀려남(fallen out), 명성 하락 → marginalized(주변화되었다).\n(iii) 연대(집단성)를 추구한 Gale을 불리하게 만드는 패러다임 = 연대와 반대되는 가치 → individual exceptionalism(개인의 탁월함).\n정답: sisterhood / marginalized / individual exceptionalism (C, D, I)", "trap": "bold risk-taking: 그럴듯해 보이지만 '여성 작가와의 연대'와 대비되는 개념이 아님. 대비 축은 집단 vs 개인.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"fame": "명성", "conservatism": "보수성", "sisterhood": "자매애, 여성 간 연대", "marginalized": "주변화된, 소외된", "studied": "연구된", "overrated": "과대평가된", "sociological accuracy": "사회학적 정확성", "bold risk-taking": "대담한 모험", "individual exceptionalism": "개인의 탁월함(예외성)"}, "src": "verbal233 Q3 · 25년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v205_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the passage, the function of the highlighted portion is to", "choices": ["Provide specific examples of organisms whose longevity does not increase in response to calorie restriction", "Illustrate the probable means by which organisms placed on a calorie-restriction diet compensate for the reduction in available food-based level", "Suggest the mechanism that is responsible for prolonging the life of organism whose calorie intake is significantly reduced", "Give an example that explain why scientists’ thinking about the physiological effects of calorie restriction changed", "Distinguish the different ways that mammalian and non-mammalian metabolisms respond to significant reductions in calorie intake"], "columns": null, "pid": "v205_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: 수명 연장 현상은 오랫동안 '대사 둔화' 때문이라고 여겨졌다 → In fact, however, 포유류 대사는 느려지지 않고, 효모·벌레에서는 오히려 빨라지고 변한다 → 그래서 과학자들은 이제 새 이론(스트레스 반응)을 제시.\n하이라이트(in yeast and worms, metabolism is both sped up and altered)는 기존 설명을 반박하는 사례.\n즉 과학자들의 생각이 바뀐 이유를 보여주는 예 → D.\n정답: D", "trap": "E: 포유류와 비포유류의 차이를 '구별'하는 것이 목적이 아니라, 둘 다 기존 '대사 둔화' 설명과 맞지 않음을 보여주는 것. A는 수명이 늘지 않는다는 말이 없으므로 틀림.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"calorie restriction": "칼로리 제한", "forestall": "미연에 방지하다", "metabolism": "신진대사", "stressor": "스트레스 요인"}, "src": "verbal205 Q4 · 25/4, 25/2, 24/9, 24/8, 23/6, 22/12, 22/9, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v205_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage implies which of the following about the explanation mentioned in the highlighted portion?", "choices": ["There are empirical findings that conflict with a presumption of the explanation.", "The explanation predicts that the effect of calorie restriction on longevity will be the greatest for the species with the highest rate of metabolism.", "The explanation predicts that the effects of calorie restriction will be uniformly positive."], "columns": null, "pid": "v205_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "해당 설명: 'This phenomenon was long attributed to a simple slowing of metabolism' — 칼로리 제한 → 대사 둔화가 전제.\n바로 뒤 'In fact, however, calorie restriction does not slow mammalian metabolism'; 효모·벌레는 오히려 대사가 빨라짐 → 설명의 전제와 충돌하는 실증 결과 → A 맞음.\nB: 대사율이 가장 높은 종에서 효과가 최대라는 예측은 본문에 없음.\nC: '균일하게 긍정적'이라는 예측도 언급 없음.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 대사와 관련된 내용이라 그럴듯하지만, 종별 대사율 비교에 대한 예측은 본문 범위 밖(out of scope).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "This phenomenon was long attributed to a simple slowing of metabolism", "glosses": {"attribute A to B": "A를 B 탓/덕으로 돌리다", "empirical": "실증적인", "presumption": "전제, 가정", "uniformly": "균일하게"}, "src": "verbal205 Q5 · 25/4, 25/2, 24/9, 24/8, 23/6, 22/12, 22/9, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v235_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Yang Hong's studies of ancient Chinese tombs transcribe the tombs' epitaphs and inscriptions, noting whether these texts corroborate available information about the deceased's life or ancestry or _____ it by presenting biographical material not found elsewhere.", "choices": ["disseminate", "contradict", "supplement", "obviate", "augment", "promulgate"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: corroborate(확증하다) A or ___ it by presenting biographical material not found elsewhere.\n'다른 곳에 없는 전기 자료를 제시함으로써' → 기존 정보에 새 내용을 더한다 = 보충하다.\nsupplement / augment = 보충하다, 늘리다.\n정답: C, E (supplement, augment)", "trap": "contradict: corroborate의 반대어라 끌리지만, '새로운 자료를 제시'하는 것은 반박이 아니라 추가. 짝도 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"disseminate": "퍼뜨리다", "contradict": "반박하다, 모순되다", "supplement": "보충하다", "obviate": "불필요하게 하다, 미연에 제거하다", "augment": "늘리다, 증대시키다", "promulgate": "공포하다, 널리 알리다"}, "src": "verbal235 Q9 · 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v239_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "When Ms. Alvarez campaigns, she tends to _____ small towns, most of her campaign appearances occur in large population centers and media markets.", "choices": ["denigrate", "eschew", "romanticize", "shun", "castigate", "overlook"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 쉼표 뒤 '대부분의 유세는 대도시와 미디어 시장에서 열린다' → 작은 마을은 피한다.\n빈칸 = '피하다, 가지 않다'.\neschew / shun = (의도적으로) 피하다.\n정답: B, D (eschew, shun)", "trap": "overlook: '간과하다'는 의도치 않게 못 보는 것이라 의미가 약간 다르고, 짝이 없음. denigrate/castigate는 '비난'이라 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"denigrate": "폄하하다", "eschew": "피하다, 삼가다", "romanticize": "낭만화하다, 미화하다", "shun": "피하다, 멀리하다", "castigate": "혹평하다, 꾸짖다", "overlook": "간과하다"}, "src": "verbal239 Q6 · 24년 2월, 22년 9월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v209_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The Red Sea town of Aydhab presents scholars with _____: medieval records describe it as a major port for ships engaged in trade, yet today there is no trace of a viable harbor at the site.", "choices": ["an illusion", "a contradiction", "a chimera", "a puzzle", "an anachronism", "a conundrum"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 빈칸을 설명: 기록상 주요 항구였는데(yet) 지금은 항구 흔적이 없다 → 설명하기 어려운 수수께끼.\n빈칸 = '풀기 어려운 문제'.\npuzzle / conundrum = 수수께끼, 난제.\n정답: D, F (a puzzle, a conundrum)", "trap": "a contradiction: 기록과 현실이 '모순'처럼 보여 끌리지만 짝이 없고, 학자에게 주는 것은 풀어야 할 '수수께끼'. illusion/chimera는 짝이지만 항구가 '환상'이라는 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"an illusion": "환상, 착각", "a contradiction": "모순", "a chimera": "망상, 허황된 꿈", "a puzzle": "수수께끼", "an anachronism": "시대착오(적인 것)", "a conundrum": "난제, 수수께끼"}, "src": "verbal209 Q8 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v223_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author argued that the industrial agricultural system that prevails in the United States is unsustainable and, therefore, anything that _____ it should be questioned.", "choices": ["streamlines", "reinforces", "encumbers", "buttresses", "endangers", "hampers"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "논리: 시스템이 지속 불가능하다(unsustainable) → therefore 그 시스템을 '___하는 것'은 의문시되어야 한다.\n문제 있는 시스템을 '강화·지지'하는 것을 의심해야 함.\nreinforces / buttresses = 강화하다, 떠받치다.\n정답: B, D", "trap": "encumbers/hampers(방해하다)는 짝이지만 방향이 반대 — 나쁜 시스템을 방해하는 것은 의심할 이유가 없음. streamlines는 짝 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"streamlines": "간소화하다, 효율화하다", "reinforces": "강화하다", "encumbers": "방해하다, 짐을 지우다", "buttresses": "지지하다, 떠받치다", "endangers": "위태롭게 하다", "hampers": "방해하다"}, "src": "verbal223 Q9 · 25/11, 25/10, 25/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v219_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true about Chaudhuri's work?", "choices": ["Most of it is now available in print in India.", "Its ornate prose style has made it unpopular with many Indian readers.", "lts political sentiments were more defensible in the context of the 1950s than they were in the context of the 1990s.", "It contains political sentiments unpopular with many Indian intellectuals.", "In the opinion of many writers, its merit lies primarily in its treatment of historical issues."], "columns": null, "pid": "v219_p10", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'largely because of controversial political opinions, has been shunned by much of the Indian intelligentsia'.\n논란이 되는 정치적 견해 때문에 인도 지식인들에게 외면당함 → D가 그대로 paraphrase.\n정답: D", "trap": "B: 'indulgent meandering and excessive allusion'은 문체 비판이지만, 그것 때문에 인도 독자에게 인기 없다는 말은 없음. A: 1997 이후 재출간된 것은 Autobiography뿐이라 '대부분'은 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"intelligentsia": "지식인 계층", "shun": "외면하다", "controversial": "논란이 많은"}, "src": "verbal219 Q10 · 25년 3월, 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v219_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage would agree with which of the following statements about Chaudhuri's work?", "choices": ["It was widely admired by Indian academics, but little known by academics in other countries.", "It was respected internationally by writers of nonfiction, but virtually unknown among English novelists.", "It was respected internationally and by certain major writers, but not widely read in Chaudhuri's native country.", "It was greatly influential among creative writers in India, but undervalued by creative writers in the United States and England.", "It has only recently been discovered by literary critics and by university faculty in both the United States and lndia."], "columns": null, "pid": "v219_p10", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'long acknowledged internationally', Naipaul·Lessing 같은 대작가들의 찬사 → 국제적으로, 주요 작가들에게 존경받음.\n'shunned by Indian intelligentsia', 1997년까지 인도에서 구할 수 없었음, 'more discussed than read' → 모국에서 널리 읽히지 않음.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 인도 학계에서 널리 존경받았다는 것은 정반대. E: 미국 대학에서 비평서가 표준 교재라는 것은 '최근 발견'이 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"acknowledged": "인정받은", "meandering": "장황하게 헤맴", "allusion": "암시, 인유"}, "src": "verbal219 Q11 · 25년 3월, 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v219_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage most probably mentions Salman Rushdie as an example of a writer who", "choices": ["has contributed to Chaudhuri's growing international prestige", "shares certain of Chaudhuri's shortcomings", "has been heavily influenced in literary style by Chaudhuri's work", "differs from Chaudhuri in his political views", "is often contrasted with Chaudhuri in university courses about Indian writers"], "columns": null, "pid": "v219_p10", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'At his best ... superb; but in his sometimes indulgent meandering and excessive allusion, Chaudhuri's work resembles that of ... Rushdie.'\nbut 뒤의 단점(장황함, 과도한 인유) 측면에서 Rushdie와 닮았다 → 단점을 공유하는 작가.\n정답: B", "trap": "C: 'resembles'는 닮았다는 것일 뿐 Chaudhuri의 영향을 받았다는 인과 관계는 없음. 'later' writer라는 말에 속기 쉬움.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"indulgent": "방종한, 제멋대로인", "excessive": "과도한", "resemble": "닮다"}, "src": "verbal219 Q12 · 25년 3월, 24년 12월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v2_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The movie has a surfeit of inscrutable characters and tortuous subplots, so it is no surprise that viewers leaving the recent screening appeared _____.", "choices": ["complacent", "phlegmatic", "nonplussed", "unsated", "beguiled"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 이해하기 어려운 인물(inscrutable characters)과 꼬인 줄거리(tortuous subplots)가 과잉 → so(결과) 관객이 ___해 보이는 건 당연.\n빈칸 = '혼란스러운, 어리둥절한'.\nnonplussed = 당황한, 어찌할 바를 모르는.\n정답: C", "trap": "unsated(만족 못한)도 부정적이라 끌리지만 '이해 불가'의 결과로는 혼란이 더 직접적. phlegmatic은 '침착한'이라 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"surfeit": "과잉", "tortuous": "꼬여있는", "phlegmatic": "냉정한, 침착한", "nonplussed": "당황한, 어리둥절한", "complacent": "자기만족적인, 안주하는", "unsated": "만족하지 못한", "beguiled": "매혹된, 속은"}, "src": "verbal2 Q2"}, {"id": "v240_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "By using (i) _____ prose throughout, the contributors to this anthology have been able to make their subject seem (ii) _____ in the extreme—of concern only to one another.", "choices": null, "columns": [["luminous", "esoteric", "colloquial"], ["parochial", "pragmatic", "egalitarian"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 대시(—) 뒤 'of concern only to one another(자기들끼리만 관심 있는)' → 편협한, 좁은 범위의 → parochial.\n(i) 주제를 내부자 전용으로 보이게 만드는 문체 = 소수만 이해하는 난해한 문체 → esoteric.\n정답: esoteric / parochial (B, D)", "trap": "colloquial(구어체)은 오히려 대중에게 다가가는 문체라 반대. luminous(명료한)도 방향이 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"parochial": "편협한, 좁은 범위의", "luminous": "명료한, 빛나는", "esoteric": "난해한, 소수만 아는", "colloquial": "구어체의", "pragmatic": "실용적인", "egalitarian": "평등주의적인"}, "src": "verbal240 Q2 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v8_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Paleoclimatic records recovered from land, the ocean, and glacial ice (i) _____ a (ii) _____ global climate over much of the last glacial cycle. Indeed, in many locations in the Northern Hemisphere, changes in climate spanning almost the full range of glacial to interglacial conditions were so (iii) _____ that the transition between climate states occurred in decades or less.", "choices": null, "columns": [["exaggerate", "confirm", "redefine"], ["potent driver of", "simple fact about", "lack of stability in"], ["abrupt", "unpredictable", "enduring"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BFG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "두 번째 문장 'Indeed'는 첫 문장을 강화: 빙하기~간빙기 전환이 '수십 년 이내'에 일어났다.\n(iii) 수십 년 안에 전환 → 급격한 → abrupt.\n(ii) 기후가 급변했다 → 기후의 불안정성 → lack of stability in.\n(i) 기록이 이를 '확인한다' → confirm (Indeed로 이어지는 증거 제시).\n정답: confirm / lack of stability in / abrupt (B, F, G)", "trap": "unpredictable: 불안정성과 어울려 보이지만 '수십 년 이내에 전환'은 예측 불가가 아니라 '속도'의 문제 → abrupt.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exaggerate": "과장하다", "confirm": "확인하다, 입증하다", "redefine": "재정의하다", "potent driver of": "~의 강력한 원동력", "simple fact about": "~에 관한 단순한 사실", "lack of stability in": "~의 불안정성", "abrupt": "급작스러운", "unpredictable": "예측 불가능한", "enduring": "오래 지속되는"}, "src": "verbal8 Q3"}, {"id": "v16_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The traditional set of nine planets could have been retained by defining a planet as any object that has the unique combination of characteristics of any one of the nine objects that were considered planets in the late twentieth century. That definition would not be (i) _____; that is, it does not contradict the evidence. Its (ii) _____, however, renders it less (iii) _____ than definitions based on astronomical criteria, such as orbit, size, and gravitation.", "choices": null, "columns": [["paradoxical", "subjective", "false"], ["arbitrariness", "inconsistency", "generality"], ["expedient", "stable", "defensible"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CDI", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'that is, it does not contradict the evidence' = 빈칸의 정의. 증거와 모순되지 않음 = 틀리지 않음 → not false.\n(ii) however: 사실과 맞지만 문제가 있음. '9개 천체 중 하나의 특성 조합을 가진 것'이라는 정의는 천문학적 원리 없이 임의로 정한 것 → arbitrariness.\n(iii) 궤도·크기 같은 천문학적 기준에 근거한 정의보다 '덜 옹호할 만하다' → defensible.\n정답: false / arbitrariness / defensible (C, D, I)", "trap": "(i) paradoxical, subjective: 'does not contradict the evidence'를 직접 정의하는 것은 false뿐. (iii) expedient(편리한)는 임의적 정의가 오히려 편리할 수 있어 방향이 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"paradoxical": "역설적인", "subjective": "주관적인", "false": "틀린, 거짓의", "arbitrariness": "임의성, 자의성", "inconsistency": "비일관성", "generality": "일반성", "expedient": "편리한, 방편적인", "stable": "안정적인", "defensible": "옹호할 수 있는, 타당한"}, "src": "verbal16 Q3"}, {"id": "v20_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author would most likely agree with which of the following statements about Scorsese's film adaptation of 《The Age of Innocence》?", "choices": ["It is not as true to the novel as are other film adaptations of Wharton's works.", "It has encouraged a misguided impression of Wharton and her work.", "It was based on a highly unusual interpretation of 《The Age of Innocence》.", "It did some damage to Wharton's reputation as a major figure in modern fiction.", "It spent too much time dwelling on subject matter that many would consider un-Whartonesque."], "columns": null, "pid": "v20_p3", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Yet she remains firmly enshrined as a scion of rarefied, upper-class America, an image reinforced by Scorsese's ... film'.\n저자는 이 상류층 이미지가 'the wrong kind of reputation'이라고 봄 → 영화가 잘못된 인상을 강화.\n정답: B", "trap": "D: 영화가 '명성을 손상시켰다'는 것은 지나침. 저자는 명성이 secure하지만 '잘못된 종류'라고 했을 뿐.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"enshrine": "모시다, 고이 간직하다", "scion": "자손, 후예", "rarefied": "고상한, 상류층의", "mores": "관습, 도덕관"}, "src": "verbal20 Q12"}, {"id": "v20_q13", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author implies which of the following about the challenge referred to in the highlighted sentence (\"Even sympathetic … mores.\")?", "choices": ["It goes against the main current of modern fiction.", "It has recently become a matter of scholarly controversy.", "It became bolder and more pronounced at the end of Wharton's career.", "It does not manifest itself in Wharton's novel 《The Age of Innocence》.", "It spanned all or nearly all of Wharton's writing career."], "columns": null, "pid": "v20_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "하이라이트: Wharton이 당대 관습에 도전한 정도.\n다음 문장 'Between her early novel ... (1905) and her last ... (1938), Wharton addressed subjects ... un-Whartonesque' → 초기작부터 마지막 작품까지 도전적 주제를 다룸.\n즉 그 도전은 경력 전반에 걸쳐 있었다 → E.\n정답: E", "trap": "C: '말년에 더 대담해졌다'는 변화에 대한 근거 없음. 'between early and last'는 기간 전체를 말할 뿐.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"mores": "관습, 도덕관", "effete": "나약한, 퇴폐적인", "genteel": "고상한 체하는"}, "src": "verbal20 Q13"}, {"id": "v214_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage takes the “significant changes” to be an indication of which of the following?", "choices": ["That the 1776 suffrage clause was not established without critical examination", "That there was little consensus among legislators regarding the final version of the 1776 suffrage clause", "That the 1776 suffrage clause was not a deviation from the norm that prevailed in other states", "That there was at least some public agitation in favor of voting rights for women prior to 1776", "That legislators in 1776 were seriously concerned about the overdemocratization of the voting process"], "columns": null, "pid": "v214_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the 1776 suffrage clause underwent close legislative scrutiny that led to several significant changes; thus, the absence of gender references ... was probably not accidental.'\n중요한 수정들 = 면밀한 입법 검토(close scrutiny)를 거쳤다는 증거 → 비판적 검토 없이 만들어진 게 아니다.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 수정이 있었다고 해서 의원들 간 합의가 부족했다는 뜻은 아님. E: overdemocratization 우려는 마지막 문장의 순자산 요건 이야기로, '수정'의 의미와 무관.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "significant changes", "glosses": {"scrutiny": "면밀한 검토", "suffrage": "참정권", "consensus": "합의"}, "src": "verbal214 Q7 · 24/11, 23/4, 22/10, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v214_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the last sentence of the passage?", "choices": ["To suggest that New Jersey legislators in 1776 were insincere in their commitment to voting rights for women", "To indicate that there was a lack of consensus among New Jersey legislators regarding the final version of the 1776 suffrage clause", "To indicate that the New Jersey legislators in 1776 did not favor unqualified access to voting rights", "To undermine the evidence suggesting that New Jersey legislators in 1776 believed that all who possessed sufficient net worth were entitled to vote", "To suggest that the absence of gender references in the final version of the 1776 suffrage clause may have been accidental"], "columns": null, "pid": "v214_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: 순자산 요건을 갖춘 사람은 모두 투표권이 있다고 믿었다.\n마지막 문장 'However, they also saw the net worth qualification as serving to prevent an overdemocratization' → 재산 요건으로 과도한 민주화를 막으려 함.\n즉 무조건적 투표권 부여를 지지하지 않았다 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "D: However가 있어 앞 내용을 '약화'하는 것처럼 보이지만, 실제로는 앞 내용을 부정하지 않고 보완하는 설명(재산 요건의 목적)을 추가할 뿐.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "However, they also saw the net worth qualification as serving to prevent an overdemocratization of the voting process.", "glosses": {"choice D": "오히려 보완적 설명", "overdemocratization": "과도한 민주화", "qualification": "자격 요건", "unqualified": "무조건적인, 제한 없는"}, "src": "verbal214 Q8 · 24/11, 23/4, 22/10, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v214_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author of the passage suggests that if there had been public agitation regarding voting rights for women in New Jersey prior to 1776, then this agitation would have", "choices": ["been largely in opposition to voting rights for women rather than in favor of those rights", "exerted an important influence on the final version of the 1776 New Jersey suffrage clause", "potentially provided historians with an explanation for the New Jersey legislature's decision in 1776 regarding voting rights", "made New Jersey's political culture less unusual in comparison to other states", "made it less likely that New Jersey would disenfranchise women sometime after 1776"], "columns": null, "pid": "v214_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Political historians have been perplexed by New Jersey's deviation ..., finding no sign of public agitation either for or against ...'\n역사가들이 당혹스러워한 이유 = 대중 운동의 흔적이 없어 설명할 근거가 없어서.\n따라서 만약 대중 운동이 있었다면 역사가들에게 입법 결정의 설명을 제공했을 것 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "B: 최종 조항에 '중요한 영향을 미쳤을 것'은 지나친 단정. 본문은 그것이 설명의 실마리가 되었을 것이라는 수준만 시사.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"perplexed": "당혹스러운", "agitation": "(정치적) 운동, 선동", "enfranchisement": "참정권 부여", "disenfranchisement": "참정권 박탈"}, "src": "verbal214 Q9 · 24/11, 23/4, 22/10, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The vast majority of universities in the United States promote themselves as institutions of free speech and thought, construing censorship as _____ their search for knowledge.", "choices": ["subordinate to", "obviated by", "secondary to", "antipathetic to", "conducive to", "inconsistent with"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 대학들은 스스로를 '자유로운 발언과 사상의 기관'으로 홍보 → 검열(censorship)을 지식 탐구와 '상충하는' 것으로 본다.\n빈칸 = '~와 맞지 않는, 적대적인'.\nantipathetic to / inconsistent with.\n정답: D, F", "trap": "subordinate to/secondary to(~보다 부차적인)는 짝이지만, 검열을 '부차적'이라 하는 건 자유 강조와 맞지 않음. conducive to는 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"subordinate to": "~에 종속된, 부차적인", "obviated by": "~에 의해 불필요해진", "secondary to": "~보다 부차적인", "antipathetic to": "~에 반감을 가진, 상충하는", "conducive to": "~에 도움이 되는", "inconsistent with": "~와 모순되는, 맞지 않는"}, "src": "verbal230 Q10 · 25/3, 23/8, 23/5, 22/6 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Stannard may be hoping to resurrect Spark's literary reputation with this book, given its _____ praise for her creative talents.", "choices": ["unctuous", "genuine", "grudging", "reluctant", "unstinting", "generous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "EF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 작가의 문학적 명성을 '되살리려는(resurrect)' 의도 → 칭찬이 아낌없고 후해야 함.\n빈칸 = 강한 긍정의 칭찬.\nunstinting / generous = 아낌없는, 후한.\n정답: E, F", "trap": "genuine(진심 어린)도 긍정이지만 짝이 없음. grudging/reluctant는 짝이지만 '마지못한' 칭찬으로는 명성을 되살리기 어려움.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unctuous": "번지르르한, 아첨하는", "grudging": "마지못해 하는", "unstinting": "아낌없는, 후한", "genuine": "진심의, 진짜의", "reluctant": "꺼리는, 마지못한", "generous": "후한, 관대한"}, "src": "verbal198 Q11 · 24년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v22_q11", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The historical study of pregnancy and childbearing began fairly recently and has been hindered by the relative __________ of records concerning these particular experiences.", "choices": ["pertinence", "dearth", "paucity", "ambiguity", "expediency", "applicability"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 연구가 '방해받았다(hindered)' + 'relative ___ of records' → 기록이 부족하다.\n빈칸 = 부족, 결핍.\ndearth / paucity = 부족.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "ambiguity(모호성)도 연구를 방해할 수 있어 끌리지만 짝이 없음. 'relative'와 어울리는 것은 양의 부족.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pertinence": "적절성, 관련성", "dearth": "부족, 결핍", "paucity": "부족, 소량", "ambiguity": "모호성", "expediency": "편의, 방편", "applicability": "적용 가능성"}, "src": "verbal22 Q11"}, {"id": "v212_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, most helps to explain why those fish species benefit from having such lenses?", "choices": ["Most of the fish with the tinted lenses hunt from below, locating their prey by the shadows passing overhead.", "In general, the fish with the tinted lenses feed on fish and other marine organisms that live at depths near 1,000 meters or deeper.", "The eyes of most fish that live significantly below the surface waters can detect light of only a limited color range.", "Most marine organisms living at depths near 1,000 meters are bioluminescent, emitting green light that is hard for most fish to distinguish from the background sunlight.", "Below 1,000 meters there is, on average, another 3,000 meters of ocean depth in which there is no sunlight at all."], "columns": null, "pid": "v212_p3", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "현상: 1,000m 깊이에서는 햇빛이 거의 파란색뿐인데, 일부 어류는 파란빛을 걸러내는 렌즈를 가짐 → 왜 유리할까?\nD: 이 깊이의 생물 대부분이 초록빛을 내지만 배경 햇빛(파란색)과 구별이 어렵다 → 파란 배경을 걸러내면 초록빛 생물(먹이 등)이 잘 보임.\n정답: D", "trap": "A: 그림자로 먹이를 찾는다면 파란 배경 빛이 오히려 필요함 — 파란빛을 걸러내면 불리. E는 1,000m 아래의 무관한 정보.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"bioluminescent": "생물 발광하는", "penetrate": "투과하다", "tinted": "착색된"}, "src": "verbal212 Q13 · 24년 2월, 23년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v4_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that \"small packets of leaf fragments\" were", "choices": ["preferred by Indian consumers over other forms of tea", "too valuable to be sold in large packets to consumers", "marketed in response to a local surplus of unsold tea leaves", "likely to sell for high prices if exported", "an ineffective way to expand the local tea market"], "columns": null, "pid": "v4_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'made only sporadic, small-scale attempts ... selling small packets of leaf fragments. Still, by 1930 only a fraction of the Indian population had tasted tea'.\nonly, sporadic, small-scale + Still(그런데도) 극소수만 차를 맛봄 → 국내 시장 확대에 효과가 없었음.\n정답: E", "trap": "C: 재고 과잉(unsold surplus)은 대공황 이후(1935)의 일로, 이 작은 시도 시기와 다름 — 시간 순서 혼동.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "small packets of leaf fragments", "glosses": {"sporadic": "산발적인", "fraction": "일부, 소수", "surplus": "잉여, 과잉"}, "src": "verbal4 Q12"}, {"id": "v4_q13", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that the Tea Cess Committee reorganized as the Indian Tea Market Expansion Board in order to", "choices": ["appeal to Indian consumers' sense of national identity", "escape the TCC's reputation for selling low-quality tea", "increase the prestige of tea by emphasizing its exotic origins", "receive a larger budget for marketing tea in India", "respond to economic conditions created by the Great Depression"], "columns": null, "pid": "v4_p3", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'The Great Depression decisively changed the picture' → 가격 폭락, 미판매 잉여 → 'uninitiated' 국내 시장이 매력적으로 보임 → TCC가 ITMEB로 재편.\n재편은 대공황이 만든 경제 상황에 대응하기 위한 것 → E.\n정답: E", "trap": "D: 예산이 확대된 것은 재편과 함께 일어난 일(provided with an expanded budget)이지 재편의 '목적'으로 제시된 것이 아님.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"plunge": "폭락하다", "uninitiated": "경험 없는, 문외한의", "reorganize": "재편하다"}, "src": "verbal4 Q13"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.3 / S2 2.5"}, {"set": 32, "sections": [[{"id": "v239_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The mating system of humpback whales appears to rely on _____: although humpbacks are found in widely varying densities throughout any winter breeding range, they frequently return in large numbers to specific locations.", "choices": ["competition", "aggregation", "courtship", "adaptability", "innovation"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤 설명: 번식지 전반에 밀도는 다양하지만(although), 특정 장소로 '대거(in large numbers)' 돌아온다.\n빈칸 = 한곳에 모이는 것.\naggregation = 집결, 집합.\n정답: B", "trap": "courtship(구애)이나 competition(경쟁)은 짝짓기와 관련돼 보이지만 콜론 뒤 근거(특정 장소에 대거 모임)와 직접 연결되지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"competition": "경쟁", "aggregation": "집결, 군집", "courtship": "구애", "adaptability": "적응력", "innovation": "혁신"}, "src": "verbal239 Q1 · 24년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v17_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Although Kito Hiroshi's portrait of Edo Japan as (i)__________ is certainly (ii)__________, the fundamental factors of population stability and resource renewal generally did favor social maintenance and even economic growth.", "choices": null, "columns": [["outwardly aggressive", "perfectly harmonious", "slowly developing"], ["derivative", "positive", "overdrawn"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Although(양보) — Kito의 묘사는 ~하지만, 근본 요인들은 실제로(did) 사회 유지와 경제 성장에 유리했다.\n→ Kito의 묘사는 긍정적이지만 '과장'되었다는 구조.\n(i) 사회 유지·성장과 같은 방향의 긍정적 묘사 → perfectly harmonious.\n(ii) 'perfectly'를 비판 → overdrawn(과장된).\n정답: perfectly harmonious / overdrawn (B, F)", "trap": "positive: 묘사가 긍정적인 건 맞지만 Although와 결합하면 대조가 성립하지 않음. 양보 구조에는 '과장되었다'는 비판이 필요.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"outwardly aggressive": "대외적으로 공격적인", "perfectly harmonious": "완벽하게 조화로운", "slowly developing": "서서히 발전하는", "derivative": "독창성 없는, 모방한", "positive": "긍정적인", "overdrawn": "과장된"}, "src": "verbal17 Q2"}, {"id": "v3_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "The potential (i) _____ exploiting mineral resources in the area combined with (ii) _____ participation among local people in conservation efforts may lead to a (iii) _____ human appreciation for the landscape and eventually contribute to disadvantageous effects for conservation.", "choices": null, "columns": [["rewards in", "ban on", "danger in"], ["an increase of interest in", "a lack of benefits for", "a shift in the direction of"], ["rise in", "shrinkage of", "dependency on"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AEH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: '보전에 불리한 효과(disadvantageous effects for conservation)'에 기여 → 모든 빈칸은 보전에 부정적인 방향.\n(i) 광물 개발의 잠재적 '이익' → 사람들이 개발 쪽으로 끌림 → rewards in.\n(ii) 지역 주민의 보전 참여에 '혜택이 없음' → a lack of benefits for.\n(iii) 경관에 대한 인간의 애정이 '줄어듦' → shrinkage of.\n정답: rewards in / a lack of benefits for / shrinkage of (A, E, H)", "trap": "(i) danger in: '위험'이 있다면 오히려 개발을 막아 보전에 유리 — 방향이 반대. (iii) rise in도 보전에 유리해서 결론과 모순.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rewards in": "~의 이익, 보상", "ban on": "~에 대한 금지", "danger in": "~의 위험", "an increase of interest in": "~에 대한 관심 증가", "a lack of benefits for": "~에 대한 혜택 부족", "a shift in the direction of": "~ 방향으로의 전환", "rise in": "~의 증가", "shrinkage of": "~의 감소, 위축", "dependency on": "~에 대한 의존"}, "src": "verbal3 Q3"}, {"id": "v213_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about the “fish populations”?", "choices": ["They were more diverse in the late 1970s than observers recognized at the time.", "They were more adversely affected by the growth of vegetation after the ban on grazing than by avian predation.", "They required a habitat that could not be sustained without measures to limit animal grazing.", "They proliferated following changes to Bharatpur’s ecosystem introduced by the ban on grazing.", "They migrated to habitats that were inhospitable to grazing cattle and buffalo."], "columns": null, "pid": "v213_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Weed species were taking over wetlands and choking canals, thereby reducing the fish populations', 그 후 'avian species then went elsewhere'.\n새들이 떠나 조류의 포식 압력은 줄었는데도 물고기는 감소 → 물고기 감소의 주원인은 잡초(식생) 증가.\n즉 새의 포식보다 식생 증가에 더 큰 타격 → B.\n정답: B", "trap": "C: '방목 제한 조치 없이는 유지될 수 없는 서식지'는 정반대 — 실제로는 방목이 '있어야' 서식지가 유지됨. D도 방목 금지 후 물고기가 감소했으므로 반대.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "fish populations", "glosses": {"plummet": "급락하다", "culprit": "원인, 범인", "proliferate": "급증하다", "inhospitable": "살기 힘든"}, "src": "verbal213 Q4 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v213_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following statements, if true, would best explain the changes in “weed species”?", "choices": ["The species were not native to Bharatpur but spread rapidly once they were introduced.", "The species had been kept in check by the large avian populations that once nested in Bharatpur.", "The species were among the preferred forage plants grazed on by cattle and buffalo.", "The species were necessary for maintaining suitable habitats for fish populations in Bharatpur’s wetlands.", "The species were unable to tolerate changing water conditions in the canals of Bharatpur."], "columns": null, "pid": "v213_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'The absence of grazing animals ... had disturbed the park's ecology. Weed species were taking over wetlands'.\n방목 금지 후 잡초가 번성한 이유가 필요 → 그 잡초가 소·물소가 즐겨 뜯어 먹던 풀이었다면, 방목이 사라지자 억제 요인이 없어져 번성.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 외래종이 빠르게 퍼졌다는 설명은 '방목 금지'와 잡초 증가의 연결을 설명하지 못함. B: 새가 잡초를 억제했다면 새 감소 이전에 잡초가 늘어난 순서가 설명되지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Weed species", "glosses": {"forage": "사료, 꼴", "graze": "풀을 뜯다", "keep in check": "억제하다"}, "src": "verbal213 Q5 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v225_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The article has been abridged for presentation to a nonspecialist audience, and the _____ by which this has been accomplished can be frustrating for any reader trying to reconstruct the argument in detail.", "choices": ["elisions", "expedients", "elaborations", "conflations", "omissions", "annotations"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 일반 독자용으로 '축약(abridged)'됨 → 축약 수단 = 빼기 → 논증을 자세히 재구성하려는 독자에게 답답함.\n빈칸 = 생략.\nelisions / omissions = 생략.\n정답: A, E", "trap": "expedients(방편, 수단)는 'by which'와 문법적으로 잘 맞아 끌리지만 짝이 없음. conflations(융합)도 축약과 관련돼 보이지만 짝이 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"elisions": "생략", "expedients": "방편, 임시 수단", "elaborations": "상술, 부연", "conflations": "융합, 합성", "omissions": "생략, 누락", "annotations": "주석"}, "src": "verbal225 Q9 · 25년 4월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v13_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "It is true that propagandists spout misinformation to serve their own ends, but if our minds were _____ such garbage, the lies would die out quickly.", "choices": ["inhospitable to", "amenable to", "unreceptive to", "unaffected by", "distorted by", "governable by"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "구조: 가정법 'if our minds were ___ such garbage, the lies would die out quickly' → 거짓말이 빨리 사라지려면 우리 마음이 그런 쓰레기(허위정보)를 받아들이지 않아야 함.\n빈칸 = 수용하지 않는.\ninhospitable to / unreceptive to.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "unaffected by(영향받지 않는)도 그럴듯하지만, 핵심은 '받아들이지 않음'으로 정보가 퍼질 토양이 없어지는 것. 짝이 없음. amenable to는 정반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inhospitable to": "~에 호의적이지 않은, 받아들이지 않는", "amenable to": "~을 잘 받아들이는", "unreceptive to": "~을 받아들이지 않는", "unaffected by": "~에 영향받지 않는", "distorted by": "~에 의해 왜곡된", "governable by": "~에 의해 통제 가능한"}, "src": "verbal13 Q6"}, {"id": "v9_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Biologists agree that snakes descended from lizards, but exactly where this first happened has been a matter of debate since the 1800s, when two _____ theories emerged.", "choices": ["complex", "competing", "dubious", "conclusive", "contending", "irrefutable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'a matter of debate since the 1800s' → 두 이론이 서로 경쟁/대립.\n빈칸 = 경쟁하는.\ncompeting / contending.\n정답: B, E", "trap": "dubious(의심스러운)는 논쟁과 어울려 보이지만 짝이 없음. conclusive/irrefutable은 짝이지만 '논쟁 중'과 모순.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"complex": "복잡한", "competing": "경쟁하는", "dubious": "의심스러운", "conclusive": "결정적인", "contending": "경쟁하는, 다투는", "irrefutable": "반박할 수 없는"}, "src": "verbal9 Q6"}, {"id": "v221_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The capacity for rational thought and its manifestation in language have long been assumed to distinguish human from nonhuman animals, but apes' proven ability to learn and teach sign language to other apes suggests that such a strict human-animal divide is _____.", "choices": ["indeterminable", "indefensible", "untenable", "intolerable", "inevitable", "unavoidable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: but — 이성적 사고와 언어가 인간을 구별한다고 오랫동안 가정됨, 그러나 유인원이 수화를 배우고 가르침 → 엄격한 인간-동물 구분은 '유지될 수 없다'.\n빈칸 = 옹호할 수 없는.\nindefensible / untenable.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "indeterminable(결정할 수 없는)은 비슷해 보이지만 '판단 불가'일 뿐 '틀렸다'는 뜻이 아님. inevitable/unavoidable은 짝이지만 반대 방향.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"untenable": "옹호할 수 없는, 지지 못할", "indeterminable": "결정할 수 없는", "indefensible": "옹호할 수 없는", "intolerable": "견딜 수 없는", "inevitable": "불가피한", "unavoidable": "피할 수 없는"}, "src": "verbal221 Q9 · 25년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v1_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, would best support the plant permissive hypothesis?", "choices": ["Aphids that feed on different species of plants produce honeydew of varying quality.", "Seasonal changes in the quality of phloem sap are a common phenomenon in plants.", "Many aphid species with extremely nutritious honeydew are not attended by ants.", "Some species of aphids inhabit more than one species of plant.", "The Rocky Mountain region and Central Europe have few plant species in common."], "columns": null, "pid": "v1_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "plant permissive hypothesis: 숙주 식물의 질이 감로(honeydew)의 질에 영향을 주고, 그것이 개미에 대한 매력을 결정.\n가설의 핵심 연결고리: 식물 → 감로의 질.\nA: 다른 식물을 먹는 진딧물은 서로 다른 질의 감로를 생산 → 식물이 감로의 질을 좌우한다는 전제를 직접 뒷받침.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 수액 질의 계절 변화는 흔한 현상일 뿐, 그것이 감로·개미 유인과 연결된다는 근거가 없음. C는 오히려 가설을 약화.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"phloem sap": "체관 수액", "honeydew": "감로(진딧물 분비물)", "myrmecophile": "개미와 공생하는 동물", "attend": "(개미가 진딧물을) 돌보다"}, "src": "verbal1 Q10"}, {"id": "v1_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence in the context of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["It presents empirical data that will be used to support a claim stated later in the passage.", "It summarizes the discussion about similarities between two regions earlier in the passage.", "It points to a key factor that is commonly overlooked by study of ant-aphid interactions.", "It elaborates on an explanation that will be faced with several objections later in the passage.", "It explains why it has been challenging to solve the puzzle mentioned earlier in the passage."], "columns": null, "pid": "v1_p2", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "하이라이트 'Both variation in the quality of different hosts ... more or less attractive to ants.'는 앞 문장의 plant permissive hypothesis를 구체적으로 설명.\n바로 뒤 'However, this hypothesis ignores ... and assumes ...' → 가설에 대한 반론 두 가지(같은 식물에서도 개미와의 관계가 다름; 수액 질 = 감로 질이라는 가정).\n즉 나중에 반론에 직면할 설명을 상술 → D.\n정답: D", "trap": "C: '흔히 간과되는 핵심 요인'은 지나침 — 이 가설은 'First among them'으로 소개된 주요 가설이지, 간과된 요인이 아님. A는 경험적 데이터가 아니라 가설 설명.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"elaborate on": "상술하다", "obligate": "절대적인, 필수적인", "host plant": "숙주 식물"}, "src": "verbal1 Q11"}, {"id": "v1_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Based on the passage, which of the following can be most plausibly inferred about \"Recent studies\"?", "choices": ["Their findings are questionable because some of the behaviors investigated may depend on plant quality.", "They were most likely conducted outside of the two regions mentioned at the beginning of the passage.", "Their results show that associations between ant species and aphid species are usually temporary.", "They were conducted only on aphid species that were known to be obligate myrmecophiles.", "They have produced some data that may be construed as evidence for the plant permissive hypothesis."], "columns": null, "pid": "v1_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Recent studies have found that feeding on woody plant parts is positively associated with ant attendance'.\n목질부(woody plant parts)를 먹느냐 = 식물의 어느 부분을 먹느냐가 개미 attendance와 연관 → 'different parts of the same host plant'가 중요하다는 plant permissive hypothesis를 지지하는 증거로 해석 가능.\n'may be construed'라는 약한 표현도 적절.\n정답: E", "trap": "A: 일부 행동이 식물 질에 의존할 수 있다는 것은 추측일 뿐, 그 때문에 결과가 '의심스럽다'는 근거는 본문에 없음. B, D는 범위 밖.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "Recent studies", "glosses": {"construe": "해석하다", "woody": "목질의", "mobility": "이동성", "attendance": "(개미의) 돌봄"}, "src": "verbal1 Q12"}], [{"id": "v8_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Ronald Ferguson, whose work is widely admired by policy makers, has never been profiled by the news media, perhaps because his views are _____ and therefore difficult to capture in a sound bite.", "choices": ["nuanced", "controversial", "empirical", "influential", "unorthodox"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'and therefore difficult to capture in a sound bite' → 짧은 한마디로 요약하기 어려운 견해.\n빈칸 = 미묘하고 복잡한.\nnuanced = 미묘한 차이가 있는, 섬세한.\n정답: A", "trap": "controversial/unorthodox: 논란이 되는 견해는 오히려 짧고 자극적인 한마디로 잡기 쉬워 언론이 좋아함 — 'therefore difficult'와 인과가 맞지 않음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sound bite": "핵심만 짧고 강렬하게 편집한 한마디", "nuanced": "미묘한, 섬세한", "controversial": "논란이 많은", "empirical": "실증적인", "influential": "영향력 있는", "unorthodox": "정통에서 벗어난"}, "src": "verbal8 Q1"}, {"id": "v208_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "At its best, the storytelling in this television series manages to accommodate a sense of historical (i) _____. The narrative shows that American independence was not (ii) _____. It was debated. It didn't happen overnight. No one was sure how it would turn out.", "choices": null, "columns": [["contingency", "plausibility", "constancy"], ["inevitable", "unforeseen", "unremarkable"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "뒷문장들이 설명: 독립은 논쟁되었고, 하룻밤에 일어나지 않았고, 아무도 결과를 확신하지 못했다.\n(ii) 독립은 '필연적이지' 않았다 → inevitable.\n(i) 역사가 정해진 게 아니라 다른 결과도 가능했다는 감각 → contingency(우연성, 불확정성).\n정답: contingency / inevitable (A, D)", "trap": "(ii) unforeseen: '예견되지 않은' 것이 아니었다고 하면 오히려 예상된 결과가 되어 '아무도 확신 못했다'와 모순. (i) constancy는 반대 개념.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inevitable": "필연적인, 불가피한", "plausibility": "그럴듯함, 타당성", "contingency": "우연성, 불확정성", "constancy": "불변성", "unforeseen": "예견되지 않은", "unremarkable": "주목할 것 없는, 평범한"}, "src": "verbal208 Q2 · 25년 8월, 23년 3월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v32_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Some academic criticism of popular novels has been (i) _____ in character, being based on the assumption that the wider the appeal, the more (ii) _____ the novel.", "choices": null, "columns": [["rigorous", "exculpatory", "elitist"], ["undesirable", "accomplished", "comprehensible"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(ii) 전제: 대중적 인기가 넓을수록 소설이 더 ___ → 비판의 근거이므로 부정적 → undesirable.\n(i) '인기 많을수록 나쁘다'는 가정에 기반한 비평 = 대중을 깔보는 → elitist.\n정답: elitist / undesirable (C, D)", "trap": "(i) rigorous(엄격한)는 학술 비평과 잘 어울려 보이지만, '인기 = 나쁨'이라는 가정은 엄밀함이 아니라 편견.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exculpatory": "면죄해주는", "rigorous": "엄격한, 엄밀한", "elitist": "엘리트주의적인", "undesirable": "바람직하지 않은", "accomplished": "뛰어난, 완성도 높은", "comprehensible": "이해할 수 있는"}, "src": "verbal32 Q3"}, {"id": "v34_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Conventionally, the ultimate measure of a scientific work’s validity is how broadly and confidently its conclusions become accepted in the relevant field, which in turn (i) _____ the extent to which its findings are replicated and extended. However, establishing such validity, especially for a novel experimental finding, can take years, and what (ii) _____ replication or extension may be (iii) _____ for some time.", "choices": null, "columns": [["derives from", "works against", "leads to"], ["justifies", "impugns", "constitutes"], ["evident", "disputed", "touted"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 결론이 얼마나 받아들여지는지는 ← 발견이 얼마나 재현·확장되는지에서 나온다 → derives from(~에서 비롯되다).\n(ii)(iii) However: 타당성 확립은 수년이 걸리고, 무엇이 재현이나 확장을 '구성하는지(constitutes)'조차 한동안 '논쟁 중(disputed)'일 수 있다.\n정답: derives from / constitutes / disputed (A, F, H)", "trap": "(i) leads to: 인과 방향이 반대 — 수용이 재현을 낳는 게 아니라 재현이 수용을 낳음. (iii) evident는 '수년이 걸린다'는 However 흐름과 모순.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"derives from": "~에서 비롯되다", "works against": "~에 불리하게 작용하다", "leads to": "~으로 이어지다", "justifies": "정당화하다", "impugns": "이의를 제기하다, 공격하다", "constitutes": "구성하다, ~에 해당하다", "evident": "명백한", "disputed": "논쟁 중인", "touted": "선전된, 칭찬받는"}, "src": "verbal34 Q4"}, {"id": "v218_q5", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following details regarding the lotus-shaped ewer supports the claim of the \"other authorities\" about the dating of that ewer?", "choices": ["The style of the ewer's incised lotus petals", "The location at which the ewer was found", "The ewer's distinctive shape"], "columns": null, "pid": "v218_p5", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Other authorities contend this ewer instead dates to the previous century, citing the similarity of its incised lotus-petals to other surviving pieces of that era.'\nA: 새겨진 연꽃잎의 양식 → 직접 근거.\nB: 발견 장소(1257년 무덤)는 오히려 첫 번째 견해(1200년대)의 근거.\nC: 독특한 모양은 언급 없음.\n정답: A", "trap": "B: 무덤 위치가 연대 논쟁에 등장하지만, 그것은 'Some authorities'의 근거 — 견해를 뒤바꾼 함정.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "Other authorities", "glosses": {"ewer": "물병, 주전자", "incised": "새겨진", "celadon": "청자", "excavate": "발굴하다"}, "src": "verbal218 Q5 · 25/8, 25/4, 24/12, 24/9, 24/6, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v218_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary function of the highlighted sentence is to", "choices": ["emphasize the long-standing tradition of crafting decorative ceramics in Korea", "emphasize the high esteem placed upon antique ceramics in Korea during the 1200s", "present concrete evidence that discredits one view regarding the age of the ewer", "provide a rationale in support of an earlier dating for the ewer", "compare early uses of copper-decorated ceramics in Korea to later uses"], "columns": null, "pid": "v218_p5", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "하이라이트: 그들은 그 물병이 묻힐 때 이미 오래된 것(아마 귀한 골동품)이었다고 주장.\n역할: 1257년 무덤에서 나왔는데도 12세기(이전 세기) 것이라는 '더 이른 연대'를 가능하게 하는 논리적 근거 제시.\n정답: D", "trap": "B: 'treasured antique'라는 말 때문에 골동품에 대한 존중을 강조하는 것처럼 보이지만, 'perhaps'로 말한 부수적 추측일 뿐 목적은 연대 주장의 근거. C: 구체적 증거가 아니라 추론.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"rationale": "논리적 근거", "antique": "골동품", "discredit": "신빙성을 떨어뜨리다"}, "src": "verbal218 Q6 · 25/8, 25/4, 24/12, 24/9, 24/6, 23/2 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q7", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, astronomers’ belief that comets are pristine relics was", "choices": ["overturned by analysis of what happens when comets approach the Sun", "supported by what observations revealed about the composition of the outer planets", "based on consideration of the conditions that prevail where comets are located"], "columns": null, "pid": "v200_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'comets—because they remain mostly in the distant Oort cloud, where temperatures are close to absolute zero—must be pristine relics'.\nC: 혜성이 있는 곳(오르트 구름)의 조건(절대영도에 가까운 온도)에 기반 → 맞음.\nA: 믿음의 전환은 실험실 시뮬레이션에서 시작; 태양 접근 시 표면이 벗겨진다는 것은 오히려 믿음을 유지시킨 생각.\nB: 외행성 구성에 대한 관측은 언급 없음.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 'approach the Sun'이 본문에 나와 끌리지만, 그것은 믿음을 '뒤집은' 분석이 아니라 내부는 순수하다는 믿음을 지키려던 생각.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"pristine": "원래 그대로의, 오염되지 않은", "relic": "유물, 잔존물", "absolute zero": "절대영도"}, "src": "verbal200 Q7 · 25/4, 25/1, 24/9, 24/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author suggests that the realization described in the final sentence of the passage had which of the following effects?", "choices": ["It introduced a new topic for study by astronomers interested in planetary formation.", "It led astronomers to adopt a number of different strategies in trying to determine the composition of cometary interiors.", "It called into question an assumption that astronomers had made about comets.", "It cast doubt on astronomers’ ability to study the interior parts of comets.", "It caused astronomers to revise their account of the composition of the outer planets"], "columns": null, "pid": "v200_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: 천문학자들은 태양 열이 오염된 표면을 제거하면 '순수한 내부'가 드러날 것이라고 여전히 믿음.\n마지막 문장: 방사성 동위원소가 내부를 데워 내부도 변했을(evolve) 수 있음 → '내부는 원래 그대로'라는 가정에 의문 제기.\n정답: C", "trap": "D: 내부를 '연구할 능력'에 의문을 제기한 것이 아니라 내부가 '순수한지'에 의문을 제기한 것. A: 새 연구 주제를 소개했다는 언급은 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "About the same time, though, scientists realized comets might contain decaying radioactive isotopes that could have warmed cometary interiors to temperatures that caused the interiors to evolve.", "glosses": {"isotope": "동위원소", "decay": "붕괴하다", "evolve": "변화하다, 진화하다"}, "src": "verbal200 Q8 · 25/4, 25/1, 24/9, 24/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v200_q9", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author would agree with which of the following statements about the “laboratory simulations”?", "choices": ["The simulations showed that despite the low temperatures in the Oort cloud, there was sufficient energy there to alter comet.", "Astronomers were initially reluctant to accept what simulation showed about the composition of comets.", "The simulations themselves did not eliminate the possibility that comets contain pristine relics of material from the early solar system."], "columns": null, "pid": "v200_p2", "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'laboratory simulations revealed there was sufficient ultraviolet radiation ... to darken their surfaces and ... cosmic rays to alter chemical bonds ... near the surface'.\nA: 절대영도에 가까운 온도에도 혜성을 변화시킬 만한 에너지(자외선, 우주선)가 있었다 → 맞음.\nC: 시뮬레이션은 '표면 근처'의 변화만 보여줌 → 내부가 순수할 가능성은 남음(그래서 천문학자들이 Nevertheless 내부는 순수하다고 믿음) → 맞음.\nB: 천문학자들이 처음에 수용을 꺼렸다는 근거 없음.\n정답: A, C", "trap": "B: 'Nevertheless, astronomers still believed'를 보고 시뮬레이션 결과를 거부했다고 착각하기 쉬움. 실제로는 표면 변화는 받아들이고 내부만 순수하다고 본 것.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": "laboratory simulations", "glosses": {"cosmic rays": "우주선(우주 방사선)", "ultraviolet radiation": "자외선", "molecular structure": "분자 구조"}, "src": "verbal200 Q9 · 25/4, 25/1, 24/9, 24/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v232_q12", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Scholars of the civil rights movement have often characterized it as springing from social, political, and economic structures _____ the South, thus overlooking the tradition of civil rights activism in other regions of the country.", "choices": ["originating in", "imposed on", "perpetuated by", "unique to", "characteristic of", "detrimental to"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: 'thus overlooking the tradition of civil rights activism in other regions' → 학자들은 민권운동이 남부에만 있는 구조에서 생겼다고 봄.\n빈칸 = 남부 특유의.\nunique to / characteristic of = ~에 고유한, ~ 특유의.\n정답: D, E", "trap": "originating in(~에서 기원한)은 그럴듯하지만 '다른 지역을 간과'하는 결과를 만들려면 남부'만의' 구조라는 배타성이 필요. imposed on/detrimental to는 근거 없음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"originating in": "~에서 비롯된", "imposed on": "~에 강요된", "perpetuated by": "~에 의해 지속된", "unique to": "~에 고유한", "characteristic of": "~ 특유의, 전형적인", "detrimental to": "~에 해로운"}, "src": "verbal232 Q12 · 25/10, 25/8, 25/1, 24/9, 23/11, 23/6, 23/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Though Fine leavens her work with humor and playfulness, she can be _____ writer, mincing no words in her judgments of other scientists’ work.", "choices": ["an acerbic", "a provocative", "an ingratiating", "a demanding", "an obsequious", "a harsh"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "단서: Though(대조) 유머와 장난기로 작품을 부드럽게 하지만 → 반대로 신랄할 수 있음. 'mincing no words(말을 가리지 않고)' 다른 과학자의 연구를 평가.\n빈칸 = 신랄한, 가혹한.\nacerbic / harsh.\n정답: A, F", "trap": "provocative(도발적인)도 끌리지만 짝이 없고 '말을 가리지 않는 판단'의 핵심은 가혹함. demanding도 짝 없음.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"an acerbic": "신랄한", "a provocative": "도발적인", "an ingratiating": "환심을 사려는", "a demanding": "요구가 많은, 까다로운", "an obsequious": "아첨하는", "a harsh": "가혹한, 거친"}, "src": "verbal198 Q10 · 25/5, 25/2, 24/5, 23/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v8_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "In owls with a facial disk, the ears are hidden behind it and are _____ placed: having one higher than the other allows the birds to locate prey both horizontally and vertically for more accurate detection.", "choices": ["advantageously", "asymmetrically", "unevenly", "unobtrusively", "discreetly", "precisely"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤 설명: 'having one higher than the other' — 한쪽 귀가 다른 쪽보다 높다.\n빈칸 = 비대칭적으로, 고르지 않게.\nasymmetrically / unevenly.\n정답: B, C", "trap": "advantageously: 위치 덕분에 먹이를 더 정확히 탐지하므로 '유리하게'도 맞아 보이지만 짝이 없음. unobtrusively/discreetly는 'hidden'에 끌린 함정.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"advantageously": "유리하게", "asymmetrically": "비대칭적으로", "unevenly": "고르지 않게", "unobtrusively": "눈에 띄지 않게", "discreetly": "신중하게, 눈에 띄지 않게", "precisely": "정확하게"}, "src": "verbal8 Q10"}, {"id": "v226_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, most seriously weakens the mayor's argument?", "choices": ["Admission to the community pool will cost most residents who frequently use it more than they would have paid in increased taxes for a pool open to all residents free of charge.", "Because of the types of accidents that can happen in and around swimming pools, the largest part of the operating expenses for the community pool will be lifeguards’ salaries and liability insurance.", "The operation of a pool would bring increased traffic to the road leading to the site of the proposed pool and would require the town to fund costly road improvements.", "The same survey that established that a majority of Oakville's residents would use a community pool also found that over one-third of the town's residents would have preferred that it be built at a different site.", "Opponents of the pool have not advanced any other proposals for the use of the currently unused town-owned land parcel."], "columns": null, "pid": "v226_p3", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "시장의 결론: 수영장 건설은 세금 인상으로 이어지지 않는다.\n근거: 부지는 무료(미사용 시유지), 입장료가 운영비 + 300만 달러 부채 상환을 모두 충당.\n가정: 수영장 관련 추가 비용은 없다.\nC: 수영장 운영으로 교통량이 늘어 비싼 도로 개선이 필요 → 입장료가 커버하지 않는 추가 비용 + 시는 재정 준비금 없음 → 세금 인상 가능성.\n정답: C", "trap": "A: 주민이 입장료로 내는 돈이 세금보다 많다는 것은 '세금이 오르지 않는다'는 결론을 약화하지 않음(세금 자체는 그대로). B: 운영비 구성일 뿐, 입장료가 충당한다는 주장을 반박하지 않음.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"financial reserves": "재정 준비금", "admission fee": "입장료", "parcel": "(토지) 구획"}, "src": "verbal226 Q13 · 24년 3월, 22년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v2_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following does the author suggest as an incentive to the development of more efficient irrigation?", "choices": ["Treatment and reuse of urban wastewater", "Revised pricing of water", "Reduced costs for urban wastewater treatment", "Development of new water sources", "Reduced urban water use"], "columns": null, "pid": "v2_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 첫 문장 'More appropriate water pricing would promote the treatment and reuse ... and also encourage improvements in irrigation efficiency.'\n더 적절한 물 가격 책정 = 수정된 물 가격 → 관개 효율 개선의 유인(incentive).\n정답: B", "trap": "A: 하수 처리·재사용은 물 가격 책정이 촉진하는 '또 다른 결과'이지, 관개 효율의 유인이 아님 — 병렬 관계를 인과로 착각.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"irrigation": "관개", "wastewater": "하수, 폐수", "incentive": "유인, 동기"}, "src": "verbal2 Q14"}, {"id": "v2_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following does the author present as generally the most cost-effective way of meeting demand for water for irrigation?", "choices": ["Reducing the amount of water consumed by large cities", "Treating wastewater that is currently being dumped", "Increasing the efficiency of current irrigation systems", "Having new wells drilled", "Increasing the efficiency of current wastewater treatment projects"], "columns": null, "pid": "v2_p4", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Treatment and reuse is more expensive than most irrigation-related conservation and efficiency measures but often less expensive than developing new water sources.'\n비용 순서: 관개 보존·효율 조치 < 하수 처리·재사용 < 새 수원 개발.\n가장 비용 효율적인 방법 = 현재 관개 시스템의 효율 향상 → C.\n정답: C", "trap": "B: 하수 처리가 '새 수원 개발보다 싸다'는 부분만 보고 고르기 쉬움. 하지만 관개 효율 조치보다는 비쌈.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"cost-effective": "비용 효율적인", "conservation": "보존, 절약", "reliable": "신뢰할 수 있는"}, "src": "verbal2 Q15"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.9 / S2 2.6"}, {"set": 33, "sections": [[{"id": "v203_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Because carbon is a relatively _____ element, much of the original carbon available to be incorporated in the Earth may have escaped during the accretion of the planet.", "choices": ["amorphous", "abundant", "inert", "malleable", "volatile"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "인과 신호 'Because': 탄소의 성질 때문에 행성 형성(accretion) 중 원래 탄소의 상당량이 '빠져나갔다(escaped)'.\n빈칸 = 쉽게 날아가 버리는 성질, 즉 '휘발성이 있는'이라는 뜻이 필요.\nvolatile(휘발성의)이 escaped와 정확히 인과로 연결된다.\n정답: E (volatile)", "trap": "inert(비활성의)는 화학 반응을 안 한다는 뜻일 뿐 빠져나가는 이유가 되지 못하고, abundant는 오히려 많이 남았어야 한다는 쪽이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"amorphous": "형태가 없는, 비정질의", "abundant": "풍부한", "inert": "비활성의, 둔한", "malleable": "펴서 늘일 수 있는, 유연한", "volatile": "휘발성의, 변덕스러운"}, "src": "verbal203 Q1 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v21_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "An affinity for (i)__________ is a characteristic of Bynum's work and of her rhetorical strategy as a historian, and it is often both refreshing and illuminating. But this predilection for (ii)__________ can be vexing, too, by appearing to eschew necessary distinctions.", "choices": null, "columns": [["paradox", "humor", "understatement"], ["daring hyperbole", "indiscriminate eclecticism", "unresolvable ambivalences"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: Bynum의 작업과 수사 전략의 특징인 (i)에 대한 애호 → 신선하고 깨달음을 준다(긍정).\n둘째 문장 'But this predilection for (ii)' → (ii)는 (i)을 다시 가리키는 말(this)이어야 하며, '필요한 구분을 회피하는 것처럼 보인다'는 단점과 연결.\n(i) paradox(역설): 모순되는 것을 함께 붙잡는 것 → 신선하고 통찰을 줄 수 있음.\n(ii) unresolvable ambivalences(해결되지 않는 양가성) = paradox의 재진술. 상반된 것을 끝까지 구분하지 않고 둘 다 유지하니 '구분을 회피'하는 것처럼 보인다.\n정답: A (paradox), F (unresolvable ambivalences)", "trap": "indiscriminate eclecticism은 '구분 없이(indiscriminate)'가 eschew distinctions와 겹쳐 보여 매력적이지만, (i)의 어떤 단어도 '절충주의'를 재진술하지 못한다. this predilection은 (i)과 같은 대상이어야 한다.", "difficulty": 5, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"paradox": "역설", "humor": "유머", "understatement": "절제된 표현, 축소해서 말하기", "daring hyperbole": "대담한 과장", "indiscriminate eclecticism": "무분별한 절충주의", "unresolvable ambivalences": "해결할 수 없는 양가감정(모순)"}, "src": "verbal21 Q2"}, {"id": "v225_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Early practitioners of the natural sciences developed methods to remove distortions caused by either the research environment or the researcher. Such methods, especially with respect to the researcher, were considered to (i) _____ those (ii) _____ subjectivity whose unbridled expression was thought to (iii) _____ research.", "choices": null, "columns": [["restrain", "reveal", "disguise"], ["incursions of", "restrictions on", "acknowledgements of"], ["corrupt", "justify", "expedite"]], "pid": null, "answer": "ADG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장: 초기 과학자들은 연구 환경이나 연구자로 인한 '왜곡을 제거하는' 방법을 개발.\n(iii) 주관성의 무절제한 표현은 연구를 망친다고 여겨짐 → corrupt(오염시키다).\n(ii) 연구에 끼어드는 주관성 → incursions of(~의 침입).\n(i) 그런 방법은 주관성의 침입을 억제한다고 여겨짐 → restrain.\n정답: A (restrain), D (incursions of), G (corrupt)", "trap": "restrictions on을 고르면 '주관성에 대한 제한을 억제한다'가 되어 왜곡 제거라는 취지와 반대가 된다. reveal도 제거와 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"restrain": "억제하다", "reveal": "드러내다", "disguise": "위장하다, 숨기다", "incursions of": "~의 침입, 개입", "restrictions on": "~에 대한 제한", "acknowledgements of": "~의 인정", "corrupt": "오염시키다, 타락시키다", "justify": "정당화하다", "expedite": "촉진하다"}, "src": "verbal225 Q3 · 25/12, 25/11, 23/10 중국후기"}, {"id": "v31_q4", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, the “shifting-baseline syndrome” is a result of which of the following?", "choices": ["Modest recovery objectives determined by political pragmatism", "The difficulty of determining existing population size and number of populations for endangered species", "Changes in the criteria that are used in determining whether a given quantitative objective has been met", "Each new generation of wildlife managers using recent conditions to set numerical baselines for wildlife populations", "The way that hopes for recovery of endangered species populations color the expectations of successive generations of wildlife managers"], "columns": null, "pid": "v31_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'successive generations of wildlife managers use as their baseline the conditions they experienced at the start of their careers, resulting in lower expectations'.\n즉 각 세대 관리자가 자기 경력 초기(최근)의 상태를 기준선으로 삼는 것이 원인이다.\nD가 이를 그대로 바꿔 말함.\n정답: D", "trap": "A(정치적 실용주의로 정해진 낮은 목표)는 shifting-baseline과 별개의 '다른 설명'이며, 오히려 낮은 목표는 증후군의 결과이지 원인이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"baseline": "기준선", "palatable": "받아들일 만한, 입맛에 맞는", "pragmatism": "실용주의", "successive": "연속적인, 잇따른"}, "src": "verbal31 Q4"}, {"id": "v25_q5", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, would enable the conclusion of the argument to be properly drawn?", "choices": ["The only place where Consuelo enjoys widely recommended movies is a movie theater.", "Widely recommended movies are never shown on airplanes.", "If a movie shown on an airplane is not widely derided, then it is invariably widely recommended.", "If the picture quality of the movies shown on airplanes was better, Consuelo would enjoy the widely recommended movies.", "Some movies are neither widely recommended nor widely derided."], "columns": null, "pid": "v25_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "전제1: 비행기에서는 널리 추천된 영화를 절대 즐기지 않음. 전제2: 널리 혹평받은 영화는 어디서든 즐기지 않음.\n결론: 비행기에서 어떤 영화도 즐기지 않음.\n빈틈: 추천도 혹평도 아닌 '중간' 영화가 비행기에서 상영될 수 있음.\nC: 비행기 영화가 혹평받지 않았다면 반드시 추천받은 것 → 모든 비행기 영화가 둘 중 하나에 속하므로 결론이 성립.\n정답: C", "trap": "B(추천 영화는 비행기에서 상영되지 않는다)는 오히려 상영 영화가 혹평작이나 중간 영화라는 뜻이라 중간 영화 문제가 그대로 남는다. E는 빈틈을 지적할 뿐 결론을 약화시킨다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"widely derided": "널리 조롱/혹평받는", "invariably": "언제나, 반드시"}, "src": "verbal25 Q5"}, {"id": "v211_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Williams argues that philosophy has become _____ occupation these days, and that it should rather be \"part of a more general attempt to make the best sense of our life.\"", "choices": ["a recondite", "an acknowledged", "an esoteric", "an exacting", "a salacious", "an altruistic"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Williams는 철학이 요즘 _____ 직업이 되었다고 비판하며, 오히려 '우리 삶을 이해하려는 더 일반적인 시도의 일부'가 되어야 한다고 함.\n'rather ... more general' 대조 → 빈칸 = 일반인과 동떨어진, 소수만 아는, 난해한.\nrecondite와 esoteric이 '난해한, 소수만 이해하는'으로 짝.\n정답: A (a recondite), C (an esoteric)", "trap": "exacting(까다로운)은 어렵다는 느낌은 맞지만 '일반적인 삶과 동떨어진'이라는 대조가 없고 짝 단어도 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"recondite": "심오한, 난해한", "salacious": "외설스러운", "acknowledged": "인정받는", "esoteric": "소수만 이해하는, 난해한", "exacting": "까다로운, 엄격한", "altruistic": "이타적인"}, "src": "verbal211 Q9 · 25/10, 25/9, 25/4, 25/3, 24/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v197_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Individuals, governments, and companies show ample ability to _____ themselves by setting goals based on current conditions and then blindly following them even when those conditions change drastically.", "choices": ["hamstring", "reinvent", "promote", "revitalize", "impair", "invigorate"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "현재 조건에 근거해 목표를 세우고, 조건이 크게 바뀌어도 맹목적으로 따른다(blindly following) → 스스로에게 해를 끼침.\n빈칸 = 부정, '스스로를 방해하다/손상시키다'.\n'show ample ability to'는 반어적 표현(스스로 망치는 능력이 넘친다).\nhamstring과 impair가 '불구로 만들다, 손상시키다'로 짝.\n정답: A (hamstring), E (impair)", "trap": "reinvent/revitalize/invigorate는 긍정어라 'blindly following'과 맞지 않는다. 'ample ability'라는 긍정적 표현에 속지 말 것.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hamstring": "무력화하다, 발목 잡다", "reinvent": "재창조하다", "promote": "촉진하다, 홍보하다", "revitalize": "활성화하다, 되살리다", "impair": "손상시키다", "invigorate": "기운 나게 하다"}, "src": "verbal197 Q9 · 25/4, 24/12, 24/11, 24/8, 24/6, 23/12, 23/2, 22/5 중국후기"}, {"id": "v9_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Some of the characters and themes depicted on the painted glass vessels found at Begram point toward an Egyptian provenance, but Egypt was not the _____ and perhaps not even the principal place of manufacture.", "choices": ["main", "leading", "sole", "likeliest", "original", "exclusive"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "일부 특징이 이집트 기원을 가리키지만(but), 이집트가 _____ 생산지가 아니었고 '심지어 주된(principal) 생산지도 아니었을 수 있다'.\n'perhaps not even' 구조 → 빈칸은 principal보다 강한 주장이어야 함 → '유일한'.\nsole과 exclusive가 짝.\n정답: C (sole), F (exclusive)", "trap": "main과 leading은 서로 짝은 되지만 principal과 같은 말이라 'not even principal'과 중복되어 논리가 깨진다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"provenance": "기원", "main": "주된", "leading": "선도적인, 주된", "sole": "유일한", "likeliest": "가장 가능성 높은", "original": "원래의", "exclusive": "독점적인, 유일한"}, "src": "verbal9 Q7"}, {"id": "v225_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Titan, Saturn’s largest moon, looks surprisingly _____, even though it is a cold, dimly lit world made from unknown materials.", "choices": ["habitable", "familiar", "forbidding", "placid", "daunting", "recognizable"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'even though' 양보: 차갑고 어둡고 미지의 물질로 된 세계 '인데도' 놀랍게도 _____ 해 보인다.\n빈칸 = 낯섦과 반대, '익숙한, 알아볼 만한'.\nfamiliar와 recognizable이 짝.\n정답: B (familiar), F (recognizable)", "trap": "forbidding과 daunting은 짝이지만 '차갑고 어두운'과 같은 방향이라 surprisingly/even though의 대조가 사라진다. habitable은 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"recognizable": "알아볼 수 있는, 익숙한", "habitable": "거주 가능한", "familiar": "익숙한", "forbidding": "험악한, 가까이하기 어려운", "placid": "잔잔한, 평온한", "daunting": "위압적인, 벅찬"}, "src": "verbal225 Q8 · 24/3, 23/11, 23/5, 22/9, 22/7 중국후기"}, {"id": "v197_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage is primarily concerned with", "choices": ["discussing a controversial aspect of specific legislation relating to CO2", "explaining the science of a new process for capturing CO2", "highlighting the shortcomings of a specific method of combating climate change", "arguing that emission technologies are the most effective method of combating climate change", "summarizing the advantages of relying on legislation to combat climate change"], "columns": null, "pid": "v197_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "글은 45Q 법안을 소개한 뒤 'The most controversial use is enhanced oil recovery'에 초점을 맞춰, 비판(위장된 화석연료 보조금)과 옹호(배출 감소, 상업화의 첫걸음)를 함께 다룬다.\n→ 특정 법안의 논란이 되는 측면을 논의.\n정답: A", "trap": "C(단점 강조)는 비판만 다룬 것처럼 한쪽으로 치우쳤다. 글은 오히려 옹호 논거로 끝난다. B는 과학적 원리 설명이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sequestered": "격리된, 저장된", "Orwellian": "기만적인(오웰식의)", "in disguise": "위장된", "enhanced oil recovery": "원유 회수 증진 공법"}, "src": "verbal197 Q10 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v197_q11", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, \"some environmental critics\" object to the 45Q legislation on which of the following grounds?", "choices": ["It will drive up the price of captured CO2.", "The process of extracting extra oil could have unforeseen environmental consequences.", "Fossil fuels extracted via enhanced oil recovery typically produce more carbon emissions than ethanol or natural gas.", "It will replace current subsidy programs that have been proven effective.", "Its proponents' claims that it is part of a climate change solution are misleading."], "columns": null, "pid": "v197_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'A climate change solution that entails producing more fossil fuels may sound Orwellian ... critics have attacked 45Q as just another fossil-fuel subsidy program in disguise.'\n즉 기후 해결책이라는 명목은 위장이고 실제로는 화석연료 보조금이라는 비판 → 지지자들의 '기후 해결책' 주장이 오해를 부른다.\n정답: E", "trap": "C는 그럴듯한 과학적 주장이지만 지문에 없는 비교(외부 정보). B의 '예측 못한 환경 결과'도 언급되지 않았다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "some environmental critics", "glosses": {"Orwellian": "(말과 실제가 반대인) 기만적인", "subsidy": "보조금", "entail": "수반하다"}, "src": "verbal197 Q11 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v197_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that Kurt Waltzer would likely agree with which of the following statements about the 45Q legislation?", "choices": ["It will likely replace some of the fossil-fuel subsidy programs that are currently in effect.", "It is likely to impede the development of economically efficient ways of recapturing CO2 for sequestration.", "The positive effects of other portions of the legislation will likely outweigh the environmental harm caused by its controversial aspects.", "The incentives it provides for the production of more fossil fuel are an ineffective means of reducing the production of CO2 byproducts.", "Its provision of corporate tax credits for using CO2 for enhanced oil recovery may offer a net gain in environmental terms."], "columns": null, "pid": "v197_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "Waltzer는 탄소 포집을 '에너지 기술'로 만드는 것이 CO2 제거의 광범위한 상업화로 가는 첫걸음이라고 주장(옹호론자).\n바로 앞 문장도 'enhanced oil recovery appears to reduce current emissions because the CO2 ... gets sequestered underground'.\n→ 석유 회수용 CO2 세액공제가 환경적으로 순이익이 될 수 있다고 동의할 것.\n정답: E", "trap": "C는 '다른 부분'의 긍정 효과가 '논란 부분의 해악'을 상쇄한다는 전제인데, Waltzer는 논란 부분 자체를 긍정적으로 본다. D는 그의 입장과 정반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"net gain": "순이익", "commercial adoption": "상업적 도입", "impede": "방해하다"}, "src": "verbal197 Q12 · 24년 12월 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v226_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The law student found traditional legal reference works unhelpful, since such works assume that the reader has a considerable familiarity with the intricacies of contract law, an assumption that was, in his case at least, _____.", "choices": ["pessimistic", "unwarranted", "incisive", "predictable", "unconventional"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "법학도가 전통 참고서를 쓸모없다고 느낀 이유(since): 그런 책은 독자가 계약법의 세부를 잘 안다고 가정하는데, 그 가정이 적어도 그의 경우에는 _____.\n쓸모없었다 → 그 가정이 그에게 맞지 않았다 → '근거 없는, 부당한'.\nunwarranted가 정확.\n정답: B", "trap": "pessimistic은 가정이 비관적이라는 뜻인데, 오히려 독자의 지식을 과대평가한 '낙관적' 가정이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incisive": "예리한, 통찰력 있는", "pessimistic": "비관적인", "unwarranted": "부당한, 근거 없는", "predictable": "예측 가능한", "unconventional": "관습에 얽매이지 않는"}, "src": "verbal226 Q1 · 25/11, 25/6, 25/4 중국후기"}, {"id": "v4_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Unlike, say, locusts, which simply raze entire fields, stinkbugs wreak their havoc (i) _____. The injury they do to corn, for instance, is (ii) _____ the ear is husked, at which point certain kernels—the ones into which a stinkbug stuck its pointy mouth—will reveal themselves to be sunken and brown.", "choices": null, "columns": [["periodically", "insidiously", "instantaneously"], ["invisible until", "ameliorated when", "apparent before"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'Unlike locusts, which simply raze entire fields' → 메뚜기처럼 눈에 띄게 한꺼번에 파괴하는 것과 대조.\n(i) 노린재는 은밀하게, 서서히 피해를 줌 → insidiously.\n(ii) 옥수수 피해는 껍질을 벗겨야(at which point) 드러남 → invisible until (껍질 벗기기 전까지 보이지 않음).\n정답: B (insidiously), D (invisible until)", "trap": "instantaneously는 메뚜기의 특징 쪽이라 대조가 깨지고, apparent before는 '그때 비로소 드러난다'는 at which point와 정반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"havoc": "피해", "insidiously": "은밀하게, 서서히 해롭게", "periodically": "주기적으로", "instantaneously": "즉각적으로", "invisible until": "~까지 보이지 않는", "ameliorated when": "~할 때 개선되는", "apparent before": "~전에 분명한"}, "src": "verbal4 Q3"}, {"id": "v12_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Even the most (i) _____ changes produce some (ii) _____ effects. Science and technology helped bring about unprecedented prosperity for Americans in the period after the Second World War, but also some (iii) _____ including a gap in social outlook between the generation that was born after 1945 and their parents, a schism that induced for many a deep alienation, something of a mutual incomprehension.", "choices": null, "columns": [["profound", "transient", "beneficent"], ["noticeable", "trivial", "unwanted"], ["problems", "opportunities", "consequences"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CFG", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "둘째 문장이 예시: 과학기술이 전례 없는 번영(좋은 변화)을 가져왔지만(but) 세대 간 단절, 소외 같은 문제도 가져옴.\n(i) '심지어 가장 _____ 한 변화도' → 좋은 변화 → beneficent(유익한).\n(ii) 그래도 일부 원치 않는 결과 → unwanted.\n(iii) 세대 간 단절, 깊은 소외 → problems.\n정답: C (beneficent), F (unwanted), G (problems)", "trap": "(iii)의 consequences는 중립어라 무난해 보이지만 'but also some'과 including 뒤의 부정적 예시(alienation)를 담기엔 problems가 더 정확하다. (i) profound도 끌리지만 '번영 vs 부작용' 대조를 살리지 못한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"profound": "심오한, 깊은", "transient": "일시적인", "beneficent": "유익한, 선을 베푸는", "noticeable": "눈에 띄는", "trivial": "사소한", "unwanted": "원치 않는", "problems": "문제", "opportunities": "기회", "consequences": "결과"}, "src": "verbal12 Q3"}, {"id": "v216_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Paradoxically, it is Sebald's isolating, melancholy inwardness that creates the (i) _____ between narrator and reader that is the hallmark of his writing. The more Sebald insists on his (ii) _____, the more powerfully he triggers a compensatory attentiveness, and even solicitude, in his reader. But as with any single tone maintained with such undeviating consistency, sooner or later, the problem of (iii) _____ arises: the sameness of his music can weary all but the most similarly predisposed listener.", "choices": null, "columns": [["aesthetic distance", "uncanny intimacy", "hierarchical relationship"], ["credibility", "authenticity", "loneliness"], ["histrionics", "modulation", "morality"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "(i) 'Paradoxically': 고립적이고 우울한 내면성이 오히려 화자와 독자 사이에 친밀감을 만든다 → uncanny intimacy.\n(ii) 그가 자신의 _____ 을 강조할수록 독자에게 보상적 관심과 염려를 촉발 → loneliness(외로움을 강조하니 독자가 보살피려 함).\n(iii) 단 하나의 어조를 한결같이 유지하면 '변조(어조 변화)'의 문제가 생긴다: 단조로움이 독자를 지치게 함 → modulation.\n정답: B (uncanny intimacy), F (loneliness), H (modulation)", "trap": "(i) aesthetic distance는 isolating과 어울려 보이지만 'Paradoxically'의 역설이 사라진다. (iii) histrionics는 과장 연기라 '단조로움' 문제와 반대.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"histrionics": "과장된 연기", "aesthetic distance": "미적 거리", "uncanny intimacy": "기묘한 친밀감", "hierarchical relationship": "위계적 관계", "credibility": "신뢰성", "authenticity": "진정성", "loneliness": "외로움", "modulation": "(어조의) 변화, 조절", "morality": "도덕성"}, "src": "verbal216 Q4 · 25년 7월, 25년 5월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v212_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following is true about the independent record labels?", "choices": ["They focused entirely on producing African American popular music.", "They refused to produce disco music, viewing it as too commercial.", "They preferred going into bankruptcy to losing their creative autonomy.", "They accounted for both artistic quality and popular appeal in producing soul music.", "They reacted to the decline of soul music by emphasizing more individualized voices."], "columns": null, "pid": "v212_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'independent labels had achieved success through a skillful balance of commercial and artistic considerations'.\nD의 'artistic quality and popular appeal'이 정확한 바꿔 말하기.\n정답: D", "trap": "A는 'largely the province of independent labels'를 거꾸로 '독립 레이블이 오로지 흑인 음악만 했다'로 극단화했다. C는 근거 없는 동기 추론.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"province": "영역, 분야", "quelled": "억눌린, 진압된", "dire": "심각한, 끔찍한"}, "src": "verbal212 Q5 · 24년 1월, 23년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v212_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests which of the following about “the more individualized voices”?", "choices": ["They were speaking out against corporate control of the music industry in the 1970s.", "They were less likely to be promoted by major corporations than by independent labels.", "Their number grew significantly between the end of the Second World War and the 1970s.", "They were largely responsible for the emergence of new musical styles in the 1970s.", "Their lack of concern for business led to the decline of independent music labels."], "columns": null, "pid": "v212_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 대기업 통제로 '마케팅 상품'이 강조되면서 'the more individualized voices ... being quelled'.\n반면 독립 레이블은 상업성과 예술성을 균형 있게 고려.\n→ 개성 있는 목소리는 대기업보다 독립 레이블에서 더 잘 육성(promoted)되었다는 추론.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 그 목소리들이 대기업에 '반대 발언'을 했다는 것인데 지문에 없음. D는 funk/disco 등장과 개성 있는 목소리를 근거 없이 연결.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "the more individualized voices", "glosses": {"individualized": "개성화된", "quelled": "억눌린", "autonomy": "자율성"}, "src": "verbal212 Q6 · 24년 1월, 23년 11월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that if a newly formed chondrule were to cool slowly, then", "choices": ["its surface tension would be dissipated", "it would be less susceptible to compression by gravitational forces", "it would contain different minerals than if it had cooled quickly", "its final mixture of minerals would closely resemble the initial collection", "its components would lack sufficient energy to form minerals"], "columns": null, "pid": "v198_p2", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 뜨거운 동안 성분들이 더 안정적(낮은 에너지)인 광물로 재조합 → 'Given enough time ... equilibrated'.\n실제 콘드룰은 빨리 식어 nonequilibrated 상태로 굳음.\n→ 천천히 식었다면 더 안정적인 다른 광물 조합(평형 상태)이 되었을 것 = 빨리 식었을 때와 다른 광물.\n정답: C", "trap": "D는 정반대: 천천히 식으면 초기 조합에서 멀어져 더 안정적인 조합으로 바뀐다. 초기 조합에 가까운 것은 빨리 식은 경우다. E도 빠른 냉각의 특징.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"chondrule": "콘드룰(운석 속 규산염 구슬)", "equilibrated": "평형 상태에 이른", "jostle": "밀치다, 비집고 나아가다"}, "src": "verbal198 Q7 · 24/10, 24/3, 23/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q8", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, chondrules are significant because they", "choices": ["facilitate a better understanding of the chemical properties of silicates", "explain why silicate fragments are common in meteorites", "illuminate the interactions between chemical and gravitational forces", "provide information about the mineral components present at the time of their formation", "point to episodes involving extremely high temperatures"], "columns": null, "pid": "v198_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'The importance of chondrules is that they show that at some time the temperature was so high that the chondrule material was vaporized.'\nE의 'episodes involving extremely high temperatures'가 그대로 바꿔 말함.\n정답: E", "trap": "D는 지문의 다른 내용(광물 구성 → 빠른 냉각)과 연결된 듯하지만, 지문이 명시한 '중요성'은 고온의 증거라는 점이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"vaporized": "기화된", "surface tension": "표면 장력", "compressed": "압축된"}, "src": "verbal198 Q8 · 24/10, 24/3, 23/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v198_q9", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence in the context of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["It describes a condition that is required for a critical process discussed in the passage.", "It discusses an empirical possibility that is later ruled out in the passage.", "It presents evidence that confirms a suggestion made earlier in the passage.", "It helps reconcile two seemingly conflicting findings described in the passage.", "It outlines a feature common to several physical processes mentioned in the passage."], "columns": null, "pid": "v198_p2", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "강조 문장: 기체 상태에서는 완전한 광물이 존재하지 않고, 다양하게 결합해 여러 광물을 만들 수 있는 '성분들'만 있었다.\n이는 뒤에 나오는 핵심 과정(성분들이 짝을 바꿔 더 안정적인 광물로 재조합 → 평형/비평형)의 전제 조건을 설명한다.\n→ 결정적 과정에 필요한 조건을 기술.\n정답: A", "trap": "C는 '앞서 제시된 주장을 확인하는 증거'라 하지만 강조 문장은 증거가 아니라 배경 조건 설명이다. 증거는 '비평형 광물 혼합'이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"components": "성분, 구성 요소", "nonequilibrated": "비평형 상태의", "reconcile": "조화시키다"}, "src": "verbal198 Q9 · 24/10, 24/3, 23/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v16_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Faced with so much conflicting information on the internet, many people come to believe that all sources are so _____ that efforts to discriminate between the true and the false are inevitably futile.", "choices": ["slanted", "imprecise", "splenetic", "tendentious", "surreptitious", "acrimonious"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "인터넷에 상충하는 정보가 너무 많아 사람들은 모든 출처가 너무 _____ 해서 참/거짓 구별이 헛되다고 믿게 된다.\n빈칸 = 모든 출처가 '편향된'(그러니 어느 것도 믿을 수 없음).\nslanted와 tendentious가 '편향된'으로 짝.\n정답: A (slanted), D (tendentious)", "trap": "imprecise는 문맥상 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없다. splenetic과 acrimonious는 '신랄한, 성마른'으로 짝처럼 보이지만 참/거짓 구별을 불가능하게 하는 이유가 되지 못한다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"surreptitious": "은밀한", "splenetic": "성마른, 심술궂은", "acrimonious": "신랄한, 험악한", "slanted": "편향된", "imprecise": "부정확한", "tendentious": "특정 입장에 치우친, 편향된"}, "src": "verbal16 Q9"}, {"id": "v12_q9", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Despite relying on the well-to-do for commissions, the portrait painter was no sycophant: he did not _____ when it came to depicting his patrons' wrinkles, blemishes, or self-satisfied expressions.", "choices": ["demur", "dissimulate", "exaggerate", "hyperbolize", "excel", "scruple"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 'no sycophant(아첨꾼 아님)'의 설명: 후원자의 주름, 잡티, 자만한 표정을 그리는 데 _____ 하지 않았다.\n빈칸 = '주저하다, 꺼리다'(그는 거리낌 없이 결점을 그렸다).\ndemur와 scruple(동사: 양심상 주저하다)이 짝.\n정답: A (demur), F (scruple)", "trap": "dissimulate(감추다)도 '결점을 숨기지 않았다'로 뜻은 통하지만 짝이 없다. exaggerate/hyperbolize는 짝이지만 '과장하지 않았다'는 아첨꾼이 아님을 보여주지 못한다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"sycophant": "아첨꾼", "demur": "이의를 제기하다, 주저하다", "scruple": "(양심상) 주저하다, 꺼리다", "dissimulate": "(감정·사실을) 숨기다", "exaggerate": "과장하다", "hyperbolize": "과장하다", "excel": "뛰어나다"}, "src": "verbal12 Q9"}, {"id": "v234_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Because they view Earth's resources as strictly limited, some environmentalists find the notion of sustainable growth to be _____, believing that self-restraint and sacrifice must be at the heart of any environmentally sound strategy for the future.", "choices": ["inevitable", "desirable", "dubious", "questionable", "chimerical", "certain"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "인과 'Because': 지구 자원이 엄격히 한정되어 있다고 보므로, 일부 환경론자들은 '지속 가능한 성장' 개념을 _____ 하다고 본다.\n뒤의 '자제와 희생이 핵심이어야 한다'와 연결 → 빈칸 = 부정, '의심스러운'.\ndubious와 questionable이 짝.\n정답: C (dubious), D (questionable)", "trap": "chimerical(공상적인)도 부정적이고 뜻이 통하지만 짝 단어가 없다. inevitable/certain은 짝이지만 방향이 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inevitable": "불가피한", "desirable": "바람직한", "dubious": "의심스러운", "questionable": "의문의 여지가 있는", "chimerical": "공상적인, 비현실적인", "certain": "확실한"}, "src": "verbal234 Q10 · 24년 5월, 22년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v12_q11", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following, if true, most strengthens the argument?", "choices": ["The repair caused the Mary Rose to be significantly more difficult to handle and ultimately may have led to the ship's sinking.", "The beams were fastened with wooden nails that came from trees felled after 1511.", "The beams came from a part of the ship that quite commonly needs to be repaired every few years.", "One structurally important timber came from a tree felled after 1528.", "Shipbuilders of the 1500s preferred to work with recently felled wood that was still green with sap."], "columns": null, "pid": "v12_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 1511년 이전에 벌목된 나무로 만든 들보는 원래 선체의 일부였을 것이다.\n숨은 가정: 1511년 이전에 벤 목재를 오래 보관했다가 1528/1536년 수리 때 쓰지 않았다.\nE: 당시 조선공은 갓 벌목한(green) 목재를 선호 → 오래된 목재를 수리에 썼을 가능성이 줄어 결론 강화.\n정답: E", "trap": "C는 그 부분이 자주 수리된다는 것이라 오히려 수리 때 교체되었을 가능성을 높여 약화시킨다. B도 수리 흔적을 시사해 약화.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"felled": "벌목된", "timber": "목재", "green (wood)": "갓 벤, 마르지 않은 (목재)"}, "src": "verbal12 Q11"}, {"id": "v28_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred from the passage that an abundance of heather beetles in Dutch heathlands", "choices": ["may be prevented by the proper management of heathlands", "can be caused by a lack of atmospheric nitrogen", "can result in grasses gaining increased access to sunlight", "helps check the growth of a wide variety of plants", "will inevitably be followed by years of heather beetle scarcity"], "columns": null, "pid": "v28_p4", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 처음엔 'the grasses cannot penetrate the canopy of its bushes'라 헤더가 우세.\n딱정벌레가 많으면 유충과 성충이 'defoliate the bushes'(잎을 다 갉아 먹음) → 덮개가 사라져 풀이 햇빛을 받게 됨.\n정답: C", "trap": "D는 '다양한 식물'의 성장을 억제한다고 했지만 딱정벌레는 헤더만 먹고 풀은 오히려 이득을 본다. E는 '불가피하게'가 지나친 주장.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"defoliate": "잎을 떨어뜨리다", "canopy": "(덤불의) 덮개, 수관", "irrevocably": "돌이킬 수 없게", "herbivorous": "초식성의"}, "src": "verbal28 Q14"}, {"id": "v28_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the followings best describes the function of the highlighted sentence in the author's explanation?", "choices": ["It supplies information to explain changes in atmospheric nitrogen pollution.", "It emphasizes the extent to which Dutch heathlands are ecologically fragile environments.", "It provides an example of a factor beyond the control of those seeking to preserve heather bushes.", "It suggests that the presence of intensive animal farming has been unfairly blamed for the demise of Dutch heathlands.", "It explains why there might be a lag between increases in atmospheric nitrogen and damage to heather."], "columns": null, "pid": "v28_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: 질소가 늘면 처음엔 헤더가 번성 → 딱정벌레 개체수는 해마다 다름(강조 문장) → 딱정벌레가 많은 해에 질소가 풍부한 헤더에서 유충이 잘 자라 덤불을 망침.\n즉 딱정벌레가 많은 해가 올 때까지 피해가 나타나지 않으므로, 질소 증가와 헤더 피해 사이에 시간 차가 생기는 이유를 설명.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(헤더 보존자가 통제할 수 없는 요인)는 사실일 수 있지만 지문이 다루는 주제(보존 노력)가 아니다. 저자의 설명 속 기능은 '처음엔 번성하다 나중에 무너지는' 시간 차다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"herbivorous": "초식성의", "abundant": "풍부한, 많은", "voraciously": "게걸스럽게"}, "src": "verbal28 Q15"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.5 / S2 2.8"}, {"set": 34, "sections": [[{"id": "v13_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "The subject of the lecture was not _____ the interests of the physicians who constituted the audience, and their attention perceptibly waned as the lecture progressed.", "choices": ["limited by", "exhausted by", "isolated from", "inimical to", "germane to"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결과 단서: 청중(의사들)의 관심이 눈에 띄게 줄어들었다(waned).\n→ 강연 주제가 그들의 관심사와 '관련이 없었다' → not germane to.\n정답: E (germane to)", "trap": "inimical to를 고르면 'not 적대적인' = 우호적이라 관심이 줄 이유가 없다. isolated from은 not과 합쳐 '분리되지 않음' = 관련 있음이 되어 반대.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"exhausted by": "~에 의해 완전히 다뤄지는", "limited by": "~에 의해 제한된", "isolated from": "~로부터 고립된", "inimical to": "~에 해로운, 적대적인", "germane to": "~와 밀접하게 관련된"}, "src": "verbal13 Q1"}, {"id": "v227_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "It would be imprecise to characterize her scholarship as (i) _____: though her etymological discussions are necessarily esoteric, there is nothing (ii) _____ about the conclusions she derives from them.", "choices": null, "columns": [["derivative", "arcane", "careless"], ["obscure", "controversial", "innovative"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "콜론(:) 뒤가 이유: 그녀의 어원 논의는 '불가피하게 난해(esoteric)'하지만 거기서 끌어낸 결론은 전혀 _____ 하지 않다.\n(ii) esoteric과 대조 → 결론은 '불분명하지 않다' → obscure.\n(i) 그녀의 학문을 _____ 라고 하는 것은 부정확하다 → 결론이 명확하므로 '난해한'이라 하는 건 부정확 → arcane.\n정답: B (arcane), D (obscure)", "trap": "(ii) controversial은 결론의 성격으로 그럴듯하지만 esoteric과의 대조(though)를 살리지 못한다. (i) derivative/careless는 문장 안에 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"derivative": "독창성 없는, 모방한", "arcane": "난해한, 비밀스러운", "careless": "부주의한", "obscure": "모호한, 이해하기 어려운", "controversial": "논란이 많은", "innovative": "혁신적인"}, "src": "verbal227 Q2 · 25년 8월, 24년 6월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "Unlike news reports, theater isn't expected to stick to the facts. Built on a sandy foundation of make-believe and (i) _____, the form, by nature, traffics in (ii) _____. Good documentary drama exploits its inherent paradox: creating artifice from verbatim texts, it uncovers truths by playing on the tension between what's real and what's (iii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["zeal", "pretense", "optimism"], ["illusion", "controversy", "platitudes"], ["remarkable", "invented", "predictable"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BDH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 뉴스와 달리 연극은 사실에 충실할 필요가 없다.\n(i) make-believe(가장)와 나란히 → pretense(가식, 꾸밈).\n(ii) 그 형식은 본래 환상을 다룬다 → illusion.\n(iii) 다큐 연극은 실제와 '지어낸 것' 사이의 긴장으로 진실을 드러낸다(what's real vs what's invented).\n정답: B (pretense), D (illusion), H (invented)", "trap": "(ii) controversy는 연극의 주제로 그럴듯하지만 make-believe 기반이라는 성격과 연결되지 않는다. (iii) remarkable은 real과 대립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"zeal": "열의", "pretense": "가장, 꾸밈", "optimism": "낙관주의", "illusion": "환상, 착각", "controversy": "논란", "platitudes": "진부한 말", "remarkable": "주목할 만한", "invented": "지어낸", "predictable": "예측 가능한"}, "src": "verbal221 Q3 · 25/6, 25/4, 23/3 중국후기"}, {"id": "v17_q4", "type": "RC_multi", "blanks": null, "stem": "The passage suggests that which of the following could help remedy the problem described in the highlighted sentence (\"Consequently, … hypotheses.\")?", "choices": ["An article written by a biologist for the general public summarizing current theories about avian and dinosaurian evolution", "A close examination of available data on avian and dinosaurian evolution", "A new hypothesis regarding the connection between avian and dinosaurian evolution"], "columns": null, "pid": "v17_p1", "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "문제의 원인: (1) 'a paucity of serious attempts to synthesize and evaluate available data' (2) 요약 작업이 'well-meaning but naive lay authors or reporters'에게 맡겨짐.\nA: 생물학자(전문가)가 일반 대중을 위해 현재 이론을 요약 → 원인 (2)를 해결.\nB: 기존 데이터를 면밀히 검토 → 원인 (1)을 해결.\nC: 새로운 가설은 이미 지나치게 다양한 가설에 하나를 더할 뿐, 혼란 해결책이 아님.\n정답: A, B", "trap": "C는 '새로운 연구'라 긍정적으로 보이지만, 지문의 문제는 가설 부족이 아니라 가설이 너무 많고 검증이 부족한 것이다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"paucity": "부족, 결핍", "exacerbated": "악화된", "naive": "순진한, 소박한", "dissemination": "보급, 유포"}, "src": "verbal17 Q4"}, {"id": "v31_q5", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "The argument given relies on which of the following as an assumption?", "choices": ["No other species of tree started growing in the bed of Lake Tomwa after 1200.", "No tree remains of any kind are present at the bottom of deeper parts of Lake Tomwa.", "There was at least one tree in the lake bed that was alive for the entire period from 1200 to 1320.", "There has not been a more recent drought that caused a drying up of the shallow end of the lake.", "The shallow end of the lake had been dry for less than 30 years by the time Jeffrey pines started growing in the lake bed."], "columns": null, "pid": "v31_p2", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "증거: 소나무는 1200~1320년(120년) 동안 호수 바닥에서 자람. 결론: 가뭄은 150년 미만.\n가뭄 끝 = 1320년(소나무 사멸). 그런데 가뭄 시작이 1200년보다 30년 이상 앞섰다면 150년 이상이 될 수 있다.\n→ 가정: 소나무가 자라기 시작할 때 호수 얕은 쪽이 마른 지 30년이 안 됐다(E).\n부정 테스트: 30년 이상 말라 있었다면 결론 붕괴.\n정답: E", "trap": "C(1200~1320년 내내 살아 있던 나무가 있다)는 필요 없다. 여러 나무가 이어서 자라도 기간은 증명된다. D의 더 최근 가뭄은 이 가뭄 길이와 무관.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"carbon dating": "탄소 연대 측정", "drought": "가뭄", "lake bed": "호수 바닥"}, "src": "verbal31 Q5"}, {"id": "v197_q7", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The environmental threat posed by the New Zealand mud snail, an invasive species, is _____ by the snail’s small size, which facilitates its spread across watersheds through human activity.", "choices": ["initiated", "ameliorated", "exacerbated", "extenuated", "mitigated", "aggravated"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "작은 크기가 인간 활동을 통해 유역 간 확산을 쉽게 한다(facilitates its spread) → 위협이 더 커짐.\n빈칸 = 부정적 강화, '악화되다'.\nexacerbated와 aggravated가 짝.\n정답: C (exacerbated), F (aggravated)", "trap": "ameliorated/mitigated/extenuated는 '완화되다'로 서로 짝이지만 방향이 정반대다. initiated는 짝이 없다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"initiated": "시작된", "ameliorated": "개선된", "exacerbated": "악화된", "extenuated": "(죄 등이) 경감된", "mitigated": "완화된", "aggravated": "악화된"}, "src": "verbal197 Q7 · 24/6, 24/3, 23/10 중국후기"}, {"id": "v19_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Since some contemporary western dieticians believe that the only function of food is to provide nourishment, these dieticians view an emphasis on the aesthetic dimension of the culinary art as ____________.", "choices": ["unprecedented", "unwarranted", "illuminating", "groundless", "promising", "novel"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "인과 'Since': 음식의 유일한 기능이 영양 공급이라고 믿으므로, 요리의 미적 측면을 강조하는 것을 _____ 하다고 본다.\n빈칸 = 부정, '근거 없는, 정당하지 않은'.\nunwarranted와 groundless가 짝.\n정답: B (unwarranted), D (groundless)", "trap": "unprecedented와 novel은 '새로운'으로 짝처럼 보이지만, 영양만 중요하다는 믿음에서 나오는 판단은 '새롭다'가 아니라 '불필요/부당하다'이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unprecedented": "전례 없는", "unwarranted": "부당한, 근거 없는", "illuminating": "깨달음을 주는", "groundless": "근거 없는", "promising": "유망한", "novel": "새로운"}, "src": "verbal19 Q6"}, {"id": "v231_q6", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The writer had little interest in realism; many of his stories take place in a world either fancifully sketched out or purposefully _____.", "choices": ["mythical", "plausible", "mundane", "enigmatic", "banal", "ambiguous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "DF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "세미콜론: 작가는 사실주의에 관심이 없었다 → 이야기의 세계는 '공상적으로 그려지거나(fancifully sketched)' 또는 '의도적으로 _____'.\n빈칸 = 사실주의와 반대, 공상과는 다른 축 → 일부러 '모호한, 불가해한'.\nenigmatic과 ambiguous가 짝.\n정답: D (enigmatic), F (ambiguous)", "trap": "mythical은 비사실적이라 끌리지만 fancifully sketched와 겹치고 짝이 없다. mundane/banal은 짝이지만 사실주의 쪽이라 반대.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"mythical": "신화적인, 가공의", "plausible": "그럴듯한", "mundane": "평범한, 세속적인", "enigmatic": "불가사의한", "banal": "진부한", "ambiguous": "모호한"}, "src": "verbal231 Q6 · 25년 5월, 25년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v205_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Terms like \"mystery fiction\" and \"crime fiction\" have connotations that may not be _____ but are hardly laudatory, at least not in the way that those of terms like \"literary fiction\" and \"metaphysical poetry\" are laudatory.", "choices": ["derogatory", "belittling", "pedantic", "enviable", "desirable", "contemporary"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AB", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'may not be _____ but are hardly laudatory': ~라고까지는 할 수 없지만 칭찬도 아니다.\n빈칸은 laudatory(칭찬)의 반대 극단, 즉 '경멸적인'이 들어가야 '경멸까지는 아니지만 칭찬도 아님'의 중간 지대가 생김.\nderogatory와 belittling이 짝.\n정답: A (derogatory), B (belittling)", "trap": "enviable/desirable은 짝이지만 'may not be 긍정 but hardly 칭찬'이 되어 but의 대조가 성립하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"hardly laudatory": "칭찬할만하지 않은", "derogatory": "경멸적인, 비하하는", "belittling": "깎아내리는", "pedantic": "현학적인", "enviable": "부러운", "desirable": "바람직한", "contemporary": "현대의, 동시대의"}, "src": "verbal205 Q8 · 25년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q10", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The primary purpose of the passage is to", "choices": ["correct a common misconception about a historical period", "identify a feature of a historical period that has often been overlooked", "challenge the validity of evidence used to support a claim", "discuss certain challenges to a particular view", "account for a particular feature of a historical period"], "columns": null, "pid": "v221_p10", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "첫 문장: 'Some historians have recently challenged the party period paradigm'.\n이후 Voss-Hubbard, Formisano의 도전을 소개하고, McCormick의 반론과 패러다임의 강점(비교적 관점)을 제시.\n→ 특정 견해에 대한 도전들을 논의.\n정답: D", "trap": "C(증거의 타당성에 도전)는 McCormick의 반박 부분만 반영해 범위가 좁다. A는 지문이 '오해를 바로잡는다'는 결론을 내리지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"paradigm": "패러다임, 이론적 틀", "antipathy": "반감", "enfranchisement": "참정권 부여", "siphon off": "빼돌리다"}, "src": "verbal221 Q10 · 25/11, 25/4, 24/10, 24/4, 22/12, 22/11, 22/10 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q11", "type": "RC_select", "blanks": null, "stem": "Select the sentence in the passage that describes how a historian might reply to attempts to call his theory into question.", "choices": null, "columns": null, "pid": "v221_p10", "answer": "SENTENCE", "answer_sentence": "Yet McCormick would deny that the existence of antiparty sentiment during the period undermines the paradigm, since he has always acknowledged the residual strength of such sentiment during the nineteenth century.", "explanation": "'자신의 이론에 대한 문제 제기에 어떻게 답할지'를 묻는다.\n이론의 주인 = McCormick(party period paradigm). 'Yet McCormick would deny that ... undermines the paradigm, since he has always acknowledged ...'가 그의 반론을 기술.\n정답: Yet McCormick would deny that the existence of antiparty sentiment during the period undermines the paradigm, ...", "trap": "마지막 문장 'In any case, the strength of the paradigm...'은 저자의 평가이지 역사가(McCormick) 본인의 대응이 아니다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"residual": "잔존하는", "undermine": "약화시키다", "acknowledge": "인정하다"}, "src": "verbal221 Q11 · 25/11, 25/4, 24/10, 24/4, 22/12, 22/11, 22/10 중국후기"}, {"id": "v221_q12", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "In the context in which it appears, “evoked” most nearly means", "choices": ["elicited", "recalled", "cited", "suggested", "elaborated"], "columns": null, "pid": "v221_p10", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'political parties ... evoked extraordinary loyalty from voters': 정당이 유권자로부터 엄청난 충성심을 '끌어냈다'.\nelicited(이끌어내다)가 정확.\n정답: A", "trap": "evoke의 흔한 뜻 '(기억을) 떠올리게 하다'에 끌려 recalled를 고르기 쉽지만 문맥은 충성을 '불러일으키다/얻어내다'.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": "evoked", "glosses": {"evoke": "불러일으키다", "elicit": "끌어내다", "elaborate": "자세히 설명하다"}, "src": "verbal221 Q12 · 25/11, 25/4, 24/10, 24/4, 22/12, 22/11, 22/10 중국후기"}], [{"id": "v18_q1", "type": "TC", "blanks": 1, "stem": "Saturn's rings seem __________, but it now appears that several decades ago, the shape of the innermost rings was altered by a mysterious event that all our telescopes and spacecraft failed to detect.", "choices": ["immutable", "fragmentary", "luminous", "unique", "concentric"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "대조 'but': 토성의 고리는 _____ 해 보이지만, 수십 년 전 미지의 사건으로 모양이 바뀌었다(altered).\n빈칸 = altered의 반대, '변하지 않는'.\nimmutable이 정확.\n정답: A", "trap": "concentric(동심원의)은 고리의 실제 모양이라 끌리지만 'shape was altered'와 대조 관계를 이루지 못한다.", "difficulty": 1, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"immutable": "불변의", "fragmentary": "단편적인", "luminous": "빛나는", "unique": "독특한", "concentric": "동심원의"}, "src": "verbal18 Q1"}, {"id": "v216_q3", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Not only is the field of behavioral genetics strewn with (i) _____ findings, but even among those findings managed to survive, many have turned out to be (ii) _____ a very restricted class of cases.", "choices": null, "columns": [["convergent", "disparate", "repudiated"], ["refuted by", "germane to", "subordinate to"]], "pid": null, "answer": "CE", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'Not only A, but even B' 점층 구조: 행동유전학은 (i) 결과로 가득하고, 살아남은 결과들조차 많은 경우 매우 제한된 사례에만 (ii).\n'those findings managed to survive'(살아남은 결과) → (i)은 살아남지 못한 결과 → repudiated(부정된).\n(ii) 살아남았어도 아주 좁은 범위에만 '해당되는' → germane to.\n정답: C (repudiated), E (germane to)", "trap": "(ii) refuted by는 '반박되었다'로 부정적 흐름에 맞아 보이지만 '살아남은' 결과가 반박되었다는 것은 모순이고 '제한된 사례에 의해 반박'은 어색하다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"germane to": "~와 관련 있는, 적절한", "convergent": "수렴하는", "disparate": "이질적인", "repudiated": "부인된, 거부된", "refuted by": "~에 의해 반박된", "subordinate to": "~에 종속된"}, "src": "verbal216 Q3 · 25/2, 24/8, 23/6, 23/2, 22/10 중국후기"}, {"id": "v8_q2", "type": "TC", "blanks": 2, "stem": "Discovering that cooler stars, which constitute three-quarters of our galaxy, can also be surrounded by habitable zones warm enough to harbor liquid water and potentially microbes and bacteria has (i) _____ the (ii) _____ the search for extraterrestrial life.", "choices": null, "columns": [["assuaged", "expanded", "jeopardized"], ["target territory in", "popular discomfort with", "primary motivation for"]], "pid": null, "answer": "BD", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "더 차가운 별(은하의 3/4)도 생명 가능 지대를 가질 수 있다는 발견 → 외계 생명 탐색의 '대상 범위'가 넓어짐.\n(i) expanded (ii) target territory in.\n정답: B (expanded), D (target territory in)", "trap": "assuaged(누그러뜨렸다)+popular discomfort with도 문법상 가능해 보이지만, 발견 내용(탐색 가능한 별이 늘어남)과 대중의 불안은 연결 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"assuaged": "누그러뜨렸다", "expanded": "확장했다", "jeopardized": "위태롭게 했다", "target territory in": "~의 대상 영역", "popular discomfort with": "~에 대한 대중의 불편함", "primary motivation for": "~의 주된 동기"}, "src": "verbal8 Q2"}, {"id": "v14_q4", "type": "TC", "blanks": 3, "stem": "William Newman and Lawrence Principe point out that, prior to the seventeenth century, the terms \"alchemy\" and \"chemistry\" were largely (i) _____ in European usage. It was from the third decade of the eighteenth century that the two terms began to (ii) _____. Newman and Principe suggest that a third term, \"chymistry,\" should be used to denote the transitional early modern phase when \"alchemy\" and \"chemistry\" were becoming (iii) _____.", "choices": null, "columns": [["interchangeable", "absent", "misapplied"], ["coalesce", "proliferate", "diverge"], ["increasingly more convoluted", "steadily less synonymous", "fundamentally less significant"]], "pid": null, "answer": "AFH", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'chymistry'라는 제3의 용어는 alchemy와 chemistry가 갈라지던 과도기를 가리킴.\n(i) 17세기 이전에는 두 용어가 대체로 같은 뜻 → interchangeable.\n(ii) 18세기 30년대부터 두 용어가 갈라지기 시작 → diverge.\n(iii) 과도기에는 점점 덜 동의어가 되어 감 → steadily less synonymous.\n정답: A (interchangeable), F (diverge), H (steadily less synonymous)", "trap": "(ii) coalesce(합쳐지다)는 방향이 정반대이고, (iii) fundamentally less significant는 두 용어의 '관계'가 아니라 중요도를 말해 흐름과 맞지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"interchangeable": "서로 바꿔 쓸 수 있는", "absent": "없는", "misapplied": "잘못 적용된", "coalesce": "합쳐지다", "proliferate": "급증하다", "diverge": "갈라지다", "increasingly more convoluted": "점점 더 복잡한", "steadily less synonymous": "점점 덜 동의어인", "fundamentally less significant": "근본적으로 덜 중요한"}, "src": "verbal14 Q4"}, {"id": "v230_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Based on information in the passage, it can be inferred that a radar image of Titan is most likely to be able to show", "choices": ["whether a lake is filled or mostly dry", "whether a surface is bedrock", "the height of a hill or mountain", "the age of a geological feature", "the contents of a deep canyon"], "columns": null, "pid": "v230_p1", "answer": "A", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 메탄으로 채워진 호수의 매끄러운 표면은 어둡게 보이고, 'Many detected river valleys and lakes appear bright ... suggesting a generally dry riverbed or lake bed filled with gravel or cobble'.\n→ 레이더 밝기로 호수가 차 있는지(어둡다) 말라 있는지(밝다) 구별 가능.\n정답: A", "trap": "B(기반암 여부)는 어두운 강 계곡에 대한 '한 가설(one theory)'일 뿐 레이더가 확실히 보여준다고 할 수 없다. C의 높이는 거칠기와 별개.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"incised": "깊이 파인", "cobble": "자갈, 조약돌", "meandering": "구불구불한"}, "src": "verbal230 Q5 · 24/6, 23/10, 22/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v230_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence in the contest of the passage as a whole?", "choices": ["It introduces a necessary consequence of the preceding sentence.", "It qualifies a general rule by examining a particular case.", "It poses a problem that is addressed in the following sentence.", "It shows how a general rule applies in a particular case.", "It proposes an interpretation that is later questioned."], "columns": null, "pid": "v230_p1", "answer": "D", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "앞 문장이 일반 규칙: 'the brightness of the reflected signal correlates with the roughness of the surface'.\n강조 문장 'Thus, ...': 그 규칙을 타이탄의 경우에 적용 → 매끄러운 호수는 어둡고, 밝은 곳은 거친 언덕.\n→ 일반 규칙이 특정 사례에 어떻게 적용되는지 보여줌.\n정답: D", "trap": "B(특정 사례로 규칙에 단서를 단다)는 다음 문장 'However, the data don't always follow this pattern'의 기능이다. A는 'necessary'가 지나침(usually suggest).", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"meandering": "구불구불한", "correlate": "상관관계가 있다", "qualify": "단서를 달다, 제한하다"}, "src": "verbal230 Q6 · 24/6, 23/10, 22/11 중국후기"}, {"id": "v30_q5", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, the “reformers” claimed that", "choices": ["neither scientific management nor reduced hours would result in an improvement in the working conditions of most workers", "the impact that the routinization of work had on workers could be mitigated by a reduction in the length of their workweek", "there was an inherent tension between the principles of scientific management and a commitment to reduced workweeks", "scientific managers were more likely than other managers to use pay differentials to encourage higher productivity", "reducing the length of the workweek would increase productivity more effectively than would increases in pay"], "columns": null, "pid": "v30_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'Those reformers who wished to embrace both scientific management and reduced hours had to make a largely negative case, portraying the latter as an antidote to the rigors of the former.'\n즉 근로시간 단축(the latter)이 과학적 관리(the former)의 가혹함에 대한 해독제 → 일상화가 노동자에게 주는 영향을 근로시간 단축으로 완화할 수 있다.\n정답: B", "trap": "C(둘 사이의 본질적 긴장)는 개혁가들이 '해독제'라는 부정적 논거를 쓴 데서 끌리지만, 그들은 둘을 '모두 수용'하려 했으므로 양립 불가를 주장한 것이 아니다. E는 Ford의 주장.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "reformers", "glosses": {"routinizing": "일상화(정형화)하는", "antidote": "해독제", "rigors": "가혹함, 엄격함", "pay differentials": "임금 격차"}, "src": "verbal30 Q5"}, {"id": "v30_q6", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage mentions “automobiles” primarily to suggest that", "choices": ["Ford’s business produced greater profits than did businesses requiring a workweek longer than five days", "Ford, unlike most other employers, encouraged his employees to use the products they produced", "Ford may have advocated shorter hours because of the particular nature of his business", "unions were more likely to negotiate for shorter hours in some businesses than in others", "automobile workers’ unions were more effective than other unions in securing a five-day workweek"], "columns": null, "pid": "v30_p1", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'few employers matched either Ford's vision or his specific interest in mass marketing a product—automobiles—that required leisure for its use'.\n자동차는 쓰려면 여가가 필요한 상품 → Ford가 근로시간 단축을 주장한 것은 그의 사업 특성 때문일 수 있다.\n정답: C", "trap": "B(직원이 자기 제품을 쓰도록 장려)는 그럴듯한 역사 지식이지만 지문에 없다. A는 이윤 비교를 지문이 하지 않는다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": "automobiles", "glosses": {"mass marketing": "대량 판매", "bargaining": "단체 교섭", "leisure": "여가"}, "src": "verbal30 Q6"}, {"id": "v30_q7", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "It can be inferred that the author of the passage would probably agree with which of the following claims about the boast referred to in the second paragraph?", "choices": ["It is based on a mistaken estimation of the number of AFL workers who were allowed to work a five-day, 40-hour week in 1928.", "It could create a mistaken impression regarding the number of unions obtaining a five-day, 40-hour week during the 1920s.", "It exaggerates the extent of the increase between 1926 and 1928 in AFL members working a five-day, 40-hour week.", "It overestimates the bargaining prowess of the AFL building trades’ unions during the 1920s.", "It is based on an overestimation of the number of union members in the AFL in 1928."], "columns": null, "pid": "v30_p1", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "AFL은 약 16만 5천 명이 주 5일 40시간 근무한다고 자랑했다(boasted).\n그러나 'about 70 percent of the total came from five extremely well-organized building trades' unions'.\n→ 숫자는 정확하더라도 많은 노조가 주 5일제를 얻어낸 것처럼 잘못된 인상을 줄 수 있다.\n정답: B", "trap": "A/E는 숫자 자체가 틀렸다고 하지만 저자는 수치를 문제 삼지 않는다. C도 7만 5천 명 증가는 그대로 인정된다. 문제는 '분포'다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"boast": "자랑하다", "convention": "(정기) 총회", "prowess": "뛰어난 능력"}, "src": "verbal30 Q7"}, {"id": "v240_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The sailors realized too late that winds had shifted the ice in such a way as to obstruct the ship's path; this process had been so _____ that it was completed by the time they discovered the effect.", "choices": ["gradual", "negligible", "unpredictable", "time-consuming", "inconsequential", "imperceptible"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "AF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "선원들은 너무 늦게 알아챘다: 이 과정이 너무 _____ 해서 발견했을 때는 이미 끝나 있었다.\n빈칸 = 알아차리기 어려울 만큼 '서서히, 눈에 띄지 않게'.\ngradual과 imperceptible이 '알아챌 수 없을 만큼 점진적인'으로 통한다.\n정답: A (gradual), F (imperceptible)", "trap": "negligible/inconsequential은 '사소한'으로 짝이지만, 배의 길을 막았으니 결과는 결코 사소하지 않다. time-consuming은 늦게 알아챈 이유가 되지 못하고 짝도 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"gradual": "점진적인", "negligible": "무시할 만한", "unpredictable": "예측 불가능한", "time-consuming": "시간이 많이 걸리는", "inconsequential": "중요하지 않은", "imperceptible": "감지할 수 없는"}, "src": "verbal240 Q10 · 25년 7월, 24년 8월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v26_q10", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "Noise suppression in phones can play an important role in making cellphone networks more efficient, since when sounds that are _____ to the meaningful signal are transmitted, precious network bandwidth is wasted.", "choices": ["unsuitable", "detrimental", "irrelevant", "confined", "limited", "extraneous"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "CF", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "잡음 억제가 네트워크 효율을 높인다: 의미 있는 신호와 _____ 한 소리가 전송되면 대역폭이 낭비되기 때문(since).\n빈칸 = 의미 있는 신호와 '무관한, 불필요한'.\nirrelevant와 extraneous가 짝.\n정답: C (irrelevant), F (extraneous)", "trap": "detrimental(해로운)은 잡음의 성격으로 그럴듯하지만 짝이 없고, 문장의 핵심은 해로움이 아니라 '불필요해서 낭비'라는 것이다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"unsuitable": "부적합한", "detrimental": "해로운", "irrelevant": "무관한", "confined": "한정된", "limited": "제한된", "extraneous": "외부의, 무관한"}, "src": "verbal26 Q10"}, {"id": "v8_q8", "type": "SE", "blanks": null, "stem": "The 1966 Mexican art exhibition \"Confrontation 66\" seemed to define the Mexican art world as one in which political alignment was _____, yet painter Joy Laville rose to prominence with paintings devoid of contentiousness.", "choices": ["inconsequential", "ineluctable", "requisite", "perilous", "pointless", "obsolete"], "columns": null, "pid": null, "answer": "BC", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "'yet' 대조: Laville는 논쟁성이 전혀 없는(devoid of contentiousness) 그림으로 명성을 얻었다.\n→ 앞부분의 미술계는 정치적 성향(편 가르기)이 '필수적인' 곳으로 정의되었어야 대조가 성립.\nineluctable(피할 수 없는)과 requisite(필수의)가 '불가피한/필수적인'으로 짝.\n정답: B (ineluctable), C (requisite)", "trap": "inconsequential/pointless는 '무의미한'으로 짝을 이루지만, 그러면 비정치적 화가의 성공이 당연한 일이 되어 yet의 대조가 사라진다.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"inconsequential": "중요하지 않은", "ineluctable": "피할 수 없는", "requisite": "필수적인", "perilous": "위험한", "pointless": "무의미한", "obsolete": "구식의"}, "src": "verbal8 Q8"}, {"id": "v224_q13", "type": "CR", "blanks": null, "stem": "Which of the following would it be most useful to know in evaluating the reasoning of the argument?", "choices": ["Whether the drop in white blood cell count that occurs in rats under conditions of stress is sufficient to make the rats more susceptible to diseases that white blood cells normally combat.", "Whether normal white blood cell counts vary widely among healthy rats that are not under conditions of stress.", "Whether the adrenal glands of rats that are under conditions of stress increase production of any hormone other than corticosterone.", "Whether the adrenal glands of rats produce elevated levels of corticosterone on occasions when the rats are not under conditions of stress.", "Whether rats’ adrenal glands are affected by hormones produced by any of the rats’ other organs."], "columns": null, "pid": "v224_p13", "answer": "C", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "결론: 부신에서 나온 corticosterone 증가가 백혈구 감소를 일으킨다.\n근거: 부신이 없는 쥐는 스트레스를 받아도 백혈구가 거의 줄지 않음 → 부신이 원인임은 보이지만, 부신의 '어떤 물질'인지는 확정하지 못함.\nC: 스트레스 시 부신이 다른 호르몬도 늘리는지 알면, 대안 원인(다른 호르몬)을 배제할 수 있는지 평가 가능.\n정답: C", "trap": "D는 관련 있어 보이지만, 스트레스 없을 때 corticosterone이 높아지는지는 스트레스 상황의 인과를 직접 검증하지 못한다. A는 결과의 의미일 뿐 인과와 무관.", "difficulty": 4, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"adrenal glands": "부신", "white blood cell count": "백혈구 수", "susceptible": "~에 취약한"}, "src": "verbal224 Q13 · 24년 3월, 23년 1월 중국후기"}, {"id": "v10_q14", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "The author mentions the fact that evening bats radio-tracked since 1993 have roosted in trees primarily in order to", "choices": ["account for a puzzling aspect of evening bat behavior mentioned earlier in the passage", "introduce evidence that indicates a change in evening bat behavior discussed later in the passage.", "undermine a theory about evening bat behavior presented earlier in the passage", "provide a contrast between evening bat behavior and big brown bat behavior", "provide an example of evening bat behavior that fits well-established scientific views of the species"], "columns": null, "pid": "v10_p4", "answer": "B", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "흐름: 1961~1993년 기록상 evening bat 둥지는 모두 건물 → 1993년 이후 추적한 박쥐는 모두 나무에서 쉼('notable').\n이후 지문은 그 변화를 설명: 건물 둥지의 사라짐, big brown bat와의 경쟁 등.\n→ 뒤에서 논의될 행동 변화를 보여주는 증거를 도입.\n정답: B", "trap": "A는 '앞서 언급된 수수께끼'를 설명한다고 하지만, 이 사실 자체가 수수께끼(설명이 필요한 대상)이다. C는 앞에 반박할 이론이 없다.", "difficulty": 3, "q_highlight": "the fact that all evening bats radio-tracked since 1993 have roosted in trees was notable", "glosses": {"roost": "보금자리, 쉬는 곳", "spillover": "넘쳐 나옴, 파급", "radio-tracked": "전파 추적된"}, "src": "verbal10 Q14"}, {"id": "v10_q15", "type": "RC_single", "blanks": null, "stem": "According to the passage, the disappearance after 1993 of known evening bat roosts in buildings suggests which of the following?", "choices": ["After 1993 evening bats in Indiana were less likely to live near rivers.", "Humans and their structures became increasingly threatening after 1993.", "The spillover of large bat populations from woods near rivers increased after 1993.", "Evening bats in Indiana inhabited the roosts previously used by big brown bats.", "In Indiana, evening bats' adaptation to buildings was ultimately undermined by other factors."], "columns": null, "pid": "v10_p4", "answer": "E", "answer_sentence": null, "explanation": "근거: 'the disappearance after 1993 of previously known roosts in buildings suggests that this adaptation became less successful'.\n이어서 big brown bat와의 경쟁 가능성 제시 → 다른 요인이 건물 적응을 약화시켰다.\nE가 정확한 바꿔 말하기.\n정답: E", "trap": "D는 정반대 방향: 지문은 evening bat이 big brown bat과의 건물 둥지 경쟁에서 밀렸을 수 있다고 한다. B는 인간 구조물이 위협이 되었다는 근거가 없다.", "difficulty": 2, "q_highlight": null, "glosses": {"roost": "보금자리", "adaptation": "적응", "compete": "경쟁하다"}, "src": "verbal10 Q15"}]], "summary": "TC 7 · SE 7 · RC/CR 13 | 난이도 S1 2.3 / S2 2.6"}]};
